window.HIFI_ENRICH = {"akai-aa-6000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥53,000. amplifier amplifier The power switch and volume control control are located in the center of the front panel, and the tone control of the left and right is placed in the lower part of the balance control. The preamplifier part has a low noise trans.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Akai AA-6000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AKAI/amp/aa-6000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/akai-aa-6000.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AKAI/amp/aa-6000.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AKAI/amp/aa-6000.jpg"}},"altec-lansing-770-a":{"more":[{"t":"Electronic crossover and power amplifier. 770A has built-in two power amplifiers for low and high fre cies and an electronic crossover network, which was used for active loudspeaker systems such as 2873A Barcelona and 2875A Granada. If you play a large dynamic range of recordings, you may experience a distortion caused by clipping of a high frequency amplifier because it tends to consume the overall energy for bass playback. By attaching this phenomenon, it realizes smooth playback sound. It has succeeded in removing DC crossover distortion and prevents the sound quality of the middle and high fre cies at low level playback. Altech is set to the optimal damping factor for driving loudspeaker, which improves the transient response, and the split frequency is designed to switch to the Altech specified 500Hz and 800Hz.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Altec Lansing 770 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ALTEC/amp/770a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/altec-lansing-770-a.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ALTEC/amp/770a.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ALTEC/amp/770a.jpg"}},"fisher-800-t":{"more":[{"t":"Vintage Fisher tube receivers are some of the most popular receivers among collectors and audio enthusiasts. Receivers such as the Fisher 500 and 800 fall into that category. During the transition from tube to solid state electronics in the late 60’s Fisher produced the Fisher 800 T which is the solid state version, figuratively more than literally, of the Fisher 800. It is actually very similar to the Fisher 500TX except that it has a dual voltage transformer and a different colored face plate. It was made by Fisher in the United States from around 1968 to 1972. I’ve read that the 800T is possibly the export version of the 500TX, hence the dual voltage capability. The Fisher 800-T puts out 65 watts per channel. An interesting aspect of this receiver is that it has four ways to adjust the tuning. First is a wired remote, the RK-30, which nowadays, is very hard to find.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Fisher 800-T","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/fisher-800-t","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"heathkit-ar-17":{"more":[{"t":"This little receiver is the Heathkit AR-17. Measuring just 10 3/8 x 3 x 12 inches it packs a small punch with just 10 watts per channel RMS from 25-35,000hz at +/- 1dB and 5 wpc of continuous power output. But, for those that liked to build their own equipment the Heathkit AR-17 was a great option. For just $69.95 you could buy the kit, without a cabinet, and build it yourself. Or, if you had no excess cash you could buy it with no money down and pay only $8 a month. There were two cabinet options available. A beige metal cabinet for an additional $3.50 or a genuine walnut veneer cabinet for only $9.95 more. A 6-position source switch allows the user to choose between FM, Phono and Aux in both mono and stereo. The Phase Control let you fine tune your chosen FM station.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Heathkit AR-17","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/heathkit-ar-17","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/heathkit-ar-17.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/heathkit-ar-17","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/heathkit-ar-17-cabinet.jpg"}},"hitachi-ia-1200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥98,000. amplifier amplifier High S/N ratio by adopting low noise and high quality trans. The power amplifier is equipped with 30Wx4 channel amplifier, and the power can be switched by the channel selector. In addition, it can be used as a compact multi-channel divider by incorporating a separate multi-channel divider. In addition, when full range connection, it becomes a bridge type output circuit, and it can get a large output. Power limit circuit is installed to prevent excessive input to loudspeaker. This circuit can be set according to the tolerance input of loudspeaker. The equalizer circuit button. Tone control with defeit switch Low cut and high cut filter","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi IA-1200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ia-1200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/hitachi-ia-1200.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ia-1200.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ia-1200.JPG"}},"hitachi-sr-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥39,000. Stereo receiver developed using our own silicon trans. The power amplifier part is the SEPP ITL-OTL configuration, and the Complementary Darlington circuit is used. LTP trans is used to handle small input signals such as equalizer amplifier and preamplifier. The front end part adopts FET and 3 varicon. It has high sensitivity and high stability, and also improves the ability to eliminate interfering waves and S/N ratio. It is equipped with a pure electronic mono-stereo switch circuit, and it is automatically switched to stereo broadcasting when FM stereo broadcast. FM muting circuit removes unpleasant local noise. ferrite bar antenna for AM. Tape monitor circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi SR-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/sr-300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-sr-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥56,800. FM/AM receiver that demonstrates the characteristics of solid state and uses the soft sound of the triode to the design policy. The part is composed of SEPP and ITL-OTL. This circuit reduces harmonic distortion and IM distortion by using a silicon power trans with hfe characteristics. LTP trans is used to handle small input signals such as equalizer and preamplifier. The front end part is high sensitivity and high stability by using the FET and the triple varicon, while also improving the ability to eliminate interfering waves such as cross-modulation and image regeneration, and the S/N ratio. The intermediate frequency a ification circuit adopts mechanical filter, which has a wide band and sharp selection. It is equipped with a pure electronic mono-stereo switch circuit, and it is automatically switched when receiving FM stereo broadcast. Equipped with ferrite antenna for AM. Scr noise filter, tape monitor circuit, loudness control The Phono input sensitivity switch is mounted.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi SR-600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/sr-600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-icm-105-m":{"more":[{"t":"4 channel power amplifier of 105 series developed for multi-channel playback. Power IC for the first time was released as a power amplifier. The power IC used in ICM-105M is equipped with a semi-complementary circuit. Also, because it is a hybrid type (mixed integrated circuit), it is compact, without worrying about heat generation while large power. MTR-10M and other multi-source tape decks can be connected to the four-channel source system. 4 VU meter The meter is equipped with a sensitivity switch, and can be switched three-stage according to the input. 4 input adjustment volume control","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC ICM-105 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/icm-105m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-2120":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥44,800. Stereo receiver. tone control It has tape monitor function.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-2120 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-2120.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-3130":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥54,800. Stereo receiver. In addition to to tone control and loudness control, noise filter is also installed. It has tape monitor function. Microphone input","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-3130 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-3130.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-4140":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥66,800. FM/AM receiver Tone control, low filter, high filter, loudness control, etc. It has tape monitor function. FM tuner","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-4140 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-4140.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-5150":{"more":[{"t":"Ok, the Kenwood KR-5150 has some strange styling. Black, white, orange and green. Almost a Halloween look and those white buttons really stand out like tusks. This Kenwood classic came out around 1971 and lasted until around 1975 and featured 50 watts per channel. This one has the optional wood case which you don’t actually see too often with this receiver. It retailed for around $320.00-$350.00. The styling definitely the design transition from the late 60’s in to the mid 70’s. Later Kenwood models had a more appealing design. This particular Kenwood model isn’t all that popular with collectors and they can be found for under $200.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-5150","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-5150","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-7070":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥150,000. FM/AM receiver with auto-tuning mechanism. It is equipped with an electronic FM mono/stereo switch mechanism. If you set the selector to FM-Auto, it will automatically switch to stereo reception when stereo broadcasting reception, and the display lamp on the dial surface will be lighted. SCA filter KR-7070 is designed to connect MC cartridge as it is, there is no need to use ascending pressure. Equipped with a pure electronic protection circuit, the power trans is protected.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-7070 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-7070.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-8140":{"more":[{"t":"Model: Kenwood KR-8140 – 4-channelType: ReceiverYear: 1970Watts Per Channel: 26 (4-channel mode)","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-8140","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/kenwood/kenwood-kr-8140-receivers-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-mq-830":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1970 at ¥23,000. Stereo power amplifier designed for multi-channel mid-range applications. The circuit is an all-silicon trans structure, and the bi-complementary circuit is used for the circuit method. The output stage is SEPP-OTL. Emitter folore circuit is inserted in front of the six trans s that make up the power amplifier part. This keeps input impedance high and prevents distortion. This is a structure that omits the protective circuit by the unique circuit method of the LUXMAN. The input level set volume control enables adjustment of input sensitivity. The loudspeaker terminal is equipped with a new Rachsman development terminal. The front panel is made of alumite dyeing of white gold by hairline.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman MQ 830 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mq830.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-mq-830.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mq830.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mq830.jpg"}},"luxman-mq-860":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1970 at ¥31,000. Stereo amplifier developed for multi-channel and 3D expansion. The circuit is an all-silicon trans structure, and the bi-complementary circuit is used for the circuit method. In addition, SEPPOTL method is used for output stage. 6 trans circuits that make up the power amplifier circuit are inserted into the emitter folore circuit. This keeps input impedance high and prevents distortion. It is a structure that eliminates the protective circuit by its own method. Volume control for input level set The loudspeaker terminal has a new Rachsman original. The front panel is made of alumite dyeing of white gold.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman MQ 860 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mq860.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-mq-860.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mq860.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mq860.jpg"}},"luxman-sq-202":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1970 at ¥141,000. The top model of the raxman integrated amplifier. The power amplifier part is variable input sensitivity by setting the emitter folore circuit at the beginning. The output of the equalizer circuit is sent to the next stage through the balancer of the switch and volume control. The output of this stage is directly connected to the input stage of the power amplifier when the tone control circuit and filter circuit are turned off. The tone control circuit adopts a negative feedback (NF) type of lux. The curve point is 3 points high and 3 points low.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ 202 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq202.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-sq-503":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1969 at ¥48,000. Based on SQ606, SQ505, etc., this integrated amplifier has been improved in consideration of the balance of performance, musical performance, style and usability. The power amplifier uses the quasi complimentary service SEPPP OTL system. By using a unique method, a protection circuit is omitted. The preamplifier section receives a 2-stage direct-coupled negative feedback (NF)-type equalizer circuit at the emitter-follower stage, converts the impedance, amplifies it to an appropriate level by an intermediate negative feedback (NF) amplifier, and adjusts the sound quality by the LUX negative feedback (NF)-type tone control. A carefully selected low-noise transistor is used in this part. Equipped with two speaker terminals. The tone controls are independent on the left and right, and the attenuator switch can reduce the gain by 18 dB. Since there is a tape monitor switch, simultaneous playback monitoring can be performed with a 3-head tape recorder, etc. The entire panel and knobs are made of aluminum material with hairline processing and white gold anodized.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman SQ 503 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/sq503-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-sq-503.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/sq503-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/sq503(1).JPG"}},"luxman-sq-503-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1971 at ¥51,000. As an economical type of SQ505X, the integrated amplifier incorporates a design that emphasizes practicality and eliminates waste. The power amplifier part adopts the full-stage direct connection circuit that removes the output capac by the ±2 power supply method. This ensures sufficient power characters and damping factors up to ultra-low ranges. Crossover distortion is also removed. It maintains high stability against the DC drift. trans uses PNP type and NPN type to improve power supply utilization. The precursor adopts ultra-low-noise trans, which is essentially composed of high-quality PNP trans. This makes trans -specific mid-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-to-high-high-quality noise less than once.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ 503 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq503x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-sq-503-x.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq503x.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq503x(2).jpg"}},"luxman-sq-505-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1971 at ¥69,500. The latest theory and methods were developed. The power amplifier part adopts the full-stage direct connection circuit which eliminates the output capac by the 2 power supply method. The front stage circuit of two differential a circuitification circuits. tone control uses a friction-type double volume control, and if you turn it normally, you can adjust it separately. The curved point frequency can be adjusted three points for both high and low. Low booster with low/high filter and attenuator.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ 505 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq505x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-sq-505-x.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq505x.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq505x.jpg"}},"luxman-sq-507-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1971 at ¥86,500. SQ505X The power amplifier part adopts a full-stage direct connection circuit that removes the output capac by ±2 power supply. In addition, there is an Emitter folore circuit behind this stage, and the input impedance of the Aux terminal is kept high. The input impedance of the Phono1 terminal can be switched three phases. Aux terminal has a level set.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ 507 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq507x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-sq-700-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥45,000. Equipped with an audible circuit design and customizable design. The electrolytic capac is eliminated from the interstage coupling capac. The power amplifier amplifier circuit is equipped with two power supply and one-stage direct connection circuit. The PNP-type and NPN-type power trans are used in the output stage to eliminate crossover distortion. It is equipped with an attenuator to lower the gain to about 1/8. tone control has LUX type negative feedback (NF) type. The tone adjustment knob of the left and right channels is independent, and the click stopper is attached so that you can see the large body's lift and umulation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ 700 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq700x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-sq-700-x.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq700x.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq700x.jpg"}},"micro-seiki-mr-411":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki MR-411 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-411-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-41-a":{"more":[{"t":"Belt drive player with excellent accuracy as a finished product player. A hysteresis synchronous motor is used for the motor, providing a structure that is resistant to voltage and load fluctuations. It also uses a belt drive system with a polyurethane belt. There was also a player unit PU-41A with only mechanism without cabinet.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-41 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-41a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-41-a.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-41a-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-41a.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-41-d":{"more":[{"t":"This record player uses a belt drive system with an 8-pole hysteresis synchronous motor. An 8-pole hysteresis synchronous motor is used for the motor. The rotation speed is reduced to 1/2 by changing from 4-pole to 8-pole, and uneven rotation is reduced by reducing the rotation ratio. The diameter of the motor pulley is also twice as thick, and rotational speed accuracy of ± 0.3% or less is achieved. The motor and board are connected using a special double structure suspension made of synthetic rubber and spring. The rubber belt used in the belt drive system is made of polyurethane. This belt has a unique scuff processing that reduces thickness unevenness to less than 5/1000mm to improve characteristics. The turntable uses aluminum alloy 31 cm diameter with thick outer circumference. The bearing has been honed, and the shaft has been precisely polished with materials with excellent wear resistance to achieve excellent inertial efficiency.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-41 D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-41d-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-1000x":{"more":[{"t":"This great little entry level receiver is the Sansui 1000x. Introduced in 1970 it is a well built and great looking receiver. Here’s what Sansui had to say about it: With an unprecedented 100 watts power, the latest FET components, functional front panel design and an ability to handle two speaker systems, the 1000X considerably advances the art of stereophonic reproduction. It puts out 28 watts per channel into 8 ohms and 35 into 4 ohms. It has a great FM tuner overall excellent build quality and is very simple to operate. Aesthetically it is a great looking receiver. It has a nice well built wood case, black dial face with green back lighting and nice front panel layout. The toggle switches are crisp and well sized. Another interesting feature is that the bass and treble can be controlled for each channel independently.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 1000X","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-1000x","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-350-a":{"more":[{"t":"The Sansui 350A was a budget receiver introduced by Sansui in 1970. It is all solid state and produces just 20 watts per channel. It was offered at a retail price of just $199.95. Given its price point it was designed to do the basics well but with minimal features. The Sansui 350A stereo receiver embodies much of the aesthetic and tactile qualities of Sansui’s more expensive models. The two tone front with smoked acrylic dial panel and silver control panel give it a sophisticated look. The broad tuning dial occupies the center of the front panel, with ample spacing between FM frequencies for clarity. A signal strength meter sits to the left of the dial, and the tuning knob rests on the right. Below are an array of controls and inputs, including the power switch, headphone jack, speaker selector (main or main plus remote), bass, treble, volume, and balance knobs, and switches for loudness/volume, stereo/mono, tape monitoring, and multiplex noise filtering.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 350 A","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-350a","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-666":{"more":[{"t":"Released May 1970 at ¥52,800. This integrated amplifier was created not only with sound quality, function and expandability, but also with a design that is full of functional beauty and is closely related to the speaker system. The main amplifier section uses a 2-stage differential-amplifier circuit and PNP and NPN for the output-transistor. It is a perfect direct connection positive and negative power supplies without an output-capacitor. It is a complete complimentary service Darlington circuit system. For this reason, uniform negative feedback (NF) is applied from the DC range to the entire audio range, the damping factor and output characteristics are constant up to the ultra-low frequency range, the speaker's exposure in the ultra-low frequency range is sharply reduced, and the intermodulation distortion in the amplifier and speaker is reduced. Since the distortion component is canceled by the combination of PNP and NPN, the distortion of the amplifier itself is kept low. A specially selected low-noise silicon transistor is used in the preamp section to minimize the noise. In order to avoid using an electrolytic capacitor with poor transmission characteristics due to large phase distortion for the coupling capacitor, we use a direct-coupled circuit as much as possible, make the capacitor higher, and use a Mylar capacitor. In addition, a Mylar type is used in parallel in areas where electrolysis is absolutely necessary to improve high-frequency characteristics.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-666 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-666-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-999":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1970 at ¥85,000. This is an integrated amplifier that is the highest grade model of Sansui's PB series and an upgraded version of AU 777 d. Aiming for more faithful sound reproduction, it was developed by accumulating thorough hearing tests. The main amplifier section uses a 2-stage differential amplifier circuit and a fully connected system with two power supplies (plus and minus) without an output capacitor. This makes NFB uniform from the ultra-high band to the ultra-low band and improves various characteristics. The equalizer stage uses a 3-stage E-E negative feedback (NF) type PNP silicon transistor with low noise, and achieves low noise, low distortion, wide dynamic range and high stability. A direct-coupled circuit is used as much as possible for the amplifier circuit, and a Mylar capacitor is used as much as possible for the necessary part of the coupling capacitor. Electrolytic capacitors with large phase distortion in the high frequency range and poor transmission characteristics are eliminated. The tone control part uses SANSUI's original triple tone control, and not only Bass and Treble but also Midrange can be adjusted. It uses a tone selector that switches between two frequencies for both the defeat point and the rising / falling point, and a click-step method with 2 db steps for low and high tones and 1 db steps for middle tones for precise adjustment.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-999 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-999-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-eight":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Sansui Eight which is part of the Sansui single digit series. The series consisted of the Six, Seven, Eight and Eight Deluxe. Most likely the Eight was the first to hit the market in the early to mid 70’s ollowed shortly thereafter by the other models. The Sansui Eight featured 60 watts per channel in to 8 ohms. Another nice feature was the relay operated speaker protection circuit which protected speakers from abnormal output levels and mutes output when powering on or off. It has a 4 gang FM tuner and a 3 gang AM tuner. The Sansui single digit series was very well built and had fantastic switching capabilities. It measures 17.5 x 6 x 13 and weighs in at around 36 pounds. These receivers sell for $500.00-$950.00 depending upon condition and functionality.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui Eight","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-eight","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-seven":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo receiver made by SANSUI with the aim of becoming a famous sound device by gathering all of its technologies. In the main amplifier section, all stages are directly connected OCL pure complimentary service and a constant current drive system is adopted to prevent degradation of distortion characteristics at high and low outputs. As a result, it is possible to achieve high-quality sound quality from deep bass to high pitch with little distortion, regardless of whether the sound is large or small. The equalizer circuit of the preamp section uses an negative feedback (NF) type with three stages of carefully selected low-noise transistors directly connected to each other to obtain excellent transient response and RIAA deviation. In addition, the tone circuit is rotary switch type and can freely adjust low, middle and high frequencies with SANSUI's unique triple tone control. The tuner and preamplifier are equipped with a stabilizing power supply that stabilizes the voltage, and the main amplifier is equipped with a constant current drive system and a two stage differential amplifier circuit that is stable against power and load fluctuations. To protect the transistors and speakers, a newly designed relay circuit and four short-cut fuses are installed to ensure safety. Equipped with a 4-channel adapter terminal that allows you to enjoy 4-channel stereo. If you don't use this feature, you can connect a tape deck to record, play, and reprint your tapes.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui Seven (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/seven-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-six":{"more":[{"t":"This high-end stereo receiver is equipped with an amplifier and tuner section that is close to the field of high-end machines with Sansui's technology. The main amplifier section uses a fully connected OCL pure complimentary service and a constant current drive system to prevent degradation of distortion characteristics at large and small outputs. As a result, high-quality sound with little distortion is achieved in both large and small sounds. The preamp section uses an negative feedback (NF) type equalizer circuit with three stages of carefully selected low-noise transistors, and a rotary switch is used for the tone circuit. The tuner and preamplifier use a stabilizing power supply to stabilize the voltage, and the main amplifier uses a constant current drive system and a two stage differential amplifier circuit that is stable against power supply and load fluctuations. To protect the transistors and speakers, a newly designed relay circuit and four short-cut fuses are installed to ensure safety. Equipped with a 4-channel adapter terminal that allows you to enjoy 4-channel stereo. If you don't use this feature, you can connect a tape deck to record, play, and reprint your tapes. You can connect a noise reduction adapter that reduces the noise unique to tape and allows for comfortable recording and playback.","s":"audio-database.com"},{"t":"The Sansui Six Am/FM stereo receiver was produced from 1972 to around 1974. It retailed for $399.99. It was the smallest of Sansui’s single digit receivers and produced 34 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It also produced a very impressive 0.3% harmonic distortion. The Sansui Seven, Eight and Eight Deluxe had more power and more features than the Six but the Six is a very well built receiver with plenty of power for a small room. It has an attractive wood case and aluminum face plate. The 4-gang FM tuner is very good. One drawback to the Sansui Six receiver are the labels on the buttons. The glue holding them on tends to dry out over the years and they fall off.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui Six (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/six-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui Six","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-six","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sanyo-dca-1400":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥33,800. amplifier amplifier The circuit configuration includes the OCL circuit. In addition, the differential a circuitification circuit is used in the first stage of the power amplifier amplifier. The equalizer circuit has a large dynamic range by using low noise trans 2SC693 with high operating voltage. By attaching a circuit using a diode to the power amplifier part, the shock sound is eliminated when the switch is turned on.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo DCA-1400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dca-1400.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sherwood-s-7100-a":{"more":[{"t":"This is one of Sherwood’s upper end models the Sherwood S-7100. The Sherwood company was founded in 1953 by Ed Miller and John snow. Their primary products were amplifiers, tuners and receivers though they also had a speaker line. In 1961 Sherwood participated in the world’s first stereo radio broadcast which utilized Sherwood equipment. The S-7100 is one of Sherwood’s later solid state models though it is said to have a warm tube like sound to it. The S-7100 puts out roughly 18 watts per channel though I have seen other specs show anywhere from 14 to 22 watts per channel. Sherwood was known for their exceptional FM tuners and the S-7100 is no exception. The Sherwood company produced the first completely solid state receiver in 1967 so they were at the forefront of the new technology of the time. While most of their line was originally manufactured in the U.S. they moved production to Korea in 1978.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sherwood S-7100 A","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sherwood-s-7100-and-s-7100a","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sherwood-s-7200":{"more":[{"t":"One company that flies a little under the radar yet is still pretty popular with a subset of collectors and enthusiasts is Sherwood. Sherwood was formed in 1953 in Chicago by the engineer Ed Miller and partner John Snow. Miller had designed an amplifier and wanted to design and build equipment under the Sherwood name. This particular stereo is the Sherwood S-7200. The S-7200 was not their top of the line receiver, more middle of the pack, but still performed very well. It was made from 1973 up until about 1976 and retailed at about $360.00 when introduced. Sherwood even took pride in the fact that they were smaller than the other dominant companies in the audio field. Basically they felt that other manufacturers marketed to the mass consumer market while their equipment was targeted toward the more discriminating connoisseur. So, of course, they would sell far fewer receivers than say Pioneer or Sansui.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sherwood S-7200","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sherwood-s-7200","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-pse-4000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥85,000. The highest class armless player system installed in the cabinet on TTS-4000. Also, vibration is reduced due to ultra-low speed. Equipped with servo amplifier to realize smoother rotation. The servo circuit adopts a specially developed IC, and the frequency generator (FG), which is directly connected to both motor and turntable, always feedback the rotation status and controls to maintain the specified rotation speed. Turntable is 1.75kg with 32cm aluminum alloy casting. Because servo motor is used, speed and speed adjustment are electronic. The rubber sheet is made of ally superior material, and it is prevented from trash.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PSE-4000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/pse-4000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-3060":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1969 at ¥36,800. A new model for multi-channel applications. We design to minimize mixed modulation distortion and carefully select not only circuit technology but also trans and other parts. This enables low distortion, and the best measuring instrument available at the time, to achieve superior characteristics, such as the distortion of the measuring instrument itself. In addition, the direct coupling method has built-in filter for loudspeaker protection because it has a positive power even in ultra-low areas.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-3060 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3060.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-3060.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3060.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3060.JPG"}},"teac-as-200-s":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥89,800. 200 Series integrated amplifier with Grade Up from AS-200. By adopting a full-fledged dual power supply system differential a circuitification circuit, capac is eliminated from the output circuit, which improves the transient characteristics of low frequency. The design of the input/output circuit for the tape deck has special consideration and can be recorded on two tape decks at the same time. The preamplifier part uses carefully selected FETs with good noise phyg, which enables stable operation regardless of impedance or input. Forno amplifier has NPN-PNP-NPN new three-stage direct connection circuit. The volume control part adopts four volume control, and the volume control is doubled before and after the preamplifier containing tone control, which improves the SN ratio even in the volume. We use a muting relay to prevent the shock sound when power supply is inserted.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – TEAC AS-200 S (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TEAC-ESOTERIC/amp/as-200s.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/teac-as-200-s.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TEAC-ESOTERIC/amp/as-200s.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TEAC-ESOTERIC/amp/as-200s(2).jpg"}},"technics-sl-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥145,000. drive direct player system with SP-10 and tonearm EPA-99. SP-10 is a direct drive (direct drive) type turntable developed by Technics Technology Team. This eliminates mechanical vibrations caused by the reduction mechanism. The turntable has a weight of 2.8 kg and iner mass of 330 kg and cm2. Each item is strictly dynamically adjusted. In addition, it is possible to adjust rotation speed independently by 33, 1/3, and 45 rotations. Balance weight with direct reading.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥88,000. Record player with optical electronic cartridge. The cartridge is equipped with C-100P, a photoelectron cartridge. The equalizer for optical electronic cartridge is built-in and connected to the AUX terminal of amplifier. The turntable part adopts 30cm aluminum die-cast turntable, which is driven by belt drive method. The drive motor adopts the 6-pole outer roller motor by electronic servo control. Tonearm is equipped with static balance S-shaped pipe arm. The smart stop mechanism adopts a pure electron type, which also supports delicateness of light needle pressure. It is equipped with the optimum needle pressure display meter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-50.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"trio-kenwood-km-4002":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥22,800. KA-2600 power amplifier. All-silicon trans structure improves the characteristics of the amplifier. You can connect two loudspeaker. With the input sensitivity switch, you can directly output from the tuner or tape deck. Headphone terminal is installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Trio Kenwood KM-4002 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/km-4002.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"trio-kenwood-m-6000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥52,500. The main part of KA-6000 is extracted as it is.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Trio Kenwood M-6000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/m-6000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"trio-kenwood-ma-5100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥44,900. Multi-channel IDS stereo amplifier with four power amplifiers and crossover networks. You can build a 3-way multi amplifier system by adding it to your own amplifier. Crossover network includes negative feedback (NF) type 12dB/oct. It is equipped with a direct output terminal, and you can retrieve the input signal as it is. Headphone terminal is installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Trio Kenwood MA-5100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ma-5100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"trio-kenwood-mx-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥22,000. Multi-channel IDS amplifier integrated with stereo power amplifier and crossover network. You can add two-way multi-amp configuration by adding it to your own amplifier. Crossover network includes negative feedback (NF) type 12dB/oct. Power supply ON/OFF, loudness control, tone control Headphone terminal is installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Trio Kenwood MX-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/mx-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-2002":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1971 at ¥26,800. ATC2000 Series tone control Deft switch, etc. The pre-maining jumper circuit can be used to upgrade to a multisystem.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-2002 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-2002.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kenwood-ka-2002.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-2002.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-2002.JPG"}},"kenwood-ka-5002":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1971 at ¥65,000. The basic circuit which is common to KA-7002 is adopted. The circuit configuration includes a full line-to-line splitter. Equipped with head amplifier for low output cartridge. 4D stereo input/output terminal and control volume control. Load impedance switch for MM is installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-5002 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-5002.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-7002":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1971 at ¥86,400. KA-6000 introduces the solid-state circuit technology and adopts the pure complementary circuit. This makes it possible to a ify from the direct current, greatly improving frequency characteristics and deepen the return amount. The output impedance is flat from ultra low to high. With this, there is no worry that the direct current flows into the loudspeaker voice coil to worsen the mechanical position. This differential a circuitification circuit has high self-stableness due to the configuration that two trans s share the emitter resistance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-7002 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-7002.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-5170":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1971 at ¥105,000.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-5170 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-5170.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2215":{"more":[{"t":"This little Marantz 2215 receiver was an entry level model from Marantz in the early 1970’s. It was produced from 1971 up to 1973 at their California facility. It retailed for about $250.00 at the time. The 2215 has the classic Marantz look with a brushed metal face plate, blue dial light, gyro touch tuner and symmetrical control layout. The Marantz 2215 is rated at a very modest 15 watts per channel and came standard with a metal case covered with a simulated wood grain vinyl. The WC-22 wood case was also an option. The front panel controls include bass and treble level controls, balance and volume controls, function selection (AM, FM, phono and aux) and button switches for FM muting, loudness, tape monitor, high and low filters, stereo/mono, and speaker selection (main and remote). There is also a lighted meter for AM and FM tuning and a red indicator light for stereo. On the left of the front panel is a headphone jack.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2215","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2215","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2215.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2215","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/marantz-2215-front.jpg"}},"marantz-2245":{"more":[{"t":"This is a classic solid state Marantz 2245 receiver. It was produced from 1971 to around 1976 and put out 45 watts per channel into 8 ohms. The retail price in 1971 was around $450. It has the typical look a a mid 1970’s Marantz receiver with the brushed aluminum face plate, blue tuning dial and flywheel tuner, which they called Gyro Touch Tuning. As you can see the Marantz 2245 has a Mid tone adjustment which is nice. It also has a Low and Hi Filter along with Loudness and Muting. It really looks great in the WC-22 wood case but keep in mind that the wood case can inhibit the flow of air into the unit somewhat which can result in overheating. Still, they do look good in wood! The color of the tuning dial is usually off quite a bit from the original color because the vellum paper that is used yellows over time giving the blue more of a greenish color.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2245","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2245","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2270":{"more":[{"t":"This is the classic Marantz 2270 receiver in a beautiful wood case. Anyone familiar with vintage audio knows that Marantz built some of the best receivers of the time. And, actually, when restored, probably still stand up against the best out on the market today in terms of sound quality. The 2270 hit the market in late 1971 and retailed for between $500 and $550. It was near the top-of-the-line receiver in the Marantz lineup with the exception of the Model 19 which was still on the market at the time. It’s rated at 70 watts per channel. The blue dial lighting is an easily recognized feature of most of the 1970’s Marantz receivers. They are also known for their horizontal wheel tuner, which they called the gyro-touch tuner, as opposed to the more common tuning knob. the WC-22 wood case was optional. The Marantz 2270 has signal strength and tuning meters backlit with blue light as is the dial scale.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2270","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2270","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-sta-1101":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥118,000. High-performance receiver which greatly improves quality by IC and unitization of circuit. Equipped with FM/AM independent tuning mechanism. Enables volume control and tone control. A musical circuit that eliminates local noise.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko STA-1101 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/sta-1101.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-sta-301":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥44,800. Compact FM/AM receiver The equalizer amplifier is equipped with an audio linear IC developed by NIKKO. Mesa-type silicon trans is available in the output circuit that affects the sound quality. Equipped with loudness control. The front end of the FM tuner series adopts dual gate FET to improve performance. Stereo-mono automatic switchable FM multiplex circuit is adopted. When stereo broadcasting is received, the stereo signal indicator is automatically lit. The tuner part has a constant voltage power supply section. NIKKO developed a protective circuit to provide NW-type circuit breakers approved by UL and CSA standards.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko STA-301 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/sta-301.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-sta-6010":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥49,900. FM/AM receiver High performance FETs and ICs are used to achieve stable performance. The power amplifier is equipped with two power supply OCL method by linear drive circuit. Two output terminals are installed. Tape head input terminal is installed for transition to 4 channel system.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko STA-6010 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/sta-6010.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-trm-1200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥67,500. amplifiered in America and Europe. Sales started in Japan in 1970. NIKKO's original hybrid IC is adopted in the equalizer amplifier part, and the quality and performance is improved by the plug-in unit. NIKKO's NW-1 circuit protector is available in the protective circuit. It is equipped with a level meter of left and right independent. In addition, input display and function display are possible.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko TRM-1200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/trm-1200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-integra-234":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo receiver that integrates the integrated amplifier of the Integra 725 and the tuner Integra 433S into a base.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo Integra 234 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra234-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-integra-613":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1969 at ¥56,200. The headphones are equipped with a dynamic divider. In this method, it is a structure that controls high-cut and low-cut at crossover frequency independently, which improves the negative connection caused by individual unit characteristics and realizes more flat characteristics. The multi-step-up method enables two-way to three-way to four-way and step-up by adding a dividend amplifier. The filter circuit has an active filter circuit. The phase inverter circuit is equipped to switch phase. 701ra 701","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Onkyo Integra 613 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ONKYO/amp/integra613.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-integra-624":{"more":[{"t":"This is a device amplifier that combines a multi-channel Divider with an additional power amplifier to complete Onkyo's unique multi-step-up system. The divider section uses a dynamic dividing system to take advantage of the characteristics of speakers. This is a method of controlling the high-cut and low-cut at the crossover frequency independently, which makes it possible to make the characteristics flatter. Cascade connection is also possible by increasing the purchase of Integra 624. The power amplifier section is a Integra 701 series direct-coupled differential amplifier circuit for all stages.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo Integra 624 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra624-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-integra-725":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier that uses all stages of direct-coupled circuits in the main amplifier section. The preamp section, especially the equalizer section, has been thoroughly analyzed to improve the equalizer allowable input.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo Integra 725 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra725-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/onkyo-integra-725.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra725-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra725(1).JPG"}},"onkyo-integra-732":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier with a full-stage direct-coupled differential amplifier circuit in the main section. Built-in MC amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo Integra 732 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra732-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-integra-733":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier that uses a pure con complimentary service all-stage direct connection circuit in the power amplifier section. It is possible to connect two systems of speaker Route 3 and tape.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo Integra 733 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra733-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-integra-931":{"more":[{"t":"This is an upgraded stereo power amplifier based on the power amplifier part of Integra 725. Distortion measures are taken for all frequencies, including those outside the audible band. It is equipped with left and right independent volume, and the input sensitivity is two step switching between 1 V and 0.5 V.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo Integra 931 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/integra931-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-2500":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-2500 is a beautiful example of a vintage receiver from the early 70’s. It was introduced in 1971 and produces 72 watts per channel. It’s a solid state unit that features AM/FM auto-tuning, an interesting center tuning capability and included a convenient wired remote control. The SX-2500 retailed for $549.95. Other Pioneer receivers on the market at the time included the SX-9000, SX-990, SX-1500TD, SX-1000TW, SX-770, and SX-440. The SX-2500 was the top-of-the-line receiver in that lineup. The SX-2500 is a relatively complex piece of equipment due to its various features. Let’s begin with the tuner section. On the left side of the dial, there are center-of-channel and signal-strength meters, which are used for tuning FM and AM stations.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-2500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-2500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rx-150":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥28,900. Stereo receiver with low cost and high performance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RX-150 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/rx-150.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-2000-x":{"more":[{"t":"This is the very highly thought of Sansui 2000X. When working properly there aren’t many receivers that sound as good as this one does within it’s price range. It was produced from around 1971 up until about 1975 and puts out about 35 watts per channel. Quite a few of these receivers were made so they aren’t exactly rare but the demand is high so they still command decent money on the auction market. A common refrain for this receiver is: Sounds bigger than it is! The features on the 2000X are fairly basic but are all you really need in a good receiver. Here are it’s basic features: One of the most commonly asked questions about the 2000x is what is the difference between it and the 2000A and 2000? Well, not a whole lot actually. The Sansui 2000 came first and the 2000A and 2000X were slightly improved versions of that model.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 2000 X","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-2000x","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-5000-x":{"more":[{"t":"Here we have the Sansui 5000x receiver. It was produced in the early 70’s and was a very popular unit. It puts out 55 watts per channel and weighs in at around 40 pounds. It features dual tuning capacitors, two phono inputs and a tunable FM IF circuit. There are a few different versions of the 5000. I believe the original Sansui 5000 was introduced in 1967 followed thereafter by the Sansui 5000a in 1969 and then the Sansui 5000x in 1971. There is a known issue with some of the 5000 series Sansui’s. The early version of the amplifier driver board tended to get hot. Very hot.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 5000 X","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-5000x","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-888":{"more":[{"t":"A newly designed stereo integrated amplifier with performance and functions similar to the AU 999. The main amplifier section is fully connected with a 2-stage differential-amplifier circuit and two positive and negative power supplies without capacitor, and adopts complimentary service Darlington circuit system. As a result, uniform NFB is applied from the DC range to the entire audio range, the damping factor and output characteristics are constant up to the ultra-low range, and the speaker's blur in the ultra-low range is reduced, reducing intermodulation distortion. The preamp section uses a PNP silicon transistor which has less noise than the NPN silicon transistor to reduce noise. We use direct-coupled circuits as much as possible, minimize capacitors, increase circuit impedance where necessary, and use a Mylar type to reduce electric field capacitors as much as possible. In addition, Mylar type capacitors are used in parallel for areas where electric field capacitors are absolutely necessary to improve high-frequency characteristics. A dedicated transistor is used for temperature compensation, a differential amplifier stabilization circuit is used for the 2-stage differential amplifier to further stabilize the differential amplifier, and a protective circuit is used with 6 quick disconnect fuses. When the power transistor is damaged, an abnormal voltage is generated and DC current does not flow to the speaker.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-888 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-888-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qr-1500":{"more":[{"t":"A 4-channel receiver equipped with Sansui QS synthesizer and decoder functions. It supports 2-channel source and 4-channel matrix source, and can be converted to 4-channel and played back. Discrete 4-channel tapes and other 4-channel sources can also be 4-channel. It is equipped with a mode switch that moves the front position of channel 4 freely backward or to the right. It is also possible to output two channels of sound simultaneously from both front and rear, or from only front or rear. A specially selected low-noise silicon transistor is used for the preamp section, an negative feedback (NF)-type tone control is used for tone control, a loudness switch and a slide-type volume control for front and rear volume control. The FM section employs a front end using a dual-gate FET and a 3-row precision varicon, and an IF stage using a 4-element ceramic filter and IC. A large ferrite bar antenna is used for the AM part.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QR-1500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qr-1500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qr-500":{"more":[{"t":"A 4-channel receiver equipped with Sansui QS synthesizer and decoder functions. The 2-2-4 method allows you to enjoy four channels of the conventional 2-channel source. You can also play 4-2-4 matrix records, 4-channel FM broadcasts, and 4-4-4 discrete 4-channel tapes. The IC developed by SANSUI is used in the synthesizer and decoder section. A slide type is used for adjusting the volume of front and rear. Semi-output ITL-OTL system is used for the complimentary service circuit. Equipped with an FM/AM tuner.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QR-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qr-500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qs-100":{"more":[{"t":"A 4-channel rear amplifier that incorporates a main amplifier for the rear in a Sansui QS synthesizer decoder. By connecting to an amplifier with a tape monitor switch, you can enjoy 4-channel playback. The function switch allows you to select the sound field effect according to your preference, as well as the recording method of the source, the number of songs and the composition. It is equipped with a phase modulation circuit, and from the rear, phase difference signals (indirect sound and reverberation components) that are transmitted in the hall changing from moment to moment are reproduced. By combining it with the sound from the front, a sound field like that of a concert hall can be reproduced. In order to obtain a natural sound field, an IC-based pure electronic circuit system is adopted. The rear amplifier uses the quasi complimentary service ITL-OTL system. It is equipped with a protective circuit using a quick disconnect fuse. The rear speaker can be arranged in two ways (2-2 system, 2-2 system in front) depending on the number of songs and composition.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QS-100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qs-100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-tac-505":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo receiver developed by inheriting the development policy of the PB series. The front-end of the FM tuner section uses an FET and an ultra-precision 3-row linear varicon to obtain high sensitivity and stability. In particular, various RF characteristics such as distortion factor and capture ratio are improved. In addition, the 4-stage IF amplifier and 3-stage limiter circuit provide a sufficient limiter effect, enabling stable FM broadcasting even in noise-prone areas and low-power areas. The tuner panel has a unique round dial that floats on the green. It also has two FM antenna terminals and a high-sensitivity ferrite bar antenna for AM. A quasi complimentary service SEPPP OTL circuit is used for the main amplifier. Low-noise silicon transistors are used in the equalizer circuit, and all-stage silicon transistors are used in the low-frequency section to improve the signal-to-noise ratio and achieve low distortion. There are two Phono inputs.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui TAC-505 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/tac-505-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-str-6045":{"more":[{"t":"The Sony STR-6045 was on the market from 1971-1974 and retailed for $237.50. It was part of Sony’s STR-60xx and STR-70xx lineup including the STR-6045, STR-6055, STR-6075, STR-7055, and STR-6200F. It produces 20 watts per channel into 8 ohms at 20Hz – 20 kHz. Despite it being at the lower end of the performance spectrum in Sony’s receiver lineup it is still a very good stereo. The STR-6045 stands out with its sleek design, carefully crafted front panel and knobs. It’s definitely eye catching. It also had an optional wood case (TAC-1) that added to the sophisticated look. However, it’s not just the aesthetics that make this receiver very good. The Sony STR-6045 boasts a double, clutched volume/balance knob to the left of the tuning scale and a tuning knob to the right, creating a visually balanced and elegant layout.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sony STR-6045","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sony-str-6045","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-1130":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥88,000. SY’s ES series is integrated. The preamplifier part uses 8 FETs in the preamplifier 10 stones, and each FET is operated at the best point. Also, this FET adopts a very low negative feedback (NF) (Noise Figure) developed specifically, and the noise is not noticeable even using a moving coil cartridge of a few mV with low output voltage. This makes it possible to perform good quality bass playback without degrading output, distortion and damping factor even in low frequency. In addition to the high filter and low filter, there is also a loudness switch that corrects the hearing at the volume. You can use preamplifier and power amplifier alone by the switch on the back. 2 sets of loudspeaker systems available. AUX3 input is installed as a jack on the front panel, making it easy to connect.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-1130 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1130.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-1140":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥59,800. The F Group’s high-end series of technologies are integrated together. The NPN-PNP type trans is used for equalizer amplifier and flat amplifier. Also, the power supply voltage of equalizer amplifier is improved by S/N. tone control uses NPB method with no sound degradation. The turnover roll-off frequency can be switched in two phases of High and Low, which can always be the best condition for the sound quality of the program source and the sound characteristics of the listening room. Center Channel Terminal","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-1140 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1140.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-2000-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1971 at ¥128,000. Preamplifier developed with Sony's many technologies. The first stage of each unit amplifier that passes through the signal is used for FET, which realizes excellent transmission characteristics. It is designed for maximum sensitivity 1.2mV and maximum tolerance input 300mV. In addition, Phono1 has built-in FET gate ground type FET head with a maximum sensitivity of 0.06mV (tolerance input 15mV) so that it can be used as low output MC cartridge. In addition, we have succeeded in obtaining a tolerance input of 1V or more so that microphone amplifier can be used in high power of professional microphone. The meter and meter amplifiers provide high accuracy to satisfy BTS standards. By using this VU meter, you can check the frequency characteristics when playing records and tapes.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-2000 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-2000f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-3120-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1969 at ¥75,000. Stereo power amplifier developed by Sony's trans development and manufacturing technology and circuit technology. We have a direct coupling method that combines all directly, not only the output coupled capac, but also the coupling capac between each stage. Because of this, power, distortion characteristics, damping factor, etc. do not decrease to ultra-low range and achieve excellent characteristics. It is equipped with a limiter switch that can be used as 25W and 50W amplifier. Two inputs can be used, and the panel can be switched. Two sets of loudspeaker switches are available. Equipped with a touch panel for input level adjustment. Built-in special circuit to protect loudspeaker when abnormal operation. There was a wooden case and mount bracket sold separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-3120 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3120f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-3120-f.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3120f.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3120f.JPG"}},"sony-ta-3130-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥59,800. Stereo power amplifier developed as the best choice for multichannel. In addition, even if an abnormal voltage occurs on the output side, it is cut and it is built-in protective circuit to protect loudspeaker. Input level control","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-3130 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3130f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-3140-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥59,800. We use carefully selected pairs of trans and multi-supplier power supply power. The use of high cut-off frequency trans s and the proper NFB circuit constants have improved frequency characteristics. Level control","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-3140 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3140f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-3200-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥80,000. ES series power amplifier that pursues ultra-low distortion rate as well as power supreme. In addition to the output coupled capac, the direct coupling method <direct coupling> is used by pairs of outstanding trans s. Protection circuit to detect output current and control output trans current. Power limiter switch with a maximum output of 1/2 or 1/4. It has two inputs and two outputs. It is equipped with a thrush for input level adjustment. A special circuit that protects loudspeaker during abnormal operation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-3200 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3200f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sa-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥89,000. 2 Power supply Stereo receiver with full-stage direct connection OCL circuit. The capac cartridge and cartridge have a built-in equalizer. You can use the preamplifier and power amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SA-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sa-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-700":{"more":[{"t":"Auto-touch switch is used for the tuning process, and AFC is automatically turned off when touching the tuning process. Music circuit The amplifier is equipped with an OCL amplifier that is directly connected to the amplifier. Equipped with loudness switch and high-low filter. Equipped with preamplifier and power amplifier switch. Microphone mixing circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CR-700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-700.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-700.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-700.JPG"}},"bang-olufsen-beogram-1202":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥89,000. A full-automatic record player who can freely select record size and speed with one control. tonearm has a full automatic type. This arm has a built-in automatic adjustment device that does not slide horizontally, and it works up and down automatically when auto operation. SP14 with MMC (MMing Micro Cross) The cabinet is separated by arm fixing and chas, and the design to float with turntable reduces the needle jump by vibration. Record size is 30cm, 25cm and 17cm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Bang & Olufsen Beogram 1202 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram1202.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/bang-olufsen-beogram-1202.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram1202.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/amp/beomaster3000-2(1).jpg"}},"bang-olufsen-beogram-4000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥215,000. Record player with linear tracking method. The turntable drive uses a belt drive method, and the drive motor uses an electronic control DC motor. The tonearm section adopts a linear tracking method, and tonearm always works by sliding the horizontally to the center of the board. The cartridge contains SP15.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Bang & Olufsen Beogram 4000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram4000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"bang-olufsen-beomaster-4000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥215,000. Stereo receiver tuner with FM tuner features such as ambiophonic.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Bang & Olufsen Beomaster 4000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/amp/beomaster4000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"bang-olufsen-beomaster-901":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥140,000. receiver with FM/AM tuner.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Bang & Olufsen Beomaster 901 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/amp/beomaster901.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-3500":{"more":[{"t":"An armless player system combining the turntable DP 3000 with a dedicated cabinet. The drive unit is equipped with DP 3000, a direct drive type turntable. A solid rotor type AC2-phase torque motor is used for the motor, and a frequency detection servo control by a magnetic recording / reproducing system is installed as a servo mechanism to achieve stable rotation. Up to 14-type arm can be attached to the pickup arm. Equipped with a removable arm board. The dust cover is finger mounted and removable. Equipped with an insulator.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-3500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-3500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"fisher-180":{"more":[{"t":"This Fisher 1800 FM – AM Multiplex Receiver is fairly rare. It is basically the same as the Fisher 800C but with slightly different cosmetics. The front panel is two toned as opposed to the single color 800C panel. During the late 60’s the first solid state gear started hitting the market and the tube gear was becoming more difficult to sell. So, the marketing brains at Fisher decided to spiff up the remaining 800C’s by changing the faceplate and model number. In short, the 1800 is basically an 800C with a half black faceplate. Unfortunately for Fisher they didn’t actually sell very many of the 1800 receivers so that is why they are so rare these days. There are even rumors that the 500C was remodeled as well into a 1500. But, I have not seen one so I’m not sure it’s true.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Fisher 180","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/fisher-1800","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"fisher-801":{"more":[{"t":"The Fisher 801 receiver was introduced in 1972 and is a four channel receiver. It retailed for $749.95 which was a fairly large sum of money at the time. It was the top-of-the-line quad receiver in Fisher’s lineup which included the 601, 701, and the 801. The 801 is an improved version of the earlier 701 which came out in 1971. In 1973 Fisher introduced the X04 series which included the 304, 404 and 504, but the 801 was still on the market at that time so there were advertisements with both the 801 and x04 series receivers in them. The Fisher 801’s FM receiver has a few notable features. One is the inclusion of a stereo beacon, which aids in the tuning process and serves as a signal strength meter for both AM and FM frequencies. The beacon also functions as a frequency indicator for the ‘autoscan’ feature (more on that later), simplifying the station-seeking process The front panel of the Fisher 801 receiver is laid out nicely given the amount of functionality required for a 4-channel receiver. It hosts a variety of controls, enabling users to tailor their audio settings.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Fisher 801","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/fisher-801","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-630":{"more":[{"t":"The Harman-Kardon 630 was produced for HK by Roland and was introduced in 1973. It produces 30 watts per channel and retailed for $359.95. The vintage Harman-Kardon look is unmistakable with the green dial face contrasting against the dark black top panel and the bright red power button. The fully illuminated dial pointer is also a recognizable feature of the x30 series of receivers. The Harmon Kardon knobs are somewhat unique as well. They are manufactured with gold anodized aluminum and have sharp ridges running the length of the knobs. In 1973, HK offered both the 630 and the top-of-the-line 930 (45 wpc and a retail price of $479.95). In 1976 they added the 430 and 730 which were built by Shin Shirasuna. The 630 was essentially replaced in the line-up by the 730.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Harman Kardon 630","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/harman-kardon-630","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"heathkit-ar-1500":{"more":[{"t":"The Heathkit AR-1500 was unveiled circa 1972 as Heath’s flagship model following the renowned AR-15. It was offered in two options: a kit version and a pre-assembled version, with the kit priced at $379.95 and an additional $24.95 for the walnut cabinet. Fully assembled and with a walnut cabinet it retailed for $649.95 (ARW-1500). The introduction of the AR-1500 had a significant impact in the market. It provided a reliable and relatively powerful receiver with an exceptional tuner, all at a reasonable cost when purchased as a kit. Stereo Review magazine said it was easily worth twice the cost. Some feel that the AR-1500 is unappealing aesthetically. This may be because of the long row of black function buttons under the dial face which gives it a table radio look. But, the optional walnut case (with elegant slotted vents on the top) combines nicely with the champagne color of the left side faceplate.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Heathkit AR-1500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/heathkit-ar-1500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/heathkit-ar-1500.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/heathkit-ar-1500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/heathkit-ar-1500-knobs.jpg"}},"hitachi-ia-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier with constant current drive system. The driver stage of the main amplifier is driven by constant current (high-impedance drive) to completely eliminate crossover distortion and distortion caused by Oire force. By adopting a constant-current drive system with excellent low-distortion characteristics instead of a direct-coupled system, an excellent linear drive is achieved. In addition, an electronic protection circuit is mounted to provide a safe circuit design. Uses carefully selected silicon transistors for Hi-Fi. The equalizer uses a high-gain, low-noise hybrid IC (FA-6001T) to achieve uniform characteristics and a wide dynamic range. The tone control uses a switch-over type BAX tone circuit. Equipped with center channel output terminal, it can be developed into center woofer system. Built-in amplifier for microphone allows mixing with other program sources.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi IA-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/ia-1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-4004":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥49,800. ±2 power supply system enables full-stage direct connection + net complementary circuit. The trans of metal can seal is added to the first stage circuit or equalizer circuit of the integrated amplifier. Various switches such as tone control and filter are directly connected to the block board to eliminate extra lead wires. This improves induction ham and SN ratio. Equipped with high/low filter, muting and toned foot switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-4004 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-4004.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-6004":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥69,800. ±2 power supply system enables full-stage direct connection + net complementary circuit. The trans of metal can seal is added to the first stage circuit or equalizer circuit of the integrated amplifier. Various switches such as tone control and filter are directly connected to the block board to eliminate extra lead wires. This improves induction ham and SN ratio. Equipped with high/low filter, muting and toned foot switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-6004 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-6004.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-2022":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥22,000. Record player with auto function such as auto return.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-2022 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-2022.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-3021":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥29,900. Tonearm has a static balance type S-shaped pipe arm. It is equipped with a lateral balance adjustment weight, it is a plug-in method of EIA standard for the shell, and it corresponds to the commercial shell. The shock noise is pressed by the muting switch when release to the needle tip or the record board. In addition, it is equipped with a slide-type repeat switch, which enables automatic repeating. When the above mechanism is working, it is equipped with a safety mechanism so that force cannot be applied to the mechanism even if the hand is given.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-3021 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-3021.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-4021":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥38,000. Record player with double drive system by belt idler. The cartridge has a MM type.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-4021 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-4021.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-5021":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥46,800. Belt idler double drive player with VM type cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-5021 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-5021.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-3200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥49,900. The tuner tun multi-section has a double-switch demodulator. The integrated amplifier is equipped with a sound quality adjustment mechanism such as a click type tone control of ±10 steps. MIC terminals are also available for microphone mixing. The loudspeaker terminal is equipped with two lines, and can be used independently of A and B, and can be used in A+B positions.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"The Kenwood KR-3200 receiver was manufactured from around 1972 to 1974 and retailed for a price of $229.95. It was near the lower end of the Kenwood receiver line up at the time and produced a very modest 13.5 watts per channel. Only the KR-2200 was less powerful with 8 wpc. Even though it was a budget receiver it is very well built and has all the basic features you’d need. Kenwood was known for building receivers at that time. They would usually outperform their rated specs. The KR-3200 is also a nice looking receiver with the bottom half of the front panel in brushed aluminum and the top half black with a green backlit dial face and tuning meter. With the wood case it has an appealing vintage look to it. The front panel of the KR-3200 has all the basic controls an entry level receiver should have.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-3200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-3200.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-3200","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-3200","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-4200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥59,900. The tuner tun multi-section has a double-switch demodulator. The front end uses circuit elements such as high-performance FET, three-wire varicon, and two-wire mechanical filter and high-gain IC. Also, it is equipped with a FM muting, and you can cut the noise between stations. When one of the detecting circuits works, the discharge circuit is turned on, and the shrink circuit is operated, and the relay circuit is driven, and the output end is separated from the amplifier circuit, and the loudspeaker is protected.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-4200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-4200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"leak-2000":{"more":[{"t":"The highest quality receiver from Reek. The complimentary service stage of the power amplifier consists of a pure output-type OCL, and the A-class driver stage uses a constant current circuit, making it resistant to load fluctuations. A differential amplifier is used at the input stage of the preamplifier to ensure a high S/N and a precise equalizer curve, and a PLL decoder is used in the MPX demodulator of the FM to ensure stable separation.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Leak 2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LEAK/amp/2000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2010":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2010 receiver was introduced in 1972 at a retail price of $199.95. It’s known as a ‘Baby Marantz’ due to its more compact design and lower power output of just 10 watts per channel. The 2010 was the lowest priced of the Marantz models at the time and was designed for the budget minded buyer. Even so, it was one of the best receivers in its price range at the time. And, though it has minimal features, it includes everything you’d need for a basic stereo system setup. The 2010 also has the iconic vintage Marantz look with brushed metal face plate, blue on black dial face and gyro touch tuning wheel. Overall it’s a great looking stereo. The Marantz 2010’s tuning section has a black background which contrasts nicely with the gold-colored main panel. Light-colored control knobs and buttons also stand out.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2010","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2010","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2230":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced in 1972 this Marantz 2230 receiver retailed for $349.95. It has all the classic Marantz attributes such as the brushed silver face plate, blue and red lights and gyro-touch tuner. The 2230 was a nice entry level model from Marantz and it put out 30 watts per channel. Production of the 2230 ended in 1974. As you can see the Marantz 2230 has all the basic features a receiver needs including a mid range tone control which many other lower end units did not have. Here is what the Marantz catalog had to say about the 2230… Best in its class. With impressive specifications and Marantz-exclusive features, the Model 2230 offers more value and performance than any other receiver in its class. We’ve known that for years. But just recently, one of the nation’s most respected independent consumer testing organizations verified it.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2230","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2230","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2230.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2230","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/06/marantz-2230-front.jpg"}},"micro-seiki-mr-211":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki MR-211 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-211-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-mr-611":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki MR-611 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-611-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/micro-seiki-mr-611.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-611-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-611(1).jpg"}},"micro-seiki-mr-711":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki MR-711 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-711-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/micro-seiki-mr-711.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-711-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-711(1).JPG"}},"philips-rh-521":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥116,000. Equipped to meet the HiFi specification 45500 of the German Industrial Standard (DIN). The power amplifier part is designed with a lot of bias current, which reduces notching and crossover distortion even in small signals. With the loudspeaker matrix circuit, 4 channels can be played.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Philips RH 521 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PHILIPS/amp/rh521.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-61":{"more":[{"t":"A belt drive player that achieves more precise rotation with a brushless DC servo hole motor equipped with a rotational speed control device. The motor is a brushless motor using a Hall element developed by Pioneer. The driving magnetic field of this motor is generated by the current from the transistor circuit that works by switching the Hall element. The magnetic force change to the Hall element is sequentially and regularly performed by a pre-magnetized magnet rotor, and accurate rotation is obtained. The low-speed motor, which rotates at 10 times the speed of the turntable, reduces vibration and improves S/N and durability. In addition, since the power supply system uses a constant voltage circuit, it is not affected by fluctuations in power supply voltage. The DC servo mechanism of the motor consists of a revolution detector and a control circuit. Since a capacitor-type detector generates an AC signal by rotation, a change in the number of revolutions changes directly into a change in the oscillation signal. Since this detector is composed of a substrate attached to the rotor and stator of the motor, even a small rotational deviation changes to the oscillation frequency and controls the drive current to keep the motor rotation constant.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-61 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-61-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-qx-9900":{"more":[{"t":"This is one of Pioneer’s four channel offerings – the Pioneer QX-9900. The QX-9900 was manufactured in the mid 70’s and featured both Matrix and SQ decoding. It’s rated at 38 watts per channel into 8 ohms and 50 watts at 4 ohms in to four channels. This unit has the distinctive holes in the top of the case. While the Pioneer QX-9900 is fairly rare it’s not a hotly desired receiver. Still, in very good working condition they can sell for up to $600. Have had the pleasure of owning a few of these. If in good condition, cleaned properly and tuned up, it is a VERY beautiful looking and sounding machine. Incredible sound, very nicely organized controls and good looking face panel.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer QX-9900","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-qx-9900","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sm-3000":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo power amplifier with the highest quality specifications with an emphasis on delicate expressions. All stages are connected directly to the 3-stage Darlington pure complimentary service OCL circuit. For the output stage, triple diffused silicon NPN and PNP power transistors with collector loss of 100W and matching characteristics and breakdown characteristics are used in parallel. In addition, a two stage differential amplifier is used to stabilize the DC potential, and a temperature compensation circuit is also taken into consideration. The high stability of fluctuation of 0 ± 0.005 V in the range from -15 ℃ to + 55 ℃ is obtained. It is equipped with a protective circuit that combines an electronic circuit with 9 transistors and 11 diodes and a power relay to protect the speakers from internal damage caused by shorting of the speaker terminals and eddy currents caused by internal accidents. This circuit automatically recovers when the problem is resolved and returns to normal condition. In addition, it has a lamp indicator that lights in conjunction with the protector so that the condition can be judged from the outside. This protector circuit also serves as a power muting to eliminate noise at the time of power-on.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SM-3000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sm-3000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-424":{"more":[{"t":"People tend to focus on the big, powerful receivers when looking at vintage stereos, but, there are some little guys out there that are very appealing as well. Not everyone has the space or desire for a 50+ pound monster in their house. Some just want a well performing, small, affordable stereo. Well, the Pioneer SX-424 is just that. Pioneer introduced it in the early 1970’s – probably sometime around late 1971. It retailed at that time for about $200 which was very affordable. By 1974 the price had dropped to about $130. The SX-424 does not pump out a boatload of power. But, the 12 watts it does put out are solid and will drive most speakers.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-424","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-424","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-525":{"more":[{"t":"In 1972 Pioneer introduced the SX-525 and continued production up until around 1974. The SX-525 is a low to medium powered receiver designed for those on a budget. Pioneer’s advertising language at the time stated: Stereo on a budget can have a lot of the power and a lot of the frills of very expensive stereo, as this superlative new AM/FM receiver from Pioneer so amply proves. The Pioneer SX-525 retailed for about $240.00 and featured the silver face plate and black dial face styling early 70’s Pioneer receivers. The blue backlit dial and signal meter, as well as the red dial indicator, make this a very appealing receiver in the dark. It is a relatively modest power producer putting out 17 watts per channel. Still, this is plenty for most users. It features a sensitive FM tuning section along with an FM muting switch. Inside is all solid state and the circuitry incorporates FET transistors.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-525","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-525","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-626":{"more":[{"t":"This Pioneer SX-626 is a great looking receiver and was the mid-range offering from Pioneer around 1971. It was out of production by 1973. While it is considered mid level it really is built with the same quality as Pioneer’s upper end stereos. It just has fewer features and less power output. It retailed for around $339 and produced 27 watts per channel into 8 ohms. The SX-626 has the usually look of early 70’s Pioneer’s just before they moved to the white dial face and amber lighting. As you can see it has the basic features you’d want in a receiver and nothing fancy. One interesting note is that the tuning meter light stays off until you switch to FM then the light comes on. It’s fairly small at 18″ x 14″ x 6″ and weighs in at 22 pounds.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-626","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-626","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-727":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-727 is widely considered one of the better receivers ever made by the company. With its beautiful walnut cabinet, elegant look, high build quality and versatile connectivity it is definitely a classic. Introduced in 1972 with a retail price tag of $349.95 it was a popular product for Pioneer. It can handle up to two tape decks, two turntables, three pairs of speakers and a microphone. It produces 37 watts per channel and was one step down from Pioneer’s top of the line 54 wpc SX-828. The SX-727 has Pioneer’s recognizable aesthetic of the early 1970’s. The walnut cabinet lends an air of sophistication paired with the receiver’s silver and black faceplate. When powered on, the dial area illuminates in a soft blue, joining the two signal meters and source indicator lights that sequentially light up when cycling through the input selector. Above the augmented tuning scale, a dedicated light indicates stereo FM reception.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-727","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-727","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-828":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-828 AM/FM stereo receiver was introduced in 1971 and was on the market until about 1973. It’s rated at 54 watts per channel and is basically a higher power version of Pioneer’s SX-727. While the SX-727 used push buttons for some of the controls the SX-828 utilized toggle switches. In 1972 it retailed for $429.95 but, for some reason, the price was increased to $469.95 in 1974. The Pioneer SX-828 is definitely one of the best looking receivers ever made. The blue dial face, with signal and tuning meters to the left, and the linear layout of the controls gives it a very nice balance. The linear scale dial also has two-step illumination so you can choose either a bright or dim setting. And, it looks fabulous lit up in a low light room. As you can see the SX-828 has a slightly slanted front panel which gives it a unique look.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-828","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-828","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-810":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥55,000. 2 The power supply system adopts all-stage direct connection amplifier circuit. The padded circuit is equipped with easy to record from tape recorder to other tape recorder.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-810 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-810.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rx-150a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥29,800. Stereo receiver that requires performance over a class while low cost. High sensitivity FET FM to FM front end. You can switch between two loudspeaker systems. It has tape monitor function. Built-in 4ch loudspeaker matrix.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RX-150A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/rx-150a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rx-200a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥35,800. The loudspeaker matrix method tries to ring the phase signal component of the conventional two-channel stereo from the rear loudspeaker, which expresses the direction by setting this rear circuit. The loudspeaker output terminal is equipped with two systems, and the push button on the front panel can be used to separate the terminal. You can also switch the rear panel to play 4 channels of the loudspeaker matrix.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RX-200A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/rx-200a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rx-400a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥45,800. Stereo receiver with 4ch loudspeaker matrix. The FM front end is equipped with three-layer varicon and high-sensitivity low noise FET. SEPP output circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RX-400A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/rx-400a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-555-a":{"more":[{"t":"The PB series integrated amplifier has been upgraded from the AU 555, and the contents and design have been renewed. All stages are composed of silicon transistors. Uses the SEPP, ITL and OTL systems of pure complimentary service and Darlington circuits that use silicon transistors as power transistors. In order to avoid adverse effects of electrolytic capacitors on music signals, we use as many direct coupled circuits as possible, reduce the number of capacitors, increase the circuit impedance where necessary, and use Mylar capacitors. Where electrolysis is absolutely necessary, a Mylar capacitor is connected in parallel to improve high-frequency characteristics. Bass, Midrange, and Treble Triple Tone Control. In addition, since it is a click step type control, more accurate compensation of program and room acoustic can be performed. The preamp section uses specially selected low-noise silicon transistors to reduce the noise. The entire amplifier circuit from the first stage to the final output stage is composed of negative feedback (NF) amplifier, and frequency characteristics, distortion and S/N are improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-555 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-555a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qrx-3000":{"more":[{"t":"A 4-channel receiver with built-in newly developed QS Barrio matrix circuit that supports all 4-channel systems. The QS QS Barrio matrix circuit is incorporated in the QS synthesizer / decoder section. The QS Barrio matrix circuit is composed of square matrices and phase shifters, etc., and emphasizes natural sound field generation while improving separation and sound quality. In the newly developed QS Barrio matrix circuit, the matrix coefficient of the input signal is changed instantaneously to control the source so that the directivity becomes clearer, and the separation is improved. Theoretically, the QS Barrio matrix circuit can achieve infinite separation between each channel by selecting the control level of the matrix coefficient. However, from the viewpoint of music playback, it is adjusted to the optimum level of audibility. This control uses a phase discriminator that detects the phase of the input signal. A 2-stage direct negative feedback (NF) circuit is used for the equalizer amplifier in the amplifier section. The tuner section uses a dual-gate MOS type FET and a precision 3-row varicon.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QRX-3000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qrx-3000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qrx-3500":{"more":[{"t":"A top-of-the-line 4-channel receiver with built-in newly developed QS Barrio matrix circuit that supports all 4-channel systems. The QS Synthesizer / Decoder section incorporates a newly developed QS Barrio matrix circuit in addition to synthesizer / decoder functions, phase shifters and phase matrix functions. The 90 ° phase shifter is designed to solve the problem of the conventional matrix circuit in which the phases of the two rear speakers were reversed. On the decoder side, the phases of the left rear speakers are shifted by -90 °, and the phases of the right rear speakers are shifted by + 90 °. The phases between the rear speakers are On the encoder side, the reverse operation is performed. The newly developed QS Barrio matrix circuit is an application of an acoustic phenomenon called directional masking. By instantaneously changing the matrix coefficient of the input signal, the reproduced signal is controlled so that the directivity becomes clear, and the separation is improved. Theoretically, the QS Barrio matrix circuit can obtain infinite separation between each channel by selecting the control level of the matrix coefficient, but from the viewpoint of music reproduction, it is adjusted to the optimum level for audibility. This circuit is controlled by using a phase discriminator that detects the phase of the input signal.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QRX-3500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qrx-3500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qrx-5500":{"more":[{"t":"This Sansui QRX-550 is one of Sansui’s Quadrophonic offerings. It puts out 30 per channel to four channels into 8ohms. It is part of the early beginnings of surround sound. I believe Sansui had six QRX quad offerings and the QRX-5500 was the middle of the spectrum receiver. It was produced in the early 70’s. There was also a QRX-5500A version that reflected a change in the syntax of the decoding from QS to QA and SQ. It has that classic early Sansui styling that was also found on the 9090DB. The Sansui quad receivers are all fairly popular. They are difficult to find in full working condition but, when they are, they sell for reasonable prices.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui QRX-5500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-qrx-5500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-qrx-5500.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-qrx-5500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/04/sansui-qrx-5500.jpg"}},"sansui-qrx-6500":{"more":[{"t":"This Sansui QRX-6500 was one of Sansui’s early contributions to the quadraphonic genre. It was manufactured from 1973 until about 1975 and produced 33 watts per channel into 8 ohms when all four channels are driven and 37 watts per channel when each channel is driven. It retailed for $750.00 and has a very distinguished design. The gold/silver front panel fits nicely with the blackout dial window and green and amber lighting. Stick all this in a nice walnut finished solid wood cabinet and you have one very nice looking receiver. The QRX-6500 has three main features; the QS 4-channel Synthesizer and Decoder, the 4-channel, 280-watt integrated amplifier section, and the super-sensitive stereo FM/AM tuner. Basically, Sansui took what they had developed in the earlier QR-6500 and improved upon it. At the time their new QS regular matrix system with vario-matrix circuitry was the most advanced method of reproducing a sound field in 4-channel. The QS synthesizer could transform a regular 2-channel signal into a rich 4-channel output.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui QRX-6500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-qrx-6500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-qrx-6500.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-qrx-6500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/05/sansui-qrx-6500-dial.jpg"}},"sony-sqr-6650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥69,800. 4 power amplifiers for 4 channels In addition, it becomes BTL connection when two channels are played, enabling higher quality 2ch playback. 2 Power supply Differential type semi-complementary direct connection amplifier. This reduces distortion and plays a clear sound to the broadband. Built-in SQ decoder developed by CBS and Sony. In addition, the R-MTX decoder is mounted to play other matrix 4 channels called the Lespere Matrix. You can enjoy four discrete channels by connecting four-channel decks or devices for discrete records. If two channel sources are played on SQ or R-MTX positions, the channel hole tone effect is obtained. Level meter is installed for four loudspeaker terminals.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony SQR-6650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/sqr-6650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-str-7065":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥99,800. A full-fledged FM/AM stereo receiver developed under the same design concept as the ES series. The MPX stereo isolation circuit has a new MPX IC. In addition, the combination of an unadjusted MPX coil unit is also open from characteristic deterioration caused by aging and heat and moisture. The AM part adopts triple tuning IFT including high-integration IC solid state filter. In the preamplifier part, the high-pressure low-noise IC was developed specially by the semiconductor technology team for audio. The power amplifier part has a loudspeaker protection circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"Produced from 1972-1974 the Sony STR-7065 is a nice looking, aesthetically well balanced, receiver. It’s Direct coupled power amp produces 60 watts per channel. It retailed for about $550.00 and was a direct competitor with Pioneer, Marantz and McIntosh. The brushed aluminum face, beveled knobs and green dial give it a sophisticated look. The sleek optional wood case is well designed too. The older Sony receivers fly under the radar these days and are underrated by most enthusiasts. The performance of the STR-7065 compares favorably with all the other top end receivers of its era. Inputs for phono and aux2 Tape outputsSeperate tone controls for each channelHigh and low filtersLoudness compensationPreamp and power amp inputHeadphone jackOptional wooden cabinet.Outputs for 3 sets of speakers","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony STR-7065 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/str-7065.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sony STR-7065","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sony-str-7065","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-110":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥62,000. SL-1100 tonearm component armless player system. With this motor, the turntable of the iner mass 320kg and cm2 reached the normal speed at 1/2 rotation, and the quick start is also possible. The turntable is made of aluminum die-casting with a diameter of 35cm and weight of 2.0kg. The motor and turntable are made of aluminum die-cast and the total weight is 13.5kg. The arm base is not threaded, so it can be detachable. The output terminal is pin jack type. Dust cover is included.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-110 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-110.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥72,000. High-end player system with direct drive motor. With this motor, the turntable of the iner mass 320kg and cm2 reached the normal speed at 1/2 rotation, and the quick start is also possible. The turntable is made of aluminum die-casting with a diameter of 35cm and weight of 2.0kg. The motor and turntable are made of aluminum die-cast and the total weight is 13.5kg. tonearm is developed for SL-1100. The balance adjustment is a rack pinion type, and if the balance is pulled, the scale will return to 0, and the scale from the point to the desired needle pressure can be read directly. In-side force punching can be done by turning the upper anti-scaling force control knob according to the needle pressure. The arm base is not threaded, so it can be detachable.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-120":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥56,800. Armless record player announced as SL-1200 armless version. Two types of arm panels are attached to your favorite short arm. Also, the same thing as the attached arm panel was released as a separate selling option. In the drive part, the electronic control ultra-low-speed DC motor is adopted as the same as SL-1100, eliminating the influence of power supply voltage and frequency ctuation, and stable rotation is obtained. In addition, the turntable of 310kg and cm2 is rotated by a large start torque by 1/2 rotation, and it is possible to turntable by hand and quick start immediately. It has excellent performance by direct drive system which has no reduction mechanism such as belt and idler. Speed is electronic, and it can be fine-tuned by 10% at 33, 1/3, and 45 rpm alone. Turntable is a large table turn table with a dynamic balance adjustment diameter of 33cm and weight of 1.75kg.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-120 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-120.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥59,800. Direct drive player system developed as the original SL-1200 series which has been produced for over 30 years. In the drive part, the electronic control ultra-low-speed DC motor is adopted as the same as SL-1100, eliminating the influence of power supply voltage and frequency ctuation, and stable rotation is obtained. In addition, the turntable of 310kg and cm2 is rotated by a large start torque by 1/2 rotation, and it is possible to turntable by hand and quick start immediately. It has excellent performance by direct drive system which has no reduction mechanism such as belt and idler. Speed is electronic, and it can be fine-tuned by 10% at 33, 1/3, and 45 rpm alone. Turntable is a large table turn table with a dynamic balance adjustment diameter of 33cm and weight of 1.75kg. Tonearm is equipped with precision die-casting S-shaped pipe arm. 0One-touch rack pinion type with balance and needle pressure adjustment. The anti-scaling force control can be done by simply setting the knob according to the needle pressure.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-3400":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier developed based on Technics 50A and SU-3600. The final stage of the power amplifier employs a complete complimentary service circuit in which NPN type transistors that operate with a + signal and PNP type transistors that operate with a - signal are to drive while inverting the phases. Switching distortion that tends to be seen in conventional circuits is eliminated because of the smooth configuration that allows current to flow easily by changing the + - signal. In addition, all stages are directly connected to the OCL circuit in the power amplifier section to keep the damping factor flat and reduce the distortion factor. In order to make the most of the circuit characteristics, a differential amplifier using a pair of low-noise PNP transistors with uniform characteristics is adopted at the first stage. Moreover, the common emitter circuit of the differential amplifier is composed of a direct-coupled circuit using a constant current circuit to obtain high stability. The equalizer stage consists of three stages of PNP-NPN-PNP directly connected circuits. The first stage uses a specially selected low-noise PNP transistor to obtain a large gain and greatly improve the SN ratio. The curve change point of the tone control can be switched in two stages each for bass and treble, and the tone control can be adjusted separately for the left and right channels.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-3400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-3400-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"thorens-td-160":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥78,000. TD125mkII The unique double suspension structure absorbs motor vibration and external shock. The drive motor uses 16-pole motorhronous motor. Turntable is 3.2kg non-magnetic zinc alloy. TP16 is available for tonearm. The TP16 is a dynamically type with a horizontal and vertical balance. The needle pressure adjustment is a structure that performs in the work of the spring, and you can choose the needle pressure that is best for use cartridge using 0.5 gr step.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Thorens TD 160 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/THORENS/player/td160.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sa-304":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥73,400. 4 channel stereo receiver. Complete Complementary System is available. If you use 2 channels, you can get about 2 times output by BTL connection. Easy to balance volume control","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SA-304 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sa-304.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-80":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥71,500. A record player with a capac cartridge. amplifier-80 is equipped with a dedicated equalizer and can be connected to the Aux terminal. This cartridge has a movable pole with a cantilever. It has excellent transient characteristics and has excellent sound resolution and distortion characteristics. Tonearm is equipped with static balance S-shaped pipe arm. headshell is detachable. The arm elevation mechanism of the oil damping type protects records and needles. Low-capacity shielded wires are used for output cords, which prevents ultra-high-fr ency curves and supports 4 channel playback. The turntable part adopts 31cm aluminum die-cast turntable and is driven by belt drive method. The drive motor adopts the 16-pole motorhronous motor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-80.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-500":{"more":[{"t":"Music circuit Equipped with loudness switch. Equipped with preamplifier and power amplifier switch. Microphone mixing circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CR-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-500.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-500.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-500.JPG"}},"accuphase-c-200":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1973. This preamplifier was released as the first of the Accuphase series. The company name at that time was Kensonic. The equalizer circuit is fully push-pull driven by direct connection to all stages to improve the bare characteristics before NFB (negative feedback) is applied, making it a high fidelity amplifier circuit. To handle input signals in a wide dynamic range, an A-class drive pure complimentary service is used in the final stage of the equalizer, and a dual plus / minus power supply system ensures a high allowable input voltage. In addition, a low-enhancement circuit is used to enhance the sense of volume when listening to music. An attenuator that can be continuously adjusted by 10 dB is provided to adjust the level of the DISC1 and DISC2 cartridges when you want to lower the level of an extremely high-power cartridge to an appropriate level, or when you want to listen to a comparison of two cartridges using DISC1 and DISC2. In addition, DISC1 is equipped with an input impedance selector switch, which allows you to select between 47k Ω, 30k Ω and 20k Ω. A 25-Hz cutoff subsonic filter is also provided for disc playback. Equipped with independent left and right tone control, the turnover frequency can be switched between 200 hz, 400 hz, 2.5 khz and 5 khz for low and high tones respectively.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1973 at ¥195,000. The first power amplifier released by Accuphase in the era of Kensonic. It was developed with the aim of an amplifier that can accurately follow subtle changes in music and strong amplitudes. All stages from input to output are directly connected push-pull configuration. Therefore, the bare characteristics before applying NFB (negative feedback) are improved. Six high-output power transistors are used for each channel at the output stage, and these are called triple push-pull. Pure complimentary service direct connection system is adopted for the circuit system. The power supply uses a 40,000 μ Fx2 large-capacity filter and condenser. The parts are tested from the viewpoint of the change of sound quality and durability, and are selected carefully. We have adopted a protective circuit that uses a relay to shut down when a cord short-circuits after the output terminal, a problem occurs in the speaker, or a problem occurs inside the P-300.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-aa-5200":{"more":[{"t":"The power amplifier section consists of a SEPP-ITL-OTL system circuit directly connected to all stages, and the phono amplifier in the pre-section uses a two stage IC directly connected circuit. Two tape decks can be connected at the same time, or the pre-main can be used alone. Also equipped with bus treble control, balance control, high / low cut filter, loudness switch and muting switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AA-5200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/aa-5200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-aa-5500":{"more":[{"t":"SEPP-ITL--ITL-OTL system circuit directly connected to all stages to achieve high output with low distortion factor. An ICZ-stage direct-coupled circuit is also used for the phono amplifier. Four tape decks can be connected at the same time, and a microphone jack with level control, muting switch, bus treble control, high / low cut, and loudness switch are installed. Built-in power transistor protection circuit allows single use of pre-main and main.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AA-5500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/aa-5500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-aa-5800":{"more":[{"t":"All stages are directly connected ITL-OTL-OCL system circuit is adopted for the power amplifier section, and PNP-NPN-NPN3-stage directly connected circuit is adopted for the equalizer of the preamplifier section. In addition, a two stage IC directly connected circuit is used for the microphone amplifier. Transistor and speaker protection circuit are mounted. Four tape decks can be connected at the same time, a tape recording selector switch is installed, and mixing by microphone level control is also possible.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AA-5800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/aa-5800-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-aa-6100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥34,500. Akai’s first four-channel integrated amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Akai AA-6100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AKAI/amp/aa-6100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"akai-aa-910":{"more":[{"t":"This is an FM/AM receiver that can be used independently for pre-main and main. The FM front-end section uses an FET and a frequency linear 3-row variable capacitor to improve sensitivity and interference rejection capability. An IC and three ceramic filters are used for the IF stage, and an IC and silicon transistor are used for the MPX circuit. The power amplifier uses a SEPP circuit to improve the damping characteristics. The bus treble control can boost or cut in 2 dB steps. It also features preset volume control, loudness control, balance control and microphone jacks.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AA-910 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/aa-910-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-aa-920":{"more":[{"t":"The FM front-end section uses a high-end dual-gate MOS FET and a frequency-linear four series varicon to improve various characteristics. The IF amplifier stage uses an IC and three ceramic filters to improve selectivity and capture ratio. The AM tuner section uses a 3-row varicon and ceramic filter. An FET is used in the first stage of the preamplifier section to eliminate distortion caused by impedance deviation, and a low-noise transistor is used in the equalizer section to improve the dynamic range. The tone control uses an negative feedback (NF) type that takes advantage of the linear characteristics of the B-type variable resistor. The power amplifier section uses a SEPP-ITL-OTL-OCL direct connection circuit. In addition to two types of dubbing jacks, a microphone jack is installed. Comes with a preset volume and can be used independently for pre-main and main. Equipped with a microphone jack.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AA-920 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/aa-920-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-aa-940":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo receiver designed with plenty of room for high-end circuitry. The FM front-end part of the tuner uses a dual-gate MOS FET and a frequency-linear four series varicon to improve various characteristics. The IF amplifier stage uses three ceramic filters to improve selectivity and capture ratio. In addition, the combination of four ICs enables FM reception with low distortion and low noise. The MPX circuit is equipped with an IC-15 kHz low-pass filter and low-noise silicon transistor to obtain stable stereo effects. Equipped with FM muting circuit. The AM tuner section uses a 3-row varicon and ceramic filter. The frequency characteristics of the preamplifier are improved by using a fully connected circuit using silicon transistors. The tone control circuit is negative feedback (NF)-type and can be adjusted in 2 dB steps.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AA-940 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/aa-940-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-as-980":{"more":[{"t":"The highest quality receiver announced as 4chFM/AM total stereo amplifier. It is designed so that you can enjoy 2 ch stereo and the output is doubled when you switch from 4 ch. The SEPP-ITL-OTL circuit is used for the power amplifier. In addition, power supply stabilization circuit and power transistor protection circuit are mounted. All stages of the preamp section are directly connected, and an negative feedback (NF) tone control is built in. It also incorporates four channel decoder amplifiers for discrete and CD-4 systems, SQ and regular matrix (RM) systems. In addition to the remote control of surround balance, it is equipped with a 4-channel dubbing jack and an impedance level meter can be installed. The front end of the FM tuner section is a 2-stage RF amplifier circuit using an FET and a frequency linear 4 series variable capacitor, and excellent interference rejection capability is obtained. In addition, a ceramic filter and 4-stage direct-coupled IC are used for the IF stage, and an IC and a 15 khz low-pass filter are used for the MPX circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AS-980 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/as-980-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-1700":{"more":[{"t":"Released May 1975 at ¥58,000. Record player with DP-1000. Direct drive type turntable DP-1000 In DP-1000, the design and basic performance of DP-3000 are inherited and the appearance is compacted. DENON’s proprietary magnetic recording regeneration method is used to detect the rotation speed important by direct drive method. This method measures 1000 pulse signals on the outer circumference of the turntable rim and controls the rotation speed by detecting it using a magnetic head. The drive motor is equipped with a solid rotary type AC torque motor. The alternating motor has no cosmos omena in the DC motor, and it has a smooth rotation with minimal vibration. In addition, it is very smooth rotation by taking into account the drive waveform of motor. The speed select knob is used in conjunction with the power supply switch, and the speed change is performed by changing the standard voltage of the circuit. Newly developed universal tonearm with anti-scaling mechanism and mechanical filter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-1700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-1700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-3700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥80,000. Direct drive player system using DP-3000. DP-3000 Tonearm is equipped with DA-305, a static balance S-shaped ton arm. Oil damping arm reflector","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-3700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-3700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-500":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier developed by DENON in pursuit of musical quality by investing the experience and technology of professional equipment. The power amplifier uses a PNP-NPN pair of Darlington power transistors manufactured by Motorola Inc. of the United States. The circuit configuration consists of a PNP-NPN Darlington power transistor with excellent symmetry in electrical characteristics and an all-stage direct connection OCL circuit. This realizes low distortion. In addition, a Darlington transistor with Tj of 55 to 200 ° C and collector loss of 150W is used, heat radiation effect and stability of temperature compensation of bias circuit are taken into consideration. Thus, a safe operating area (ASO) is considered in the design and stable operation is achieved. The power supply section is equipped with a non-inductive high-ripple type chemical capacitor and a power transformer that reduces internal resistance to suppress temperature rise and takes into consideration the effects of leakage flux from the material aspect. The preamplifier section is composed of a direct-coupled circuit of a high-voltage low-noise transistor and is structured in consideration of various characteristics. In addition, the power supply unit is used as a stabilizing power supply to stabilize the operation, and an emitter-follower buffer amplifier is used at every important point.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ia-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥53,000. Equipped with constant current drive method on the driver stage. The driver stage of the power amplifier is controlled by constant current drive to reduce crossover distortion and distortion at small input. Selected Hi-Fi silicon trans. The equalizer circuit uses a hybrid IC to achieve uniform characteristics without variation. Tone control has a step variable negative feedback (NF)-type tone circuit. Microphone terminal 2 loudspeaker output Phono input sensitivity switch is installed. It is equipped with pre-main separation terminal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi IA-600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ia-600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/hitachi-ia-600.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ia-600.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ia-600.JPG"}},"kenwood-ka-3004":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥39,800. Developed with the design concept of Hi-ATC series advanced machines. The power amplifier part is equipped with a full-stage direct connection and a pure complementary circuit. Also, the equalizer unit has two-stage direct connection two power supply system. Tone control also has a tone-feet switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-3004 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-3004.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-8004":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥93,000. Solid state integrated amplifier released as the top model of the HI-ATC series. In addition, the ±2 power supply method using the first step differential method is adopted. By making the power position of the output end to 0, the deep NPB is applied, various characteristics are extended to the ultra-low range. In addition, the PNP-NPN Derlington system is used for the output stage to reduce the distortion of amplifier. This improves dynamic range and stability. A constant current drive system is adopted for the net complementary circuit, which improves various characteristics and realizes stable power supply. tone control uses NFB-compatible tone control, which releases undulating characteristics around the turnover frequency that could not be avoided.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-8004 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-8004.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-2022-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥25,000. The automatic return player is carefully selected from the stability of the rotation to the lifting and dropping of the needle, adjusting the needle pressure, and preventing howling. Arm has a total lateral balance type anti-vibration tapered pipe arm. The cartridge connection uses a plug-in method and various cartridges are available. It also has auto mechanism such as auto return and pose elevation, so it can be used without worrying about operation mistakes.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-2022 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-2022a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-3022":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥33,000. In addition to the full automatic mechanism, full automatic player adopts resonance prevention design such as tapered arm and low foam cabinet. Fully-automated mechanism enables auto lead-in, auto-cut, auto-return and auto-repeat. In addition, the shock noise when the needle tip releases on the record board is shut out by the muting switch. The original delay circuit is adopted by the electromagnetic relay method, and the arm starts working immediately after the start. In addition, the center shaft has accurate rotation by adopting the ball vanishing process by the carbide steel ball. Arm adopts oval tapered arm which prevents resonance over broadband by tapering static balance type high sensitivity pipe arm. In addition, the pivot part adopts special damper material to improve howling and SN ratio. This tonearm is designed to balancing lateral across the arm, and therefore it is possible to reduce the tonearm's efficacy because it is necessary to attach the balancer to the arm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-3022 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-3022.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-5022":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥49,800. Record player with direct-drive motor and full auto mechanism. direct-drive motor DC motor is adopted by ultra-low-speed electronic control in the heart of direct drive. If you set the rotation speed once, the servo circuit maintains the accurate rotation speed without affecting the power supply voltage ctuation. In addition, the power supply frequency does not need to replace the capstan, and the speed reduction mechanism by the belt and the idler can be used for semi-permanent performance. In addition, it is equipped with an independent tuning mechanism of 33, 1/3 and 45 rpm. The direct drive player has a turntable iner performance, but the KP-5022 has a structural mass distribution, and the iner performance is large as 200kg/cm2, and it reaches a constant speed rotation with only 1/2 rotation. The arm is designed to prevent resonance over broadband by tapering the static balance type high sensitivity pipe arm. In addition, the pivot part adopts special damper material to improve howling and SN ratio.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-5022 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-5022.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-2300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥39,900. AM/FM Stereo Receiver KR-4200 The microphone mixing circuit can be mixed with records, AUX, AM, FM, etc. It becomes MIC ONLY by pullOff the mixing volume control, and the microphone level is changed only by microphone volume control. Two loudspeaker terminals","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-2300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-2300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-5340":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥99,800. A high-end receiver with four power amplifiers and two BTLs on both sides. In addition, FM DET terminal is installed in preparation for FM discrete broadcasting which was expected to start broadcasting at that time. SQ Decoder RM circuit is built-in, and you can add two loudspeaker for the rear to create achch system. CD-4 (CD-4)","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-5340 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-5340.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-6340":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥135,000. High power receiver by connecting 4 power amplifiers and 2 BTLs on both sides. with good regulation. The tuner MPX is equipped with a double-switching demodulator, and the front end is equipped with the latest circuit elements such as FET and IF-stage ceramic filter. In addition, the long dial scale of 200mm is equipped with a frequency linear varicon. FM 4ch","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-6340 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-6340.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kenwood-kr-6340.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-6340.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-6340.JPG"}},"kenwood-kr-7340":{"more":[{"t":"Model: Kenwood KR-7340 – 4 channelType: ReceiverYear: 1973Watts Per Channel: 55 (20 per channel in 4-channel mode)","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-7340","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/kenwood/kenwood-kr-7340-receivers-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-8340":{"more":[{"t":"Model: Kenwood KR-8340Type: ReceiverYear: 1974Watts Per Channel: 60 in stereo, 25 in 4-channel","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-8340","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/kenwood/kenwood-kr-8340-receivers-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-8840":{"more":[{"t":"Model: Kenwood KR-8840Type: ReceiverYear: 1974Watts Per Channel: 40 in 4-channel mode","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-8840","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/kenwood/kenwood-kr-8840-receivers-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-9340":{"more":[{"t":"Model: Kenwood KR-9340Type: ReceiverYear: 1973Watts Per Channel: 40 in 4-channel mode","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-9340","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/kenwood/kenwood-kr-9340-receivers-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-9940":{"more":[{"t":"Model: Kenwood KR-9940Type: ReceiverYear: 1972Watts Per Channel: 50 in 4-channel mode","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-9940","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/kenwood/kenwood-kr-9940-receivers-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-308":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1973 at ¥108,000. an integrated amplifier with almost the same configuration as L- amplifier. The power amplifier part adopts the full-stage direct connection circuit which removes the output capac by the 2 power supply method. The driver stage is composed of two differential a ifications, and the circuit is designed to reduce crossover distortion. In the preamplifier part, the circuit is directly connected to the equalizer circuit. The circuit is composed of NPN (2SC1222), PNP (2SA640), and NPN (2SC1222). This circuit has a strong power supply utilization and provides excellent linearity. In addition, this circuit improves the transient characteristics by applying sufficient DC return. A linear equalizer circuit is installed in the middle amplifier part after the equalizer circuit. In this circuit, a kind of tone control circuit gives you two kinds of linear characteristics: \"lower, higher\", \"lower, higher\" and \"lower, lower\" without affecting the output for recording.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman L-308 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/l-308.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-150":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1973 at ¥146,000. A large power trans is used in the output stage. Power meter It has subsonic filter and input level set function. There are two types of white wooden boxes and rosewood wooden boxes.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-150 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m150.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-sq-700xg":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥55,000. Compact and easy integration. Equipped with an attenuator or loudspeaker switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ 700XG (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq700xg.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-sq-700xg.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq700xg.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq700xg.JPG"}},"luxman-sq-707":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1969 at ¥35,000. amplifier amplifier amplifier The power amplifier is equipped with a semi-complementary circuit. In addition, the output stage adopts the SEPP-OTL method, and the protection circuit is omitted by the original method of the LUX. These circuits have a carefully selected low noise trans. Two loudspeaker terminals -18dB attenuator The tone control is mounted on the left and right. Tape Monitor Switch The front panel is made of alumite dyeing with white gold.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ 707 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq707.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2220":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2220 was an entry level model in 1973 but was still a very good performing receiver which retailed for about $300. While officially producing 20 watts per channel many report that it is underrated. The 2220 receiver also has the classic mid 70’s Marantz styling with a silver face, gyro or fly wheel tuner, and blue dial glow. While most 2220’s have a silver faceplate there seem to be some out there that have a more gold anodized or champagne look to them. The blue dial sometimes has a more green tint to it as well. This is because the vellum paper behind the dial face has yellowed over the years. The vellum can be replaced and/or new LED lamps installed. The LED’s do tend to give it a brighter than original look though that some don’t like. The entire Marantz 22xx line is known for its warm and musical sound quality and the 2220 is no exception.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2220","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2220","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-4230":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 4230 receiver is a 4-channel quadraphonic model that was introduced in 1973 and was on the market until around 1978. It retailed for $499.95 and featured options of a wood cabinet and RC-4 remote control. While it was at the lower end of the Marantz quadraphonic line it still has a plethora of features and controls. The 4220 was the bottom end of the line at 20 watts per channel in stereo and 8 wpc in quadradial mode. Then came the 4230 at 30 wpc in stereo and 12 wpc in quad. These were followed by the 4240 (40 wpc in stereo / 17 wpc in quad) and the 4270 (75 wpc in stereo / 25 in quad). At the higher end were the 4300, at 100 wpc in stereo and 40 wpc in quad, and the top-of-the-line model 4400 which featured 125 wpc in stereo and 50 in quad. The Marantz 4230 has the classic 1970’s Marantz look though the front panel is a little crowded with controls because of all the 4-channel features. It has both signal strength and tuning meters to the left of the dial face and the iconic gyro tuning wheel to the right.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 4230","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-4230","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-4240":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 4240 is one of their Quadraphonic offerings in the 4xxx series. The Model 4240 is a high quality stereo + quadradial receiver and incorporates Marantz’s exclusive Vari-matrix circuit which simulates 4-channel sound from normal 2-channel stereo programs, and is capable or reproducing 4-channel sound from any matrix encoded source. It can also reproduce any discrete 4-channel program as well as regular stereo and monaural programs. An optional plug-in decoder adapts the 4240 for any specific matrix system such as Columbias SQ. The 4240 debuted in 1974 and was on the market until 1978. The receiver had a retail price of $599.95. It had options for an SQA1 Quad Decoder and the SQA2 Quad Decoder as well as the RC4 Remote Control. Of course you could also purchase the WC-22 wood cabinet. With the mode selector you could choose between Mono, 2 Channel, Discrete, Vari Matrix or SQ Decoder modes.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 4240","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-4240","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-4300":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 4300 Quadradial was one step down from the Marantz 4400 Quadradial. It is a 2 channel or 4 channel receiver with built in Dolby B Noise Reduction. It also has an optional plugin for and SQ decoder. In 4 channel mode it is rated at 40 watts per channel. In a 2 channel setup it is rated at 100 watts per channel. I believe it was first produced in 1972 and ended production in 1978. It listed at $899.95. The Marantz 4300 has inputs for Phono, FM, AM, 2 tapes sources, and an external discrete 4-channel source. The Mode knob can switch between Mono, 2-channel, Discrete, Vari-Matrix, and SQ Decoder modes.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 4300","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-4300","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"philips-rh-520":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥76,000. RH521 The power amplifier part is designed with a lot of bias current, which reduces notching and crossover distortion even in small signals. With the loudspeaker matrix circuit, 4 channels can be played.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Philips RH 520 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PHILIPS/amp/rh520.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-qx-949":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer QX-949 is one of Pioneer’s larger quadraphonic receivers and was top of the line when it was introduced in 1973. This was mainly due to the fact that it had essentially all the available decoding built in to it. It has a built in CD-4 demodulator as well as regular matrix and SQ matrix. So there was no need for the audio enthusiast to have to buy a separate demodulator or decoder. The QX-949 was on the market until 1976 and was part of Pioneer’s new collection of quadraphonic receivers including the QX-949, QX-747, and QX-646. Pricing for the receivers (including walnut cabinets) was as follows: Its long, elegant, three-dimensional gold and black front panel has enough controls on it to delight the most demanding knob -twirler and yet, when viewed overall, is executed without imposing a cluttered feel. The upper portion of the panel projects forward slightly, its blacked-out dial area illuminated in blue when power is applied. The QX-949 puts out a pretty decent 40 watts per channel into 4 channels and 60 watts into 2 channels (at 8 ohms). A distinguishing feature of the QX-949 is the 4-channel level indicator.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer QX-949","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-qx-949","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-qx-949.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-qx-949","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/09/pioneer-qx-949.jpg"}},"pioneer-sx-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥33,900. A stereo receiver that embodies the charm of its components in a simple form. The front-end of the FM tuner uses carefully selected FETs. The equalizer amplifier uses a 2-stage direct connection negative feedback (NF) type circuit. Equipped with a loudness contour and a mono-stereo changeover switch. Two auxiliary power outlets are installed.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SX-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sx-300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-1210":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥73,000. A fully-separated 2 power supply method ( cap, capac, independent on the left and right channels) is used for power amplifier. Since there is no output capac, you can get stable output with less distortion from low to high. PNP type trans only three-stage direct connection E-E return. power supply If the power supply voltage is not working, pop noise is generated and the pulse noise enters, the loudspeaker is damaged. In order to deal with this, there is a delay circuit, and there is also a circuit breaker in the loudspeaker circuit that puts each fuse in the power supply circuit. Since the circuit breaker is auto-return, even if it is overloaded, it will arrive for a while.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-1210 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-1210.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-211":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥21,000. Compact size and easy to use. trans Two sets of loudspeaker can be connected.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-211 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-211.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-311":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥27,500. amplifier amplifier ITL-OTL Built-in 4ch loudspeaker matrix.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-311 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-311.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-611":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥49,500. Integrated amplifier that pursues cost performance while maintaining excellent characteristics and sound quality. OCL power amplifier amplifier Power supply is mounted on equalizer and preamplifier circuit. Pre and power can be separated.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-611 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-611.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rp-1000":{"more":[{"t":"A record player that pursues high performance at low cost. A 4-pole synchronous motor is used for the drive part. An S-shaped tone arm is used for the tone arm. In addition, an oil dump type arm lifter is mounted. A high-compliance type MM cartridge is used. Equipped with auto-return and auto-cut mechanism.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Rotel RP-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ROTEL/player/rp-1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rx-450":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥44,500. A stereo receiver that introduces the technology of the router to achieve high performance. The tuner part is a 5-stage IF configuration and includes FET and ceramic filters. The audio part adopts all silicon trans SEPP output circuit. preamplifier and power amplifier can be separated and used.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RX-450 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/rx-450.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-pa-100":{"more":[{"t":"A monaural mixer amplifier that enables simultaneous mixing of a total of six circuits, one microphone Route 3, one record player and two AUX systems. Equipped with main amplifier section of 40W effective output. The pre-section and main section can be used independently. It has a built-in output matching transformer and can be used with many speakers. Built-in monitor speaker. Equipped with a VU meter. Equipped with 50k Ω and 600 Ω microphone inputs. Each input has a volume with an operating indicator.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui PA-100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/pa-100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qa-7000":{"more":[{"t":"A 4-channel integrated amplifier with a new QS synthesizer. The QS regular matrix method is adopted for the synthesizer and decoder section. This system consists of a 90 ° phase-shifter with a square matrix as the reference, and the signal is transmitted through a QS Barrio matrix at the time of playback to improve acoustic separation and musical performance. In addition, the newly developed 2-4 conversion encoder circuit can convert conventional 2-channel sources into 4-channel sources. It is equipped with a 90 degree phase shifter developed by SANSUI. In the conventional matrix method, the phase relationship between the two rear speakers is said to be opposite to each other, resulting in poor sound connection. To solve this problem, a 90-degree phase shifter shifts the phase of the decoder side by -90 degrees from the left rear and by + 90 degrees from the right rear to the positive phase. This improves the orientation of the sound image in all directions. Equipped with QS Barrio matrix circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QA-7000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qa-7000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qrx-2000":{"more":[{"t":"A 4-channel receiver with a newly developed QS Barrio matrix circuit. Equipped with QS Barrio matrix circuit developed by SANSUI. This circuit applies an acoustic-psychological phenomenon called directional masking. When strong and weak sound simultaneously reach the ear, the direction of the weak sound is masked and becomes unclear. This phenomenon is electronically incorporated into a 4-channel circuit. Compared to conventional 3-dB-type RM decoders, this method provides theoretically infinite channel separation, so the QRX2000 is set to the most desirable value for music playback. It also provides more accurate localization and better sound quality than conventional RM decoders. Equipped with a function switch that can select various 4-channel effects. If you press the QS Synthesizer switch, you can enjoy two channel records and other four channels with the new QS Synthesizer function.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QRX-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qrx-2000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-qrx-2000.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qrx-2000-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qrx-2000.jpg"}},"sansui-qs-1":{"more":[{"t":"This is a 4-channel synthesizer equipped with a unique phase modulation circuit and phase shifter based on the Sansui QS method. By adding a QS-1 and a rear power amplifier or integrated amplifier, you can play four channels. In addition to Matrix 4-channel records and FM broadcasts, you can enjoy 4-channel playback of 2-channel sources from records, tape, or FM stereo broadcast transmission, as well as discrete 4-channel source playback control. Equipped with a function switch, you can select a 4-channel sound field effect and reproduction method according to the number of songs, composition and recording method. There are two types of front and rear output circuits, Low and High, so you can choose your favorite amplifier whether it is a main amplifier or an integrated amplifier. SANSUI's original phase modulation circuit allows the dynamic range to be expanded. A specially developed IC-based quasi-electronic circuit is used to obtain a natural sound field. 4-channel recording of 2-channel source is possible with 4-channel tape deck. Left / right balance of front and rear can be independently adjusted.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QS-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/etc/qs-1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qs-10":{"more":[{"t":"A 4-channel rear amplifier consisting of a Sansui QS synthesizer / decoder section and a rear main amplifier section. You can enjoy 4-channel playback by connecting it to a tape monitor switch of your own amplifier such as a separate type, modular type or receiver. Equipped with a function switch that allows you to you to choose the effect that matches the difference in the music number and composition of the source and the difference in the recording method. The rear speaker can be arranged in two ways (2-2 system, front 2-2 system) depending on the number of songs and composition by using the switch. By switching the switch, you can enjoy the 4-channel effect by comparing 2 methods. A slide type is used for front and back volume adjustment. Equipped with a stereo main amplifier using silicon transistors. The synthesizer and decoder uses a pure electronic circuit system that employs an IC originally developed by SANSUI.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui QS-10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/qs-10-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sanyo-dca-1100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥79,800. A pure complimentary is adopted. The power amplifier part is equipped with a pure complimentary circuit. The equalizer circuit has negative feedback (NF) type. tone control circuit Variable width is ±10dB at 2dB step, and turnover frequency isasss and Treble. The protective circuit includes a relay to the electronic circuit. Two-system tape monitor circuit, tape dubbing circuit, low/high filter, etc.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo DCA-1100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dca-1100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sanyo-dca-650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥63,800. Equipped with good material to achieve superior naked characteristics. In addition, phase correction is limited to one place between pre- and main, and it is suppressed to the minimum 10pF (usually 50 to 100 pF). In addition, it is possible to release the tray capacity (floating capacity). In addition, it is equipped with a thru-lat switch mechanism to support people with poor recording sources, soft and soft sound. The power amplifier part adopts the full-stage direct connection with the differential amplifier circuit. In the circuit, there is no pathcom that is inserted into the first step differential circuit or drive stage for the purpose of increasing the gain for deep negative feedback (NF). Pascon is an alternate drop of the emitter into the earth and eliminates the local negative feedback caused by the emitter resistance. Thus, the gain is affected, but in circuit, it becomes unstable.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo DCA-650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dca-650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-str-7055":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥79,800. A full-fledged FM/AM stereo receiver developed under the same design concept as the ES series as a receiver that can be considered as a pre-main. It is equipped with a stable local oscillation circuit and FET mixer circuit. The MPX stereo isolation circuit has a new MPX IC. In addition, the combination of an unadjusted MPX coil unit is also open from characteristic deterioration caused by aging and heat and moisture. The AM part adopts triple tuning IFT including high-integration IC solid state filter. In the preamplifier part, the high-pressure low-noise IC was developed specially by the semiconductor technology team for audio.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"The Sony STR-7055 was made from 1972 until 1976. It has a clean and classic styling and looks especially good with the wood case. It was near top of the line with only the STR-7065 above it. It produces 55 watts per channel into 4 ohm loads and 35 wpc into 8 ohm loads.. The STR-7055 boasts an elegantly designed satin-finish panel and knobs. It features a highly efficient medium-power amplifier with versatile control options. The STR-7055’s front panel showcases a prominent dial cut-out surrounded by green-lit scales and a meter face. Adjacent to it are two large knobs for tuning and volume adjustment. The balance control, which is located below the volume knob, can be operated using a small lever.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony STR-7055 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/str-7055.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sony STR-7055","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sony-str-7055","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-1066":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥27,800. ES series design concept is inherited, the program source is faithfully pulled out, and the aim is not to color. In addition, the preamplifier part adopts the transizer which was developed for low noise as TA-1140 to equalizer amplifier. negative feedback (NF)-type tone control enables you to adjust sound quality according to the sound characteristics of the program source and listening room.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-1066 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1066.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-1150":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥49,800. It was developed by tilting all the power to design a circuit that does not make sound and does not color the sound. The output stage adopts a circuit push circuit using a reliable large output trans, which drives loudspeaker even with low impedance load. The preamplifier circuit adopts high-pressure low-noise IC developed by the Sony semiconductor technology team to equalizer and tone amplifier. tone control adopts NPB method with no distortion, and the turnover roll off frequency is reble in two steps. One-touch, all-push-button input selector is installed. Center Channel Terminal Two sets of loudspeaker switches are equipped.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-1150 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1150.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-1150.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1150.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1150(1).JPG"}},"technics-sa-5200":{"more":[{"t":"An FM/AM stereo receiver with a built-in matrix 4-ch circuit that connects two tape decks and a microphone. The main amplifier section uses a fully connected OCL circuit that uses a differential amplifier circuit at the first stage. The equalizer stage employs a 2-stage direct connection configuration with low-noise PNP transistors, and bias current is also stabilized by applying DC negative feedback (NF). The tone control circuit configuration uses the negative feedback (NF) circuit of the main amplifier section. The feedback amount of the negative feedback (NF) loop at the first stage of the main amplifier section is attenuated by frequency and controlled. In this method, since the signal is manipulated after amplification, the distortion generated in the tone control circuit is minimized. The front-end of the FM tuner section employs an FM3-row varicon and a 4-pole MOS FET to achieve stable high gain and high sensitivity. The IF amplifier stage consists of six stages using three differential stages, and three 2-element ceramic filters are used as selection elements to achieve 60 dB selectivity. The MPX circuit uses a monolithic IC and a sealed coil unit to eliminate the influence of temperature and humidity.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SA-5200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/sa-5200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-5500":{"more":[{"t":"An FM/AM stereo receiver that combines an FM/AM tuner and integrated amplifier. The power amplifier section uses an all-stage direct-coupled differential amplifier OCL circuit without the output capacitor, which causes the degradation of low-frequency characteristics. As a result, a smooth frequency characteristic is obtained from the ultra-low band to the ultra-high band, and the damping factor in the ultra-low band is kept flat. The equalizer circuit of the preamp section employs a two stage direct connection configuration of PNP-NPN using carefully selected low-noise transistors. The front end of the FM section is equipped with two FETs and four frequency linear type variable capacitor. In addition, high input impedance, low noise 4-pole MOS FET is used for the first stage of RF, and 3 ceramic filters with 2 elements and 2 stages of retuned LC filter are used for the IF stage to realize excellent performance. Uses an FM muting circuit using two LC filters. The stereo MPX circuit uses a monolithic IC.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SA-5500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/sa-5500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-10000":{"more":[{"t":"The power amplifier of the 10000 series was developed without any compromise in order to improve the performance and pursue the reproduction sound with the total power of the technics engineering team and the results of the research and development accumulated over many years. The circuit configuration has been developed from the all-stage direct-coupled OCL circuit used in all Technics amplifiers since the Technics50A, and employs a four stage differential amplifier in the amplifier stage. The complimentary service transistor is a complete output circuit combining PNP and NPN types. In order to improve the stability at the output terminal, which is a problem in the OCL circuit, we used carefully selected components such as a 4-stage differential amplifier with hfe in the amplification stage. We also adopted a circuit method using a DC feedback amplifier to compensate for voltage fluctuations at the output terminal. As a result, the voltage fluctuation is stabilized within ± 3 mv at -10 ℃ to + 60 ℃, resulting in a highly reliable circuit design. The power supply section employs the world's first large-capacity constant-voltage power supply to reduce fluctuations in power supply voltage and voltage fluctuations during large output.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-10000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-10000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-10000":{"more":[{"t":"The 10000 series stereo preamplifier was developed without any compromise in order to improve the performance and pursue the reproduction sound with the total power of the technics engineering team and the results of the research and development accumulated over many years. The equalizer amplifier section has a 4-stage direct circuit configuration consisting of 3-stage direct differential amplification and emitter follower. The first stage uses a specially selected low-noise PNP transistor, and the last stage uses a circuit configuration with a high voltage of 162 V, which greatly improves various characteristics. For both Phono1 and 2, the input impedance can be switched in three stages and the input sensitivity can be switched in two stages. When the switch on the rear panel is panel, the input impedance is indicated on the front panel. A differential amplifier circuit is also used for the tone control circuit to improve various characteristics. The characteristics can be changed in steps of 2.5 dB. Moreover, the turnover frequency can be changed up to three steps in each of the high and low frequency ranges. Moreover, a tone defeat switch is mounted so that the characteristics can be returned to a flat characteristic.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-10000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-10000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-3000":{"more":[{"t":"An excellent integrated amplifier of CP that challenged the limit of cost reduction while maintaining excellent characteristics. The power amplifier stage is composed of all stages directly connected OCL circuits with a differential amplifier circuit at the first stage. Also, a PNP pair transistor developed for a differential amplifier is used. The equalizer circuit is composed of two stages connected together with specially selected low-noise PNP-NPN transistors. The power supply voltage of the equalizer stage is set high by the + -2 power supply, and the allowable input is set large. It is equipped with a microphone amplifier, and the microphone volume and source volume can be adjusted separately for level adjustment. Two pairs of tape monitor circuits are installed. Equipped with tone control.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-3000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-3000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥35,800. Integrated amplifier with fully integrated OTR circuit. Built-in loudspeaker matrix 4ch circuit. The microphone terminal is installed. You can split the preamplifier and power amplifier. You can connect two loudspeaker.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥58,000. 2 Power supply Fully integrated stereo amplifier with integrated OCL circuit. capac cartridge cartridge Built-in MFR (multi-sonic creative device) enables adjustment of frequency characteristics. Built-in microphone mixing circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥23,900. Record player with IM cartridge. IM cartridge C-27M cartridge. The turntable part adopts the belt drive method, and the drive motor is equipped with a 4-pole motorronus motor. Auto cut and auto return mechanism are specified. The arm elevation mechanism that does not hurt records and needles. The cabinet has a walnut wood grain finish.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥45,000. It has a fully integrated structure. The power amplifier part is equipped with a circuit of the OTR system, which has high stability. The preamplifier SN equalizer amplifier adopts the monolithic IC, which is high SN and low distortion. In addition, the tone control circuit adopts a two-stage direct amplifier negative feedback (NF) type, as with CA-700, the linear is low in the middle point of the thrush, and the residual noise is suppressed. Low filter, high filter, and loudness circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥65,000. Stereo integrated amplifier with abundant input and output circuit and affordable circuit design. The power amplifier has an OCL circuit. Two Phono circuits are available. Two equalizer amplifiers are available for each application. Phono1’s equal amplifier amplifier is used for MM type and IM type cartridge with large output voltage. It has a dynamic range and has high stability at large input, and has improved SN and distortion rate. The circuit configuration is a high-gain and high-SN 4-stone amplifier using the base grounding method. The power trans and loudspeaker output circuit are equipped with a protective circuit. tone control circuit is a negative feedback (NF)-type sampling method using two-stage direct connection.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-400":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥59,000. Stereo receiver with high sensitivity and cost performance. The power amplifier part is equipped with the OCL circuit. In addition, the first step of the axial amplifier has a high degree of stability compared to the positive negative feedback using FET as a constant current source. In addition, the power amplifier amplifier circuit has an active subsonic filter, which is cut by a 12dB/oct slope with a 20Hz (3dB down point) or less. The equalizer amplifier adopts the monolithic IC of the three-stage straight circuit to realize high stability, low distortion rate and high gain. We also use high quality parts for equalizer element to improve the characteristics. The Tone Okunto Roll circuit adopts a unique negative feedback (NF) type that returns negative feedback between the two-stage direct amplifier amplifier emitter and has a straight control characteristics and low distortion rate. The microphone mixing circuit is equipped with a dedicated amplifier for three-tone configurations independent of other program sources. You can use the Pre out terminal to record the mixed signal to the tape.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"No, the Yamaha CR-400 receiver isn’t big. It isn’t powerful. It doesn’t have a lot of features and it’s not sought after by collectors. But, what it is, is a well built little receiver that will perform perfectly in a smaller room. Besides, the more features there are the more that can go wrong with it right? At $330 it was Yamaha’s entry level offering which, at the time, included the CR-600, CR-800 and CR-1000. The CR-400 was introduced in 1975 and is rated at 16 watts per channel so it isn’t going to blow the doors off your room. It may be the lowest power output of all the vintage Yamaha receivers. Even the later CR-240 put out 20 watts per channel.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CR-400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-400.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-400","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-400","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-400.jpg","xc":2,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-400","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/yamaha-cr-400-wood-case.jpg"}},"yamaha-yp-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥43,000. Record player developed by high accuracy processing technology. Turntable is 30cm aluminum die cast. In addition, the belt drive method is used for the motor which uses a constant belthronous type. (motor vibration off) method and suppresses vibration from the motor and the external. Tonearm has a simple J-type light alloy pipe arm. It is a total mass balance type that fits the additional mechanism in the frame with an effective length of 221.6mm, and it is a tonearm with high traceability. In addition, the headshell of the international standard plug-in exchange method is adopted, and the needle pressure is adjustable, and the anti-skater mechanism is equipped. It has an easy-to-use auto mechanism. This mechanism is a mechanism that mixes the good points of the manual and the auto.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥49,000. Record player developed by high accuracy processing technology. The mechanism part adopts a belt drive method using a 30cm aluminum die cast turntable and a beltronous outer motoror motor. In order to reduce unwanted vibrations, we use our own double-float suspension method to remove the whole player mechanism. This method is a double suspension mechanism that combines turntable and tonearm to float from the player panel, and also float the motor part, and it blocks external vibrations and motor vibrations. The arm adopts a light alloy S-shaped pipe arm with a solid structure that has no resonance, and it has a high tra ability with a sharp sensitivity both horizontally and vertically. It also comes with a direct reading needle pressure adjustment and a subweight for weight cartridge. In addition, we also have a lateral weight for the balance of the left and right balance centered on the tonearm axis and a thread suspended anti-skater to cancel the inside force. The headshell uses the international standard plug-in exchange method. This headshell enamel is gold-plated and prevents contact failure.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-e-202":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase E-202 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/E-202-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-250":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1974 at ¥175,000. This is a stereo power amplifier developed with the policy of pursuing sound quality to the limit instead of pursuing powerful power. Carefully selected parts are used, and sound quality and durability are well considered. 100W/ch (8 Ω) is achieved by parallel push-pull drive using a large power transistor at the output stage. In addition, by thoroughly examining the bias current of each stage, the distortion at a small output is eliminated to the limit. The power supply section is equipped with a large power transformer and a 20000 μ Fx2 capacitor in order to send sufficient energy to the speakers and to follow signals that change rapidly and greatly. We have adopted a method of switching the damping factor of the amplifier so that it matches the speaker designed in the era of tube amplifier. With an 8 Ω load, you can choose from three options: 20 or more (NORMAL), 5 (MEDIUM), and 1 (SOFT). This allows you to enjoy the unique sound quality of the tube type amplifier. In the event of a short-circuit of the cord after the output terminal or an error inside the amplifier, a protective circuit is mounted which is cut off by a relay from the moment.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-250 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-250-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"bang-olufsen-beogram-4002":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥250,000. Record player with linear tracking method. MMC-4000","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Bang & Olufsen Beogram 4002 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram4002.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"c-e-c-bd-320":{"more":[{"t":"Semi-auto player with belt drive system.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – C.E.C. BD 320 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/BD320-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/c-e-c-bd-320.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/BD320-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/bd320.JPG"}},"harman-kardon-330-b":{"more":[{"t":"The Harman Kardon 330B was a modest offering from the company. It was designed as a budget receiver that still produced hi-fi level sound. It produces 18 watts per channel so if you want to shake your foundation then it’s probably not for you. However, for a low end, budget minded receiver it produces some really nice sound and sold for only $199 when introduced. The 330B was introduced around 1973, followed by the 330C, and was somewhat of a staple for many years. You’ll find many people who still own and rave about their 330B and many others who regret selling their 330B. That should tell you something about their performance. They are very minimalist in their design. A simple red power button, black switches, and corrugated knobs run across the front.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Harman Kardon 330 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/harman-kardon-330b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-citation-19":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥245,000. A new model that was developed to reproduce the sound field in the depth. Switches can be used as a mono power amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon Citation 19 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citation19.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-4vr-5456":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced in 1974, the JVC 4VR-5456 receiver is a quadraphonic (4-channel) model that retailed for $799.95. It’s packed with features including an AM/FM tuner, CD-4 demodulator, two-position matrix decoder, and SEA multiband tone controls. It was made by the Victor Co. in Japan and distributed by JVC America. It’s not the greatest looking receiver but it has some power and is very flexible. Apparently JVC bet heavily on the success of the 4-channel market but, unfortunately for them, that market dwindled quickly. They also bet on their own CD-4 decoding format which would have to compete with the more popular Sony SQ format and Sansui QS format. In the end the 4-channel market collapsed as consumers just didn’t seem to want them. JVC allegedly rebadged most of their 4VR line at the time and marketed them as 2-channel stereos that were “4-channel ready” as opposed to straight up 4-channel receivers. Still, they didn’t sell many overall which is why they aren’t that common today.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – JVC 4VR-5456","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/jvc-4vr-5456","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-jl-a-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥29,800. Built-in auto-cutting mechanism. Also, when arm is on the upper side, the power supply of motor is cut. 4-pole motorronus motor is used for drive motor. Tonearm has a TH-type universal arm. The cartridge uses a MM type cartridge, which can be used for CD-4 playback only by needle exchange.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JL-A 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/jl-a1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-700-m":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥300,000. Stereo power of the supreme series. 700M has a wide range of naked properties in all responses with NFB removed, and has a moderate NPB effect. Also, by inserting the buffer stage between the first stage and the A-class drive stage, distortion and phase zure are released. In the drive stage, the boots circuit is removed to enhance the naked characteristics, and the distortion by low frequency constant is also shut out. This greatly improves various characteristics that are not present in normal measurement, such as out-of-band characteristics, motion characteristics, and ultra-small signal characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood 700 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/700m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-3006":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥48,000. Equipped with high power design. In addition, the ±2 power supply method using the first step differential method is available. This improves the various characteristics of the bass area thoroughly and obtains stable output throughout the frequency band. Trio's proprietary ASO-detected limiter method is available. This enables better power supply usage and low impedance and low distortion rate with high dynamic range and high input impedance. In addition, shock noise is suppressed because the DC current at the output end is 0V. Low filter, high filter, -20dB Stereo/Mono","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-3006 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-3006.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-5006":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥57,000. Stereo-integrated amplifier with full-stage direct-connected and pure-complication circuit. In addition, the ±2 power supply method using the first step differential method is available. This improves the various characteristics of the bass area thoroughly and obtains stable output throughout the frequency band. The trans protection circuit uses a limiter-type protection circuit to protect loudspeaker and protect power supply ON/OFF. Reduce the limiter level within 100m/sec when the output end is shortened and protect the trans. This enables better power supply usage and low impedance and low distortion rate with high dynamic range and high input impedance. In addition, shock noise is suppressed because the DC current at the output end is 0V. tone control circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-5006 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-5006.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-7006":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥75,000. Stereo-integrated amplifier with full-stage direct-connected and pure-complication circuit. In addition, the ±2 power supply method using the first step differential method is available. This improves the various characteristics of the bass area thoroughly and obtains stable output throughout the frequency band. The trans protection circuit uses a limiter-type protection circuit to protect loudspeaker and protect power supply ON/OFF. Reduce the limiter level within 100m/sec when the output end is shortened and protect the trans. The equalizer has a three-stage direct connection method. tone control circuit supports DLOA (dual low noise optional amplifier). This enables better power supply usage and low impedance and low distortion rate with high dynamic range and high input impedance. In addition, shock noise is suppressed because the DC current at the output end is 0V.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-7006 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-7006.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-9006":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥120,000. Stereo integrated amplifier mounted on top model with full-stage direct connection + net complementary circuit. In addition, the ±2 power supply method using the first step differential method is available. This improves the various characteristics of the bass area thoroughly and obtains stable output throughout the frequency band. The trans protection circuit uses a limiter-type protection circuit to protect loudspeaker and protect power supply ON/OFF. Reduce the limiter level within 100m/sec when the output end is shortened and protect the trans. In addition to the three-stage direct connection method of the first-stage differential circuit, equalizer has two power supply methods. The tone control circuit has a two-step switch betweenasss and Treble. Low filter features subsonic filter and lanble filter. High filter","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-9006 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-9006.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-9400":{"more":[{"t":"The Kenwood Kr-9400 is one of Kenwood’s iconic receivers from the mid 1970’s and was their top of the line receiver at the time. At 120 watts per channel into 8 ohms it was an early predecessor of the later monster receivers. It debuted around 1976 and retailed for about $750.00. The KR-9400 features the classic Kenwood styling from the 1970’s. Blue, green and red lighting on the dial and meters makes for a colorful display. The volume and tone functions have detent controls. Kenwood uses a triple function meter for Signal Strength, Multipath, and Deviation depending upon which button is depressed. It also features triple tone controls and a Dolby FM switch (requires a Dolby adapter). The build quality of the KR-9400 is exceptional.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-9400","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-9400","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kenwood-kr-9400.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-9400","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/kenwood-kr-9400-front.jpg"}},"luxman-mq-80":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1974 at ¥169,000. A stereo power amplifier using 6336A vacuum tube. Dual triode 6336A used for OTL amplifier MQ36 is used for the output tube. In the MQ80, one push-pull circuit per one channel is constructed using this 6336A, and 40W output is obtained at 8 Ω load. An output transformer similar in appearance to the conventional OY15 type is used. However, in order to achieve the effect of cross-shunt push-pull operation, the primary side winding is divided into the plate side and the cathode side, and this is wound around the bifilar. In addition, the high-frequency characteristics of the output transformer are extended to 200 kHz, and the phase characteristics are also excellent. Therefore, the naked characteristics of the amplifier are improved and the stability when negative feedback is applied is also excellent. For the output stage of cross-shunt push-pull operation, 50% of the output voltage returns as negative feedback. In addition, 6336A requires a large drive voltage because of low rp and high Gm.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman MQ-80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/mq80-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2015":{"more":[{"t":"Clicking a link to eBay may result in a referral commission being paid if a purchase is made.Loading...","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2015","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/model/marantz-2015-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2220b":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Marantz 2220B. It was at the lower end of the Marantz offerings but still offered great quality manufacturing and sound. It’s rated at 20 watts per channel into 8 ohms. These little receivers are great for someone just getting into vintage audio. They can be purchased for a reasonable amount and, once serviced, will last for years. Nothing too complicated inside which makes them easier to work on. The 2220B’s sell from around $450.00 for an average condition un-serviced unit all the way up to $1000.00 for a clean and restored unit. Hi… I picked up one of these Marantz 2220B’s a few years ago and hooked it up and it works fine. It does have static in the knobs and I assume that it needs to be cleaned up and some parts replaced.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2220B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2220b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2220b.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2220b","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/05/marantz-2220B.jpg"}},"marantz-2235":{"more":[{"t":"Clicking a link to eBay may result in a referral commission being paid if a purchase is made.Loading...","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2235","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/model/marantz-2235-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2240":{"more":[{"t":"Produced in 1974 this Marantz 2240 had a list price of $449.95. It had the option of the WC-22 wood case and weighs just over 30 pounds. It puts out a modest 40 watts per channel in to 8 ohms. It features both tuning and signal meters as well as a phono input and two tape inputs. It also has separate Bass, Treble and Mid controls, Dolby FM, Muting and High/Low filter controls. Marantz receivers are very popular with collectors and audio enthusiasts. The Marantz 2240 is a low to mid range model but still sells for decent money. Both the 2240 and 2240b (a revised version of the 2240) can sell for up to $900 in excellent working condition. More commonly they will sell for around $400 in average used condition.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2240","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2240","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2275":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2275 had a retail price of nearly $600.00 back in 1974 and was made until 1977. It put out 75 watts per channel in to 8 ohms and featured a phase-lock-loop FM multiplex demodulator. It also has direct coupled output amplifiers, a five gang tuner, Dolby FM and mid tone controls. The 2275 used the WC-22 wood case as an option. The Marantz 2275 was the focus of an interesting Marantz ad campaign that ran in Stereo Review. The ad showed a burned 2270 that the owner claimed had been recovered from the charred remains of his home after a house fire. After replacing the power cord the 2270 allegedly worked perfectly. Of course, some anti-Marantz types began insinuating that it was actually the 2270 that started the fire in the first place. There was no Marantz 2275b.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2275","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2275","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2275.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2275","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/10/marantz-2275-1.jpg"}},"marantz-2325":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2325 came out around 1974 with a list price of $799.95. It was discontinued some time around 1976. It produces 125 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It’s known for more than adequate warm power, a beautiful spacious sound stage, thunderous bass, and on top of that, it’s pleasing to the eye. The 2325 is a handsome receiver. It looks especially good in the optional WC-43 walnut case. I believe the WC-123 case also fits this model. The 2325 was Marantz’s flagship receiver at the time and part of their 22xx lineup. That lineup included the 2275, 2250B, 2240B, 2235B, 2225, 2220B, and 2215B.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2325","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2325","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-dd-1":{"more":[{"t":"A direct drive player focusing on basic performance. A brushless direct drive motor with a DC servocontrol is used in the drive system to obtain excellent characteristics. The tone arm is designed to utilize the rotating part of MA-202 as it is, and the head shell uses H-303 with less resonance. A damping material is used for the arm mounting part to prevent resonance as a player system. The Inside Four Scan Seller uses Micro's unique spring tension and is a simple needle pressure-compatible variable type. 33 Fine adjustment of 1/3 and 45 rpm is independent structure, and can be changed within ± 6%. It is also equipped with a large mirror type strobe for speed check. The cartridge uses M-2100mkII which is an improved version of M-2100. Equipped with an oil dump-type arm lifter, linked to on-off and turntable start.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki DD-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/dd-1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/micro-seiki-dd-1.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/dd-1-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/dd-1.JPG"}},"micro-seiki-mr-222":{"more":[{"t":"A belt drive record player developed with an emphasis on operability and functionality. The drive system is a belt drive system with a 4-pole synchronous motor, and the belt uses polished belt. Straight pipe integrated type is adopted for the tone arm, and even the head shell is integrated. In addition, this arm is equipped with an inside for scan cellar, which cancels the arm being pulled inward when playing a record. The cartridge is replaced by a unique carrier system. An oil dump type arm lifter is adopted. When the lifter knob is turned off → on, the power is turned on and the turntable rotates. When on → play, the tone arm slowly begins to fall onto the record surface. At the end of the performance, turn play → on → off to stop the turntable and turn off the power.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki MR-222 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-222-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-mr-322":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki MR-322 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-322-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/micro-seiki-mr-322.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-322-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-322.JPG"}},"micro-seiki-mr-622":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki MR-622 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-622-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/micro-seiki-mr-622.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-622-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/mr-622.JPG"}},"micro-seiki-solid-5":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki Solid-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/solid-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nakamichi-610":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥130,000. Preamplifier developed to target the best preamplifier for recording. In addition, low distortion rate is realized by adopting the current drive driver step. It is also considerable for microphone input, and each of the two stereo channels has an amplifier. The microphone amplifier part is a sensitivity of 0.2mV at 1kΩ0dB, and is equipped with a 15dB, 30dB attenuator, and the S/N is a unique circuit design. Dynamic margins have a sufficient amount of looseness with +46dB at 0dB of attenuator. A dedicated monitor for headphones. The circuit method adopts the differential input Pure Complementary OTR method, which can drive the headphones from 8Ω to 200Ω with a clear motion. This unit reduces the circuit and sound quality of circuits by conventional code wiring.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nakamichi 610 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/610.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-cp-55-a":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo CP-55 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/player/cp-55a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-cp-60-a":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo CP-60 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/player/cp-60a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-cp-80-m":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo CP-80 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/player/cp-80m-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-c-1700":{"more":[{"t":"An armless player with a brushless DC servo direct drive hole motor. The motor is a direct drive phono motor that uses a Hall element. In place of the brush, which was indispensable for conventional DC motors, we applied the hole stopping method developed by Pioneer to the magnetic field detection of the switching mechanism. This reduces vibration compared with DC motors with mechanical switching mechanism, and improves S/N and durability. Since the direct drive system directly drives the turntable, there is no intermediate reduction mechanism that causes uneven rotation, and excellent characteristics are obtained. The Hall element is a kind of semiconductor. It is a cross-shaped thin film metal made of N-type Insb alloy. It uses the \"Hall effect\" in which a voltage is generated between two terminals when an electric current flows through two terminals and a magnetic force is applied at a right angle to the other two terminals to convert magnetism into electricity. Pioneer has developed a new manufacturing method called the vacuum deposition method, and has reduced the thickness from the previous limit of 30-50 μ m to 0.8 μ m, realizing a low-cost and small-size Hall element.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-C 1700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/plc-1700-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sa-9900":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier that pursues high output and low distortion and employs a unique side terminal system. The side terminal method is adopted. The input terminals are integrated with the equalizer board, and the shield line connecting the phono terminal and the equalizer terminal is eliminated to prevent degradation of the high-frequency characteristics due to stray capacitance of the shield line. All stages of the power amplifier are directly connected and pure complimentary service OCL circuit with 3-stage Darlington connection, and the output stage is parallel push-pull type. The 2-stage differential amplifier and bias compensation circuit provide sufficient stability by controlling the DC component to the speaker terminal even when there is a change in external temperature. The two constant-current circuits expand the operating range of the transistor and increase the bare characteristics of the circuit. Moreover, not only NFB from the output stage but also appropriate NFB is applied to the differential part to improve the bare characteristics. In addition, by applying NFB from the output stage, deterioration and instability of transient characteristics are eliminated. Furthermore, by providing a large time constant to this circuit, phase shift in the ultra-low frequency range is eliminated.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-9900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-9900-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-1010":{"more":[{"t":"There is really nothing special about the Pioneer SX-1010. Well, of course, it was THE receiver that started the Monster Receiver wars of the late 1970’s. And, it’s probably one of the best built receivers of all time. Oh, and it is usually at the top of the list of performance amongst the heavyweight receivers of the time as well. Just looking at it doesn’t inspire any special feelings in the observer but take off the case and have a look at the insides or power it up for a listen and you’ll become a believer. In late 1974 Pioneer threw down the gauntlet at other audio manufacturers and brought the SX-1010 to market. Rated at a conservative 110 watts per channel the SX-1010 was top of the line and the last of the black dial face receivers for Pioneer. Marantz, Sansui and Kenwood all upped the ante soon afterward which led Pioneer to design and release the SX-1250 with an all new look. Some prefer the all silver face look of the later generation Pioneer’s over the earlier black dial versions but there is no arguing the SX-1010’s place in audio history.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-1010","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1010","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-434":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥50,000. A high-cost performance receiver with improved performance by incorporating the latest technologies of the time into the tuner and integrated amplifier. The EQ amplifier is a 2-stage direct connection type with accurate RIAA deviation, and the power amplifier section is a pure complimentary service OCL system directly connected to all stages. The tuner section has a circuit configuration that uses a low-noise FET and a 3-series varicon for the FM front end and a high-integration IC and ceramic filter for the IF section. In addition, an FM muting switch is cut off unpleasant inter-station noise during FM channel selection. The dial scale is wide type, and the FM scale is linear (equal interval) scale. A microphone mixing circuit allows you to sing along with program sources for records, tapes, FM and AM broadcasts. The mixed signal can be recorded to tape or used as a microphone amplifier if the volume of the program source is minimized. There are two sets of speaker jacks (A and B), and you can use them in four positions (A, B, A + B and OFF) by changing the switch.","s":"audio-database.com"},{"t":"The Pioneer SX-434 was basically the bottom end of the Pioneer lineup from 1974-1976. There was, of course, the unforgettable Pioneer SX-300 which pumped out 7 watts per channel but that receiver tended to be packaged by dealers with a low end turntable and speakers for the absolute budget shopper. The SX-434 is a legitimate receiver but with minimal power and sparse features. Still, it was a good entry level stereo at the time. Actually it’s not a bad entry level receiver for those just getting into vintage audio today. Pioneer listed the SX-434 at $239.95 but I’ve seen a number of dealer ads that had it for sale as low as $159 in 1976. How much power does the SX-434 have? Well, it produces 15 watts per channel. You’re not going to blow the doors off the house with that output but that’s not really what it was designed to do anyway.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SX-434 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sx-434-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-434","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-434","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-535":{"more":[{"t":"This Pioneer SX-535 was a modest offering from Pioneer in the mid 1970’s and retailed for $299.95. On the market from 1974 until about 1976 the SX-535 produced 20 watts per channel into 8 ohms. Other Pioneer receivers released in 1974 included the SX-636 and SX-737. The wood cabinet, walnut end caps, brushed aluminum silver front and blackout dial face gave it a distinctive mid 70’s look. Pioneer always had the classy beveled knobs as well. Developed before the wattage war of the late 70’s the SX-535 wasn’t a power monster. In fact, Pioneer marketed it as being efficient and asked, “Why pay for watts that are wasted?” Their marketing brochure stated: “The Pioneer SX-535 combines practical power with advanced features and high performance to prove that high power is not always the answer when it comes to good high fidelity listening.” Pioneer backed up their marketing claims with a number of quality features. The FM tuner section is excellent and uses a low noise FET and a 3 gang variable tuning capacitor in the front end. The FM MPX circuit is a Phase Lock Loop (PLL) type with an IC.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-535","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-535","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-636":{"more":[{"t":"This Pioneer SX-636 was a mid-range offering from Pioneer in 1974 and retailed for $350.00. It only produces 25 watts per channel into 8 ohms but, as Pioneer stated in their marketing brochure: “Not all high fidelity situations require high powered equipment. If your listening room is of average size, and what you really want is more efficiency and more sophisticated versatility in a medium-powered model, Pioneer’s new SX-636 will be a good choice.” The SX-636 came out a few years before the wattage wars so 25 wpc didn’t seem inadequate. And it wasn’t for most listening situations. Besides, the receiver looks good and has a number of features that lower end receivers don’t have. The front panel has bass and treble controls, high filter, mono and loudness switches, and a function control for FM, AM, PHONO, MIC and AUX. The blackout style, FM-linear dial scale has two tuning meters, illuminated program indicators, and a stereo headphone jack. The control switches are push button instead of the toggle style you see on many of the later model Pioneers. The illuminated dial pointer is a nice touch as well.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-636","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-636","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-737":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-737 was a mid to higher end stereo in their lineup of the SX-424, SX-535, SX-636, SX-737, SX-838 receivers. Produced in 1974 it churns out 35 watts per channel. Pioneer advertised it by saying: It has the power to do the job – not too much and not too little. That about sums it up. It retailed for about $300. The SX-737 really is a nice looking receiver. The blue dial light and meter are accented by red and green indicator lights. Add in the wood cabinet and brushed aluminum face plate and it exudes that vintage audio look. It has the usual array of features one would expect in a mid range stereo.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-737","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-737","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-838":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-838, released in 1974, features a combination of excellent sound quality, power, and classic design. Its retail price was $499.95. It delivers 50 watts per channel into 8 ohms with 0.3% total harmonic distortion. Today the x3x line from Pioneer is highly desired for both its performance and its looks. The controls on the SX-838 are well laid out. Notice the horizontal row of black push buttons just under the dial face. The SX-838 was produced during the transition into the silver faced era. The black push buttons essentially represent the older design aesthetic and the brushed aluminum knobs and switches the new aesthetic. Later models from Pioneer used almost all brushed aluminum controls.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-838","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-838","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-939":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-939 is a vintage stereo receiver that was released by Pioneer Corporation in 1974. It belongs to the Pioneer SX line that includes the SX-1010, SX-939, and SX-838. The SX-1010 was top of the line with 100 watts per channel. The SX-939 produced 70 watts per channel and the SX-838 50 wpc. The SX-939 retailed for $599.95 while the SX-1010 was $699.95 and the SX-838 $499.95. These prices included a walnut cabinet. The SX-939 looks great, has an excellent FM tuner and phono amp, and, at 70 wpc it can power most any 8 ohm speakers. The SX-939 is also easy to maintain as many parts including, knobs, bulbs, transistors and circuit boards are all available on eBay. Check HERE for currently available parts.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-939","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-939","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-221":{"more":[{"t":"The Sansui 221 receiver is a hidden treasure. Despite its small size and modest power rating of 8 watts per channel, this little powerhouse delivers sound quality that often surprises people. Offered by Sansui in 1975, with a price tag of around $180, it was definitely their budget oriented unit in a lineup that included the 331 and 551. Sansui also offered the 9090, 8080, 7070, 6060 and 5050 at the same time which took over for the earlier 661, 771, and 881 models. The 221 has all the basic functionality you’d need without any fluff and it performs very well. Sansui cut costs on the cabinet and knobs, and by eliminating extraneous features, but they didn’t skimp on the quality of the circuits. Some sources show the 221 producing 10 watts per channel while others state 8 into 8 ohms. The Sansui advertisement below states 8 wpc. Either way, with such low power output, you’ll need to pair it with some efficient speakers.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 221","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-221","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-331":{"more":[{"t":"This is an easy-to-use FM/AM receiver that combines a high-sensitivity FM/AM tuner section and an audio amplifier focusing on sound quality into a compact design. The power amplifier section uses a high-performance hybrid IC with sufficient power and low distortion characteristics. Equipped with tone control with stable operation and straightforward characteristics. The FM front-end uses a high-sensitivity dual FET to catch weak radio waves with excellent high-frequency characteristics. Equipped with tape monitor switch and loudness switch. Equipped with speaker switching switch.","s":"audio-database.com"},{"t":"The Sansui Model 331 entered the market as an affordable stereo receiver, priced around $200. It delivers 12 watts per channel and has only basic features. It was produced from 1975 to 1977. Don’t let the modest specs fool you though. The Sansui 331 is a bit of a hidden gem. It punches well above its weight, delivering a sound that’s way more impressive than you’d expect from a 12-watt unit. The FM tuner is surprisingly crisp, and the whole thing just feels good in a way that makes you appreciate vintage audio gear. It’s one of those components that proves you don’t always need to spend big to get great sound. Aesthetically, the 331 looks great.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui 331 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/331-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 331","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-331","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-331.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-331","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/03/sansui-331-lamps.jpg"}},"sansui-441":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥52,800. FM/AM receiver with functional simplicity of panel layout and improved usability. A dedicated large IC is used for the power stage. A dual gate MOS FET is used for the FM front-end section. It is equipped with tone control, loudness and tape monitor switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui 441 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/441-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-551":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥65,000. FM/AM receiver with improved basic performance in both the audio and tuner sections. The power stage uses a SEPP quasi complimentary service circuit. A high-gain IC is used for the equalizer. Various characteristics have been improved by adopting a dual gate MOS FET in the FM front-end section. Equipped with a loudness, high filter and FM muting switch.","s":"audio-database.com"},{"t":"The Sansui 551 is a mid-range receiver that was on the market from around 1974 to 1976. It retailed for $259.95 and is a solid state receiver that produces 16 watts per channel. For a mid-range, low powered receiver it does its job well and looks good too. It has most of the connections you’d want including a phono, a tape, 2 speaker outputs, 2 AC outlets, and an AUX connection. Its features are somewhat limited with just the basic functions incorporated into the receiver. There is a signal strength meter, bass and treble controls, a high filter, loudness switch, a headphone jack, and a muting button. That’s about it. The 551’s silver face coupled with faux wood-metal case, and the green dial scale gives it a great vintage look, and it’s smaller size makes it perfect for a small room, office, or garage.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui 551 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/551-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 551","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-551","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-661":{"more":[{"t":"This is a high-quality receiver developed using Sansui's accumulated technology. Each circuit is integrated into three printed circuit boards, and ICs are used everywhere to eliminate troubles such as failure and improve reliability and durability. In particular, the volume and switches of the control section of the preamplifier are directly mounted on the printed circuit board for reliable operation. All stages are directly connected with pure complimentary service OCL system for the circuit configuration of the power amplifier. The coupling capacitor that causes distortion is removed, and a differential amplifier circuit and ± 2 power supply are used. The equalizer amplifier section uses a 2-stage direct-coupled circuit system using carefully selected low-noise transistors. The tone control circuit is CR type. The protective circuit consists of four short-cut fuses, plus an electronic circuit and relay to protect the speakers and power transistors. This circuit also functions to prevent pop noise when the power is turned on.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui 661 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/661-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-771":{"more":[{"t":"This gem from 1973 is the Sansui 771 receiver. It was at the upper end of Sansui’s xx1 lineup which consisted of the 221, 331, 441, 551, 661, 771, and top of the line 881. MSRP was $430 in 1973 but I’ve seen prices all over the place in different advertisements of the time. Even as low as $289.95 in 1974. Regardless, it is a very good receiver. It’s styling may leave a little to be desired but it’s performance is excellent. It produces 32 watts per channel into 8 ohms. That’s at 20-20,000Hz. At 1000Hz it produces 40 wpc.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui 771 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/771-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 771","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-771","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-881":{"more":[{"t":"Released in 1974 the Sansui 881 retailed for $529.95 and was the top-of-the-line receiver in the Sansui lineup at the time. Others in the line included the 771, 661, 551, 441, 331, and 221. At an underrated 60 watts per channel into 8 ohms it packs plenty of power and total harmonic distortion comes in at a respectable 0.3%. Sansui claimed it was the best receiver on the market and they may have been right. The Sansui 9010 is the same receiver as the 881 but the upper half of the front panel is black. The Sansui 881’s gold anodized front panel and metal endcaps give it a clean metallic look. The black out dial face holds the tuning dial and both a signal and tuning meter. Both the dial and meters are backlit with a soft green light. The source indicator lights are orange and the FM stereo indicator light is red.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 881","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-881","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-5500":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier that uses triple tone control and complete defeat system to improve practical performance and sound quality. A differential amplifier circuit in which a pair transistor capable of stable amplification is combined at the first stage of the power amplifier section is adopted. A 3-stage Darlington connection circuit is used for the drive stage, and a heteropolar power transistor with uniform characteristics is used for the final output stage. A high-gain monolithic dedicated IC is used for the equalizer amplifier. Because of the high gain, a large NFB is applied, resulting in flat characteristics and a wide frequency band. In addition to Bass and Treble, the tone amplifier uses triple tone control with adjustable Midrange. This circuit is an negative feedback (NF) type circuit that uses a selected low-noise noise type transistor for the first stage input, and flat characteristics can be obtained by fully disabling the tone control circuit. The chassis ground is not used for grounding at the input of the equalizer amplifier without using chassis ground. As a result, each circuit operates normally and stability is improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-5500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-5500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-qrx-7500":{"more":[{"t":"In the early to mid 1970’s Quadraphonic sound was just coming to the forefront. Sansui was one of the leaders of the 4-channel movement with their QR line of quadraphonic receivers. Around 1974-1975 they introduced the QRX line which included this beauty, the Sansui QRX-7500. The QRX-7500 was the top of the line at the time in terms of power output at about 30 watts per channel (4 channels into four 8 ohm speakers). The receiver features a built in CD-4 album decoder, SQ decoder (phase matrix), QS decoder (regular matrix), two phono inputs, and outputs for two sets of four speakers. What’s the difference between the QRX-7500 and QRX7500A? Well, it all has to do with the decoding. The QRX-7500A was a “hybrid” unit as Sansui moved from the discrete component vario-matrix decoder circuits to their custom Vario-matrix IC’s that were used in the QRX-7001/8001/9001. There were two distinct ICs.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui QRX-7500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-qrx-7500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-sr-212":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥29,800. An auto return player with excellent operability. When the performance is finished, it will automatically return to the arm value and turntable will also stop. In addition, if you want to cut the playing in the middle, if you operate the operation, arm will auto return and turntable will stop. The arm can be operated without hurting the record or needle tip. Turntable is made of double rim mould 30cm aluminum alloy diecast with precision finishing. Special polyur belts with low aging change enable driving. The motor uses a 4-pole motorronus motor that is resistant to voltage and load ctuation, and can be rotated at a constant speed. Arm is equipped with a lightweight static balance S-shaped pipe arm which is both horizontal and vertical.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-212 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-212.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-sr-313":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥39,800. Manual record player with belt drive method. S-shaped pipe arm with knife edge support system that can be faithful trace. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge. The cabinet has a thick board.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-313 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-313.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-sr-717":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥69,800. Record player with direct drive. 20 pole brushless DC servo motor A self-position detection method with accurate rotation. The bearing part adopts precision special alloy with good durability. The arm support unit adopts a knife edge (vertical), and a one-point support method is used horizontally. The cabinet has a solid board.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-717 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-717.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-4750":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥53,800. Direct drive and player system with SBMC and magnetic disk servo system. Furthermore, because the servo response range has expanded significantly, it realizes good load characteristics and wow-flotter characteristics that improve the servo effect. In order to keep the record close to turntable and reduce resonance, the suction cup type insulation mat is available. With this, the long dinal signal of the record groove is related to the stereo effect, so it has the effect of improving the position. In addition, the noise is removed and the noise is suppressed. SBMC is a new material developed by Sony Technology Team in cabinet and turntable. This material is a thermosetting resin that contains calcium carbonate and fiberglass as a base of polyester resin. The shrinkage rate is equivalent to 2 to 3 / 10,000, so it is possible to process high-precision machining with no madness after molding.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-4750 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-4750.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-5100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥24,800. Belt drive player with semi-automated mechanism for high cost performance. Turntable 30cm turntable Newly developed universal tonearm with arm lifter and in-side force camper. Semi-auto mechanism for auto-cutting and auto-return. IM type cartridge is used for cartridge. It is possible to replace cartridge because the shell is international standard. Low-capacity type is available for output code. This is a free-stop design with acrylic dust cover.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-5100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-5100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-sqa-2030":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥44,800. 4 channel decoder with 3 SQ/IC and back amplifier. In addition, it enables stable 4ch playback by SQ and IC. Built-in power amplifier for back channel using hybrid power IC developed for audio. Built-in SQ decoder and RM decoder, and discrete 4ch can be used with a CD-4 demogulator. Equipped with 4ch master volume control, you can adjust the volume by master volume control. The mode switch is equipped to switch between 4 channels and mono. negative feedback (NF) tone control for back ch. A loudness control for front ch and back ch. 2-ch input is switched to Low-Normal-High.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony SQA-2030 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/etc/sqa-2030.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-tae-8450":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥285,000. The highest-class stereo preamplifier for true waveform transmission. Equipped with a waveform transmission unit, the first N-channel FET axial amplifier, the second PN trans axial amplifier, and the end amplifier and all stages are fully connected directly. The equalizer circuit has two amplifiers with negative feedback (NF) and CR. Built-in new light-in peak program meter, which can be followed up to 1ms waveform. The head amplifier has a low noise trans. The headphone terminal is equipped with a full-stage direct connection method that combines the audio IC and the Pure Complementary output stage. High accuracy attenuator level control. The narrowing error of each step is less than 5dB. 20dB muting circuit with a method bypassed unit amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TAE-8450 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/tae-8450.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-tan-8250":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥315,000. Highest-class stereo power amplifier developed for faithful waveform transmission. The A class stage is a three-stage amplifier configuration, and the first stage is a dual FET with two high input impedance FETs. This circuit adopts DC amplifier configuration to improve phase characteristics. The B class stage is composed of triple push pull and pure complementary output stage in the driver stage of the triple Darlington. The peak program meter is equipped with a light-direction system that is easy to follow even for palmib waveforms. With a protective circuit, the power trans protection circuit is equipped with a load impedance-sensitive circuit with an electron circuit with a very fast response. and thermal-detecting-type protection circuit circuit to detect heat sink temperature rise. Also, the protection circuit of loudspeaker adopts pure electron type to ensure that the DC voltage is generated.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TAN-8250 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/tan-8250.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-tan-8550":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥295,000. In order to realize the theme of waveform transmission that is similar to the waveform of input and output signal as it is, the highest-class stereo power amplifier adopting the newly developed V-FET. V-FET is a power FET with a vertical structure, while the conventional FET is a yoco-shaped structure. This V-FET has a static characteristics similar to the triode vacuum tube, but it can handle large currents more than a triode vacuum tube, and the output resistance is also reduced. In addition, the polarity element of the N and P channels is obtained, so the output stage of the Pure Complementary can be obtained without the need for phase inverted circuits like vacuum tubes. In addition, because the temperature coefficient is negative, it has self-control effect on the fever. As a result, it has strong properties for thermal destruction (secondary destruction).","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TAN-8550 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/tan-8550.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"tandberg-tr-2075":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Tandberg TR-2075 from Norway. It was built from 1975-1977 and retailed for $999.00. The Tandberg’s unique styling with the large square push buttons and dark blue meter and dial lights make it easily identifiable. They are very well built receivers and have great FM tuning sections. Their phono section is a little weak though. There was also a later MK II model. The TR-2075 put out 75 watts per channel in to 8 ohms and had some interesting features such as: Tandberg receivers are fairly popular with collector’s and audio enthusiasts – especially in Europe. Some models require DIN plugs which can be a little difficult to find. I’m looking for one.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Tandberg TR-2075","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/tandberg-tr-2075","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/tandberg-tr-2075.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/tandberg-tr-2075","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/08/tandberg-tr-20752.jpg"}},"toshiba-sb-404":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥69,800. 4 channel amplifier integrated with 4 channel decoder. SB-404 is equipped with QM decoder unit. SB-404S is equipped with SQ decoder as the top model. It is equipped with a separate pre-main circuit, and it can be used as a discrete 4-channel system as it is when connecting the four-channel deck. The pre-main circuit has four independent lines. Toshiba trans 2SC1000 is used for trans inside the circuit. It has excellent characteristics of 1/3 at 1/2 and 10kHz at 100Hz compared to conventional low noise type. SB-404S uses 27 2SC1000 in total. The equalizer circuit for capac cartridge cartridge is built in.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB 404 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-404.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-514":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥129,000. Built-in RM/SQ circuit to support CD-4. Push button selector is available. It comes with real datasheet.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB 514 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-514.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥98,000. The power-stage operation method is used to switch to B and A, so you can freely select the stable power of B and low distortion of A. In addition, the constant voltage power supply is adopted to drive all stages except the power stage, and the overall stability is improved. The protection circuit has two steps for power trans and loudspeaker. It reduces the load to 2Ω or shortens the output terminal, and the protection circuit breaks instantly to prevent trouble. Because this circuit is an input limiter method, playback will not be interrupted only if the output is reduced even during the protection circuit operation. The loudspeaker protection circuit adopts the unique circuit method of the cable, and when the DC voltage of the output terminal exceeds ±2V, the relay is different instantly and the signal path to the loudspeaker is blocked.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥75,000. Low distortion power amplifier. The power amplifier part is equipped with a full-stage, direct-container OCL circuit that enables clear playback from ultra-low to ultra-high. In addition, it realizes stable operation by the first step of power amplifier. When the DC voltage of the output terminal exceeds ±2V, the relay immediately operates and shuts off the circuit. This protection circuit also has a power supply muting circuit, which prevents shock noise when power switch is ON/OFF. In addition, the output stage adopts the emitter follower method that reduces the output impedance, and drives by the +50V constant voltage to achieve high stability, low distortion rate, and high S/N. The circuit design uses a computer-based circuit analysis (CAD method), and the circuit board and terminal are wiring at the shortest distance when the distortion rate and S/N are good, and the pattern is also the best data obtained.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥85,000. It also has two-stage protection circuit with large heat sinker, power Tr protection and loudspeaker protection to ensure stable operation. It is equipped with a constant voltage power supply, which drives all stages except the power stage, to increase overall stability. The loudspeaker protection circuit with power supply muting prevents shock noise when power switch is turned on. In addition to the high supply voltage and low output impedance of 50V constant voltage, low distortion rate and high stability are obtained by computer-powered circuit analysis (CAD method).","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-ca-800.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-800.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-800(2).JPG"}},"yamaha-cr-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥180,000. Highest grade FM receiver developed by in FM technology. The phase correction circuit determined by many experiments and computer-based circuit analysis (CAD method) realizes high stability from ultra-low to ultra-high areas, making positive negative feedback. The power supply circuit is equipped with a large power circuit with good regulation. All other circuits are driven by constant voltage power circuit supply to avoid stable operation. Two-stage protection circuit for power trans and loudspeaker. Also, the loudspeaker protection circuit adopts the unique circuit method of the cable, and the relay works when the DC voltage of the output terminal exceeds ±2V, blocking the signal path to the loudspeaker. This circuit also includes power supply muting, which prevents shock noise when power switch ON/OFF.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"Introduced in 1974 the Yamaha CR-1000 was a high end receiver that was offered in both the U.S. and Japan markets. It was part of Yamaha’s lineup that included the CR-400, CR-600 and CR-800. Pricing in the U.S. was: One significant aspect of the CR-1000 is its surprisingly affordable price, considering all the excellent features it offers. This makes the CR-1000 a truly unique proposition in the world of stereo equipment. The CR-1000 is rated at 70 watts per channel. While this is somewhat low for a top end receiver of the time, Yamaha chose to focus less on power output and more on reducing distortion. This concept was incorporated in their tagline “Natural Sound”. Their marketing quote was: By virtually eliminating IM’s (intermodulation distortion) brittle dissonance, we’ve given back to music what it’s been missing. A clear natural richness and brilliant tonality that numbers alone cannot describe.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CR-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-1000.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-1000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-1000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥95,000. Stereo receiver with MOS FET. The power amplifier part is equipped with a pure complimentary OCL circuit. The power supply unit has a good power generation function. In addition, the voltage is measured from the constant voltage circuit to all circuits except for the power amplifier. This circuit also includes power supply muting, which prevents shock noise caused by power switch ON/OFF. The equalizer amplifier part adopts monocyclic IC, which realizes high S/N ratio and low distortion rate, and has high stability characteristics. Loudness has a Contained Athraudness circuit, which enables you to correct your hearing according to the actual listening environment by installing a tuned knob dedicated to loudness. In this circuit, if you set the loudness snail to the FLAT position and set volume control to the usual position, you can control the volume by keeping the optimal listening balance while increasing the loudness volume from the volume to the 20 dB level down. tone control circuit is a two-stage direct connection between the amplifier and emitter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"The clean and orderly Yamaha CR-600 was a mid range offering from Yamaha from around 1973 until about 1976. It retailed for $460.00 and incorporates Yamaha’s signature Natural Sound technology and is known for a detailed and accurate sound. This era of Yamaha’s has a subtle futuristic look to them with the brushed aluminum face and linear, orderly placement of the knobs and switches. In a dark room the big rectangular dial lens lights up but not too much to be distracting. The rest of the dial face does not have lighting. Both meters are lit. Original replacement bulbs are not easy to find but many have had success with Mouser part # 606-CM2182. They do require some soldering or can be spliced into the existing leads. The CR-600 produces 30 watts per channel though many have bench tested them at around 40 watts per channel so they are most likely under rated.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CR-600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-600.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-600","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥125,000. Two-stage configuration of power trans protection and loudspeaker protection as protection circuit is available. The power trans protection circuit adopts the limiter method by ASO detection, and the playback will not be interrupted only if the protection circuit is operated such as overload. Also, the loudspeaker protection circuit is a method that shuts off the circuit by relay when the output terminal voltage exceeds ±2V, it will be automatically returned if it is within ±2V. This protection circuit also includes power supply muting, which eliminates shock noise when power switch is turned on or off. The equalizer circuit is composed of a four-stage direct connection circuit, and it realizes low distortion and high S/N by design and computer-based circuit analysis (CAD method). The tone control circuit adopts a unique negative feedback (NF) method using a 3-stage direct amplifier. In addition to the low distortion rate, there is no swelling at the middle point of the thrush, and flat frequency characteristics are obtained.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"The Yamaha CR-800 receiver made its debut in 1974 with a retail price of $580.00. It was number 2 in the Yamaha lineup just behind the top of the line CR-1000. It produces 45 watts per channel with 0.1% total harmonic distortion and employs Yamaha’s Natural Sound circuitry for clean and crisp sound. The clean, stark styling and sleek, low profile cabinet give the CR-800 a premium look and feel. The Yamaha CR-800 receiver has a clean, minimalist style typical of Yamaha gear at the time. The main design feature is a big rectangular cutout for the dial that takes up a large portion of the brushed aluminum front panel. Unlike the dark “blackout” dials on a lot of the receivers of the time, the CR-800’s dial has a matching brushed silver finish under a clear window. The FM tuning scale is linearly marked in 0.5 MHz increments. It uses a wide, clear plastic pointer with a thin red line to precisely tune stations.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CR-800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cr-800.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-800","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-800","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-400":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥39,000. Belt drive player developed by inheriting the latest player technology. The belt drive system adopts the belt drive method, which drives 30cm aluminum die-cast turntable by high-precision finish with full dynamic balance. In addition, the YP-700 is equipped with a mechanism, and the player is suspended with its own double float suspension. When the tonearm is mounted on the record surface and the tonearm is pressed, the arm starts to slow down, and the arm starts to turntable automatically. This auto mechanism is mechanical-free during recording, so it does not burden the needle tip or record. Tonearm uses a J-shaped tonearm made of light alloy pipes, making it a simple total mass balance design that suppresses resonance in the arm. In addition, the player panel has a built-in anti-skater mechanism for 1.5g to 2.5g needle pressure. It also comes with a subweight for heavy weight cartridge. The headshell is an EIA standard plug-in, and gold-plated on the left side.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-400.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥98,000. A record player developed using the experience of making players. YP-800 has two variations: YP-800 with SHURE M75EMII cartridge and YP-800CL without cartridge. Turntable is made of aluminum die-cast with a diameter of 31cm. This rubber sheet is specially selected for the hardness of the material to reduce the resonance of turntable, and the shape is carefully examined to make it fit in the best condition with the record surface. 12-pole 24-slot brushless DC servo motor developed for direct drive. This motor is an uns rated electronic control method that performs rotation control in the electronic commutator circuit. The turntable is a mechanism that transmits the rotation of the motor as the constant speed rotation speed (33, 1/3, 45 rpm) of the record.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"bang-olufsen-beogram-6000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥295,000. Record player for 4 channel playback. MMC-6000","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Bang & Olufsen Beogram 6000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram6000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-790":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1975 at ¥47,000. Direct drive Record player with MM type cartridge DL-8. Direct drive system is available for driving. DENON provides high-precision magnetic recording playback method developed for broadcast stations to detect the rotation speed important by direct drive method. The drive motor adopts the smooth AC torque motor of rotation. Speed-adjusted thrush is equipped with a Normal position (click stop). In this position, the internal stable standard voltage will automatically be the exact rotation speed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-790 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-790.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-232":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥47,500. Integrated amplifier designed to emphasize transmission characteristics. This greatly improves the tolerance input of 10kHz or more of conventional problems. Tone circuit is equipped with NPB method with emitter folore in the previous stage. Fast response speed protection circuit protects loudspeaker.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PMA-232 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pma-232.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-255":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥86,500. The power trans of the PNP/NPN80W class is available at the output end of the power amplifier. In particular, the front-stage differential a ification circuit selects the trans and has a separate power supply circuit, which increases the stability by detaching it with a large current drive. Emitter-Emitter negative return circuit is used for equalizer amplifier. This circuit is operated at high voltage of 70V, and the voltage gain is very large when no negative return is applied.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PMA-255 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pma-255.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-350-z":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥62,000. A high-quality integrated amplifier with excellent circuit technology and high reliability parts. This considers that loudspeaker's braking ability is not worse in ultra-low range. This enables stable operation even for many years of use. The ideal circuit constant is selected for the equalizer part. tone control circuit adopts the negative feedback (NF) tone control circuit which uses the good FET of the noise phyg to the intermediate amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PMA-350 Z (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pma-350z.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-500-z":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥87,500. The circuit method adopts the OCL circuit, which is directly connected to the whole unit. High stability with large heat sink and temperature compensation circuit. 2 power supply circuit is available for power supply. Specify low-cut filter and high-cut filter. It is equipped with three-stage switch. PMA-500Z has AU-303 for MC cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PMA-500 Z (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pma-500z.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-700-z":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥145,000. an integrated amplifier developed in pursuit of the concept of Simple is Best. an integrated amplifier usually consists of a pre-stage amplifier section such as an equalizer amplifier, an intermediate control section such as a tone preamplifier, and a final stage amplifier section such as a power amplifier. In the direct-coupling method adopted in the PMA 700 z, the intermediate control section can be disconnected from the main circuit when it is not necessary, and a unique gain switch is provided to avoid unnecessary saturation. When the Toudin Feet and two filter switches are turned off, the signal from the equalizer amplifier and other function inputs only passes through active circuits with good transmission characteristics, such as emitter-follower stages and, if necessary, a + 10 dB booster amplifier, or through a nonreactive attenuator, and is connected to the power amplifier section with flat frequency characteristics in the range from 10 Hz to 150 kHz. This allows for less coloring and less playback sound. The power amplifier section uses a 2-stage Darlington pure complimentary service direct-coupled 2-power supply OCL circuit. DC stability and balance are required for all stages of OCL circuit and complimentary service circuit. However, PMA-700Z uses two differential amplifiers in the driver section to increase DC control capability and obtain stability. In addition, all stages of OCL improve low-frequency characteristics.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-700 Z (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-700z-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-430":{"more":[{"t":"The Harman Kardon 430 receiver was introduced in 1976 along with the 730. It followed in the footsteps of the Harman Kardon 630 and 930 which were released a few years earlier. The 430 puts out 25 watts per channel and has a simple yet elegant design that features some slight changes over the earlier 630 and 930. It retailed for about $325 which was a little pricey relative to other similar stereos. Here is the sequence of Harman Kardon’s release of the 430 through 930 receivers: The Harman Kardon 430 is definitely a classic and features unique H/K circuitry. “Twin Powered” means that each channel has an independent power supply which really enhances performance. So, even though it’s rated at only 25 wpc it can handle most anything you throw at it and still produce outstanding clarity and detail. Harman Kardon said in their ad for the HK 430: As the 430 receiver vies for attention on your dealer’s shelf, it may seem almost diffident. Don’t believe it! For within its graceful contour lies such power as to meet truly demanding conditions – without compromise of sound quality.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Harman Kardon 430","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/harman-kardon-430","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-a-402":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥94,000. Wide dynamic range, broadband of frequency characteristics and low distortion ratio are designed with a focus. Power supply 2 power supply LED level meter enables more accurate response. You can set the sensitivity switch according to the output. Low cut filter, high cut filter, and contour switch to correct the presence at small output.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon A 402 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/a-402.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-citation-16":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥450,000. The amplifier circuit is a DC amplifier structure which greatly improves the low phase characteristics. You can also use the A-class drive with the Complementary Circuit. It can be used as a mono high power amplifier. The power supply section is independent and independent. It can be used for high power drives and guarantees excellent regulation. The peak level indicator is mounted by the LED method. The sensitivity switch can be set according to the output, and the instant output level can be read by changing red (0dB, -3dB), yellow (-6dB, -9dB), green (-12dB, -24dB, -30dB) by color dot display. The protection circuit uses a unique hold-back method to protect the power trans by sensing impedance changes, short circuits and temperature rises.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon Citation 16 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citation16.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-citation-17":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥250,000. preamplifier with audio equalizer. By installing an audio equalizer with a slide type 5 element, it is possible to correct the correction more strict than conventional tone control. The equalizer section uses an active network to obtain accurate f-specific and high S/N ratios. filter is a subsonic filter that is cut by 12dB/oct. Two loudspeaker can be switched on the front panel. Citation17S is a configuration that omits audio equalizer from Citation17. Citation17 has two color variations. The volume control of Citation17 is different depending on the time of production.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon Citation 17 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citation17.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-rabco-st-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥210,000. Record player with linear tracking method. Linear tracking method is available in tonearm section. In this method, there is no tracking error because tonearm does exactly the same linear operation as the cutter head. rolamite bearing is used for vertical operation. It is possible to replace the cartridge which is a problem of linear tracking method. Because the earth terminal is long when the tonearm is removed during the cartridge replacement, it is easy to attach to the main body, and it prevents instantaneous noise. belt drive by DC servo motor. FEATHER-Touch Speed Switch is available. In addition, motor from 33, 1/3 to 45, 45 to 33, 1/3 is prevented by touching the stop switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon Rabco ST-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/player/rabcost-7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-1100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥130,000. This is a stereo integrated amplifier developed with Lordi's technical capabilities, with the goal of creating an amplifier with comprehensive value. The power amplifier uses an inverted Darlington pure complimentary service OCL circuit configuration with two stage constant-current drive emitters to achieve low distortion factor. In addition, the parallel push-pull of the pair transistors with the same characteristics ensures good linearity of current characteristics, and the large capacity power supply realizes faithful transmission from small output to large output. The equalizer stage has a 3-stage configuration with an FET differential amplifier in the first stage. It is driven by ± 2 power supply to obtain large dynamic margin and low distortion. The tone control circuit uses the same 3-stage differential input amplifier as the equalizer circuit, and the final stage is an emitter follower with a constant current load to suppress the degradation of the SN ratio and the fluctuation of frequency characteristics depending on the tone position. With this tone control, you can change the turnover frequency in three stages for both Bass and Treble, so that you can adjust the tone quality to your preference. In addition, you can obtain a flat frequency response with the tone defeat switch. The volume uses a 22-contact switch type attenuator.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HA-1100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/ha-1100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥37,800. Developed with Hitachi's semiconductor technology. The power amplifier part is equipped with the Emitter Ground Inverter Darlington Circuit. In this circuit method, power gain is obtained as conventional as well as voltage gain, so it is possible to use low noise and low distortion monolithic IC which can be used as equalizer in the first stage of the power stage, and realize high S/N. This IC has a built-in differential amplifier, and the medium potential of the amplifier is fixed stably. In addition, the monolithic IC equipped with a three-stage direct amplifier. This IC has a small dynamic range and has a high S/N. Microphone mixing circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-610":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥85,000. an integrated amplifier that realizes low distortion and loose output by gathering Lordi's technological achievements. The power amplifier uses carefully selected transistors for Hi-Fi and consists of a constant-current drive emitter-grounded inverted pure complimentary service OCL circuit. The inverted Darlington circuit is a circuit that can obtain not only power gain but also voltage gain at the power amplifier stage. It also has a large naked gain and provides stable feedback. In addition, since the drive voltage of the driver stage is low, it is possible to use semiconductors that are excellent for noise figures. In addition, the two stage differential constant-current drive suppresses crossover distortion at the time of very small output by constant-current drive of the driver stage, and enables more beautiful reproduction of pianissimo. At the same time, stable drive is possible by differential amplification. The equalizer stage of the preamplifier section has a 3-stage configuration consisting of differential input, FET and bipolar transistor. The circuit is driven by ± 2 power supplies and has a dynamic margin of 280 mV, while accurate elements and sufficient feedback keep the RIAA deviation to ± 0.3 dB.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HA-610 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/ha-610-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ps-38":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥39,800. A direct drive player developed using Lordi's motor technology. The drive section uses an 8-pole 24-slot non-commutator DC servo motor with a direct drive system. In addition, it is equipped with a DC servo mechanism that controls even slight rotational deviation to maintain accurate rotational speed. Electronic control system is used for speed switching and fine adjustment of rotational speed. Fine adjustment of ± 3% of rotational speed is independent of each rotational speed and can be performed by strobe and neon lamps installed on the periphery of the turntable. The power switch and the number of revolutions can be changed by one lever method. As a countermeasure against howling, we have reduced resonance by installing a newly developed large insulator and an arm with rubber vibration isolators in cabinets with large howling margins. The tone arm uses a low center of gravity S-shaped needle pressure direct reading static balance type with excellent tracing capability. In addition, for the sliding of the arm, it is equipped with a dial type anti-skating mechanism which enables stable tracing.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi PS-38 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/player/ps-38-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-cd-4-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥480,000. CD-4 moderator of 1000 series of laboratory designed specifically for commercial use such as studios. The laboratory 1000 series is designed and produced by the selected staff of Victor Lab Center. The characteristics are compensated with all actual measurement data, and some specifications can be changed according to the purpose. In addition, all reliable parts are used, and one resistance is checked. DET BAND CONTROL switch is installed on the rear panel. In the case of this switch in Auto position, the decomposition wave band of the sub-channel is automatically changed according to the input, and sometimes the high-blend operation is added to keep the stable operation without noise. If the switch is in the FIX position, these actions are not performed and locked to the maximum range, so it can be used for recording noise checks and cartridge test. The CD-4 recording circuit is designed to slow the main channel 40μs to correct the delay time of the sub-channel generated by the cartridge and the moderator at the time of decomposition. In addition, in CD4-1000, it is possible to select the delay time in the range of ±25μs by a 11-step switch to consider the variation of the cartridge delay characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC CD-4 1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/etc/cd4-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ja-s-31":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥39,800. Equipped with a merit of components to reduce costs by streamlining production processes. Power pack is available in the output stage. The circuit configuration adopts the pure-con OCL circuit. The preamplifier part is a constant voltage ±2 power supply method, which provides a design that focuses on A-class operation and transient response. The shield wire is designed to reduce the shield wire, and the shield wire is not used in the front panel. The mode selector of 5 positions is also available for checking L, R reverse and single channel in addition to Stereo and Mono. Master volume control with 19 clicks. tone control","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JA-S 31 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s31.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ja-s-8":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥79,800. JA-S5 has expanded and expanded the scale as a development model. The power amplifier part is equipped with a pure complimentary OCL circuit. The equalizer circuit ensures a wide dynamic range and low distortion rate with differential input A-class operation and constant voltage power supply. Also, two constant voltage power supply, plus and minus, especially for wide equalizer steps. volume control The main volume control is a super-linked type that is less than 1dB, and the volume balance of the left and right does not change depending on the opening. You can use it as a 4ch master volume control by adding another 2ch amplifier. Three major protection circuits for automatic return.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JA-S 8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s8.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-jm-s-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥480,000. In addition, all reliable parts are used, and one resistance is checked. The circuit configuration is a cascade-operated input type, direct-connected triple, push-pull and pure-complementary OCL method. 3287cm2x2 It is designed to withstand high power operation for a long time, and it is a compact shape with a chimney effect, which is a super large size that reach 1.5 times of newspaper in the area. The power supply section is equipped with a large troidal contact.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JM-S 1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/jm-s1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-jp-s-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥170,000. The preamplifier was created with the original design concept of Japan Victor, such as the final circuit deter by shielding lines and hearing. The equalizer circuit adopts a three-stage direct connection of 7 stones with differential input A-class push-pull output, and has a total gain of 350mV tolerance input and 40dB due to the high voltage operation of ±59V. This eliminates all shield lines on equalizer substrates from input terminals and prevents time-to-day changes from oxidizing and sulfide of the machine. The volume control is a four-series slide type, which reduces residual noise by narrowing the volume of the output buffer amplifier. Newly developed semiconductor L circuit is used in the SEA graphic equalizer. You can adjust the slide volume control with a 2dB step click. A flat amplifier part other than SEA is composed of an inverter Darlington circuit with excellent frequency characteristics at low distortion rate.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JP-S 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/jp-s7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-jp-v-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥480,000. 4ch preamplifier of the laboratory 1000 series, specially developed for commercial use such as studios. The laboratory 1000 series is designed and produced by the selected staff of Victor Lab Center. The characteristics are compensated with all actual measurement data, and some specifications can be changed according to the purpose. In addition, all reliable parts are used, and one resistance is checked. JP-V1000 is equipped with many functions such as the four-channel SEA controller, and has a control function that supports both two and four channels. In the internal structure, the circuit board is plug-in unitized. Also, the master volume control and selector switches with high frequency are also considered to be able to be replaced by removing each substrate. The output stage is A-class single operation, so there is no crossover distortion seen in the SEPP circuit. In particular, Phono equalizer circuit achieves more than 90dB naked gain by adopting the high voltage operation of ±75V.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JP-V 1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/jp-v1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-2002-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥26,800. KA-2002 It is a simple structure that eliminates circuits such as tone control defeit switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-2002 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-2002a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-3300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥34,500. Equipped with FET differential a ification ICL method. The power amplifier circuit circuit can be connected to all stages. In addition, the large plate has high thermal radiation efficiency and improves stability. In order to prevent shock noise during power supply ON/OFF, the circuit is equipped with a delay start circuit to delay the start of the power amplifier until the preamplifier is upstream stable. There was a wood case with Brazilian rose finish sold separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-3300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-3300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-7300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥65,000. Equipped with power supply to improve dynamic crosstalk. When a large transient signal of bass energy is entered into a single channel of amplifier, such as a powerful pulse collective like a Japanese drum, and a sound signal that is focused on the bass, the power supply voltage will be shaken and a dynamic crosstalk occurs in other channels, causing distortion. tone control section prevents interference by separating and independently circuits/Treble circuits. By adopting the new logic AND circuit,asss control and Treble control can be completely tone jumped. In addition, the direct connection between the input terminal and equalizer is adopted, and the low-level signal from the player has improved the SN ratio and sound quality by eliminating the floating capacity of the wiring.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-7300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-7300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-8300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥78,000. High speed DC integrated amplifier with MC head amplifier. The equalizer amplifier uses the newly developed FET and lowers the impedance of the entire circuit. It is a simple circuit only for equalizer and straight DC amplifier when analog disk playback. Tone preamplifier uses proprietary negative feedback (NF)-CR type with optional amplifier. This circuit is an excellent circuit that does not have gains and does not invert phases. It has the characteristics that it can be inserted anywhere, regardless of the previous impedance. The power amplifier part is a high gain type that absorbs the gain of about 20 dB which has conventional flat amplifier. The circuit configuration is a three-stage direct connection ICL, OCL, and DC power amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-8300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-8300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-9300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥150,000. A complete integrated amplifier using all the audio theory, technology and know-how that can be considered at the moment. This eliminates distortion caused by phase difference caused by capac time constant. 2 power supply We promote our own dynamic cross-talk theory and completely separate power supply from equalizer to power amplifier. The equalizer amplifier part adopts the ICL method by the four-stage direct-connected all-FET which adopts the differential a circuitification circuit at the first stage. It improves phase and improves temperature and distortion characteristics. The Phono1 terminal has a three-stage impedance switch. In addition, the Phono2 terminal has a gain control and can be adjusted with the front panel.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-9300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-9300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kenwood-ka-9300.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-9300.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-9300(1).JPG"}},"kenwood-kr-8040":{"more":[{"t":"Model: Kenwood KR-8040 – 4-channelType: ReceiverYear: 1974Watts Per Channel: 42 (in 4-channel mode)","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-8040","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/kenwood/kenwood-kr-8040-receivers-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"leak-2200":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier that has inherited the tradition since Point One. The power amplifier employs a pure complimentary service OCL stage and a constant current drive class A driver stage. By applying a deep and stable DC NFB, it is designed to operate stably without being affected by temperature changes, load fluctuations, shock noise, etc. A protective circuit is provided to protect the speakers and output transistors in the event of an accident such as output terminal short-circuit or excessive input. A circuit with differential inputs is used for the equalizer stage, and the DC NFB is applied to the overall stage so that it is shock-resistant and stable. It is equipped with functions such as a BTL circuit that can produce monaural output with a single switch, and a speaker matrix switch that can produce a hall tone effect.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Leak 2200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LEAK/amp/2200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-c-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1975 at ¥200,000. A preamplifier using transistors. The equalizer uses a cascode, differential and direct coupling method to improve linearity, stability and signal-to-noise ratio in the high frequency range. In addition, a class A inverted Darlington push-pull configuration is adopted for the final stage so that it is not affected by the load condition connected after the equalizer stage. In addition, a constant current drive is provided at important points to improve the linearity of the transistor itself and to improve the bare loop gain to ensure the full differential function. The intermediate amplifier section and tone control section also employ the cascoded direct-coupled method to improve linearity, stability and signal-to-noise ratio in the high-frequency range. The tone control part uses LUX system negative feedback (NF) type with 3-point switching of bending point frequency, and it is also possible to defeat. The output section uses a two chip emitter-follower circuit, and by using one chip for constant current drive, linearity is improved over a wide band. Highly reliable CAN type transistors are used for all stages, and ± 2 power supply system with constant voltage is used for all stages.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman C-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/c-1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1975 at ¥225,000. M-4000's sister machine was released as a stereo power amplifier. The linearity of the hfe-Ic characteristics of each trans is used to measure stable operation with low distortion rate from large output to small output. In addition, there is an emitter forroa between the pre-drive stage of the A-class operation and the output stage of the B-class operation. The protection circuit is equipped with a DC drift detection circuit that separates and protects the loudspeaker system in the event of a direct voltage of ±3V or higher in the loudspeaker terminal. In the input circuit, 1dB step precision detent volume control is used as a high-grade attenuator for each left and right channels as a level set.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-4000":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1975 at ¥350,000. M-6000 small output model. A triple push-pull configuration that uses six power trans s per channel, which can only be gained in the output stage and has a high fT (high frequency breaking). The emitter folore circuit is set between the pre-drive and B-class operation of the A-class operation. In addition, the output stage of the B-class operation is used as a separate system for the left and right channels, and the power supply supply to the pre-drive stage of the A-class operation is set to voltage. The circuit is equipped to control the lash current when power supply switch is on. As a protective circuit, it is equipped with DC drift detection circuit for loudspeaker protection and abnormal current detection circuit for amplifier protection, heat sink abnormal temperature detection circuit, power trans monitoring fuse fuse fuse detection circuit. The input circuit has 1dB step precision level distent volume control which is the same as the high-grade attenuator for the level set.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-4000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m-4000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-6000":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1975 at ¥650,000. A stereo amplifier that overcomes the drawbacks of conventional large power amplifiers and has achieved excellent characteristics. In addition, the emitter folore circuit is set between the pre-drive stage of the A-class operation and the output stage of the B-class operation. In addition, constant current drive is performed at the required points. The power supply supply is completely separate from the left and right channels. In addition, power supply is equipped with a full-fledged constant-voltage circuit, which is supplied to the A-class operation part up to the pre-driver stage.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-6000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m-6000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-121":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1975 at ¥135,000. Armless player developed with the material unique to the manufacturer aiming for attractive players. 20 pole 60 slots brushless DC servo motor Turntable is made of aluminum die casting. In PD121, it is not only necessary iner mass, but it is designed to weight as much as possible, considering motor bearings, resonance of each spindle and strength. The arm is equipped with a bayonet mounted arm base and is designed to replace various arms with one touch. The arm base comes with the SME standard, and there are other variations such as general, ortophone, and other special, and raw arm base. These are firmly fixed with rubber and wooden frames with damper effect as anti-vibration.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-121 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd121.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-pd-121.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd121.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd121.jpg"}},"luxman-pd-282":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1976 at ¥49,500. A record player with a simple design that flows through PD121 and PD131. The direct drive method is used for turntable. The drive motor adopts AC capac progressive motor, and it keeps motor rotation constant by electronically controlling by servo mechanism. Tonearm has a universal tonearm design. A precision ball bearing is adopted in the horizontal direction, and the horizontal contact ball bearing is adopted in the vertical direction. In addition, the teco-in-side for scanning cellar with a needle pressure of 1g to 3g, the oil damping arm elevation mechanism, a 0.5g-step direct reading counterweight of 0 to 3g, and a lateral balancer that corrects horizontal unbalance, improves tonearm performance and ease of use. The cabinet is made of aluminum hairline finish with the top panel, and it has a slim cabinet that is resistant to hauling by considering the material, thickness and structure of the wooden frame. The cartridge contains a MM type cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-282 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd282.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-r-1500":{"more":[{"t":"The beautiful Luxman R-1500 receiver was introduced in 1975 and on the market until about 1979. It was Lux’s most powerful receiver at the time and the top-of-the-line in their R series of stereos that included the R-600 and R-800. It produces 75 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It has an interesting mix of knobs, switches and push buttons on the front panel and two large meters to the left of the dial scale. What does the R-1500 sound like? Well, some have claimed that it sounds like a Yamaha Natural sound receiver but with better bottom end bass response. The gold / orange backlighting of the Signal strength and FM tuning meters contrasted with the soft white backlighting of the dial scale really adds to the sophisticated look of the R-1500. The meters are very large compared to other receivers of the time. There are a few different versions of the R-1500 including the R-1500E and the R-1500S but they are essentially identical both in looks and performance.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Luxman R-1500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/luxman-r-1500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2250":{"more":[{"t":"This is the 2250B which was introduced by Marantz in 1976 and was really only on the market for about a year. Still, it is a very good mid-range Marantz receiver. I say mid-range because it’s rated at 50 watts per channel but many will attest to the fact that it is under rated and is perhaps closer to 70 watts per channel when fully restored and recapped. On some of the Marantz receivers the “B” designation indicates Dolby but with the 2250’s it’s more of an upgrade designation. The Marantz 2250 is known for problems with its power switch as well as relay failure. It appears as though Marantz remedied these problems in the 2250B with a better designed switch and relay as well as better capacitors. The FM tuner is very sensitive, the low distortion preamp is very good and Marantz used two direct coupled power amplifiers as well. Overall the 2250B is a very well built and good performing receiver. It also had the option of the WC-22 wood case.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2250","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2250-b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2250.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2250-b","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/12/marantz-2250B-left.jpg"}},"marantz-2252":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2252 stereo receiver, produced from 1975 to 1978, is one of the iconic Marantz receivers of the 1970s. With an output of 52 watts per channel and a total harmonic distortion (THD) of 0.1%, this receiver is known for its warm sound signature and quality construction. The 2252 was introduced during the company’s post-Superscope era, which focused on good performance at a consumer friendly price. It retailed for approximately $460 in 1977 and occupied the mid-range tier of Marantz’s receiver lineup, positioned between the 40-watt 2238 and the 65-watt 2265. Unlike the later 2252B, which featured circuit refinements to achieve 0.05% THD, the original 2252 retained a discrete component layout. The 2252 also has the slider balance control as opposed to the 2252B’s conventional knob. Here is a picture of the 2252B for comparison. The 2252’s brushed aluminum faceplate, blue backlit tuning dial, and fluorescent signal meters epitomized the mid to late 70’s Marantz industrial design. Its 440mm width and 137mm height allowed easy integration into stereo racks, while the optional WC-122 wooden cabinet added a bit of warmth to its utilitarian aesthetic The Marantz 2252 competed with Sansui’s 6060 and Pioneer’s SX-850, offering superior tuner sensitivity and more power than the 40W Sansui 6060 but less than the 65W SX-850.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2252","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2252","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2252.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2252","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/marantz-2252-receiver.jpg"}},"marantz-2285":{"more":[{"t":"This is the classic Marantz 2285b. It is one of the more sought after Marantz receivers. Even though it’s only listed at 85 watts per channel it has plenty of power to drive most any speakers. It featured DLB-1 dolby noise reduction as well. It was offered from 1977 up until 1980 and retailed for around $670.00. It weighed in at just over 37 pounds. It has the following inputs: As you can see from the inside picture these units were built like tanks and with a high level of quality. Though not shown in these pictures the Marantz 2285B also came with an optional WC 22 wood case which gave it a fantastic sophisticated look. These receivers sell for quite a bit when restored.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2285","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2285-b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-4400":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 4400 is a classic quadraphonic 4 channel receiver into which Marantz pretty much threw everything they had. Offered from about 1974 until 1978, it pushed out 125 watts RMS per channel into 8 ohms in 2 channel mode and 50 watts per channel into 4 channels which was pretty powerful for a quad receiver. It did this with under 0.15% total harmonic distortion from 20 Hz to 20 KHz. A buyer could all this for the retail price of $1250.00. Marantz also not only incorporated built in Dolby Noise Reduction into the 4400 but gave it six different controls. The tuning section of the 4400 utilized Phase Lock Loop FM Multiplex Demodulation which is a complicated way of saying that it could effectively lock onto an FM channel and hold it. If you bought the Marantz 4400 quadraphonic receiver but really only had 2 channell recordings theyou didn’;t have to worry because the 4400 has what is called Vari-Matrix Synthesis which “synthesizes” 4-channel sound from 2-channel material.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 4400","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-4400","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-mr-215":{"more":[{"t":"Clicking a link to eBay may result in a referral commission being paid if a purchase is made.Loading...","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz MR-215","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/model/marantz-mr-215-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-mc-2120":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo power amplifier equipped with a power guard system unique to Macintosh. The configuration of the MC2125 is almost the same as that of the MC 400 except for the power meter. The Power Guard System is a circuit realized by a waveform comparison circuit originally designed by the Macintosh. It electrically compares the output waveform with the input waveform. When the waveform difference reaches 0.5%, the Limit lamp lights and the Normal lamp goes off. When the waveform difference reaches 1%, the Power Guard circuit operates to prevent clipping of the amplifier, to prevent distortion from reproducing from the speaker, and to protect the speaker. The input and output waveforms are compared by an IC differential amplifier, and the waveform difference due to distortion of the output waveform is converted into a voltage. This voltage is amplified approximately 100 times, passed through a full-wave rectifier circuit, and supplied to a Schmidt trigger circuit. This voltage activates the power guard circuit and activates the power guard circuit when the voltage rises above the level that turns on the Limit lamp.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MC 2120 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc2120-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-mc-2205":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo power amplifier with built-in power meter, equivalent to MC2200 with built-in power meter. Distortion is eliminated by using a low-noise monolithic transistor differential amplifier at the input side of the power amplifier circuit, which provides both input and feedback signals. The next stage circuit is a voltage amplifier circuit with class-A operation. The driver circuit and complimentary service circuit are designed to operate close to class-A to reduce crossover distortion. The circuit is always designed to be moderately biased against changes in temperature. The power transistor is class AB operation and the bias current is secured by a thermistor. The output-stage employs a single-ended para-push method and consists of six highly reliable complimentary service power transistors. Since this circuit is a balanced emitter-follower connection, it has good stability and low distortion. Moreover, the unique output-bias circuit realizes class B operation without crossover distortion.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MC 2205 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc2205-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-a-800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥69,900. NIKKO's know-how is introduced to achieve the highest quality. The power amplifier is equipped with a Pure Complementary OCL circuit. The two-stage differential a circuitification circuit adopted in the first stage is equipped with a zener diode to perfect the temperature compensation and achieve stable operation. The protective circuit adopts pure electron type, and the relay and fuse are combined. The relay is set to work when the DC component of about 2V is spread to the output terminal and protects loudspeaker and the output trans. In addition, there is a muting yesterday at power supply ON, and it prevents the occurrence of unpleasant shock and transient distortion when ON/OFF. tone control circuit has a low impedance modified BAX circuit. Both Treble andasss can switch the turnover frequency to three stages.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko A 800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/a-800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-4500":{"more":[{"t":"In 1979 Onkyo introduced the Onkyo TX-4500 MKII. It retailed for $479.95 and was the mid range offering in their lineup. Onkyo took the design of their TX-4500 stereo and optimized it, renaming it the TX-4500 MKII. I see a lot of variation regarding the watts per channel specifications. According to the Onkyo TX-4500 MKII service manual, number 3046, the wattage is 60 watts per channel RMS at 8 ohms, both channels driven. It also produces no more than 0.1% total harmonic distortion. So, those are the numbers I’ll go with. The earlier TX-4500 is listed at 55 watts per channel. As a comparison the top of the line TX-8500 MKII listed at $1000 and produced 160 wpc.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-4500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-4500-mkii","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sa-6300":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier with standard configuration and Pioneer's traditional amplifier design technology. The power amplifier section employs an all-stage direct connection OCL circuit that eliminates all interstage capacitors from the first stage to the last stage. In addition, the characteristics are improved by carefully selecting the transistors to be used and combining PNP-NPN with good matching pair characteristics. An IC is used for the equalizer, and a 3-stage direct connection circuit configuration with differential amplification at the first stage is used. By using differential amplification in the first stage, the DC stability of the circuit is improved and the operation is stabilized. At the same time, the cancellation effect is obtained against temperature change, power supply fluctuation, and mixing of noise components. In addition, the 3-stage direct-coupled circuit allows sufficient DC NFB to be applied to the differential part, so that the distortion component is suppressed over a wide band. Both Bass and Treble use an 11-point tone control with a Klix/Klukš top. To improve sound quality at low volume, a Loudness Contour is also installed.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-6300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-6300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sa-6300.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-6300-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-6300(2).JPG"}},"quad-405":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥180,000. A compact design that considers home use and has a power of 100W+100W. This amplifier adopts the current damping circuit which applied feed forward theory. This method detects and corrects input and output signal difference (distortion) on the bridge circuit. Small output amplifier is A-class operation, it generates distortion signal and reduces distortion by canceling distortion caused by high amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Quad 405 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/QUAD/amp/405.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-3300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥39,800. This integrated amplifier is based on the concept of focusing on sound quality, with power and sound quality adjustment function. All stages are directly connected OCL circuit with ± 2 power supply system without harmful coupling condenser. In addition, the differential amplifier, which is the core of this circuit, uses dual transistors with uniform characteristics and excellent stability, and achieves highly stable operation even against DC fluctuations. Power transistors of the same polarity (NPN-NPN and PNP-PNP) are connected to the complimentary service stage, and pure output system is adopted. The equalizer circuit uses a PNP-NPN2-stage direct-coupled circuit that combines a low-noise transistor and carefully selected equalizer elements. The tone control section uses a 2-stage direct-coupled tone amplifier with carefully selected transistors and a CR-type tone control circuit with highly accurate elements. The knob uses a Klix/Klukš top type that can be adjusted in 10 stages each. Equipped with a microphone mixing circuit with a microphone level adjustment function. Mixed sound can be output from the recording terminal.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-3300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-3300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-3300.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-3300-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-3300.JPG"}},"sansui-au-6600":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier has been developed taking over the basic performance of the advanced AU 7700. By using a back panel with a unique structure, the input terminal is mounted facing up and directly connected to the equalizer board at the shortest distance. This eliminates the use of shielding wires, which degrade the high-frequency characteristics, and improves the SN ratio. In conventional amplifiers, the chassis was used as a common ground for each circuit, but this affected the sound quality due to current interference. The AU 6600 provides one point grounding near the equalizer amplifier to improve sound quality. The first stage of the power amplifier section employs a pure complimentary service OCL circuit directly connected to all stages. To maintain the 0 VU potential of the output point, a highly stable differential amplifier and bias compensation circuit are employed. The drive stage is composed of three stage Darlington connection with carefully selected transistors. In addition, a large heat sinker is installed in the lower part of the input terminals on the back panel, and as a result of putting it out of the amplifier, the heat radiation effect becomes good, and large output with allowance is obtained.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-6600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-6600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-6600.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-6600-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-6600.JPG"}},"sansui-au-7700":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier was completed by making full use of experience and technology in high-grade components. The rear panel structure consists of a phono circuit and input terminals that face upward and are connected directly to the equalizer amplifier board at the shortest distance. This eliminates the need to use shielding wires, which cause degradation of high-frequency characteristics, and realizes a high SN ratio and good sound quality with high-frequency characteristics. The printed circuit board of the preamplifier, rotary switches, lever switches, and various volumes are directly attached to the integrated structure. This prevents failures such as poor connection and improves reliability. With the chassisless structure, one point grounding is implemented to suppress current mutual interference. The power amplifier consists of a 3-stage Darlington drive stage with a differential amplifier circuit at the first stage and a parallel push-pull type power stage. The parallel push-pull system combines four power transistors with the same characteristics per channel, and the linearity of current characteristics is good. The pure complimentary service circuit directly connected to all stages has excellent phase characteristics, large negative feedback is applied over a wide band, and flat frequency characteristics are obtained.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-7700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-7700-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-9900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥140,000. This integrated amplifier has improved audio characteristics and operability by adopting a unique chassis structure. The AU 9900 has a partitioned layout with the preamplifier and tone control located on the front panel side, and the power and power supplies such as heat sinker and power transistor located on the rear side. As a result, each function and operation are integrated into a single integrated amplifier an independent state, reducing mutual interference. The input terminals for players and other devices are installed on the front right side panel, and the output terminals for speakers are installed on the left side panel, so that the signal flow can be smoothly amplified along the shortest path. In addition, the input terminal, selector switch and equalizer amplifier are close to each other, reducing the shielding wire and preventing the degradation of high-frequency characteristics due to stray capacitance. The power amplifier section uses a fully connected pure complimentary service OCL system with a differential-amplifier circuit at the input stage. The output stage employs a parallel push-pull circuit that provides sufficient power at a low distortion rate. The input circuit of the equalizer section consists of two amplifiers, a flat amplifier and an equalizer amplifier, with a differential amplifier circuit using dual transistors.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-9900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-9900-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-ba-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥89,800. A stereo power amplifier using a vertical power FET for audio as an amplifying element. A newly developed vertical power FET is used for the output stage. Since the vertical power FET has excellent linearity especially in a large current region, the input and output signals are proportional to each other even when a large amplitude signal is added to the gate. In addition, the BA-1000 operates as a source follower, which further reduces distortion and enables amplification with excellent linearity. It also has a self-controlling function against heat generation, has no temperature drift, and is resistant to thermal destruction. Moreover, it is suitable for driving a reactance load such as a speaker with a wide safe operation range. In addition, since the slope of the maximum output curve with respect to the load impedance is gentle, a large output can be obtained even at high impedance. In addition, considering the characteristics of a speaker in which the impedance rises near the lowest resonance frequency, this element is suitable for driving. This vertical power FET is available in N-channel and P-channel types, making it possible to construct a pure complimentary service circuit with low distortion and excellent characteristics.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui BA-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/ba-1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-ba-1000.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/ba-1000-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/ba-1000.JPG"}},"sansui-ba-3000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥190,000. High power and low distortion rate was developed as a basic idea. It is the output stage of the Pure Complementary OCL circuit. Use 6 trans s per channel to get a large output. We provide heat sinker with unique chimney effect for heat dissipation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui BA-3000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/ba-3000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-ba-5000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥390,000. A stereo power amplifier developed as a highly reliable high-power amplifier by introducing the latest circuit technology and new materials everywhere. The power amplifier consists of two differential stages with active load and two drive stages. 8 power transistors per channel are used for the output-stage quad parallel push-pull, pure complimentary service system. In addition, the buffer amplifier in the preceding stage is composed of three elements using differential amplification for the input circuit. Phase inversion in mono operation is combined with relay, and high power of 600W is realized in mono operation. The power supply uses a toroidal transformer with a capacity of 1 kVA with good regulation and low leakage flux. The left and right wires are independently wound to prevent influence between channels and obtain good regulation. In addition, with the exception of the output stage, a stabilized power supply is supplied to the buffer amplifier and the drive stage to provide more margin. Equipped with auto trans-type output transformer.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui BA-5000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/ba-5000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-1350":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥33,800. Belt drive and player system with smart mechanism. A 4-pole motorronus motor with very little vibration developed specifically for turntable. 30cm aluminum die cast is available for turntable. A new rubber sheet that suppresses harmful vibration of the record board is adopted, and the record board is designed to match the rubber sheet. static balance universal tonearm. The bearing part uses precision pivot bearings to measure high sensitivity, and the support part is supported by damper, making it a highly vibration resistant design. Equipped with an in-side for scanning cellar. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge. Equipped with auto-cutting mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-1350 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-1350.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-1350.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-1350.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-1350.JPG"}},"sony-ps-6750":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥74,800. Direct drive player system with magnetic disk servo. The magne disk servo button is used for the servo motor. This increases servo detection accuracy. The turntable adopts a die cast of precision die-casting with deadning, reducing the resonance sharpness. SBMC is used in cabinet. This SBMC is a thermosetting resin that contains calcium carbonate and fiberglass based on polyester resin. The strength is 1.5 to 2 times the strength of wood (rawan plywood), and the resonance sharpness (Q) has an excellent feature of less than 1/3 of aluminum die casting. This reduces howling and improves SN ratio. The turntable sheet has an oil damping type insulation mat.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-6750 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-6750.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-8750":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥168,000. Direct drive player system with crystal lock or magnetic servo. Crystal lock servo mechanism is available to avoid the problem of rotation speed accuracy. The servo motor detecting unit is equipped with the magnetic disk servo method which introduces the technology of Sony Magnescale precision measuring machine. Moreover, because the servo response range has expanded significantly, it has obtained good load characteristics and wow-flotter characteristics that improve the servo effect. It is equipped with an electronic brake, it is not only a stop operation but also a brake when45 from 45 rpm to 33 / 1 / 3 rpm. Because it is an electronic brake, it is impossible to bear the mechanism part. Speed can be switched by pitch control. Because the crystal lock effect is large, the pitch control operation is done by removing the crystal lock.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-8750 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-8750.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-8750.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-8750.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-8750.JPG"}},"sony-str-7025":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥57,800. AM/FM stereo receiver with improved operability. We adopt new junction FET for FM front end to improve reception ability. The frequency linear varicon is used to make more accurate adjustments by dialing equal intervals. The AM tuner section contains a solid state filter. 2 power supply direct coupling method is available in the power amplifier section. tone control circuit Built-in microphone amplifier for mixing. Equipped with a loudness switch and filter switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony STR-7025 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/str-7025.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-str-7035":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥67,800. We adopt new junction FET on FM front end to improve reception ability. In the AM part, the solid state filter is used. The power amplifier is equipped with a hybrid power IC2 power supply direct coupling method. tone control circuit Built-in microphone amplifier for mixing. Equipped with a filter switch that removes scratches and scratches, as well as a loudspeaker switch for simultaneous or single use of loudspeaker and two sets of loudspeaker.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony STR-7035 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/str-7035.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-1700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥36,800. The circuit has an ITL-OTL circuit. It is equipped with a stereo/monomode switch. High-cut filter and loudness switch are supplied. The loudspeaker switch can be connected to two lines of loudspeaker.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-1700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-4650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥84,800. V-FET integrated stereo amplifier. Nch and Pch V-FET are all stages of pure complimentary SEPP OCL circuit and DC amplifier. LEC trans and V-FET for small signals. Aiming to be faithful waveform transmission, we are adopting the DC amplifier to be a flat amplifier. Equipped with a muting switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-4650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-4650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-5650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥99,800. V-FET integrated stereo amplifier. The equalizer stage adopts V-FET for ultra-low noise LEC trans and small signal with linearity characteristics. Direct coupling and DC unit amplifier are available to aim for the design policy of the ES-II series.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-5650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-5650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-tae-5450":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥89,800. V-FET stereo power amplifier developed by inheriting the technology of TAE-8450, which is the best ES-II series. The equalizer amplifier part, the tone preamplifier and the flat amplifier part, respectively, are unit amplifier. This unit amplifier reduces distortion by adding a buffer to two differential steps. The first step is dual FET, and the next step is differential amplifier. This unit amplifier is essentially a DC amplifier that has no time constant on the return circuit. By adopting this unit amplifier, it has excellent characteristics not only low distortion rate but also from the DC to high range, and phase distortion is also reduced. The equalizer amplifier uses a dual FET, which reduces malformed harmonic distortion. High-precision attenuator level control is available for volume control. This is a 2dB step-type control with high-precision printing technology and silver-sintered sliding control of the resistor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TAE-5450 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/tae-5450.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-tan-5550":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥87,800. V-FET stereo power amplifier developed by inheriting the technology of TAN-8550, which is the best ES-II series. V-FET is a power FET that has a vertical structure, while the conventional FET is a yoko-shaped structure, it realizes a vertical structure with its own manufacturing method and selective oxidation method. In addition, because the N-channel and P-channel complementary element are obtained, the pure complementary output stage can be configured, and the phase reverse circuit is unnecessary, so the signal of the A-class stage is given to the B-class stage as it is, and the sound with low distortion is obtained. The high input impedance and low output impedance characteristics make it possible to demonstrate V-FET power without affecting the circuit before and after. Because the heat source is dispersed, the safety of the element is high, and it is possible to make it light and compact. The V-FET protection circuit is equipped with a PC limiter combination load impedance detection circuit with a very fast response electronic circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TAN-5550 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/tan-5550.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-5150":{"more":[{"t":"FM/AM stereo receiver with FM/AM tuner. The main amplifier section uses a direct-coupled differential amplifier OCL circuit IC. The tone control circuit reduces distortion by using the negative feedback (NF) circuit of the main amplifier. It is equipped with a loudness switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SA 5150 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/sa-5150-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-9200":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo power amplifier with 4-stage output impedance switching. The output impedance can be switched to 4 levels of 0.08 Ω (normal), 0.8 Ω, 2.7 Ω and 8 Ω. The circuit is bridge type with no gain change. By changing the output impedance, the damping factor can be changed and the performance of the speaker can be further extracted. In the case of an 8 Ω speaker, it can be switched to 100, 10, 3 or 1. The circuit configuration of the power amplifier section is based on a differential-amplified full-stage coupled complete complimentary service OCL, and various devices are devised to realize low distortion and high stability amplification. An emitter follower is inserted in the next stage of the differential amplifier to increase the amplification degree of the first stage to improve the SN ratio and optimize the impedance matching up to the pre-drive stage to prevent the generation of distortion. In the predrive stage, the bootstrap capacitor is removed to improve low-frequency stability, and the output stage stability is also improved. The power supply unit uses a constant voltage power supply of ± 42 v for the voltage amplifier stage and a large capacity transformer and 10,000 μ F capacitor for the output stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-9200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-9200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-9600":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo power amplifier that employs a constant voltage power supply drive for all circuits including the output stage. Equipped with 3 types of protection circuits: power supply, current, and temperature. Equipped with an output impedance 4-stage switching switch, an appropriate damping factor can be set according to the speaker. Equipped with a peak output direct reading power meter equipped with 3-step range switching. A radiator fin with a label is also used to inform the temperature change.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-9600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-9600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥69,800. Direct drive player developed with Technics know-how. Direct drive is available in the drive section. In addition, SL-1300 is integrated with turntable, and the fixed part is integrated with the case. This eliminates the need for stacking case, motor and turntable to improve performance and reliability. The tonearm bearing part adopts high sensitivity gimbal suspension method using precision pivot bearing. It has excellent trace performance coupled with the proper effective mass setting and the precision and light weight of the auto mechanism. The headshell uses a die-cast shell, and gold-plated terminals. Start cut is possible by operation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-sl-1300.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1300.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1300.JPG"}},"technics-sl-1400":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥59,800. servoD.D player with unique integrated D.D motor and B/FG servo circuit that realizes one-chip IC. The world's first D.D motor IC (AN630) circuit is equipped with one-chip motor drive unit, control unit and various functions. The B/FG (Back Electro Mo Force Frequency Generator) method is used to detect the speed to accurately maintain the rotation speed of the motor. Motor has a unique integrated D.D motor. In addition, the rotation part of the motor is integrated with turntable, and the fixed part is integrated with the case, and the stacking of the case, motor and table turn is unnecessary, so performance and reliability are improved. Equipped with a smart return mechanism, the detection mechanism is working at the end of the performance, and tonearm automatically returns to the left and the power supply of the player is cut. The cartridge uses an elliptic needle to avoid more faithful traces. High-sensitivity tonearm for high compliance cartridge performance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1400.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥49,800. Record player with direct drive. The direct drive method is used for the drive part, and the motor rotation part is integrated with turntable, and the fixed part is integrated with the case. Turntable has a tapered edge for easy removal of records. It has an independent rotation speed adjustment mechanism for each 33, 1/3 and 45 rpm. MM type cartridge Tonearm is equipped with a gimbal suspension method.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-20":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥26,800. belt drive player with FG servo DC motor. FG servo DC motor The FG servo circuit has a built-in coil for frequency detection inside the motor, which converts this frequency to a DC voltage proportional to the motor rotation speed. And this voltage is measured from the standard voltage oscillator and the difference is sent to the motor drive circuit to keep the motor drive voltage constant. SL-20 uses an IC equivalent to 21 trans s in the FG servo circuit. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge. In order to enhance the overall performance of the pick-up process, MM type cartridge is the world's first structure that combines cartridge and shell. This makes it compact and lightweight, and has enough strength while improving the effective mass of the finish. The compatibility problem between cartridge and shell is also eliminated.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-20 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-20.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-3150":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier developed based on the same design concept as the SU-3500 and 3200 series. The main amplifier uses an all-stage direct-coupled OCL circuit that guarantees stable output and damping factor, and the output-stage uses a complete complimentary service configuration to reduce harmonic distortion and intermodulation distortion. The first stage differential amplifier circuit uses a carefully selected pair transistor with the same characteristics. In addition, a zener diode is used for constant voltage to improve circuit stability. The Zener diode for circuit stabilization and the Zener diode inserted into the power supply of the differential amplifier suppress the shock sound generated when the power supply is turned on / off. The equalizer circuit consists of two stages directly connected. High voltage and low noise PNP transistor is used for the first stage and high voltage and low noise NPN transistor is used for the second stage. In addition, a wide range of cartridges can be used by ensuring a large dynamic range by raising the power supply voltage with two power supplies (plus and minus). The tone control circuit uses the negative feedback (NF) circuit of the main amplifier section to control the tone by attenuating the feedback amount from the speaker output terminal to the first stage operation amplifier by frequency.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-3150 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-3150-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-3500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥86,800. an integrated amplifier that improves circuit stability with a constant voltage power supply of ± 40 v. The EQ circuit is a 3-stage direct-coupled circuit configuration using a differential-amplified 2-power supply system with a pure complimentary service SEPP output stage. In addition, the input impedance can be switched in 3 levels of 25k Ω / 50k Ω / 100k Ω. The main amplifier section is composed of a pure complimentary service OCL circuit connected to all stages. In addition, the power supply voltage is lowered and two 10,000 μ F electrolytic capacitors are used for the output stage to pursue low distortion rate and high stability. The tone control circuit is negative feedback (NF)-type and equipped with a tone defeat switch that instantly restores the characteristics. Uses a preset volume that can also be used as an audio mute. Two tape decks can be connected. Equipped with two Phono terminals.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-3500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-3500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-7600":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo integrated amplifier with fully discrete power amplifier. The power amplifier is a discrete type using low-noise and low-noise transistors. The OCL circuit consists of an all-stage direct-coupled differential-amplified complete complimentary service OCL circuit. An emitter-follower is inserted at the latter stage of the differential amplification to improve matching with the latter stage and to reduce distortion at the time of small signals. A specially selected IC is used for the equalizer circuit to achieve low noise and high stability. The circuit configuration is 3-stage direct connection system. The tone control method has succeeded in reducing frequency fluctuations and increasing the range of tonal changes. The electric field capacitor in the power supply circuit has a high withstand voltage of 40 v and a large capacity of 10,000 μ F. The Master-Level control uses a 41-point step type for precise fine adjustment.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-7600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-7600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-8600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥79,800. an integrated amplifier that further pursued the dynamic distortion introduced in SU-10000 and SE-10000. In order to improve the stability of the power supply part and suppress transient distortion, the ± 6 power supply system is adopted and the accuracy of parts is improved. The output stage of the tone control circuit and the pre-drive stage of the main section use a constant current load that combines a transistor and a diode. This ensures constant current even when voltage changes, and provides stable performance with little gain change or distortion. A constant voltage power supply of ± 6 power supplies enables highly stable operation even at the time of Tsutomu Dainyu. The equalizer circuit consists of two stages directly connected, differential amplifier and modified SRPP output stage. The selective use of low-noise transistors also improves the SN ratio. The main amplifier consists of differential amplification, emitter-follower, voltage amplification, and output stage. The dynamic characteristics are improved by adopting a stabilized power supply of ± 4 power supply, using a high-permeability core and a power transformer with good regulation by increasing the diameter of the winding, and using 15000 μ f electrolytic capacitor.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-8600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-8600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-9200":{"more":[{"t":"Control center for a wide range of cartridges by capacitance switching circuit, etc. In addition to the resistance of the equalizer circuit, it is also possible to change the capacitance of the equalizer circuit. This improves the performance of the cartridge and allows playback with excellent characteristics. There are three levels of resistance and two levels of capacitance. The Phono2 is also equipped with an input sensitivity adjustment function. An allowable input of 520 mVrms is achieved by the high power factor of the output stage and the constant voltage power supply of ± 42 V. The constant voltage power supply provides a stable voltage even when the primary AC line voltage changes, eliminating interference through the power supply. The output-stage consists of a differential-amplifier circuit using a low-noise PNP transistor at the first stage, and the output-stage is a 3-stage direct connection structure with a perfect complimentary service SEPP circuit to suppress the occurrence of crossover distortion and switching distortion. Equipped with 11 contact rotary switch type negative feedback (NF) tone control.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-9200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-9200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-9600":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo preamplifier that uses a constant voltage power supply for all circuits. The two Phono inputs can switch impedance in three stages. The input sensitivity of Phono2 can also be continuously variable in the range from 1 mv to 3 mv. negative feedback (NF) type tone control circuit of differential amplifier configuration is mounted. Equipped with Acti-Blow high filter.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-9600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-9600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥400,000. Preamplifier developed to maximize the performance of stereo power amplifier B-I. C-I was developed at the same time with B-I, but it took much more time to complete because it was a very complex configuration. The circuit of C-I is composed of two types of amplifiers, which have the signal path all stages of FET. The unit amplifier A and unit amplifier B are designed for FET and is designed for the first time by FET.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-400":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥55,000. The monolithic IC is used for equalizer amplifier. The power amplifier part adopts the fully-directed Pure Complementary OCL circuit, and the axial amplifier output is pulled out with a push-pull, and the A-class driver step is driven by constant current. In addition, the loudspeaker protection circuit works in case of abnormal DC voltage in the output terminal due to some trouble. The equalizer amplifier adopts the monolithic IC of the middle emitter/follower type three-stage direct connection circuit. In this circuit, dynamic margins are also sturdy because they are driven by the +30V constant voltage while taking the first gain.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-400.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥140,000. Record player with direct drive. Turntable is 310mm in diameter and 2.4kg in weight. Also, the resonance of the turntable itself is prevented, and the resonance of the turntable is eliminated by using a face contact method to the joint with direct drive motor. In addition, the rubber sheet section is embedded with rubber rings designed for materials and shapes that fit the contact surface of the record. The direct drive method is used for the drive, and the motor is equipped with a 20-pole 60-slot brushless DC servo motor developed specifically for the fono motor. This eliminates mechanical reduction mechanisms such as rim drives and belt drives. In addition, the pitch control mechanism of ±6% variable is independently equipped to each rotation speed of 45/3 and 45 rpm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-301-c":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥31,500. Simple design record player. Turntable is equipped with 30cm aluminum die cast turntable. In addition, the belt drive method is used for the drive method, and the 4 pole beltronus motor is used for the drive motor. Tonearm has a S-shaped pipe arm. This arm has a lateral balancer. The cartridge contains the M75 series of Shure. Built-in semi-auto mechanism. Silver gray and castor finish.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-301 C (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-301c.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-yp-301-c.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-301c.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-301c.jpg"}},"yamaha-yp-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥49,000. A high-end belt drive player developed for mania. Turntable is made of zinc alloy turntable with iner mass 300kg/cm2. This turntable is made of a method that tries to fully balance the dynamic balance by giving feedback to the mold. It adopts belt drive method, and the drive motor is equipped with a smooth AC servo motor with no cosmos. The exclusive double-float suspension is available. In this method, the motor is first floated to the exclusive cabinet and player panel, and the turntable and arm are integrated. This double suspension mechanism is double blocked motor vibration. YP-600 introduces high viscosity silicon oil damping in this suspension, making it effective for the absorption of harmful vibrations.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-d-51":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥49,000. A record player with FG servo on the servo mechanism and omitting the auto stop mechanism. Motor has a newly developed high torque coreless slotless DC hole motor. This makes the cosmos very low and has strong torque. A quick FG servo system is available to respond to sudden load ctuations. The FG servo frequency detector adopts a magnet pattern and a coil that is placed throughout the motor circumference to detect the eccentricity and the pitch error of the pattern, making it more accurate and stable control. Turntable is made of aluminum cast 1.8kg. Tonearm uses a 4-point full gimbal support system to achieve the initial sensitivity of 7mg horizontally and vertically. Also, the arm body has a long type of aluminum arm. The arm base has a zinc die-cast base.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-D 51 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d51.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-d-71":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥59,000. FG servo is available for servo circuit. FG servo is a structure that controls the rotation speed of FG (Fr encyGenerator), which generates a frequency proportional to turntable rotation. YP-D71 has a FG that detects the rotational speed and is installed on the outer circumference of the motor, making it difficult to understand the eccentricity and the pitch error of the detector. In order to increase the rotation accuracy increased by FG servo, we adopt the quartz lock PLL servo. This quartz lock PLL servo is a method that controls the gap between the reference signal generated by the frequency from FG and the crystal oscillator. This makes turntable’s rotational accuracy higher to the crystal oscillation frequency accuracy, which shows very good stability such as load ctuations, voltage ctuations, and temperature ctuations. Also, in the area where the quartz lock is removed, FG servo is designed to work, and when the constant speed is reached, the lock indicator is lit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-D 71 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d71.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"adc-accutrac-4000":{"more":[{"t":"Record players equipped with functions such as universal selection and remote control. It is equipped with a unique program selection mechanism. For example, it is possible to freely select 3rd-7th-1st-6th. In addition, 24 programming can be done at once by programming repeatedly. You can remove all memory with Clear button when you program incorrectly. Also, if you want to remove only one song from the program, press the Reject button when it is the song. Since tonearm is automatically canceled even if the 8th button is pressed with a record that contains only 7 songs, it will not drop in abnormal position. Press the Cue button to stop playing. Once again, I will start playing again.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – ADC Accutrac 4000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ADC/player/accutrac4000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/adc-accutrac-4000.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ADC/player/accutrac4000.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ADC/player/accutrac4000(2).jpg"}},"denon-dp-6700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥140,000. Record player with analog parts sold separately. Turntable DP-6000 DA-307 is a dynamic damping tonearm. The appearance is leather-plated.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-6700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-6700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-poa-1000-b":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥395,000. Stereo power that pursues the limits of performance and functional beauty as a tube sphere amplifier. The ultra-low phase compensation circuit is inserted in case of large negative feedback. The driver stage is composed of cathode followers using low internal resistance, high plate loss and high pressure double triode 12BH7A. It is directly connected between the power tube 6GB8, and it makes the operation of the AB2 class of 6GB8 smoothly. High-volume NFB and multiple negative feedback systems ensure good performance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon POA-1000 B (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-1000b.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-poa-1001":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥178,000. A single push pull pursuing a large output. This reduces crosstalk and pursues more ideal stereo playback. The Pc150W class bipolar trans is used for the output stage. Each power trans is fixed to a heat sink with a heat resistance of 0.8°C/W, which suppresses temperature rise and increases stability. The power supply section is powered by Orient Core. Measures the peak meter of multiple compression.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon POA-1001 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-1001.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pra-1000-b":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥270,000. Preamplifier pursuing the limit of performance as a tube ball type amplifier and the extreme of function beauty. We have carefully selected ECC-83, a twin triode tube made by Telefunken, which is the smallest of the flicker noise in the entire inspection of the internal and external electronic tube. This 6DJ8 operates at a high plate supply voltage of 350V and has a high sampling level of 60Vrms. The booster amplifier part is based on the minimum 12 dB required for gain, tuner, tape deck, etc. The NFB has a deep NPB of 30dB and has been working to improve the characteristics of the NFB. It compresses the dynamic range of equalizer amplifier. In addition, the gain control switch of 10dB2 steps is installed just before this.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PRA-1000 B (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pra-1000b.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pra-1001":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥139,000. The preamplifier was developed by reexamine function, performance, operability and design. All trans s are equipped with a low-noise high-pressure epitaxial type. When each input terminal is not connected, it is short circuit to the earth and prevents the occurrence of unpleasant noise. In addition, Phono2 input is equipped with an impedance switch, so you can select the impedance suitable for cartridge. The Rec out terminal has a Complementary SEPP buffer circuit, which prevents negative impacts from connected decks and cables. The volume control part adopts a special structure with 21 clicks of volume control that does not affect L/R, which greatly improves crosstalk.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PRA-1001 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pra-1001.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"dual-cs-621":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥79,000. Direct drive player with dual-tradi straight arm. CS-721 Tonearm has a straight arm with headshell and arm. It eliminates resonance on the joint part of the universal type headshell by using the integrated structure. In addition, cartridge replacement can be done by sliding the finger arm of the shell horizontally, and it does not force the branch point. By using a straight arm, it reduces the effective mass, and tonearm uses special polymer materials for aluminum and headshell. The support mechanism provides four-point gimbal support using ball bearings. The new motor is equipped with a control circuit using C-MOS IC.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Dual CS 621 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/cs-621.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/dual-cs-621.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/cs-621.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/cs-721(3).jpg"}},"hitachi-ha-330":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥39,800. Low filter Two tape decks can be connected to each other. Equipped with loudness switch. Equipped with loudspeaker A/B switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-330 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-330.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-5300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥59,800. amplifier amplifier amplifier The power amplifier is equipped with the Dyna method. In this method, the peak of the music signal is large output, and usually it works as a small output, and it realizes the same operation as a large output amplifier. This achieves the weight reduction of the amplifier and the expansion of the safety operation area, lower cost and lower distortion rate. In HA-5300, we have 4 power supply of ±25V as low voltage and ±57V as high voltage, achieve effective output 75W+75W and peak power 150W+150W, and we have 2 times more dynamic margin than normal amplifier. The power amplifier part is equipped with two-stage mirror circuit. This prevents the output signal of the cartridge from degrading by the input capac. In order to correspond to the sound quality change due to the difference in the load capacity of the cartridge, it is equipped with a load capacity switch function.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-5300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-5300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hca-8300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥60,000. This is a stereo preamplifier developed to be paired with a power amplifier of the dynamic harmony system. The equalizer circuit section adopts a 3-stage connected 7-chip configuration of first stage FET differential-PNP differential-constant current drive NPN. The coupling capacitor uses a capacitorless (ICL) system for the input and a non-inductive metallized polyester film capacitor with superior high-frequency characteristics for the output to improve the frequency and phase characteristics. In addition, low-noise FETs and high-voltage low-noise transistors are used to provide sufficient feedback for stability over a wide band to improve various characteristics. The tone control circuit adopts a 3-stage direct connection 6-chip configuration of PNP push-pull with a first stage FET differential low-current drive, and realizes low distortion factor by using carefully selected low-noise FETs and high-voltage low-noise transistors. In addition, the tone volume is lost at the center, and a method is adopted in which the tone quality can be continuously changed without waviness. In addition, the volume can be adjusted separately on the left and right by the 2-axis volume, and the sound quality can be corrected by changing the turnover frequency or by the tone defeat switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HCA-8300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hca-8300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hma-8300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥140,000. This is a stereo power amplifier that adopts Dynaharmony (E-class drive) system. The dynamic harmony method is a circuit method that efficiently realizes a large output of the amplifier through analysis of the level distribution of music. It works as a large output at the peak of the music signal, usually as a small output, and effectively operates as a large output amplifier. This reduces the weight of the amplifier, expands the safe operation range, reduces the cost, and reduces the distortion factor. The power section adopts the Dynaharmony system and consists of ± 2 power sources for each of low voltage power source and high voltage power source (total 4 power sources), thereby realizing large output. Class A driver circuit uses a current mirror circuit for power stage drive. It is equipped with an external magnetic meter that can directly read the peak output level by the value of power. It is equipped with a subsonic filter that eliminates harmful vibrations outside the audible band caused by sleds of records. This filter can be turned on and off as needed.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HMA-8300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hma-8300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ps-48":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥49,800. Autoplayer with new Unitorque motor. The drive system adopts direct drive method, and the drive motor is equipped with a newly developed Unitorque motor. The Unitorque motor is composed of 8 poles of donut-shaped rotary magnets and 2 sets of star-shaped flat coils with 22^5 °. The torque generated from these two coils and magnets is always constant and stable rotation is achieved. Also, Unitorque motor has high reliability with a simple structure of brushless slotless coreless. tonearm has a low gravity tonearm. VM type cartridge. Equipped with autoplay mechanism. Oil damping arm reflector Equipped with anti-skating mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi PS-48 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ps-48.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ps-58":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥59,800. A full automatic player with the newly developed Unitorque motor. The drive system adopts direct drive method, and the drive motor is equipped with a newly developed Unitorque motor. The Unitorque motor is composed of 8 poles of donut-shaped rotary magnets and 2 sets of star-shaped flat coils with 22^5 °. The torque generated from these two coils and magnets is always constant and stable rotation is achieved. Also, Unitorque motor has high reliability with a simple structure of brushless slotless coreless. VM type cartridge. Oil damping arm reflector Equipped with anti-skating mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi PS-58 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ps-58.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/hitachi-ps-58.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ps-58.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ps-58(3).jpg"}},"jvc-ja-s-11":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥29,800. Equipped with the basic characteristics of all circuits for faithful waveform transmission. In particular, equalizer adopts a monolithic IC with 12 stones per channel. Two-system tape terminals are available for mutual dubbing. One unit is mounted on the front panel. Wood case is sold separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JA-S 11 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s11.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-ja-s-11.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s11.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s11.JPG"}},"jvc-ja-s-41":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥56,500. Power supply emphasizing design. The power supply part is a completely separate structure for A-grade amplifier and B-grade amplifier. This suppresses distortion caused by moving (drift) of the A-class voltage amplifier. The volume control adopts four twins and volume control, which suppresses the residual noise of the preamplifier cable during the volume and increases the sense of hearing S/N. The equalizer circuit effectively reduces noise generated from the preamplifier part by putting volume control in two places after the tone control circuit. The phono stage has a three-stage casscode structure with a newly developed low noise FET. ICL circuit without input capac is realized by setting the first stage as FET. One of the two tape terminals is installed on the front panel. Cover is included when not used.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JA-S 41 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s41.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-5500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥49,800. ICL and two-stage direct-connected two-stage power supply structure make it possible to improve equalizer stage characteristics. The circuit configuration is ±2 power supply. The protection circuit is equipped with ASO detection limiter and relay double protection circuit. The equalizer amplifier is equipped with a ±2 power supply method using a low noise amplifier. The CR element is a low distortion tone control that is in the NFB circuit, and the CR element of the NFB circuit is removed in the tone-feet position, and it is a buffer that is excellent in DC stability and phase characteristics. It is equipped with independent power meter which can read output directly.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-5500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-5500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kenwood-ka-5500.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-5500.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-5500(2).JPG"}},"kenwood-kr-3600":{"more":[{"t":"The Kenwood KR-3600 receiver was one step up from the bottom of the line KR-2600. Both the KR-2600 and the KR-3600 utilized slightly lower grade components relative to their upper end brothers the KR-5600, KR-6600 and the top of the line KR-9600. They had JT-FET transistors as opposed to the better MOS-FET and SIL-IC in the amp circuit instead of the Dual Range Operational Amplifier used in the larger models. Still, the KR-3600 is a good receiver. It’s 22 watts per channel can fill a room with sound. It has the signature styling of the mid 1970’s Kenwood stereos with fat push buttons and a big weighted tuning knob. It also has the basic features any music listening would need with a high filter button, loudness control, tape monitoring facilities, a protection circuit and connections for two sets of speakers, a tape deck, phono, auxiliary jack as well as headphones. The dial face has the beautiful Kenwood blue and amber glow to it and incorporates a dual purpose signal strength tuning meter as well. The KR-3600 was introduced in 1974 and was on the market until around 1978.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-3600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-3600","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-5600":{"more":[{"t":"Produced from 1976-1978 the Kenwood KR-5600 was one of Kenwood’s mid range receivers. Above it were the KR-6600 and the monster KR-9600. Below were the KR-4600, KR-3600 and entry level KR-2600. The KR-5600 retailed for around $250.00. The KR-5600’s blue lamps and wood side panels make it a very nice looking receiver. It’s rated at 40 watts per channel at 8 Ohms. Kenwood had a history of making fine Ham radio equipment so the tuners in their mid to late 1970’s receivers are excellent. The KR-5600 is built well. It has direct coupled amplifier stages and a fully complimentary power output stage.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-5600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-5600","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-6600":{"more":[{"t":"The Kenwood KR-6600 was introduced in 1976 and was part of Kenwood’s KR-X600 lineup that included the KR-3600, KR-4600, KR-5600, KR-6600, KR-7600, and KR-9600. The KR-6600 was obviously an upper mid range offering from Kenwood and it had an adequate amount of power and features for the average user. The KR-6600 is a nice looking receiver, especially with its optional wood cabinet which has unique venting slots edge to edge on the top. Most of the KR-6600’s you’ll see for sale do not have the wood cabinet but instead a black metal case. Kenwood’s mix of lighting and knob layout make for an aesthetic front panel. The meters are back lit by actual orange bulbs which was unique at the time. Of course, finding orange replacement bulbs today isn’t so easy. The dial face is black with nice blue backlighting for the tuning scale. The tuning needle has a red bulb at the tip which some people refer to as the ‘ball of fire’.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-6600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-6600","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kenwood-kr-6600.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-6600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/06/kenwood-kr-6600-wood-case.jpg"}},"kenwood-kr-7600":{"more":[{"t":"Kenwood receivers have a distinct look about them with their mix of blue, red and amber lights. Such is the case with the Kenwood KR-7600. Add the silver face plate and black dial face and you have the very recognizable look of the 1970’s Kenwood receivers. While the KR-7600 was not their top of the line receiver, that would have been the KR-9600, it was at the higher end of the performance spectrum. It retailed for around $270.00. The KR-7600 was introduced in 1976 and was rated at 80 watts per channel. Its build quality is very good as it was produced just before Kenwood started cutting some production corners in the late 70’s. At first glance the 7600 looks like it has large heat sinks on the side of the unit but these are, in fact, just for decoration. One of the unique features of the KR-7600 is the mic input.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-7600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-7600","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kenwood-kr-7600.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-7600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/05/kenwood-kr-7600-front.jpg"}},"kenwood-kr-9600":{"more":[{"t":"The Kenwood KR-9600 is one of the best receivers ever made by Kenwood. In fact, it’s one of the better tuners ever made by anyone. Manufactured from 1976 to around 1978 and with an MSRP of nearly $800 the KR-9600 was Kenwood’s flagship receiver. It puts out a massive 160 watts per channel into 8 ohms with only 0.08% total harmonic distortion. It also features dual power supplies, a FET differential amplifier phono input and state of the art tuner design. In fact, the KR-9600 is popular among audio enthusiasts who modify it to bring it up to modern specs and turn it into a fantastic tuner even by today’s standards. It actually has two separate phone EQ’s to accommodate different cartridges. They are switchable from the front controls. It has two step loudness control, 3 speaker system capability, ASO (Area of Safe Operation) protection circuit, dual power meters and triple tone controls.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-9600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-9600","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-b-12":{"more":[{"t":"The power amplifier is designed to be a mono power amplifier. Triple push-pull connection is used in the output stage. It is a design that uses heat sink as a part of the front design. The power supply section is equipped with a large troidal contact.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman B-12 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/b-12.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-c-1010":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1975 at ¥180,000. trans and preamplifier mounted on C-1000 successor. Basic circuit configuration and function style are almost the same. tone control","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman C-1010 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/c-1010.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-c-12":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1977 at ¥125,000. DC preamplifier with thin design. All amplifier circuits are DC enabled. And the output circuit with constant current circuit is included. The flat amplifier part is a circuit amplifier that combines the output circuit with the emitter folore with constant current to the same DML-IC as equalizer amplifier. By adopting our own DML-IC, we deal with the occurrence of DC drift due to changes in external conditions such as temperature. The chas layout is used for all angles, and the input circuit is routed in the shortest course by eliminating the shield of the signal path. In addition, all circuits that are basic as equalizer part and amplifier part are placed on a single board, and it realizes excellent frequency characteristics and S/N ratio, stability and cross-talk characteristics by fully separating between left and right channels. The volume control is a continuous variable type, but it is very accurate, there is little interlocking error between the left and right channels, and the new volume control is improved sound quality.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman C-12 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/c-12.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-cl-350":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1972 at ¥79,000. The first preamplifier with trans. CL350 has a unique amplifier for your input terminal and select the input terminal only on the output circuit side. tone control: LUX tone control In addition, the curved point frequency is three-stage switchable, and fine sound quality can be adjusted. This circuit has a deft switch and you can also skip the circuit if not used. High-cut filter and low-cut filter have two cut-off fre cies, minimizing the impact on the program source and enabling noise reduction.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman CL 350 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/cl350.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-cl-350.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/cl350.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/cl350.JPG"}},"luxman-l-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1977 at ¥128,000. A thin integrated amplifier developed in pursuit of density as an amplifier. In order to deal with DC drift due to changes in external conditions such as temperature, DML-IC is adopted. In addition, the output stage is notch distortion in power amplifier by making circuits such as AB-class operation. In order to improve crosstalk characteristics and overall distortion rate, lines that handle large currents such as loudspeaker wiring are arranged at the shortest distance, and it is not crossed between the left and right. In addition, the power amplifier circuit board also separates the left and right channels, and the sounding circuit relay and the loudspeaker terminal are also considered to be independent.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman L-10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/l-10.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-12":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1977 at ¥150,000. Stereo power amplifier. Parallel push-pull method has a small current per trans, which provides excellent wide-area properties and improves linearity for current. It also has features such as Pc can be enlarged. DML-IC is available for power amplifier circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-12 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m-12.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-1600":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1976 at ¥146,000. Stereo power amplifier with full-line pure complimentary circuit. High capacity power trans is available in the output stage. Level meter The wood cabinet is made of rosewood.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-1600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m-1600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-mb-3045":{"more":[{"t":"8045G The output tube uses the 8045G of the lux brand, and the AB1 class push-pull operation has 60W output. The output power supply is equipped with GX100-3.6 developed for 8045G.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman MB 3045 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mb3045.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-272":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1977 at ¥69,000. PD121/PD131 Direct drive system is available for driving. The drive motor has a brushless & slotless flat type DC servo motor. Tonearm has a straight type static balance tonearm. This arm is designed to enhance rigidity by integrating the cartridge shell and tonearm to reduce the resonance of tracability. The dust cover is equipped with a dust cover of acrylic boards, which is suitable for the hauling characteristics. The weight is applied to the player's body when the dust cover is closed. The flutter mat has a shape that fits perfectly with the record.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-272 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd272.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2215-b":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced in 1973 the Marantz 2215B receiver is one of the classic “baby” Marantz stereos. It originally retailed for around $250 but came down in price until its last year on the market in 1977. It only produces 15 watts per channel but they are a sweet 15 watts. Many people will tell you that the early smaller Marantz receivers sound better than their higher powered receivers. The Sound of Marantz is the compelling warmth of a Stradivarius. It is a dancing flute, a haughty bassoon and the plaintive call of a lone French horn. The sound of Marantz is the sound of beauty. While that statement might be a bit overdone, most owners of the 2215B do say that its all solid state design has a surprisingly warm and smooth sound. While the bass isn’t extremely heavy it is adequate when paired with efficient speakers.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2215 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2215b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2215-bl":{"more":[{"t":"Clicking a link to eBay may result in a referral commission being paid if a purchase is made.Loading...","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2215 BL","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/model/marantz-2215bl-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2216":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2216 was one of Marantz’s lowest powered units at 16 watts per channel. It’s sometimes referred to as a “baby” Marantz. It was produced from 1977 until about 1980 and retailed for roughly $240. It has the classic Marantz silver face styling and the centered Balance control slider. The build quality of the 2216 is excellent. The tuner section boasts a Phase Locked Loop FM Stereo Demodulator, ceramic filters in the IF amplifier section, a three gang tuning capacitor and FET RF amplifiers. The 2216 also has the gyro touch tuning wheel that Marantz is famous for. There is also a 2216B unit which is different in appearance with a Balance control knob instead of a slider and Speaker selector buttons instead of a knob. Of course all Marantz receivers are popular these days and even the lower end models like the 2216 are no exception.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2216","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2216","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2216.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2216","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/marantz-2216-left.jpg"}},"marantz-2225":{"more":[{"t":"This is the classic low power Marantz 2225. Yes, it only puts out 25 watts per channel but, in this case, that’s a good thing. The lower powered Marantz receivers are known for their great warm sound. Some think that the higher powered Marantz units are a little too muddy due to excessive bass. But, each to their own ears. The 2225 was produced from 1976 to about 1977 and retailed for about $350.00. I’ve seen estimates that show around 8000 of these stereos were made. The reality is that the 2225 is underrated and is the dark horse of the 22XX line from Marantz. Bench tests have shown it to produce closer to 30 watts per channel.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2225","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2225","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2226":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2226 is one of the great low powered Marantz receivers. At 26 watts per channel it’s not a powerhouse but the lower powered Marantz receivers are known for their sweet sound. Marantz introduced the 2226 in 1977, at a retail price of $329.99, and it stayed on the market until 1979. The 2226 has no more than 0.3% total harmonic distortion and a damping factor of 45. It’s direct coupled amplifier design provides very high damping factors at low frequencies and great low frequency response. The 2226 came with a simulated wood grain vinyl covered metal case but the purchaser had the option to buy the WC-122 wood cabinet if they wanted. The tuning section has a dual-gate MOSFET FM front end and 3 gang tuning capacitor. It’s a sensitive and very quiet tuning section. It utilizes a phase locked loop (PLL) FM demodulator, and ceramic IF filters and IC amplifier system.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2226","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2226","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2235b":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2235B made its debut in 1977 with a retail price of $449.95. It is a 2-channel, all solid state stereo and was positioned towards the lower end of the Marantz lineup. The 2235B features a sensitive FM tuner, a highly selective AM tuner, a low distortion preamplifier and two direct coupled amplifiers. The FM tuner uses an FET front end, ceramic IF filters, and a phase locked loop multiplex decoder. The AM tuner features an advanced integrated circuit and ceramic IF filters for high selectivity and sensitivity. It has connections for two pairs of loudspeakers, a turntable, two tape recorders, stereo headphones, and an auxiliary source such as an additional tuner, CD player or a TV sound source. The 22xx series of receivers from Marantz are generally considered to be some of the best looking solid state receivers of all time. The 2235B is no exception. The brushed aluminum faceplate, black lettering, and blue dial scale set against a blackout panel are iconic.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2235B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2235b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2238":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2238 was introduced in 1976 and retailed for around $360. As the model number implies it produces 38 watts per channel at 8 ohms. It’s a 2 channel solid state receiver in the mid range of the Marantz offerings. It also has the classic Marantz styling with the silver face plate and gyro touch tuning wheel. The WC-122 wood case was also an option with the 2238. It measures 17 5/16 x 5 3/8 x 14 3/8 and weighs in at just over 26 pounds. The Marantz 2238 is a Direct Coupled design which provides wide power bandwidth, excellent low frequency response and superior damping. It also incorporates a highly sensitive dual gate MOSFET FM front end and Phase Locked Loop (PLL) FM stereo demodulator. These result in low distortion levels, superior noise reduction and excellent stereo separation.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2238","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2238","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2240-b":{"more":[{"t":"Clicking a link to eBay may result in a referral commission being paid if a purchase is made.Loading...","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2240 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/model/marantz-2240b-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2250-b":{"more":[{"t":"This is the 2250B which was introduced by Marantz in 1976 and was really only on the market for about a year. Still, it is a very good mid-range Marantz receiver. I say mid-range because it’s rated at 50 watts per channel but many will attest to the fact that it is under rated and is perhaps closer to 70 watts per channel when fully restored and recapped. On some of the Marantz receivers the “B” designation indicates Dolby but with the 2250’s it’s more of an upgrade designation. The Marantz 2250 is known for problems with its power switch as well as relay failure. It appears as though Marantz remedied these problems in the 2250B with a better designed switch and relay as well as better capacitors. The FM tuner is very sensitive, the low distortion preamp is very good and Marantz used two direct coupled power amplifiers as well. Overall the 2250B is a very well built and good performing receiver. It also had the option of the WC-22 wood case.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2250 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2250-b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2500":{"more":[{"t":"This is one of the more powerful Marantz receivers ever made. It’s the Marantz 2500. It is somewhat rare and was produced from 1977 to 1979. It retailed for around $1600.00 and was eventually replaced by the 2600. The 2500 put out 250 watts per channel in to 8 ohms and was second only to the 2600 at 300 watts. The Marantz 2500 utilized a massive toroidal dual wound power transformer. This accounted for a large portion of the 2500’s 60 pound weight and the fact that it had a cooling fan in the back. Still, given its weight it was not a huge receiver and only measured 19.25 x 17.25 x 7 inches which, compared to other monster receivers, was not that large. It was probably the first of the awe inspiring receivers.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-mc-2125":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo power amplifier equipped with a power guard system unique to Macintosh. The Power Guard System is a circuit realized by a waveform comparison circuit originally designed by the Macintosh. It electrically compares the output waveform with the input waveform. When the waveform difference reaches 0.5%, the Limit lamp lights and the Normal lamp goes off. When the waveform difference reaches 1%, the Power Guard circuit operates to prevent clipping of the amplifier, to prevent distortion from reproducing from the speaker, and to protect the speaker. The input and output waveforms are compared by an IC differential amplifier, and the waveform difference due to distortion of the output waveform is converted into a voltage. This voltage is amplified approximately 100 times, passed through a full-wave rectifier circuit, and supplied to a Schmidt trigger circuit. This voltage activates the power guard circuit and activates the power guard circuit when the voltage rises above the level that turns on the Limit lamp. The Limit lamp is designed to light up when the amplifier is overloaded, and is lit for a visible period of time, even when the overload condition is very short.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MC 2125 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc2125-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-mc-2200":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo power amplifier with a unique power guard circuit, equivalent to the MC2205 without a power meter. Distortion is eliminated by using a low-noise monolithic transistor differential amplifier at the input side of the power amplifier circuit, which provides both input and feedback signals. The next stage circuit is a voltage amplifier circuit with class-A operation. The driver circuit and complimentary service circuit are designed to operate close to class-A to reduce crossover distortion. The circuit is always designed to be moderately biased against changes in temperature. The power transistor is class AB operation and the bias current is secured by a thermistor. The output-stage employs a single-ended para-push method and consists of six highly reliable complimentary service power transistors. Since this circuit is a balanced emitter-follower connection, it has good stability and low distortion. Moreover, the unique output-bias circuit realizes class B operation without crossover distortion.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MC 2200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc2200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-dd-10":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki DD-10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/dd-10-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-dd-100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥250,000. Direct drive player with 40cm turntable. DD-100 has a separate control box. Turntable is 40cm in diameter and 5.2kg in size. This turntable makes iner mass as large as possible by making it a structure with mass on the outer circumference as much as possible, and has gained the rotational force which is not affected by changes in the external load resistance. The iner mass of DD-100 has reached 1,500kg/cm2. The motor bearing of the drive mechanism is equipped with an interchangeable type. In order to value the shaft, we select the material that is easy to wear, and wear about 0.1mm for about 1,000 hours.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki DD-100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/dd-100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-ddx-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥138,000. Armless player that eliminates the traditional player system concept and pursues functionality. The neon lamp has a dedicated oscillator. The oscillation frequency is 33 1/3 (81) and 45 (60) rpm. The player's frame adopts its own three-point support structure, increasing the stability of the system.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki DDX-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/ddx-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/micro-seiki-ddx-1000.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/ddx-1000.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/ddx-1000.jpg"}},"mitsubishi-da-a-10":{"more":[{"t":"Feature series power amplifier. Uses 2-monaural construction in which power supplies for left and right channels and 2 monaural amplifiers are configured on the same chassis. As a result, the channel separation has been greatly improved by suppressing the mutual interference from the power supply. Uses a symmetrical complimentary service 3-stage Darlington OCL circuit and a differential-amplified 2-stage current mirror drive system. A 3-stage Darlington circuit with a large DC current amplification factor and a current mirror circuit with a high gain, a target drive and a low distortion are used to enable a low distortion factor. By combining a current mirror drive and a transistor with excellent high-frequency characteristics, pulse rise characteristics and high-frequency distortion characteristics are improved. The power supply circuit uses two 200 VA power transformers and two 63 V, 10000 μ Fx2 power supply capacitors. A huge heat sink of 0.35 ° C / W per channel is installed externally. As a result, the cooling effect is very high and the junction temperature of the power transistor can be kept sufficiently low for use.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-A 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-a10-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-a-15":{"more":[{"t":"Feature series power amplifier. The power supply for each left and right channel and two monaural amplifiers are configured on the same chassis. As a result, the separation between channels is improved by eliminating mutual interference from the power supply and time coupling and electrostatic coupling in the high frequency range. Uses a symmetrical full complimentary service 3-stage Darlington OCL circuit and a differential-amplified 2-stage current mirror drive system. A 3-stage Darlington circuit with a large DC current amplification factor, a high-gain symmetric drive, and a low-distortion current mirror circuit combine to enable a low distortion factor. By combining a current mirror drive and a transistor with excellent high-frequency characteristics, pulse rise characteristics and high-frequency distortion characteristics are improved. The power supply is equipped with two 250 VA power transformers and a 70 V, 12000 μ Fx2 electrolytic capacitor. A heat sink of 0.35 ° C / W per channel is installed externally. As a result, the cooling effect is high and the junction temperature of the power transistor can be kept sufficiently low for use.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-A 15 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-a15-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-m-10":{"more":[{"t":"A power meter to be used in combination with a DIATONE power amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-M 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/etc/da-m10-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-p-10":{"more":[{"t":"Feature series preamp. The power supply for each left and right channel and each unit amplifier are of a separate monaural configuration for the left and right channels, and the volume and switches are used with sufficient consideration for separation. This improves the separation. In addition to improving the separation by minimizing the number of auxiliary circuits that cause sound quality degradation, a constant voltage power supply is used for the power supply at the heart of the amplifier to eliminate interference between the circuits. The tone circuit uses a current mirror circuit with high voltage amplification, symmetric drive and low distortion, and the filter circuit uses an inverted Darlington emitter-follower circuit to achieve low distortion. A low-noise transistor developed by Diatone is used in the first stage differential amplifier stage of the equalizer amplifier to obtain an input equivalent noise of -126dB (V) (IHF, A-curve correction). A variable resistor with a unique switch is used for the tone control, and the time constant circuit is completely disconnected in the flat position to obtain a flat frequency characteristic. The tone control volume is provided separately for the left and right channels to improve the separation, and the sound quality can be adjusted separately for the left and right channels. A muting circuit using a reed relay is adopted to prevent noise when the power switch is turned on and off.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-P 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-p10-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-dp-ec-1":{"more":[{"t":"A record player that achieves both basic performance and automatic mechanism by introducing EC (Electronic Control) system. In order to maintain high basic performance even after automation, we have adopted a non-contact arm position detection mechanism that does not apply any side pressure to the arm. Since the arm lifter is designed to operate while detecting the state of the arm lifter (whether the arm is up or down) and the position of the arm within the horizontal drive without contact, automatic operation is possible from any position. In addition, manual operation is possible without switching between auto and manual operation except when the arm is moving with auto. The system uses a reflector to detect the size of a record. In this system, a reflector (prism) emits light from obliquely above the record, guides the light to a sensor corresponding to each record size, and sends the output from the sensor to a logic circuit to determine the size of the record. This size detection mechanism automatically determines the needle down position, performance end position, and turntable rotation speed during automatic performance. A true black switch is used for the control knob. The automatic mechanism is controlled by an IC-based logic circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DP-EC 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-ec1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-7075":{"more":[{"t":"Mention a Nikko receiver and you’ll find opinions on both sides of the aisle with regards to build and sound quality. Most will agree that they are great looking receivers and they do have a nice clean look to them. In fact they look a little like a Kenwood. They were made in Japan from about 1976 to 1980 and were intended to be lower priced high margin unit for retailers. In other words you’d go in to the audio store to look at a Pioneer and you’d get led over to the Nikko and they would try to sell you that instead. Happened all the time with house brand audio components as well. Still, from what I’ve heard, some of the Nikko receivers really do sound good and will last for years. This is the Nikko 7075. It puts out 42 watts per channel and retailed at $400.00.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Nikko 7075","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/nikko-7075","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-9095":{"more":[{"t":"The Nikko 9095 was the top-of-the-line receiver from Nikko in 1976. It retailed for $519.95 and was part of a lineup that included the 2025, 3035, 5055, 6065, 7075, 8085, and 9095. Nikko was not a very well known brand in the U.S. and the receivers are not that common today. The brochure for the 9095 had some interesting wording: You have just approached an exciting new dimension in stereophonic listening enjoyment; With your purchase of the NIKKO 9095 Stereo Receiver, you have secured a measure of “Daily Happiness” for yourself and your family. NIKKO, translated means ‘‘Daily Happiness” … and translate it does; takes broadcast electronic impulses and translates them into a special brand of music … pleasureful listening for every musical taste. Nikko equipment of the 1970’s is regarded as well built and a great value in terms of performance and looks. Nikko also made a really good line of separates under the Alpha/Beta/Gamma series name in the very early 1980’s. In the late 80’s they were purchased by ASTI Corp and the build quality went down until they stopped making audio equipment in the 90’s.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Nikko 9095","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/nikko-9095","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-c-201":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥180,000. Professional preamplifier for all FET configuration. CR type has a surface that can not be expected to have a good effect on S/N ratio and dynamic range, but C-201 uses low-noise FET and low-noise metal film resistance, etc., to achieve superior S/N ratio by carefully selected components. A circuit design that emphasizes naked characteristics has gained FLAT characteristics to ultra high fre cies. We also use the characteristics of the FET element itself to measure low distortion rate.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko C 201 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/c-201.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-c-203":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥80,000. All FET preamplifier with FET. In C-203, we focus on naked characteristics to operate the element in the best condition. This improves naked properties and improves physical properties with NFB. The volume control uses an attenuator type four-unit volume control to improve the S/N ratio. In FET, the narrowness of the dynamic range, S/N ratio, distortion rate, etc., which is the fault that comes from the nature of the element itself was a problem. In order to overcome this, the C-203 equalizer amplifier part adopts the newly developed high-pressure FET and uses a high pressure of ±70V and a vacuum tube circuit to ensure a robust dynamic range. Flat amplifier circuit is a low-noise all FET configuration with differential input and two-stage direct connection. Tone amplifier circuit has negative feedback (NF) type. Also, it is equipped with a de-feet switch and can fly tone circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko C 203 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/c-203.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-m-110":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥380,000. A flagship stereo amplifier with AC-DC switch. The M-110 has a continuous output of 100W+100W with all stages A-class operation, and it can work as DC amplifier. DC amplifier t is not allowed to change the center voltage when input is not allowed for external circuitctuations such as temperature, and it is affected by circuit configuration and parts used. We consider naked characteristics from all aspects to minimize NFB. In addition, it is possible to reduce low distortion characteristics and residual noise by comparing all power supply as a constant voltage circuit. All power supply parts are constant voltage.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko M 110 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/m-110.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-m-204":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥120,000. DC stereo power amplifier with all-stage A-class operation. By using the circuit operation method as A-class operation, it eliminates notching and crossover distortion caused by B-class operation. In the first stage, we use a dual FET with excellent temperature characteristics, which suppresses DC current ctuation of output for temperature change, etc., and achieves DC amplifier at the same time. The power amplifier is a triple push-pull configuration of the Pure Complementary connection so that the power amplifier has a two-stage darlington connection with a spare pre-drive tier that flows the drive current to the left side. In addition, the drive stage has the advantage of A-class amplifier using full-scale powerbilization power supply.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nikko M 204 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NIKKO/amp/m-204.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-cp-700m":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥41,800. Player-based and tonearm. The drive method is direct drive, and the motor is equipped with 8-pole 24-slot DC servo motor. Turntable is 1.6kg. Tonearm uses ultra-precise bearings, which are highly sensitive and reliable. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge. cabinet has a dual ated cabinet. This is a structure that supports tonearm and motor. It suppresses harmful vibrations to the signal transmission system in conjunction with the general 10.5kg weight design. CP-700M and CP-700MR have different appearance finishes. CP-700MR","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Onkyo CP-700M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ONKYO/player/cp-700m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-8500":{"more":[{"t":"Onkyo’s contribution to the Monster receiver genre is the Onkyo TX-8500. It was Onkyo’s top of the line receiver at the time and put out an under rated 150 watts per channel into 4 ohms and 110 watts per channel into 8 ohms. This line of Onkyo receivers including the TX-2500, TX-4500, TX-6500 and TX-8500 are all under appreciated units. The build quality, performance and features are all second to none. Onkyo was a little late to the scene with their monster receiver so it didn’t receive the fanfare that the Pioneer and Marantz receivers received at the time but it is easily comparable. A later MK II version was released that had a digital tuner along with the analog tuner. As you can see below it is fairly easily distinguished from the original TX-8500 shown above. The TX-8500 does not have an Aux input though it does have 3 Tape inputs so you shouldn’t be short inputs. The amplifier section is one of the best around and the tuning section is no slouch either.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-8500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-8500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/onkyo-tx-8500.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-8500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/onkyo-tx-8500.jpg"}},"pioneer-m-22":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer M-22 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/m-22-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-m-25":{"more":[{"t":"This stereo power amplifier was developed based on the design concept of \"Magni-wide Power Range,\" which requires full power reproduction with low distortion over an ultra-wide band as well as within the audible band. In order to enable low-distortion full-power regeneration in the ultra-high frequency range, we have developed and adopted a group transistor RET (Ring Emitter Transistor) with superior high-frequency switching characteristics. This transistor consists of hundreds of low-power transistors with superior high-frequency characteristics that are synthesized in parallel. This transistor is designed to increase the breakdown strength and power consumption without compromising the high-speed switching characteristics of the low-power transistors. Structurally, it is an epitaxial planar transistor, named ring emitter transistor because the emitters are arranged in a toroidal ring around the base electrode. Compared with conventional power transistors, RET has excellent switching characteristics, good signal response, and low carrier accumulation. A DC amplifier configuration is adopted to ensure sufficient power at the minimum distortion rate even in the ultra-low frequency range. Since the DC amplifier configuration does not have a capacitor in the NFB circuit, it eliminates transient distortion and phase distortion to the ultra-low frequency range.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer M-25 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/m-25-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-570":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥59,800. Full automatic player with SH/Router coreless motor. PL-570 is a full-automatic player with auto- -in auto-return auto-cut auto-repeat without touching tonearm. In addition, the START/STOP lamp flashes and warns when the start switch is pressed while the tonearm is fixed to the arm clamp. After a certain period of time, the lamp disappears automatically. SH/Router coreless motor is used for drive motor. And it servos turntable rotation by increasing the naked characteristics of the previous motor to servo.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-570 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-570.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-1050":{"more":[{"t":"Another of the silver faced Pioneer line the Pioneer SX-1050 was the little brother to the giant SX-1250 in 1976 and 1977. While it may not necessarily be considered a “Monster” receiver it is close. It weighs in at just over 50 pounds and has many of the features of the top of the line SX-1250. It’s rated at 120 per channel into 8 ohms as compared to the SX-1250 which was rated at 165 watts per channel. There were some fairly significant differences between the lower end Sx-850, SX-950 and the SX-1050. The SX-1050 incorporated a large toroidal transformer, a huge power supply with step-start circuit and two large capacitors, a step attenuator volume control, a shielded multi-gang tuning capacitor, and a well improved FM tuning section as well. So, the SX-1050 is really far more comparable to the SX-1250 then it is to the SX-850 and SX-950. It retailed at around $700.00. The Pioneer SX-1050 was eventually replaced by the SX-1080 in 1978.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-1050","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1050","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sx-1050.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1050","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/10/pioneer-sx-1050-back.jpg"}},"pioneer-sx-1250":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-1250 remains one of the most coveted receivers ever made. Released in 1976 with a $900 price tag, it represented everything Pioneer had learned about crafting high-end audio equipment. This wasn’t just their flagship model – it was a statement piece that showed what was possible during the golden age of stereo. The design alone tells you this is something special. From its brushed aluminum face to the warm amber glow of its display, every detail was carefully considered. The faceted control knobs feel perfectly weighted in your hand, while the walnut cabinet adds a touch of warmth to all that precision engineering. Decades later, the SX-1250 still turns heads. The late 1970s marked the peak of the receiver wars, when companies like Pioneer, Marantz, and Sansui were locked in an arms race to build the most impressive equipment possible. The SX-1250 was Pioneer’s answer to this challenge – a receiver that combined raw power with exceptional build quality.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-1250","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1250","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-450":{"more":[{"t":"The smallest receiver in the Pioneer lineup during the mid to late 70’s was the Pioneer SX-450. These entry level receivers were only rated at 15 watts per channel but were still built with quality materials and craftsmanship. Sure, there were fewer features then the bigger receivers had and vinyl veneer instead of wood but the SX-450 is still a good receiver for a second system or garage stereo. It will hold its own in a smaller room but tends to lack the power for a larger room. Made from about 1977 until 1979 the SX-450 retailed for just under $200.00 and, as you can see, it has the usual late 70’s look that personified the Pioneer receivers of the time with the silver face, beveled knobs and “wood” case. Inside it has the usual great Pioneer build quality. It is small so it only has 40 capacitors and 8 lamps. The Pioneer SX-450 isn’t something that audio collectors are going to fight over but they still have a market. Anyone interested in vintage audio on a budget would be wise to try one of these receivers before spending a large amount of money on a more expensive unit.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-450","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-450","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-550":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-550 is one of the smaller receivers that Pioneer produced. It is the successor to the SX-535 and produces a whopping 20 watts per channel. It was introduced in 1976 and was discontinued in 1978. It has the standard styling of the late 70’s Pioneer SX line with the silver face and faceted knobs. It had wood side panels but the top panel was made of metal. Early on it had a list price of nearly $250.00 but dropped to around $200.00 in 1977. This made the SX-550 a very affordable unit for someone on an audio budget. Of course the lower retail price came at the expense of local production as Pioneer outsourced its manufacture to the Republic of Korea. It weighs roughly 21 pounds and measures 18 x 15.5 x 12 inches.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-550","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-550","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-5580":{"more":[{"t":"Wow, there’s something about the black faced receivers that makes them stand out. A few of the receiver manufacturers produced dark faced models during the mid to late 70’s. Most were produced for the European market or for U.S. military base exchanges in Europe and Japan. Pioneer was one of the companies that did this. The “black” faced models were essentially the same as their silver faced brothers but had different model numbers. This Pioneer SX-5580 is the dark faced clone of the SX-1050 and was manufactured around 1976. Other matching models from Pioneer were: This model also has a black cabinet though I’ve seen some with the standard wood cabinets as well. The SX-5580 puts out 120 watts per channel into 8 ohms with no more than 0.1% harmonic distortion. It weighs in at just over 51 pounds and is big (20 3/4″ x 6 13/16″ x 17 7/8″).","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-5580","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-5580","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-5590":{"more":[{"t":"This Pioneer SX-5590 is the European version of Pioneer’s SX-1250. It would definitely be considered a “Monster” receiver as it produces a whopping 160 watts per channel. It incorporates a huge toroidal power transformer. It has the usual dark faceplate as is common with most European versions. Given that many feel the SX-1250 was the best receiver Pioneer ever produced it stands to reason that the SX-5590 is in a similar position. It features: The SX-1250 is an extremely popular receiver and has a huge following among collectors. It’s European version , the SX-5590, is probably even harder to find but at the same time is less well known. Still, the SX-5590 can sell for a good sum of money in good working condition . You must be keeping the power turned down because you will smoke the tweeters in the HPM 100s.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-5590","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-5590","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-650":{"more":[{"t":"One of the classic mid-range receivers offered by Pioneer in the mid 70’s was this Pioneer SX-650. As you can see it has the classic silver face styling of Pioneer’s 50 series which, when coupled with the wood case, makes for an exceptionally clean and stylish looking receiver. The SX-650 was produced from 1976-1977 and sold for around $300.00. The SX-650 puts out 35 watts per channel in to 8 ohms and was designed and marketed for those with an average sized listening room and who wanted good value for their money. The 650 didn’t have to many frills but what it did it did well. The Pioneer SX-650 weighed in at around 29 pounds and its dimensions are: 19 x 6 x 14.5 inches. For those with dial lighting issues the standard bulb in the SX-650 was an 8V 300mA globe bulb. Those are a little difficult to find these day so a good substitute is a 10mm 8V .250A wedge bulb. They can still be fairly easily found and are not too expensive.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-650","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-650","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-750":{"more":[{"t":"Here’s another of the classic Pioneer receivers. The Pioneer SX-750 was an upper mid range receiver with a perfect complement of features and performance for someone wanting good performance while, at the same time, not breaking the bank. The SX-750 did just that while putting out 50 watts per channel at 0.1% total harmonic distortion. Manufactured during the heyday of silver faced receiver’s this particular model was introduced in 1976 and made through 1977. It had a retail price tag of around $400. One interesting feature of the SX-750, and Pioneer SX-650 for that matter, is that the input/output terminals and circuits for the pre amp and tuner section are laid out on one large circuit board. According to Pioneer this allowed the use of unshielded input cables and also resulted in better overall tonal quality. Interestingly the performance of the SX-750 is not that far off from the flagship Pioneer SX-1250 with the exception of power output. So, not a bad value for $400 at the time.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-750","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-750","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-850":{"more":[{"t":"This classic receiver the Pioneer SX-850 was made from 1976 to 1977 and, while not the top of the line, it was one of their higher end offerings. It has the tradition mid to late 70’s styling that is easily recognized as Pioneer. The silver face, wood case and amber lights are all characteristic of Pioneer receivers of that time. You’ll be hard pressed to find someone that doesn’t like the SX-850. It really epitomizes what vintage audio is all about. The great look, quality build and above average performance make it a fantastic receiver for someone wanting to build a good quality vintage system. It’s rated at 65 watts per channel but most agree that is probably low. It phono stage and bass response are also known for being top quality. Hook a turntable up to this receiver and you won’t be disappointed.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-850","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-850","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-950":{"more":[{"t":"This is the stylish Pioneer SX-950. This receiver was offered by Pioneer from 1976 through 1977. It had a list price of around $600.00. This model was in the upper end of the quality range and sold well. The 950 is rated at 85 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It weighs just under 42 pounds. The weight stated in this article is incorrect for the SX-950. It weighs 41.6 pounds, not 55 pounds. It also neglects to mention a handy feature — the Adapter switch which can be used for an EQ or RG processor, which is preferable to using the Pre-out/Main-in jumpers.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-950","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-950","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"revox-a-740":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥538,000. Stereo power amplifier with traditional European tone. Even if the static characteristics are increased by the transient NFB, the dy ism of music will be damaged by the occurrence of TIM distortion. This reduces the occurrence of TIM distortion by only 26dB of overall NPB. 2 loudspeaker output Peak program meter","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Revox A 740 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/amp/a740.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rx-1603":{"more":[{"t":"This one is a monster! It’s the Rotel RX-1603 and is the biggest receiver they ever made. It earns its way into the Monster Receiver hall of fame by churning out 180 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It was made in Japan and would set you back a hefty $1100 when it hit the market in 1976. You would probably have to have someone help you get it to your car because it weighs in at a plump 73 pounds! It has a beautiful white/amber glow that emanates from the dial face, FM tuning meter and signal strength meter. I wouldn’t necessarily call the receiver aesthetically pleasing because it has somewhat of a robotic look to it and the alternating knobs and switches give it a mechanical Morse Code look. The Rotel RX-1603 didn’t just perform at high levels it was also built with exacting standards. It featured top of the line Sanken 2SC1586 output transistors that were hand picked and hand tested.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Rotel RX-1603","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/rotel-rx-1603","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/rotel-rx-1603.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/rotel-rx-1603","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/rotel-rx-1603-left-1.jpg"}},"sansui-au-5900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥53,000. AU-7900 The power amplifier part is equipped with a fully-directed pure complementary circuit. The first step adopts a differential a ification using a dual trans, and the drive stage has a three-stage darlington configuration with active load. In addition, the power supply of the pre-drive stage is set as a separate circuit. This reduces the occurrence of non-linear distortion even when linearity occurs and transient signals are included. We have enough space by supplying ±2 power supply by high voltage of 51V. Selected CR element is available for equalizer element. Phono1 input can switch the impedance to three stages. The input terminal part on the back has a unique structure that is mounted upwardly.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-5900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-5900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-607":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥69,800. This integrated amplifier was developed in pursuit of physical characteristics under the development theme of creating new sound with a novel circuit that understands the essence of audio. When a program source with a large dynamic range and a dense music signal is reproduced by an amplifier with a large bare gain and a large amount of negative feedback (NF) applied to improve the distortion, transient intermodulation distortion (Transient Intermodulation) occurs due to an unstable element such as delay in the amplifier circuit, and the resolution deteriorates. Transient Intermodulation Distortion (TIM) occurs at the summing point, which is the synthesis point of the input signal and negative feedback (NF) signal, because the negative feedback (NF) operation is momentarily lost due to the delay in the circuit, and an excessive input enters the amplifier. Therefore, it was difficult to achieve a wide range with conventional amplifiers. In the AU 607, we examined the bare characteristics before applying negative feedback (NF), and expanded the frequency characteristics, improved the phase characteristics, and reduced the distortion factor. We also improved the phase characteristics up to several tens of MHz by combining a unique phase correction circuit with an appropriate stagger ratio for phase advance and phase delay. By applying the minimum necessary negative feedback (NF), the transient intermodulation distortion is improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-607 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-607-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-6900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥65,000. AU-7900 The power amplifier part is equipped with a fully-directed pure complementary circuit. The first step adopts a differential a ification using a dual trans, and the drive stage has a three-stage darlington configuration with active load. In addition, the power supply of the pre-drive stage is set as a separate circuit. This reduces the occurrence of non-linear distortion even when linearity occurs and transient signals are included. AU-6900 combines four power trans s per channel with improved linearity of current characteristics to achieve low distortion rate and large output. We have enough space by supplying ±2 power supply by high voltage of 51V. Selected CR element is available for equalizer element.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-6900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-6900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-7900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥85,000. an integrated amplifier that realizes power and low distortion rate which can be affordable by original I/O terminal structure and power supply part-focused design policy. The power amplifier part is equipped with a fully-directed pure complementary circuit. The first step adopts a differential a ification using a dual trans, and the drive stage has a three-stage darlington configuration with active load. In addition, the power supply of the pre-drive stage is set as a separate circuit. This reduces the occurrence of non-linear distortion even when linearity occurs and transient signals are included. AU-7900 combines four power trans s per channel to improve the linearity of current characteristics to achieve low distortion rate and large output. We have enough space by supplying ±2 power supply by high voltage of 51V. Selected CR element is available for equalizer element.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-7900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-7900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-ba-2000":{"more":[{"t":"This is a high output stereo power amplifier that not only faithfully reproduces the original music but also reproduces the sound of the music itself. In the final stage, a parallel push-pull system is adopted, in which two high-output transistors with the same characteristics are used for each channel. Since the current flowing through each transistor is reduced to 1/2, operating points with good linearity can be selected, stable high output can be obtained continuously, and low distortion rate can be obtained over a wide range. The circuit configuration is further refined from the pure complimentary service OCL circuit directly connected to all stages. The pre-drive stage is a 2-stage class A amplifier with active load, and the drive stage is a parallel push-pull type with 3-stage Darlington connection. The differential amplifier uses a newly developed dual transistor with the same operating point and temperature characteristics to improve the stability of the midpoint potential. At the same time, the DC balance is made more stable by combining a constant current circuit and a current mirror circuit. In addition, high-quality parts such as ultra-low-noise transistors, low-leak capacitors with low loss and leakage current, fuse resistors, non-flammable resistors, and varistors are actively to determine sound quality not only by physical characteristics but also by rigorous listening tests.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui BA-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/ba-2000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-sr-525":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥44,500. The drive unit adopts direct drive, and the drive motor adopts the DC servo motor, which is a multi-polar multi-groove structure of 20 poles 30 slots with a built-in biased magnetic position detection mechanism. In addition, the three-phase alternating voltage proportional to the rotation speed is controlled by the electric potential difference compared with the standard voltage, and the high precision rotation speed is obtained. Tonearm has a static balance type S-magnetic pipe arm. Zinc alloy die-casting is used for the hold and base part that holds this arm. It not only increases strength, but also prevents the occurrence of harmful part resonance that affects the sound quality. In addition, we use double-structure special washer to strengthen the rigidity of the mounting part of the arm body, and we also insert special damping material into the cavity inside the pipe arm, eliminating resonance of the pipe part. Tonearm provides a knife edge support system with good follow-up by special steel. This method is simple structure, so it has high mechanical strength and lasts its initial performance for a long time.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-525 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-525.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-sr-525.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-525.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-525.JPG"}},"sansui-sr-929":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥73,000. A high-end player system that adopts quartz servo and knife edge one-point system tonearm. The direct drive method is used for the turntable drive, and the servoatsu servo method is used for the servo circuit. The quartz servo method controls the motor with the PLL servo and FG (fr ency generator) servo FG2 system including the crystal oscillation circuit and phase comparison circuit. Based on the crystal oscillation frequency, the drive motor is rotated, and it detects the delay or progress of the turntable rotation by FG, and controls it by the PLL circuit. This 2-system servo system realizes precise rotation speed that is important in the player system. servo-929 adopts the latest C-MOS type IC at the time of the PLL section, and the FG servo part adopts two high concentration ICs to achieve high reliability. FG servo is designed to work independently when FGtz servo is turned off. The drive motor is equipped with a brushless DC servo motor with a built-in biased magnetic core position detection mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-929 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-929.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sanyo-dca-1001":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥39,800. amplifier amplifier amplifier The power amplifier part uses a power IC of 70W+70W, and it is possible to improve the characteristics and sound quality by using it with a margin of 50W+50W. In addition, we are making low distortion rate with k consideration for equalizer element.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo DCA-1001 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dca-1001.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sanyo-dcc-3001":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥200,000. The preamplifier was developed with the theme of absolute precision, aiming to be one of the most active in history. DCC-3001 has improved TID (transient mixed modulation distortion) due to a large amount of negative feedback. By doing this, we have eliminated the delay phase correction capac for prevention of oscillation, which is essential for deep overall negative feedback, and achieved excellent through-rate. In addition, the dynamic range of the first stage is expanded by inserting high resistance as a local negative return in both the first step amplifier emitter. At the same time, the effect of the advanced phase correction circuit which was inserted in this stage is improved naked character and it is improved so that it can be used without return. The equalizer circuit has a high complete power amplifier circuit. The two-stage differential a ification and the full-stage direct connection method consisting of the output stage of the current mirror-type phase-inverted A-class push-pull method are adopted. This circuit achieves a ification of 40dB and a large allowable input of 500mV.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo DCC-3001 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dcc-3001.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sanyo-dcc-3001.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dcc-3001.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dcc-3001(3).jpg"}},"sanyo-dcp-3001":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥260,000. Aiming to be one of the most active in history, we developed a stereo amplifier based on the theme of ripe radiation. DCP-3001 is designed to improve transient modulation distortion by overall negative feedback. The best circuits are prepared for each stage, and the local negative feedback improves naked properties and reduces overall negative feedback to 25dB. The circuit configuration adopts the SEPP OCL system. A-class operation is performed by push pull from the first stage to the pre-driver stage, and the driver stage and output stage are B-class operation. The first step of the differential amplifier is a complimentary push-pull method of the differential amplifier to make enough naked gains, inserting high resistance to each emitter, and lowering the local negative feedback game gain.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo DCP-3001 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dcp-3001.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sanyo-dcp-3001.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dcp-3001.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dcp-3001(3).jpg"}},"sanyo-tp-1200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥49,800. Direct drive system. The drive motor is equipped with a 20-pole 30-slot DC servo motor with overs rated magnetic core. Rotary sintered slide volume control with 33/45rpm independent speed adjustment function. The cabinet uses CGR, a new material with superior gravity and internal loss.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo TP-1200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/player/tp-1200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-2700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥37,800. Full automatic player with a full automatic mechanism such as the tonearm protection mechanism. The 30cm aluminum die-cast turntable is powered by belt drive, and the motor is equipped with a beltronus motor with less vibration developed specifically for players. arm adopts static balance tonearm. The bearing part uses pivot bearings to measure high sensitivity, and the support part is supported by damper, making it a highly vibration resistant design. In addition, we are preparing an Inside For Scan Cellar to cancel the Inside Force depending on the performance points of the record. It comes with a detachable acrylic dust cover. We supply replacement shell stand.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-2700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-2700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-4300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥59,800. Full automatic player with full automatic mechanism in the same configuration as PS-3750. Auto-cut and repeat operation are also possible. This photocoupler method detects light intensity and generates signals. The full automatic mechanism is designed for easy-to-use and safety. If you stop tonearm while auto-reed in and auto-return operation, or switch the size selector, it is easy to force mechanic and tonearm and cause failure.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-4300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-4300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-9":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥380,000. A high-end player system with MC head amplifier and equal amplifier amplifier thanks to the integrated idea that the record player has equal amplifier. motor is a linear slotless motor with a traditional 6-fold torque developed specifically. Linear slotless motor achieves quiet and smooth rotation by removing the slots causing the torque mura (co ). In addition, it has more stable rotational accuracy by adopting linear drive method, and it realizes powerful torque of starting torque 7kg-cm by polarized structure and large magnet ring. The motor housing uses 5mm thick iron castings, and the rotational system is modified by its robust structure. The crystal lock is applied to the servo circuit by the crystal oscillator, and the magnetic disk rotation speed detection method is used for the rotation speed detection unit. A large weight turntable button with a diameter of 38cm. Because it is a turntable with conventional iner mass and weight, it suppresses the madness of the rotation speed caused by needle pressure load. It is also considered for transmission system because it supports head amplifier and equal amplifier built-in.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x9.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-sqd-2010":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥69,800. SQ decoder with a variable blend full logic circuit. The F/B logic circuit adopts a new variable blend method, and it is suppressed by blending the crosstalk with the opposite side of the left and right. This blend can be variable depending on the input signal. The SQ decoder and RM decoder are built in, and the discrete 4ch can be played by using the CD-4 demogulator. Equipped with 4ch master volume control. You can adjust the balance of each channel while watching the VU meter. Built-in tone control for back amplifier. Also, the back output can be switched to high/low two stages. With phase switch, you can set the phase of the front and back amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony SQD-2010 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/etc/sqd-2010.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-str-6800-sd":{"more":[{"t":"I’ve always liked the vintage Sony receivers. I’m not sure I can state exactly why, but they just have a different look about them while still retaining that classic vintage appeal. The layout of the controls is completely different than other stereos of the time and this Sony STR-6800 SD has a subtle look as opposed to the more polished and flashy look of other late 1970’s and early 1980’s receivers. I guess I would describe it as muted technical sophistication. Whatever that means. Nonetheless, the early Sony receivers are great machines. Their design, build quality and performance all live up to, and usually exceed, expectations. While Sony doesn’t attract the same level of interest that Pioneer or Sansui do it does have a fairly rabid following of collectors. Offered from 1977 through 1982 the STR-6800 retailed for around $600.00.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sony STR-6800 SD","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sony-str-6800-sd","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-2650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥39,800. The ES-II series is integrated with Sony's semiconductor technology. The power amplifier part is the OCL circuit. The function as a preamplifier is also enriched, such as tape copy function in two directions, and the input and output jack of Tape2.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-2650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-2650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-3650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥63,800. A circuit structure with a high degree of stability, and integrated amplifier with a focus on layout and wiring of substrates. The power amplifier part adopts the Pure Complementary OC system directly connected. High-precision distent and volume control","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-3650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-3650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥32,000. A newly developed power supply circuit which was obtained in the development process of TA-F3. The multi-power supply filter system employs six decoupling filter between each amplifier, which improves the crosstalk of the bass. W-100W direct reading power meter Equipped with a muting switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥48,000. As the circuit technology of the a ification stage is increasing, the key to the sound quality leaps is called power supply. The new FET buffer power supply is used to improve crosstalk between channels. Adopts the pure complementary direct connection circuit that uses dual trans s with the same characteristics. W to 100W Self-deft tone control with flat frequency characteristics in the center position and muting switch are equipped.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-7-b":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥178,000. Highest grade DC integrated amplifier with V-FET. DC from preamplifier to power amplifier, all DC amplifiers are adopted. The power supply section adopts the power supply of each block. By using FET buffer power supply, we have developed a thorough low crosstalk. Phono input is directly coupling to the current mirror differential amplifier by dual FET.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 7 B (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f7b.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-8000x":{"more":[{"t":"Taking a step back into Quad territory this is the Technics SA-8000x Quad receiver. Not the most stylish receiver it was offered from late 1973 until early 1975. It is rated at 13 watts per channel into 4 channels and 36 watts per channel into two channels (though I have seen some ratings at 16 and 42 wpc). The manufacturer’s suggested retail price was around $550.00. The SA-8000x measures 19 5/8 inches x 13 3/4 inches x 6 1/8 inches. It accommodated both CD-4 (Discreet) and SQ (Matrix) decoding. A reconditioned Technics SA-8000x recently sold for $284 (8-26-2019). They generally sell for $350-$400. A recent sale in June of 2023 was for $320.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Technics SA-8000X","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-8000x","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-9060":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo power amplifier that uses the best circuit technology to achieve the ultimate level of high performance. We have achieved 0.27% bare characteristics at 50W output power, and further applied negative feedback (NF) to improve the characteristics to the extent that measurement cannot be performed. The first stage consists of a current mirror load differential-amplifier circuit with low noise and high gain, the voltage amplifier stage consists of a pure resistance load with distortion factor priority, and the output-stage consists of a 3-stage Darlington full complimentary service SEPP circuit with sufficient current amplification. A ± 6 power supply configuration with excellent dynamic characteristics is adopted, and two power transformers are used in a left-right independent two power supply system. Equipped with a protection circuit that also serves as a muting to prevent shock noise.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-9060 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-9060-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-01":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥80,000. Developed with the development of SP-10mkII, the quartz-fade-locked control direct-drive player system. Quartz Fade Control method can be superior rotation control by phase control method based on crystal oscillator. 2.9kg turntable (iner mass 360kg/cm2) is a high torque motor that reaches a constant speed rotation at 90 ° (1/4 rotation). Tonearm uses a gimbal suspension method that realizes initial motion sensitivity 7mg. The armrest adjustment mechanism is equipped with a adjustable range of 6mm. Electronic brake mechanism is equipped.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-01 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-01.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥49,800. Player system with improved operability and stability by newly developed B/FG type one-chip IC. Equipped with AN630, one-chip IC of B/FG (Back Electromo Force Frequency Generator). This enables one-chip IC of motor drive unit, control unit, and various addition functions to improve the reliability of the player system by configuring the B/FG method using the reverse power frequency of motor drive winding. The Auto Mechanism incorporates the SL-1300 Auto Mechanism. In addition, it is also possible to respond to light needle pressure cartridge coupled with the adoption of high sensitivity gimbal suspension tonearm. Tonearm is equipped with a universal tonearm for gimbal suspension. The bearing structure of the gimbal suspension system using precision pivot bearings for horizontal and vertical bearings of tonearm realizes initial motion sensitivity 7mg. cartridge is equipped with EPC-270C, which is the MM cartridge of Technics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥44,800. The world's first D.D motor IC (AN630) circuit is equipped with one-chip motor drive unit, control unit and various functions. The B/FG (Back Electro Mo Force Frequency Generator) method is used to detect the speed to accurately maintain the rotation speed of the motor. Motor has a unique integrated D.D motor. In addition, the rotation part of the motor is integrated with turntable, and the fixed part is integrated with the case, and the stacking of the case, motor and table turn is unnecessary, so performance and reliability are improved.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-sl-1700.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1700.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1700.JPG"}},"technics-sl-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥29,800. Direct drive player with high basic performance with slim design. A one-chip IC (AN620) equipped with motor drive and control unit integrated into one-chip. The drive unit is equipped with a DC servo motor with low power consumption and high rotation power. MM type cartridge is used for the shell integrated structure. Rotation speed can be adjusted by 33, 1/3, and 45 rpm alone.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-23":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥31,800. Record player with FG servo motor with the same performance as SL-26. Equipped with a smart return mechanism, the detection mechanism is working at the end of the performance, and tonearm automatically returns to the left and the power supply of the player is cut.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-23 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-23.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-8080":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier that employs an integrated DC configuration to achieve more faithful waveform transmission. The DC main amplifier section, which directly drives the high-level input, consists of a first stage differential amplifier, a voltage amplifier stage with a pure resistance load, an output stage with an emitter follower and a two stage Darlington connection, and the gain is increased to 42 dB to directly drive the high-level input. By making the power supply circuit configuration independent on the left and right, transient distortion is reduced. In addition, the power supply of the voltage amplification stage is all constant voltage, and not only crosstalk distortion but also self-transient distortion in the own channel is minimized. The transformer has a strict magnetic shield and is located on the diagonal most distant from the equalizer circuit. This is a low-noise design. The PhonoSN ratio has been improved by adopting the newly developed low-noise transistor M47L for the first stage amplifier. In addition, excellent characteristics have been obtained by the adoption of a high-precision equalizer element. For tone control, we use a volume where the CR is out of the signal system at the midpoint.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-8080 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-8080-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-9070":{"more":[{"t":"This flat pre-amplifier has a simple configuration with a flat amplifier in the equalizer circuit to eliminate coloring and improve basic performance. The combination of 1% metal coating resistance and 2% polypropylene capacitor realizes excellent characteristics. The first stage employs a differential amplifier circuit with a current mirror load to achieve a high gain of 60 dB and low noise. The next stage consists of a voltage amplification stage with a pure resistance load. The distortion factor is 0.26% at a gain of 90 and 20 V output. A subsonic filter switch is mounted on the equalizer stage. In order to eliminate coloring due to changes in frequency characteristics, a flat amplifier without any accessory circuit is adopted. Uses a 26-point high-precision attenuator type master level controller. A subsonic filter switch is mounted on the equalizer stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-9070 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-9070-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-220":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥31,800. High CP is pursued by polishing sound quality without pursuing high power. The power supply indicator uses LED. tone control is a click-stop type of 11 times.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB-220 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-220.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-420":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥56,800. Integrated amplifier with rich functions. The circuit configuration is a three-stage direct connection circuit, including one differential, and the input is 350mV by applying high voltage of ±40V. The power amplifier part adopts the OCL circuit, which has excellent stability including the axial amplifier. Power supply: 10,000μFx2 Microphone mixing circuit with independent volume control. The tape-duplication switch is equipped to copy between two decks simultaneously. The tone control part can be switched to two turnover frequency. Deft position is also available.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB-420 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-420.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-620":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥85,000. Achieve both power and quality. The power amplifier part is equipped with the OCL circuit. The equalizer amplifier has a high voltage of ±55V. The circuit is a three-stage direct connection circuit. This circuit is also a ±2 power supply configuration. A duplication switch that can be copied between two decks is installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB-620 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-620.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-820":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥135,000. Stereo amplifier pursuing wide range and low distortion rate. In addition, the driver stage of the 3-stage direct-connected Darlington connection is operated constant current, and the distortion at the time of a small signal is greatly reduced. The tone amplifier part adopts the negative feedback (NF) type of two-stage direct-connected active load, including one differential using FET. This circuit has a high stability of ±2 power supply.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB-820 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-820.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sc-55":{"more":[{"t":"A thin-design stereo power amplifier with affordable output and high quality playback sound. A 2-stage 3-stage Darlington direct-coupled pure complimentary service OCL circuit with cascode connection at the first stage is adopted. In addition to making the phase correction capacitor as small as possible, by adopting a differential driver circuit that changes from common-emitter to common-base in the high frequency range, the naked gain at the high frequency range is improved. The power supply section has an independent power transformer for the left and right channels to improve the separation. The power supply unit is equipped with two low-magnification 10,000 μ F capacitors for each channel. This capacitor increases the current density by widening the current path and keeps the impedance low. In addition, a metalized polyester film capacitor is used in parallel for the electrolytic capacitor to improve the high-frequency characteristics. Each stage up to the driver stage is supplied with power by a constant voltage circuit to improve the stability of operation. Copper foil with a thickness of 70 μ m is used for the PC board, and the SN ratio and separation are improved by reducing the impedance of the signal system.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Toshiba SC-55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AUREX/amp/sc-55-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sc-77":{"more":[{"t":"This monaural power amplifier has a thin structure and pursues the appeal of monaural amplifiers. All stages are directly connected and pure complimentary service OCL circuit of 3-stage Darlington connection including 2-stage differential with cascode connection at the first stage. The circuit up to the driver stage is supplied with power by a low impedance constant voltage circuit, which improves the S / N ratio and distortion factor at small output as well as stabilizing it. In addition, a non-inductive metallized polyester film condenser is used for the input part, and the deterioration of sound quality is suppressed by eliminating the electrolytic condenser. The power supply section is equipped with a large toroidal transformer and two low-magnification 11,000 μ F electrolytic capacitors. The low-magnification capacitor has a structure in which the area ratio magnification of etching is controlled to 10 to 12 times. Although it has a large capacity, the current density increases because the current path is thick, and it has succeeded in reducing the DC impedance of the electrode. In addition, the AC impedance is also reduced by using a multi-terminal structure in which the electrode is discharged from several places of the anode foil. The power supply for class A circuit and class B circuit is divided, and consideration is given to prevent the waveform of class B circuit from jumping into class A circuit in terms of structure layout.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Toshiba SC-77 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AUREX/amp/sc-77-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-220":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥29,800. Record player with auto-cut mechanism. The turntable part uses a belt drive method and uses a 16-pole belthronous motor for the drive motor. It is equipped with the auto return mechanism, it automatically raises the arm when the record is over and returns to the position of the arm headphone. In addition, this operation is equipped with an auto-cut switch that can be used even during playing. With the anti-scaling mechanism, you can adjust the right channel balance by canceling the inside force. Needle pressure stamping adopts convenient needle pressure straight reading type. MM type cartridge C-230M","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-220 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-220.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-255":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥37,800. Direct drive player with two types of turntable. turn-255 andSR-255D contain turntable materials to choose from. DC servo motor Tonearm has a static balance S-shaped tonearm. It is equipped with an anti-scaling mechanism that corresponds to needle pressure. cartridge is equipped with MM type cartridge C-230M. Speed can be adjusted according to 33, 1/3, and 45 rotations. The cabinet’s player board uses a high-density molding material, AD Solid, which suppresses resonance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-255 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-255.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-355":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥44,800. Record player with strong sandwich structure. Direct drive method using DC servo motor is used for drive motor. Each speed of 33, 1/3, and 45 rotations is equipped. Tonearm has a static balance S-shaped tonearm. We supply oil damping elevation mechanism and needle pressure read counterweight. With anti-scaling mechanism, it is easy to adjust with the scale of the needle pressure type. The needle pressure seal is equipped with a direct reading method. cartridge comes with a MM type cartridge C-210M.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-355 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-355.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-370":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥64,800. There is no cartridge. Features are hard, heavy, strong (hard to break), and the material has the properties of wood, metal, and stone. In addition, the internal loss is almost the same as plywood and is superior to aluminum die casting, and the specific gravity is 3 to 4 times larger than plywood. The mechanism is powered by direct drive, using servoDC motor on the drive motor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-370 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-370.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sy-77":{"more":[{"t":"A preamplifier with a simple circuit configuration that emphasizes characteristics and sound quality without sacrificing functions. The circuit of the SY-77 is designed so that a high voltage of ± 70 v can be applied with two positive and negative power supplies, ensuring sufficient margin for the first stage of the system. The flat amplifier section has a first stage cascode connection and a two stage differential pure complimentary service circuit. The configuration of the flat amplifier is similar to that of a power amplifier, so that the characteristics of an EQ are fully exhibited. The output stage is a class A parallel push-pull operation, and the output impedance is set to 600 Ω to minimize the characteristic change due to connection. The tone amplifier section also employs a two power supply configuration, positive and negative. It pursues a low distortion rate and stable operation. It is designed for sound quality in terms of audibility, with the first priority being that the quality does not deteriorate due to the insertion of the tone circuit. The circuit configuration employs a two stage direct-coupled active broad circuit including one stage differential.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Toshiba SY-77 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AUREX/amp/sy-77-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-b-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥335,000. The vertical power FET for audio is used. Dual horizontal FET is used for input circuit. In addition, the full-stage FET configuration gain 0dB preposition amplifier has the function of impedance conversion for runble filter, level control and remote control. It is designed to make this amplifier through the rear switch. The power amplifier part uses a large output vertical FET of 300W (Tc=25°C) for drain loss on the output stage with a single push pull, and the drive circuit is equipped with a direct connection drive by source forroa for all stage FETs. Because of the single push pull by FET of the same channel, pair sorting is easy, and stable operation is improved because the balance of the push pull is easy. In B-I, FET input/output characteristics close to two-way characteristics reduce the number of malformed harmonic distortions that are easier to hear. In addition, because the push-pull circuit breaks even higher harmonic distortion, the sound quality with less distortion component is realized.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-b-1.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-1.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-1.jpg"}},"yamaha-b-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥200,000. This FET is designed to reduce the power FET2SK77 for B-1. In addition, it is developed by devising its own manufacturing method and pair sorting method. Pch, Nch's device chip size, impurity concentration, gate mesh structure are carefully examined and controlled strictly in the manufacturing process. We are paired by our unique pair sorting method. In addition, we can suppress the occurrence of distortion by using the combination of current mirror load and all stages except the first stage to push-pull. It has excellent characteristics even with low-profile NPB.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥150,000. Preamplifier with original super low noise FET. The basic circuit configuration is a simple structure of equalizer amplifier, tone preamplifier and MC cartridge head amplifier. To pursue the performance as a preamplifier, the accessory circuit is minimal and has excellent characteristics. In the second circuit, the first load is lightened by the constant current load emitter ground of the Darlington connection, and the gain is sufficient. The output stage is high fre cies (ft ~ 100MHz), and it is a Pure Complementary A-grade Parallel Push Pull Circuit that uses two pairs of trans s that are well-matched with Complementary characteristics. The equalizer amplifier circuit is double shielded.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-c-2.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-2.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-2(2).jpg"}},"yamaha-ca-1000-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥125,000. CA-1000 The power amplifier part is equipped with a pure complimentary OCL circuit. All circuits are analyzed using a CAD method using a computer.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-1000 II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-1000ii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-800-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1974 at ¥95,000. The power amplifier part is equipped with all stages of Pure Complementary OCL circuit. In addition, by adopting the constant voltage power supply of a separate setting that drives all stages except the power stage, the stability is increased. Two protection circuits with power trans protection and loudspeaker protection. The loudspeaker protection circuit adopts the unique circuit method of the cable, and if the DC voltage of the output terminal exceeds ±2V, the relay will operate and block the signal path to the loudspeaker. This protection circuit is automatically restored if it is less than ±2V.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-800 II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-800ii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-ca-800-ii.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-800ii.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-800ii(2).JPG"}},"yamaha-ca-v-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥33,000. Integrated amplifier for circuits, characteristics and functions at affordable prices. The equalizer circuit adopts two-stage discrete circuit with low noise trans. The circuit is designed to improve the SN ratio by not using ICs with less freedom to select circuit constants. The tone control circuit is a two-stage direct connection type similar to the equalizer circuit. The circuit method is the CR-negative feedback (NF) mixed type of the negative feedback (NF) method. In the case of boosting, the circuit gain is raised by the CR inCR with the negative feedback (NF) split resistance, and when cutting, the CR is sintered by the output side. In this method, the CR time constant of the boost side and the cut side can be the same, so you can use the B type which is easy to produce the accuracy of the volume control curve, and you can get the characteristic that is not swelling in the middle position. The power amplifier amplifier circuit configuration is an input differential-emitta earth-pure-complementary OCL circuit that combines current mirror circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-V 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-v1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-ca-v-1.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-v1.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-v1.JPG"}},"yamaha-cr-450":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Yamaha CR-450. This little receiver was made from 1976-1978 and was listed at $390.00. It put out 32 watts per channel and had a rated total harmonic distortion of 0.1%. It has the late 1970’s iconic Yamaha look with a white dial face inset on a silver faceplate, big wafer switches, and a minimalist cabinet. The CR-450 falls into the CR-200 through CR-1000 family. It is a contemporary of the Yamaha CR-400 and looks almost the same with the exception of an extra toggle switch on the front panel. The earlier CR-400 had some issues with 4 ohm speakers so Yamaha made some adjustments in the CR-450 to accommodate them, mainly by doubling the outputs to drive higher current. The CR-450 has controls for Bass and Treble as well as Low and High filter switches. It also has a variable Loudness control.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-450","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-450","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-450.jpg","xc":2,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-450","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/yamaha-cr-450-meters.jpg"}},"accuphase-c-220":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1977. A disc preamplifier developed as a pre-amplifier for records only. Since it is a recording player, there is no auxiliary terminal or tape input terminal. Instead, there is a terminal that is directly connected to the power amplifier when the power switch of the C-220 is turned off. Using this, you can connect a tuner or tape recorder to the preamplifier you already own, and the output of the amplifier is connected to the C-220 EXT. Preamp. By connecting to Input, you can automatically connect the output of the preamplifier you already own to the power amplifier. Also, when correcting frequency characteristics with tone control, C-220 Fixed You can use it as an equalizer amplifier by taking the signal from the Output and connecting it to the aux input of an existing preamplifier. The head amplifier for the MC cartridge is built in, and the gain is 26 dB for the head amplifier and 60 dB from the equalizer to the output. In addition, the head amplifier is switched by relay control so that MC and MM can be selectively used with one arm, and shock noise is eliminated by having a time difference with the output muting relay by electronic circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-220 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-220-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-m-60":{"more":[{"t":"This monaural power amplifier was completed over a long period of time without any compromise with the aim of further improving the quality of reproduced music. The use of a monaural power amplifier reduces interference between the left and right channels while keeping the weight and size within a range that can be handled by one person. The circuit configuration is based on an active element with excellent high-frequency characteristics, and all amplification stages are composed of symmetric push-pull. By applying a small amount of NFB, excellent rise characteristics, linearity and stability are achieved. This prevents the occurrence of TIM distortion and provides low distortion output even at full power. In addition, in order to achieve sound quality with less coloration, the condenser inside the NFB loop has been removed to create a DC amplifier configuration. A large transformer and a 22,000 μ Fx2 filter capacitor apply a high voltage to the power supply section obtain a large energy of 152 joules (120 joules for the P-300 type). This greatly improves the low-frequency output characteristics. The output meter uses a logarithmic compression type that can read directly from 3 mW to 300W continuously.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase M-60 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/M-60-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-20":{"more":[{"t":"Released May 1976 at ¥190,000. This is a stereo power amplifier developed for high-efficiency floor-type speaker systems for a long period of time without compromise in pursuit of \"perfection\" for true high-quality music playback. It is composed of two monaural power amplifiers with independent power supply, so that mutual interference caused by layout and wiring is minimized. The circuit configuration employs a push-pull circuit in all stages, with less phase disturbance over a wide bandwidth and excellent linearity over a wide dynamic range. In addition, in order to keep residual noise low, specially selected parts and careful circuit examination are carried out, and residual noise is reduced to the extent that it can hardly be heard even when it is directly connected to a high-efficiency horn driver as a multi-channel amplifier system. Tube type amplifier In order to be compatible with models with low damping factors, such as speakers developed in the heyday of the amplifier, a damping factor selection switch is mounted to control the tone balance and volume of the reproduced sound by changing the damping factor. Since the value of the damping factor is changed by current feedback, there is no power loss due to switching. As long as an AC signal (music waveform) is being input, no matter how large an input is input, a new protection circuit has been developed and adopted to prevent the sound from being cut off due to the differential of the protection. This is a countermeasure against overload.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-20 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-20-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/accuphase-p-20.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-20-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/p-20.JPG"}},"bose-360":{"more":[{"t":"If you’re ever in the mood to stir up a polarizing debate then bring up the quality and performance of any Bose equipment. Some hate it, some love it, and there are not many opinions in between. This Bose 360 receiver was part of the Bose Direct/Reflecting Music System and doesn’t get a lot of love from most audio enthusiasts. To be fair, it wasn’t a top of the line Bose product like their Spatial Receiver or 1801 amplifier. It was an entry level stereo that was paired with a simple turntable and a pair of bookshelf speakers. Sort of an early all-in-one system. The Direct/Reflecting Music System hit the market in 1977. The model 360 receiver is a 10 watt per channel stereo with Total Harmonic Distortion of 1%. Not very impressive.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Bose 360","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/bose-360","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-poa-1003":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥145,000. DC amplifier. The circuit configuration is an ICL circuit that is directly connected to all stages. The Pc=100W-class bipolar type power trans is used for the output stage. In addition, this part is an earthing potential, so it deteriorates S/N and causes crosstalk as it passes through the first stage or preamplifier of the left and right channels that handle small signal voltage. POA-1003 has a dual-busline (DualBusline) that uses a copper plate with a thickness of 1 mm in this part to eliminate harm. There are various measures to reduce DC drift problems with DC amplifier. In the first step differential circuit, TR1/2 is heat coupled, and the casscode connection (TR3/4) is used to reduce gate current.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon POA-1003 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-1003.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pra-1003":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥93,000. A preamplifier that thoroughly reviewed the equalizer amplifier that is important to record playback. This enables more faithful waveform transmission. This realizes high S/N with input-converted noise level -138dB(V). The emitter follower output is a ified with the current mirror differential circuit by the A-class push pull and drives the output stage of the pure complementary push pull. Each input terminal is grounded when the code is not connected and prevents unpleasant noise.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PRA-1003 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pra-1003.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"fisher-rs-1060":{"more":[{"t":"Many would consider this Fisher RS-1060 a monster receiver since it produces 125 watts per channel. It was manufactured from 1977 until 1979 and retailed for around $700. Emerson Electric took over Fisher in the early 70’s and by 1975 Sanyo had taken over the brand and added ‘Studio Standard’ to the name. Build quality had declined by that time but the higher end solid state receivers were still built pretty well. The RS-1060 was second in line, in terms of size and features, to the RS-1080 which put out 170 watts per channel and was a true monster. The RS-1060 was built to compete with the the Sansui 9090DB, Pioneer SX-1080 and Marantz’s 2325. There is some debate whether it was truly competitive or not, but some believe it performs at least as well. It is certainly harder to find than the other above mentioned receivers. The RS-1060 is huge.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Fisher RS-1060","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/fisher-rs-1060","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/fisher-rs-1060.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/fisher-rs-1060","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/04/fisher-rs-1060-lamps.jpg"}},"hitachi-hca-9000":{"more":[{"t":"A is a preamplifier designed to give the highest priority to sound quality by keeping the number of circuits to the minimum necessary and carefully selecting the components constituting each of the circuit blocks through repeated trial listening. The power supply section uses a toroidal transformer with high efficiency and low leakage flux. In addition, the constant voltage current is negative feedback (NF) type, and the Route 6 independent power supply system is adopted in which the source impedance is lowered and one set of constant voltage power supply is used for all amplifiers. On the output side, a large-capacity capacitor and a metallized polyester film capacitor with excellent sound quality are connected in parallel to improve sound quality. We are working to improve the quality of all parts, with particular attention paid to the use and selection of types of capacitors. The phase compensation capacitor uses a Styrofoam capacitor with a 500 V resistance. Two capacitors are arranged in a series for circuits that have a particularly high impact on sound quality. Equalizer circuit The RIAA device uses metalized polyester film capacitors, the flat amplifier uses two back-to-back electrolytic capacitors, and the power supply uses metalized polycarbonate film capacitors. The HCA 9000 circuit consists of an MC head amplifier, an equalizer amplifier and a flat amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HCA-9000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hca-9000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hma-3700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥30,000. Stereo power amplifier. Power level meter Built-in electronic protection circuit to protect loudspeaker. Carrying handle was sold separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HMA-3700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/hma-3700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hma-6500":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo power amplifier using power MOS FET. DC amplifier configuration is adopted.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HMA-6500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hma-6500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hma-9500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥230,000. First stereo power amplifier using power MOS FET. Power MOS FET is adopted as the amplifying element of the power stage. Compared with conventional small-signal MOS FETs, this power MOS FET has high amplification factor (mutual inductance) and good linearity. Moreover, it has superior high-frequency characteristics by more than one order of magnitude compared with bipolar transistors. In addition, the switching speed is fast based on the operating principle. It is more resistant to electrical breakdown than power transistors and can simplify the protection circuit of the amplifier. Since the input characteristics are enhancement characteristics, the bias circuit is simpler than that of a FET with depletion characteristics. When used as an audio amplifier in a complimentary service circuit, it can be used as a push-pull amplifier with less distortion compared to an amplifier using a power transistor. The circuit configuration consists of a differential amplifier in the first stage and a differential amplifier in the second stage with a current mirror circuit as a load.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HMA-9500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hma-9500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-350":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥31,800. Autoplayer with Unitorque motor. The turntable part adopts a direct drive method, and the drive motor is equipped with a Unitorque motor. Unitorque motor is a brushless, slotless, and coreless structure, which provides stable rotation without torque. In addition, because it is flat structure, it is good to apply to the player, and the structure is simple, so it is reliable. Auto-return and auto-cut are available. tonearm has a static balance tonearm. The main body of the pipe arm and the main weight axis are made of damper rubber. Stable traceability by anti-skating mechanism. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-350 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-350.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ja-s-22":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥47,000. Stable by current mirror input circuit. We make careful considerations for patterns of circuit components and printed circuit boards, and make all circuits low distortion. The front panel is equipped with two tape terminals and multiple compression power meter. Three-size relay protection circuit It is equipped with subsonic filter to cut bass noise.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JA-S 22 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s22.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-ja-s-22.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s22.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s22.JPG"}},"jvc-m-3030":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥105,000. The AB/LR power supply system adopted by M-3030 has developed this method, and it is designed to reduce distortion by making B-grade power supply dedicated to the left and right channels. ICL (input, capac, wrestling) circuit circuit eliminated input capac coupling and capac. Measures level control of left and right independent. Directo and Subsonic","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC M-3030 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/m-3030.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-p-3030":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥70,000. A preamplifier that challenged thin design while pursuing quality and various control functions unique to the Separate amplifier. The MC head amplifier uses FETs that are highly effective for improving the SN ratio, and the circuit configuration that utilizes FET features ensures excellent SN ratio and low distortion rate. The ICL (impt capac wrestling) circuit is used to remove the coupling capac input in all signal circuits such as equalizer and tone amplifier. In addition, both the first stage are using the noise sorted FET, and the equalizer and the tone amplifier are double differential input. This circuit is very effective for reducing distortion and has a combined effect with the ICL circuit to achieve a full harmonic distortion rate of 0.005%. volume control This volume control reduces current distortion by 0.003% or less due to homogenization of resistor material and improvement of manufacturing process, and voltage distortion is less than 0.005%. In addition, this volume control is an interlocking type of twin configuration arranged before and after the amplifier, so the residual noise during the volume is cut effectively. In addition, AC code has a capacity of 15A.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC P-3030 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/p-3030.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-p-3030.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/p-3030.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/p-3030(2).jpg"}},"kenwood-ka-8100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥63,000. High speed DC integrated amplifier. The newly developed high-speed circuit is used to improve the collapse and disturbance of the waveform that is easy to generate when it is high-speed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-8100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-8100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-05-m":{"more":[{"t":"The high speed power amplifier was completed with the theme of improving transient response in high fre cies that meet improved low fre cies. Newly designed high-speed circuit and newly developed high-speed element have gained a wide-band characteristic of DC to 600 kHz.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-05 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-05m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-07-m":{"more":[{"t":"The power amplifier needs to keep the loudspeaker code within 1m to fully drive the loudspeaker system. A mono power amplifier developed from the conclusion. The circuit is very simplified and the signal is supplied to the output terminal by following the shortest route from the input terminal. These circuit designs improve various characteristics such as S/N ratio and distortion rate.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-07 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-07m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-07c":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥100,000. The direct drive and amplifier system has all the controls. 10Ω low impedance output design that can extend the audio cable fully from preamplifier to power amplifier, preventing power amplifier from directly driving loudspeaker. 2 sets of ICL type equal amplifier for MM cartridge and MC cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-07C (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-07c.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-cl-32":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1976 at ¥128,000. Tube s ical thin preamplifier. Tone Control The circuit configuration uses 7 twin poles.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman CL-32 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/cl32.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-cl-32.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/cl32.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/cl32.jpg"}},"luxman-pd-441":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1977 at ¥125,000. Player system with floating motor. PD441 is the same design as PD444, and the size is compact by using one standard tonearm. The drive unit has a direct drive system with quartz lock. The quartz lock method reduces the turbulence of the direct basin and the outer turbulence of less than 1 Hz, and suppresses instant drift and temperature drift. We use our own load free spins dollar method to deal with this problem. This reduces the load of turntable on the bearing to about 1/5.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-441 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd441.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-444":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1977 at ¥165,000. Armless player system developed as a player who can use two tonearms, including long arm in the smallest space. It is a direct drive method that uses quartz lock method for driving method. The drive motor adopts a newly developed motor using the unique load free spins dollar method of the lux, and the load of turntable is expected for the bearing. However, this is the life of the bearing. In the load free spins dollar method, the weight of turntable is canceled by suctioning the loader upward using the magnetic force inside the motor. This reduces the load of turntable on the bearing to about 1/5. Because the PD444 method has the power that the motor itself can float turntable, it is different from the conventional magnet float method that uses the rebound force of the magnet later. PD444 uses two 3.2mm iron plates, which are sandwiched between high density chipboards.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-444 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd444.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-r-1120":{"more":[{"t":"This the beautifully styled Luxman R-1120 receiver. As you can see it has a nice symmetrical design and beautiful wood veneer case. Introduced in 1976 this was Luxman’s top of the line unit until it was discontinued in 1979. It had a retail price of $995.00. There was apparently also an R-1120A that came out near the end of the production run that had some revisions made to it as well. The R-1120 had discrete power transistors while the R-1120A did not. From the Luxman brochure:The Luxman R-1120 is the long awaited advent of super powered ‘tuner-amplifier’ from Luxman. It has a giant power output of 120W per channel, truly useful and equally eye catching LED peak indicators allowing easy reading of instantaneous output power level, and 3 pairs of speaker terminals, one of which is specially designed for exclusive use with such low impedance loudspeakers as electrostatic types which have been gaining remarkable popularity among discerning audiophiles. A Luxman R-1120 recently sold (6-22-2011) for $400.00.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Luxman R-1120","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/luxman-r-1120","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2226-b":{"more":[{"t":"This Marantz 2226B receiver has the classic vintage Marantz look that most collectors can spot from a hundred feet away. I’ve been driving past garage sales before and spotted a Marantz receiver from half a block away. Maybe it’s the Gyro Touch Tuning knob or the big black Marantz lettering at the top of the silver face or even the industrial looking bolts they used to secure the faceplate. Whatever it is these receivers are instantly recognizable. When properly lit up there aren’t many receivers that are better looking. Unfortunately you don’t find them too often with all the lamps functioning. And, if they are the blue color has usually changed to more of a green. This is because the velum paper that Marantz used behind their dial faces has usually degraded and turned yellow or burned. Fortunately you can purchase lamp kits for these receivers and even change them to LED’s which slightly enhance the color and reduce the heat inside the unit at the same time.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2226 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2226b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-2226-b.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2226b","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2012/12/marantz-2226B-front-lit.jpg"}},"marantz-2230b":{"more":[{"t":"Clicking a link to eBay may result in a referral commission being paid if a purchase is made.Loading...","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2230B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/model/marantz-2230b-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2238-b":{"more":[{"t":"Clicking a link to eBay may result in a referral commission being paid if a purchase is made.Loading...","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2238 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/for-sale/model/marantz-2238b-for-sale","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2252b":{"more":[{"t":"Ahhh…another classic Marantz. I know there are some audiophiles out there that feel Marantz receivers are over rated and over priced. Perhaps, but they ooze vintage audio. Their distinct industrial look and design sets them apart as well. This Marantz 2252B is one of the best performers out of all the Marantz models. It’s well known for its warm sound and exceptional build quality. Add to that 52 watts per channel and you’ve got yourself a good receiver. Originally offered in 1977 and discontinued around 1979 the 2252B retailed for $460.00. You could also pick up the optional WC-22 wood cabinet for that extra top end look.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2252B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2252b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2265b":{"more":[{"t":"Aesthetically the Marantz 2265B was one of their most well balanced receivers. Everything just seems really well proportioned and laid out well. The 2265B was made from 1977 until 1979 and is a great mid range receiver. It puts out 65 watts per channel and retailed for $580.00. It is basically a redesign of the 2265 and has slightly better distortion numbers as well so there are probably some slight circuitry differences too. You can see obvious design differences between the 2265 and 2265B. The 2265 below has a black dial face while the 2265B has a silver face. You’ll also notice the balance control on the 2265 is a slider while on the 2265B it’s a knob. Another aspect that is different is the meter backlighting on the 2265B.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2265B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2265b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2285-b":{"more":[{"t":"This is the classic Marantz 2285b. It is one of the more sought after Marantz receivers. Even though it’s only listed at 85 watts per channel it has plenty of power to drive most any speakers. It featured DLB-1 dolby noise reduction as well. It was offered from 1977 up until 1980 and retailed for around $670.00. It weighed in at just over 37 pounds. It has the following inputs: As you can see from the inside picture these units were built like tanks and with a high level of quality. Though not shown in these pictures the Marantz 2285B also came with an optional WC 22 wood case which gave it a fantastic sophisticated look. These receivers sell for quite a bit when restored.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2285 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2285-b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2330":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2330B was produced from 1977 through 1979 at the height of the audio craze. As you probably already know Marantz built some of the best receivers offered during that time. This particular unit put out 130 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It also featured: An average 2330B will sell for around $1500 in decent working condition. Over $2000 in very good working condition. Update: Recent sale for $2100 on 8-2021. This receiver was in excellent condition and fully serviced with new LED lamps and a new wood case as well. Whoa! Please tell me where I can get a 2330B for a mere $200 as you suppose in your blog?","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2330","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2330-b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2330-b":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 2330B was produced from 1977 through 1979 at the height of the audio craze. As you probably already know Marantz built some of the best receivers offered during that time. This particular unit put out 130 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It also featured: An average 2330B will sell for around $1500 in decent working condition. Over $2000 in very good working condition. Update: Recent sale for $2100 on 8-2021. This receiver was in excellent condition and fully serviced with new LED lamps and a new wood case as well. Whoa! Please tell me where I can get a 2330B for a mere $200 as you suppose in your blog?","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2330 B","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2330-b","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-2385":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Marantz 2385. The one pictured is most likely a European version as it has no Dolby. The Euro version also has two Aux inputs. The 2385 was made from 1977 through 1980 and retailed for round $1100.00. The 2385 had some muscle and put out 185 watts per channel using a large toroidal power supply. Marantz was known for under rating their power output back in those days so it probably put out more then the specified 185 watts. It measures 19.25 x 17.25 x 7 and weighs in at just over 57 pounds. This Marantz 2385 has what appears to be a reproduction wood cabinet. The original optional WC-124 wood case is, I believe, a three piece cabinet with grills on the side as well as the top.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 2385","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-2385","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-c-32":{"more":[{"t":"This is a preamplifier created from uncompromising traditional craftsmanship. An output of 12W + 12W is available at the speaker connection terminal on the rear panel. When used in conjunction with an input selector switch, it is also possible to drive an active speaker system. The headphone port on the front can be driven by either a dynamic type or a condenser type and has a dedicated volume. FET is used for all input changeover switches. Minute DC voltage turns ON/OFF the FET, does not affect the frequency characteristics, and suppresses the generation of switching noise. Equipped with a 5-band program, equalizer and defeat switch. Adjustment of ± 12 dB is possible around 30 Hz, 150 Hz, 500 Hz, 1500 Hz and 10000 Hz. It is equipped with separate switches for both playback and recording.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh C 32 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/c32-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-dqx-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥150,000. Armless player pursuing custom made player system as the successor of DDX-1000. Turntable is made of aluminum die-cast diameter 31cm. In particular, it depends on the iner moment of turntable to improve overall characteristics. The drive motor is equipped with a PLL quartz lock type DC motor. The speed dev is 0% when 3g needle pressure is added to the outermost part.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki DQX-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/dqx-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nakamichi-410":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥70,000. Preamplifier for improved distortion and SN ratio. In the actual circuit, the signal source impedance Rs is added to hie. In this case, because the value of Rs is larger than hie and the thermal noise generated by Rs is more large, it is often ignored. However, if MC cartridge is very small Rs, hie will increase the influence of SN ratio. In addition, the SN ratio is improved by using the transdB with low current noise. Normally preamplifier adopts differential amplifier because it is easy to configure negative feedback (NF) circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nakamichi 410 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/410.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nakamichi-420":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥75,000. 400 Series Stereo Power The circuit method has a complete mirrored push pull circuit. Nude characteristics with no negative feedback (NF), 0.1% of harmonic distortion (1kHz, 50W) and negative feedback (NF) are measured by Narrow band real-time and Spectrum analyzer. In fact, it has a simple configuration and a gain 100dB required for negative feedback (NF).","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nakamichi 420 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/420.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nakamichi-620":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥150,000. 600 Series Stereo Power The circuit configuration includes the newly developed complete mirrored push pull circuit. This circuit is the initial stage of the current mirror load differential, but the output stage has been changed. It is named as a complete mirror because it has a structure like a mirror. In order to solve this problem, the complete mirrored configuration is developed as a way to cancel differences in characteristics by successfully NPN and PNP in the circuit. This circuit configuration realizes a low distortion rate of 5PPM while having 100W+100W output.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nakamichi 620 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/620.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nikko-nr-1415":{"more":[{"t":"The Nikko NR-1415 was introduced in 1978 and comfortably fits within the Monster Receiver category as it produces 175 watts per channel. It was Nikko’s top-of-the-line receiver at the time and retailed for $830. In Japan Nikko was known for their high quality industrial products and they tried to apply the same design principles to their audio line. They focused on over performance and reliability. They certainly succeeded with the NR-1415. The limited edition NR-1415. An important statement in pure power, styling and luxury of features. It’s an AM/FM stereo receiver with character. The NR-1415 has signal and tuning meters as well as a mid range tone control.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Nikko NR-1415","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/nikko-nr-1415","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-2500":{"more":[{"t":"This Onkyo TX-2500 receiver is a low to mid-range offering from Onkyo with the TX-8500 being the big dog at the time. I’ve always liked the look of the Onkyo receivers – even the bolt on front dial glass. When all the bulbs work and they are lit up they have the warm glow of candle light. This particular TX-2500 is the MK II version which does differ slightly from the regular TX-2500. I believe the TX-2500 came out around 1976-77 and the revised MK II around 1978. The MK II had a retail price of around $360.00. Onkyo’s TX-2500 is listed at 27 watts per channel while the Tx-2500 MK II is listed at 40 watts per channel. Of course, the late 70’s were the height of the receiver wars where each manufacturer was trying to outdo the other with more watts per channel and other features. This is probably why Onkyo decided to up the ante with the power output.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-2500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-2500-mki","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"revox-b-790":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥198,000. Turntable using linear tracking method. The turntable part adopts the direct drive method by quartz control. The tonearm section contains only 38mm ultra short Tangential tonearm. Tonearm control requires an electronic servo. VMS20EmkII","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Revox B 790 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/player/b790.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sae-2100":{"more":[{"t":"A preamplifier that can handle any music source and has been developed to make all components work flexibly. As a control function, it is equipped with SAE unique parametric equalizer which can continuously change frequency, level and band width. Equipped with two tape copy circuits and 30Hz/100Hz switching low filter.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – SAE 2100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SAE/amp/2100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sae-2600":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo power amplifier with high power design of 400W + 400W. All stages of complimentary service circuit is adopted for circuit structure. The first stage is a differential-amplified dual complimentary service circuit, and the pre-driver stage is a push-pull amplified full complimentary service circuit. Up to this point, the amplification is class A. The driver stage is divided into Pch and Nch, amplified by a push-pull amplified complimentary service circuit with separate transistors, and connected to the complimentary service stage of the full output circuit. This characteristic circuit is called a PSO (Parallel-Series-Output) circuit. In general power amplifier designs, the circuit system from a single-configuration driver stage to a differential amplifier output stage cannot avoid low-frequency modulation noise for a large output and causes a decrease in SN ratio. However, by adopting a PSO circuit, a low distortion factor is realized over a wide band. Various considerations have been added to the transformer used in the power supply section to cope with high power.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – SAE 2600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SAE/amp/2600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sae-2900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥220,000. preamplifier with parametric equalizer. Two tape monitors are equipped. Low filter is mounted on 2 points of 30Hz and 100Hz.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE 2900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/2900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-707":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥93,800. The first integrated amplifier of the 707 series was developed in pursuit of physical characteristics under the development theme that new sound is produced by a novel circuit that understands the essence of audio. When a program source with a large dynamic range and a dense music signal is reproduced by an amplifier with a large bare gain and a large amount of negative feedback (NF) applied to improve the distortion, transient intermodulation distortion (Transient Intermodulation) occurs due to an unstable element such as delay in the amplifier circuit, and the resolution deteriorates. Transient Intermodulation Distortion (TIM) occurs at the summing point, which is the synthesis point of the input signal and negative feedback (NF) signal, because the negative feedback (NF) operation is momentarily lost due to the delay in the circuit, and an excessive input enters the amplifier. Therefore, it was difficult to achieve a wide range with conventional amplifiers. In the AU 607, we examined the bare characteristics before applying negative feedback (NF), and expanded the frequency characteristics, improved the phase characteristics, and reduced the distortion factor. We also improved the phase characteristics up to several tens of MHz by combining a unique phase correction circuit with an appropriate stagger ratio for phase advance and phase delay. By applying the minimum necessary negative feedback (NF), the transient intermodulation distortion is improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-707 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-707-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-2000":{"more":[{"t":"The Sansui G-2000 was added to the Sansui receiver lineup around 1977 and retailed for about $240.00. It was advertised as a High Specification AM/FM Receiver at a Competitive Price. The ‘G’ series of receivers from Sansui are some of the most popular Sansui gear nowadays. The G-2000 is at the bottom of the line in terms of performance but is still built exceptionally well and looks great too. The G-2000’s features are limited with just Bass and Treble tone controls, a Loudness button as well as FM Muting, Mode, and Tape Monitor buttons. Sansui had an eye for symmetry and the front panel looks very balanced. The meter located just above the Volume and Tuning knobs add to the effect. The knobs also have a beveled edge that add a touch of class to its appearance. 16 watts per channel is all this little guy puts out but that’s plenty for use in a garage or bedroom.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-2000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-2000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-3000":{"more":[{"t":"The Sansui G-3000 receiver was introduced in 1977 and was on the market until about 1979. It retailed for around $280 and while it was at the lower end of the Sansui lineup it was by no means a cut-rate receiver. It is full featured, produces 26 watts per channel, and is known for its clean, detailed sound. The G-3000 was part of a Sansui receiver line that included the G-2000, G-5000, G-6000, G-7000, G-8000, G-9000, G-22000 and the monster G-33000. Quite a lineup! The aesthetic of the G-X000 series is a little different than other receiver lines at that time due to their gold dial face and warm yellow lighting. Sansui marketed it as: The Sansui G-3000 certainly doesn’t look like a budget stereo. The simulated woodgrain cabinet has a more finished look than the typical black painted metal, and the brushed aluminum faceplate with gold dial adds visual appeal. Details like the oversized, flywheel-assisted, tuning knob and stepped volume control also give it a high-end feel.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-3000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-3000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-5000":{"more":[{"t":"Pure Power! That was the tag line for Sansui’s G-Series receivers from the late 70’s and they lived up to the advertising hype. Even this mid range Sansui G-5000 is one great performer. In fact, many audio enthusiasts make the claim that the early Sansui G series receivers are some of the best receivers ever made in terms of both build quality and performance. The audio industry was evolving at the time and technology was advancing to a point where audio equipment could do a far better job of amplifying sound in a manner that kept it as close to the original recorded sound as possible. Sansui’s DC circuitry did just that. If you had grown up listening to music on late 60’s tube equipment or early 70’s Pioneer or Marantz gear then you might find the G series receivers a tad bright and less warm. But, personal preferences aside, they produce a more accurate sound than their earlier counterparts that tended to “color” the music. The G-5000 was produced from 1978 to 1980 and really is a great representative of the vintage audio years.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-5000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-5000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sanyo-tp-1100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥44,800. Direct drive type player system with customized return function. 20 pole 30 slots DC servo motor is available for drive motor. Equipped with auto-cutting mechanism. Tonearm is equipped with anti-scaling mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo TP-1100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/player/tp-1100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥39,800. Record player with linear slotless motor. A direct drive system using a new linear slotless motor is available. This motor has a stable constant torque with a linear drive method, and the coil and magnet are more thinner and more efficient because of the polarized structure. Equipped with a fully automatic mechanism for auto-reed in, auto-return, auto-cut and auto-repeat. Our proprietary clutch mechanism enables smooth operation. Front control enables operation with closed dust cover. Manual operation is possible by changing the size selector. tonearm provides a static balance type with precision pivot bearings in the bearing section.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥45,800. Manual type crystal lock player. The motor adopts a new linear slotless motor, which is a direct drive system that turns turntable directly. This motor uses a very low torque linear drive system, which enables smooth and quiet rotation. In addition, the use of polarized air core coils and magnet rings with strong magnetic force increases torque efficiently, and the simple structure increases reliability and durability. The servo detection unit is equipped with a magnet disk rotation speed detection method that introduces the technology of Sony Magnescale precision measuring machine. This detection method greatly improves the rise characteristics, and has a stable rotation that is not affected by disturbances. are caught up to the detection limit. Turntable is made of 32cm aluminum die cast.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥59,800. Full automatic player with slotless motor and crystal lock. The direct drive method is used to rotate the turntable directly by the motor. The motor is equipped with a new linear slotless motor. Kono motor uses a linear drive system with very little torque unevenness in principle, making it smooth and quiet. In addition, the use of equilibrium air core coils and magnet rings increases torque efficiently. The servo detection unit is equipped with Sony's proprietary magnetic count detection method which introduces the technology of Sony Magnescale precision measuring machine. This detection method greatly improves the rise characteristics and realizes stable rotation that is strong to external disturbance. The crystal lock is adopted for PS-8750 to achieve greater rotational speed accuracy. The difference between the conventional servo circuit of this method is that it adds the phase control circuit of the crystal oscillation to the speed servo circuit servo the magnetic disk.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x6.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-1630":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥29,800. The power and solid sound quality are the top priority.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-1630 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-1630.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-8650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1973 at ¥295,000. V-FET adoption No. 1 integrated amplifier to realize true waveform transmission. This was the first model of the ES-II series, which developed the ES series up to that by developing a new device, such as V-FET, a modularized DC amplifier, etc. V-FET is a unique device developed by Sony. It has features such as high input impedance low output impedance characteristics, N-Channel P-Channel complementary characteristics, and voltage responsiveness. It has excellent high frequency characteristics and has low crossover distortion and notching distortion. The equalizer stage is equipped with BX-2IC and IC amplifier. It has excellent phase characteristics from direct current to MHz order. Phono1 is general use, Phono2 has three positions: Low, High, MC type amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-8650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-8650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-e-7-b":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥150,000. High-end preamplifier with a thorough improvement of physical properties, realizing simple signal pathways and rich control functions. The main signal transmission path is a very simple structure called equal amplifier → flat amplifier. In the first stage, a dual-FET casing mirror differential a ification, and the second step is a negative feedback (NF) type equalizer amplifier that connects PNP trans with a constant current load. The flat amplifier is the DC amplifier of the two-stage direct connection circuit called PNP trans, which is the first step of the differential a ification by FET and the second step has a constant current load. Direct coupling method is adopted on the input side. The head amplifier part for MC cartridge is the same as the head amplifier HA-55, and the first stage is the same as the LEC trans-55 with low noise and lowers the equivalent noise resistance and improves the SN ratio. FET power supply is available to bring out the goodness of each amplifier stage. By simplifying Phono inputs and signal paths by changing relays, we have improved low crosstalk and SN ratio. Three-mode indicator large-level meter is equipped with a touch panel hold function that enables the peak level change to be read appropriately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-E 7 B (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-e7b.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-4":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥49,800. In addition to excellent regulation, DC integrated amplifier adopts power supply without power supply ham. Tone control is equipped with a self-defeit tone control, which automatically defeits the tone circuit when the thrush is placed on a defeit position. In addition, it is equipped with two-way tape copy switch that can be Tape1→2, and 2→1 regardless of the signal of the amplifier body.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f4.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥59,800. DC integrated amplifier with pulse power supply with superior regulation of conventional power supply. In the pulse power supply, when AC100V is activated, it becomes DC and eliminates the influence on the ham signal system. By increasing the gain of the low-noise design equal amplifier, the MC input works similar to the built-in head amplifier. Tone control uses a self-defeit tone control that automatically defeits the tone circuit when setting a thrush to the center position. Tone amplifier is negative feedback (NF) type, and it uses carefully selected parts.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-6-b":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥99,800. DC integrated amplifier developed and mounted pulse lock power supply using electronic circuit technology to realize better power supply. In addition, voltage from power to pre-voltage is reduced according to FET buffer power supply. Dual FET is equipped with equalizer amplifier of current mirror differential a ification configuration, which improves low frequency transmission characteristics with direct coupling. The power amplifier part adopts the source folois circuit using dual FET and the monolithic IC on the driver stage, and the end is the Pure Complementary SEPPOTL circuit. We have a DC configuration that does not have a low phase.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 6 B (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f6b.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-n-7-b":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥160,000. We use semiconductors carefully selected from V-FET, and also introduce technologies such as FET buffer power supply. TA-N7B solves the problem of stability that is the problem of DC amplifier, such as suppressing DC drift with a dual FET developed by Sony semiconductor technology. In order to suppress the mirror effect caused by the return capacity of the output side, the casscode connection prevents the transmission capacity at high frequency and greatly improves the linearity. FET buffer power supply circuit reduces noise distortion caused by power supply. This makes it possible to obtain channel separation characteristics beyond the measurement limit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-N 7 B (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n7b.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-a-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1977 at ¥1,000,000. A + Stereo DC power amplifier that realizes low distortion and high power by class operation. A developed by Technics + Class amplification system is adopted. Class A amplifier has the advantage of sound quality because the straight line part of the amplifier element is used in the full cycle of the signal, so there is no switching distortion or crossover distortion in principle. However, it has the disadvantage that half of the peak current must always be supplied even when there is no signal, and it is inefficient as an amplifier circuit. A adopted for SE-A1 + In the class operation, the ground potential of the class A amplifier, which requires a constant current, is floated, and if necessary, a high voltage is supplied from a separate power amplifier in synchronization with the amplitude of the audio signal, thereby eliminating forced air-cooling fans while maintaining output. The power supply section is equipped with a large-capacity toroidal transformer with low DC resistance, one on each of the left and right sides, and an electrolytic capacitor is A. + It is equipped with 4 100,000 μ Fx4 for class amplifier and 4 22,000 μ Fx4 for power amplifier. It is composed of 2 monaural with 4 power supplies per channel and total 8 power supplies. A DC amplifier configuration that eliminates the input / output coupling capacitor and the capacitor in the NFB loop realizes excellent waveform transmission characteristics.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1400-mk-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1977 at ¥95,000. SL-1300mk2 Auto-stop is available. Also, cabinet is matte black finish. We use the quartz synthesizer method to lock all 199 pitches. The tweak amount displays the light emitting diode display digitally. Tonearm uses a gimbal suspension method that intersects horizontal and vertical rotation at a point and achieves the initial motion sensitivity 7mg. It is equipped with a 6mm armrest adjustment mechanism to use cartridge for sibbia.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1400 MK 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1400mk2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1500-mk-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1977 at ¥80,000. Manual type Quartz Synthesizer direct drive player. We use a quartz synthesizer method to lock all pitches of 199 points.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1500 MK 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1500mk2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1600-mkii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥75,000. Fully automatic player with continuous pitch control by newly developed IC and automatic mechanism by micro computer and infrared application technology. The record size and the presence of the record are three LEDs and optical placed under turntable. Turntable uses aluminum die-casting products, as well as rubber deadening of the back surface to ensure thorough hauling. In addition, the drive motor is equipped with a unique integrated direct-drive motor. In addition, all-round detection FG is adopted to the rotation speed detection mechanism to realize high-precision rotation speed detection. The Quartz Synthesizer circuit adopts a new development IC, which enables continuous pitch control in the range of ±6%. In addition, any pitch is locked to the oscillation frequency of the diaper. The pitch change can be confirmed with the LED pitch display in the bar graph display, and the red LED lights at 0% in the pitch or at 1% in +. Built-in electronic brake to stop turntable instantly.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1600 MKII (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1600mkii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-7300":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier with a side terminal structure to realize a straight circuit structure. A side terminal structure is adopted. All input signal terminals are laid out on the right side, and the speaker terminals are laid out on the left side. This realizes a circuit configuration according to the signal flow. The equalizer circuit uses an IC of the first stage differential amplifier configuration with current mirror load. In the pre-drive stage of the main amplifier section, a differential amplifier of the current mirror load is configured in the first stage to realize a low distortion factor. In addition, since tone control is performed using the negative feedback (NF) circuit of the main amplifier, the circuit block has a simple structure consisting of an equalizer section and a power amplifier section. The power supply circuit is equipped with a high-density winding transformer and 6,800 μ Fx2 electrolytic capacitor. Equipped with a power meter that can switch the range between 0 dB and -10dB.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-7300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-7300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-7700":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier with a side terminal structure to realize a straight circuit structure. The terminals are directly connected to the printed circuit board without wires, and input signals are directly input to the circuit. In addition, the side terminal layout enables straight transmission. An IC configuration is used for the equalizer circuit. The first stage consists of differential amplification of a current mirror load, which can select an operating current with very little noise, and the output stage consists of an emitter follower with a constant current load. The noise level is reduced because the gain of the first stage is large. In order to obtain accurate frequency characteristics, a metal film resistance of ± 1% deviation and a polypropylene capacitor of ± 2% deviation are used for the equalizer element. In the first stage of the main amplifier section, a differential amplifier is composed of a pair transistor of one package, and it is operated by the current mirror load. In the first stage, a high gain is obtained with low distortion, and the negative feedback by negative feedback (NF) technology is being promoted.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-7700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-7700-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-a-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1977 at ¥1,600,000. A preamplifier with low distortion by class-A operation in all stages. In order to completely remove switching distortion and crossover distortion, all stages are operated as class A. As a result, the rated distortion factor of 0.003% is achieved at 20 Hz to 20 kHz and 1 V output from the Phono MM to the output terminal. A low-noise dual FET is used for MM, and newly developed low-noise transistors M67L and M68L are used for MC preamp, resulting in high S / N ratio. The SU-A2 employs a DC amplifier configuration that eliminates the interstage capacitor of the signal system and the capacitor with a time constant in the NFB loop. As a result, the amplifier has a DC gain and eliminates the phase loop, improving the fidelity of waveform transmission. Moreover, the coupling capacitor is removed from the phono equalizer to form a DC equalizer. In order to suppress DC drift, which is the most important point of DC amplifier, an active thermal servo amplifier with thermal feedback is adopted. For switching the input selector and the recording mode selector, a touch switch method is adopted in which a high-reliability relay for small signals is operated by a micro switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a2-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sa-520":{"more":[{"t":"Here’s an interesting receiver from Tokyo Shibaura, otherwise know as Toshiba. This Toshiba SA-520 is a mid range model and, as you can see, has a little bit of a different design than many of the other receivers of the same era. This unit was made around 1977-1978 and almost looks like two thin units set atop one another. The big square push buttons and slider knobs give it a distinct look as well. I can’t really say it’s appealing to the eye. The tuner dial and face look a little like Pioneer while the bottom, well, I’m not sure. The SA-520 is listed as 40 watts per channel and, believe it or not, weighs in at roughly 35 pounds! That’s a pretty hefty weight for a mid range receiver. But, these Toshibas were actually built really well and the SA-520 has a large transformer and big power supply caps which add to the weight.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Toshiba SA-520","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/toshiba-sa-520","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sc-330":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥30,000. Stereo power of Opus series. It is designed to withstand pulsed instant signals, and it supports music sources such as jazz, rock and orchestra.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SC-330 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sc-330.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sy-330":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥23,000. Stereo preamplifier for Opus series. Two-system tape monitor switch is mounted. Equipped with the microphone mixing mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SY-330 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sy-330.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-eq-7070":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥178,000. phono stage of laboratory 7070 series using EL-FET. EQ-7070 is a phono stage with a large number of inputs and can be used as a preamplifier. EQ-7070 is equipped with EL-FET, which is the element of new development. This EL-FET has a very high inter-inductance Gm (Gm55mΩ at ID 10mA, 8 times or more of the conventional high GmFET) and can design ultra-low noise amplifier. The MC head amplifier section uses 5 EL-FETs in the first stage. In addition, high linearity is ensured by flowing a large current of 50mA per channel. A high S/N ratio is realized by a robust high Gm and affordable dynamic range. The newly developed EL-FET is adopted for the first time of the equalizer series.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor EQ-7070 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/etc/eq-7070.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-m-2020":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥79,500. In this method, power supply for A-grade amplifier is set independently from power itself. instead of constant voltage. It is a DC amplifier configuration that does not have a low frequency time constant in the signal path, and a new development dual FET is installed in the first stage circuit to increase stability. Dual FET is a single package containing two FETs of characteristics. It has good thermal equilibrium and very low DC drift due to temperature change.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor M-2020 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/m-2020.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-p-2020":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥54,500. 2020 series preamplifier. To support MC cartridge, we have a head equipped with 6 carefully selected low-noise FETs. Tone circuit is the same as equalizer. In addition, new consideration is added to volume control accuracy and accuracy to pursue the accuracy of change characteristics. With this, a total of 21 clickpoints have less swelling properties. In addition, the frequency characteristic and distortion rate of the tone switch on/DEFEAT are almost unchanged in the flat position.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor P-2020 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/p-2020.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/victor-p-2020.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/p-2020.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/p-2020.JPG"}},"yamaha-a-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥115,000. Simple design and straight DC & DC configuration. The circuit configuration of A-1 is a simple one called low noise MC head amplifier -DC equalizer -DC high gain power amplifier. In addition, when the DISC switch is OFF, all functions stored in the sealing panel can be selected, and tone control circuit of 0dB gain can be used as needed. This circuit configuration is realized by accepting the gains around 20dB which are usually received in the tone amplifier to the high gain power amplifier. The equalizer circuit is a DC amplifier configuration that eliminates capac circuit and capac of input circuit. In the first stage, the original Super Low Noise DualFET is equipped with the current mirror cast cord boots circuit. In addition, we are equipped with a muting relay to prevent pop noise when power supply ON-OFF. The MM type cartridge differs depending on the input impedance of the amplifier, and the optimum load resistance depends on the cartridge. Therefore, in A-1, the specified load resistance value is obtained by inserting the Cartridge Load plug (47kΩ, 68kΩ) attached to the CartridgeLoad terminal of the rear panel.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-b-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥200,000. SIT for B-3 (tictic Induction Trans = electrostatic induction trans ) 2SK76A (Nch) and 2SJ26A (Pch) are the world's first high-gain SIT2SK-77 developed for B-1, and it is a complementary. In addition, we examine the chip size, impurity concentration, and gate mesh structure of the Pch/Nch device, and strictly control in the manufacturing process to match the pair characteristics of the wide operating range. This dual FET (2SK-100) is supplied in the same package with low-noise and high-gm electrical and thermal characteristics of two FETs. It ensures sufficient pairability required for the first stage of the DC amplifier. This dual-FET is operated with a constant voltage (8V) regardless of the input signal or output voltage, thus the parameter change due to the rise of the element temperature is suppressed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥158,000. The equalizer amplifier, the tone preamplifier, and the MC head amplifier are almost the same circuit configuration as C-2. The first stage is composed of a differential amplifier with the original Super Low Noise FET, and the casscode boots circuit has been adopted and the signal source impedance is high, there is no signal deterioration of the distortion rate. The assembly of the current mirror circuit ensures robust gain and low distortion rate. The voltage amplifier of the first and second stages is supplied with the voltage of ±70V from the constant voltage power supply separately set from the drive and output stage. The power amplifier of the drive and output stage has a high output at low distortion rate, making it a darlington connection pure compound push pull circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-1020":{"more":[{"t":"Manufactured in 1977, the Yamaha CR-1020 receiver was the younger brother of the Yamaha CR-3020 and CR-2020. It incorporated the trademark Yamaha styling with rectangular switches, linear layout, and white meter and dial faces. The CR-1020 puts out a hefty 70 watts per channel and has a rated total harmonic distortion of 0.1%. It retailed for around $540. The CR-1020 has advanced design features borrowed from Yamaha’s high-end audio components such as the B-1 and B-2 power amps, C-1 control amp and CT-7000 tuner. The borrowed features include power meters, presence control, LED function indicators, and a signal quality meter. These give the receiver excellent sound quality, precise control, and useful visual feedback. Non-Step Master Volume Control –The receiver has a smooth, continuous volume control that maintains consistent left/right stereo balance at all levels. This avoids the abrupt volume jumps that can occur with other designs.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-1020","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-1020","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-1020.jpg","xc":2,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-1020","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/01/yamaha-cr-1020-receiver.jpg"}},"yamaha-cr-2020":{"more":[{"t":"If you’re familiar with monster receivers then you know that the Yamaha CR-3020 is a Monster! Well, this receiver is just shy of a monster. Maybe Beast would be appropriate? It’s the Yamaha CR-2020 and is, of course, the smaller sibling of the CR-3020. Yes, the CR-3020 put out a massive 160 watts per channel but this CR-2020 shells out a very respectable 100 watts per channel. Besides, the CR-3020 didn’t even sell all that well. The CR-2020 is a fantastic mix of everything you want in a big, powerful receiver. Lots of power, tons of features, sharp, clean styling and a cool look when the room lights are dimmed. And, for that macho effect it weighs in at about 43 pounds and is over 21 inches wide and 16 inches deep.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-2020","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-2020","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-420":{"more":[{"t":"The Yamaha CR-420 was offered from 1977 through about 1980 and retailed for $290. It was part of Yamaha’s Natural Sound line of audio equipment. It was marketed as a low-powered, affordable integrated receiver that offered the control features and flexibility commonly found in more powerful, expensive models. The CR-420’s styling is classic Yamaha with a brushed aluminum silver face and dial scale, sleek cabinet, and large selector switches. The Natural Sound concept is to reproduce natural, unbiased sound that is very clean and true to the original source. Many feel this is the case with the Yamaha receivers. Others think this is just marketing hype. Either way the Yamaha CR line of receivers does produce a very clean sound. The CR-420 has a narrow front dial display with linear frequency scales for FM and AM radio bands.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-420","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-420","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-620":{"more":[{"t":"The Yamaha CR-620 was one of Yamaha’s mid-range units from 1977-1979. It produces 35 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It has the classic Yamaha styling and was rated at 0.015% total harmonic distortion. The unit weighs in at just over 23 pounds. The CR-620 was part of Yamaha’s CR-xx20 series that included the CR-220, CR-420, CR-620, CR-820, CR-1020, CR-2020, and, eventually, the monster CR-3020. The CR-620 stereo receiver has a sleek and minimalist design. The front panel is made of satin aluminum with a long dial cut-out in the center. The dial cut-out contains no decorative bezels or multi-colored illumination, giving the CR-620 a clean and uncluttered look. The main tuning dial in the center is flanked by red LED power and stereo indicators.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-620","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-620","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-820":{"more":[{"t":"This is a classic upper mid-range receiver from the late 1970’s. It is the Yamaha CR-820 and was on the market from around 1977 to 1979. It produced 55 watts per channel into 8 ohms and had low distortion ratings. In fact, while most manufacturers measured distortion at the rated output of the unit, Yamaha measured the distortion over a wide range of power output. They called this the Noise Distortion Clearance Range (NDCR). They trademarked the phrase ‘Real Life Rated’ because they measured noise and distortion at -20dB from the inputs all the way through to the speaker output as opposed to just measuring the amp section. They believed this would give a better indication of performance in a true listening environment. The Yamaha CR-820 retailed for around $460.00 and had the classic Yamaha styling of the time with monochrome face plate, clean knobs and over sized rectangular switches. The receivers from this series all have a clean, almost sterile, machined look to them.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-820","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-820","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-1000-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1976 at ¥150,000. The motor is equipped with a 20-pole 60-slot, multi-pole, high torque DC servo motor. The turntable adopts 31cm self-heavy 2.8kg in diameter, and the thick aluminum plate is sharpened with high processing accuracy, and the dynamic balance is precise. This turntable has a sufficiently large value of iner mass 380kg/cm2, and maintains accurate rotation against load ctuations. The power supply has a strict shield that suppresses the negative impact of vibration. Tonearm is a UA-7 company manufactured by Stax. In addition, the in-side for scanning cellar is adopted by the counter bar and roller arm method to obtain the cancellation amount according to each needle pressure. Needle pressure adjustment is double weight method, and the needle pressure adjustment is possible.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-1000 II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-1000ii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-yp-1000-ii.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-1000ii.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-1000ii.JPG"}},"yamaha-yp-211":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥30,000. Belt drive player with stable basic performance. This motor is difficult to measure voltage ctuations and load ctuations. Turntable bearings and motor pulleys are made by micron order. Tonearm uses a light alloyed S-shaped pipe arm to make high sensitivity. In addition, gold plating is installed on the headshell terminal. cartridge has MM type cartridge cartridge-4500II. With the semi-auto mechanism, arm automatically rises from the record surface and turnstable stops when it finishes.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-211 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-211.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-yp-211.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-211.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-211.JPG"}},"yamaha-yp-311":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥33,000. belt drive player with easy to use and simple design. The drive system adopts a belt drive system with high technical stability, and drives a 30cm aluminum die-cast turntable with a 4-pole motorronus motor. Tonearm is a S-shaped pipe arm made with precise processing technology while pursuing simplicity. Equipped with in-side for scanning and arm height adjustment mechanism. M75BM is a MM type cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-311 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-311.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-yp-311.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-311.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-311.JPG"}},"yamaha-yp-511":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1975 at ¥43,800. A record player who is trying to reduce the negative impact of vibration by increasing the weight of the required part. Motor features 8-pole 24-slot DC servo motor with large torque. In addition, by improving the response of the servo circuit, it is possible to maintain accurate rotational speed even for load ctuations. In addition, the turntable rubber sheet also has strict hearing test to determine the sound material and shape. With a 1.3kg arm base made of lead alloy die-cast on the arm base, it prevents harmful vibrations by fixing the arm’s feet firmly and suppresses negative impact on regenerative sound. The arm adopts a special filling material in a light alloy pipe that is resistant to twist and suppresses resonance of the pipe itself. In addition, the weighted shaft for the main shaft of the rotating bearing part and the needle pressure applied is connected via the rubber damper and the bearing case and the main shaft are connected via the rubber damper. In addition, the main shaft also eliminates aluminum pipes that are usually often used, and it reduces resonance by cutting out brass.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-511 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-511.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-yp-511.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-511.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-511(3).jpg"}},"yamaha-yp-b-4":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥40,000. Record player with excellent parts for each point. The drive method is a belt drive method, and the turntable made of aluminum die-cast with a diameter of 30 cm and weight of 1.1 kg is driven by a 4-pole motorronus motor. The turntable is precisely dynamically balancing from the mold stage, and it is precisely finished with the table turn bearing and motor pulley, which are the driving point. Tonearm adopts precisely lateral-balanced S-shaped pipe arm and holds it with zinc die-cast holders with high rigidity and low sound. In addition, it is equipped with a direct reading scale in-side for scancera, arm lifter, and 0.5g step countering needle pressure adjustment. Headshell is an EIA standard plug-in method that reduces contact failure by gold plating output terminal. In addition, we have a dynamic damping system that reduces arm resonance by matching the resonance frequency of the balance weight mass and the rover bush schifness around 10 Hz. M75BM is a MM type cartridge. Equipped with auto mechanism such as auto-reed in, auto-return, auto-cut and auto-repeat.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-B 4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-b4.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-d-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥128,000. A record player who pursues high-dimensional sound by Ultimate Refining Method. The UR method focuses on changing the sound by parts and materials that make up every part, and it controls the vibration mode by suppressing micro-vibration to the level of human hearing. This increases the completeness of the sound. In order to achieve more stable rotation, YP-D10’s drive system is a three-stage structure that provides FGtz PLL servo for low frequency disturbances, and FG servo for high frequency disturbances. The motor has a large torque of 1.2kg and cm. The FG servo method is a method to control the rotation speed of turntable by detecting the signal and controlling the rotation speed of turntable. The quartz PLL servo method introduced to further enhance the rotational accuracy of this FG servo method is a method that controls the frequency of the output signal from FG to the phase threshold of the reference signal oscillation by the crystal oscillator. The rotation accuracy of this quartz PLL is within ±20ppm including the temperature drift. The turntable is made of aluminum die-cast with a diameter of 31 cm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-D 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d10.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-d-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥39,800. Record player with direct drive. The DC servo motor has a 600g/cm startup torque. The turntable is 33cm in diameter and the iner mass is 220kg/cm. Tonearm uses a static balance type S-shaped pipe arm, which is firmly fixed with a zinc die-cast holder with high rigidity and low sound. It is a standard type that can be used for self-heavy 4g to 11g cartridge. A dynamic damping system that suppresses arm resonance. The headshell uses the EIA standard plug-in light shell, which can be replaced. In addition, gold plating is applied to the connector part with arm to reduce sound quality deterioration caused by poor contact.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-D 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-d-9":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥75,000. A record player with almost the same configuration except eliminating two silent ending mechanisms and pitch controllers from YP-D10. DC motor drive system with 1.2kg/cm startup torque is available in the drive unit. Turntable is a 31.5cm aluminum die-cast table turn table with precise dynamic balance. The power supply part has a powerful one that can take out a large capacity of 1000mA and maintain a constant voltage of 24V. In addition to triple-structure shielding in the power supply section, the SN ratio is improved by taking note of the anti-vibration measures of SN. Tonearm is a gimbal support system made by a pivot polished chromium molybdenum steel. The special aluminum alloy S-shaped pipe arm with a horizontal and vertical initial sensitivity of 3mg or less is adopted. In addition, headshell has sufficient strength and light weight by adopting special aluminum alloy diecast. It also supports various cartridges by arm height adjustment mechanism of 6mm stroke.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-D 9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d9.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-und-micro-seiki-px-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥480,000. The PX-1 arm feed mechanism is designed to move the arm base with six dellin bearing rollers on the guide rail polished to two precision. In order to move this arm base at a stable and smooth speed that matches the pitch of the record, the high-precision non-contact photoelectric arm angle detection mechanism detects the arm angle and controls the signal to the arm drive mechanism using the coreless motor controlled by the servo circuit that suppresses the erroneous operation of the record. This arm drive mechanism drives arm base with a precision polishing finish drive screw low friction. Also, it is paid attention such as conveying torque through the rubber belt so that the vibration is not transmitted to the drive screw. Linear tracking arm is a 190mm short arm, and the iner mass is 40% less than offset arm by adopting a horizontal balance weight in a rectangle and attaching a shell connector to the arm perspective.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha und Micro Seiki PX-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/px-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-c-240":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1978. Stereo preamplifier designed for high-end audio systems. The panel layout is completely unique with a push switch. The circuit configuration is a class A DC system with a symmetrical push-pull drive for all amplification stages. Elements that affect sound quality are also used. The panel face consists of four rotary knobs, one lever switch and 57 push switches. In particular, the input selector is electronically controlled to control the relay in the circuit, and can be switched by feather touch. By taking advantage of the electronic control system, it is possible to store ON/OFF information for each cartridge in accordance with DISC1 and DISC2. Also, in order to improve contact resistance of push switches and relays which affect sound quality and durability, all of them are constructed using two circuit arrangement. A fully symmetrical push-pull circuit is used from the head amplifier inlet to the output and in all the amplification stages of the headphone amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-240 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-240-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-e-303":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1978 at ¥245,000.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase E-303 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/E-303-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-1200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥49,800. Direct drive A record player equipped with an auto lift mechanism that considers ease of use without compromising the basic performance of the player. Direct drive system is available for driving. DENON's proprietary high-precision magnetic recording detection method is used to detect rotation speed. DENON’s proprietary method of detecting magnetic heads with 1,000 high-precision pulse signals on the magnetic body coated inside the turntable rim. Even if the load conditions such as needle pressure and arm position change, there are few changes in rotation speed even if the external conditions such as power supply voltage, frequency ctuation, and humidity change are changed. The drive motor is equipped with AC servo motor. Equipped with an auto lift mechanism by contactless end detection. The DP-1200 record end detection method adopts a contactless method that optically detects the speed of moving tonearm when moving from the sound and groove of the record to the leadout.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-1200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-1200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-501":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier equipped with a newly developed PCC system to bring out the essence of records. While maintaining almost the same configuration as the PMA-701, cost reduction has been attempted. The PCC (Phono Crosstalk Canceler) is a device that adds reverse crosstalk to the Phono Pickup type crosstalk and cancels it out. By using the attached adjustment record to operate two knobs, it is possible to improve the frequency range most easily perceived by the ear to approximately -40dB. The power amplifier section is composed of a direct-coupled OCL circuit for all stages of differential amplification. It is composed of a low-impedance power supply circuit, and new power transistors such as double epitaxial structure and triple diffusion structure are adopted for the output final stage respectively. To protect the speakers from errors and accidents, it has a built-in protection circuit with extremely fast response time and high reliability. In consideration of the effect on sound quality, we have adopted a relay with a special structure. In order to improve crosstalk caused by interference between channels, mutual interference is reduced by a circuit configuration in which two circuits are separated, and by disconnecting the power supply of a power circuit with high current and the power supply of a preamplifier circuit with low current.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-501 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-501-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-630":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥65,000. Simple circuit configuration is used as a pre-atta amplifier. PMA-630 is a straight type amplifier that combines two high-performance amplifiers. The non-disk playback program is directly connected to the DC power amplifier so there is no worry about the turbidity or distortion of the sound in the middle amplifier. For this reason, the power amplifier unit achieves high power while obtaining high power. The equalizer amplifier part is larger than 42dB (1kHz, 125 times).","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PMA-630 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pma-630.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-701":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier equipped with a newly developed PCC system to bring out the essence of records. The PCC (Phono Crosstalk Canceler) is a device that adds reverse crosstalk to the Phono Pickup type crosstalk and cancels it out. By using the attached adjustment record to operate two knobs, it is possible to improve the frequency range most easily perceived by the ear to approximately -40dB. The power amplifier section is composed of a direct-coupled OCL circuit for all stages of differential amplification. It is composed of a low-impedance power supply circuit, and new power transistors such as double epitaxial structure and triple diffusion structure are adopted for the output final stage respectively. To protect the speakers from errors and accidents, it has a built-in protection circuit with extremely fast response time and high reliability. In consideration of the effect on sound quality, we have adopted a relay with a special structure. In order to improve crosstalk caused by interference between channels, mutual interference is reduced by a circuit configuration in which two circuits are separated, and by disconnecting the power supply of a power circuit with high current and the power supply of a preamplifier circuit with low current. To prevent the small signal sent from the record player from being degraded by wiring or changeover switches, one phono input circuit is used and the input terminal is directly connected to the equalizer amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-701 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-701-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-830":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥89,000. amplifiermetric push pull method is used. PMA-830 is the first 850metrical push-pull circuit used in all stages. In order to get the most out of this circuit, the new A-class motion amplifier is added to the B-class motion amplifier configuration. Also, the equalizer amplifier gain is 42dB (1kHz, 126 times) and the equalizer amplifier amplifier output can be directly connected to the power amplifier. Direct couples can be switched to a simpler circuit configuration if no control function is required. The amplifiermetrical A-grade push pull circuit is used in the middle amplifier, which plays the role of the tone amplifier and flat amplifier. In addition, tone control is a structure that removes the control element in the Deeat position.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PMA-830 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pma-830.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-850":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥109,000. This integrated amplifier has been developed by integrating various technologies for the basic performance of audio players such as transmission characteristics, dynamic range, distortion, and crosstalk. Each unit of the MC head amplifier, EQ amplifier, flat amplifier and power amplifier consists of a full complimentary service (complementary symmetry) circuit using both NPN and PNP transistors over all stages. In each part, the first stage is a differential stage using high-gain NPN and PNP transistors, and the last stage is a push-pull stage. By using such a symmetrical circuit structure, even order harmonic distortion is cancelled out by each other and the total distortion is reduced. The power amplifier uses a newly developed power transistor E. B. T (emitter ballast transistor). F for E. B.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-850 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-850-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-citation-16-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥360,000. Citation16 is based on improved power and improved the completeness. We have succeeded in suppressing the transient distortion component of NFB to less than 80dB from the maximum output level. 2 power supply LED peak level indicator This level meter can set the sensitivity switch according to the output. Citation16S is a model that omits peak level indicator from Citation16A.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon Citation 16 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citation16a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-citation-16-a.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citation16a.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citation16a(1).JPG"}},"harman-kardon-hk-503":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥65,000. Equipped with improved dynamic distortion during cartridge and loudspeaker implementation. New high-speed electronic circuit for high reliability.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 503 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk503.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-hk-505":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥85,000. Equipped with improved dynamic distortion during cartridge and loudspeaker implementation. 21-step tone control button. Phono equalizer High reliability protection circuit with new high-speed electron elements.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 505 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk505.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-hk-340":{"more":[{"t":"The Harman Kardon HK 340 was a budget oriented receiver that was introduced in late 1978 and was at the lower end of the HK lineup. It’s retail price was under $250 and at 20 watts per channel output it was designed to compete with the likes of the Pioneer SX-580, Yamaha CR-220 and Marantz 1520. The hk340 receiver is one of a new series from Harman Kardon designed, built, and tested with new understandings that go far beyond conventional ideas about distortion and the factors that make one component sound better than others. They are the most musically accurate receivers ever devised. The HK 340 followed HK’s famous x30 series of receivers by a few years and differed in appearance from the older line quite a bit. Here’s the earlier HK 630. While the x30 series has a kind of Scandinavian look, the 340/540/560/670 series has a brushed metal, silver face plate and a more conventional tuner dial and meter. The knob design was changed as well and it does seem as though Harman Kardon was looking to reduce production costs somewhat. I don’t believe the HK 340 had an optional wood cabinet available either.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Harman Kardon hk 340","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/harman-kardon-hk-340","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-hk-340.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/harman-kardon-hk-340","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/08/harman-kardon-630-stereo.jpg"}},"hitachi-hca-6500":{"more":[{"t":"A low-noise FET transistor is used in the first stage of the equalizer circuit, and an IC for the equalizer is used in the second stage to achieve high performance. The ICL / DC configuration is used in pursuit of sound quality. Tape dubbing is also possible while enjoying playback from other sources.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HCA-6500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hca-6500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hca-7500":{"more":[{"t":"7500 series preamplifier. The EQ circuit consists of three stages and five elements, with a low-noise bipolar transistor at the first stage, a constant current load at the second stage, and a pure complimentary service push-pull circuit at the last stage. The EQ circuit is driven by a ± 32 v power supply. HCA 7500 has an excellent S / N ratio by selecting the elements and adopting a circuit configuration that considers the mechanism of noise generation. Newly developed capacitors are used for both input and output. Equipped with a cartridge load selection switch, the optimum load can be selected for various cartridges by switching between 4-stage load resistance and 4-stage load capacity. The tone control circuit is a 6-stage FET differential constant-current bipolar push-pull 3-stage direct-coupled circuit. It uses carefully selected low-noise FETs and high-voltage low-noise transistors to achieve low distortion. Under the rated output of 1 V or less, it achieves low distortion over the 20Hz-20kHz band, where the distortion component is hardly detectable against residual noise.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HCA-7500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hca-7500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hma-7500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥95,000. 7500 Series Stereo Power MOS FET HMA-7500 is a new complementary power MOS FET manufacturer. Rodi focuses on the power amplifier of MOS FET, which is used for front end of FM tuner. The power MOS FET has a wide range of N-channel and P-channel complimentary characteristics, which reduces the output naked distortion. This second step differential amplifier directly drives the power MOSFET Pure Complementary Circuit. We eliminate parts that cause sound quality degradation coupled with simple circuit configurations and provide accurate waveform transmission. The power supply section has a power supply circuit on both sides and independently, eliminating transient crosstalks through power supply.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HMA-7500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/hma-7500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-354":{"more":[{"t":"An auto player that uses a unitorque motor. The motor is equipped with a unitorque motor based on Lordi's proprietary technology. The Unitorque Motor is a motor which obtained perfect circular motion from the principle. It consists of a doughnut-shaped rotor magnet magnetized with 8 poles and two sets of star-shaped flat coils offset by 22 ^ 5 degrees. The torque generated by these two coils and magnets is constant at any moment. This principle is called sin 2 Θ + cos 2 Θ = 1 \". The Uni-Torque Motor also adopts a simple structure that is brushless, slotless and coreless, and has significantly improved durability. Equipped with auto return and auto cut auto mechanisms that enable reliable tracing even with light needle pressure cartridges. Equipped with anti-skating mechanism, strobe with neon lamp, and oil dump type arm lifter.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HT-354 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/player/ht-354-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-sr-2004":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced in 1978, the Hitachi SR-2004 receiver fits snugly into the monster category at 200 watts per channel. Hitachi’s top-of-the-line receiver was on par with, or better than, other leading brand receivers. At $949.95 the retail price of the SR-2004 was steep but reasonable given its features and performance. The amplifier, phono and FM sections are all excellent. The styling of the SR-2004 is a bit industrial but still looks nice. The cabinet is similar to the Pioneer SX-1250 in that the front half of the cabinet is wood (actually rosewood vinyl I believe) and the back half, metal and heat sinks. The back half is where the massive toroidal transformer sits along with four large power supply capacitors. The front panel is well laid out and symmetrical. The light-colored dial scale for FM station frequencies is flanked on the left by a pair of power output meters.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Hitachi SR-2004","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/hitachi-sr-2004","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-bn-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥39,800. Biphonic processor to play the binaural recorded source with loudspeaker. The combination of the trans and the delay circuit can reproduce a completely different sound field space. It is equipped with a listening angle switch that clearly determines the sound source such as distance, direction, and depth. It also removes the extract effect of general stereo tape.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC BN-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/etc/bn-5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-bn-5.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/etc/bn-5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/etc/bn-5.JPG"}},"jvc-ja-s-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥65,000. The equalizer part is equipped with a pair FET. ICL circuit using FET to improve the characteristics of the cartridge. The DC circuit of FET/ICL input is used in the same way as equalizer in the tone amplifier. The power amplifier is equipped with a DC amplifier. This reduces power supply impedance over a broadband and reduces distortion to prevent large-current magnetic lines from flying. Low distortion rate multi-contact volume control. Power meter","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JA-S 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ja-s-77":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥80,800. equalizer and tone amplifier, the tri-DC const ent integrated amplifier with the power amplifier. The power amplifier is a complete DC amplifier with low noise dual FET. The preamplifier part is also DC compatible with power amplifier DCDC. In addition, the tone amplifier part is also the DC configuration of the first step FET differential ICL, and the frequency characteristics and distortion rate are almost unchanged regardless of the tone control element ON-Defeat. The equalizer part and the tone amplifier part adopt the pair FET which is joined to keep the same temperature condition.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC JA-S 77 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s77.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-ja-s-77.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s77.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ja-s77.JPG"}},"kenwood-kr-11000-gx":{"more":[{"t":"Well, you don’t see these too often. This is the Kenwood KR-11000 GX. This is the European version of the Eleven GX and many times was purchased by military personnel overseas so it is difficult to find in the U.S. Nonetheless, it is a beast. One of the largest receivers I’ve seen. There are a few different versions of it including the KR-11000G and the Model Eleven G. It is one gorgeous receiver with it’s dark gray face and mix of blue, amber and red lights. Definitely in the class of Monster Receivers it puts out 120 watts per channel. It features a five band EQ with both low and high filters as well.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-11000 GX","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-11000-gx","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-2090":{"more":[{"t":"BOTL, or bottom of the line, receiver sounds a bit harsh for this little Kenwood KR-2090. While it only produces 16 watts per channel it’s not a bad performer. Introduced in 1978 it was an affordable option for budget conscious stereo buyers. It has the classic Kenwood styling of the late 1970’s with silver face plate, large knobs and large, dark gray dial face. It’s a Kenwood so of course its tuner is far above average. Kenwood’s engineers incorporated a 3 gang tuner with a FET front end for high FM sensitivity. At the time of production the KR-2090 had the lowest distortion of any receiver in its class and the quietest phono section as well.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-2090","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-2090","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-6030":{"more":[{"t":"This is a nice Kenwood offering from circa 1978 until about late 1979. It’s the Kenwood KR-6030. It has the classic look of 1970’s Kenwood’s with the exception of the large push buttons that the earlier models used. Instead Kenwood went to toggle switches. The KR-6030 generates plenty of power at 80 watts per channel into 8 ohms and total harmonic distortion of 0.1%. Like a lot of the other Kenwood models it has a great FM tuner section as well. Not bad for a retail price of $525.00. The KR-6030 also has a loudness switch, tone defeat switch and a subsonic filter switch. The analog meters are for tuning and signal strength.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-6030","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-6030","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-8010":{"more":[{"t":"This classic is the Kenwood KR-8010. It was introduced in 1978 and was on the market until about 1981. With 125 watts per channel and 0.03% total harmonic distortion it was near top of the line in Kenwood’s lineup – one step down from the KR-9600. It wasn’t cheap at a retail price of $675 but overall, it is a great looking receiver and excellent performer. The KR-8010 is a beautiful receiver with a brushed aluminum front panel, diamond-machined knobs, analog meters, and an elegant slide-rule dial. The beveled glass is a nice touch as well. Buyer’s had the option of purchasing the CB-14K walnut veneer cabinet, B-14 walnut veneer side panels, or the D-10 carrying handles. The KR-8010 provides sophisticated controls and features. For example, you can copy tapes while listening to another audio source.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-8010","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-8010","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-cl-36":{"more":[{"t":"Released April 1978 at ¥228,000. As a revised version of CL36, a bulb-tube type preamplifier was created with extensive modifications including sound quality, mechanism, and function. The output stage is not a cathode follower but an SRPP (Shunt Regulated Push-Pull) circuit to reduce distortion. This SRPP output circuit is characterized by high input impedance and low output impedance due to its large output voltage and excellent distortion factor characteristics compared with the cathode follower output circuit. The first and second stages use a specially selected low-noise type 12AX7 to improve the signal-to-noise ratio. In addition, careful consideration is given to setting the operating point of the equalizer circuit to improve the distortion factor characteristics, such as canceling waveform distortion mutually. The output stage is a cathode follower circuit, so the input impedance is high. The load condition of the second stage is adjusted, so the distortion factor characteristics and input resistance characteristics are improved. The output impedance is also sufficiently low, ensuring stability that is not affected by the severe load condition to be connected later. When you defeat the tone control circuit, the output is taken directly from this circuit, and a low-boost circuit using an negative feedback (NF) element is inserted into this flat amplifier circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman CL-36 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/cl36-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥54,800. amplifierXMAN's technology is condensed into a slim body. L-1 eliminates flat amplifiers and provides circuit configurations that connect equalizer amplifiers and power amplifiers directly. By simplifying the circuit, we can improve S/N and reduce TIM initial distortion. tone control circuit is set within the amplifierNF loop. Also, the function of high-cut, low-cut filter, loudness etc. is adopted by feather touch switch, making it easy to make sound. It is possible to connect two tape decks.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman L-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/l-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1978 at ¥59,800. an integrated amplifier with low output and low sound quality. The power amplifier uses a pure complimentary service OCL system. In addition, the power transistor and other devices themselves are carefully selected and used, especially those with high high-frequency cutoff characteristics and low collector capacitance. The operating point is set in the part with good linearity of each transistor to improve the distortion factor characteristics over the entire band. The equalizer circuit, flat amplifier circuit and tone amplifier circuit of the pre-amplifier section use a two stage direct connection system. By increasing the current supplied to each circuit, low impedance is achieved and high-frequency characteristics are improved. In addition, the circuit is constructed by carefully selecting ultra-low-noise transistors, and by driving with a negative power supply, the SN ratio is improved. In order to minimize the distance of each input system and to eliminate shield wires, an input terminal board is provided at the bottom. In addition, the signal path has been simplified for flatter characteristics and higher S / N ratio.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-3-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1978 at ¥89,800. This integrated amplifier was developed in pursuit of quality in every aspect including performance, mechanism, function and design. The power amplifier section uses a DC amplifier configuration without the time constant circuit in the NFB loop, which is one of the causes of deterioration of the transient response. In addition, the problem of drift due to fluctuations in external conditions such as power supply voltage and temperature is minimized to a negligible level by taking electrical and mechanical measures at each major point. The power transistor is carefully selected to have high breakdown strength and high cut-off frequency, the driver transistor is EBT (ballast and transistor), and the pre-driver stage is driven by constant voltage and current to achieve stable high-pass characteristics with less notching distortion. The preamp section consists of a 3-stage directly connected equalizer circuit, a 2-stage directly connected flat amplifier circuit, and a 2-stage directly connected tone amplifier circuit. Furthermore, in order to further reduce the distortion factor and increase the S / N ratio, we conducted a fundamental review of the circuit and carefully selected ultra-low-noise transistors with a wide linear region, high high-cut-off frequency, and low collector output capacity. These transistors are driven by a negative power supply, and a large amount of current is passed through each circuit to achieve low impedance.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-mq-68-c":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1978 at ¥108,000. This is a non-feedback tube type stereo power amplifier that does not rely on NFB and pursues bare characteristics from the bottom. With NFB switching, it is possible to apply a light NFB of 16 dB. The output tube uses a 3-pole tube 50CA10 for power amplification, which is used in 38 series integrated amplifier and 60 series power amplifiers. This ball has a large plate loss of 30W and can produce 30W of power with push-pull operation. It also has a low internal resistance and the speaker is driven by a constant voltage, which helps improve the bare characteristics of the power stage. The new OY series OY15-6KHP is used for the output transformer. This transformer was newly designed to bring out the performance of 50CA10. Compared with the conventional OY type, the power loss is reduced by half by increasing the diameter of the wire used. Moreover, by taking advantage of the wide optimum load range of the 3-pole output tube, the secondary side winding is unified, and frequency characteristics, phase characteristics, and AC balance are improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman MQ-68 C (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/mq68c-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-mq-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1978 at ¥135,000. 5 pole output tube 6CA7 duct type stereo amplifier. The output tube is 6CA7, a 5-pole tube that is well-known in the world of audio. 6CA7 is a relatively small and smart shape, but it can be used to pull out a large 100W output by push-pull operation. This 6CA7 is used as a push-pull output circuit for ultralinear connection, and it has high durability by adding enough space to obtain 45W/45W output. OY15-6.5KHF has been developed for MQ70. In addition, in order to significantly improve frequency characteristics, phase characteristics, and interchangeable balance, we are uniting the secondary side winding.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman MQ-70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/mq70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-1515":{"more":[{"t":"Produced from 1978 through 1980, the Marantz 1515 receiver occupied the entry-level position in Marantz’s budget-oriented 15xx series. With a modest output of 15 watts per channel and minimal features, it was designed to provide an affordable introduction to the Marantz audio lineup. Priced at around $230, the receiver offered budget-conscious audio enthusiasts an accessible entry point into the brand. The 15xx series—which included models 1515, 1520, 1530, 1535, and 1550—represented Marantz’s strategic attempt to broaden its market reach during the late 1970s. By leveraging more affordable Taiwanese manufacturing and using lower-cost materials, the company sought to capture a more price-sensitive segment of the hi-fi market. Despite the cost-cutting measures, the core technology remained consistent across the models, with primary variations existing in the amplifier sections. These receivers would prove to be among the last Marantz components produced before the company’s acquisition by Philips in 1980. Marantz also introduced “L” variations of the 15xx series receivers, primarily sold in Europe. These models incorporated a longwave tuner but were otherwise identical to their standard counterparts.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 1515","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-1515","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-1530":{"more":[{"t":"The Marantz 1530 came on the market in 1978 and lasted for a few years before being moved off the shelves via discounting. It retailed at about $340 in 1978 but by 1980 was down to $299. It’s not a high powered receiver but was their mid range offering. It produces 30 watts per channel into 8 ohms. Cost cutting was the name of the game for Marantz in the late 1970s into the early 80’s, and beyond, so build quality suffered with the later models. To be fair, all audio manufacturers were heading down the same cost cutting road. Some might argue that quality at Marantz took a big hit when Saul Marantz left the company in the mid 1960’s. But, they still made good quality equipment from 1964 into the very early 1980’s while they were owned by Superscope. Philips bought the company in 1992.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 1530","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-1530","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-1550":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced in 1978, the Marantz 1550 receiver was part of the 15xx series that included the 1515, 1530, and 4025. Superscope owned the Marantz brand at the time and Philips would buy them from Superscope a couple years later in 1980. The 1550 produced 50 watts per channel into 8 ohms and was the top of the line in the 15xx series. The 1550 design did away with the iconic gyro tuning wheel that most associate with Marantz stereos. Still, the design is sleek and well balanced. The Marantz 1550 receiver’s front panel offers a range of controls for customizing audio output and managing various input sources. The Speaker System switches allow you to select between two sets of speakers or operate both simultaneously. These switches can be disengaged to use headphones exclusively. You can tailor the sound of the 1550 through several specialized switches and controls.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz 1550","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-1550","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sc-7":{"more":[{"t":"A preamplifier developed for Low-TIM. The equalizer stage is responsible for amplifying the weak output from the record and compensating for the recording characteristics. The first stage is a cascode differential circuit with low-noise FET → phase inversion amplifier, the second stage is a complete push-pull amplifier circuit, and the output stage is a DC-configuration equalizer stage with low distortion and good transient characteristics with Darlington SEPP. Furthermore, the first stage FET is a luxurious FET specially made by Marantz that has low-noise characteristics and excellent thermal and electrical pair characteristics. As a result, the S/N ratio is exactly 90 dB (IHF-A) at 7.75 mV input. In addition, the RIAA deviation, which indicates the accuracy of record reproduction, is ± 0.2 dB (20 Hz to 20 kHz) by carefully selecting an equalizer element with good characteristics and high accuracy. It has a built-in MC head amplifier, a DC configuration using a low-noise FET at the first stage, and an extremely low feedback impedance to improve the S/N ratio. While listening to FM music, you can record completely different sources on each of the two decks independently, from the Phono input on the A deck and from the AUX terminal on the B deck. This not only expands deck play, but also eliminates the hassle of pin plug connections when dubbing from deck to deck, and improves playability.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SC-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sc-7-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-7":{"more":[{"t":"A power amplifier developed for Low-TIM. The main amplifier section consists of a full DC amplifier, and the first stage employs a dual FET source follower amplifier with matching pair characteristics to prevent characteristic degradation due to impedance changes at the input stage. The main amplifier section consists of a dual Tr differential amplifier → emitter follower buffer amplifier, and the power amplifier stage consists of a three stage Darlington circuit with a newly developed Super Hi-fT Tr parallel push-pull. This Super High-fT transistor was born based on the Low-TIM concept, and is the latest emitter ballast type power transistor at that time, which can be called the crystal of LSI process technology and high-frequency Tr technology. In spite of the large Pc of 200W, the fT shows 60 mhz. It has excellent high-frequency characteristics, switching characteristics, and stable amplification performance with a margin to the ultra-high band. This is a custom-made Marantz product. As a result, the high-speed response of the SM-7 is remarkably improved over the wide band from the ultra-high band to the ultra-low band. The power transformer is equipped with a large power transformer that does not vibrate even at the maximum continuous output at the rated load.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-7-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-c-29":{"more":[{"t":"A preamplifier that takes over the amplifier technology of C28 and C32. The input selector is a double-silver contact for structural robustness. In addition, a shielded network at each high-level input and a short switch to ground unwanted inputs prevent feedback of signals between input circuits. The Phono equalizer incorporates a newly developed IC and OP amplifier to achieve a low distortion and low noise differential input circuit. In order to fully realize the low-noise effect, parts with less error are used for the feedback circuit. We have developed and adopted an IC headphone amplifier with a distortion factor of 0.1% or less as a headphone amplifier. It is possible to operate two dynamic headphones at the same time. The volume can be adjusted with the headphone volume. A pushbutton is used for switching, and the switch is mounted directly on the printed circuit board.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh C 29 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/c29-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-c-504":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980. Compact size preamplifier. IC is used for all input changeover switches. By turning the circuit ON/OFF with a minute DC voltage, we have succeeded in suppressing switching noise without affecting frequency characteristics. ± 12 db adjustment is possible for each frequency of 30 Hz, 750 Hz and 10 kHz, and the sound quality adjustment is free. The loudness control can be controlled continuously with the \"LOUD\" knob. The FLAT position provides maximum volume and a flat frequency response, while turning it to the right reduces volume and increases the loudness effect. The Loudness effect is a system that controls the balance between volume and quality by increasing the low-frequency range to match the characteristics of the human ear when listening at a lower volume.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh C 504 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/c504-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/mcintosh-c-504.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/c504-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/c504.JPG"}},"mcintosh-mc-502":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980. This compact stereo power amplifier is based on the same design concept as the C504. The Normal (green) and Limit (red) lamps on the front panel are operated by an originally designed circuit called a waveform comparison circuit. In this circuit, the Limit lamp lights up and the Normal lamp goes out when the difference between the output waveform and the input waveform is 0.5%. When the difference reaches 1%, the power guard circuit operates to prevent clipping of the amplifier, to prevent distortion from being reproduced from the speaker, and to protect the speaker safely. In this case, the amplifier is still at its rated maximum output. The Limit lamp lights up when the amplifier is overloaded, and is lit for a visible period even when the overload condition is very short. The input and output waveforms are compared by an IC operation amplifier, and the waveform difference due to distortion of the output waveform is converted into a voltage, which is amplified approximately 100 times and supplied to a Schmidt trigger circuit through a full-wave rectifier circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MC 502 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc502-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/mcintosh-mc-502.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc502-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc502.JPG"}},"micro-seiki-dqx-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥80,000. Record player with large diameter turntable and dynamic balance tonearm. Tonearm is equipped with a dynamic tonearm MA- X. In the dynamic balance method, it is a structure to crimp the needle tip to the disk sound groove by applying the spring component. It has excellent traceability, not affected by the disc warpage or the level of the player. This arm has a constant crimping performance by light needle pressure according to the needle tip compliance of the cartridge used because it has a superior horizontal vertical sensitivity of the bearing. In addition, the mass (moving mass) of the pipe movable part mounted on the bearing is also small, and it is possible to operate according to the characteristics of the high-compliance type cartridge. The pipe uses a large super aluminum alloy with a small mass strength. In addition, a new ultra-thin coaxial cable (non-oxygen-free copper) that matches the Romans type is used for internal wire material, and the effect on transmission characteristics due to eddy current loss is as low as possible. Turntable has a 35cm diameter turntable.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki DQX-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/dqx-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-a-10-dc":{"more":[{"t":"This is a DC stereo power amplifier. We emphasize phase distortion in the low frequency range and eliminate distortion by realizing DC without any capacitor that acts as the time constant of the amplifier circuit. In the high-frequency range, distortion is reduced by improving the frequency bandwidth before negative feedback (NF) is applied, enabling low-distortion reproduction over a wide range. We have developed and adopted a dual FET with excellent characteristics, large gm (mutual conductance), and extremely low noise. We are working to improve the S/N ratio. In addition, by using this dual FET, the drift of output terminal potential due to DC conversion is extremely small and stable operation is obtained. A 2-monaural construction is adopted in which the power supply for each left and right channel and two monaural amplifiers are arranged on the same chassis. This eliminates the mutual interference of the power supply and greatly improves the separation. A heat sink of 0.35 ° C / W per channel is installed on the outside.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-A 10 DC (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-a10dc-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-a-15-dc":{"more":[{"t":"This is a DC stereo power amplifier. We emphasize phase distortion in the low frequency range and use a DC method without any capacitor that acts as a time constant for the amplifier circuit. In the high-frequency range, the pre-negative feedback (NF) frequency bandwidth is improved to reduce distortion, enabling low-distortion playback over a wide frequency range. In addition, the pre-negative feedback (NF) gain is optimally distributed to each stage, making it easier to apply negative feedback (NF) to higher frequencies. We have developed and adopted a dual FET with excellent characteristics, large gm (mutual conductance), and extremely low noise. We are working to improve the S/N ratio. In addition, by using this dual FET, the drift of output terminal potential due to DC conversion is extremely small and stable operation is obtained. A 2-monaural construction is adopted in which the power supply for each left and right channel and two monaural amplifiers are arranged on the same chassis. This eliminates the mutual interference of the power supply and greatly improves the separation.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-A 15 DC (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-a15dc-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-u-680":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier whose characteristics are improved by DC conversion after the high-level input. In order to improve phase distortion and transient distortion in the low range, dual FET developed by Diatone is adopted in the power block for DC. In addition, the pre-block has ICL-OCL configuration to eliminate capacitors from the signal path after high-level input and improve the rise and transient characteristics of sound. We have also improved the S/N ratio by reviewing the usage of the first stage transistor. The MC head amplifier uses a different type of transistor based on the idea of looking at the transistor itself. In addition, a circuit configuration that reduces noise is adopted for the circuit, which improves characteristics compared with the case of using a step-up transformer. Phono1 can be used exclusively for MM cartridges, and Phono2 can be used for both MM and MC types of cartridges. The DA-U680S is equipped with a power level indicator ON/OFF switch with 15 LEDs arranged in a V-shape. Since the power supply for the pre-block and power block is independent, it is difficult for the high temperature and magnetic influence generated from the power block to reach the pre-block, and stability of elements and circuits is improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-U 680 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-u680-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-dp-84-da":{"more":[{"t":"An auto-player system that omits some functions of the DP-86DA. The tone arm is equipped with a counter-weight resonance prevention mechanism to prevent sharp resonance that occurs in the pipe and head shell. In addition, the counter-weight has a double structure and a rubber damper is installed between the counter-weights to improve sound resolution in the low frequency range. A 12-pole 24-slot brushless servo motor is used as the drive motor. Equipped with auto mechanism, Oatley turn and auto cut are possible. All control levers are centrally located in the front of the cabinet and can be operated with the dust cover closed. The cabinet is molded with iron powder and a large insulator is used to suppress howling. Equipped with anti-skating mechanism and oil dump-type arm lifter.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DP-84 DA (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-84da-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-dp-86-da":{"more":[{"t":"A full-auto player system that employs a direct drive system. The tone arm is equipped with a counter-weight resonance prevention mechanism to prevent sharp resonance that occurs in the pipe and head shell. In addition, the counter-weight has a double structure and a rubber damper is installed between the counter-weights to improve sound resolution in the low frequency range. A 12-pole 24-slot brushless servo motor is used as the drive motor. Equipped with auto mechanism, auto start, Oatley turn, auto cut, auto repeat are possible. We have also adopted a mechanism that automatically determines the number of turns of the turntable when the size of the record to play is set. All control levers are centrally located in the front of the cabinet and can be operated with the dust cover closed. The cabinet is molded with iron powder and a large insulator is used to suppress howling. Equipped with anti-skating mechanism and oil dump-type arm lifter.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DP-86 DA (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-86da-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-dp-ec-3":{"more":[{"t":"EC (electronic control) full auto player developed by inheriting the technology of DP-EC1mkII. The counter weight of the tone arm has a built-in anti-resonance filter. This anti-resonance mechanism reduces resonance in the 30 Hz to 80 Hz range and improves resolution in the low frequency range. In addition, stainless steel pipe with high rigidity is adopted for the pipe arm instead of the conventional aluminum pipe, and it is combined with the counter weight with the damper built-in, and the deflection of the pipe part is almost eliminated. A force is applied to the tone arm in the direction of twisting or pulling the pipe. If the pivot is loose at this time, these forces will be applied to the needle tip and the sound quality will deteriorate. To prevent this, the span of the pivot is expanded, and a full-scale radial ball bearing is used for water plain bearing. This eliminates the looseness of the pipe and suppresses resonance. The tone arm is driven by two separate motors, one for horizontal direction and the other for vertical direction.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DP-EC 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-ec3-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-m-a-01":{"more":[{"t":"A compact stereo power amplifier that maintains high performance. In order to improve low-frequency phase distortion and transient cross-modulation distortion, we have adopted DC without any capacitor, which is the time constant of the circuit, thereby realizing flat characteristics up to the DC range. A RET (Ring Emitter Transistor) is used for the power transistor in order to improve the elongation of the high-frequency range. In addition, the gain before applying negative feedback is optimally distributed to each stage to improve the bare characteristics, making it easier to apply stable negative feedback to high frequencies. Specifically, we propose distortion by reducing the negative feedback at low frequencies and increasing the negative feedback at high frequencies. In the first stage, a unique low-noise dual FET with uniform characteristics, high gm (mutual inductance) and extremely low noise is adopted, which improves the S/N ratio. The power supply consists of two 55V/20,000 μ F filter capacitors and a 250 va power transformer with a highly efficient and compact cut core. This power supply occupies approximately 40% of the volume inside the amplifier and is small but has a strong power supply. It is equipped with peak level indicator by 12 LED display of one channel.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi M-A 01 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/m-a01-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-m-p-01":{"more":[{"t":"A small preamplifier of discrete configuration realized by a push switch and 4-layered printed circuit board. Built-in MC head amplifier with new type transistor adopted for DA-P15 type. In the first stage of the equalizer amplifier and tone amplifier, we use a low-noise FET that is carefully selected in terms of noise and performance in order to minimize the noise generated by the transistor. In addition, we increase the S/N ratio by reducing the impedance of the feedback circuit. Also, in terms of circuit, we have adopted a differential 2-stage amplifier circuit + class A push-pull circuit with a current mirror load with less distortion. This circuit reduces distortion in open loop and improves bare characteristics such as a wider band. This enables stable negative feedback and low distortion factor. Equipped with digital tone control by fixed resistor and push switch. Accurate tone control can be achieved in 2 dB steps by selecting plus or minus and the amount of change with the push switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi M-P 01 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/m-p01-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-m-8000":{"more":[{"t":"A power amplifier with improved dynamic characteristics by using a dual channel system in which all circuits are composed of two monaural amplifiers. The circuit system is all-stage direct connection semi - complimentary service SEPP / OTL circuit. 0.01 ~ 100W direct reading type LR power meter and -24 ~ 0dB5 point peak indicator are mounted. Equipped with 2 AC inputs.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo M-8000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/M-8000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-4500-mkii":{"more":[{"t":"In 1979 Onkyo introduced the Onkyo TX-4500 MKII. It retailed for $479.95 and was the mid range offering in their lineup. Onkyo took the design of their TX-4500 stereo and optimized it, renaming it the TX-4500 MKII. I see a lot of variation regarding the watts per channel specifications. According to the Onkyo TX-4500 MKII service manual, number 3046, the wattage is 60 watts per channel RMS at 8 ohms, both channels driven. It also produces no more than 0.1% total harmonic distortion. So, those are the numbers I’ll go with. The earlier TX-4500 is listed at 55 watts per channel. As a comparison the top of the line TX-8500 MKII listed at $1000 and produced 160 wpc.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-4500 MKII","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-4500-mkii","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-6500-mkii":{"more":[{"t":"This is one of the less common receivers – the Onkyo TX-6500 MK II. It was made by Onkyo from around 1978 to 1981. They made a series of receivers with the entry level unit being the TX-1500. From there was the TX-2500, the TX-4500, the TX-6500 and the monster TX-8500. I believe they were 40, 60, 100, 160 watts per channel respectively. So, the TX-6500 MkII chimed in at 100 watts per channel. The TX-2500 and TX-4500 were Onkyo’s last ditch effort to survive in the audio market around 1977. They had originally entered the U.S. market selling speakers in a collaboration with Mitsubishi but that did not go well. So, they put everything they had into the development of their receiver line.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-6500 MKII","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-6500-mkii","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-l-1":{"more":[{"t":"The development and installation of the Linear D. D> arm solves the problem that had been a bottleneck until now. The Linear D. D. Arm developed by Pioneer Shinkai is mounted in order to move the strong arm base horizontally precisely and quietly. By this, factors that cause harmful noise and vibration are completely eliminated. The Linear D. D. arm is structurally very simple because the magnetic repulsion force generated by electrical energy can be directly converted into linear motion. Unlike conventional systems, the arm base can be directly driven without any transmission mechanism such as a rotary motor, gears, belts, or strings.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-L 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-l1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-1080":{"more":[{"t":"You’ll recognize this receiver by its styling as a late 70’s Pioneer. In fact, it’s the Pioneer SX-1080, a direct descendant of the SX-1050. The SX-1050 was produced in 1976-1977 while the SX-1080 showed up in 1978-79. Despite the fact that the SX-1080 is supposedly an improved version of the SX-1050 you’ll find opinions on the matter split amongst collectors and audio enthusiasts. Some swear that the SX-1050 sounds better or is built better while others claim the opposite. The SX-1080, like the 1050 puts out 120 watts into 8 ohms. The 1080 also has two VU power meters, one for each channel, that the 1050 does not have. Interestingly, the 1050 has outputs for 3 pair of speakers while the later 1080 only has outputs for two pair. The 1080 also featured turnover tone controls and 6dB/octave high and low filters.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-1080","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1080","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-1280":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-1280 is one of Pioneer’s classic receivers. It came out in 1978 and took over for the SX-1250. It is rated at 185 watts per channel which is second only to the monster SX-1980’s power output in the Pioneer lineup. MSRP was around $900.00 which was a decent chunk of change in 1978 and rose to $950.00 in 1979 which was the last year of production for the 1200 series receivers. The SX-1280 was released during a time when high-fidelity audio equipment was in high demand. It was designed to deliver exceptional sound quality and power, catering to audiophiles and music enthusiasts who sought the best audio experience. Pioneer was known for its innovative engineering and high-quality audio equipment, and the SX-1280 showcased their expertise in receiver manufacturing. The SX-1280 is a stunning example of Pioneer’s beautiful design work from the 1970’s. The faceplate is brushed aluminum and houses a wide array of controls.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-1280","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1280","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sx-1280.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1280","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/pioneer-sx-1280-power-meters.jpg"}},"pioneer-sx-1980":{"more":[{"t":"This of course is one of the icons of vintage audio – the Pioneer SX-1980 receiver. This receiver is highly sought after today and prices can reach well into the thousands of dollars for a well maintained unit. Some will argue that other Pioneer models sound better, but the fact still remains that the monster SX-1980 was the king of the audio mountain in it’s day. It was the Pioneer’s flagship model and one of the most powerful and sought-after receivers of its time. The SX-1980 was designed as a high-end receiver that combined powerful amplification with advanced features and high-quality components. It was built to handle large speaker systems and deliver clean, distortion-free sound at high volumes. The development of the SX-1980 began in the mid-1970s, when Pioneer engineers set out to design a receiver that would surpass their previous flagship model, the SX-1250. The new receiver was to have a power output of 270 watts per channel, which would make it the most powerful receiver on the market at the time. In fact, Pioneer called the SX-1980 a “Super Receiver”.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-1980","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1980","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-580":{"more":[{"t":"This little Pioneer SX-580 was the bottom of the line from Pioneer around 1979. It only produces 20 watts per channel and has minimal features. Still, it’s a good little receiver for an entry level unit. It’s not going to be enough to power large speakers but for a garage or small room it could work well. I believe they retailed for about $250 when new. As you can see they have the stereotypical look of late 70’s Pioneer receivers with the silver face and white dial. Pioneer also produced the SX-590 which was essentially the same receiver only with a black dial face. The SX-580is fairly small at 17.5″ x 12.5″ x 5.25″ and weighs in at just over 18 pounds. If you need a service manual you can find it at HiFiEngine.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-580","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-580","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-680":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Pioneer SX-680 receiver. It was introduced by Pioneer in 1978 and was on the market until about 1980. It is a descendant of the SX-650. It retailed for about $199 and produced 30 watts per channel. It was at the lower end of the x80 line from Pioneer that year but had the features most consumers would need and performed above its specifications. The entry level receiver was the SX-580, followed by the SX-680, SX-780, SX-880, SX-980, SX-1080, and the legendary monster SX-1980. The light metallic dial face (almost white) and black meter faces give it an interesting look. The dial illumination is a clear, warm white. Its precursor, the SX-650, had the same light dial face but had white meter faces.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-680","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-680","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-780":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Pioneer SX-780. It was the last of Pioneer’s 700 series receivers and was very well built. It was produced from 1978 up until 1980 and had a list price of $325.00. The SX-780 was rated at 45 watts per channel but that was probably under rated. The internals were high quality with Darlington STK-0050 Power Packs in the output stage as well as high quality Nichicon capacitors. While it had crisp FM reception some feel that its FM selectivity is a little weak. It also has a great phono pre-amp section but could have used some more AUX inputs. Overall a great starter receiver for someone just getting into the vintage audio scene. I have one of these that powers on but doesn’t deliver sound through the speaker outputs or the headphones.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-780","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-780","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sx-780.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-780","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/06/pioneer-sx-780-front.jpg"}},"pioneer-sx-880":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-xx80 series came after the SX-xx50. This Pioneer SX-880 is a classic example of that generation of Pioneer receivers and was the last of the 800 series. It premiered around 1978 and retailed for about $425 at the time. The main aesthetic difference between the two series are the dark faced meters with white lettering. This change was made to improve visibility. The SX-880 produces 60 watts per channel with total harmonic distortion at 0.05%. It can handle a speaker impedance of 4 Ohms. The tuning section utilizes a 3 gang variable capacitor tuner. Other features include: The general consensus is that the xx80 series does not have quite the same quality build as the xx50 series did.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-880","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-880","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-980":{"more":[{"t":"Here is another late 1970’s classic receiver. It’s the Pioneer SX-980 and was produced from 1978 to 1979 and was the last of the 900 series receivers from Pioneer. The SX-980 is basically a slightly restyled SX-950. You’ll notice that the meter faces are black instead of white to improve the legibility of the analog meters. The SX-980 is rated at 80 watts per channel into 8 ohms. As a comparison the SX-950 was rated at 85 WPC. While the sound difference between the 980 and 950 may not be very noticeable to most listeners the build quality of the two units is different. The consensus is that Pioneer’s 50 series receivers are built better than the 80 series. Aesthetically these receivers are extremely nice to look at.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-980","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-980","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"revox-b-750-mk-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥265,000. A740 The basic circuit of the power amplifier part is A740. Tone control includesences and Treble plus 3kHz presence. The equalizer is equipped with a cartridge load three-stage switch function and a fono input sensitivity adjustment function. Equipped with loudness control, low cut/high cut filter, tape copy switch, toned foot switch, and muting switch. Pre-Power Separate Switch","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Revox B 750 MK II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/amp/b750mkii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-2020":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥65,000. DC integrated amplifier. Power amplifier: The DC power amplifier series adopts a dual FET with its characteristics, coupled with the Pure Complementary OCL circuit to achieve superior sound quality. In addition, the drift of the mid-point potential that is a problem with DC amplifier is suppressed power supply supplyctuations in each stage, improving the pair characteristics and increasing stability. We use AB-class operation method which can produce sound quality of A-class amplifier and obtain large output. Normally, the A-class operation automatically switches to B-class operation when major signals that require large power. We realize low distortion rate by thoroughly penetrating materials, parts, printed circuit board design and shielding cord placement. As a protective circuit, it is equipped with electro-caly control ASO circuit and DC feedback power limit circuit. The electro carry control ASO circuit protects the trans and loudspeaker of the amplifier by relay actuation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-2020 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-2020.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-2030":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥98,000. DC integrated amplifier. Power amplifier: The DC power amplifier series adopts a dual FET with its characteristics, coupled with the Pure Complementary OCL circuit to achieve superior sound quality. In addition, the drift of the mid-point potential that is a problem with DC amplifier is suppressed power supply supplyctuations in each stage, improving the pair characteristics and increasing stability. We use AB-class operation method which can produce sound quality of A-class amplifier and obtain large output. Normally, the A-class operation automatically switches to B-class operation when major signals that require large power. We realize low distortion rate by thoroughly penetrating materials, parts, printed circuit board design and shielding cord placement. As a protective circuit, it is equipped with electro-caly control ASO circuit and DC feedback power limit circuit. The electro carry control ASO circuit protects the trans and loudspeaker of the amplifier by relay actuation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-2030 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-2030.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-2040":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥148,000. The DC power amplifier series adopts a dual FET with its characteristics, coupled with the Pure Complementary OCL circuit to achieve superior sound quality. In addition, the drift of the mid-point potential that is a problem with DC amplifier is suppressed power supply supplyctuations in each stage, improving the pair characteristics and increasing stability. We use AB-class operation method which can produce sound quality of A-class amplifier and obtain large output. Normally, the A-class operation automatically switches to B-class operation when major signals that require large power. We realize low distortion rate by thoroughly penetrating materials, parts, printed circuit board design and shielding cord placement. The power supply unit is equipped with a high-efficiency, high-resolution, high-resolution, large-size Troidal Core transformer. As a protective circuit, it is equipped with electro-caly control ASO circuit and DC feedback power limit circuit. The electro carry control ASO circuit protects the trans and loudspeaker of the amplifier by relay actuation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-2040 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-2040.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rb-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥110,000. Dual FETs carefully select low-noise type of thermal and electrical characteristics and maintain the necessary pair characteristics for the first stage of the DC amplifier. The problem is that the medium-point drift increases the stability of the middle-point potential of the differential a ification part while circuitbilizing the DC balance by circuit technology. We use AB-class operation method which can produce sound quality of A-class amplifier and obtain large output. Normally, the A-class operation automatically switches to B-class operation when major signals that require large power. We realize low distortion rate by thoroughly penetrating materials, parts, printed circuit board design and shielding cord placement. The power supply unit is equipped with a high-efficiency, high-resolution, high-resolution, large-size Troidal Core transformer. As a protective circuit, it is equipped with electro-caly control ASO circuit and DC feedback power limit circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RB-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/rb-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-rc-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥110,000. preamplifier for all stages of DC configuration. We realize low distortion rate by thoroughly penetrating materials, parts, printed circuit board design and shielding cord placement. Equipped with direct fono function. When this feature is turned on, you can sort the top priority circuit for Phno and the circuit that affects Phno signals is eliminated from the signal system. This function can be used for volume control and subsonic filter. The equalizer amplifier part adopts two-stage DC differential input circuit by low noise FET, which has excellent characteristics due to the configuration of the output stage as a push-pull. Forno selector, recording selector, and function selector control switches are included in the rear panel, minimizing the shielding code.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RC-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/rc-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-22000":{"more":[{"t":"This is the giant Sansui G-22000. It listed at over $1400.00 and was only surpassed by it’s big brother the Sansui G-33000. The G-22000 was made from 1978 to 1980 and put out a whopping 240 watts per channel. Sansui engineers also utilized what they called the Diamond Differential DC circuit design. This allowed the audio signal to through the DC amplifier directly to the output without passing through a capacitor. Therefore, capacitors had no distorting effect on the audio signal. The G-22000 also had a unique two piece design in which the power amp and the preamp are contained in separate units. This made it easier to move the preamp without having to move the heavier power amp and also helped reduce any interference the power amp might have on the preamp circuit. Together the unit weighs in at a massive 95 pounds!","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-22000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-22000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-33000":{"more":[{"t":"You’ll hear people refer to a vintage receiver sometimes and say “You don’t see those around very often”. Usually it’s hyperbole. With the monster Sansui G-33000 it’s not hyperbole. You REALLY don’t see these very often. It would be hard to argue that this isn’t the holy grail for Sansui collectors much less vintage receiver collectors in general. I recently wrote a post on the holy grail for Marantz collectors which is the Marantz 2600. One of those rare beasts recently sold for just over $6000. Well, the Sansui G-33000 has that one beat as one just sold for $7700 (12-17-2013). The G-33000 has the wattage to back up its size as well.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-33000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-33000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-sr-333":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥33,000. Equipped with a 20-pole 30-slot DC brushless servo motor with improved rotational accuracy, stability and hauling function as a player system, and a cost-effective record player. High sensitivity tonearm eliminates unnecessary resonance. Large turntable sheet with contact area.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-333 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-333.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-sr-333.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-333.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-333.JPG"}},"sansui-sr-535":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥39,800. A full automatic direct drive type record player. Auto start and auto stop can be performed by one-lever operation. Manual operation is also possible. 1 to 5 memory repeats 20 pole 30 slots direct drive motor is available for drive motor. The tonearm section improves sound quality by wide span effect. You can also use zinc diecast on arm base. SV-44 is a MM type cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-535 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-535.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-sr-535.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-535.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-535.jpg"}},"sansui-sr-636":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥53,000. direct-drive player in the PLL servo system that pursues the basics of the player system such as accurate rotation speed and excellent wow/fla characteristics. The PLL servo method is used to combine accurate pulses of high-precision photoelectric generators with high stability oscillation. tonearm to enhance arm branch and improve sound quality. Luxury piano finish weight cabinet.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-636 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-636.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-sr-838":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥63,000. In addition, it focuses on ease of use by focusing on the operation mechanism. Improves wow/futter characteristics and SN ratio by improving mechanical accuracy and electrical accuracy. Tonearm uses a mass-in tonearm, which uses special cylinders on the rotating shaft. Thick finish with piano finish.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui SR-838 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/sr-838.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sanyo-jcx-2600":{"more":[{"t":"The Sanyo JCX-2600K receiver was introduced in 1978 and retailed for $449.95. While Sanyo may not have a reputation for high quality today, the receivers they produced in the late 1970’s could compete with most of the other top brands in the industry such as Marantz and Pioneer. Their build quality is above average and their performance is excellent. The JCX-2600K produces 85 watts per channel and has essentially every feature you’d need. On top of all that it’s a beautiful receiver Sanyo was founded by Toshio Iue in 1947 and made their name making portable radios and washing machines. The company’s name means ‘three oceans’ in Japanese, referring to the founder’s desire to sell their products worldwide, across the Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian oceans. They certainly succeeded at that. The brand was introduced in the U.S. in 1970 and is now a household name. They bought Fisher Electronics in 1975 to expand their home audio reach.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sanyo JCX-2600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sanyo-jcx-2600k","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-b80":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥200,000. Full automatic player system with all-electronic control tonearm \"biotracer\". Tonearm is equipped with a biotracer that electronically controls all complex movements. The biotracer has a speed sensor, position detection sensor, and linear motor respectively in the vertical and horizontal direction of the arm. The speed sensor works to improve characteristics, such as resonance and in-side force at the same time, and the position detection sensor works in conjunction with a 128-word x4-bit microcomputer to perform arm operations, such as full auto operation, needle pressure adjustment, and in-side force cancellation. Normally several hundred logic decisions are performed for one operation, and the arm position, speed, and operation switch state are checked, and the instruction is processed at a speed of 1/1000 seconds or less. Auto-reed-in/auto-return is available, each time is ergonomically set to 6 seconds. The photoelectric record size selector automatically detects the size of the record board (30cm, 17cm).","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-B80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-b80.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-b80.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-b80.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-b80.JPG"}},"sony-ps-lx-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥50,000. A compact, fully automatic player with a unification of the components and sizes of the Liberty Series. High torque is increased because it is more efficient. MagneDisk Speed Detection detects high-density magnetized signals on turntable by multi-gap head to detect the average number of rotations. In addition, because it has a relatively high occurrence signal frequency, it is possible to compensate servo to the high frequency even in the flutter component. We use quartz lock to achieve stable rotational characteristics for changes in ambient temperature and power supply voltage and frequency. MM type cartridge XL-200 is equipped with Romans straight arm. With the front-operated feather touch control, operation such as start, stop, repeat, and turn count change can be done in a state where the dust cover is closed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-LX 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-p-7-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥65,000. motor features linear BSL motor. The magne disk speed detection method is used for the speed detection section of the servo system. In this method, the magnetic body is coated on the inner wall of the outer circumference of the turntable, where the rotating area is wide, and the detection signal of 512 waves is magnetized here, and the multi-gap head detects the average value and sends control command to the servo system. In addition, because it has a high generated signal frequency of about 284 Hz at 284/3 rpm, it is possible to compensate servo to a relatively high frequency even in the flutter component. A crystal lock is available with a phase control circuit of the crystal oscillation to the magnetized speed servo circuit. By locking the detected signal phase, not only the initial drift caused by self-heating of the body, but also the rotational speed due to voltage ctuation caused by self-heating, and the rotational speed decline caused by needle pressure load are obtained excellent rotational characteristics. The cabinet adopts SBMC, which has a large internal loss of metal, and has high accuracy and high strength. It is equipped with a gel-like high viscoelastic material in the inner rubber cup to achieve effective vibration absorption.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-P 7 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-p7x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-40":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥49,800. A full automatic player developed with advanced technology. The motor features a simple linear BSL motor that does not require a brush or a slot. High torque, reliability and durability are improved because of its efficiency. The servo-based speed detection unit is equipped with a magnet disk speed detection method developed by using Sony Magnescale’s precision measurement technology. In this method, the magnetic body is coated on the inner wall of the outer circumference of the turntable, where the rotating area is wide, and the detection signal of 512 waves is magnetized here, and the multi-gap head detects the average value and sends control command to the servo system. In addition, it has a high generated signal frequency of about 284 Hz at 33, 1/3 rpm, so it is possible to compensate servo to a relatively high frequency among the flutter components. A crystal lock is available with a phase control circuit of the crystal oscillation to the magnetized speed servo circuit. By locking the detected signal phase, not only the initial drift caused by self-heating of the body, but also the rotational speed due to voltage ctuation caused by self-heating, and the rotational speed decline caused by needle pressure load are obtained excellent rotational characteristics. The arm pipe has a special aluminum alloy that has greatly increased rigidity, and the J-shaped type with high bending strength has gained about 8 times the rigidity of conventional aluminum pipes.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 40 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x40.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥54,800. Automatic return player system with thorough resonance. The motor features a simple linear BSL motor that does not require a brush or slot. High torque, reliability and durability are improved because of its efficiency. The servo-based speed detection unit is equipped with a magnet disk speed detection method developed by using Sony Magnescale’s precision measurement technology. In this method, the magnetic body is coated on the inner wall of the outer circumference of the turntable, where the rotating area is wide, and the detection signal of 512 waves is magnetized here, and the multi-gap head detects the average value and sends control command to the servo system. In addition, it has a high generated signal frequency of about 284 Hz at 33, 1/3 rpm, so it is possible to compensate servo to a relatively high frequency among the flutter components. In addition, it is possible to use the crystal lock with the phase control circuit of the crystal oscillation. By locking the detected signal phase, not only the initial drift caused by self-heating of the body, but also the rotational speed due to voltage ctuation caused by self-heating, and the rotational speed decline caused by needle pressure load are obtained excellent rotational characteristics. Low capacity cord with gold plated terminal is available.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x50.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-60":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥62,800. A full auto-preyer system equipped with a full-auto mechanism that pursues safety and ease of use with the idea of Human Automecha. The motor features a simple linear BSL motor that does not require a brush or slot. High torque, reliability and durability are improved because of its efficiency. The servo-based speed detection unit is equipped with a magnet disk speed detection method developed by using Sony Magnescale’s precision measurement technology. Turntable magnetic body is coated on the inner wall of the outer circumference, and the 512 wave detection signal is magnetized here, and the multi-gap head detects the average value and sends control command to the servo system. This method has a high generated signal frequency of about 284 Hz at 33, 1/3 rpm, so it is possible to compensate servo to a relatively high frequency even in the flutter component. In addition, the speed servo circuit adopts the crystal lock with the phase control circuit of the crystal oscillation. By locking the detected signal phase, not only the initial drift caused by self-heating of the body, but also the rotational speed due to voltage ctuation caused by self-heating, and the rotational speed decline caused by needle pressure load are obtained excellent rotational characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 60 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x60.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-x-60.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x60.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x60.JPG"}},"sony-ps-x-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥79,800. Fully automatic player system with dedicated motor and logic circuit for arm drive. In addition to normal full-auto operation, tonearm can be used only or turntable. In addition, when the arm drive power is larger, the auto mechanism is separated and the mechanism is not burdened. It is equipped with a muting mechanism that suppresses noise when the needle tip descends on the record board and leaves. A simple linear BSL (throttleless) motor that does not require a brush or a slot is installed to release the torque swelling of the DC motor. High torque, reliability and durability are improved because of its efficiency. The servo-based speed detection unit is equipped with a magnet disk speed detection method developed by using Sony Magnescale’s precision measurement technology. Turntable magnetic body is coated on the inner wall of the outer circumference, and the 512 wave detection signal is magnetized here, and the multi-gap head detects the average value and sends control command to the servo system.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-40":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥49,800. Developed with technology acquired from the development of high-grade amplifier. It can realize straight transmission by heat pipe. Heat dissipation uses a heat pipe with a heat conductivity of hundreds of times the copper rod to heat dissipate, eliminating the need to use lead wires for wires between trans and circuit boards, and preventing electromagnetic wave generation from lead wires. Power supply The pulse power supply contributes to the non-fluxing of 50Hz/60Hz magnetic field to make AC100V DC instantly. Hi-fT trans was born from Sony’s proprietary semiconductor engineering. This trans has excellent high-speed response characteristics, so it is possible to suppress the dynamic distortion such as transient modulation distortion with a simple circuit, preventing the negative impact on the sound quality caused by the complexity of the circuit. MC cartridge Direct input is possible. Self-defeit tone control and loudness switch","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 40 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f40.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-60":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥69,800. Integrated amplifier developed under the theme of reducing total dynamic distortion. We provide straight transmission to ensure the shortest distance part placement in line with the signal flow. The input is led to the front panel equalizer amplifier from the terminal on the back. The wire ring to equalizer amplifier avoids the use of large shielded wires and prevents signal deterioration using print patterns. Heat pipe structure is available in the cooling system. Heat pipes contain special liquids in decompressed copper pipes and continuously perform vaporization and liquidation, which instantaneously transmits heat from the end of the pipe to the end. For this reason, the thermal conductivity is realized by hundreds of times the same diameter metal rods of copper and silver. This heat pipe structure enhances the freedom of power trans placement and enables pulling by wire material.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 60 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f60.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥89,800. Integrated amplifier developed under the theme of reducing total dynamic distortion. In order to achieve simple and straight thinking, we adopt a straight transmission and pre-power separation structure, which ensures the shortest wiring of input/output terminals, natural component placement along the flow of signals, and avoid cross-section of signals. Heat pipe structure is available in the cooling system. Heat pipes contain special liquids in decompressed copper pipes and continuously perform vaporization and liquidation, which instantaneously transmits heat from the end of the pipe to the end. For this reason, the thermal conductivity is realized by hundreds of times the same diameter metal rods of copper and silver. This heat pipe structure enhances the freedom of power trans placement and enables pulling by wire material. The Hi-fT trans has reduced transient modulation distortion (TIM distortion). This trans was developed using Sony’s semiconductor engineering. It realizes safe operation for large power.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-f-70.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f70.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f70.JPG"}},"sony-ta-f-80":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥158,000. Based on the theme of reducing total dynamic distortion, we have developed a high-end integrated amplifier that enables simple and straight thinking to the transmission characteristics of individual parts. In order to achieve simple and straight thinking, we adopt a straight transmission and pre-power separation structure, which ensures the shortest wiring of input/output terminals, natural component placement along the flow of signals, and avoid cross-section of signals. Heat pipe structure is available in the cooling system. Heat pipes contain special liquids in decompressed copper pipes and continuously perform vaporization and liquidation, which instantaneously transmits heat from the end of the pipe to the end. For this reason, the thermal conductivity is realized by hundreds of times the same diameter metal rods of copper and silver. This heat pipe structure enhances the freedom of power trans placement and enables pulling by wire material. The Hi-fT trans has reduced transient modulation distortion (TIM distortion). This trans was developed using Sony’s semiconductor engineering. It realizes safe operation for large power.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f80.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-f-80.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f80.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f80.JPG"}},"sony-ta-n-9":{"more":[{"t":"As a power amplifier, the high-quality source of dynamic range that was born by the appearance of PCM equipment is more faithful, and the latest technology and devices were introduced, and the mono power amplifier was developed to achieve the highest performance and sound quality. This power MOS-FET is capable of handling large currents (up to 10A) with high pressure resistance (210V), making it easy to produce large outputs, and it is highly reliable and safe, and it has excellent naked characteristics of high area, so it has less transient mixed modulation. The complete DC amplifier configuration has no problem of phase rotation in the bass.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-N 9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n9.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-p-7-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1978 at ¥69,800. Compact amplifier for micro- onent PRECISE composite. By using the heat pipe developed for audio, the power trans attached to the substrate can be directly cooled, improving distortion and SN ratio. Newly developed and adopted solid state switches for function switches and monitor switches. This switch is a semiconductor switch that operates signal ON/OFF by DC control. It enables internal remote control, which greatly reduces signal cable material.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-P 7 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-p7f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"tandberg-tr-2060":{"more":[{"t":"Pictures don’t really do this Tandberg TR-2060 receiver justice. Having owned one in the past I know full well how nice they are on the eyes. Tandberg is a Norwegian company probably more know in vintage audio circles for their tape decks rather than their receivers. But, those who’ve seen and heard either their Huldra, SolvSuper or TR lines of receivers know just how good they are. During the early 1930’s Vebjørn Tandberg’s company started manufacturing radios based loosely upon the German Telefunken radios of the time. Known for their radio reception they grw in popularity. During the 1950’s the quality of their reel-to-reel tape decks brought them recognition in the US and really overshadowed the quality of their receivers. The TR-2060 was introduced in late 1977 and was in US markets until about 1981 or so. The TR-2060 is rated at 60 watts per channel into 8 ohms.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Tandberg TR 2060","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/tandberg-tr-2060","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/tandberg-tr-2060.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/tandberg-tr-2060","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/09/tandberg-tr-2060-top.jpg"}},"tandberg-tr-2080":{"more":[{"t":"I’ve always though that Tandberg built some of the nicest looking receivers during the late 70’s. This Tandberg TR-2080 is no exception. The sleek design and logical layout are enhanced by it’s lighting scheme. Originally built in Norway from 1978 up in to the early 80’s, this receiver puts out 125 watts per channel into 4 ohms. The faceplate is aluminum and it came with wood cabinet in either natural wood grain or black. The TR-2080 was one of Tandberg’s top of the line models and is known for its exceptional tuner. While not nearly as well recognized in the U.S. as the Pioneer, Sansui or Kenwood it can definitely hold its own performance wise with those behemoths. Another interesting feature of the Tandberg receivers is that I see quite a few of them with fairly exotic veneer. I’m not sure if they came from the factory like that or were re-veneered by their owners.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Tandberg TR-2080","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/tandberg-tr-2080","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-700":{"more":[{"t":"The Technics SA-700 receiver debuted in 1978 and was at the higher end of the Technics receiver lineup at the time. It’s rated at a hefty 100 watts per channel and retailed for a price of $700. With style, numerous features, and power to spare, the SA-700 fits well into any vintage audio setup. The SA-700 has the signature Technics look with brushed aluminum faceplate, warm dial lighting, and especially the recessed black out knobs and switches. Technics did introduce a sign of things to come with the use of LED’s for the power meters even though the tuning meters are analog. Technics’ receiver lineup in 1978 was extensive and included the SA-200, SA-300, SA-400, SA-500, SA-600, SA-700, SA-800, and the monster SA-1000. Here are the rated watts per channel and retail price for each model: The front panel of the SA-700 has many of the standard controls and a couple that are more nuanced. It has bass, treble and mid range tone controls as well as low and high filters. There are also switches for loudness and muting.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Technics SA-700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-700","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-80":{"more":[{"t":"The Technics SA-800 is one of Technics by Panasonics’ higher end models. It has the classic Technics look with dark insets around the knobs and warm glow of the tuning dial. The red and green program and power level LED’s give it a colorful visual effect. The SA-800 produces 125 watts per channel into 8 ohms with no more than 0.04% total harmonic distortion. An interesting aspect of this receiver is its Automatic Load Impedance Detector circuitry. When the power is turned on a low level signal is sent to the speakers to determine their impedance. Then a relay selects the correct power supply voltage depending upon whether the speakers are 4 or 8 ohm. So, the SA-800 can produce optimal power output regardless of speaker impedance, delivering 125 watts per channel into 8 ohm speakers and up to 160 watts per channel into 4 ohm speakers without risking damage to the amplifier section. This ensures maximum performance and protection when paired with a wide variety of speakers without compromising sound quality or safety.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Technics SA-80","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-800","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-sa-80.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-800","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2019/01/Technics-sa-800-front-lamps.jpg"}},"technics-sa-800":{"more":[{"t":"The Technics SA-800 is one of Technics by Panasonics’ higher end models. It has the classic Technics look with dark insets around the knobs and warm glow of the tuning dial. The red and green program and power level LED’s give it a colorful visual effect. The SA-800 produces 125 watts per channel into 8 ohms with no more than 0.04% total harmonic distortion. An interesting aspect of this receiver is its Automatic Load Impedance Detector circuitry. When the power is turned on a low level signal is sent to the speakers to determine their impedance. Then a relay selects the correct power supply voltage depending upon whether the speakers are 4 or 8 ohm. So, the SA-800 can produce optimal power output regardless of speaker impedance, delivering 125 watts per channel into 8 ohm speakers and up to 160 watts per channel into 4 ohm speakers without risking damage to the amplifier section. This ensures maximum performance and protection when paired with a wide variety of speakers without compromising sound quality or safety.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Technics SA-800","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-800","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1300-mk-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1977 at ¥105,000. We use the quartz synthesizer method to lock all 199 pitches. The tweak amount displays the light emitting diode display digitally. Tonearm uses a gimbal suspension method that intersects horizontal and vertical rotation at a point and achieves the initial motion sensitivity 7mg. It is equipped with a 6mm armrest adjustment mechanism to use cartridge for sibbia. Die-cast shell with anti-vibration design. Convenient cursor for overhang adjustment.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1300 MK 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1300mk2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1301":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥59,800. Quartz direct-drive We have accumulated know-how accumulated over 1100 elements necessary for quartz lock, and we have accumulated over 3 ICs using circuit and semiconductor technology. DN860, AN660, the phase speed control circuit by the sample hold, and AN640, the driving circuit, are used to detect high-precision standard signals and rotation speeds. We provide phase control based on the oscillation of high-precision quartz crystal units. In addition, the FG is used to detect all-round signals of the push-pull method to cancel the influence of external induction. It detects high-precision comparison signals by detecting all-round of the rotation axis. The drive is equipped with a DC motor with three-phase omnidirectional drive. It is equipped with an electronic brake mechanism that removes turntable and stops quickly. motorrate the motor's rotary and turntable. TECHNICS' proprietary integrated D.D motor enables high accuracy and reliability.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1301 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1301.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-220":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥29,800. Record player with F.G servo. TNRC (Technics, non-resonance compound) developed by Technics is used to block and absorb vibrations from the outside due to its superior anti-vibration and damping properties. F.G servo is used to detect the motor rotation speed. It detects the rotation axis at the whole circumference and obtains high accuracy detection signal. All control switches are equipped with a front panel control system, and the dust cover can be closed and queued. Tonearm uses a gimbal suspension method that intersects the axis of horizontal rotation and vertical rotation axis at a point, and the initial motion sensitivity is 7mg high sensitivity both horizontal and vertical. MM type cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-220 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-220.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-d-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥39,800. A full automatic player with unique integrated direct-drive motor and sound material TNRC. B/FG method is used to detect motor rotation speed. In addition, the motor is equipped with a unique integrated direct-drive motor, which the motor rotation unit is integrated with turntable. TNRC is a double anti-vibration structure used for cabinet and base by changing vibration characteristics. It is designed to absorb vibrations most effectively by reducing unnecessary resonance space as much as possible and thorough vibration analysis. High sensitivity gimbal suspension system is adopted by bearings with high precision pivot bearings made in the bearing structure of tonearm. This crosses horizontal and vertical rotation axis at one point, and the initial motion sensitivity is 7mg horizontal and vertical. cartridge has MM type cartridge (270C). This cartridge directly connects the CKS magnet with a light and rigid high-strength aluminum alloy cantilever to reduce the oscillator’s effective mass. This results in more flat frequency characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-D 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-d3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"telefunken-trx-3000":{"more":[{"t":"Here is a receiver that you’ve probably never seen before. Most vintage audio enthusiasts know of Telefunken for their tubes but many don’t know they also made receivers. I posted in the past on the Telefunken Concerto 105 which most wouldn’t call a great looking receiver (it’s ugly). This is the Telefunken TRX-3000, and, in contrast to the Concerto line, it is actually a very interesting looking receiver. I might even call it appealing. It was made during the late 70’s so it was a little ahead of its time with the black face, LED meters and digital tuner display. The case is metal and not plastic. The TRX-3000 is a quadraphonic receiver and has some power with 160 watts per channel into two channels and 90 WPC into four channels. It also has some interesting features that were ahead of it’s time such as soft touch buttons, relay-activated inputs and PLL tuner.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Telefunken TRX 3000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/telefunken-trx-3000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sa-7100":{"more":[{"t":"Toshiba’s candidate in the monster receiver category was the Toshiba SA-7100. The later SA-7150 was is similar but had one of the early digital tuners as opposed to the analog dial on this unit. The big Toshiba receivers are probably under appreciated by the collecting community and don’t bring as high a price as some of the more well known brands but they are built well and sound great. this receiver put out 110 watts per channel in to 8 ohms and 140 watts per channel in to 4 ohms. The SA-7100 has a neat flip top cover for the tone and balance controls and switches. Overall very nice styling and performance. The Toshiba SA-7100’s can be picked for a lot less than a comparable Pioneer or Sansui. If they are in very good cosmetic and working condition they can be found for less than $800.00. These are some of the most well buit receivers ever made and some of the most rare ones because you dont see the market flooded with them like others So well built they put the others units to shame and they sound great doing it","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Toshiba SA-7100","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/toshiba-sa-7100","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sa-7150":{"more":[{"t":"The Toshiba SA-7150 was a high-quality stereo receiver that was released in 1978, during the era of powerful “Monster Receivers”. It produces 150 watts per channel and retailed for a hefty $1100 at the time. Despite being a lesser known brand than the likes of Marantz and Pioneer, the SA-7150 featured excellent build quality and superb stereo performance that rivaled or exceeded the major brands. The SA-7150 had innovative features like the world’s first quartz-locked digital synthesizer tuner. Toshiba was able to produce high quality components for their receivers since they were already manufacturing quality parts for other major high end brands. In fact, the SA-7150 offered comparable quality to top models from Marantz, Pioneer and Sansui. However, Toshiba’s smaller dealer network meant the SA-7150 was not as widely marketed. As a result, the excellent SA-7150 tends to be rarer and more obscure today compared to vintage receivers from the bigger brands. But for those in the know, the Toshiba SA-7150 represents an underrated high performance stereo receiver from the late 1970s.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Toshiba SA-7150","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/toshiba-sa-7150","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/toshiba-sa-7150.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/toshiba-sa-7150","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/toshiba-sa-7150.jpg"}},"toshiba-sa-850":{"more":[{"t":"The Toshiba SA-850 is a sleek looking receiver. While other audio manufacturers were loading up the front panels of their receivers with a bunch of knobs, switches and buttons, Toshiba was going for the clean look. Introduced in 1979 the SA-850 produces 50 watts per channel into 8 ohms and that’s with less than 0.03% total harmonic distortion. It retailed for $519.95. It really is a nicely styled piece of equipment with its walnut side panels and brushed aluminum front. Note the lack of a tuning knob or analog meters of any kind. The lower half of the front panel swings down and disappears into the unit to reveal most of the lesser used controls. These include the tone controls, speaker selector switch, subsonic filter, tone defeat, loudness and others. The digital LED tuning display is a nice green color as is the signal strength meter.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Toshiba SA-850","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/toshiba-sa-850","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-630":{"more":[{"t":"A record player that employs the quartz lock servo system. In the quartz-lock servo system, the output of the FG (frequency generator) is compared with the phase of the reference oscillator for servo control. By using a highly stable crystal oscillator as the reference oscillator, we have succeeded in suppressing speed deviation within 0.003%. A stop mechanism is adopted in which when the stop button is pressed, the power of the drive circuit is turned off and a brake works to stop the rotation of the turntable. It is a mechanical system by combination of electromagnetic plunger and lever, and stops at about 1/3 of 33 1/3 of rotation. It uses a sandwich structure in which a wood case is sandwiched between steel boards and insulators. The weight is increased by the steel board, and the special sandwich structure keeps the lowest resonance frequency of the cabinet sufficiently low, making it resistant to howling. In addition, steel board is a shielding material, so it also works to prevent magnetic leakage flux from transformer and motor. Uses a frequency-frequency illuminator that is proportional to the number of revolutions regardless of the power source frequencies.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Toshiba SR-630 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AUREX/player/sr-630-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sr-f-330":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥37,800. A full automatic player of the Opus series. The belt drive method is used for turntable. The cartridge contains a MM type cartridge that is integrated with the shell.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SR-F 330 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-f330.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/toshiba-sr-f-330.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-f330.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/player/sr-f330(1).jpg"}},"victor-m-7070":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥210,000. A mono power amplifier of the laboratory 7070 series with D-class power supply. Power MOS FET is available for output stage active element. This element has excellent properties such as wideband, low distortion rate, linearity at large current, and the risk of thermal runaway. In the protective circuit, we use a protector IC that adds and integrates functions based on the Japan Victor’s proprietary three-dimensional protection circuit. This IC is equipped with functions such as power supply ON, power supply OFF, medium potential detection, relay drive, etc.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor M-7070 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/m-7070.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥59,000. The MC head amplifier is the same as A-1, and the new low noise trans is adopted. It is equipped with DISC switch, you can listen through a very simple signal path that the record is equalizer → DC high gain power amplifier. The Phono selector is equipped to replace the load resistance in three phases and supports various cartridges. We also have a 100Ω position for high power type MC cartridge without head amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-b-4":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥138,000. Stereo power amplifier with newly developed RO (output impedance) control. The first step is low-noise and high-gm dual-FET source forroa, and boots circuits are assembled in the casscode-connected dual trans equilibrium feed differential a circuitification circuit. The dual FET used here is a pair of low noise and high gm electrical and thermal characteristics of the two FETs, which are placed in the same package, and has sufficient pair characteristics for the first stage of the DC amplifier. The current mirror circuit, adopted in the pre-drive stage, obtains a positive gain as a voltage amplifier, and two trans s work a kind of push-pull circuit, and even the next harmonic distortion.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-4.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-b-4.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-4.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-4.JPG"}},"yamaha-ca-r-11":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥73,800. CA-R1-based CA-S1 technology integrated amplifier. The basic circuit configuration is composed of three circuits of DC equalizer, DC flat amplifier, and HighSpeed High ft trans, equipped with Ro control, which can continuously change output impedance from -1Ω to+1Ω, and is inserted if low noise MC head amplifier and 0dB gaintone circuit are required. In the development of CA-R11, we have introduced a new HP-IB audio analyzer and a computer, and we are considering the characteristics of each unit amplifier at a level beyond the analysis limit of the conventional instrument. The equalizer circuit adopts the DC amplifier configuration, it has a differential input current Miracus cord boots with low noise Dual FET, Darlington connection predrive, and Pure Complementary SEPP-OCL. The first Dual FET is the same package with two high-gm FETs of electrical and thermal properties. It has excellent characteristics as the first element of the DC component amplifier. The second stage is the circuitification circuit of the emitter of the constant current load of the Darlington connection, which lightens the load on the first stage. Flat amplifier circuit is almost equal to equalizer amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-R 11 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-r11.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-s-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥95,000. Developed to achieve the highest peak amplifier based on technology obtained by C-2a and B-3. The basic circuit configuration is a DC power amplifier with a high-speed high-fT trans, equipped with a high-speed high-speed high-fT trans power capable of continuously variable output impedance of DC equalizer → equalizer with low noise Dual FET at the first stage. In the development, we have introduced a new HP-IB audio analyzer and a computer to examine the characteristics of each unit amplifier at a level beyond the analysis limits of conventional measuring instruments. This circuit detects the output current of the amplifier and controls it by adding it to the NFB circuit of the amplifier via the Ro preamplifier. This reduces the characteristic deterioration caused by the sound control of the loudspeaker and the resistance of the loudspeaker code. The first low-noise Dual FET fits into the same package with the electrical and thermal characteristics of the two FETs of the High-gm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-S 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-s1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-3020":{"more":[{"t":"This monster Yamaha CR-3020 hit the audio market in 1978. It is the BIG brother of the CR-1020 and CR-2020. The CR-3020 is rated at 160 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It also has a frequency response of 5-100,000 Hz and total harmonic distortion of 0.01%. It is arguably the most collectable of the vintage monster receivers. It has been speculated that only around 2000 of the CR-3020 were made. Yamaha began manufacturing them at a time when the power war (meaning watts per channel) amongst the audio giants like Pioneer, Sansui and Marantz was subsiding. Other manufacturers were already transitioning to lighter weight designs and cheaper components and demand for bulky, heavy, monster receivers was dwindling. As a result not many were sold.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-3020","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-3020","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-yp-d-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥58,000. Direct drive player developed with a focus on three points: accurate rotation and high sensitivity and hazardous vibration isolation. The DC hole motor is equipped with 1kg/cm startup torque. This turntable achieves 270kg/cm2 of iner mass compared to rubber sheets because of the thickness of outer circumference. The power supply part adopts the power supply circuit with a constant voltage feedback circuit that maintains the voltage of 24V even when the output current of 800mA is flowing. Tonearm adopts new designed aluminum S-shaped pipe arm. This arm pipe is packed with special fillers to prevent sound quality deterioration caused by pipe resonance. In order to achieve high sensitivity, the gimbal support method has a double structure for vertical and horizontal movement, which achieves high sensitivity by holding accurately with the pivot. It has high sensitivity that shows the initial motion sensitivity of 3mg in both horizontal and vertical directions.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha YP-D 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-yp-d-7.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d7.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/yp-d7(3).jpg"}},"accuphase-p-260":{"more":[{"t":"Released April 1979 at ¥200,000.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-260 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-260-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-400":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1979 at ¥400,000. Stereo power amplifier equipped with two monaural power amplifiers. Equipped with a class A operation selection switch, Normal operation and Class-A operation can be selected. It is designed to operate as a pure A-class amplifier by switching with a switch. Class A operation mode is an original operation mode in which the operation area of the push-pull element always completely overlaps. The operation is switched by a pure electronic switch (PAT, PEND) instead of switching the circuit bias resistance with a switch. The output stage is a triple push-pull configuration using MOS FET. MOS FET has easy-to-handle characteristics compared with bipolar transistor or SIT, and at the same time, high-frequency characteristics are improved because notching distortion does not occur in high-frequency transmission. In order to minimize coloring for sound quality, the large capacitor and input capacitor of the NFB loop have been removed. In this state, even direct current is amplified and causes failure.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-400-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"bose-spatial-control":{"more":[{"t":"Well, Bose may not be known for their receivers but this is one nice looking stereo! This is the Bose Spatial Control Receiver which is model number 108787 but is more commonly referred to as the SCR. It puts out 100 watts per channel and has a built in EQ for the Bose 901 series IV speakers. Bose also made a model 550 that had a built in EQ as well but only sported 40 watts per channel and had no spatial control. The power switch is on the back of the unit and when it is on you can still turn the unit on and off by touching the Bose logo on the front of the unit. These Bose receivers aren’t that common and it’s probably due to the fact that not that many were sold. The sales copy explanation behind how the “spatial” effect worked was somewhat complicated and, of course, they were really designed to work with the Bose 901 speakers (though they could work with any speakers). Many customers probably opted for a more simple solution to their audio needs. Nonetheless, these receivers do sell for a decent amount of money.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Bose Spatial Control","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/bose-spatial-control-receiver","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-70-m":{"more":[{"t":"A manual record player with a double structure turntable. A double structure is adopted for the turntable part. Structurally, it consists of a high-cut filter that connects the upper and lower turntables with springs and dampers, and is fixed to the motor shaft, thereby blocking external vibrations such as acoustic feedback from speakers. An out Rocester type AC servo motor is used as the drive motor. The tone arm is equipped with a high-sensitivity S-shaped tone arm with dynamic damping mechanism. Equipped with a helicoid arm elevation mechanism that can adjust the height of the tone arm according to the cartridge. Uses a 70 mm thick cabinet made of particleboards with a Bubinga natural wood finish. The tone arm can be replaced with the light mass tone arm DA 401, which is compatible with high compliance type cartridges.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-70 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/DP-70M-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/denon-dp-70-m.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/DP-70M-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-70m.JPG"}},"denon-poa-3000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥350,000. This is a stereo power amplifier equipped with DENON class A, which was created by thoroughly investigating class A operation. Equipped with DENON Class A by DENON's unique real bias circuit, it realizes high output while operating as A class amplifier. The output transistor is a newly developed high-speed power transistor (f) with particularly excellent high-frequency characteristics. T: 100 MHz, Pc: 150W). This transistor can be operated at high power. FE It has good linearity and can maintain the rated output with low distortion even at 100 Hz. This high-speed power transistor has five parallel push-pull connections per channel, dramatically improving linearity and achieving low-distortion characteristics over a wide bandwidth. A real bias circuit has been adopted to solve the problems of low efficiency, heat generation and large size which were the defects of A class amplifier. Because this circuit performs class A linear amplification using the linear region of the amplification characteristics of the transistor without distortion of the signal waveform, it is controlled so that a DC bias current equal to the peak value of the signal current flowing in the transistor is supplied.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon POA-3000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/poa-3000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pra-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥200,000. A preamplifier equipped with a real-time equalizer amplifier that challenges the limits of disc playback. The EQ section uses a non-feedback real-time equalizer amplifier, a further development of the CR type. The configuration consists of two stages of DC linear amplifier with newly developed low-noise FET and CR-type equalizing filter between stages. The first stage FET is parallel differential, and a cascode boot-strap circuit is adopted to prevent degradation of high-frequency characteristics while greatly improving S/N. In addition, high S/N has been achieved by reducing impedance of the CR-type equalizing filter. The CR element uses a polypropylene capacitor and ± 1% metal film deposition resistance. The Phono3 terminal is directly connected to the MC head amplifier composed of 22 transistors. This head amplifier has the same circuit configuration as DENON's top-of-the-line head amplifier HA-1000. For example, a PNP type low-noise transistor, which is advantageous for low noise, is connected in parallel at the first stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PRA-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pra-2000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-7700":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier equipped with power MOS FET applying the know-how obtained in HMA 9500 to premain. The power MOS FET has achieved a switching speed of 0.05 μ sec and an amplification factor of 1 MHz (-2dB). Compared with conventional bipolar transistors, it has achieved a high performance of more than one order of magnitude. As a result, a power gain of 85 dB at 100 kHz is achieved. Even at 100 kHz, a stable negative feedback can be obtained. Moreover, since the switching speed is fast, excellent push-pull operation can be achieved even in class B circuit configuration. In order to maximize the performance of the power stage, a simple 3-stage power circuit with little phase change is adopted. In addition, the operation stability is improved by the all-stage DC amplifier configuration. In the equalizer amplifier section, three stages of cascode differential ICL circuit, current mirror differential circuit and SEPP circuit are directly connected to each other to ensure an allowable input of 300 mV against an SN ratio of 85 dB and an input sensitivity of 2.5 mV.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HA 7700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/ha-7700-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-660":{"more":[{"t":"A full auto player system with quartz lock and electronic return. The motor is equipped with a unitorque motor based on Lordi's proprietary technology. The Unitorque Motor is a motor which obtained perfect circular motion from the principle. It consists of a doughnut-shaped rotor magnet magnetized with 8 poles and two sets of star-shaped flat coils offset by 22 ^ 5 degrees. The torque generated by these two coils and magnets is constant at any moment. This principle is called sin 2 Θ + cos 2 Θ = 1 \". The Uni-Torque Motor also adopts a simple structure that is brushless, slotless and coreless, and has significantly improved durability. In the HT-660, this uni-torque motor is equipped with crystal control (quartz lock PLL servo) which is hardly affected by voltage fluctuation, aging and temperature change, and achieves high precision rotation. The start-up a constant speed at 1/2 revolution.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HT-660 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/player/ht-660-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-860":{"more":[{"t":"A computer-controlled full-auto player with centralized computer control. It is equipped with a 4-bit microcomputer. By detecting and processing signals from the front switch and various detection mechanisms, almost all functions of the player, from variable rotation quartz lock to auto size / auto speed selector, memory repeat, arming, etc. are controlled centrally. The motor is equipped with a unitorque motor based on Lordi's proprietary technology. The Unitorque Motor is a motor which obtained perfect circular motion from the principle. It consists of a doughnut-shaped rotor magnet magnetized with 8 poles and two sets of star-shaped flat coils offset by 22 ^ 5 degrees. The torque generated by these two coils and magnets is constant at any moment. This principle is called sin 2 Θ + cos 2 Θ = 1 \". The Uni-Torque Motor also adopts a simple structure that is brushless, slotless and coreless, and has significantly improved durability.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HT-860 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/player/ht-860-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-x-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥69,800. Equipped with a super A circuit. In A-X5, all signal circuits are cleaned. The power amplifier is equipped with a super A circuit. This circuit is composed of the A-class power stage that combines power efficiency and high linearity comparable to the B-class amplifier. A-class sound quality and high power. New DC servo equalizer is available in the equalizer amplifier. This circuit is a servo amplifier that cuts the ultra-low area that is unnecessary for music playback, increases DC stability, and realizes high gain of equalizer that was impossible in the past. It supports MC/MM cartridge without MC head amplifier. The power supply section adopts direct power supply method, and the secondary side of the large circuit is separated for voltage amplifier and power amplifier, and connected directly with each circuit, reducing the supply power impedance in the broadband.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-X 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-x-9":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥158,000. Equipped with a super A circuit. The power amplifier is equipped with super low distortion rate and high efficiency. High-level input is connected directly without passing the preamplifier. This makes it possible to realize a complete DC amplifier configuration without any coupling capac from Tuner, Tap, Aux input to loudspeaker output. The latest high-fT power trans is available in the output stage. TIM distortion measurement is achieved by coupled with the super A driver circuit with fast response speed. The equalizer part is a high-gain DC configuration using a pair of EL-FETs unique to Japan Victor. The servo method cuts the ultra-low area that is unnecessary for music playback and increases DC stability. In addition, the circuit technology of Super A is used to reduce distortion.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-X 9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x9.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-a-x-9.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x9.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x9.JPG"}},"jvc-m-7050":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥250,000. Super A automatically controls the bias voltage of the power stage according to the input signal. In addition, the Super A bias circuit provides even better linearity and lower distortion than the conventional A-class power stage. In addition to the power stage, the Super A has a unique concept for the driver stage. A-class operation is often used because the power of the power stage is not used in the general driver stage. However, the A class cannot cover the nonlinearity of the semiconductor itself. Super A reexamines the use of semiconductors. By setting the motion trajectory of the emitter ground circuit static characteristics that were changed by the input signal level, it realizes low distortion rate of 1/10 or less compared to the conventional driver stage.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC M-7050 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/m-7050.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-9050":{"more":[{"t":"Many audio enthusiasts consider a monster receiver to be one that puts out 100 watts per channel or more. Well, this Kenwood KR-9050 puts out just that – 200 watts per channel. So, I guess it would be considered a monster receiver. It certainly has the size at almost 2 feet wide, over 18 inches deep and over 52 pounds! Still, the KR-9050 probably takes a back seat to the KR-9600 that collectors are the most fervent over. I’m not sure why because the 9600 has some design issues that can be difficult to overcome and only puts out 160 watts per channel. Perhaps it’s that the KR-9600 so firmly established itself as the top of the line receiver for Kenwood it overshadowed the KR-9050 when it came out. The KR-9060 is really just a KR-9600 with a bronze faceplate. The Kenwood KR-9050 is the largest and most expensive receiver ever built by Kenwood.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-9050","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-9050","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-07-c-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥160,000. preamplifier with a built-in ultra-low impedance output circuit of less than 10Ω to faithfully transmit input signal waveform to amplifier near the loudspeaker system. The output impedance is 10Ω or less buffer amplifier so that the audio cable can be extended to the power amplifier installed near the loudspeaker. With this, even if the 180PF/m shield line is connected to 20m, the frequency characteristic is only 0.1dB in the ultra-high area of 500kHz, and the high frequency loss in the cable is almost no problem. The equalizer amplifier has developed and adopted a circuit with a low distortion ratio and high SN ratio. The circuit configuration is casscode differential with high gain mirror using ultra-low noise FET. In order not to lose the first gain, the second step is equipped with an Emitter Forroer, and the third step is a differential motion with a current mirror, and the end is a pure complementary SEPP. Even with low impedance, it works with a low distortion rate and has a large dynamic range. As a result, low distortion rate of 0.003% is increased. The SN ratio is 90dB for 2.5mV input, and the noise level is 0.079μV with input conversion IHF A correction value, and -142dBV.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-07 C II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-07cii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-07m-ii":{"more":[{"t":"A power amplifier designed to be on the side of the loudspeaker system. The circuit is simplified and the signal is supplied to the output terminal with the shortest path from the input terminal. We design the power supply section from the signal amplifier to minimize the impact on the signal system. The voltage amplifier adopts the three-stage direct connection ICL, OCL, and DC amplifier with dual FET with low temperature drift. CMRR (same partial removal ratio) is greatly improved and DC stability is improved. In addition, the current amplifier is a double-stage darlington triple push pull circuit using EBT, which ensures power with the extreme distortion rate. The power supply unit is designed to avoid common with other circuits as much as possible. Made of aluminum die-cast chimney type heat sink.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-07M II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-07mii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-c-5000a":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1979 at ¥355,000. The control center was developed for the top-of-the-line audio system by LUX's unique technology such as duo-beta circuit. In order to improve sound quality, we have adopted LUX's own duo-beta circuit. In this circuit, the minimum necessary amount of NFB is applied to all bands, and a DC servo circuit is combined. This eliminates TIM distortion by reducing the amount of NFB by keeping the gain of the amplifier low. In addition, the DC servo circuit not only cuts ultra-low frequency noise, which causes intermodulation distortion, but also uses a low-noise FET amplifier and a high-quality film capacitor in the low-pass filter circuit low-pass reproduction. In order to realize an amplifier with low gain and good characteristics suitable for a duo-beta circuit, we have adopted a combination of a cascode differential input bootstrap circuit and a transistor dynamic resistance circuit at the input stage. In the output stage, a four transistor SEPP circuit is used to keep the output impedance low. In order to minimize wiring, all switches are remotely connected to the board so that the circuit on the board can be directly switched by the knob on the panel. In addition, multi-circuit switches are used in parallel to prevent noise degradation caused by contacts.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman C-5000A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/c-5000a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lx-33":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1979 at ¥138,000. Simple configuration tube sphere integrated amplifier. It is designed to reduce various distortions to improve sound quality. The output tube has 6CA7, and 15 types of LX33. The output stage is an ultralinear connection. LUX tone control circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman LX-33 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lx33.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-lx-33.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lx33.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lx33.jpg"}},"luxman-m-4000a":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1980 at ¥398,000. This stereo power amplifier is based on the large power amplifier M-4000 released in 1975, and has been further improved by introducing the latest technology. Equipped with LUX's own duo-beta circuit to improve sound quality. In this circuit, an appropriate amount of NFB is applied to all bands, and a DC servo circuit is coupled to the ultra-low band to determine the characteristics of sound quality in all bands and to modify the ultra-low band out of the audible band to obtain the overall unity. In addition, the higher the bare characteristics of the amplifier, the higher the gain (gain). In order to suppress this, a large amount of NFB is applied and the sound quality deteriorates. To solve this vicious circle, we have made an amplifier with excellent bare characteristics and low gain, and greatly reduce NFB. As a result, we eliminate TIM distortion caused by the difference between NFB application in the low and high frequencies. In addition, the DC servo circuit reduces the ultra-low frequency noise and improves the resolution of the low-frequency reproduction by increasing the damping factor of the ultra-low frequency. It also solves the DC drift problem and protects the speakers.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman M-4000A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/m-4000a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-5":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier capable of switching between pure class A and class AB. In addition to pure A-class 20W/ch, AB-class 80W/ch can be switched. Moreover, in order to raise the quality of AB-class to the level of pure A-class, a high-speed high-fT transistor with a high cut-off frequency of 90 MHz is adopted in the power stage, eliminating the switching distortion that is a defect of AB-class to the limit. The PM-5 adopts a complete push-pull DC amplifier configuration in all stages to eliminate TIM distortion from every corner of the amplifier, thereby improving the bare characteristics. Transient cross-modulation distortion and static characteristics are improved without applying a large amount of NFB. In order to improve the stable operation of the power transistor, a newly developed heat pipe system has been adopted for the heat radiation mechanism. Since heat is out of the circuit and cooled by a radiator, the transistor can be placed in an ideal position, simplifying the circuit and reducing distortion. The power supply section is equipped with a large-capacity capacitor developed for audio equipment and a compact high-power transformer filled with a special resin for heat resistance. The phono amplifier block is designed with low distortion and high S/N ratio by using transistors lavishly.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-6":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier that adopts the design of separate amplifier SC-6 and SM-6. Pure A-class 30W + 30W with full push-pull DC configuration for all stages. The power is high in freshness and does not cause switching distortion in principle. In addition, it can be changed to AB class 120W/ch with a single switch. In order to reduce the difference in sound caused by switching, a high-speed high-fT transistor with a cut-off frequency of 90 MHz is adopted in the power stage. Switching distortion, which was said to be a weak point of AB class, is minimized, and it is finished as a delicate yet powerful AB class amplifier. Low-TIM design for the preamplifier as well as the power amplifier. Carefully selected materials and sophisticated circuitry improve the bare characteristics. The amount of negative feedback (NF) is reduced to eliminate audible distortion.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-6-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sc-6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥88,000. preamplifier that uses Low-TIM construction. The complete push-pull DC configuration of all stages by Low-TIM construction drives the dynamic characteristic distortion which does not appear in the data to the limit, and sends a beautiful signal to the power amplifier. For disc playback with low output voltage, special emphasis is placed on the choice of material for the phono amplifier, which has been tested by measurement and ear test. Its characteristics are as follows: 0.005% or less at minimum guaranteed total harmonic distortion rate, 0.003% or less intermodulation distortion rate, and 86 dB S/N ratio. In addition, the built-in head amplifier has a DC configuration with low-noise FET at the first stage and uses transistors as large as 13 single-channel transistors. The tone control circuit, which is essential for sound field correction in the listening room, is independent on the left and right sides so that a more critical balance can be achieved. In addition, the tone circuit is equipped with a defeat switch so that the circuit can be simplified by jumping when it is not necessary, enabling higher fidelity playback. The tone circuit is also equipped with a loudness control so that you can choose between 2 points, + 8 dB or + 4 dB, depending on the volume. In addition to the ash filter that cuts the hissing of the tape, the filter is equipped with a subsonic circuit that reduces the fluctuation of the speaker that occurs when the record is played back.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SC-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sc-6.-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥950,000. This is a stereo power amplifier developed by putting in all the technologies of Marantz at that time and eliminating all the cost constraints. All stages of the power block are completely push-pull configuration in order to take out the large output of 400W single-channel with high quality and stability. In addition, it uses 18 single-channel power transistors of up to 200 W PC, divided into 6 groups of 3 transistors each and driven by 6 drivers. It is a luxurious circuit that uses only the best parts of hfe reality. With our unique Low-TIM design, the open-loop gain is kept at an extremely low level of 56 to 57 dB, so that the amount of negative feedback (NF), which adversely affects dynamic characteristics, is reduced to the same level as a vacuum tube amplifier. On a highly reliable glass-epoxy double-sided through-hole substrate developed for computers, dual transistors and diode array with ideal characteristics are used at each point. These elements are arranged in perfect symmetry to perfectly switch electrical and thermal coefficients and eliminate DC drift from materials and circuits. The sound quality deteriorates as the number of contact points increases. The SM1000 does not include a speaker protect relay because it allows a direct signal with no contact points to the speaker terminals.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-6":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo power amplifier capable of switching between pure A class and AB class. Pure class A operation is adopted, and the output for pure class A is 30W/ch. It can also be used as class AB operation of 120W/ch by switching the switch. In addition to introducing an advanced low-TIM design, we use carefully selected materials. The power transistor is a high-speed high-fT transistor with a sufficient collector loss margin and superior high-frequency characteristics. This transistor has a cutoff frequency of 90 MHz, which suppresses switching distortion that cannot be avoided in class AB, and flattens high-frequency phase characteristics. In addition, all stages have a complete push-pull DC amplifier configuration to improve the bare characteristics and reduce the amount of negative feedback (NF). The TIM distortion is reduced without compromising the static characteristics. In addition, DC drift, which is a problem in DC amplifiers, is controlled by parts with ideal characteristics and DC servo circuits, ensuring high reliability.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-6-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-tt-1000":{"more":[{"t":"A direct drive player with a 3-layer structure cabinet. Returning to the foundations of oscillation theory, where materials of different masses can be used in the sandwich structure to convert vibrational energy into thermal energy, we focused on high-density glass and pure aluminum to drive vibration transmission out of the cabinet. It has a three layer structure consisting of 8 mm thick aluminum plates and special glass (15 mm thick and 7.5 kg weight), which is designed to increase the accuracy of the plane, on top and bottom, so that no unnecessary howling or reverberation is generated. For the turntable seat, we do not use materials with high internal loss such as rubber to absorb vibration, but we use 5 mm thick hard glass with excess hardness and weight for non-core copper based on the concept of structure that does not absorb vibration itself. In order to ensure that uniform weights are always applied to discs with sleds, and to achieve the full performance of all types of cartridges, we have adopted a mass variable dynamic balance tone arm that can change the effective mass of the arm according to compliance. For the aluminum material of the straight type with reduced effective mass, super aluminum alloy with small mass and high strength is used, and the connector part with the head shell is a semi-integrated type with insert-type surface contact that does not generate resonance due to rattling.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz TT-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/player/Tt1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-ma-6200":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1979 at ¥478,000. an integrated amplifier developed by integrating the Macintosh technology into one unit. It is equipped with a 5-band independent program equalizer, two tape circuits capable of mutual dubbing, a pre-main separation terminal, and a continuously variable loudness compensator. As a protective circuit, it is equipped with Power Guard System which is unique to Macintosh. Clipping distortion is suppressed automatically, and the speaker is protected from accident.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MA 6200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/ma6200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-a-600":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo power amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-A 600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-a600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-p-600":{"more":[{"t":"Preamplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-P 600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-p600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-da-u-630":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier with improved play functions such as a triple mixing circuit. The power amplifier section is a first stage differential amplifier and all stages are directly connected and pure complimentary service OCL circuit to obtain excellent distortion factor characteristics. The equalizer amplifier and tone control flat amplifier are first stage differential amplifier, and 4-stage direct-coupled low-noise IC is adopted. The built-in mixing amplifier allows for triple microphone mixing using two wired microphones and one wireless microphone. You can also echo the microphone by using a reverb circuit. The LED power level indicator on the digital display is used to indicate the power level. The output level can be read directly by 9 points of one channel. A built-in protective circuit that combines an electronic circuit and a relay. When a DC potential higher than a certain level is generated at the output terminal of the power amplifier, the output of the amplifier and the speaker are instantly disconnected to protect the speaker from damage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DA-U 630 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/amp/da-u630-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nakamichi-530":{"more":[{"t":"A high-quality stereo receiver that can be used as a second main system. The tuner section has a self-lock tuning mechanism. In this system, a kind of electronic servo is operated by detecting the deviation of the local oscillation frequency to suppress the tuning deviation forcibly. In the 530, this self-lock tuning is linked to the motor drive mechanism for self-tuning by soft touch, and four preset stations are also available. A low-noise dual-gate MOS-FET is used in the front end section to reduce various kinds of distortion generated in the high-frequency Zofuku-ji Temple. In addition, multi-stage tuning is performed by an air varicon, which is essentially excellent as a tuning element, to increase the image interference ratio, IF interference ratio, spurious interference ratio, etc., and excellent interference rejection capability is obtained. A specially selected high-quality ceramic filter is used in the IF section to achieve both low distortion and selectivity. The MPX section uses a PLL circuit to suppress degradation of the separation and enable stable stereo reproduction. If you want to receive only broadcasting stations with high antenna input sensitivity, turn the threshold switch off.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Nakamichi 530 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/NAKAMICHI/amp/530-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/nakamichi-530.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/NAKAMICHI/amp/530-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/NAKAMICHI/amp/530.JPG"}},"pioneer-c-21":{"more":[{"t":"This is a simple preamplifier with a monofunctional to achieve high-quality sound. The equalizer amplifier uses a 2-stage differential, class A SEPP current mirror circuit. Various characteristics are improved by this circuit with emphasis on reducing distortion and improving SN ratio. In addition, carefully selected elements such as precision small metal film resistors with a resistance error of ± 0.5% and temperature characteristics of ± 100 ppm / ℃, and polypropylene capacitors with a capacitance error of ± 1% are used for the equalizer elements. A high voltage of ± 37 V is applied to this circuit to ensure a dynamic margin of 300 mV maximum allowable input for sensitivity of 2.5 mV. In order to demonstrate the performance of various cartridges, 6 load resistances and 6 load capacities can be independently selected, and a total of 36 cartridge loads can be set. The load resistance position of 100 Ω is suitable for direct connection of MC cartridge with large output voltage. The flat amplifier section uses two stage differential amplification as well as the equalizer section. A low-noise transistor is used in the first stage, and a current mirror circuit is used in the intermediate amplifier stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer C 21 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/c-21-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-c-21.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/c-21-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/c-21.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-l-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥99,800. Linear tracking player designed using technology and know-how obtained by the development of PL-L1. It is equipped with an electronic full automatic mechanism, which enables precise operation of auto-reed-in, auto-return and auto-repeat. The drive motor adopts the SH loader motor to achieve excellent characteristics. linear DD arm The cabinet adopts core-chial suspension cabinet, which improves howling properties. Equipped with quick play and quick stop mechanism. Because it is a front operation type, you can operate tonearm as it is even if the cover is closed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-L 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-l5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sa-8800":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo integrated amplifier with high cost performance such as control using FET and extra power. The power amplifier section consists of a pure complimentary service OCL circuit directly connected to all stages of the first stage. In addition, high-quality sound has been achieved by adopting a pair of transistors with uniform characteristics and a large radiator, and by using a pre-driver as a stabilized power source to eliminate transient crossover distortion at minute output. In addition, to improve stability, ± 2 power supply by OCL circuit is adopted, and bias compensation circuit which always suppresses DC component leaking to output due to temperature change is installed. The flat amplifier in the control section has an FET in the first stage, so that noise does not change depending on the volume position, and noise is suppressed at any volume position. In addition, NFB is applied both AC and DC to the 2-stage direct-coupled flat amplifier, so that the distortion component can be minimized and low impedance can be fed to the tone circuit of the next stage, making the tone circuit work under more ideal conditions. The control circuit also uses ± 2 power supply to suppress noise caused by switching. The tone circuit uses a two stage turnover switch, which expands the range of tone control and allows for more ideal adjustment. The equalizer uses a 3-stage direct-coupled amplifier with ± 2 power supplies and a low-noise transistor at the first stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-8800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-8800-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sa-9800":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo integrated amplifier developed by inheriting the design philosophy of SA-9900. Like SA-9900, it adopts a side terminal system in which input / output terminals are arranged on the left and right panels. As a result, the input terminal is completely integrated with the equalizer board to prevent degradation of the high-frequency characteristics caused by the shielding wire. The power amplifier section uses a pure complimentary service OCL circuit directly connected to all stages. It consists of a single stage differential with ± 2 power supplies and a parallel push-pull configuration. By making the load of the pre-driver constant current, the bare gain is increased, and by applying the optimum NFB, the distortion is reduced over a wide band. By using the power supply before the output stage as a stabilizing power supply, the transient crossover distortion at minute outputs is eliminated. By using the parallel push-pull output stage, the linearity of current characteristics is improved and distortion is reduced. In addition, a differential amplifier and a bias compensation circuit are adopted to improve stability, so that fluctuation of offset voltage due to external temperature change is minimized.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-9800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-9800-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"quad-44":{"more":[{"t":"Preamplifier with module configuration. All input / output terminals of QUAD44 are modularized and can be replaced as needed. Equipped with tilt control and base control, it can respond to changes in characteristics depending on the listening room and speakers. The tilt control adds gradual changes throughout the frequency band without changing the overall level. The base control consists of a LIFT position and a STEP position. The LIFT position is used to smoothly increase the low-frequency characteristics of small speakers, and the STEP position is used to cut howling when speakers are installed on walls or corners. Phono Input has 5 types of modules to support all MM/MC cartridges. In addition, matching with the cartridge is handled by replacing the module. There was a separately sold wood case named sleeve.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Quad 44 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/QUAD/amp/44-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-607":{"more":[{"t":"This is a DC integrated amplifier equipped with a diamond differential circuit that identifies the essence of audio amplifier as music playback. The design further improves the DC conversion of the amplifier section. The equalizer section, flat amplifier section, and power amplifier section are all composed of DC amplifiers with excellent dynamic characteristics. In addition, all block stage inputs are all FET inputs and are used as a push-pull input circuit, and the input capacitors of all block stages are eliminated in the direct coupling system. This eliminates the low-frequency phase rotation that occurs when a capacitor enters the signal path, and other factors that degrade sound quality. As a result, pure music signal transmission and a wide range are achieved. A diamond differential circuit is mounted on the power amplifier. The first stage adopts a differential circuit with constant current using dual FET capable of passing a large current with low noise characteristics, and the second stage adopts a diamond differential circuit with cascode bootstrap. And, NM (Non Magnetic) transistor with good linearity is used for the power stage, and the whole circuit is composed of symmetrical symmetrical circuit and 2 pole phase correction circuit, which realizes waveform transmission with little distortion up to high frequency range.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-D 607 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d607-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-d-607.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d607-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d607.JPG"}},"sansui-au-d-707":{"more":[{"t":"A DC integrated amplifier with a 3 DC amplifier configuration with a diamond actuation circuit mounted on the equalizer section. The equalizer, flat amplifier / tone amplifier, and power amplifier are all DC amplifiers. The direct coupling method is adopted in which input capacitors of all stages are eliminated. The straight DC amplifier configuration provides pure music signal transmission and a wide range. The inputs of all block stages are FET inputs with low-noise, high-gm characteristics and a full push-pull input circuit. In addition, each block stage greatly reduces the harmful dynamic distortion in the target circuit configuration. The power amplifier section follows the circuit configuration of the AU-D907. In other words, the first stage is equipped with a constant-current operation circuit using dual FET that has excellent low-noise characteristics and allows large current to flow, and the second stage is equipped with a diamond complimentary service circuit using dual differential with improved dynamic characteristics to enhance the drive capability of the pre-drive stage. In addition, SANSUI Custom NM (Non Magnetic) transistor with excellent linearity is used for the power stage, and it has a symmetrical circuit structure with good dynamic characteristics and excellent sound quality.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-D 707 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707.-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-d-707.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707.-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707(1).JPG"}},"sansui-au-d-907-limited":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥175,000. Based on the AU-D907, this is a custom model that removes all restrictions and thoroughly pursues both sound and technical aspects. In addition, it is a custom model that uses a lot of know-how and new materials cultivated in the development of AU-X1. The equalizer circuit has the same 20-chip configuration as the AU-X1. Coupled with a cascode boot-strap circuit that brings the diamond differential circuit closer to the ideal operation, the dynamic range is expanded. The MC head amplifier uses an all-FET input and full push-pull input / output circuit, and Pch/Nch FET is used for the element. Non-ferrous linear high-speed element LAPT (Linear Amp. Power Tr.) is used in two parallel connection, further improving the real value of the diamond differential circuit. This realizes a high response speed of ± 300 through rate of ± V / μ sec and suppresses the occurrence of TIM distortion to nearly 0. The power supply section has been strengthened with the theme of high-speed response.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-D 907 Limited (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d907limited-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-d-907-limited.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d907limited-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d907limited.JPG"}},"sansui-au-x-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1979 at ¥210,000.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-X 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-x1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-ba-f1":{"more":[{"t":"DC power amplifier with a diamond differential circuit. A diamond differential circuit is used in the pre-drive stage. The first stage employs a direct-coupled voltage-differential amplifier circuit with current source using dual FET with low noise and large current flow, the second pre-drive stage employs a dual complimentary service diamond differential circuit with cascode and bootstrap, and the final power stage employs a current-differential push-pull circuit using Sansui Custom NM transistors. Coupled with a 2-pole phase correction circuit, it realizes low-distortion transmission up to high frequencies. The power supply section has a large EI transformer located in the center of the chassis. This transformer has two independent windings on the left and right sides and two rectifier circuits to maintain reliable operation even at full power. It also uses a newly developed custom electrolytic capacitor 15,000 μ Fx4. In order to dissipate heat generated by the power transistor, a large chimney type heat sink and a bonnet design that utilizes the heat sink are used to cope with heat radiation. It is equipped with a large power meter.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui BA-F1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/ba-f1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-ca-f-1":{"more":[{"t":"A thin DC preamplifier using a diamond differential circuit and toroidal transformer. Uses MC head amplifier. The circuit configuration employs a symmetrical circuit with push-pull input and push-pull output. It also adopts a symmetrical circuit which is further advanced from the symmetrical circuit and the parallel connection of low-noise, high-gm P-channel and N-channel FET developed by SANSUI for the first time, and symmetrical circuit which is further advanced from symmetrical circuit. In addition, stable operation is achieved by independent power supply for left and right channels. It uses a monophonic construction configuration, and each block is a symmetrical circuit with independent left and right arrangements. Furthermore, in order to improve separation and crosstalk, left and right independent wafers are used for switches. Furthermore, in pursuit of high-quality sound, we use not only patterns on circuit boards but also jumper with lead wires that allow sufficient current to flow. A newly developed thin toroidal transformer is used for the power supply section.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui CA-F 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/ca-f1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-fr-q-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥47,500. Computer LSI is available in the full automatic electronic circuit. arming full-auto operation, the following signals are output by repeating check of arm, arm lifter position, record size setting, repeat etc. The end groove counts time between one pulse of arm position sensor at the pulse counter and also reads a slight difference of 33, 45rpm. And when set time and pulse width are changed, arm will start the end operation by determining that the end groove of the record is running. This mechanism is a stop-priority design, so you don’t have to worry about painful cartridge needles because it just goes into the stop operation at any position of the full auto. The full auto mechanism features a dedicated motor to ensure accurate operation. The arm and mechanism are structured to separate with the circular clutch, making it a contactless design that does not stop from the mechanism during the trace.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui FR-Q 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/fr-q5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-fr-q-5.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/fr-q5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/fr-q5.jpg"}},"sanyo-dca-301":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥27,800. Built-in microphone mixing function. The power amplifier is equipped with a hybrid power IC. This IC is equipped with an OCL circuit, which is directly connected to the power supply. Low noise and monolithic ICs are available in the Ikoli Zamp section. Equipped with a microphone mixing circuit, you can blend records, FM broadcasts and microphone sounds. tone control circuit Equipped with loudness circuit and tape monitor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sanyo DCA-301 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANYO/amp/dca-301.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-75":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥89,800. Full automatic player with contactless full automatic mechanism based on electronic control arm \"biotracer\". The biotracer is equipped with a speed sensor, position detection sensor and linear motor respectively in the vertical and horizontal direction of the arm. Normally several hundred logic decisions are performed for one operation, and the arm position, speed, and operation switch state are checked, and the instruction processing is performed at a speed of 1/1000 seconds or less. This biotracer suppresses the peak of low frequency fo within 3dB and improves crosstalk. You can move tonearm to the left and right, or turntable to work alone, and you can perform strict queuing. In addition, it is possible to adjust the needle pressure while playing because it can be done by the knob on the front panel. The contactless system enables smooth and quiet operation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 75 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x75.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-35":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥45,000. Equipped with microphone mixing mechanism for simple and straight transmission. Like TA-F55, it has 4 step cartridge load selector. The power amplifier is the DC power amplifier of the discrete configuration using the current mirror differential amplifier circuit. By simple and straight transmission, we are pursuing the shortest distance part placement along the signal flow, preventing sound quality degradation by electrostatic bonding between wires and components. MC cartridge Self-defeit tone control and loudness switch Gold plated terminal is available for fono input terminal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 35 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f35.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-f-35.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f35.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f35.JPG"}},"sony-ta-f-45":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥54,000. Equipped with TA-F55 circuit device. Like TA-F55, it has 4 step cartridge load selector. The Hi-fT trans is powered by a DC power amplifier. This trans has excellent high-speed response characteristics, so it is possible to suppress the dynamic distortion such as transient modulation distortion with a simple circuit, preventing the negative impact on the sound quality caused by the complexity of the circuit. Heat pipe method is used for heat dissipation, and using heat pipe with a heat conductivity of hundreds of times the copper rod, it is necessary to use the lead wire for the trans and circuit board, and it prevents electromagnetic wave generation from the lead wire. The power supply unit uses a high-speed type rectifier to improve stability. The pulse power supply contributes to the non-fluxing of 50Hz/60Hz magnetic field to make AC100V DC instantly. The preamplifier is equipped with a dedicated FET buffer power supply. By simple and straight transmission, we are pursuing the shortest distance part placement along the signal flow, preventing sound quality degradation by electrostatic bonding between wires and components.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 45 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f45.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-f-45.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f45.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f45.JPG"}},"sony-ta-f-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥59,800. Equipped with integrated amplifiers such as step cartridge load selector and simple & straight transmission, which focus on how to use cartridge. The Hi-fT trans is powered by a DC power amplifier. This trans has excellent high-speed response characteristics, so it is possible to suppress the dynamic distortion such as transient modulation distortion with a simple circuit, preventing the negative impact on the sound quality caused by the complexity of the circuit. Heat pipe method is used for heat dissipation, and using heat pipe with a heat conductivity of hundreds of times the copper rod, it is necessary to use the lead wire for the trans and circuit board, and it prevents electromagnetic wave generation from the lead wire. Power supply The pulse power supply contributes to the non-fluxing of 50Hz/60Hz magnetic field to make AC100V DC instantly. In addition, TA-F55 realizes more stable power supply by using high-speed type rectifier. The preamplifier is equipped with a dedicated FET buffer power supply.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-f-55.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f55.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f55.JPG"}},"technics-sl-1015":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥220,000. SH-15B1 and EPA-500 SP-15 series using SP-15 turntable synthesizer. The direct-drive motor is integrated with the motor and turntable. It boasts excellent load characteristics of 0% rotational dev up to 500 g needle pressure. In addition, the servo circuit adopts all-round detection FG to realize more accurate rotation speed. In addition, SL-1015 adopts pitch control of quartz synthesizer method, which can be ±9.9% pitch control in 0.1% steps. LED is used for display. The turntable brake mechanism adopts a double brake system that combines electronic brakes and mechanical brakes, enabling smooth and quick stoppage. In the turntable part, the electronic circuit exceeding 3000 elements is integrated into four ICs to improve stability and reliability. The power supply circuit is equipped with efficient pulse power supply circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1015 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1015.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1025":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥160,000. A direct drive turntable system with a universal type of system tonearm. Tonearm EPA-250 is available for pickup. Dynamic damping system, gimbal suspension support structure, precision helicoid arm arm adjustment mechanism is available. Turntable is SP-25. Motor features high torque integrated direct-drive motor. SH-15B2 In addition to using a special viscoelastic rubber, turntable is a triple deadening structure by special rubber.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1025 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1025.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1200mk2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥75,000. Direct drive player with a continuous pitch control system. All-round detection FG is used to obtain accurate detection signals than the one-point detection method to detect the entire rotation axis. In addition, the motor is equipped with an integrated direct-drive motor. The Gimbal suspension system is used to achieve a superior initial sensitivity of 7mg both horizontally and vertically. The arm arm adjustment mechanism with lock mechanism is equipped with a precision helicoid-finished height adjustment cylinder, enabling fine adjustment in the range of 6mm. In addition, direct-drive motor, tonearm, and dust cover are connected to special rubber, and we provide thorough anti-vibration measures to isolate each part separately. Also, turntable improves vibration resistance by deadning rubber on the back of the rubber sheet and turntable. A slide is available for pitch adjustment.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1200MK2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1200mk2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-d-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥34,800. SL-D3 full-auto function is omitted and only auto-return and auto-stop player. B/FG method is used to detect motor rotation speed. In addition, the motor is equipped with a unique integrated direct-drive motor, which the motor rotation unit is integrated with turntable. TNRC is a double anti-vibration structure used for cabinet and base by changing vibration characteristics. It is designed to absorb vibrations most effectively by reducing unnecessary resonance space as much as possible and thorough vibration analysis. High sensitivity gimbal suspension system is adopted by bearings with high precision pivot bearings made in the bearing structure of tonearm. This crosses horizontal and vertical rotation axis at one point, and the initial motion sensitivity is 7mg horizontal and vertical. cartridge has MM type cartridge (270C). This cartridge directly connects the CKS magnet with a light and rigid high-strength aluminum alloy cantilever to reduce the oscillator’s effective mass. This results in more flat frequency characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-D 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-d2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-q-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥44,800. Direct drive player with quartz phase locked control. Auto-stop system for auto-return and auto-stop. The cabinet has a two-layer structure with precision aluminum die-casting and TNRC, which has high vibration-proof effect on the bottom base and cabinet top. The front operation method can be operated by all control switches until the dust cover is closed. Equipped with a high sensitivity tonearm with a gimbal suspension system that achieves 7mg horizontally and vertically. Arm is equipped with anti-scaling force control function.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-Q 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-q-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥49,800. Direct drive full automatic player with quartz-fade locked control. Fully automatic mechanism for auto start, auto return and auto stop. The cabinet has a two-layer structure with precision aluminum die-casting and TNRC, which has high vibration-proof effect on the bottom base and cabinet top. The front operation method can be operated by all control switches until the dust cover is closed. Equipped with a high sensitivity tonearm with a gimbal suspension system that achieves 7mg horizontally and vertically. Arm is equipped with anti-scaling force control function.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-Q 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v-10":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated DC amplifier that uses Technics' new classA circuit. The new classA circuit was developed as a circuit having only the excellent points of classA operation and class B operation, and it is realized by a synchronous bias circuit. This synchronous bias circuit controls the bias of the output stage in synchronization with the input signal. It has a structure in which a constant bias current is supplied to the - side output stage when the + side signal is being reproduced, and to the + side output stage when the - side signal is being reproduced. In this structure, a constant bias current is supplied to the + side output stage when the - side signal is being reproduced. Therefore, the transistor of the output stage is always active regardless of the presence or absence of the signal and switching distortion does not occur. The circuit of SU-V10 consists of an initial stage composed of FET differential circuit and cascode circuit, a voltage amplifier stage with constant current load, a voltage driver circuit for emitter-follower output with A-class operation up to SEPP connected transistors, and a Darlington connected SEPP output stage through a synchronous bias circuit. A straight DC method is adopted in which a capacitor with a time constant is eliminated from the stage between the high-level input and the output terminal of the speaker and negative feedback (NFB).","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v10-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sc-m-15":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥67,000. BTL connection can be used as a mono power amplifier. SC-M15 adopts the DC configuration of two differential and full-stage pure complementary OCL. In addition, it is a single push-pull configuration considering the sound quality. The phase reverse circuit is built-in and can be used as a mono power amplifier with BTL connection. In the BTL (Ba BT formerless) connection, the loudspeaker code is connected using the plus side of the output terminal, and the front BTL switch is used. The power supply section is equipped with a large troidal contact. New IC (TA-7317P) protection circuit This circuit protects the trans when the output is short and protects the loudspeaker if the DC appears.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SC-M 15 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sc-m15.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sy-c-15":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥55,000. DC preamplifier with compact design. Two-block structures of equalizer and tone (flat amplifier) are used. The sameizer amplifier has a new dual FET (2SK146). In addition, the circuit configuration has two differential and full-stage direct connection OCL, and the output stage is SEPP, and the output impedance is low, increasing the stability of the load. It is placed at 2dB. The power supply is ±2 power supply method, adding the voltage of ±32V. The gain is about 34dB. Tone amplifier part is a two-stage and all-stage direct connection circuit using dual FET at the first stage, and the output is SEPP. The same as equalizer is ±2 power supply.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SY-C 15 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sy-c15.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-5":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier with slim proportions and technologies such as DC power amplifiers. The circuit configuration consists of an equalizer amplifier with a differential-amplifier circuit using a low-noise transistor, a Yamaha negative feedback (NF)-CR tone preamplifier with a low-distortion ICs using an input differential-final stage SEPP, a differential-input using a low-noise dual transistor, and a DC-power amplifier with a pure complimentary service SEPPOCL. Each unit is analyzed by an HP-IB system combining a spectrum analyzer and a computer with a measurement limit of 0.00005%. All units are ± 2 power supply system, and consist of input differential-output stage complimentary service SEPP. The equalizer amplifier is the first stage current mirror differential amplifier, the second stage common-emitter amplifier, and the final stage A-class PURE CON SEPP-OCL. A-5 is also compatible with MC cartridge by switching between MM and MC with Phono SW. The power amplifier consists of a current mirror differential amplifier using a low-noise dual transistor at the first stage, a grounded emitter amplifier at the pre-drive stage, and a Darlington connected pure SEPP-OCL at the last stage. The tone control uses Yamaha's original negative feedback (NF)-CR type tone control, which has excellent control characteristics and low distortion rate. The control characteristics are as follows: Bass at 500 Hz turnover and 20 Hz control range ± 10 dB, Treble at 3 kHz turnover and 20 kHz control range ± 10 dB.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Yamaha A-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/YAMAHA/amp/a-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-9":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥245,000. amplifier's new high-end amplifier that follows the CA-2000 series. The basic circuit configuration of A-9 is a pure ca servo amplifier DC equalizer, a pure ca servo amplifier, an A-class/B-class servo DC power amplifier with a new linear circuit circuit. Also, you can insert low-noise MC head amplifier and pure ca servo amplifier type tone preamplifier if necessary. A-9 has a pure ca servo amplifier on the preamplifier circuit. This pure current servo servo amplifier is a method that does not flow at all to power supply or earth line, and it always flows constant current to power supply line. This realizes zero element sensitivity not only the L/C/R component of power supply and wiring, but also nonlinear power supply due to current change. In addition, because the signal current flows to the earth in Pureca servo servo amplifier, the ground impedance is difficult to understand and the low crosstalk is improved. The DC equalizer circuit is installed in the equalizer amplifier part.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-9.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-b-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥250,000. Stereo power amplifier with linear contact fa circuit and all FET circuit configuration. The basic circuit configuration of the B-5 is the Cascode Boot Strap Differential A circuitification Circuit by Low Noise High-gm Dual FET, and the pre-drive stage is a DC amplifier structure with a 3-stage Emitter Forroer with a linear contact fa circuit, and a 3-stage Pure Complementary Triple Push Pull OCL with a linear contact fa circuit. The development of this B-5 is equipped with a HP-IB audio analyzer that combines computer and spectrum analyzer. All data are measured and designed. This HP-IB system can parse harmonic distortion components of 2nd to 10th or more with 0.0000005% order, and it is a measurement system that can be examined by dBdB orders over 10MHz for frequency characteristics. The first stage is low noise and high-gm Dual FET assembled a casscode boots circuit. This DualFET is a low-noise, high-gm, two FETs of electrical and thermal properties, and it is placed in the same package, and it has obtained a positive characteristic as the first element of the DC amplifier. The pre-drive stage is a push-pull differential a ification circuit using the current mirror circuit. The FET of the first stage and the pre-drive stage has a large capacity to charge the capacity by flowing the current of 5mA or more, and the response to the transient signal is also good, and there is no internal clip at transient time.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-2a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥170,000. Preamplifier is used for new development parts, starting with low noise High-gm Dual FET. The basic circuit configuration is a low-noise equalizer amplifier for MC cartridge and a high-precision tone preamplifier with low-noise equalizer amplifier for current noise reduction circuit. The main improvement points of C-2 to C-2a are improved properties and added functions. First of all, all characteristics such as distortion rate, SN ratio, frequency characteristics, transient characteristics are greatly improved. Added PhonoSelector and Rec out Selector, and added tone control. In addition, we have adopted all kinds of parts carefully selected by sound quality. In the first stage of the series, the newly developed low-noise high gm Dual FET (2SK101) was added. This 2SK101 has excellent low-noise properties, especially with low 1/f noise, and has a high gm of 120mmho (Typ.), and Nch silicon junction FET with electrical and temperature pair characteristics of pair FET. The circuit configuration uses a low-noise high gm Dual FET differential circuit to improve DC drift and increase signal source impedance during cartridge implementation to prevent deterioration of distortion rate, improve frequency characteristics, and reduce current noise.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-2a (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-2a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-4":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥98,000. Preamplifier with superior overall mounting characteristics such as current noise reduction circuit. The basic circuit configuration is a simple structure of the equalizer stage of the low-noise dual FET differential input current mirror casscode boots developed by and the flat amplifier of almost the same configuration. Tone control circuit, MC head amplifier, etc. In addition, the original current noise reduction circuit is mounted to determine the SN ratio during the cartridge implementation. In addition, the newly developed current noise reduction circuit (PAT.PEND) is mounted to improve the SN ratio at the time of cartridge implementation. Low-noise dual FET is available for the first step differential a ification. This dual FET is designed specifically for the same package with low-noise specifications and high-gm electrical and thermal characteristics of the two FETs. It has gained many advantages as the first element of the DC amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-4.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-2040":{"more":[{"t":"The most likely King of the Yamaha family is the CR-3020 but the Queen is probably the CR-2040. You might get some arguments from owners of the CR-2020 but the Yamaha CR-2040 could probably be considered a “Monster” receiver given it’s size and power output. It 1979 it retailed for $859.00 which was a hefty sum of money back then. Of course the CR-3020 was priced at $1500.00 so I guess it’s all relative. Probably underrated at 120 watts per channel, with less than 0.02% THD, this power hungry receiver can easily power most any set of speakers you can find. Many would say that the CR-2020 is a better looking receiver but that the CR-2040 has a better sound. Of course this is one of Yamaha’s “Natural Sound” receivers and when one usually listens to one of these receivers for the first time it may sound as though it’s lacking a little in bass. The reality most likely is that other receiver manufacturers “color” their circuitry to emphasize more bass so that’s what many listeners are used to hearing. The Yamaha circuitry does not do this so you are hearing the sound closer to how it is actually supposed to sound.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-2040","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-2040","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-2040.jpg","xc":2,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-2040","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/yamaha-cr-2040-left.jpg"}},"yamaha-cr-440":{"more":[{"t":"The Yamaha CR-440, released in 1979, is a well built stereo receiver with a classic design and reliable performance. It features a clean, sleek layout and minimalist wood cabinet. It was one of the last receivers with Yamaha’s classic look. Although it delivers a modest 30 watts per channel, the CR-440 is known for its good sound quality. Originally priced at $320, the CR-440 was at the low end of Yamaha’s offerings at the time. The faceplate on the CR-440 is brushed aluminum with a dial scale that runs the length of the faceplate. The dial is backlit with a soft white lighting. There are two large paddle knobs for controlling Rec/Out and Input sources. these knobs are one of the styling features that give the classic vintage Yamaha’s their distinctive look. The CR-440 only has 4 push buttons in contrast to the higher end models that tend to look more cluttered due to all the push buttons.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-440","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-440","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-440.jpg","xc":2,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-440","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/yamaha-cr-440-meters.jpg"}},"yamaha-cr-640":{"more":[{"t":"The Yamaha CR-640 Natural Sound Receiver was a mid range offering from Yamaha in 1979. It was on the market until about 1981 and retailed fro $395.00. It has a slightly more modern look than Yamaha’s earlier CR-x20 line. The front panel has three distinct rows with most of the auxiliary controls on the bottom row. The meters, selector switches and volume and tuning knobs are on the middle row. The top is dominated by the full length dial. It also has a matte finish look to the knobs. When settled into the minimalist wood cabinet it has a very clean and bright look. At 40 watts per channel into 8 ohms it has enough power for most speaker setups.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-640","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-640","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cr-840":{"more":[{"t":"This ebony classic is the Yamaha CR-840 receiver. It was produced from 1979 to around 1981 and retailed for about $500. It was a mid range receiver in Yamaha’s CR-XX40 lineup. It puts out 60 watts per channel into 8 ohms. The CR-840 has the big flat toggle switches as do many of the other Yamaha models. Overall it has a very nice sleek hi-tech look to it, though some think the Yamaha models look somewhat sterile. The CR-840 has a built-in AUTO-DX circuit that monitors the signal strength and amount of interference present. If needed it will automatically switch to the DX Mode IF Stage to increase the selectivity to 83dB. It also has continuously variable loudness control which means that the frequency balance and volume are adjusted simultaneously to compensate for the ear’s insensitivity to high and low frequencies at low volume settings.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha CR-840","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-840","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cr-840.jpg","xc":2,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-cr-840","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2016/08/yamaha-cr-840-meters.jpg"}},"accuphase-c-200-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1980. This stereo preamplifier is based on the C-200 and C-200S and has been greatly improved by introducing the latest technology. The cascode bootstrap push-pull differential input method is based on the full-amplification stage push-pull method. The cascode bootstrap improves the high-frequency characteristics while obtaining a large gain. At the same time, it also improves the distortion factor due to the increase in input impedance. This circuit is used for an equalizer amplifier and a high-level tone preamplifier. A DC servo system is used for the equalizer amplifier and high-level tone preamplifier, and the input and output of the MM disk are completely directly connected. The DC servo amplifier uses an IC. The output of the IC does not directly control the signal system of the differential input amplifier, but controls the base current of the constant current source. This servo circuit minimizes the influence of servo system noise on the signal system and has excellent DC drift control capability.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-200 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-200X-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-c-230":{"more":[{"t":"Released May 1979. This is a preamplifier that Accuphase has developed by combining the technologies it has developed over many years. It is equipped with a head amplifier for MC cartridge and a full-fledged headphone amplifier as well as various sound adjustment functions. A fully symmetrical push-pull circuit is used for all stages, from the head amplifier inlet to the final output stage, and even the headphone amplifier. In addition, the capacitor for DC cut is removed from the negative feedback (NF) loop of all unit amplifiers for DC method, and coloring for sound quality is eliminated. In addition, the input capacitor is removed for ICL method. MOS FET is used for output stage of equalizer amplifier and high-level amplifier to improve various characteristics. To prevent the impedance of the power supply from increasing, each unit amplifier is equipped with a dedicated constant-voltage power supply on the printed circuit board of each unit amplifier. The power supply is adjusted to the ideal power supply and the power supply, and excellent stability and characteristics are obtained. In order to operate as a DC amplifier even when tone control is active, the DC servo system is used to suppress DC drift to almost zero.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-230 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-230-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-300-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1980 at ¥300,000. Based on the P-300 and P-300S, this is a stereo power amplifier that has been greatly improved by introducing the latest technology. A MOS FET is used for the drive stage and a wide-band transistor is used for the output. By using a MOS FET in the preceding stage, the bias voltage of the output stage is stabilized, and the emitter resistance of the output stage can be removed, so that the bias of the output transistor at the time of large output is not cut off and the generation of switching distortion is almost eliminated. The MOS FET drive has a high input impedance, which makes it easier to operate in the previous stage, thus enabling higher performance. The pre-drive stage employs a cascode connection of transistors for stable wide-band amplification. The input circuit uses a cascode bootstrap differential push-pull input to obtain a large gain, improve the high-frequency characteristics, and prevent the deterioration of the distortion factor due to the increase of the input impedance. By configuring the FET input, the input coupling capacitor is removed and connected directly. In addition, DC feedback is applied by a DC servo amplifier to shut off DC, and DC drift generated in the circuit is suppressed. In the power supply section, the power transformer is wound only on the right and left sides, and interference between the left and right sides caused by the exclusive rectifier and filter circuit is suppressed.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-300 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-300X-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-33-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥59,800. The position selector is mounted and you can choose any position on the record board with the locale. The cabinet is made of H.D.C. (High Density cabinet). H.D.C. is made by mixing and compressing special materials. It has a specific gravity of 2 and achieves superior hauling characteristics and high strength. In addition, due to high heat treatment for processing molding, there is no change in the use for a long time. cartridge is equipped with DL-8A, a MM type cartridge. Equipped with smart repeat function.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-33 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-33f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-70-l":{"more":[{"t":"An auto lift player equipped with an auto lift mechanism using a contact-free end sensor. Equipped with lifter speed control function, the lowering speed of the arm can be freely adjusted. Uses a double-structured turntable. An out Rocester type AC servo motor is used as the drive motor. The tone arm is equipped with a high-sensitivity S-shaped tone arm with dynamic damping mechanism that is not affected by external vibration. Equipped with a helicoidal arm elevation mechanism, the height of the tone arm can be adjusted according to the cartridge. A 70 mm thick heavyweight cabinet has been adopted.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-70 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-70l-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/denon-dp-70-l.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-70l-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-70l.JPG"}},"denon-pma-510":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier is composed of two amplifiers, a super equalizer amplifier and a power amplifier. The basic configuration consists of two amplifier configuration consisting of only the MC/MM super equalizer amplifier and non-switching A power amplifier installed in the PMA-550/PMA-540. DENON technology has been introduced to enhance the completion. It employs a direct DC servo system that eliminates the coupling and condenser that degrade sound quality. All signal paths are designed without a capacitor, and there is no coupling capacitor from the MC input terminal to the SP output terminal that affects sound quality. The equalizer amplifier section is equipped with a super equalizer consisting of an negative feedback (NF)-type DC amplifier with low-noise dual-FET and a CR-type equalizing filter to realize ultra-wide bandwidth. In addition, the gain and S/N are designed to focus on the MC cartridge in order to realize the advantages of the super equalizer. The power amplifier section uses a non-switching A method equipped with a 0 cross linear bias circuit. The 0 cross linear bias circuit is equipped with a high-speed thermal feedback circuit to further enhance the merits of the non-switching system.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-510 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-510-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-540":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier with super equalizer and real drive circuit. When using MC cartridges as well as MM cartridges, capacitors are removed from all stages of the signal path from the phono input terminal to the speaker output terminal. The fully capacitorless configuration is realized by adopting the direct DC servo circuit that is also included in the PMA 970. It effectively shuts out DC drift and ensures stability in the ultra-low frequency range. The EQ amplifier section is equipped with a super-equalizer that combines the advantages of the negative feedback (NF) (feedback type) and CR (non-feedback type) types, thereby achieving excellent RIAA deviation. The super equalizer consists of an negative feedback (NF)-type DC amplifier with low-noise dual FET and a CR-type equalizing filter. The first stage consists of parallel differential amplification with dual FET of direct DC servo system. This eliminates DC temperature drift while improving S/N and distortion factor. A real drive circuit is mounted to reduce distortion factor.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-540 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-540-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-550":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier is equipped with a super equalizer to take advantage of the cartridge performance. The basic configuration consists of two amplifiers, an MC/MM super equalizer amplifier and a non-switching A power amplifier. In addition to this simple configuration, a complete DC configuration is adopted from the MC input terminal to the SP output terminal without using a coupling capacitor in the signal path. This fully capacitor-less configuration is realized by installing DENON's direct DC servo system in both the equalizer and power amplifiers to shut out DC drift and achieve the sound quality inherent in DC-configured amplifiers. The EQ section is equipped with a super equalizer for use with cartridges capable of wide-band playback. The amplifier consists of an negative feedback (NF)-type DC amplifier with newly developed low-noise dual FET and a CR-type equalizing filter. The first stage is parallel differential amplifier with dual FET of direct DC servo system. As a result, in addition to the ultra-wide range, we have obtained a high gain equivalent to that of a head amplifier for MC. It is also compatible with low-output MC cartridges.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-550 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-550-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-950":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier that pursues high efficiency and high output while taking advantage of the quality of class A operation. Although it is equipped with a class A power amplifier, it is equipped with a real bias circuit to achieve almost the same body size as an equivalent amplifier of class B operation. Using the same principle as the POA 3000 and PMA 970, the real bias circuit uses a method in which the bias current rises before the signal current. This reduces power consumption by approximately 1/10 compared to the conventional method in which a large amount of bias current is supplied when there is no signal. The power amplifier circuit consists of a low-noise FET parallel differential amplifier + direct DC servo in the first stage, and a pre-driver stage of differential amplifier 3-stage current mirror cascode bootstrap output with powerful drive capability in the second stage. It is equipped with a real drive circuit to improve the phase difference between voltage and current when the speaker is actually loaded. In this circuit, attention is paid to the operation of the amplifier when the speaker is mounted. In addition to parallel use of power transistors, a real drive line with electronic elements is installed in the protection circuit to eliminate signal loss at the time of a large signal. When a general speaker system is connected, distortion near the high-output fo is reduced by approximately 1/50.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-950 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-950-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-citation-xxp":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥750,000. The preamplifier was developed by inheriting the tradition of the design concept of Hermann Cardon AMP. CitationXXP offers a wide band and fast speed compared to all circuit signals by increasing open loop characteristics. By applying the negative feedback (NF) of the small amount as the finish above, it realizes stable performance. In addition, it is made not to enter any signal component outside the band that exceeds the capacity of the circuit, and the occurrence of TIM (transient mixed modulation distortion) is simple, and the complexity of the circuit is measured. The phono stage circuit is basically divided into two types: negative feedback (NF) and CR. negative feedback (NF) type has excellent characteristics such as SN ratio, dynamic range, and distortion rate. In addition, the CR type has excellent transient characteristics, but it has a characteristic that it is difficult to understand good characteristics in terms of SN ratio and dynamic range. In this case, negative feedback (NF) is deep at high frequency, and it is only shallow at low frequency, so it becomes very uneven in the number of bands with the negative feedback (NF) volume, and it is a problem if you look at the dynamic characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon Citation XXP (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citationxxp.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-citation-xxp.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citationxxp.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/citationxxp.jpg"}},"hitachi-ha-5700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥69,800. integrated amplifier using power MOS FET. The power amplifier circuit is basically the same as the HMA 9500 and uses a simple 3-stage direct connection DC power circuit. Newly developed low-noise integrated circuits are used for the equalizer amplifier and tone amplifier. The circuit configuration is a differential input 3-stage directly connected push-pull output. The use of high-gain integrated circuits makes it possible to connect MC cartridges. The power supply section uses two power transformers and a smoothing capacitor (1000 μ F + 1000 μ F) to provide a sufficient power supply section for large amplitude. Equipped with a low filter, tone defeat switch, monitor switch, loudness and speaker selector switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HA-5700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/ha-5700-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-8700":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier developed by applying the know-how obtained with HMA 9500 to pre-main. Power MOS FET, a newly developed new power amplifier, is adopted. The power MOS FET achieves a switching speed of 0.05 μ sec and an amplification factor of 1 MHz (-2dB) in frequency characteristics, which is more than one order of magnitude higher than that of conventional bipolar transistors. The power MOS FET achieves a power gain of 85 dB at 100 kHz in bare characteristics, provides stable negative feedback even at 100 kHz, and achieves excellent push-pull operation even with class B circuit configuration because of its high switching speed. In order to realize the performance of this power stage, a 3-stage power circuit with small phase change is adopted. In order to further improve low-frequency characteristics, a power supply section using a DC amplifier configuration, left and right independent power supply with excellent dynamic characteristics, and high-quality large-capacity capacitor is mounted. The gain of the main amplifier is increased from 29 dB to 45 dB, and a main direct switch is used to connect the main amplifier directly to the output of the equalizer amplifier. It is also possible to be used to reduce the gain of the main amplifier to the gain when the main direct is off.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HA-8700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/ha-8700-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-l-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥70,000. This arm has excellent follow-up against record headphones, significantly reducing tracking errors and in-side force, especially tracking errors are about 1/20 compared to traditional swing arms. The drive motor has a thin Unitorque motor developed by the Unitorque motor, which provides smooth, constant speed rotation. Auto-DRPS (Auto-Digital Selector) function enables quick heading of songs you want to hear. Computer-controlled full automatic mechanism is installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-L 70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/hitachi-ht-l-70.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l70.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l70.JPG"}},"jvc-a-x-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥53,000. A bias circuit is integrated. The VICTOR’s unique super-A circuit is used to achieve high power and efficiency comparable to the B class. In addition, A-X3 has earned high reliability by IC of Super A bias circuit. The signal circuit is a simple structure of equalizer amplifier and DC power amplifier. The power supply unit adopts the direct power supply system, and the rectifier circuit is connected to each circuit separately for voltage amplifier and power amplifier. Contains volume control, which enables you to freely change the correction amount depending on the conditions of music and systems. It is equipped with equalizer subsonic filter to cut ultra-low noise during record playback. Two loudspeaker selectors and two tape circuits for dubbing. Equipped with toned foot switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-X 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-a-x-3.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x3.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x3.JPG"}},"jvc-l-e-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥59,800. Fully automatic player with linear tracking system. This is the application of electronic control arm technology developed by QL-Y series players to realize accurate and stable tracking. The arm has a roman straight short arm. In addition, the bearing part is equipped with a virtual one-point support new gimbal support method with high sensitivity and excellent stability. The cartridge is equipped with a dual-magnetic cartridge of the Roman Sintegrate type developed for L-E5. Microncomputer control electronic servo full auto mechanism is available for printing mechanism. This mechanism is a method that uses the drive system of linear tracking arm as it is.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC L-E 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-l-e-5.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e5.JPG"}},"jvc-ql-y-3-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥65,000. Record player with electronic control arm and full auto mechanism. Tonearm uses electro servo tonearm. The electro servo tonearm on the QL-Y3F has the power for full-auto operation and the coreless linear motor is directly driven by the microcomputer command. This is why there is no mechanic noise. In addition, it does not damage the sensitivity of the bearing or cause resonance. Height adjustment is also possible. This arm adopts manual operation priority design, which can be performed freely without switch. The QL-Y3F tonearm is equipped with a horizontal drive control similar to QL-Y7 and QL-Y5 ED servo tonearm. It suppresses the low-range resonance (fo) peak and in-side force generated horizontally by electron servo circuit and linear motor without mechanical friction to the bearing.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC QL-Y 3 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y3f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-ql-y-3-f.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y3f.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y3f.JPG"}},"kenwood-ka-800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥64,800. Σ drive mounted integrated amplifier. In the Σ drive system, the idea of the traditional NPB that was completed in the axial housing is expanded to the input terminal of the loudspeaker side, and the loudspeaker cable is also considered as one of the internal wiring of the amplifier, and the performance is guaranteed with the input terminal of the loudspeaker. First, we have a unique Σ cable that connects loudspeaker's + side and power amplifier Σ return point, and controls various types of distortions, including the reverse distortion caused by the magnetic circuit of loudspeaker, not to occur with the input terminal of loudspeaker. In addition, by separating the power supply loop, the cable on the side is completely eliminated from the input terminal of the loudspeaker and the potential difference between the earth points. MM/MC amplifier method is available for equalizer amplifier. The circuit uses low noise IC. The power amplifier part adopts a new high-speed method that makes the NFB uniformly across the hearing band. In addition, all signal systems, including the negative feedback (NF) loop, from the Tuner (AUX) terminal to the SP terminal, have a straight DC amplifier that does not have a capac amplifier for low-range cutting. tone control The main tone method using power amplifier is available.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥79,800. Σ drive mounted integrated amplifier. In the Σ drive system, the idea of the traditional NPB that was completed in the axial housing is expanded to the input terminal of the loudspeaker side, and the loudspeaker cable is also considered as one of the internal wiring of the amplifier, and the performance is guaranteed with the input terminal of the loudspeaker. First, we have a unique Σ cable that connects loudspeaker's + side and power amplifier Σ return point, and controls various types of distortions, including the reverse distortion caused by the magnetic circuit of loudspeaker, not to occur with the input terminal of loudspeaker. In addition, by separating the power supply loop, the cable on the side is completely eliminated from the input terminal of the loudspeaker and the potential difference between the earth points. In the amplifier part, we develop and install the new high speed that extends the open loop gain to the outside of the audible band. In the past, NFB was stable, because the phase correction circuit was different, and the cutoff frequency of the open loop was present in the audible band, the absolute amount of NFB was lacking in high frequency. As a result, the frequency characteristics of the open loop that was around 1kHz (equivalent to NFB removed) have been successfully extended to 10kHz. The damping factor around the fo (minimum resonance frequency) of the woofer is emphasized.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-80":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥65,000. Stereo receiver with synthesizer FM/AM tuner. The tuner part adopts the voltage synthesizer method, and it holds the same point firmly with the automatic tuning correction function. The front end is equipped with a 3-stage burri-cap tuning circuit, and the MPX part is equipped with a PLL circuit. Local/DX switch is installed so that even the strong electric field can receive clear. The AM antenna adopts a newly developed loop antenna. You can call the desired broadcast station by presetting 10 stations of FM5 and AM5 stations. It is equipped with a memory backup mechanism by lithium battery, and it will not forget about the preset frequency for about 10 years if it is memory once. The last channel memory mechanism is installed to remember the broadcast station that was listening before returning the power supply switch. The amplifier part adopts a simple circuit called equalizer + high gain power amplifier, which improves overall characteristics as a DC configuration.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"},{"t":"This classic is the Kenwood KR-8010. It was introduced in 1978 and was on the market until about 1981. With 125 watts per channel and 0.03% total harmonic distortion it was near top of the line in Kenwood’s lineup – one step down from the KR-9600. It wasn’t cheap at a retail price of $675 but overall, it is a great looking receiver and excellent performer. The KR-8010 is a beautiful receiver with a brushed aluminum front panel, diamond-machined knobs, analog meters, and an elegant slide-rule dial. The beveled glass is a nice touch as well. Buyer’s had the option of purchasing the CB-14K walnut veneer cabinet, B-14 walnut veneer side panels, or the D-10 carrying handles. The KR-8010 provides sophisticated controls and features. For example, you can copy tapes while listening to another audio source.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KR-80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/kr-80.html","lang":"ja"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-80","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-8010","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-01-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥270,000. L-01A is composed of non-magnetic objects in order to suppress magnetic distortion that has a significant impact on hearing. Dynamic power supply to realize loudspeaker control in higher dimension. With this power linearity, you can pull out the power even if you connect the loudspeaker with the intense impedance change.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-01 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-01a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-08-c":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥180,000. Stereo preamplifier with power amplifier. L-08C can connect Σ between preamplifier and power amplifier. In addition, the primary and secondary parts of the preamplifier are connected via AC code. The current flowing through this loop causes the potential difference in the earth-to-earth connection cable to enter the power amplifier, and the distortion of the level that cannot be ignored by the hearing is entered into the loudspeaker. For this reason, it is possible to connect the power between the earth earth when the power is connected with the pre and the power is connected to the separate amplifier purpose, and it is equipped with faithful signal transmission. The power supply unit has a newly developed multi-power supply + power supply current absorption circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-08 C (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-08c.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-08-m":{"more":[{"t":"A mono power amplifier that uses Σ drive method for each between amplifier and loudspeaker. L-08M is a model that incorporates a three-dimensional design and provides a functional beauty that heatsinks the entire body. The Σ drive system enables Σ wires with loudspeaker. The Σ drive method is designed to prevent distortion caused by the reverse voltage generated by the corn paper (voice coil) of loudspeaker, and the NFB concept that was completed in AMP is expanded to the input terminal of loudspeaker, and the input terminal of loudspeaker is suppressed by importing it as one of the internal wiring of amplifier. This method realizes high performance of the ketter difference of dumping factor 15,000 at the tip of 3mΣ cable. First of all, we have a unique Σ cable that connects loudspeaker's + side and power amplifier's return point, and controls various distortions such as reverse distortion caused by the magnetic circuit of loudspeaker to not occur with the input terminal of loudspeaker. The Σ cable is also installed on the side, and the side cable is separated from the ground point and power supply loop. This eliminates the potential difference between the input terminal and the earthpoint of the loudspeaker. In L-08M, Σ connections between preamplifier and power amplifier are possible.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-08 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-08m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-c-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1980 at ¥220,000. Stereo control center using duo-beta plusX circuit. A duo-beta circuit is used to control sound quality while eliminating excess NFB in favor of physical characteristics. This circuit produces an amplifier circuit that is practical even with bare characteristics, and adds an appropriate amount of NFB and b and DC servo as a finishing touch of sound quality. By doing so, we can suppress the generation of transient distortion such as TIM caused by excessive NFB and suppress the suppression of musical performance by NFB, thereby improving musical performance. Duo Beta plusX is also used for the feedback circuit of the power supply unit, introducing the concept of appropriate control. In general stabilized power supplies, the impedance characteristics of the power supply itself, which is not stabilized, rise in the low-frequency range, and sound quality is improved. However, there are problems such as less damping in the low-frequency range and no stability in the DC range. In plusX, we have created a low-impedance power supply that does not need to rely on excessive feedback, and we have set control that takes advantage of this bare characteristic in the middle and high range, and control that corresponds to the amplifier circuit in the low range. In the equalizer circuit, cascode bootstrap input by high-Gm low-noise dual FET is adopted at the first stage with current mirror load to obtain low distortion factor and high SN ratio.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman C-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/c-300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-cl-34":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1980 at ¥168,000. This tube type preamplifier was developed by applying the technology cultivated in transistor circuits such as duo-beta circuit and DC amplifier. A 3-stage direct-coupled amplifier circuit is used for the equalizer circuit to obtain sufficient gain, and the output stage (third stage) is S. R. P. P. (shunt-regulated push-pull). The S. R. P.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman CL-34 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/cl34-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1980 at ¥290,000. A stereo power amplifier using duo-beta plusX circuit. In order to control the NFB of the amplifier circuit appropriately, we developed a duo-beta circuit and adopted it in the M-300. This is a practical amplifier with bare characteristics, and an appropriate amount of NFB and DC servo are added as a finishing touch of sound quality. Thus, suppression of reproduced sound due to excessive NFB and transient distortion such as TIM are suppressed. In addition, the M-300 also introduces the concept of appropriate control into the power supply circuit as a power supply duo-beta plusX. On the assumption that there is a large power supply in the plusX, it has a loose controlling force to achieve both sound quality and stable operation. M-300 can be used by switching between A class and AB class. Since class A operation amplifies the signal waveform as it is, it is free from switching distortion and crossover distortion switching distortion and crossover distortion and has no cause of distortion other than the linearity of the device itself. Ideal class A operation is realized by adopting LAPT with excellent high-frequency characteristics for the device, duo-beta for the amplifier circuit, and plusX for the power supply circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman M-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/m-300-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-555":{"more":[{"t":"Released April 1980 at ¥450,000. Press the record board to turntable. In addition, there are two grooves and inlets on the turntable surface as air suction route, and the inside of the table turn has an air passage and is connected with the pump on the tube. Stabilizer absorbs the record board and keeps airtight for a long time. This is because the surface effect of the sealing pad on the turntable surface and the air-tight retention of the air passage is completed with seal rings and liquid packing (silicon).","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-555 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd555.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-4":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier that can switch between class A and class AB using the form of external heat sink used in #14, #15 and MA-5. A dual FET with good pair characteristics is used for the input stage of the power amplifier section, and deterioration of characteristics due to impedance change is prevented by the source follower configuration. By switching the bias current of the output stage, both A class and AB class can be enjoyed. The power element uses a super high-ft transistor with a cutoff frequency of 90 MHz to minimize switching distortion. By adopting an external heat sink, the operating temperature of the transistor is designed to be always maintained at around 60 ℃, less than half of the normal operating temperature of around 150 ℃. Low-TIM design is consistent from the power amplifier section to the control section. The bare characteristics are improved by the original 2-pole phase correction circuit, the open-loop gain is kept low at 64 dB and the negative feedback (NF) amount is kept at 26 dB, and the transient intermodulation distortion in the high-frequency region is reduced. The phono amplifier is a low-noise, high-gain type with a unique Low-TIM design that allows direct connection of an MC cartridge. The RIAA curve is set to a device with a particularly low impedance particularly low impedance to improve the SN ratio of the auditory sense.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-4-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-8":{"more":[{"t":"A DC integrated amplifier that pursues a low-TIM design not only for the power amplifier but also for the preamplifier. A 3-stage direct SEPP output type is used for the equalizer stage. In addition, it has excellent low-noise characteristics, and Marantz special order FET with almost perfect matching of pair characteristics in thermal and electrical characteristics is used to obtain excellent SN ratio. Also, the equalizer element is carefully selected to have good characteristics, and the RIAA characteristic is ± 0.2 dB. The BAX tone amplifier is equipped with not only Bass/Treble but also Mid control for more precise sound field correction. In addition, the variable range can be changed with the Turn-Over switch. Tone correction is also available for the source during recording in conjunction with the TapeEQ switch. Newly developed Super Hi-f in the main amplifier section T Transistor is used. This transistor is an element developed by combining LSI process technology and high-frequency power transistor technology.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-8-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥220,000. A stereo power amplifier that can also be used as a high-output monaural power amplifier. Just as Marantz developed the Stereo Power Amplifier #15 by combining two monaural power amplifiers, the heat sink and hood are completely independent on the left and right. The circuit configuration is based on Marantz's original Low-TIM design to reduce dynamic distortion. In order to obtain sound quality equivalent to that of pure A class in AB class, the parallel push-pull amplifier stage with 3-stage Darlington connection employs a super high-ft transistor that has amplification characteristics with a margin up to ultra-high frequencies to reduce switching distortion. Operation can be switched between pure class A and class AB. It can also be used as class AB monaural power amplifier by BTL connection. In addition to a large transformer, the power supply section uses a highly reliable computer grade audio capacitor for one channel 22,000 μ Fx2. Built-in protection circuit using high-speed relay with temperature sensor for higher reliability. Uses gold-plated input terminal.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-10-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-sm-10.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-10-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-10.JPG"}},"marantz-sr-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced in 1980 the Marantz SR-1000 was a budget minded receiver that produced 20 watts per channel. It retailed for $275. Superscope sold the Marantz brand to Philips Electronics in 1980, so the SR line may be the first one produced under Philips although most of the design must have occurred under Superscope. Build quality was definitely on the downswing at that time and the SR line reflects that. Still, they’re not bad considering the quality of audio products (from almost all manufacturers) that came in the years to follow. And, they were made in Japan. The SR-1000 receiver, and SR line in general, essentially signified the end of the dominant Marantz era and ushered in the eventual decline of Marantz as a high end brand. Despite questions about its build quality the SR-1000 looks great. It still has the classic Marantz look with the silver face and Marantz gyro touch tuning wheel.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Marantz SR-1000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/marantz-sr-1000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sr-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥64,800. Stereo receiver that refined and released popular models for Japan such as design, feature and performance. 35W+35W In order to eliminate the characteristic change caused by wiring, power supply and power amplifier parts are put together in a single board. In addition, the input terminal is connected directly to the board, and the selector switch is also directly attached to the board to prevent the occurrence of cross-talk caused by using the lead wire. The tone control part adopts tri tone control, which control tone control in addition to bass and high frequency. Tone amplifier is negative feedback (NF) type and trans 4 pieces per channel. In addition, the front end adopts a three-layer varicon to achieve high sensitivity. The gyro-touch tuning mechanism of the Marantz tradition was built. This method drives large flywheels directly and enables smooth selection.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Marantz SR-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MARANTZ/amp/sr2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sr-4000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥84,800. Stereo receiver that refined and released popular models for Japan such as design, feature and performance. The power amplifier adopts the voltage IC on the front of the amplifier input, and the power IC is equipped with the Darlington power IC on the output stage. The power supply and power amplifier are one board to eliminate the characteristic change caused by wiring. In addition, the input terminal is connected directly to the board, and the selector switch is also directly attached to the board to prevent the occurrence of crosstalk which is used for lead wire. LED peak power meter By using high-sensitivity ICs, you can quickly follow the pulsive sound and read the peak value accurately. tone control circuit defines tone control which can control both low and high. The circuit is negative feedback (NF) type, and it uses two trans s on the amplifier part and two tone control parts. The tuner part adopts the Quadrature IC on the wave stage, making it ideal for superior separation and low distortion. The front end is equipped with a dual gate MOS-FET and a triple varicon.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Marantz SR-4000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MARANTZ/amp/sr4000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-bl-51":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥78,000. A record player using a belt drive system with a circumference drive. The turntable shaft adopts a stainless steel shaft with a diameter of 16mm, which clarifies the branch point and ensures stable rotation performance. The stainless steel shaft is further polished with a pair of metal bearings after heat curing and polishing. This makes the precision of mirror finish less than 0.4 microns. In addition, we use special alloys for bearing metals, which ensures smoothness by oil bath method (lubrication with shaft and bearing metal). The drive mechanism is equipped with a belt-ap external drive system. The drive side adopts outer rotor type brushless servo motor, and the ur material which contains carbon material with low aging change is precisely processed by 8mm width and 0.45mm thickness. Tonearm has a new static balance tonearm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki BL-51 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/bl-51.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-bl-91":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥110,000. A record player using a belt drive system with a circumference drive. BL-91 is a model that comes with dust cover, and BL-91L is dedicated to long arm with no dust cover. In order to introduce our unique know-how to improve sound quality around the turntable shaft and bearing, we use the belt drive method by the external drive method. The drive motor uses an outer roller brushless servo motor, and the belt uses a ur material that contains a carbon material that has less aging than 8mm width and 0.45mm thickness. The turntable shaft has a 16mm long shaft (stainless steel). In addition, bearings combine special alloy bearings and unique thrust metals, which are stored in large shaft housings. In addition, high accuracy machining of the shaft is performed within 0.4 micrometers. The bearing metal on the side of the shaft adopts special alloy, granulates the lead and deposits it into the crystal grain of the metal base. Because of this, the thin film by lead and oil is formed on the friction surface with the shaft which is regarded as rotation, and smooth rotation without oil film cutting is obtained.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki BL-91 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/bl-91.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-dp-84da":{"more":[{"t":"An auto-player system that omits some functions of the DP-86DA. The tone arm is equipped with a counter-weight resonance prevention mechanism to prevent sharp resonance that occurs in the pipe and head shell. In addition, the counter-weight has a double structure and a rubber damper is installed between the counter-weights to improve sound resolution in the low frequency range. A 12-pole 24-slot brushless servo motor is used as the drive motor. Equipped with auto mechanism, Oatley turn and auto cut are possible. All control levers are centrally located in the front of the cabinet and can be operated with the dust cover closed. The cabinet is molded with iron powder and a large insulator is used to suppress howling. Equipped with anti-skating mechanism and oil dump-type arm lifter.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DP-84DA (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-84da-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/mitsubishi-dp-84da.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-84da-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-84da.JPG"}},"mitsubishi-lt-1":{"more":[{"t":"A linear tracking system full auto player developed by gathering DIATONE technology. It employs a linear tracking system in which the arm moves linearly on the record board in the same way as the cutting machine. In this system, the tangential direction of the groove is accurately traced, so tracking error and harmonic distortion can be reduced. In addition, since there is no inside force, the needle tip can contact the object, so that overall tracking capability can be improved. A stainless steel wire is used for the drive of the moving base that fixes the tone arm. This wire combines 49 fine wires of 0.05 mm diameter with nylon coating to obtain excellent durability and flexibility. Tracking error is detected by the potential difference between the two photodiode outputs at the rear of the arm, and the error angle is suppressed to 0.03 ° to 0.05 °. As for the vibration caused by the movement of the arm base, the vibration generated in the moving base of the arm should be minimized. Second, the vibration generated in the moving base should not be transmitted to the needle tip.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi LT-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/lt-1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-lt-3":{"more":[{"t":"A linear tracking system full auto player developed by inheriting the LT-1 technology. It employs a linear tracking system in which the arm moves linearly on the record board in the same way as the cutting machine. In this system, the tangential direction of the groove is accurately traced, so tracking error and harmonic distortion can be reduced. In addition, since there is no inside force, the needle tip can contact the object, so that overall tracking capability can be improved. A stainless steel wire is used for the drive of the moving base that fixes the tone arm. This wire combines 49 fine wires of 0.05 mm diameter with nylon coating to obtain excellent durability and flexibility. Tracking error is detected by the potential difference between the two photodiode outputs at the rear of the arm, and the error angle is suppressed to 0.03 ° to 0.05 °. As for the vibration caused by the movement of the arm base, the vibration generated in the moving base of the arm should be minimized. Second, the vibration generated in the moving base should not be transmitted to the needle tip.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi LT-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/lt-3-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-lt-5-v":{"more":[{"t":"A vertical-type record player that uses a linear tracking system. There were 2 types, LT-5V without cartridge and LT-5VC with Diatone original cartridge MM-2 made by Orthophone. The LT-5V has a vertical structure that is rare for a record player. In a typical horizontal player, since the direction of vibration of the cartridge and the direction of floor vibration are the same, when mechanical vibration caused by tracing of the sound groove is converted into electrical signal by the cartridge, floor vibration is combined with the reproduced signal, which causes howling phenomenon. On the other hand, the vertical player has a structure that is resistant to howling because the direction of floor vibration does not interfere with the direction of vibration for the cartridge to generate power. Since the direction of the weight of the cartridge is different from the direction of the needle pressure, once the appropriate needle pressure is set, there is almost no trouble of readjusting the needle pressure even if the cartridge is replaced. The tone arm uses a linear tracking system. In this system, the tone arm is moved horizontally along with the fulcrum, so it operates in exactly the same way as a cutting machine that cuts a sound groove in the original record. The LT-5V consists of two parts: an optical sensor part that detects the verticality of the tone arm and a drive part that operates the tone arm based on commands from the tracking servo circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi LT-5 V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/lt-5v-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/mitsubishi-lt-5-v.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/lt-5v-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/lt-5v.JPG"}},"nad-7020":{"more":[{"t":"NAD, or New Acoustic Dimension, was formed in 1972 by Martin Borish and others. Bjorn Erik Edvardsen did most of the engineering. NAD’s initial concept was to build audio components that rivaled the performance of separates but that were affordable to younger buyers or audiophiles without large budgets. This NAD 7020 receiver fits that description perfectly. It’s basically similar to NAD’s famous 3020 amplifier but with an integrated tuner. The NAD 3020 is one of the best selling amplifiers of all time and it’s performance-to-cost ratio caused other audio manufacturers to scramble in order to compete with NAD. The 7020 came out in 1979, a little after the 3020, and packed a big performance punch that didn’t hurt the wallet. You might think the NAD 7020 receiver (not to be confused with the later 7020e) is under powered at 20 watts per channel but the way the amp circuit is engineered gives it a huge amount of headroom. 3 dB in fact.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – NAD 7020","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/nad-7020","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-30-l-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥69,800.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-30 L II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-30lii-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-30-l-ii.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-30lii-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-30lii.JPG"}},"pioneer-sa-710":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo integrated amplifier using pure complimentary service OCL ocL system directly connected to all stages. The equalizer uses a carefully selected PNP type low-noise transistor for the first stage and a 3-stage direct amplifier with an emitter follower circuit for the second stage. The high gain of the first stage satisfies the requirements for a low-noise, high-gain head amplifier. In order to completely suppress the deviation of the RIAA playback curve, the NFB element of the equalizer and the element of the part receiving NFB use nichrome evaporated metal film resistance with 1% error and styrene capacitor with 2% error. In the preamplifier section, an FET with high input impedance is used for the first stage, so no noise change occurs regardless of the adjustment position of the volume control. Bass and Treble are equipped with independent turn-over switches, each of which can independently select the turn-over frequency, so you can control the tone according to the characteristics and effect of the source. Equipped with a tone defeat switch that can select tone flat with one touch regardless of the turnover position or tone characteristics. The power circuit uses a direct-coupled pure complimentary service OCL system for all one stage differentials.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-710 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-710-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-3500":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-3500 receiver was produced between 1980 and 1982, during Pioneer’s transition away from the heavily built receivers of the late 1970s. It retailed for approximately $225, positioning it as an entry level option in Pioneer’s lineup of the era. The unit delivers 20 watts per channel with remarkably low total harmonic distortion of no more than 0.05%. The SX-3400 produced 15 wpc while the SX-3900 produced 120 wpc. Obviously the SX-3400 was at the lower end of the performance spectrum. The models in the SX-3X00 series were: Aesthetically, the SX-3500 features a silver front panel with wooden cabinet side panels and metal top covered in a simulated walnut vinyl. It has Pioneer’s famous Fluroscan display – the distinctive blue fluorescent lights used for the tuning and level indicators, which gave the front panel a sleek, modern glow that set the SX-3X00 series apart from other receivers. The SX-3500 has a practical feature set for everyday listening. While it lacks the muscle of Pioneer’s SX-series giants from the previous decade, the SX-3500 has earned a reputation among vintage audio enthusiasts for its surprisingly clean and refined sound, with performance that punches well above its modest wattage rating.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-3500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-3500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-3600":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced in 1980, the Pioneer SX-3600 is a stylish receiver incorporating aspects of both digital and analog engineering. It was in the middle of the Pioneer performance ladder, and retailed for an affordable $275, but still produced a respectable 30 watts per channel. Most of the SX-3600’s were made in Korea. The Pioneer SX-3600 receiver has a clean, uncluttered front panel design that aligns with Pioneer’s focus at the time on minimalism and simplicity. They referred to it as Smart Styling. The SX-3600 also came with a “walnut-like” metal top and walnut grained vinyl side panels. The main analog tuning dial for FM and AM stations is wide, tilted back, and easy to read. The tuning knob is large and smooth. The control buttons and knobs have a sturdy, high-quality feel.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-3600","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-3600","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-3700":{"more":[{"t":"From that slightly awkward time that lies between the fully analog and fully digital eras come the Pioneer SX-3700. It was 1980 and digital displays were just catching on and Pioneer sought to capitalize on the movement with its Fluroscan technology. The SX-3700 produces 45 watts per channel and incorporates a direct coupled amplifier design. There is a variant of the SX-3700 labelled the SX-820. Apparently it is a European version but has a black dial face and white Fluroscan. A couple other SX-3000 series receivers also had European variants in the SX-620, SX-720. The Fluroscan display shows the tuning for the AM or FM bands depending upon AM or FM selector button is pushed. The analog dial shows both FM and AM tuning as well. The power output meter is also a Fluroscan display.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-3700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-3700","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-3900":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Pioneer SX-3900 which was Pioneer’s top of the line Fluoroscan receiver. It’s the big brother to the SX-3800 and was introduced in 1980 at a retail price of about $800.00. It represents Pioneer’s transition from analog receivers to the more contemporary digital receivers. In fact, the SX3900 basically has both analog and digital features. As you can see it has an old school analog tuning dial, the mechanism is mechanical, as well as a five digit digital tuning display. The displays use fluorescent bulbs hence the nick name fluoroscan. The blue fluorescent display is beautiful and one of the more iconic displays in vintage audio. Still, the FM Quartz Locked SX-3900 was not all looks. It pumps out 120 watts per channel with less than 0.005% total harmonic distortion and is built with quality engineering.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-3900","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-3900","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"revox-b-780":{"more":[{"t":"Revox, the consumer division of Studer, is probably more known for their fantastic reel-to-reel machines, such as the B77 and PR99, than anything else. However, this German made Revox B780 is one fine receiver and was introduced to the market in 1980. It is not an AM/FM receiver. It is FM only and produces 70 watts per channel into 8 ohms with no more than 0.05% total harmonic distortion. It definitely has a distinctive appearance and looks a little more like a piece of electronic test equipment you’d see in a lab rather than a receiver. There is something about the look that is appealing though. I guess the stereo has a feel of precision to it. Pretty straightforward credo. To achieve this Revox took their B760 digital frequency synthesizer tuner and their B750 mkII integrated amplifier, re-engineered them into what they called a ‘symbiotic relationship’, and created the B780.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Revox B 780","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/revox-b780","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"rotel-ra-315":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥26,900. All-trans integrated amplifier with ITL and OTR. ITTL, OTTL power circuit using silicon trans. Two sets of loudspeaker can be connected. Tape monitor switch, loudness control, tone control Two types of phono are available. Headphone terminal is installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Rotel RA-315 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ROTEL/amp/ra-315.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sae-a-1001":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥590,000. The power of the 01 series has been developed to respect the musicality. The loudspeaker is constantly changing the load on the amplifier, and even if it is a loudspeaker with a rating of 8 Ω, it may be less than 1 Ω in extremes. In order to respond to these low impedance loads, the 01 series has a power stage that considers large outputs. In addition, it is also avoided from the effects of crossover distortion by developing into a precision compounding circuit with improved component characteristics and construction accuracy. This improves linearity and naturaity at low levels. In the 01 series, we are trying to improve the natural damping factor by the internal resistance of the amplifier, not the artificial damping factor in the conventional NPB.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE A 1001 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/a1001.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sae-a-201":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥250,000. 01Series concept developed stereo amplifier. The loudspeaker is constantly changing the load on the amplifier, and even if it is a loudspeaker with a rating of 8 Ω, it may be less than 1 Ω in extremes. In order to respond to these low impedance loads, the 01 series has a power stage that considers large outputs. In addition, it is also avoided from the effects of crossover distortion by developing into a precision compounding circuit with improved component characteristics and construction accuracy. This improves linearity and naturaity at low levels. In the 01 series, we are trying to improve the natural damping factor by the internal resistance of the amplifier, not the artificial damping factor in the conventional NPB. LED digital meter is mounted to display peak level.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE A 201 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/a201.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sae-a-501":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥390,000. The same technology as A1001, the same idea was developed from the same idea. The loudspeaker is constantly changing the load on the amplifier, and even if it is a loudspeaker with a rating of 8 Ω, it may be less than 1 Ω in extremes. In order to respond to these low impedance loads, the 01 series has a power stage that considers large outputs. In addition, it is also avoided from the effects of crossover distortion by developing into a precision compounding circuit with improved component characteristics and construction accuracy. This improves linearity and naturaity at low levels. In the 01 series, we are trying to improve the natural damping factor by the internal resistance of the amplifier, not the artificial damping factor in the conventional NPB. LED digital meter is mounted to display peak level.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE A 501 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/a501.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sae-p-101":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥250,000. Preamplifier with built-in microcomputer to achieve significant reduction in signal path and multifunction. We adopt computer direct line design using the latest device. By electrically completely separating the signal system and the operation system, we realize the simplification of the signal path and make it compatible. In P101, all conventional mechanical switches are released, and the front panel is equipped with an electronic switch. In addition, the control route and signal path are separated by a completely independent relay circuit of the left and right channels, and it connects with the attached circuit only when necessary. With this method, the audio signal is ideally passed in the amplifier without being complicated from the input/output terminal on the back of the panel. In addition, P101 reduces signal routes by 50% or more compared to conventional SAE preamplifier. The volume control circuit is electronic and can control the volume of 94.5 dB at 1.5 dB. Also, conventional volume control does not generate gari noise.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE P 101 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/p101.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-5900-z":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Sansui 5900Z from Sansui’s Z series of synthesized digital receivers. Introduced in 1980 these receivers featured digital as well as analog tuning displays. While the tuner was digitally synthesized the amp section was still the classic Sansui DC coupled analog circuitry. The Z line of Sansui receivers didn’t have the same high end build quality of the G series but were still very good performing receivers. This Sansui 5900Z puts out 75 watts per channel and is the mid range offering in the Z series. Note also that there are no volume, tuning or selector knobs on these units as they have been replaced with push button controls. The 5900Z also makes use of LED’s which were just coming into fashion at the time. The power meters use red LED’s as does the analog portion of the tuning dial. It’s a strange mix of old and new and represents the period of evolution from analog to digital.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 5900 Z","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-5900z","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-607-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥76,000. This integrated amplifier is equipped with a newly developed super feed-forward system that transcends the limits of NFB. In order to supplement the NFB technology used in conventional amplifiers and to further reduce distortion, this circuit is equipped with a newly developed Super Feedforward System. This circuit is based on the feedforward theory devised by H. S. Black in 1928. In 1975, SANSUI explored the possibility of practical use, but it crashed into a wall and was interrupted. In 1978, the research was restarted but failed. In 1980, we obtained a hint that NFB technology could be used in combination, and finally completed this circuit. This feed-forward circuit takes out only the distortion component from the original signal, combines it with the output in opposite phase, and cancels the distortion.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-D 607 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d607f-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-d-607-f.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d607f-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d607f.JPG"}},"sansui-au-d-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥59,800. A newly developed linear A circuit with diamond differential circuit. Diamond differential circuit adopted by the AU-D series. This circuit is the ideal circuit for instantaneously supplying a large amount of drive current corresponding to any input. The TIM (transient mixed modulation distortion), which is the most harmful dynamic distortion for music playback, is limited to zero. In this way, AU-D7 realizes high-speed responsiveness equivalent to about twice the conventional class amplifier, such as through rate ±120V/μsec (inside-thru rate ±220V/μsec). At the same time, we gain high efficiency comparable to B class. The MC output also has a simple and straight structure that is directly input to equalizer.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-d-7.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d7.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d7(1).jpg"}},"sansui-au-d-707-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥108,000. This integrated amplifier is equipped with a newly developed super feed-forward system that transcends the limits of NFB. In order to supplement the NFB technology used in conventional amplifiers and to further reduce distortion, a newly developed super feed-forward system is incorporated. This circuit is based on the feed-forward theory devised by H. S. Black in 1928. At Sansui, we explored the possibility of practical use in 1975, but it crashed into a wall and was interrupted. In 1978, we restarted our research but failed. In 1980, we obtained a hint that NFB technology could be used in combination, and finally completed this circuit. This feed-forward circuit takes out only the distortion component from the original signal, combines it with the output in opposite phase, and cancels the distortion.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-D 707 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707f-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-d-707-f.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707f-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707f.JPG"}},"sansui-au-d-907-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥168,000. AU-F series integrated amplifier with super feed forward system. Super Feed Forward System is available for output. The NFB circuit used in general amplifiers is not only distortion but also frequency characteristics, S/N ratio and input/output impedance are improved. However, it is not completely distorted and has problems such as decreased effect in high frequency. Feed forward theory was developed to address this issue. Sansui is a super feed forward system combined with NFB. In the superfeed forward system, NFC is mainly working for distortion improvement in the audible band, and it plays a role to extract the reverse phase distortion for the feed forward. By using computer technology, we are able to remove distortion over a broadband by developing a Symmetrical 2-pole output saming network that can be distorted even for two-pole phase compensation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 907 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d907f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-4700":{"more":[{"t":"This Sansui G-4700 is from their line of Pure Power DC receivers from the late 1970’s. It was at the bottom of their G-X700 line but still produced a respectable 50 watts per channel. Sansui had other budget oriented receivers at the time such as the G-301 and G-401 so the G-4700 was really in the middle of their performance lineup. It retailed for about $430. The G-X700 line all featured a symmetrical layout with two big knobs a the center bottom of the face plate that control volume and tuning. It also has push buttons for FM Mode, Subsonic Filter, Loudness and Tape Monitor The Sansui G-4700 looks alright when it’s powered off but hit the power switch and dim the lights and you’re in for a treat. It is one of the better looking receivers from the late 1970’s when lit up. Interestingly it has both digital and analog tuning displays. FM tuning is digitally quartz locked to prevent drift.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-4700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-4700","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-5700":{"more":[{"t":"The Sansui G-5700 is one of those ‘in between’ receivers that was made during the transition from analog to digital readouts. It has both a traditional analog dial as well as a digital tuner display. Built from 1979 until 1980 it produces 75 watts per channel into 8 ohms and total harmonic distortion of 0.03%. The G-5700 has the characteristic Sansui large Volume and Tuning knobs set symmetrically in the center of the face plate. It also utilizes the square buttons used on earlier Sansui models. The dual analog/Digital displays make it a little strange looking but the backlit logo and model number at the left of the receiver is a nice touch. The G-5700 has plenty of power for most speakers and a great tuner section as well. Overall, the sound from Sansui’s Pure Power DC stereos is very good. The volume control is aggressive.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-5700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-5700","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-g-5700.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-5700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/sansui-g-5700-front.jpg"}},"sansui-g-6700":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Sansui G-6700. It was produced from 1980-1982 and had a list price of $730.00. It was rated at 90 watts per channel into 8 ohms and had a total harmonic distortion of 0.025%. The Sansui G-6700 weighs approximately 35 pounds. It has tone controls for Bass and Treble and Filters for both Subsonic and High. It also has a loudness control. It has outputs for two sets of speakers as well as headphones. For inputs it has Phono, Tape 1+2 and Aux. Nearly all the Sansui G series receivers are very collectible.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-6700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-6700","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-g-6700.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-6700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/06/sansui-g-6700.jpg"}},"sansui-g-7700":{"more":[{"t":"From 1979 to around 1980 Sansui offered their G-X700 line which ranged from the low end G-4700 up to the top end G-9700. In the middle of the range was the Sansui G-7700 Pure Power DC Stereo Receiver which is featured here. It puts out 120 watts per channel compared to the G-4700 with 50 WPC and the G-9700 at 200 WPC. There were actually 3 G series receiver model lines from 1978-1980 with the G-X700 series being the last. The G-7700 is a DC, or Direct Coupled, receiver which means that is has no capacitors in the signal path of the circuit. This keeps any unwanted distortion to a minimum as capacitors can ‘color’ or influence the sound signal. So, Sansui designed the signal path portion of the circuit with no capacitors. As with all the G-X700 series the G-7700 featured LED power meters and a special green Safely Operate LED. Here is what Sansui had to say about it in their marketing literature: ‘Our exclusive DD/DC-circuitry has been widely accepted as a landmark in the search for the most natural sound reproduction.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-7700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-7700","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-g-7700.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-7700","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/08/sansui-g-7700-front.jpg"}},"sansui-xr-q-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥74,800. The direct drive method is adopted for the drive system, and the new SilentSynchrotor technology eliminates the twist vibration of the cabinet. In the direct drive method, the motor drive is located almost at the center of the cabinet enclosure, so the rotational force that is the reaction of the motor drive occurs in the cabinet. In order to eliminate this rotational swelling, servo causes torque ctuation, and the rotational thread vibration is caused to the cabinet as its reaction. For this reason, if the servo effect is strong, the greater the reaction, the twisting vibration of the cabinet will evaporate. This reduces the rotational vibration level of the cabinet to 41/4 or less when Silent Synchroter is off. The drive motor features a new FF coreless motor that eliminates the problem of conventional coreless motors.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui XR-Q 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/xr-q7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-lx-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥29,800. Autoplayer with less basic performance and thorough ease of use. We supply SBMC material with excellent internal loss and strength for cabinet material to ensure system resonance. Equipped with a Romans straight arm to utilize a light needle pressure and high compliance type cartridge. MM type cartridge XL XL The set record board automatically selects 30cm LP board or 17cm EP board and features a photoelectron disk size selector that accurately leads tonearm. The auto-return mechanism is equipped to finish the performance. It comes with a guide to measure needle pressure, which is suitable needle pressure, and a disc centering guide that makes it easy to put 30cm LP board.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-LX 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-lx-2.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx2.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx2.JPG"}},"sony-ps-lx-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥35,800. Fully automatic player developed to enjoy disc sound with easy operation. MM type cartridge for light needle pressure and high-compliance type is equipped with Romans straight arm. Servo control is performed by linear BSL motor and magnet disk speed detection. The set record automatically selects 17cm or 30cm and is equipped with a photoelectron disk size selector that accurately leads in. The cabinet adopts SBMC material with excellent internal loss and strength. Includes needle pressure guide and disc centering guide.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-LX 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-lx-3.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx3.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx3.JPG"}},"sony-ps-lx-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥43,800. A full automatic player developed in pursuit of ease of use based on Sony's revolutionary technology \"Three-stage block\". Three-stage block of linear BSL motor, magnetic disk speed detection, and quartz lock is available for the rotation system. With the use of linear BSL motor, which removes brushes and slots from DC motor, it is possible to release mechanical torque changes called ko and achieve quiet and smooth rotation. High torque is increased because it is more efficient. MagneDisk Speed Detection detects high-density magnetized signals on turntable by multi-gap head to detect the average number of rotations. In addition, because it has a relatively high occurrence signal frequency, it is possible to compensate servo to the high frequency even in the flutter component. We use quartz lock to achieve stable rotational characteristics for changes in ambient temperature and power supply voltage and frequency. Tonearm is equipped with a romans-straight arm to bring light needle pressure and high compliance cartridge. Automatically selects the record board and has a photoelectron disk size selector that accurately leads tonearm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-LX 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-lx-5.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx5.JPG"}},"sony-ps-x-45":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥42,800. direct-drive Player system with full automatic mechanism that enhances safety. In addition to auto-cutting, auto-repeat is also possible by the front panel operation, so you can start and stop playing until you close the dust cover. You can switch to manual operation. The arm limiter mechanism protects the mechanism by eliminating the auto mechanism even if the arm is in operation. The motor has a linear BSL motor that does not require a brush or slot. This reduces torque swelling and realizes quiet and smooth rotation. Because it is efficient, it has high torque and improves reliability and durability. The magne disk speed detection method is used for the speed detection part of the servo circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 45 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x45.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥52,000. Quartz Rock direct-drive Player System with Biotracer. tonearm provides a microcomputer that performs hundreds of logic decisions between 1/1000 seconds and a biotracer that electronically controls the operation with speed, position detection sensor and linear motor. This biotracer can suppress the peak of low-range resonance within 3dB even if any cartridge is used, and the crosstalk is also improved. In addition, because it is a speed type sensor, the detection output is reduced as low frequency, and the feedback amount is reduced, and the vibration is difficult because it is applied to speed feedback, so it is a structure that is resistant to hauling and shock. The tonearm is automatically up when the performance is finished, and the turntable stops from the record. In addition, because of its efficiency, it improves reliability and durability due to high torque. The magne disk speed detection method is used to detect the speed of the servo circuit, and the magne disk speed detection method is used to detect the sensitivity of high-density magnetized signals on the turntable by multi-gap head, and the change in the rotation speed is observed. Because it has a high generated signal frequency of about 284 Hz at 33, 1/3 rpm, it is possible to compensate servo to a relatively high frequency among the flutter components.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥49,800. Fully automatic player with improved operability and reliability by installing a microcomputer. A microcomputer with a built-in operation such as select record size, lead-in/return operation, and repeat playback. The arm-specific motor and electronic circuit ensure smooth and safe auto operation. The record end detection mechanism adopts a contactless method that improves reliability. The motor has a linear BSL motor. This motor does not require any brushes or slots, so it reduces torque and realizes quiet and smooth rotation. Because it is efficient, it has high torque and improves reliability and durability. The speed detection unit of the servo circuit requires magnetic disk speed detection. Because it has a high generated signal frequency of about 284 Hz at 284/3 rpm, it is possible to compensate servo to a relatively high frequency even in the flutter component.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-65":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥59,800. Fully automatic player with computer control arm. PS-X65C comes with cartridgeless PS-X65 and MM type cartridge XL-25A. The computer control arm is equipped with the electronic control of the biotracer and the conventional static balance method. This arm is to measure horizontal speed sensor, position detection sensor, and linear motor, and electronically control horizontal drive. This has been a successful improvement in low frequency. In addition to the normal auto operation, you can control the front of the armorous queuing and rotational speed change by the start/stop of the arm and turntable only. In addition, it is not necessary to touch the dust cover except when setting the record, except for the case of setting the record, except for automatic record size select, electronic side force cancellation, etc. The arm lifter is equipped with a muting mechanism. The motor uses a simple linear BSL motor that does not require a brush or a slot.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 65 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x65.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥43,000. Simple and straight transmission. In addition, by inserting pulse power supply and heat pipe, we achieve low distortion rate. Two-tape monitor/independent tape copy function is equipped. Self-deft tone control Push function switch with indicator. Equipped with loudness. Equipped with a microphone mixing mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-4":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥55,000. Equipped with a regat linear method. MC cartridge compatible high gain equal amplifier. Two-speed feather touch volume control Two-tape monitor/independent tape copy function is equipped. Self-deft tone control Features such as audio muting, subsonic filter and loudness control. Gold plating is applied to the fono terminal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax4.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥69,800. Microcomputer-controlled ASP is integrated with simple and straight. This enables simple and straight transmission of audio signals. All-push control is available with a feather-touching of key parts such as 1dB step digital volume control. The power amplifier is equipped with a regat linear method. You can preset three different frequency characteristics of flat and arbitrary two, from the frequency characteristics of 1764, which can be operated by subsonic and high filter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥89,800. Equipped with the same structure as TA-AX8. The audio current method is used to disconnect the power between preamplifier and power amplifier. This enables the four separate separate amplifier configurations with the preamplifier and power amplifier for each left and right channels. This enables the ideal grounding while pursuing independent characteristics and improves performance effectively. In addition, input signals and loads are determined by kk, and the influence of earth loops, power supply impedance, and the influence of line materials and switches intervened in signal pathways are ignored. In addition, the power supply part of the preamplifier adopts a constant current centre polarizer, which can cut the influence from the power amplifier power supply, and ensures stable regulation because power supply impedance is almost zero. In principle, high-speed output element Hi-ft trans works in the ultra-small cut-off area, there are no non-linear elements added to the signal system, and there is a feature that does not change the operating condition by the large and small input signal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-ax-7.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax7.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax7.JPG"}},"sony-ta-ax-8":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥130,000. A new idea of current drive is introduced in pursuit of simple and straight transmission. The audio current method is used to disconnect the power between preamplifier and power amplifier. This enables the four separate separate amplifier configurations with the preamplifier and power amplifier for each left and right channels. This enables the ideal grounding while pursuing independent characteristics and improves performance effectively. In addition, input signals and loads are determined by kk, and the influence of earth loops, power supply impedance, and the influence of line materials and switches intervened in signal pathways are ignored. In addition, the power supply part of the preamplifier adopts a constant current centre polarizer, which can cut the influence from the power amplifier power supply, and ensures stable regulation because power supply impedance is almost zero. In principle, high-speed output element Hi-ft trans works in the ultra-small cut-off area, there are no non-linear elements added to the signal system, and there is a feature that does not change the operating condition by the large and small input signal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax8.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-n-900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥250,000. The power stage features a dual-diffusing power MOS FET developed by Sony. Common power MOS FET has features such as high input impedance, fast response speed, and wide safety operation area. TA-N900 uses this power MOS FET and adopts a new development distortion reduction circuit to operate the A class in most areas while controlling the drive voltage to correct the linearity of the power stage. This significantly reduces the impact of TIM and loudspeaker load reactions by improving the power stage distortion rate of more than one digit compared to conventional models. The terminal is the SEPP output of the Complementary Emitter. It has a NNB loop from this output terminal to the first stage, but the signal is separated by the power stage even from a small loudspeaker load, so most problems with TIM and reactive load are ignored. The prestige gain is a structure that drives the power stage strongly with about 27 dB.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-N 900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-818":{"more":[{"t":"This is the classic Technics SA-818. The SA-818 put out 110 watts per channel rms. It listed for $850.00 when introduced in 1980 and weighs just under 41 pounds. The SA-818 and it’s younger brother the SA-616 only lasted one year as they were totally redesigned the following year. One of the SA-818’s features was called Synchro-bias which was a change in the circuitry to eliminate distortion from transistors switching on and off. It’s rated maximum Total Harmonic Distortion is .005% or less. Not bad. It also had Quartz Synthesized Tuning and a new Class A amplifier section. The SA-818 also featured LED meters instead of the older analog needle meters (Vu).","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Technics SA-818","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-818","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-sa-818.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-818","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2010/06/technics-sa-818.jpg"}},"technics-se-a-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1979 at ¥300,000. This is a stereo power amplifier that is at the top of Technics's new class A amplifier that eliminates switching distortion and crossover distortion. It uses a new classA amplifier using a synchronous bias circuit unique to Technics. The synchronous bias circuit detects the positive and negative cycles of the signal prior to the output stage and always applies a constant bias to the output transistor whose amplification is stopped to prevent the occurrence of switching distortion. In addition, since the signal path and the bias current are independent, the output transistor always maintains an appropriate operating point. Furthermore, since the fast response diode switching between the positive and negative half-cycle has characteristics close to the ideal square characteristic, the new classA as a whole shows that the rise and fall waveforms of the current are very close to the ideal square characteristic, and the resultant transfer characteristic becomes a straight line near the 0 cross point. This eliminates the problem of crossover distortion. The DC amplifier configuration does not include any capacitors in the signal path from input to output and in the feedback loop to obtain excellent transmission characteristics. The first stage of the circuit consists of one chip dual FET differential amplifier with uniform temperature characteristics, bootstrap cascode and current mirror load.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a3-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-a-808":{"more":[{"t":"A simple stereo power amplifier consisting of two ICs and one transistor. The input stage IC is a differential amplifier with a current mirror load capable of selecting an operating current with a low distortion factor, and realizes a low distortion factor while maintaining a high gain. Power ICs of the complimentary service stage are composed of pure output circuit of two stage Darlington connection. Equipped with a relay type protection circuit that protects the output stage IC even if the speaker terminal is short-circuited. Uses a low-distortion 2-power transformer power supply circuit with reversed winding and canceled flux.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 808 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a808-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1979 at ¥100,000. A full automatic player developed with TECHNICS player technology to record jacket size of 31.5 cm wide and depth. Tonearm uses linear tracking tonearm. Linear tracking arm uses DC motor with high rotational accuracy for arm running, and controls this microcomputer. By adopting a sliding bearing with a small coefficient of friction, it realizes quiet and accurate arm running without unnecessary vibration than using ball bearings and rollers for arm movement. Arm polarization detection uses a proprietary optical sensor (optical non-contact type), which enables accurate control over the detection method of the bearing by detecting at the tip of the arm. The turntable drive unit adopts the unique integrated direct-drive Fully-automated microcomputer control mechanism is integrated into four buttons.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-10.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-15":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥150,000. A full automatic player with 10 programs in a compact body of 31.5 cm in width and depth. Linear tracking arm adopts a unique dynamic balance method, and the center of the rotation axis is designed to match the center of the center of the rotation axis, eliminating the need for strict horizontal adjustment. The arm bearing structure adopts four-point support gimbal suspension with pivot and ball bearings, and has high initial sensitivity. In addition, the HPF core of precision mirror surface polishing is adopted in the magnetic circuit, and the high performance of vibration and power generation system enables wide-band playback. The plug-in connector method is used for bonding cartridge and arm. Because the lead wire is unnecessary, it prevents contact defects, binding errors, and partial resonance of bonding with the lead wire bond. The electronic control full automatic mechanism makes it easy to operate with four keys after setting the record. Up to 1 to 10 programs can be selected automatically according to the order set by the program key. The order of the song is pressed by the program key, and if you programming, the LED next to each key is lit and you can check it.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-15 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-15.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥45,000. DD. full automatic player condensed function to LP jacket size of 31.5cm in length. In linear tracking method, tonearm is able to line the record board, as well as the machine where the tonearm exists, so it has the merit such as tracking errors that cause distortion, and in-side force that causes unbalance between channels to0 0. SL-5 uses a unique linear tracking method with tonearm in the upper cabinet. The arm drive adopts a DC motor with high rotation accuracy and excellent response, and it is electronically controlled by a microcomputer. In order to increase driving accuracy, arm polarization detection requires a proprietary optical sensor (optical non-contact detection) that detects near the needle tip of the cartridge. cartridge the detection of the bearing part, the high-precision detection signal is used to control the sound groove tracking of the cartridge in the ideal state. With this, the tracking error angle is less than 1 ° and the inside force is almost 0. Also, the arm runway is a small slide bearing with friction coefficient, which realizes high-precision arm running without unnecessary vibration due to ball bearings and rollers. We use a unique dynamic balance system that matches the center of the arm rotation axis with a center of gravity. It achieves stable trace performance without strict horizontal adjustment and needle pressure adjustment.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-q-33":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥59,800. In addition to SL-Q3’s performance, a full automatic direct drive player with a fully-functional Quartz Face Locked Control. The cabinet has a two-layer structure with precision aluminum die-casting and TNRC, which has high vibration-proof effect on the bottom base and cabinet top. The front operation method can be operated by all control switches until the dust cover is closed. Equipped with a high sensitivity tonearm with a gimbal suspension system that achieves 7mg horizontally and vertically. Arm is equipped with anti-scaling force control function. The arm operation is controlled by a dedicated DC motor and a precise reduction mechanism. Built-in musical circuit to eliminate needle tip noise.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-Q 33 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q33.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-ql-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥79,800. Linear tracking player with performance and functionality. The SL-QL1 is equipped with a compact, high-precision linear tracking tonearm inside the upper cabinet and has excellent needle tip tra ability due to accurate operation. The arm polarization that is the driving condition of the linear tracking arm occurs with the movement of the cartridge. The polarization detection mechanism of SL-QL1 uses optical sensor (optical non-contact detection) and microcomputer control to obtain high driving accuracy. cartridge detection at the bearing part, we control the sound grooving performance of the cartridge to be ideal for polarized detection near the cartridge needle tip. The tracking error angle is less than 1 °, and the inside force is almost 0. In addition, the DC motor is equipped with high rotation accuracy and excellent response to servo. In addition, arm running is a very small slide bearing with friction coefficient, which realizes quiet and smooth arm running without unnecessary vibration due to ball bearing and roller adoption. SL-QL1 tonearm has its own dynamic balance method.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-QL 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-ql1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-a-4":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1979 at ¥200,000. An amplifier that pursues the ideal waveform transmission in a preamplifier. All stages are class A operation and all stages are FET inputs. The MC pre-preamp of the ICL, the phono equalizer of the ICL, and a full DC amplifier (flat amplifier and buffer amplifier) are added. This allows two MC inputs and one MM input to pass through only one coupling capacitor, while the high-level input is DC-amplified to the output terminal without passing through any capacitor. The flat amplifier and buffer amplifier have a two stage configuration with a SEPP output stage as a dual FET differential amplifier circuit with well-matched input characteristics, cascode, and current mirror load. The output transistor uses a high-ft SLPT to reduce distortion and provide wide and flat frequency characteristics. The MC pre-pre-amplifier is composed of 4 para-elements of super-low noise FET, and the phono equalizer is an input stage of differential amplification cascode current mirror load by super-low noise dual FET with well-matched characteristics, thereby realizing ICL. The equalizer section is equipped with an equalizer subsonic filter to cut out ultra-low frequency noise caused by warping of records, etc. The SU-A4 is equipped with a DC buffer amplifier in the next stage of the DC flat amplifier to limit the output impedance to 0.2 Ω.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A 4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a4-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-c03":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-C03 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-c03-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v6":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated DC integrated amplifier with new class A system using Technics original synchronized bias circuit. In the new class A amplification method, a constant bias current is applied to the - side output stage that stops amplifying when the + side signal is received, and to the + side output stage for the - side signal, a constant bias current is applied to the + side output stage. The output stage is always active regardless of the presence or absence of the signal, and the transistor is non-cutoff to eliminate switching distortion. In addition, since the signal path and bias current are independent, the output transistor always keeps an appropriate operating point, and the high-speed response diode that switches the waveform has a composite transfer characteristic close to the ideal square characteristic, eliminating crossover distortion. A straight-DC method is adopted in which the DC amplifier directly amplifies the signal after the high-level input. This realizes faithful waveform transmission characteristics up to the DC range and further flattens amplitude and phase frequency characteristics in the audible frequency range. In the first stage of the main amplifier, a single-chip dual FET with excellent temperature characteristics is adopted. In normal operation at -10 ℃ to + 50 ℃, the DC drift is less than ± 10 mv, which is about 1/5 of the conventional level, and is kept at the minimum level.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v6-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v8":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1979 at ¥99,800. Integrated DC amplifier using Technics original new class A system. It employs a new class A amplification method using a synchronous bias circuit unique to Technics and eliminates switching distortion, which is the cause of sound turbidity. Switching distortion occurs in class B and class AB amplifiers because the positive and negative waveforms become symmetrical near the 0 cross point of the signal due to the accumulation effect of carriers when the output transistor is turned on/off. In a synchronous bias circuit, a constant bias is applied to the output stage so that the output stage is always active and the switching distortion is 0. In the new class A, crossover distortion is also eliminated. The crossover distortion is caused by a time lag between the positive and negative waveforms due to excess or deficiency of idling current, and the waveform itself does not have an ideal square characteristic and the combined positive and negative transfer characteristic does not become a straight line. In the new class A, the signal path and bias current are independent, so the output transistor always keeps an appropriate operating point, and the high-speed response diode that switches between the positive and negative waveforms has almost ideal square characteristic, so the crossover distortion is 0.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v8-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥66,500. Pure current servo amplifier and X power supply Power supply is equipped with X power supply by Phase Angle Control Circuit. This X power supply mechanism is a precise feedback circuit from the secondary side of the power supply cable to the primary side. Icoliza A servo is equipped with a pure current amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-6.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥89,000. amplifierX Series is the 3rd amplifierX series that realizes high power and light weight. The main circuit configuration is tone control of 0dB gain and control function. Each unit amplifier has a stable power supply from X power supply, and each circuit operates in the best condition to achieve superior characteristics. X power supply This X power supply has the same effect as the large power supply by conventional technology. It is obtained by small and lightweight power supply, and it realizes constant voltage up to the power amplifier output stage. The mechanism of X power supply is a precise feedback circuit from the secondary side of power supply to the primary side, and it detects the secondary supply voltage by the voltage comparison amplifier. This controls the operation of AC inserted into the primary side of. powerAC is a structure like a switch that repeats on⇔off by powerhronizing to power supply frequency.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-b-6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥190,000. A unique pyramid-shaped stereo power amplifier. X a ification is added to the a ification circuit. The power amplifier amplifier circuit configuration is a floating bridge complimentary push pull, cascode pure complimentary predrive, three-stage emitter foroa pure complimentary push pull drive output.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-6.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥98,000. Preamplifier for C-4 successor with pure ca servo servo amplifier and parametric tone control. The C-6 is composed of a DC equalizer with a pure ca servo amplifier and a flat amplifier with a pure ca servo amplifier. The MC head amplifier, which can be used as needed, is equipped with a new MC development parametric tone control circuit. The pure ca servo servo amplifier is available to prevent the power supply system from negatively affecting the sound quality by nonlinear of the element used for amplifier. This pure current servo servo amplifier always flows constant current on the power supply line, not only the L/C/R component of power supply and wiring, but also non-linear power supply due to current change. In addition, since there is no signal current on the earth line, the crosstalk of the low area is improved due to the difficulty of ground impedance. In the equalizer part, the casscode boot strap current mirror differential input with low noise high gain Dual FET, the darlington connection to the pre-drive stage, and the DC amplifier configuration with the Pure Complementary SEPP circuit in the output stage. The low-noise high-gain Dual FET, which is used here, is particularly low-noise specification, and is included in the same package with the electrical and thermal characteristics of two FETs with high gm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-6.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-p-550":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥39,800. A record player who changed or omitted some functions of P-650. The difference between the P-650 is that the servo method controls the rotation speed of the motor becomes the FG servo circuit with the pitch control and the armrest cannot be adjusted. tonearm adopts the ARS (AntiResonance Straight) arm developed by arm to reduce any resonance of the arm itself. In addition, the pipe holder is large and thin, and the double structure of 30mm from the branch point is coping with the wrinkle vibration around the pipe. The arm’s low-range resonance frequency is also determined to 12 Hz from the result of reflecting the playback spectrum of the direct cut record. In addition, we have determined the effective mass of arm by seeking the average value of the mass and compliance of the typical MM/MC type cartridge 30 models. The headshell part adopts a plug-in type that is reliable and easy to replace cartridge. In addition, needle pressure adjustment is a slide weight type.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-550 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-550.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-px-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥135,000. PX-1 and PX-2 are developed to enhance stability and operability. Tonearm is equipped with a linear tracking servo system. There is a non-contact/optical tracking error sensor in the arm base, and if the arm rotation (arm rotation) occurs slightly, the CdS has an unbalanced voltage. In PX-3, the same design as PX-2 is used only when arm down, using servo motor which can accommodate up to three times for rough pitches of the disc, and the vibration-proof design that suppresses the noise and vibration of the arm-based drive. Tonearm has an original ARS (anti-resonance straight) arm. This arm introduces know-how such as using high rigid materials and increasing the processing and assembly accuracy of parts. In addition, the rigidity is increased by making the maximum stress working pipe holder part a double structure up to 30mm forward.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha PX-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/px-3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-by-micro-seiki-px-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥180,000. In addition to the know-how obtained by PX-1, the player system has improved the completeness of the linear tracking method to improve costs and stability. The linear tracking arm features a tracking error sensor to improve the accuracy of the mechanism to move the arm. If the arm is lost from the right angle, the corresponding unbalance voltage will occur in CdS. This photo sensor is non-contact type, so it does not degrade the sensitivity of arm. In addition, there is a dead zone (unsensitive band) to correspond to the eccentricity of the record, and the transmission of the sound groove is always on the inside to suppress the impact of eccentricity. The value is 5mm in the dev position of the needle tip, and the servo circuit starts to work with the dev of 15 degrees in the tracking error angle, and it does not work under this value. Linear tracking servo works only when arm is down, and when arm is up, it is controlled by left and right feed signal. The servo motor for arm drive adopts the coreless motor with large torque and low mechanical noise.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha by Micro Seiki PX-2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/px-2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-e-301":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1981 at ¥198,000.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase E-301 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/E-301-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-m-100":{"more":[{"t":"A monaural power amplifier developed in pursuit of the ideal power amplifier with emphasis on \"low open-loop output impedance\" and \"high current supply power supply and output stage\" for ideal speaker drive. The output stage consists of 12 parallel push-pull wide-band bipolar transistors with Pc (collector loss) of 200W (total 24 output transistors) for a total power capacity of 4.8 kW with sufficient margin. The output transistors are divided into two groups and attached to the left and right large heat sinks to improve the heat dissipation effect. Since both heat sinks are not thermally coupled, the tendency is accelerated when there is a thermal imbalance, and only one of them will overheat and lead to the destruction of the element. In order to prevent such thermal imbalance, a bias balance circuit is adopted. In this circuit, the element connected to the base of the output element is attached to the other heat sink, the temperature is detected, and the bias current is controlled. By making the temperature almost equal to each other, stable operation is achieved. The drive stage is composed of MOS FET for power amplification which is an original of AccuPhase. It performs low-impedance high-current drive and significantly improves high-frequency characteristics.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase M-100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/M-100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"aiwa-ap-d-35":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥21,800. Mini component my Pace series autoplayer. The turntable motor is equipped with a 4-pole motorronus motor. tonearm is equipped with an integrated straight arm of the Romans type. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge. We use a production system to prevent accidents caused by operation errors.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Aiwa AP-D 35 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AIWA/player/ap-d35.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"aiwa-ap-d-80":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥46,800. Front-loading full automatic player of my Pace series. Front loading system is available. The tray and turntable move forward and backward by the button operation, and there is no need to open and close the dust cover when setting the record. A record size sensor that automatically detects infrared. Direct drive using FG servo motor. 560g resin concrete sheet is used to reduce resonance. AD operation mechanism with AD-L80 Equipped with auto-repeat mechanism. VM cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Aiwa AP-D 80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AIWA/player/ap-d80.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/aiwa-ap-d-80.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AIWA/player/ap-d80.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AIWA/player/ap-d80.jpg"}},"bang-olufsen-beogram-2402":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1970 at ¥135,000. Beomaster2400 The turntable drive adopts a high-precision motor using an electronic servo system, giving stable power through the belt. This automatically neutralizes the static electricity of the record and suppresses the effects of dust and dirt. In addition, a special sensing capability is given to the adapter embedded in the center, which detects the size of the record and sets it to the specified rotation speed. If you don’t have a record, you can also command to protect the needle tip of cartridge. Tonearm uses a new bearing structure based on the knife edge method and a new material to withstand light weight. We also reduce inertial moments by positioning the light counterweight made of brass tonearm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Bang & Olufsen Beogram 2402 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram2402.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/bang-olufsen-beogram-2402.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram2402.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/BANGandOLUFSEN/player/beogram2402(1).jpg"}},"bang-olufsen-beomaster-8000":{"more":[{"t":"Most vintage audio enthusiasts will recognize this receiver as a product of Bang & Olufsen. Bang & Olufsen audio components have a very distinct modern look. This is the Bang & Olufsen Beomaster 8000 and, at the time of its production, was the largest most powerful receiver they had ever produced. Its power output is 150 watts per channel which is coupled with a more modern digital frequency synthesized tuner and automatic fine tuning system. The user can also control associated audio components with the Beomaster 8000 such as a phono or tape deck manually or via remote. It also has 9 user-programmable FM stations. The Beomaster 8000 was available in the US from about 1980 up until 1985. It was dramatically different from most receivers produced in the US or Japan at the time. Bang & Olufsen changed from a mechanical to a 60 step electronic attenuator for volume control on this model.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Bang & Olufsen Beomaster 8000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/bang-olufsen-beomaster-8000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/bang-olufsen-beomaster-8000.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/bang-olufsen-beomaster-8000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/bang-olufsen-beomaster-8000-top.jpg"}},"c-e-c-hs-510":{"more":[{"t":"Semi-auto player with direct drive system. Uses a 20-pole 30-slot DC servo D. D. motor. The servo circuit eliminates the influence of external factors such as power supply voltage and frequency. Straight type is used for the tone arm. Howling is suppressed by the adoption of float suspension. Equipped with auto return and shut-off mechanism.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – C.E.C. HS 510 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/hs510-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/c-e-c-hs-510.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/hs510-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/hs510.JPG"}},"c-e-c-hs-610":{"more":[{"t":"A full-auto player with a direct drive system. Uses a 20-pole 30-slot DC servo D. D. motor. The servo circuit eliminates the influence of external factors such as power supply voltage and frequency. With the front operation method, it is possible to operate a record performance with the dust cover closed. Straight type is used for the tone arm. A float suspension system has been adopted to prevent howling.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – C.E.C. HS 610 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/hs610-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/c-e-c-hs-610.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/hs610-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/hs610.JPG"}},"c-e-c-hs-910":{"more":[{"t":"A full auto player with a quartz PLL servo DC motor. In addition to the full-auto mechanism, it uses a photo-sensor system that detects the return position. This system is a completely contactless type that uses a high-sensitivity IC made of Cds and does not adversely affect the arm sensitivity. In addition, an oil dump type arm lifter is mounted. Adopts the feather touch type front operation which is also adopted in the DD-8200. Straight type is used for the tone arm. Excellent mass distribution is obtained by the uniform lateral balance of the straight pipe arm, and combined with the reduction of effective mass by the adoption of the lightweight carbon fiber head shell, it is compatible with high compliance cartridges. In order to reduce the adverse effects of vibration caused by sound pressure from speakers and external vibration, we have adopted a suspension system with independent tone arms.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – C.E.C. HS 910 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/CEC/player/hs910-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-100":{"more":[{"t":"An armless record player developed by integrating all of DENON's player technology. The drive motor employs a 10 kg out Rocester 3-phase AC servo motor with a torque of 10kg-cm that is used for cutting machines as well as for broadcasting station players. This powerful motor has a weight of 6.5 kg and a moment of inertia of 1,260kg-cm. 2 To 33 1/3 revolutions in only 0.4 seconds from the start. A high S / N ratio has been achieved by the adoption of an AC3-phase drive system that eliminates the third harmonic of the rotating magnetic field, which causes vibration and reversing torque, and by the adoption of a winding system that ensures uniform magnetic flux between the rotor and stator, even if there is a gap between the rotor and stator, and by the consistent vibration resistant structure including the frame. The shaft is made of special stainless steel with a diameter of 14 mm. After heat treatment and high-precision polishing, it is wrapped. A special alloy is used for the radial bearing, and smooth rotation is obtained by lapping, and high durability is obtained by using a mirror-finished sapphire bearing for the thrust bearing that supports the entire rotating system. It is equipped with a safety mechanism to prevent troubles caused by unexpected external forces.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-100-m":{"more":[{"t":"A record player equipped with a dynamic servo tracer as a tone arm in the mechanism of the DP-100. The DP-100M has a dynamic servo tracer in its tone arm. The low resonance frequency (fo) set by the cartridge compliance and the effective mass of the tone arm should ideally be around 10 Hz in order to avoid the effects of record warping and eccentricity. In DENON, the negative effects such as modulation distortion were reduced by making the single tone arm and the tone arm of the player system lighter. However, if the fo peak (Q) remains high, the cantilever of the arm and cartridge vibrates more than expected in records with warpage, etc., and the needle pressure changes occur and the tracing capability deteriorates, causing intermodulation distortion. In the dynamic servo tracer, the Q of fo is electronically damped to prevent deterioration of sound quality due to increase of intermodulation distortion caused by low-frequency resonance and deterioration of crosstalk. First, the vibration of the tone arm is detected as an electric signal by two detection coils (vertical and horizontal). This signal is passed through a high-pass filter with a variable cut-off frequency volume. After passing through a gain volume, the signal is applied to a power amplification drive coil to provide a signal opposite to the vibration of the tone arm, and the vibration of the arm is controlled.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-100 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-100m-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-11-f":{"more":[{"t":"A microprocessor controlled compact player. A non-contact tone arm controlled by a microprocessor is mounted on the tone arm drive system. In addition, an electronic servo lifter is adopted to realize smooth arm operation. The tone arm is equipped with a light weight straight arm. A quick repeat system is adopted, and the record is lead-in without returning to the armrest. The cartridge is equipped with DL-60 MM type cartridge. DENON quartz is used for the drive part to improve rotational accuracy. Uses a dust cover with opaque coating on the back of the ceiling. The operation part uses a soft type push button, and by eliminating the unevenness of the button, the design quality is improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-11 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-11f-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-31-f":{"more":[{"t":"This is a microcomputer operated full auto player that has introduced DENON technology in various places. A direct drive system is adopted for the turntable part. The drive motor is equipped with a newly developed linear drive MF (Magne-Float) motor. It uses the attractive force between the rotor magnet and the stator yoke to reduce the load applied to the pivot by the weight of the turntable and rotor. This structure is effective in reducing uneven rotation, prevents wear of the pivot, and maintains smooth rotation performance. The servo circuit employs a bi-directional servo DENON quartz system that combines a high-precision magnetic recording detection system and a quartz lock system. The high-precision magnetic recording detection system uses a magnetic head to detect 1,000 pulse signals recorded at an accurate pitch inside the rim, which is almost the outermost peripheral position of the turntable, and controls them while comparing them with a reference voltage. It has high detection accuracy, high-speed response, and speed detection at the outer circumference where wow flutter appears most often. In addition, both forward and reverse servos provide a severe response to slight increases and decreases in rotational speed, improving static dynamic load characteristics.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-31 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-31f-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-32-f":{"more":[{"t":"Uses an electronic Q-dump light mass straight arm. Tone arm float. Contactless electronic servo arm equipped with microprocessor. With electronic anti-skating. With electronic brake.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-32 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-32f-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-60-l":{"more":[{"t":"Auto lift player equipped with auto lift mechanism with non-contact type end sensor. The up / down speed of the arm is optimally controlled by the electronic servo lifter, protecting the record board and needle. An arm pipe replaceable type is adopted for the tone arm part, and it is equipped with 2 of light mass straight tone arm and universal S-shaped tone arm. It is compatible with all types of cartridges including high compliance type cartridges by exchanging the arms. DENON quartz and AC servo motor are used for the rotating system to realize low wow flutter and high S / N ratio.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-60 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-60l-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-75-m":{"more":[{"t":"Player system with DP-75. The Turntable DP-75, which is sold separately, is mounted on the turntable part. This turntable has a dual structure and an external rotor type AC servo motor is used as the drive motor. Uses an electronic brake. Two types of arm pipes, straight and universal S-shaped, are attached to the tone arm part, and can be exchanged for a wide range of cartridges. In addition, the straight arm comes with a lightweight cartridge counterweight. Equipped with non-contact anti-skating mechanism and oil dump lifter. Equipped with a helicoid type arm height adjustment mechanism. The cabinet has a laminated structure of 90 mm thick particle board.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-75 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-75m-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-970":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier developed with POA 3000 and PRA 2000 PRA technologies. In order to shorten the signal system, we have adopted a two amplifier configuration consisting of an equalizer amplifier and a power amplifier, so that the tone circuit cannot be used as a servo circuit at the front of the power stage. In addition, the direct DC servo circuit removes all capacitors from all signal paths from the MC input to the SP output to achieve a complete DC configuration. A direct DC servo circuit that realizes a capacitor-less configuration for all stages is used for the equalizer amplifier and power amplifier. In the direct DC servo system, stability in the ultra-low frequency range is ensured by shutting out minute latent DC drift. Moreover, since this circuit has an extremely simple configuration with only the parallel connection of the first stage FET differential amplifier and servo elements, characteristic degradation due to the servo circuit does not occur. The equalizer amplifier section is equipped with a non-feedback real-time equalizer with two DC linear amplifiers. This circuit consists of two stages of DC linear amplifier with newly developed low-noise dual FET and a CR-type equalizing filter. The first stage is a dual-FET parallel differential amplifier with direct DC servo system, which fundamentally eliminates DC temperature drift while improving S/N and distortion factor.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-970 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-970-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-3800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥42,800. Equipped with non-cut off A circuit. The equalizer amplifier adopts high-pressure low-noise IC. The loudspeaker can connect two lines. Power self-illuminated switch is available. High capacity (6,800μFx2)","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-3800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-3800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-4800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥52,800. Integrated amplifier with non-cut off A circuit and dual servo circuit. Dual servo circuit developed in pursuit of NFB theory. In this circuit, the servo circuit, separately set from the negative return loop of the signal, detects the direct current component and the distortion component that occurs in the output terminal, and performs a negative return. This reduces DC and distortion components that occur in the output terminal. B-class amplifier is equipped with non-cut off A circuit that pursues the quality of A-class amplifier. The operation of this circuit is basically the same as the B-class amplifier, but it is automatically controlled according to the input signal without fixing the bias voltage of the output stage. This prevents the output trans from being cut off by maintaining the ON status and using the power according to the signal. The equalizer amplifier is a simple ICL equalizer circuit that can be connected directly to the MC cartridge. In addition, low noise IC is used in the output stage.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-4800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-4800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-6800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥69,800. A dual servo circuit that was born in pursuit of NFB theory. This effectively removes the distortion component generated in the output terminal and realizes high resolution music playback. With the main direct switch, you can connect the output of equalizer amplifier directly to the power amplifier without passing the amplifier. The power amplifier is equipped with a newly developed high-efficiency heat loop (heat-releasing fin). This prevents the deterioration of the SN ratio and distortion by de ing unnecessary patterns by focusing on the power MOSFET of the output stage. Also, the power supply line earth can be separated by the left and right side, minimizing crosstalk between channels.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-6800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-6800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-m-l-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥350,000. For this reason loudspeaker The phase of voltage and current at load is not a problem, and the same operation and performance as the net resistance load is ensured. In order to realize the power cascode super A circuit, the output trans is a new one. In addition to that, we carefully examine the sound quality of the core of power supply supply, and we offer only high-quality elements that have been carefully selected for both reliability and hearing as well as P-L10. In addition, it is important to consider the board pattern. The cabinet is the same as the P-L10 model.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC M-L 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/m-l10.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-p-l-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥250,000. A high-end preamplifier of the laboratory series that uses a thorough listening-focused approach to development, constructing a signal circuit with completely different shipping than before, and seeking the highest level of sound quality and functionality. Because of this, it does not affect the characteristics and sound quality of the amplifier. Since the noise level is decreasing in proportion to volume control narrowing, there are also features such as superior SN ratio in actual use. The equalizer circuit is also equipped with a Gm processor, and the current equalizer is different from the conventional negative feedback (NF) type and CR type. The circuit element has been carefully selected compared to listening with exceptional consideration.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC P-L 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/p-l10.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ql-a-75":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1981 at ¥95,000. Record player with arm pipe replacement method. Tonearm is equipped with a pipe replacement method using a thin threaded connector. QL-A75 offers high-rigidity Roman tapered straight pipes and S-shaped universal pipes with chaking-lock head connectors for unresonant oscillation. The combination of the included subweights and large weights for separate weight cartridges enables optimal matching for a wide range of cartridges. Also, QL-A95 type special high rigid material straight pipe PH-200 can be used. We have a unique high sensitivity and high stability New Gimbal support system for rotating bearings. A dynamic Q damping mechanism is built in the counterweight to suppress the resonance of arms that cause harmful mixed distortion and coloration. In addition, in order to suppress mixed modulation distortion due to the difference between turntable and tonearm-based vibration mode, the docking plate is used to bond both sides at the shortest distance. Also, turntable adopts a turntable of inertial mass 350kg-cm2 with a weight of 2.35kg including a mat, and the shaft adopts a thick shaft of 10mm in diameter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC QL-A 75 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-a75.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥145,000. Σ drive mounted integrated amplifier. In the Σ drive system, the idea of the traditional NPB that was completed in the axial housing is expanded to the input terminal of the loudspeaker side, and the loudspeaker cable is also considered as one of the internal wiring of the amplifier, and the performance is guaranteed with the input terminal of the loudspeaker. First, we have a unique Σ cable that connects loudspeaker's + side and power amplifier Σ return point, and controls various types of distortions, including the reverse distortion caused by the magnetic circuit of loudspeaker, not to occur with the input terminal of loudspeaker. In addition, by separating the power supply loop, the cable on the side is completely eliminated from the input terminal of the loudspeaker and the potential difference between the earth points. A non-magnetic structure is used to further the damaging distortion caused by magnetic distortion. In addition, the effect on equalizer is suppressed by resin on the side plate. Using large-capacity loud to L/Rch, it is equipped with a stable drive even if it connects loudspeaker with impedance change.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kr-1000":{"more":[{"t":"The Kenwood KR-1000 Galaxy Commander receiver has some, shall we say, unusual styling. It hit the market in late 1982 and was indicative of early to mid 1980’s aesthetics with a lot of colorful lights and a multitude of button controlled features. If you’re into silver faced gear then this receiver is probably not appealing to you but if you grew up in the 1980’s with boomboxes and digital clock radios then you might think it looks great. It listed for between $900 and $1000 so it wasn’t cheap by any means. The KR-1000 is no slouch when it comes to power output at 120 watts per channel into 8 ohms. It even has a dynamic power capability of 460 watts giving it plenty of headroom. It also has a respectable 0.01% Total Harmonic Distortion rating. The “Program Commander” is one of the main features of the KR-1000. It includes four different memories which allow the user to set volume, EQ and Source settings for each memory button and activate any of them via the Timer.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kenwood KR-1000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kenwood-kr-1000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-510":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1981 at ¥135,000. integrated amplifier with DUO β circuit / S. DUO β circuit / S is adopted for the power part, and the contents of the circuit are almost equivalent to L-530. The input of the power section is a parallel connection of a high-gm low-noise FET. A large current is supplied to obtain all necessary gains, and the pre-drive stage is eliminated. In addition, an \"appropriate amount NFB\" and a \"DC servo\" are provided to complete the sound quality. The class A operating range has been expanded to 8W, and most of the normal listening level is covered by the class A operation. In addition, the maximum output power of 100W has been realized in the class AB, and it is also applicable to large signal input which rapidly rises. The output stage is a parallel P. P. by adopting R.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-510 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-510-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-550":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1981 at ¥250,000. integrated amplifier with DUO β circuit / S. We have developed the DUO β Circuit / S, which combines an \"appropriate amount NFB\" and a \"DC-servo\", and the DUO β Circuit / S, which adds a \"single-stage amplifier\" in addition to the control feedback power supply plusX, which is superior in sound quality. These circuits are installed in the equalizer and power section. The first stage amplifier uses an FET for the MC head amplifier in the first stage. Originally, this FET has high gm and low noise, and it has a structure in which a large current of 7 mA per 1 stone is applied to obtain the necessary gain. At the same time, the output stage is completely independent so as not to affect the first stage, and the second stage is removed. This realizes an ideal circuit with only one stage for voltage amplification. The output section has an intrinsic class A operation with fixed bias current, and realizes a large output of 50W/ch. The large amount of heat generated by class-A operation is handled by two large heat pipes, which are symmetrical in shape to eliminate heat radiation noise.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-550 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-550-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1980 at ¥163,000. It eliminates harmful resonance caused by the material and warpage of the record board. In addition, there are two grooves and inlets on the turntable surface as air suction route, and the inside of the table turn has an air passage and is connected with the pump on the tube. This indicator detects the vacuum degree between the record and turntable to operate.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-310":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1981 at ¥95,000. It removes the contrary of the record that generates mixed modulation distortion, and also releases the resonance between the record and turntable. The basic structure of the PD310 is composed of a 30mm thick coniferous high-density particle board, and it sandwiches between the bearing and the arm base mounting section with a 5mm thick steel plate. This makes the record-turntable-bearing-arm-base solidified and releases harmful resonance. The FG servo motor FG motor is fixed with a brush and slotless FG servo motor FG motor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-310 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd310.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-ma-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥100,000. Monaural power amplifier capable of switching between class A and class AB operation. The circuit configuration is a Low-TIM design, and it is a 3-stage Darlington circuit with a power amplification stage which is a parallel push-pull type of super high-fT transistor excellent in high-frequency characteristics and switching characteristics. A large transformer and 22,000 μ Fx2 large audio capacitor are used for the power supply. The main amplifier uses a specially selected Meiler capacitor for phase correction. In addition, three boards (power supply board, relay circuit board, and main board) are made into a joint structure, and the power supply for the pre-stage amplifier of the main amplifier is made into a separate board. In order to improve the sound quality, priority is given to the pattern of the signal system. Equipped with a temperature-sensitive protection circuit, a temperature sensor detects when the heat sink reaches an abnormal temperature and a high-speed relay circuit protects each circuit. The input terminal can be either an AC couple or a DC couple, and each has a different system of direct input terminals. The terminal uses a gold plated terminal with less trouble of contact failure.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz MA-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/ma-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sc-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥490,000. Simple and straight configuration preamplifier dedicated to high-purity signal transmission. All blocks are fully push-pull pure class A DC unit amplifier to enhance bare characteristics. In addition, in order to release the signal system from interference between unit amplifiers and channels, and fluctuation of power supply, the power supply section is strengthened to the level equivalent to a power amplifier, and 8 sets of independent power supply including 6 sets of shunt regulator which realizes 0 power source impedance are installed. The equalizer circuit uses an negative feedback (NF)-CR type with excellent dynamic range and transient response characteristics to realize stable ultra-low output impedance. A balanced output terminal is installed in parallel with the pin jack. The volume uses L/R independent variable high precision conductive system which does not require balance control, and the tone control uses push switch type which eliminates sound quality degradation and characteristic disturbance. It is thoroughly simplified and equipped with two independent outputs, Flat Out and Tone Out. Only parts carefully selected by hearing are used. The high-precision oxygen-free copper wire used for the wiring material uses a crimping method without using a connector, taking into consideration the deterioration of sound quality caused by solder materials, which is a problem in general soldering.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SC-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sc1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sc-8":{"more":[{"t":"A preamplifier with a symmetrical design, polished sound quality and various functions. The full push-pull configuration is applied to all stages from MC head amplifier to flat amplifier, and the Low-TIM design eliminates dynamic distortion such as transient intermodulation distortion by improving bare characteristics and reducing NFB. The MC head amplifier consists of a complete push-pull circuit consisting of nine single-channel channels from the first stage of the ultra-low noise transistor 2 parallel push-pull to the SEPP output stage. In addition, the phono amplifier has a complete push-pull circuit configuration that is affected by input / output impedance fluctuations, and the equalizer element has a metal-coated resistor within 1% error and a polypropylene capacitor within 2% error. The flat amplifier is a pure class A amplifier with a unique push-pull circuit for all stages. Especially in the last stage, super high f T (200 ~ 250 MHz) Uses a two stage Darlington system with power transistors. The Phono selector is equipped with a 3-position MM cartridge load selector in addition to the MC head amp position. Features include independent left and right tone control, two deck dubbing, two stage switching loudness control, two output switching, and both High and EQ Subsonic filters.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SC-8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sc-8-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sc-9":{"more":[{"t":"This is a preamplifier with an advanced circuit structure and carefully designed materials that emphasize sound quality. In addition, it is equipped with functions that enhance the enjoyment of music playback. The basic circuit consists of a phono amplifier with a first stage of ultra-low-noise FET differential input and a pure A-class SEPP output stage with exactly matching pair characteristics, as well as a DC amplifier configuration for all circuits including an MC head amplifier with ultra-low-noise FET input, to enhance bare characteristics. In addition, the impedance of the feedback circuit is completely lowered to improve the SN ratio. This makes it possible to reduce the distortion factor and noise with the minimum necessary amount of NFB, and achieves the Low-TIM design that eliminates the occurrence of excessive navy blue distortion caused by excessive NFB. Equipped with MM/MC independent cartridge load selector, MC can select load resistance value of 4 position and MM can select load resistance value of 5 position, and it is compatible with all cartridges. In addition to the Bass and Treble, which have two low and two high turn-over frequencies and can be controlled by ± 10 dB each, it is equipped with an independent left and right tritone control equipped with a Mid control. In addition, a Tape EQ switch is mounted to guide this control signal to the recording output.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SC-9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sc-9-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥690,000. This stereo power amplifier was developed to realize the ideal amplifier called \"straight wire with gain\". All stages including the output stage using 12 metal can power transistors per channel are complete push-pull configuration complete DC amplifier realized the unique Low-TIM design, and the purity of high power is enhanced with a straight signal path that eliminates all capacitors and switching contacts from input to output. Two types of speaker terminals are installed, one is direct and the other is sub 1 and sub 2. With the direct terminal, the emitter and output terminal of the power transistor are directly connected, and high-purity power can be delivered. The protector that protects the speakers from DC components uses an SCR crowbar circuit with no output contacts to achieve reliable operation without degrading sound quality. The power supply section uses a 800 VA large-capacity transformer and a custom capacitor, making it completely independent of L and R. The peak power meter uses a high-precision logarithmic compression indication type that can directly read the output of 8 Ω load. 2-stage switching of recovery time is possible. The heat radiation system adopts a high-efficiency type with a unique finger decipeter and a two speed clean fan.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm700-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-8":{"more":[{"t":"Stereo power amplifier equipped with Quarter A circuit. The Quarter A system consists of an input level detection circuit and a high-speed switching circuit. It has a structure in which the bias current is fixed until a certain power (30W for SM-8) is used for complete class A operation, and when the power exceeds the fixed power (30W to 120W for SM-8), it automatically switches to class AB operation. In addition to realizing the excellent power quality of pure A-class, super high f T By using a power transistor and unique Low-TIM design, crossover distortion and transient distortion are minimized even during high-power driving of class AB operation. The basic circuit configuration is a push-pull DC amplifier with a built-in servo circuit. The power supply section is equipped with a compact but large-capacity transformer and a super audio condenser of 22,000 μ Fx2 + 20,000 μ Fx2 that has been carefully examined in terms of characteristics and sound quality. Heat resistance is improved by filling with special resin. Using a heat pipe with high heat radiation effect, the stable operation of the power transistor is guaranteed even in class A operation which consumes large current and class AB maximum output. In addition, a protection circuit is mounted to detect excessive output and keep the power stage within the safe operation range, and the speaker is driven in a stable condition.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-8-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-9":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo power amplifier developed based on Marantz's tradition of making full use of the best power device with the best operation and best circuit. For all stages push-pull full DC configuration circuit, super high f T By using a (90 MHz) power transistor, bare characteristics are greatly improved. Marantz's unique Low-TIM design, which eliminates transient intermodulation distortion by reducing NFB, provides high-quality Class AB output from low level to maximum output. The power supply section is equipped with a large-capacity transformer for the power amplifier stage, with the secondary side fully wound on the left and right sides. In addition, the voltage amplifier stage is equipped with a dedicated transformer to reduce interference between channels and stages. In addition, the use of a 15,000 μ Fx4 filter condenser with excellent high-frequency characteristics and other highly reliable configurations ensures stable and ample power supply capability. High-purity oxygen-free copper wires are used for all lead wires including transformer lead wires. In addition to the sub-speaker terminal which can be switched to 1/2, a direct speaker terminal which does not use contact is mounted. The protection circuit uses an energy sensor type that detects excessive output and keeps the drive transistor signal within a safe range.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-9-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-mc-2255":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥1,098,000. This is a stereo power amplifier developed by the Macintosh to realize the policy of \"better sound longer\" more surely. Equipped with a unique power guard mechanism. A waveform comparison circuit is built into the circuit to compare the waveform states of the input and output signals. Equipped with a self-diagnosis device, the circuit is divided into seven circuits and automatically checked. If there is a problem, the output to the speakers is automatically stopped until repair is done, preventing naming due to excessive operation. By adopting an output transformer originally developed by Macintosh, impedance matching is greatly improved, and the power transistor can be operated at a temperature about 20 ℃ lower than that of a normal amplifier. As a result, a large output can be obtained with a sufficient margin, extending the time when the system can demonstrate its ability.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MC 2255 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc2255-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/mcintosh-mc-2255.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc2255-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc2255.JPG"}},"micro-seiki-bl-71":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥98,000. A record player using a belt drive system with a circumference drive. Turntable is 3.2kg (3.2ing sheet) weight. This turntable is designed with a thick outer circumference and has a large inertial moment of 550kg/cm2. The outer circumference of this turntable is realized by the belt drive. The turntable shaft adopts a stainless steel shaft with a diameter of 16mm, which clarifies the branch point and ensures stable rotation performance. The stainless steel shaft is further polished with a pair of metal bearings after heat curing and polishing. This makes the precision of mirror finish less than 0.4 microns. In addition, we use special alloys for bearing metals, which ensures smoothness by oil bath method (lubrication with shaft and bearing metal). The drive mechanism is equipped with a belt-ap external drive system.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki BL-71 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/bl-71.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-lt-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥69,800. A full-auto player with linear tracking system. It uses a linear tracking system in which the arm moves linearly on the record board. The linear tracking tracking method, tracking error and harmonic distortion can be reduced because the tangential direction of the sound groove is accurately traced. In addition, since there is no inside force, the needle tip can be made symmetrical contact, and overall tracking capability can be improved. A stainless steel wire is used for the drive of the moving base that fixes the tone arm. This wire realizes excellent durability and flexibility by combining 49 fine wires of 0.05 mm diameter and applying nylon coating. Tracking error is detected by the potential difference between the two photodiode outputs at the rear of the arm. To detect the record size, an optical system is applied to the automatic record size detection mechanism. In this system, the reflector emits light from an obliquely upward direction, guides the light from the turntable seat reflector to the sensor, and changes the output of the sensor by irradiating or shielding the light according to the size of the record.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi LT-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/lt-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-px-100-m":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥500,000. A high-grade linear motor system with drastically improved rotational bare characteristics, aiming at the ideal phono motor. The PX-100M uses an induction type linear motor that drives the turntable directly around its outer circumference. This motor realizes excellent rotational accuracy. In addition, from the principle of operation as an induction type motor, the rotor has no magnetic pole, and there is no cocking phenomenon associated with the pushing and pulling of the magnetic pole in the movement of the rotor, and ideal smooth rotational characteristics are ensured by the continuous thrust given from the stator. The PX-100M has excellent bare characteristics and does not require a servo circuit. However, since the PX-100M has some slight variable elements such as temperature characteristics of lubricating oil between shaft and bearing, the minimum necessary servo is applied. The principle of linear motor rotation is that when a current is applied to a coil, a magnetic field is generated, and eddy currents are generated in the conductor in the magnetic field. When this magnetic field is moved in the rotational direction, the magnetic flux that cuts the overcurrent changes, so the disk is guided in the direction of the magnetic field. To move this magnetic field, a sine wave with a 90 ° phase difference is added.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo PX-100 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/player/px-100m-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-5":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo record player that took advantage of the technology used in the PL-4 and was released at an affordable price. A hysteresis synchronous motor is adopted for the motor, which is resistant to voltage and load, and realizes more accurate rotation. The turntable has a diameter of 30 cm, a weight of 1.4 kg, and a precision finish of cast aluminum. In addition, the lower end of the shaft is conical, and the bearing is precisely machined from a gunmetal to achieve more precise rotation. The tone arm uses a dynamic balance type. In the dynamic balance type, the weight of the pickup itself is 0 and the needle pressure is applied by a special spring so that the pressure at the tip of the needle is constant and uniform needle pressure is applied to both sides of the sound groove. The cartridge mounting part conforms to JIS and EIA standards. The MM type cartridge PL-C1 is used. The mass of the vibration system is reduced by using a 0.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-5.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-5-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-5.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-7":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer PL-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-7-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-7.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-7-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-7.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-x-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥39,800. Front-loaded full automatic player with a compact design of 21cm depth. It adopts the front loading method, it can be placed slim on the book shelves, and you can stack the amplifier and tuner up. Easy operation full auto is used to automatically detect the record size by simply setting the record and turning on the START switch. SH Rotor type motor is used for drive motor. The cartridge has a high output MC cartridge that does not require cartridge or head amplifier. All operation switches are concentrated on the upper left side of the front to improve operation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-X 50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-x50.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-x-50.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-x50.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-x50.JPG"}},"pioneer-sa-520":{"more":[{"t":"An authentic integrated amplifier designed for ease of use. All stages of the power amplifier are connected to a semi-power complimentary service system. The first stage is equipped with an operation amplifier and an input bias compensation circuit to achieve high DC stability. The equalizer amplifier is a 2-stage direct-coupled system that combines a low-noise transistor with a low-noise resistor and a styrofoam capacitor to improve S/N and stability. CR-type tone control has been adopted, and in pursuit of component accuracy, the tone control knob has obtained characteristics with less waviness in the frequency characteristics in the flat position.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-520 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-520-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sa-620":{"more":[{"t":"In line with the original purpose of the integrated amplifier, this model is designed with full functionality and sound quality as the goal. The equalizer amplifier uses a 2-stage direct-coupled circuit with transistors that further select the low-noise type to improve S/N and stability. In addition, high-precision parts (resistors and capacitors) are used in order to reproduce the recording characteristics of the record with fidelity. It is equipped with two Phono terminals and two pairs of terminals for tape decks so that two tape decks can be connected at the same time. With a built-in microphone mixing amplifier, you can mix and play the program source and the sound from the microphone. The mixed signal can be taken out from the Tape Rec jack (DIN jack), so you can also record by connecting a tape deck. It can also be used as a simple microphone loudspeaker device. The tone circuit is a 2-stage direct connection NFB type with three carefully selected transistors. By adopting the emitter follower circuit, the flat position of the tone control knob provides a simple characteristic with less waviness.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-620 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-620-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sa-620.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-620-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-620(1).JPG"}},"pioneer-sx-4":{"more":[{"t":"This 2-way speaker system was developed by investing 15 years of know-how in making small speakers. A 18 cm cone type woofer is installed in the low range. This unit uses highly heat-resistant covered copper wire for the voice coil and has a large diameter of 48 mm Φ to improve heat radiation effect and input resistance characteristics. A 2.5 cm dome-shaped tweeter is installed in the high range. Titanium diaphragm is used for the diaphragm, and as with Woofer, highly heat-resistant coated copper wire is also used for this unit. The enclosure is hermetically sealed. The exterior is finished with Rosewood tone. It can be hung on the wall by using the hole on the back.","s":"audio-database.com"},{"t":"People tend to focus on the big, powerful receivers when looking at vintage stereos, but, there are some little guys out there that are very appealing as well. Not everyone has the space or desire for a 50+ pound monster in their house. Some just want a well performing, small, affordable stereo. Well, the Pioneer SX-424 is just that. Pioneer introduced it in the early 1970’s – probably sometime around late 1971. It retailed at that time for about $200 which was very affordable. By 1974 the price had dropped to about $130. The SX-424 does not pump out a boatload of power. But, the 12 watts it does put out are solid and will drive most speakers.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SX-4 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x4-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-4","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-424","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-5":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-50 was introduced in 1983 and had a retail price of $380. It is a computer controlled stereo receiver and embraced emerging audio technologies, supporting TV audio inputs and also anticipating the rise of the compact disc. It pioneered multiple audio inputs and allowed switching between emerging formats like CD players and hi-fi videodisc soundtracks. Its forward-thinking design made high quality audio integration intuitive and uncomplicated. The SX-50 produces 50 watts per channel and has a very low rating of .007% total harmonic distortion. The sound is characterized as clean as opposed to warm and the tuner is adequate in areas of strong signals. It was part of Pioneer’s lineup that included the SX-40, SX-60, and the top of the line SX-V90 which came out a bit later. Here are the prices and power outputs of the models: If you’re into the retro 1980’s look then the Pioneer SX-50 probably looks cool to you. The numerous push buttons with different coloration and of course the large green vacuum fluorescent display give it a new wave look.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-5","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-50","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-6":{"more":[{"t":"A speaker system that pursues quality sound beyond its size. The basic design of the S-X6 is a simple 2-way design, and a super-high frequency unit is added after determining an appropriate crossover value. A 22 cm cone type woofer is installed in the low range. The diaphragm uses carbon graphite, which has excellent physical properties such as high rigidity, high internal loss, high airtightness, and no aging. A large ferrite magnet of 134 mm outer diameter with high magnetic flux density is used for the magnetic circuit. A 5.2 cm cone type tweeter is installed in the high range. Carbon graphite is used for the diaphragm as well as woofer. The ultra-high frequency band is equipped with Pioneer's exclusive full-surface drive ribbon type Super Tweeter. Each unit has a diamond cut ring design on the edge.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SX-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x6-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sx-6.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x6-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x6.JPG"}},"pioneer-sx-7":{"more":[{"t":"A small speaker system suitable for the rear speakers of surround systems. A 8.7 cm full range type unit has been adopted. It is equipped with a switch that can change the output sound pressure level between Low and High, and the surround level can be adjusted. The enclosure is black wood-grain with round baffles to reduce sound diffraction, and the bass reflex duct has a unique horn shape. Since it comes with embedded nuts for mounting stand and hanging fittings for wall mounting, etc., free setting is possible.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SX-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x7-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-907-f-extra":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥175,000. AU-D907F The power amplifier is equipped with a unique superfeed forward system. AU-D907F EXTRA adopts MOS-FET to the error collection amplifier to further improve the quality of this circuit. In addition, the pre-driver stage features a diamond differential circuit that suppresses TIM distortion to zero. Linear step MC cartridge is installed to support MC cartridge. High impedance and low impedance can be switched to accommodate any MC cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 907 F Extra (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d907fextra.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-fl-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥65,000. Record player with flat roof and linear scanning mechanism. The linear scanning mechanism developed by TC-K88 is adopted. The front panel and table turn body are pulled out to the front and the record hash can be pulled smoothly. We also have a flat roof style similar to cassette decks and tuners. This enables you to stack decks and amplifiers, and you can load up to 20 kg at the top of the free. All FL5 operations are structured by buttons on the front panel, making it smooth and full-auto by microcomputer and arm-driven motor. In addition, FL5 has improved ease of use and safety by linking the linear scanning mechanism with another dedicated motor. Set the record with the turntable body being pulled out and press the start button to automatically store it inside. Then turntable starts and tonearm is lead in.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-FL 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-fl5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥59,800. Fully automatic player system with biotracer straight arm. There are two variations of PS-X600 and MM type cartridge XL-20. tonearm provides a microcomputer that performs hundreds of logic decisions between 1/1000 seconds and a biotracer that electronically controls the operation with speed, position detection sensor and linear motor. This biotracer can suppress the peak of low-range resonance within 3dB even if any cartridge is used, and the crosstalk is also improved. In addition, because it is a speed type sensor, the detection output is reduced as low frequency, and the feedback amount is reduced, and the vibration is difficult because it is applied to speed feedback, so it is a structure that is resistant to hauling and shock. With electronic needle pressure adjustment and auto-in-side for scanning cellar, you can adjust the needle pressure during recording. Adopts a contactless photoelectric auto record size selector, automatically select the record size and queue. In addition, this function works as a safety mechanism when the start instruction is made without setting the record. Two tonearm Move buttons allow you to queue any position of the record. It is also possible to adjust about 1mm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥99,800. A full automatic player system that expands the potential of biotracers by incorporating smart zero balance mechanism and digital display of needle pressure. Tonearm is equipped with an electronic tonearm biotracer. This makes it possible to suppress the peak of low-range resonance within 3dB even if any cartridge is used, and at the same time, cross-talk is improved to achieve excellent low-range regeneration. The arm pipe uses an aluminum alloy with a high rigidity, and the J-shaped structure with a large bending strength makes it possible to achieve a rigidity of about eight times the conventional aluminum pipe. With a contactless optical electronic auto disc size selector, the record size is automatically selected. Also, when the record board is not installed, tonearm works as a safety function. Three-stage block of linear BSL motor, magnetic disk speed detection, and quartz lock is available for the rotation system.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ps-x-700.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x700.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x700.JPG"}},"sony-ps-x800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥150,000. Linear tracking player system with active trace servo system in addition to the biotracer. Tonearm is equipped with a biotracer. The biotracer has a speed sensor, position detection sensor, and a linear motor. This is yro, which enhances the follow-up of the disk, and enables some sorts and eccentricity to play without problems. In addition, even when using any cartridge, the peak of low frequency resonance is reduced to 3dB or less, and it is possible to extract the individuality of the cartridge. In addition, we can improve crosstalk. A linear tracking system equipped with a newly developed active trace servo. Active Tra servo focuses on the main focus of moving the disc’s pitch on the inside while changing to the barrier. It rotates the arm-side feed motor in advance and makes the pitch change read to the position detection sensor of the biotracer.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥32,800. Panel height 45mm slim design amplifier integrated. Two-system tape terminals can be used for simultaneous recording of two decks and mutual tape copying. Equipped with a microphone mixing mechanism. Push function switch with indicator. Equipped with loudness switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥69,800. This makes the internal impedance of the preamplifier seen from the power amplifier endless, and electrically separates the preamplifier and power amplifier between the left and right channels. Volume control eliminates the attenuator type volume control and provides a linear gain controller. The linear gain controller generates pure input voltage in the power amplifier stage. This also reduces impedance as much as gains are lowered, thus improving sound quality during actual use. The power amplifier is equipped with a regat linear method. This enables low distortion over broadband/wide dynamic range. Straight transmission using heat pipe is realized.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax6.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-e-900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥600,000. A stereo preamplifier with a high degree of completeness in both characteristic and sound quality. The MC head amplifier is composed of the base ground push pull amplifier, and the casscode connection improves linearity. For this reason, it has a characteristic that the power supply is difficult and the impact on power supply is very small. The equalizer amplifier is a dual-FET differential amplifier. This FET is equipped with electrical characteristics, and has good thermal equilibrium, and is designed specifically to make the mutual inductance large, and the return capacity is reduced. S/N compensates for good and stable operation. The second step is PNP trans amplifier. Like the first stage, the casscode connection is used to prevent temperature drift and improve linearity and reduce distortion. The output stage is an emitter spruce PP type with a Darlington connection so that it can cope with a certain amount of load.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-E 900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-e900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"teac-ma-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥180,000. TEAC and TANNOY co-developed Armonia series power amplifier, under the theme of \"Use high quality MC cartridge to play TANNOY loudspeaker with high quality sound\". This amplifier was evaluated by Mr. Norman J-Clocker, the president of TANNOY, to use it as a system for TANNOY products. MA-7 is a complete DC power amplifier configuration with a newly developed protection circuit, and double mono configuration is available to prevent cross-interference of left and right channels. Feed forward circuit. Load Short Circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – TEAC MA-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TEAC-ESOTERIC/amp/ma-7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"teac-pa-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥180,000. The Armonia series preamplifier jointly developed by TEAC and TANNOY under the theme of \"Play TANNOY loudspeaker with high quality MC cartridge\" This amplifier was evaluated by Mr. Norman J-Clocker, the president of TANNOY, to use it as a system for TANNOY products. The PA-7 is a DC preamplifier with a dual servo circuit, which uses MC cartridge as a prerequisite. Built-in headphone amplifier. Tone control enables recording sound quality correction. Protected circuits and clicks. Equipped with subsonic filter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – TEAC PA-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TEAC-ESOTERIC/amp/pa-7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-103":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥49,800. This is an FM/AM stereo tuner amplifier that combines a 20W + 20W amplifier and a tuner in a slim size. The FM front-end is designed with high sensitivity by adopting a junction FET and a high-precision 3-row varicon in the RF stage. In addition, two ceramic filters are used in the IF stage, and low distortion and high selectivity are achieved by the all-stage differential configuration with excellent limiter characteristics. The MPX demodulation circuit employs a double differential switching system using a PLL IC. Equipped with a tuning monitor mechanism that lights up orange when detuning and green when tuning. The input stage of the main amplifier consists of a differential amplifier with a current mirror load capable of selecting a low-distortion operating current, and a low-impedance emitter follower drives the pre-drive. The complimentary service stage consists of a two stage Darlington semi-output push-pull circuit. The equalizer circuit of the preamplifier section employs a differential 2-stage amplifier circuit that combines a discrete configuration with low-noise transistors and an IC. It is equipped with a pure electronic protection circuit to protect the amplifier from shorting of the speaker terminals.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SA-103 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/sa-103-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-a-5":{"more":[{"t":"This is a stereo power amplifier that inherits the philosophy and quality of the SE-A1 and SE-A3 and is equipped with a linear feedback circuit. A new class A system consisting of a synchronous bias circuit and a concentrated power block is equipped with a new linear feedback circuit. This circuit was developed by putting the best effort into multiple feedback circuit technology. It forms an independent period circuit in the NFB loop that enables the naked amplification degree = ∞ of the amplifier. As a theoretical value, it realizes distortion = 0, pure gain without the influence of elements and power supply, and speaker drive without the influence of back electromotive force and wire. A synchronous bias circuit is mounted, and a constant bias is supplied in synchronization with the pause cycle to each output transistor on the + side and the - side which are alternately paused in class B operation. The output stage is always in active state, and switching distortion is eliminated. In addition, since the signal path and the bias current path are independent, the output stage maintains an appropriate operating point. Together with the function of a high-speed diode with square characteristics, crossover distortion is eliminated.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-a-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1981 at ¥80,000. 1U stereo / mono DC power amplifier equipped with new class A system and linear feedback circuit. In addition to a synchronous bias circuit that eliminates switching distortion and crossover distortion, it is equipped with a linear feedback circuit that realizes theoretical distortion = 0 and output impedance = 0. Monaural driving is possible by switching the switch on the rear panel. The tap of the high power transformer is switched according to the load impedance, and the rated output is 60W + 60W at 4 Ω load in the same manner as at 8 Ω load. This greatly reduces the amount of heat generated and reduces the radiator capacity to 70% of conventional capacity. Two ultra-thin transformers are used. The two transformers are arranged to cancel electromagnetic radiation to each other and prevent external induction. By adopting a high-efficiency radiator using a heat pipe, the heat generated by the output transistor is dispersed laterally. The power meter uses an FL display tube of 12-segment logarithmic compression display.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a7-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥70,000. Full automatic player with LP jacket size of 31.5cm in width and depth. Tonearm uses a dynamic balance linear tracking arm to achieve precise trace performance regardless of the angle of installation. In addition, the polarization detection function by the optical sensor near the needle tip, microcomputer control, gimbal suspension support structure, slide bearing structure, etc. are used to enhance the trace performance. It is a full automatic player that starts playing just by setting the record and clicking the start button. cartridge is equipped with EPC-P202C which is a MM type cartridge of plug-in connector method. The drive unit has excellent rotational characteristics by adopting proprietary integrated direct-drive and all-round detection FG. The upper part of the cabinet is made of precision aluminum die-casting, and the lower part is made of zinc die-casting and TNRC bottom base. You can use a separate player stand.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-b-303":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥32,800. Record size automatic detection, full automatic player with no record detection function. The detection mechanism and internal mechanism embedded in turntable automatically detects the presence and size of the record and automatically controls tonearm. FG servo motor circuit Built-in DC motor. The cabinet adopts TNRC, which has excellent vibration damping and absorption rate. MM type cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-B 303 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-b303.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-d-303":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥39,800. Direct drive full automatic player with automatic detection mechanism. Automatic detection of record size and non-detecting of records. The record detection mechanism and internal mechanism embedded in turntable automatically detects whether or not and size of records and automatically controls tonearm. Unique integrated structure direct-drive, full-fr ency FG flat motor, etc. Tonearm uses a gimbal suspension method to achieve the initial motion sensitivity of 7 mg or less. Front operation control with electronic control soft touch switch is available. TNRC is a unique sound material that has excellent vibration damping and vibration damping rate on the bottom base. MM type cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-D 303 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-d303.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-dl-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released March 1981 at ¥59,800. Direct drive linear tracking full automatic player with superior basic performance. The arm is equipped with a linear tracking arm that runs straight in the upper cabinet. It is equipped with DC motor with high rotation accuracy and good response performance for servo. The arm runway adopts a small slide bearing with a friction coefficient and realizes high-precision arm running without unnecessary vibration. The arm support structure is a four-point gimbal suspension bearing structure, which adopts its own dynamic balance method and has a stable balance performance. The cabinet adopts TNRC, which has excellent vibration isolation and absorption characteristics, and is thoroughly anti-vibration. A unique integrated direct-drive You can use your own plug-in connector to connect cartridge and tonearm. Relieves defects in contact with cartridge terminals and arm terminals due to lead-wire bonding, resulting in less performance deterioration and increased reliability for bonding.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-DL 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-dl1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-q-202":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥47,800. The cabinet is made of precision aluminum die-casting, and the bottom base is TNRC. In addition, double-isorated suspensions are used to provide superior sound characteristics. We use the quartz-fade locked control to control the turntable rotation with the accuracy of the quartz. With a reliable full-fr ency detection FG, it combines the adoption of integrated direct-drive and two-phase full-wave drive system flat-to-face slotless DC motor to achieve superior rotational performance. Tonearm is equipped with a 4-point support structure with pivot and ball bearing. This is a structure that intersects the axis of horizontal rotation axis and vertical rotation axis at a point, obtaining a high initial sensitivity of 7mg.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-Q 202 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q202.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-sl-q-202.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q202.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q202.JPG"}},"technics-su-a-6":{"more":[{"t":"Based on the technology used in the SU-A2 and SU-A4, this preamplifier offers a high level of saturation of performance and functions. All stages are class A operation to eliminate switching distortion and crossover distortion. In addition, all basic circuits are ICL, and a straight DC amplifier is realized in which the Phono input passes through only one coupling capacitor and the high-level input does not pass through any capacitor. The equalizer amplifier uses a low-noise dual-FET parallel configuration, and MC cartridges can be directly connected. In addition, gain switching is available for MM cartridges. Low output impedance design with SEPP buffer amplifier. As a result, even if a power amplifier with a low input impedance is connected, or even if several power amplifiers are connected, waveform degradation caused by such power amplifiers will not occur. Equipped with a unique shelving tone. This shelving tone can be adjusted in four levels: Super Base, Super Treble, Bass, and Treble.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A 6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a6-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-a-8":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1981 at ¥70,000. A 1U size stereo DC preamplifier with A-class operation in all stages, ICL configuration in all stages, and a presettable electronic selector. The equalizer circuit is based on the MC high-gain basic design by using a low-noise FET in parallel and combining a cascade connection input for differential amplification with a high-performance operational amplifier. The tone circuit is also fully DC-integrated flat / tone amplifier, which increases the fidelity of waveform transmission. Switching distortion and crossover distortion are eliminated by the class A operation of all stages. In addition, all basic circuits are ICL, forming a straight DC amplifier in which the phono input passes through only one coupling capacitor and the high-gain input does not pass through any capacitor. An electronic selector is used for the input selector. The phono and high-level selectors are 2-wei-switchable electronic selectors (MM ⇔ MC, tuner ⇔ aux) that can be used to preset the buttons by pressing down firmly. It is equipped with sliding volume and touch fader which can fade in and fade out the volume. Two tape decks can be connected.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A 8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a8-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-c04":{"more":[{"t":"This is a Concise Integrated Amplifier equipped with a Technics original linear feedback circuit that realizes theoretical distortion = 0. Going back to the origin of NFB theory, we have adopted a linear feedback circuit that makes NFB work more ideally. This circuit forms an independent feedback circuit that can provide infinite amplification in the NFB loop. It theoretically realizes an amplifier that performs ideal operation with theoretical distortion = 0, pure gain without influence of elements and power supply, and speaker drive without influence of back electromotive force and wire, further enhancing the quality of the new class A system. This realizes low distortion and high sound quality. It employs a new class A method using a synchronous bias circuit unique to Technics and eliminates switching distortion, which is the cause of sound nigori. Switching distortion is caused by the asymmetry of the positive and negative waveforms near the 0 cross point of the signal when the output transistor is turned on/off in class B and class AB amplifiers. In order to solve this problem, the synchronous bias circuit applies a constant bias current to the output transistor and keeps it active at all times, thereby eliminating the switching distortion. New Class A also eliminates crossover distortion, which is another cause of sound nigori.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-C04 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-c04-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥64,800. Based on the new class A amplifier technology developed in the SU-V10, this integrated amplifier further reduces distortion by installing linear feedback that realizes the distortion theoretical value = 0. The linear feedback circuit is a circuit that returns to the ideal of NFB theory and assumes that the naked amplification degree of the amplifier is ∞. By forming an independent feedback circuit that enables the naked amplification degree of the amplifier to be ∞ in the NFB loop by making the best of the multiple feedback circuit technology, the theoretical value of distortion = 0, pure gain without the influence of elements or power supply, and speaker drive without the influence of back electromotive force or wire. In the SU-V7, the bandwidth of the independent feedback circuit is limited, and the feedback amount is gradually reduced as the frequency increases. With this configuration, a gain increase of about 20 dB is obtained at 100 kHz. Even in the ultra-high frequency range, the NFB is 10 times more stable than the conventional one, and the distortion is greatly reduced. In the DC region, gain increase up to infinity is obtained, and the input conversion is 2 μ V / ℃, which is excellent stability against DC drift.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v7-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"thorens-td-226":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥398,000. TD226 has five different types of arms that are equipped as an original system. Two-layered turntable and one-step belt drive system are available. The turntable is made of zinc alloy diecast with a diameter of 30cm and weight of 3.2kg. It is driven by a high torque 72 pole DC motor. By adopting the 72-pole multi-pole motor, it reduces the rotation mura of the drive source itself, and it increases the flywheel drop of turntable by reducing the iner mass of motor, which increases the iner mass of turntable, and obtains smooth and accurate rotation. Also, the motor realizes constant speed by servo circuit. The electronic logic circuit is used to change the oscillation frequency of the tacho generator. Rotation speed can be adjusted within ±6% range.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Thorens TD 226 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/THORENS/player/td226.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sb-66":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥69,800. Equipped with a clean drive. Equipped with our own clean drive. In the clean drive method, the code for detecting the distortion component is added to the minus terminal of loudspeaker, which detects the distortion component generated by loudspeaker and feedbacks within the amplifier. Then, adjust the return amount to cancel the distortion component in the amplifier and send it. This eliminates the distortion caused by the loudspeaker cable transmission characteristics and the reverse power generated by the loudspeaker to improve the dynamic characteristics. The cord also detects impedance with the loudspeaker cable, so the voltage in the loudspeaker input terminal is not equivalent to the output voltage of the amplifier. By adopting this clean drive method, the harmonic distortion rate is reduced to less than 1/10 when used with loudspeaker, and the mixed distortion is greatly improved. In addition, since all the impedance of the amplifier and loudspeaker command line can be canceled, the impedance when the amplifier side is seen from the loudspeaker input terminal becomes zero, and the damping factor in the loudspeaker input terminal is infinite.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SB-66 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sb-66.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-ql-y-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥96,000. Record player with quartz lock and electronic control arm. Tonearm uses ED (electro dynamic) servo and tonearm. ED servo tonearm uses a method to detect arm vibrations in a pure electronic form, and to revoke the same force in the reverse direction with feedback control. The two coreless linear motors directly connected to horizontal and vertical bearings are driven by the electronic circuit. This cancels unnecessary vibrations and in-side force due to low frequency resonance and disturbance, and controls both needle pressure and anti-scaling. ED servo tonearm realizes soft touch operation. After zero balance, it is not necessary to touch the arm body. You can also perform auto return, reject on the way, and manual operation. In addition, needle pressure, anti-scaling, and fo's Q damping are continuously variable by independent volume control.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor QL-Y 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-ql-y-77-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥105,000. ED servo tonearm ServoED tonearm is a microcontroller controlled servoED tonearm. ED servo tonearm is an electronically in contactless method that suppresses the peak of fo harmful to sound quality by mechanical friction such as oil damping. Two coreless linear motors directly connected to arm horizontal and vertical bearings detect arm vibrations in a pure electronic form, and the vibration is turned off by microcomputer feedback control. In QL-Y77F, this double direct drive type ED servo tonearm is further improved, and the servo gain has been increased to 5 times more than conventional by strict consideration of the mounting position of the coreless coil and the improvement of bearing accuracy. The tapered straight pipe is light and rigid for the pipe, but you can easily replace cartridge by adding optional spare pipes and universal S-shaped pipes. The pipe exchange method and the low center of gravity TH (tra hold) structure enables optimal traces in various cartridges. By attaching the arm base and turntable base with a docomo plate, the phase of each vibration is aligned and the mixture is suppressed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor QL-Y 77 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y77f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-5d":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥49,800. A-5-based amplifier integrated. Icoliza AMP is equipped with low-noise FET differential input + high-precision OPAC IC. In the power amplifier part, it is a high reliability hybrid IC on the voltage amplifier stage, and the power amplifier is a DC configuration using the SEPP-OCL of the discrete 3-stage darlington connection. In addition, the preamplifier part which deals with fine signals is especially powerd power supply, and the constant voltage is sent separately for lamps. The protection circuit includes a loudspeaker protection relay, PC limiter circuit, etc. that automatically detects when the DC voltage is harmful to loudspeaker. tone control circuit has a unique negative feedback (NF)-CR type. In addition, new volume control makes it possible to obtain the correct characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-5D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-5d.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-8":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥169,000. In addition, MC head amplifier with the Complementary Push Pull FET differential input and negative feedback (NF)-CR tone control circuit can be inserted as needed. The MC head amplifier is a circuit configuration targeted for power supply, which is the Complementary Push Pull FET input → Complementary Push Pull output. The first-stage complementary push-pull operates on the source ground, so the FET’s two-way characteristics are offset and the distortion is low. In addition, the constant current circuit and the pure current amplifier method are used to treat a particular low signal, and the noise from the power supply side is eliminated by various non-linear components. In addition to the 100Ω position, 10kΩ position is provided. The higher the input impedance of the amplifier, the less the non-linear impact such as failure of contact during the middle.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-8.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-b-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥180,000. Stereo power amplifier with ZDR (Zero Distortion power), X power supply, linear contact fa circuit etc. power A ZDR is developed and mounted with a distortion detection circuit and input addition circuit to completely eliminate the distortion that occurs at the end. The distortion detection circuit detects only the distortion component in taking complete bridge configuration. It also detects distortion caused by reverse power from loudspeaker. In addition circuit, distortion component is added as floating bridge circuit from floating power supply to power stage input part. Since the signal source has a series addition method, the independentity of the drive signal current and the distortion correction current from the voltage amplifier is maintained, and the correct distortion cancellation operation is measured without adverse effects on each other.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-5100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥48,000. System component Passage series integrated amplifier. Cut unnecessary ultra-low frequency to improve sound quality. The switch has a feather touch. Built-in microphone mixing circuit. YP-9100 and YP-7100","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-5100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-5100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ca-7100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥59,800. System component Passage series integrated amplifier. Cut unnecessary ultra-low frequency to improve sound quality. The switch has a feather touch. Built-in microphone mixing circuit. Fade-in-mute mechanism Equipped with subsonic filter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CA-7100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ca-7100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-p-650":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥49,800. Record player with unique ARS arm and quartz PLL servo. tonearm adopts the ARS (AntiResonance Straight) arm developed by arm to reduce any resonance of the arm itself. In addition, the pipe holder is large and thin, and the double structure of 30mm from the branch point is coping with the wrinkle vibration around the pipe. The arm’s low-range resonance frequency is also determined to 12 Hz from the result of reflecting the playback spectrum of the direct cut record. In addition, we have determined the effective mass of arm by seeking the average value of the mass and compliance of the typical MM/MC type cartridge 30 models. P-650 can adjust arm height. The headshell part adopts a plug-in type that is reliable and easy to replace cartridge. In addition, needle pressure adjustment is a slide weight type.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-650 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-650.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-p-650.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-650.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-650.JPG"}},"yamaha-p-850":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥59,800. It has two-size and pure electronic full-auto function. When the record is played, put the record on turntable, select the size by the DiscSize button, and auto-read at the beginning of the first song. In P-850, it works by a photo sensor consisting of three photointertars fixed to the cabinet and a logic shutter fixed to the tonearm. The built-in microcomputer handles three-bit signals from the photointertar, even if tonearm is in any position and controls the way tonearm is located. This photo sensor also detects the arm's position and return zone. All detection behavior of this fully automatic function is optical, so there is no negative impact on sound quality with non-contact. Up-down, auto-return, auto-repeat, and auto-cut operation with microcomputer. If you want to stop playing in the middle of the song, the motor for arm lifter is turned on by the signal from the microcomputer and the arm rises. The horizontal control will start when it is complete, and tonearm will return to the left position.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-850 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-850.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-p-950":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥69,800. Record preyer released as a high-end model of the P series. Equipped with one-touch automatic selection mechanism with built-in optical intersection. P-950 uses a dedicated cartridge cartridge-8000 built-in optical sensor that detects the intersection of the record, and can automatically select the desired song from 1st to 8th. This function is not available if the dedicated cartridge cartridge-8000 is not used. Microcomputer control features full auto control, controlling auto lead-in, up-down, auto-return, auto-repeat, and auto-cut. Smart Lead-in works with a photo sensor consisting of three photo-intertarpters fixed to the cabinet and a logic shutter fixed tonearm. This photo sensor also detects the target position and return zone of arm. Since the detection operation is optical, there is no negative impact on sound quality. In addition, auto return is a speed detection type that uses a large pitch of the lead-out groove of the record.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-950 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-950.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-p-950.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-950.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-950.JPG"}},"yamaha-r-500":{"more":[{"t":"The Yamaha R-500 receiver was released in 1981 as part of Yamaha’s popular R-Series line. At the lower end of the R-Series lineup, the R-500 provided adequate power at 40 watts per channel and all the necessary features of a low to mid-range receiver. It retailed for $330. Designed to provide low distortion, wide frequency response, and high power output, Yamaha used key components to achieve this performance. The amplifier section uses negative feedback techniques to reduce distortion. The preamplifier features low-noise circuitry and a flat RIAA equalization curve for accurate phonograph reproduction. The AM/FM tuner provides excellent sensitivity to deliver clean, static-free reception. The Yamaha R-Series of receivers included the top of the line R-2000 ($900 – 150 wpc) as well as the R-1000 ($700 – 100 wpc), R-900 ($550 – 70 wpc), R-700 ($450 – 50 wpc), R-500 ($330 – 30 wpc), and R-300 ($260 – 30 wpc). The R-500 includes all of the features expected in a mid to high end receiver of that era.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Yamaha R-500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/yamaha-r-500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-c-280":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1982. This stereo preamplifier was developed for both analog and digital disc playback in response to the advent of digital audio and digital discs. The circuit configuration combines the Accuphase traditional A-class push-pull amplifier stage with the cascode method to improve the element characteristics before NFB is applied. The cascode connection provides good performance, especially at high frequencies, with little feedback. In addition, linearity is maintained up to the operating limit of the device, distortion is reduced, and the signal-to-noise ratio is improved. By using A class push-pull, linearity and distortion characteristics are further improved, and element characteristics before NFB is applied are improved. The basic circuit configuration of the unit amplifier is the same as that of the head amplifier, equalizer amplifier, and high-level amplifier. It is basically 3-stage amplification. It consists of 2 stages of input cascode push-pull differential amplification with 8 elements and 2 stages of cascode push-pull amplification with 4 elements. In addition, it is equipped with an IC-based DC servo circuit that detects DC generated at the output and returns it to the input to prevent DC drift.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-280 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-280-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥49,800. A full automatic player that omits microcomputer function from DP-5. Fully automatic detection of record size. A quick repeat method is used for repeat playback, and the arm is replayed from the first song without returning back to the left. Tonearm is equipped with a linear tracking arm, and the tonearm offset angle is always 0.1 ° or less by the sensor and servo circuit applied with photo transLED and LED. In this method, arm and servo circuit move arm straight to the groove of the record. Because of this, there is no tracking error distortion and clear sound is realized. arm has a long size cartridge integrated design arm which is strong against the record. The arm lifter mechanism adopts the linear motor for the first time and adopts the V-block, which is the original new mechanism. The V-block is a mechanism that increases the speed servo and the needle tip vertically. It realizes quiet operation with linear motor and prevents the record from hurting.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/denon-dp-3.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-3.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-3.jpg"}},"denon-dp-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥59,800. Fully automatic player with linear tracking system. Record play function by microcomputer and memory. You can set your favorite song or song order freely. Built-in musical circuit to eliminate unpleasant noise during release of records and needles. It is equipped with an interlocking terminal that can start with the deck. Fully automatic detection of record size. A quick repeat method is used for repeat playback, and the arm is replayed from the first song without returning back to the left. Tonearm is equipped with a linear tracking arm. In this method, arm and servo circuit move arm straight to the groove of the record.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/denon-dp-5.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-5.jpg"}},"denon-dp-51-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥69,800. Full auto player with almost the same configuration as DP-52F and MM type cartridge installed Adopts a full auto mechanism. The tone arm is driven by a non-contact structure that does not affect the tone arm sensitivity or rotation system, and smooth operation is achieved by microprocessor commands. In addition, it is designed for safety. When there is no record on the turntable, the tone arm does not operate, so there is no trouble of needle tip. In addition, by the adoption of electronic servo lifter, it is not affected by temperature and needle pressure, etc., and the tone arm shows up and down movement at a constant speed, and the impact between the needle tip and the record is minimized. With the full auto function, when you press the Start button, the sensor automatically detects the size and rotation speed of the record (33 1/3 rotation for 30 cm, 45 rotation for 17 cm) and the performance starts. In the case of a record such as a 45 rotation disc for 30 cm records, you can respond by pressing the Start button and then pressing the specified rotation speed button. The tone arm is equipped with a dynamic servo tracer light mass straight arm. As a straight arm with a light mass, the fo is set at around 10 Hz to avoid the influence of the modulation noise in the ultra-low band caused by the warping of records, etc., and further to be out of the audible band.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-51 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-51f-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-730":{"more":[{"t":"A stereo integrated amplifier equipped with a non-feedback 0 dB power amplifier and super equalizer. The non-feedback system is realized by a direct distortion servo circuit. This servo circuit compares the input signal with the signal obtained from the output side (main signal + distortion component) to detect only the distortion component, inverts the phase of this distortion component, and adds it to the input side, reducing the static distortion to the theoretical 0 range. Unlike the negative feedback (NFB) method, this non-feedback method does not return the output signal to the input side, so there is no dynamic distortion, no influence of the back electromotive force of the speaker, and the circuit can be simplified and high-speed. In order to support low-impedance speakers, the power supply and power amplifier stages have been strengthened so that full-power playback can be performed safely up to 4 Ω speakers. The power amplifier circuit consists of a two stage current mirror with a low-noise transistor for the first stage and a low-impedance complimentary service and emitter follower for complete separation from the power amplifier. The power amplifier stage is a push-pull configuration of a high-speed power transistor for higher power. The input of this power amplifier has a built-in filter that cuts out harmful ultra-low frequency noise.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-730 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-730-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-750":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier is equipped with a non-feedback 0 dB amplifier that realizes 0 dynamic distortion and an ultra-wide band super equalizer. The basic circuit is the same as that of the high-end model PMA 770. It consists of two amplifiers including a direct-DS (distortion servo) no-feedback 0 dB and an MC/MM super equalizer equipped with a real drive circuit and a direct-A system. Equipped with an MC/MM super equalizer, it achieves broadband characteristics of 20 hz to 100 khz ± 0.2 db. The amplifier consists of an negative feedback (NF)-type DC amplifier with newly developed low-noise dual FET and a CR-type equalizing filter. The first stage is a dual-FET differential amplifier with direct DC servo system. The power amplifier section uses a non-feedback 0 db amplifier. In this method, the static distortion caused by the nonlinear amplification characteristic of the power transistor is driven to the 0 region by the effect of the direct DS circuit, and high sound quality is achieved. The circuit configuration consists of a 3-stage current mirror with a low-noise FET at the first stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-750 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-750-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-770":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier was developed by introducing original technologies such as a non-feedback 0 db amplifier, direct A system, and super equalizer. From the MC input terminal to the speaker output terminal, all stages are capacitorless (complete DC configuration) without using even a single capacitor in the main signal path. The signal path is made pure and high-speed. This fully capacitorless configuration uses the direct DC servo circuit installed in the PMA 970 and PMA 950 to suppress DC drift and ensure stability in the ultra-low frequency range. Equipped with an MC/MM super equalizer, this cartridge has excellent RIAA deviation characteristics of 20 Hz to 100 kHz ± 0.2 dB, exceeding the upper reproduction limit frequency of high-end cartridges. It consists of an negative feedback (NF)-type DC amplifier with newly developed low-noise dual FET and a CR-type equalizing filter. The first stage consists of parallel differential amplification with dual FET of direct DC servo system. The power amplifier section uses a non-feedback 0 dB amplifier. The non-feedback 0 db amplifier compares the signal obtained from the output side of the main amplifier (main signal + distortion component, etc.) with the input signal by the direct distortion servo circuit, and extracts components other than the input signal (distortion, noise, etc.).","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-770 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-770-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-poa-8000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥350,000. Monaural power amplifier using DENON non-feedback system. In the POA-8000, a non-feedback system that does not generate dynamic distortion is adopted from the beginning, which is a complete change from the system that cancels dynamic distortion. In the non-feedback system, input signals are amplified in only one direction. First of all, a signal transmission and amplification system that does not generate transient response distortion is adopted. Distortion and noise generated in the amplification system are removed by a distortion removal circuit. The circuit configuration of the POA-8000 is such that the main amplification system does not have a phase compensation circuit or β circuit, and the amplification stage can be reduced by half. Therefore, the main amplification system amplifies the signal in real time from input to output. Moreover, since it is one way without return, no transient distortion occurs, and excellent dynamic characteristics are obtained. The distortion removal circuit is equipped with a voltage type at the first stage and a power type at the last stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon POA-8000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/poa-8000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pra-6000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥450,000. Based on the development and design philosophy of real-time audio technology, this preamplifier incorporates pure non-feedback circuits in all stages from MC head amplifier to equalizer amplifier and final high-level amplifier. The pure non-feedback circuit cancels the distortion of the output signal by combining the input transistor and the transistor operating in the reverse mode. The basic circuit is a single-stage amplifier circuit in which a constant current source is inserted at the common connection point of the N-channel FET and the PNP transistor and the P-channel FET and the NPN transistor. Since the output current of the FET has a power transfer characteristic with respect to the input voltage, the distortion generated in the FET is only the second harmonic distortion. The distortion is canceled by combining the N-channel FET and the P-channel FET. Two sets of pure non-feedback circuits are installed in the equalizer amplifier section to ensure high S/N, low distortion rate, and wide dynamic range. Furthermore, by utilizing the characteristics of current amplification, which is a feature of pure non-feedback circuits, and by combining high-precision C and R elements, ultra-wide band and high precision are realized. The circuit consists of 16 ultra-low noise Hi gmFET and 30 transistors per channel. The MC head amplifier uses carefully selected 16 ultra low-noise Hi-channel and 18 transistors (per one gmFET).","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PRA-6000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pra-6000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-pm-655":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥98,000. A PM series integrated amplifier that pursues the music of the source by improving its own naked characteristics and minimizing NPB. Even if loudspeaker impedance is drastically reduced, stable power supply is always possible even if a major threshold occurs in phase. Low NFB is achieved by increasing naked characteristics, and the frequency characteristics from 1 Hz to 150 Hz are cleared in the range of 12-20 dB. The protection circuit provides unique high-speed electronic protection. This circuit continuously monitors current and time, and stops operation immediately before the hazard area. This method prevents sound quality deterioration without using relay on the output side. By adopting the inverter darlington method, the driver step is constant voltage drive.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM 655 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm655.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ha-md-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥52,000. System component Wing series integrated amplifier. Flat panel design using stainless steel leaf switch is available. FEATHER TOUCH OPERATION is used in the operation section. You can operate the function selector and volume control UP/Down. You can choose the sound quality of your choice from 6 modes. Equipped with a CD player terminal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-MD 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-md5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥49,800. A record player with a thorough reduction of vibration and resonance. V.C.ME tonearm This tonearm is a structure that creates fine voids inside the pipe by making stainless steel pipes particulate by chemical processing. Unitorque motor is used for the mechanism part. The torque generated from these two coils and magnets is very constant and stable.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/hitachi-ht-500.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-500.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-500.JPG"}},"hitachi-ht-l-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥45,000. Record player with linear tracking method and program repeat mechanism. The arm is equipped with a linear tracking arm where the needle tip is the same linear movement as the record cutting machine. In addition, the arm has improved its followability by the romans dynamic arm and gimbal suspension with an effective length of 95 mm. The drive motor is powered by a thin Unitorque motor developed by Rodi's proprietary Unitorque motor. With a program repeat, you can play repeats as many times by setting the start and end points of the repeat. Microcomputer controls all auto-in, auto-return, auto-cut, arm-in-out, arm-up-down, program repeat, auto-size and auto-speed detection mechanisms. The velocity detection method is adopted by a non-contact optical sensor to detect returns at the end of the performance. It prevents extra burden on mechanisms and needles. It is equipped with a contactless auto-size and auto-speed detection mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-L 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-hta-3000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥46,800. A tuner amplifier that combines an amplifier and a tuner. It is designed with an emphasis on operability and feeling of operation, and each switch is considered. Equipped with LED signal indicator. Equipped with a microphone mixing circuit and a loudness switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Hitachi HTA-3000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Lo-D-HITACHI/amp/hta-3000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-e-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥39,800. Equipped with a microphone mixing circuit and two tape terminals.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-E 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-e5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-x-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥75,000. Equipped with linear transmission and mounting performance. It is almost the same configuration as A-X77, which is the upper model. MC, MM, DC servo, equalizer and Dynamic Super A power amplifier. Isolate drive circuit is inserted between pre-drive and power stage. This circuit is a type of impedance conversion circuit that uses FET characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-X 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-a-x-55.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x55.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x55.JPG"}},"jvc-a-x-77":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥110,000. Equipped with linear transmission and mounting performance. MC, MM, DC servo, equalizer and Dynamic Super A power amplifier. Isolate drive circuit is inserted between pre-drive and power stage. This circuit is a type of impedance conversion circuit that uses FET characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-X 77 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x77.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-a-x-77.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x77.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x77.JPG"}},"jvc-l-e-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥51,800. Fully automatic player with linear tracking system. The full automatic mechanism of microcomputer control enables automatic detection of record size, and the rotation speed is automatically selected. It is also possible to change arm manual feed by soft touch and rotation speed. Tonearm is equipped with a high rigidity arm of romans, straight, integrated with cartridge. This arm is plug-in type, you can use MC cartridge with arm pipes sold separately by simply changing the pipe. There is no need to adjust needle pressure. The coreless DD motor series eliminates DC motor specific vibrations. The combination of high-precision FG speed detection realizes accurate rotation, and the pitch control of ±2.5% is also equipped. Equipped with an infinite repeat device.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC L-E 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-l-e-3.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e3.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e3.JPG"}},"jvc-ql-y-55-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥75,000. The record player tonearm with the same function as the advanced QL-Y77F has the same electronic control ED servo tonearm. This arm controls horizontal and vertical movements with microcomputer and two coreless linear motors. In addition, you can freely control the Q-dumping and anti-scaling of needle pressure marking and low frequency resonance with separate volume control knob. In particular, the electron Q-dumping is a structure that converts arm vibrations to electrical signals and transmits them to microcomputers, and suppresses vibrations by giving back torque to linear motors. It suppresses arm vibrations due to various external disturbances as well as low frequency resonance. In addition, there is no mechanical friction, so it does not damage the sensitivity of the bearing. ED servo tonearm, adopted by QL-Y55F, has been improved, and servo gain has been increased to 5 times more than conventional. Soft-touch switch enables full automatic operation and optional selection. The arm part adopts the arm pipe exchange method, and the bearing block connector can replace the cartridge by pipe and enjoy the grade up.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC QL-Y 55 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y55f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-990":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥79,800. Equipped with DLD (Dynamic Linear Drive) circuit. The DLD circuit is a structure with two amplifiers: low power amplifier and high power amplifier. It handles most of the signal with a low power amplifier of 0.001% or less. The high power amplifier also has fewer heat generation and fewer internal losses because the peak signal is only a short moment. In addition, the Σ drive method is used to improve performance with the input terminal of loudspeaker. This method reduces the deformation of the waveform in the input terminal of loudspeaker and drives loudspeaker with faithful waveform. The layout of each block is reviewed and each stage is arranged according to the flow of the signal. In addition, B-class and A-class are shielded with large heat dissipator in power amplifier. ICL high GmFET differential input and IC are available for equalizer amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-990 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-990.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-02-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥550,000. Trio’s two loudspeaker drive theory combined with a unique dynamic linear drive circuit. Dynamic power supply with stable output for low impedance loads and the ability to control loudspeaker. It is equipped with a dynamic linear drive circuit that combines the Σ drive theory that guarantees performance with loudspeaker input terminals. The dynamic linear drive circuit has two amplifiers: low power amplifier and high power amplifier. In addition, the high power amplifier operates only a short moment when the peak signal passes while maintaining low distortion, so there are few internal losses. This eliminates the sacrifice of the quality at the middle and small level, which was a problem with high power amplifier, and realizes high sound quality from small output to large output. In addition, the trio’s unique Σ drive system reduces distortion during the loudspeaker implementation and realizes high damping factor even at the top of the loudspeaker program. The equalizer amplifier is equipped with a unique dual-head equalizer that replaces the difference circuit and negative feedback (NF) element of input cable for MC cartridge and MM cartridge. For MC cartridges with low output impedance, input circuit by casscode load with bipolar trans, and MM cartridge with relatively high output impedance are used for different input circuit by casscode load with Hi-gmFET.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-02 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-02a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kyocera-r-851":{"more":[{"t":"Here is another receiver made during the transition from quality made audio to cheap black plastic audio. Yeah, I know that’s a generalization but it holds true for most of the audio market as it moved into the 1990’s. This Kyocera R-851 is a very interesting receiver. I actually had one of these for a while along with its companion CD player and tape deck. It may not look like much in the pictures but it really is a beautiful piece of equipment. It is rated at 85 watts per channel which is most likely a conservative rating. It retailed for around $850 when it was introduced in the mid 1980’s. In the early 1980’s Kyocera (a contraction of Kyoto Ceramics) purchased a company named Cybernet which propelled them into the audio manufacturing industry. I owned a Cybernet amp and tuner at one time as well.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Kyocera R-851","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/kyocera-r-851","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/kyocera-r-851.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/kyocera-r-851","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/kyocera-r-851-knobs.jpg"}},"luxman-c-05":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1983 at ¥380,000. A preamplifier that uses a single-stage amplifier along with the M-05. The C-05 employs a class A symmetrical push-pull operation in all stages of the head amplifier, equalizer amplifier and flat amplifier, making it an amplifier circuit with extremely stable open-loop characteristics. The C-05 uses a single-stage amplifier developed from duo-beta technology. Luxman's original duo-beta circuit combines an appropriate amount of NFB for sound quality with a DC servo that tightens the sound image from outside the audible band. In addition to improving performance in the open loop before applying NFB, a small amount of NFB is applied to improve the performance not only in pursuit of characteristics but also in music reproduction performance. This duo-beta circuit eliminates the need for high open-loop gain, which is required when applying a large amount of NFB, and realizes a single-stage amplifier configuration without the second stage amplifier, thereby simplifying the circuit. The adoption of a single-stage amplifier realizes two epoch-making improvements. In conventional amplifiers, the second amplifier stage is an amplifier circuit with a reference to the power supply. Therefore, the power supply used as the reference for amplification fluctuates due to changes in the input signal, and the music signal is modulated.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman C-05 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/c-05-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-c-05.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/c-05-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/c-05(1).jpg"}},"luxman-l-400":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1982 at ¥59,000. This is an integrated amplifier of the Revolver series with duobeta technology. The power amplifier section is equipped with a duo-beta circuit, and high sound quality is achieved by DC servo which tightens the sound image from the appropriate NFB over the whole band and from the ultra-low band outside the super-band. Built-in high-gain MC equalizer. The tone control is equipped with a turnover frequency shift tone control. The amount of change and the amount of change and the frequency at which it begins to change, making it possible to adjust sound quality naturally and effectively to the audibility.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-400 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-400-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-410":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1982 at ¥79,000. This is an integrated amplifier of the Revolver series with duobeta technology. Duo-beta circuit / S of one stage amplifier is installed in the power amplifier section. DuoBeta Circuit / S is a general term for three technologies. It is a single-stage amplifier that achieves low distortion while maintaining an open loop by setting the amplifier circuit to only one stage. It is a duobeta circuit that combines an appropriate amount of NFB over the entire band with a DC-servo that tightens from the ultra-low band out of the audible band with respect to the amplifier circuit. It is equipped with a power supply circuit plusX that provides a stable braking force with a margin of power supply. The single-stage amplifier is stable enough to eliminate the need for high-frequency correction due to phase shift because there is little high-frequency distortion. The duo-beta circuit is free from all of the circuits in the amplifier except for the limits of the elements. The plusX power supply circuit is free from the ground power supply circuit, and the SN ratio is improved by being free from the adverse effects of power supply noise.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-410 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-410-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-430":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1982 at ¥99,000. This is an integrated amplifier of the Revolver series with duobeta technology. Duo-beta circuit / S of one stage amplifier is installed in the power amplifier section. DuoBeta Circuit / S is a general term for three technologies. It is a single-stage amplifier that achieves low distortion while maintaining an open loop by setting the amplifier circuit to only one stage. It is a duobeta circuit that combines an appropriate amount of NFB over the entire band with a DC-servo that tightens from the ultra-low band out of the audible band with respect to the amplifier circuit. It is equipped with a power supply circuit plusX that provides a stable braking force with a margin of power supply. The single-stage amplifier is stable enough to eliminate the need for high-frequency correction due to phase shift because there is little high-frequency distortion. The duo-beta circuit is free from all of the circuits in the amplifier except for the limits of the elements. The plusX power supply circuit is free from the ground power supply circuit, and the SN ratio is improved by being free from the adverse effects of power supply noise.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-430 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-430-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-530":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1981 at ¥165,000. integrated amplifier with DUO β circuit / S. Uses DUO β circuit / S which eliminates the pre-drive stage of the power amplifier circuit. A low-noise FET parallel push-pull input is received by a differential cascode and connected to the parallel push-pull output of the R. E.T. (ring emitter transistor) to realize an amplifier circuit with excellent bare characteristics such as SN ratio and distortion factor. By using parallel push-pull R. E. T. with high-speed switching characteristics for the output stage of the power section, the class A operation range is expanded to 15W, and the class AB maximum output is 120W/ch. The heat sink uses a Sky-Fin type heat sink with high heat radiation effect.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-530 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-530-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-05":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1983 at ¥490,000. Stereo power amplifier with twin monaural configuration. In the circuit system, true class A operation by the direct method of fixing bias current is adopted, and a large output of 105W + 105W is realized. In addition, by adopting a large heat sink block of original design and a fan with low operating noise, high quality power is obtained with plenty of margin. The M-05 uses a single-stage amplifier developed from duo-beta technology. Luxman's original duo-beta circuit combines an appropriate amount of NFB for sound quality with a DC servo that tightens the sound image from outside the audible band. In addition to improving performance in the open loop before applying NFB, a small amount of NFB is applied to improve the performance not only in pursuit of characteristics but also in music reproduction performance. This duo-beta circuit eliminates the need for high open-loop gain, which is required when applying a large amount of NFB, and realizes a single-stage amplifier configuration without the second stage amplifier, thereby simplifying the circuit. The adoption of a single-stage amplifier realizes two epoch-making improvements. In conventional amplifiers, the second amplifier stage is an amplifier circuit with a reference to the power supply.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman M-05 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/m-05-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-rx-103":{"more":[{"t":"Luxman is known for making extremely good looking and performing audio equipment. Especially their early amps and receivers. However, this Luxman RX-103 receiver may be one of the strangest looking stereos ever made. It’s like some weird two-faced hybrid receiver – part silver face with knobs and part black face with push buttons and digital displays. Luxman called it eye-catching and I guess they weren’t wrong. To each their own, though. Some may find it beautiful. Introduced by Lux Corporation of Japan in 1982 and probably made for export only, it retailed for about $1000, which was a pretty hefty sum back then. It was also Luxman’s first foray into the digital aspect of audio.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Luxman RX-103","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/luxman-rx-103","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-rx-103.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/luxman-rx-103","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/12/luxman-rx-103-controls.jpg"}},"marantz-pm-420":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥45,800. integrated amplifier that can check all functions with fantastic LED display. There are 2 kinds, gold and silver.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-420 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm420-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-520-dc":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥59,800. Stereo integrated amplifier with 5-band graphic equalizer. There are 2 kinds, gold and silver.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-520 DC (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm520dc-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sr-1100":{"more":[{"t":"A slim design FM/AM stereo receiver with an emphasis on usability and smartness. The amplifier section uses a power amplifier block of Low-TIM design with DC amplifier configuration. In the tuner section, a dual gate MOS FET with excellent noise removal performance is mounted on the front end to obtain excellent reception performance. In addition, it is equipped with a tuning guide using LED and a pilot canceler that make it easy to find the optimum tuning point. It is equipped with functions such as loudness and high filter, microphone mixing circuit, FM muting switch and LED indicator.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SR-1100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sr1100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-bl-10-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥99,800. A belt drive player system developed by Micro to return to the origin of the player. The turntable uses hydroxy special aluminum which has excellent sound characteristics. In addition, high-pressure casting method avoids the occurrence of internal distortion during molding, so it is hard to cast in low pressure to maximize the goodness of the material. It is set to the maximum 7mm in this class based on the result of hiring the turntable plane. The turntable shaft adopts the micro original oil bath type turntable shaft to achieve smooth rotation. The belt drive method adopts the belt drive method, and the belt adopts carbon-contained ur material with low deterioration over time. Tonearm uses a static balance tonearm developed for BL-10X. This arm adopts a knife edge type for vertical bearings, and it realizes high sensitivity by using high-strength special stainless steel. In addition, by tuning the pipe holder part to the optimum balance weight with the knife edge, it accurately follows the movement of the sound groove and realizes clear sound quality without distortion.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki BL-10 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/bl-10x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-bl-101":{"more":[{"t":"This is an armless player that pursues higher perfection by introducing various technologies such as the direct coupling method which gained a reputation in RX 5000 and BL 111. The vibration mode is thoroughly analyzed by the Structural Dynamic Analyzer, and Micro's unique direct coupling method is adopted. In this method, the shaft assembly of the turntable and the arm mount are completely integrated with the connecting frame, the vibration circulation system is in phase, and the turntable and the arm do not cause any phase shift due to vibration, enabling more accurate tracing. In addition, this integrated structure makes the vibration circulation system as short as possible and increases the rigidity, minimizing the conversion loss when the cartridge converts the vibration energy from the sound groove into an electric signal. The turntable section uses special aluminum for the main turntable (305 mm diameter) and zinc for the sub turntable (180 mm diameter), and adopts a double turntable system in which the surfaces are firmly joined by three screws. The joint surface has a flat surface by high-precision polishing which Micro boasts. This double structure dumps the main turntable's squeal and improves the playback sound by adding weight to the sub-turntable and increasing the moment of inertia.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki BL-101 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/bl-101-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-tokyo-japan-bl-77":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥80,000. Armless record player with a mechanism and parts suitable for the new generation of micro. BL-77 is armless type, and tonearm can be replaced to develop the system. Arm mount base comes with one A-1700 series. This base is made of brass and weighs 1.5kg. A belt drive method is used for the driving method. The drive side adopts outer rotor type brushless servo motor, and the ur material which contains carbon material with low aging change is precisely processed by 8mm width and 0.45mm thickness. The shaft adopts 16mm diameter stainless steel. Oil bath method is used for lubrication, and smooth rotation is realized. Turntable is 3.2kg (3.2ing sheet) weight.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki Tokyo/ Japan BL-77 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/bl-77.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"mitsubishi-dp-ec-8":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Mitsubishi DP-EC 8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-ec8-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/mitsubishi-dp-ec-8.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-ec8-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MITSUBISHI-DIATONE/player/dp-ec8.JPG"}},"onkyo-pl-33":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo PL-33 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/player/pl-33-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/onkyo-pl-33.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/player/pl-33-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/player/pl-33.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-66-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥69,800. Full automatic player with front loading type that can also be selected for elevation. The full auto mechanism is equipped with one-track selection function. For example, you can cancel the listening song from the second to the fifth track, and then jump to the song you want to hear. This function is realized by optical dual-eye sensor and microcomputer that detects between the tracks of the record board. Dual-i-sensor is a new mechanism of pioneering using two. In addition to this, it is possible to accurately drop the needle while servo is applied to the center between songs by linking with the horizontal DD motor for the arm drive of computer control. Front loading method is available. In this method, the slider with turntable and tonearm can slide forward and set the record. There is no need for space to open the cover like a conventional record player, and the cabinet has a strong design that can withstand the loading of 40 kg, so it is possible to stack the amplifier and tuner, and it is possible to make the layout more free.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-66 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-66f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-66-f.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-66f.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-66f.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-x-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥39,800. Front-loaded full automatic player. The front loading design of the 21cm depth enables installation and stacking on narrow shelves. MC cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-X 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-x7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sa-05":{"more":[{"t":"A sound mixer / integrated amplifier that combines the functions of a mixing amplifier with those of a general integrated amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SA-05 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-05-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sa-05.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-05-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/sa-05.JPG"}},"pioneer-sx-9":{"more":[{"t":"A surround speaker system that can be used for various purposes such as surround sound. A 8.7 cm full-range cone type unit has been adopted. Midship mount system is used to reduce excess vibration from the baffle. A unique horn shape bass reflex duct has been adopted to improve directivity and reduce wind noise. The surround level can be adjusted with the Low/High sound pressure switch.","s":"audio-database.com"},{"t":"The Pioneer SX-9000 receiver was introduced in 1970 and was on the market until around 1973. It was one of Pioneer’s premium receivers at the time. It produces 50 watts per channel into 8 ohms. While it had all of the standard features of high end stereos of that era it also incorporated what some feel was a marketing gimmick – a reverberation amplifier. More on that later. The SX-9000 is a very nice looking stereo. It’s front panel is clean and uncluttered. This is because most of the controls are hidden behind the hinged, flip-down door running along the bottom of the front panel. Flip down the panel and you’ll find controls and connections for headphones, Bass and Treble, Reverb, Filters, Muting, Loudness, Tape monitor, Balance, Mode, and Mic.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SX-9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x9-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-9","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-9000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"quad-34":{"more":[{"t":"A preamplifier with the same basic configuration as 44 but with a different number of input terminals. Equipped with tilt control and base control, it can respond to changes in characteristics depending on the listening room and speakers. The tilt control adds gradual changes throughout the frequency band without changing the overall level. The base control consists of a LIFT position and a STEP position. The LIFT position is used to smoothly increase the low-frequency characteristics of small speakers, and the STEP position is used to cut howling when speakers are installed on walls or corners. The QUAD34 has phono inputs, tuner inputs, tape inputs, and auxiliary inputs. MM and MC can be used for phono input by changing modules. In addition, matching with the cartridge can be handled by replacing the module. There was a separately sold wood case named sleeve.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Quad 34 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/QUAD/amp/34-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/quad-34.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/QUAD/amp/34-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/QUAD/amp/34.JPG"}},"quad-405-2":{"more":[{"t":"Improved stereo power amplifier based on 405. The 405 / 2 is based on the 405 and has been improved to greatly increase the driving capability against load fluctuation. To solve the problems caused by the normal load line protection circuit, the QUAD has its own protection circuit, which smoothly reduces the abnormal current to within the safe operating range of the transistor and protects against short circuit. It is also integrated with the speaker protection circuit, which prevents the speaker from being destroyed by the trouble inside the amplifier. A current damping circuit developed by QUAD is adopted. This circuit consists of a single-output, small-power pure class A amplifier that amplifies voltage and supplies power for small signals, and a push-pull circuit with complete class B operation called a damper circuit. For small signals, current is supplied from the small-power pure class A amplifier to the load, and when the signal level increases, the damper circuit operates to supply a large current to the load. The low-power pure class A amplifier always detects and corrects errors between input and output signals and cancels all distortion at the output stage. In addition, it has low power loss, eliminates the need for idling adjustment, temperature compensation, and offset adjustment, and has excellent stability over time.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Quad 405-2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/QUAD/amp/405-2-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sae-x-10-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥380,000. X-series slim stereo power. The basic design concept is the same as the X-25A/X-15A, but the output is different. The X-Series introduces dynamic loading theory that aligns loudspeaker temples on all circuit design bases and is designed to deliver the best performance for both amplifier and loudspeaker when used. Thornton type A grade amplifier is available in the output stage. This circuit was developed to be a modern A-class amplifier that seeks the benefits of the A-class amplifier and completely disseminates its shortcomings. The name comes from the name of the Chief Engineer, B.Thornton. The design of the circuit was warmed up early in SAE, but at the technical level of the semiconductor industry at that time, it was not possible to develop a good power diode for this circuit, and it was not practical. Constant voltage bias keeps the gain linearity and keeps the output linearity by maintaining the minimum current level required by constant controlled current sources. In addition, all open-loop processes achieve stable A-class operation while gaining a large output.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE X 10 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/x-10a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sae-x-15-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥520,000. X Series Stereo Power The basic configuration is the same as X-25A, but the output is different. The X-Series introduces dynamic loading theory that aligns loudspeaker temples on all circuit design bases and is designed to deliver the best performance for both amplifier and loudspeaker when used. Thornton type A grade amplifier is available in the output stage. This circuit was developed to be a modern A-class amplifier that seeks the benefits of the A-class amplifier and completely disseminates its shortcomings. The name comes from the name of the Chief Engineer, B.Thornton. The design of the circuit was warmed up early in SAE, but at the technical level of the semiconductor industry at that time, it was not possible to develop a good power diode for this circuit, and it was not practical. Constant voltage bias keeps the gain linearity and keeps the output linearity by maintaining the minimum current level required by constant controlled current sources. In addition, all open-loop processes achieve stable A-class operation while gaining a large output.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE X 15 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/x-15a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sae-x-25-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥750,000. X-Series Stereo Power The X-Series introduces dynamic loading theory that aligns loudspeaker temples on all circuit design bases and is designed to deliver the best performance for both amplifier and loudspeaker when used. Thornton type A grade amplifier is available in the output stage. This circuit was developed to be a modern A-class amplifier that seeks the benefits of the A-class amplifier and completely disseminates its shortcomings. The name comes from the name of the Chief Engineer, B.Thornton. The design of the circuit was warmed up early in SAE, but at the technical level of the semiconductor industry at that time, it was not possible to develop a good power diode for this circuit, and it was not practical. Constant voltage bias keeps the gain linearity and keeps the output linearity by maintaining the minimum current level required by constant controlled current sources. In addition, all open-loop processes achieve stable A-class operation while gaining a large output.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – SAE X 25 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/x-25a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sae-x-25-a.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/x-25a.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SAE/amp/x-25a(1).jpg"}},"sansui-au-x-11":{"more":[{"t":"This master integrated DC amplifier was developed in pursuit of the ideal form of i-Integrated Amplifier and by putting all sound technologies into it. Super FF & diamond differential circuit is adopted for the power stage. The Super FF system is a combination of NFB and feed-forward, and theoretically cancels any distortion generated in the power stage. The structure of this system is that the distortion is reduced by NFB, and the distortion component is extracted after the pre-drive stage by its distortion component detection function. The distortion cancellation signal is amplified by the error collection amplifier forming the feed-forward circuit in the same way as the red signal circuit, and the two signals are synthesized at the output. In addition, the summing point is matched by the adoption of accurate and stable summing network. The diamond differential circuit has a structure in which transistors are arranged in the shape of a diamond, and the current margin of the drive stage can be made infinitely large to realize the high-speed response of the drive stage. The equalizer amplifier uses a low-noise, high-gm dual FET and a diamond differential circuit to enhance sound quality. In addition, a DC servo configuration is adopted.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-X 11 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-x11-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-xr-q-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥59,800. XR-Q7II is a full automatic player with MC cartridge. This reduces the rotational vibration level of the cabinet by absorbing the reaction between motors and eliminates the screw thread vibration. FF (Friction Free) coreless motor is used to solve the problem of conventional coreless motor. This motor stator is made of non-magnetic, and the yokelower for forming a magnetic circuit is fixed on the left side. Because of this, the suction force between the stator and the magnet is not working by rotating exactly the same as the magnet of the rotary, and the bearing has no pressure other than the weight of the rotation. In addition, since the yokelower forming a magnetic circuit is rotated with a magnet, it is possible to operate ideally because it does not generate magnetic histeresis or eddy current. In addition, using a linear drive method with a sign wave that can minimize torque swelling, smooth rotation is measured. This FF coreless motor removes the turntable and rotates it by hand to make it smoother and smoother than the conventional coreless motor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui XR-Q 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/player/xr-q5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-fl-77":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥49,800. Fully automatic linear tracking player with biotracer. Biotracer is used tonearm for electronic control. The linear tracking method uses a speed sensor to detect subtle arm tracking errors and feedback to drive motors to reduce the tracking errors by up to 1/10. Linear BSL motor is used for the rotation system. With the start button, the turntable part is stored and a full auto mechanism is available. You can also use the manual by pulling the turntable part. The repeat operation is equipped with a quick repeat mechanism to resume playing immediately from the head of the record board without arm back to the position of the game. Automatically select the record size and use the photoelectron disk size selector tonearm accurately leads. In addition, tonearm is equipped with a safety mechanism that does not hurt the needle tip even if you press the start button without setting the record board.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-FL 77 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-fl77.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-110":{"more":[{"t":"The Technics SA-110 is a low budget receiver that debuted in 1983 for $160. Its rated output is 20 watts per channel with total harmonic distortion of 0.5%. It has a small profile at around 17 inches wide, 10 inches deep and only 4 inches high which makes it easy to place on a smaller desk or shelf. The SA-100 isn’t great looking and has a somewhat sterile look, but it was more than likely designed to perform its basic functions well rather than look flashy. Some have called it ‘sleek’ but I’m not sure about that. The front panel of the Technics SA-110 is fairly minimalist due to the lack of features. There are separate bass, treble and balance sliders on the left of the panel. The FM muting/Mode button works a little strangely. Muting only works on FM and when in the Stereo mode muting is on all the time.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Technics SA-110","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-110","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1000-mk3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥500,000. Turntable system that combines tonearm EPA-100mk2 and turntable base SH-10B5, centering on turntable SP-10mk3. Turntable adopts low-speed electronic rectifier brushless DC motor with huge startup torque, and realizes the maximum 16kg/cm startup torque for technics as a consumer device, and the turntable of 10kg is 0.25 seconds and the rotation angle is 30 degrees. The stop mechanism is equipped with mechanical brakes and electronic brakes which instantaneously operate the reverse-ro driving circuit, which stops table turn in 0.3 seconds. In addition, it is possible to switch instantaneously by actuating an electronic brake circuit from high speed to low speed by a huge start torque from low speed to high speed. Aluminum die-casting and copper alloy double-layered turntable ensures a weight of 10kg and achieves the iner mass of 1.1ton/cm2. The motor’s rotary magnet is integrated with turntable, and the unique integrated direct-drive is used to make the rotation characteristics stable. to detect the rotation speed. By obtaining high-precision F.G. By adopting the quartz synthesizer method, pitch control of ±9.9% is possible at 0.1% step.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1000 MK3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1000mk3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥34,800. Linear tracking player with technics player technology on a compact LP jacket size. arm is equipped with linear tracking arm to line the record board. In addition, the arm bearing structure is a four-point support gimmal suspension system with pivot and ball bearing, and the dynamic balance method that matches the center of the arm rotation axis is adopted to realize stable trace driving without strict horizontal adjustment and needle pressure adjustment. The cartridge adopts the MM cartridge which is plug-in connector used for SL-6. In addition to the ease of installation, the cartridge and arm performance matching are realized. DC servo belt drive This is a full automatic electronic control type that aggregates all operations into four buttons. All operations can be done with the top cabinet closed. The number of rotations is automatically set according to the record size by just tapping the start. It is also possible to perform repeatedly by arm forward and re control and repeat button. Arm auto-return after playing.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥54,800. Jacket-size linear tracking DD player with automatic selection of any program up to 10 songs. All of the basic operations are electronically controlled, and all the operations related to recording are fully automated. From the setting of the rotation speed to the lifting of the needle, all operations are completed just by setting the record and clicking the start button. 10 songs are equipped with automatic selection mechanism. LEDs on the touch panel and on the top are lit and the program can be easily checked. In addition, while playing, the LED of the song number display flashes, and lets you know how many songs are playing. In addition, it is designed to not program even if the button of the number of edited songs is incorrectly pressed to read the number of songs of records automatically. You can change the program freely before the start button. After the start of the program, press the stop clear button to cancel the program and the arm will auto return.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-6.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-dl-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥49,800. Linear tracking full automatic direct-drive player with excellent basic performance and operability in a slim body. The motor structure and drive system adopts two-phase full-wave drive system flat-to-face slotless DC motor. cartridge is a plug-in connector type MM cartridge that adopts all- ated core to magnetic circuit. A simple operation unit is integrated into four keys. In addition, automatic detection of record size and rotation speed is also performed. arm It is equipped with a dial scale for driving position check.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-DL 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-dl5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1982 at ¥24,800. A jacket size integrated amplifier with a compact body of 315 mm width and 43.6 mm panel height. Equipped with Super Bass to improve heavy bass reproduction. By using a bridge-type MFB, it automatically detects the fo (lowest resonance frequency) of the speaker and enhances only the frequency near that point. Compared with conventional loudness and tone control, it can improve the bass playback of small speakers without artificially enhancing the middle and high frequencies. It uses a unique direct connector, and simple wiring is possible when connecting to ST-3, SH-E5, RS-5, etc. High-efficiency heat radiation design allows for additional tuner mounting. It has a slim body and uses a thin OI power transformer with low vibration and low leakage flux. It is equipped with an electronic short-circuit protection circuit to protect the amplifier from speaker short-circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-3-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥34,800. Slim compact body integrated amplifier with 315 mm width and 43.7 mm height. It uses a bridge type MFB and is equipped with a super base that enhances the low frequency range. Since only fo is emphasized, the medium and low frequencies are not enhanced unnaturally compared with the conventional loudness and tone control. Even small speakers can enjoy heavy bass playback. SLPT is used for the output transistor to realize low distortion and wide and flat frequency characteristics. It uses a unique direct connector, and no pin cord is required when connecting to a 315 mm wide tuner ST-5 or graphic equalizer SH-E5. Uses a slide-type volume. It is equipped with an electronic protection circuit to protect the amplifier and speaker from overcurrent.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1982 at ¥52,600. 315 mm wide jacket size integrated amplifier. It adopts a new class A system using a synchronous bias circuit unique to Technics. The synchronous bias circuit always keeps the output stage active by supplying a constant bias current to the output transistor to eliminate switching distortion. In addition, the new class A is independent of the signal path and bias current, so it is coupled with the action of a fast response diode with nearly ideal square characteristics to eliminate crossover distortion. Equipped with a high-precision large power meter that can read directly from 0.001W. It is equipped with a super base that automatically detects the fo (lowest resonance frequency) of the speaker and enhances the point. The volume is a slide-type volume. Equipped with electronic protection circuit. A unique direct connector is adopted, and no pin cord is required for connection of ST-5 and SH-E5.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-7-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-su-7.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-7-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-7.JPG"}},"technics-su-v3":{"more":[{"t":"New Class an integrated amplifier with linear feedback circuit. It is equipped with a linear feedback circuit that realizes theoretical distortion = 0. This circuit forms an independent feedback circuit that enables infinite amplification in the NFB loop. It theoretically realizes an amplifier that performs ideal operation with theoretical distortion = 0, pure gain without influence of elements or power supply, and speaker drive without influence of back electromotive force or wire. Switching distortion is eliminated by a synchronous bias circuit unique to Technics. In order to obtain high efficiency, the output stage is always kept active by supplying a constant bias in synchronization with the pause cycle to each of the + side and - side output transistors which are alternately paused in the class B and class AB operation. This eliminates switching distortion caused by the pause of the output stage. In addition, since the signal path and bias current path are independent, the output stage can always maintain an appropriate operating point. Together with the function of a fast response diode with ideal square characteristics, crossover distortion is eliminated.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v3-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v5":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier uses a new class A system and consists of three main elements: a synchronous bias circuit that eliminates switching distortion and crossover distortion, a linear feedback circuit that achieves 0 theoretical distortion, and an attached power block that virtually eliminates high-frequency distortion caused by electromagnetic radiation. The linear feedback circuit forms an independent feedback circuit to enable infinite amplification in the NFB loop, and theoretically realizes ideal operation such as theoretical value distortion = 0, pure gain without influence of elements and power supply, and speaker drive without influence of back electromotive force and wire. Switching distortion is eliminated by a synchronous bias circuit unique to Technics. In order to obtain high efficiency, the output stage is always kept active by supplying a constant bias in synchronization with the pause cycle to each of the + side and - side output transistors which are alternately paused in the class B and class AB operation. This eliminates switching distortion caused by the pause of the output stage. In addition, since the signal path and bias current path are independent, the output stage can always maintain an appropriate operating point. Together with the function of a fast response diode with ideal square characteristics, crossover distortion is eliminated.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v5-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v9":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥125,000. an integrated DC amplifier equipped with a new class A method and linear feedback circuit as a top-of-the-line model of the new generation V series integrated amplifier. The power amplifier class A system has been adopted for the power amplifier section, and low distortion and high power have been obtained by synchronous bias circuit, linear feedback circuit and concentrated power block. The basic circuit configuration is a push-pull complimentary service configuration for all stages from the first stage FET differential amplification, current mirror load and bootstrap configuration to the third stage Darlington. Bare distortion is reduced thoroughly. The power transistor uses a large power type of Pc200W to achieve high power and low distortion stable operation. The linear feedback circuit is a circuit that returns to the ideal of NFB theory and assumes that the naked amplification degree of the amplifier is ∞. By forming an independent feedback circuit that enables the naked amplification degree of the amplifier to be ∞ in the NFB loop by making the best of the multiple feedback circuit technology, the theoretical value of distortion = 0, pure gain without the influence of elements or power supply, and speaker drive without the influence of back electromotive force or wire.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v9-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"thorens-td-147":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥150,000. A belt drive-type record player with long-term tolerance technology. We use our own belt drive method. This method provides a very stable rotation because the motor rotation is fixed voltage. Turntable and tonearm are floated from the player's body using the spring, and the high S/N and howling margin are realized by separating motor and external vibration. tonearm is equipped with TP16 which is also used for TD126mkIIIC. In TP16, we have a basic way to remove unnecessary weights from tonearm to achieve low-activity mass. In addition, no lateral balance correction is required. By arming the characteristics of straight arm with high strength and accuracy, the joint part of the head tube is installed near the rotation of arm. The tonearm tube also has a special surface treatment with split-wave technology that absorbs unnecessary resonance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Thorens TD 147 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/THORENS/player/td147.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"toshiba-sy-88":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥180,000. The preamplifier is not just a good element, but a preamplifier that has been thoroughly pursued by developing elements that match the circuit. Newly developed V-type induction film capac. And the metalized film is rolled as a positive and negative electrode, and the vibration is reduced by crushing it flat. By narrowing the width of the electrode and the electrode, the electrical resistance is reduced, and it is a robust structure even for impedance. In addition, the vibration mode is simplified to wind the film homogeneously for mechanical vibrations, and electrical noise is difficult to trigger. SY-88 focuses on Phono playback to simplify the function as a result of pursuing sound quality thoroughly. The linearity of the high-voltage value of ±60V is improved along with the output stage and low distortion rate is achieved.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Toshiba SY-λ 88 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AUREX/amp/sy-88.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-ql-a-95":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1982 at ¥170,000. Tonearm uses a pipe-replacement method to replace the special high-rigidity material Romans tapered straight pipe and universal S-shaped pipe. The tapered straight pipes are not only optimized for low frequency resonance, but also have high stress against twists and wrinkles, and less electrical contacts for signal systems. In addition, the headshell part has been carefully treated. In addition, S-shaped pipes are also resonated with vibration-proof material enclosed and type chucking lock head connectors. We use the unique high sensitivity and high stability virtual one-point support structure of Victor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor QL-A 95 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-a95.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-ql-y-33-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥59,800. Fully automatic player with unresonant and non-vibration technology. Fully automatic mechanism of contactless electronic control is available. A record-size auto-sensor is equipped to detect the presence or absence of a record and the size of the record by light, and the microcomputer automatically selects the rotation speed and descends the arm to the specified position. In addition, since the rotation speed corresponds to a special record, it is possible to change the rotation speed manually. When you want to start playing from the middle of a record, you can move arm freely. Tonearm is equipped with electro servo straight arm. This arm directly connects the linear motor to the horizontal rotation axis, and the microcontroller accurately controls the full auto operation. Therefore, there is no mechanical noise of arm drive, and it does not damage the sensitivity of the bearing or trigger resonance. In addition, the electron Q-damping system has a function to push the peak of ultra-low resonance (fo) that occurs horizontally with microcomputer control.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor QL-Y 33 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y33f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-4d":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier developed using Yamaha's amplifier technology. In the equalizer section, a differential input by FET is used for the first stage and a low-noise, wide-band IC operational amplifier is used for the last stage. This eliminates the input capacitor which adversely affects sound quality. In addition, MC cartridge can be used by gain switching method. The tone preamplifier uses the Yamaha negative feedback (NF)-CR type to reduce sound quality degradation, and the negative feedback (NF) attenuation MIX type eliminates clicks near the center. The power amplifier uses a differential-input hybrid IC for the voltage amplifier stage and a discrete two stage Darlington SEPP-OCL circuit for the power amplifier stage. Equipped with a microphone mixing function. By adding auto-level control (ALC) to a high-sensitivity FET-input microphone amplifier and adopting a balanced mixing circuit, excellent sound quality can be obtained. In addition, the source and microphone levels can be and recording effects such as fade-in and fade-out can also be controlled.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Yamaha A-4D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/YAMAHA/amp/a-4d-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-6a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥69,800. ZDR circuit and X power supply The power amplifier has its own ZDR to eliminate the distortion that occurs at the end of the program. This detects only the distortion component that occurs at the end of the amplifier, and by adding it to the input side with the same gain, the absolute amount of distortion generated at the end of the amplifier is zero. In addition, there is no harmful distortion such as crossover distortion or thermal distortion, and the distortion caused by the speaker is canceled. Icolyzer is equipped with a pure ca servo servo amplifier. This method idealizes the amplifier operation so that the signal current (current) does not flow into the power supply line or the earth line. The X power supply method has a power supply capacity equivalent to a small but large power supply. DISC switches are equipped to always select DISC (record) regardless of the position of the selector. Rec Out selector and loudness circuit","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-6a (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-6a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-a-6a.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-6a.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-6a.JPG"}},"yamaha-a-7a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥96,000. Equipped with a new ZDR (zero distortion rule). ZDR, a unique cancellation technology, is installed to zero all the distortions of the end of the amplifier. In principle, the distortion detection circuit and the addition circuit are made of two. In the end, the distortion component is removed by the bridge configuration, and the distortion is returned to the input side to zero. Ikoliza A servoifier is an original Pureka servo amplifier. This protects the equalizer from the effects of L, C and R components of power supply and wiring, as well as non-linear due to current changes. In addition, in the 47kΩ position of the Phono switch, the capacity switch of 220pF and 330pF is newly added, and it can be used to enjoy the exact matching and sound quality change with cartridge. The power supply unit has a unique X power supply. This X power supply uses high-speed feedback from the secondary side of power supply to the primary side.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-7a (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-7a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-a-7a.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-7a.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-7a.JPG"}},"yamaha-b-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥135,000. Power supply power A ZDR is developed and mounted with a distortion detection circuit and input addition circuit to completely eliminate the distortion that occurs at the end. The distortion detection circuit detects only the distortion component in taking complete bridge configuration. It also detects distortion caused by reverse power from loudspeaker. In addition, since the element of this bridge is pure resistance, there is no distortion of this part and the accuracy is very high and stable. In addition circuit, distortion component is added as floating bridge circuit from floating power supply to power stage input part.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-50.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-bx-1":{"more":[{"t":"Pure ka servo servo amplifier We have developed a Pureca servo servo amplifier that does not affect the sound quality. Because the power supply line always flows constant current, it realizes zero element sensitivity that does not affect power supply such as non-linear due to power supply and wiring L, C, R component and current change. In addition, since there is no signal current on the earth, it is difficult to understand ground impedance and low frequency crosstalk is improved. BX-1’s basic circuit configuration is composed of high-speed positive 0dB gain buffer, high-speed inverted 0dB gain buffer, and two completely identical neulinear waves A-class power amplifiers with a circuit. It is composed of three kinds of 4 amplifiers and mono power amplifiers. In the circuit operation, the high-speed positive amplifier and the high-speed reverse amplifier create high-precision equilibrium signals, input two power amplifiers of exactly the same configuration, and extract them as floating output. In this circuit, the output current from the amplifier is always absorbed to the other amplifier. For this reason, to be a constant DC current that flows through the common power line does not depend on the output signal, two amplifier power supply current waveforms must be completely similar to the output current without distortion.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha BX-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/bx-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥105,000. Preamplifier with Pure Current Dam and New Linear Wave Fa. The C-50 circuit is a pure A-class system made by the New Linear Polarizer, a DC configuration, and a unit equipped with Pure Current Dam, which is the development of Pure Current Servo. 6dB amplifier · Tone preamplifier · amplifier amplifier each unit amplifier adopts Pure current servo's development type Pure current dam. Only DC components flow. With this, each unit amplifier is blocked from power supply at low AC, and the current change of the earth line is also suppressed. In addition, this Pure Current Dam operates without the need for bypass current, so it is efficient and excellent power supply method. The new linear circuit fa circuit is installed in the unit except buffer amplifier and amplifier amplifier. In this circuit, the voltage drop of the emitter resistance between two elements is always constant, and the current with no same distortion is supplied from power supply. This eliminates the influence of current distortion caused by the gm of the element that could not be avoided by conventional bias circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-50.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥170,000. Preamplifier with Pure Current Dam and New Linear Polarizer. All C-70 components are DC or DC servo. In addition, the A-class system by the New Linear Wave Fa and Pure Current Dam are equipped. The circuit configuration is MC/MM independent equalizer amplifier -0 dB buffer - volume amplifier - inverted amplifier. All units except tone control and amplifier amplifier are equipped with Pure Current Dam. In Pure Current Dam, a semiconductor inductance and a large capac in line with power supply cut off nonlinear components that flow into the power supply line in several Hz. The power supply line has only direct current components, and each unit amplifier is interconnected from power supply. In addition, because the current change of the earthline is also suppressed, each has the same effect as having independent power supply. The new linear wave circuit is mounted on the output stage of each unit amplifier except buffer amplifier and amplifier amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-gt-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥99,800. A record player who inherited the technology obtained in GT-2000 and made high C/P. Turntable is a high precision turntable made of aluminum die-cast with a weight of 3kg in 36cm diameter. Achieved iner mass of 600kg/cm2, coupled with 400g SBR sheet with good orption. A direct drive method using DC coreless hole motor with 1.2kg startup torque and cm is available in the drive unit. By adopting the quartz PLL method, it realizes rotational accuracy of 20ppm or less of crystal oscillation level. The motor shaft that supports turntable is 10mm diameter. arm support adopts a virtual one-point support gimbal support arm. It realizes elimination of gutter and a horizontal/vertical initial sensitivity 7mg. The arm is a S-shaped light heavy arm made of aluminum and has a long arm with an effective length of 262mm. The arm reduces S-shaped uneri and reduces horizontal tracking errors in a narrow range.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha GT-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/gt-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-gt-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥138,000. Turntable is made by hot forging method. In addition, GT-2000 has enlarged the diameter of 374mm to make inertial moments huge. Inertial moments are the same weight, the larger the diameter, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight, the greater the weight. The motor adopts DC coreless hole motor which is not included in ko in principle with the start torque 2kg and cm. The servo system realizes a positive and negative servo that can measure the torque of each opposite direction at the time of acceleration and de ration. It shows a sharp response to subtle load ctuations, and absorbs the occurrence of rotation uneven.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha GT-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/gt-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-p-700":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥44,800. Full automatic player with full-scale MC type cartridge. MC-101 The motor part adopts direct drive method using DC 4-phase 8-pole coreless hole motor. In addition, the servo method has a quartz PLL servo method. BMC is available in cabinet. Fully automatic mechanisms such as auto-reed-in, auto-return, auto-cut and auto-repeat.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-p-700.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-700.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-700.JPG"}},"accuphase-c-222":{"more":[{"t":"Released March 1983. As a successor to the C-220, whose production was terminated in 1980 due to the unavailability of major components, this preamplifier focuses on disc playback while improving input terminals and functions. The circuit configuration of the equalizer amplifier and high-level amplifier consists of differential input via FET buffer, pre-drive by cascode and final by Darlington. All stages are push-pull. As a result, the element characteristics before NFB are improved and high quality is achieved. The head amplifier for the MC cartridge has a configuration in which a dedicated flat amplifier is inserted in front of the equalizer amplifier. The circuit configuration is directly input without the FET buffer. Low-noise elements are carefully selected. At the same time, the impedance of the NFB loop is reduced to prevent noise generation. The MC head / N of the signal system is greatly affected by the noise of the constant voltage circuit of the power supply in the MC head amplifier section, the elements of the constant voltage power supply section are carefully selected and a thorough low-noise design is applied.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-222 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-222-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-e-303-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1983. This is a new generation integrated stereo amplifier with consideration for the playback of digital sources such as PCM and CD, based on the development technology and materials cultivated in high-grade separate amplifiers. The output stage employs a triple push-pull configuration with six MOS FETs, allowing a sufficient margin of P D (maximum drain loss power) of 600W. In the whole power amplifier section, the pre-stage is a differential push-pull, the next is a cascode push-pull, and the pre-drive by two transistors is a MOS. The FET is driven. Cascode is a circuit method used in high frequency amplification circuits of tuners. It does not cause mirror effect at high frequencies and has excellent high-frequency characteristics. The MC head amplifier, equalizer amplifier, high-level amplifier and power amplifier are all directly connected to each other to achieve high reproduction without coloring. The problem of DC drift caused by direct connection is solved by stabilizing each unit amplifier with DC servo. The equalizer amplifier consists of a differential input through an FET buffer, a pre-drive cascode, and a final stage Darlington.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase E-303 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/E-303X-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-266":{"more":[{"t":"Released March 1983 at ¥220,000. This is a stereo power amplifier using MOS FET, which was created by the development technology of AccuPhase cultivated over many years. Four types of power amplifiers are available: stereo power amplifier, class A stereo power amplifier, monaural power amplifier and class A monaural power amplifier. Unlike bipolar transistors, Power MOS FET (Metal-Oxide Semiconductor Field Effect Transistor) has no charge storage, so it has excellent high-speed switching characteristics. It does not generate notching distortion even in high frequencies, and it can obtain excellent distortion characteristics over a wide band. Since it is a voltage-controlled device, power amplification can be performed only by applying a signal voltage to the input gate. Compared with bipolar transistors, which require a large signal power, a low-power device is sufficient for the drive stage at the front stage, and excellent devices can be selected. Moreover, since it is a high-gain element, the number of amplification stages can be reduced, and stability can be improved by simplifying the signal path. Since the temperature coefficient of the high-current region is negative, if the current of the element increases abnormally for some reason, the temperature of the pellet will rise sharply, and the negative temperature coefficient acts in the direction of reducing the current, and the temperature will decrease to prevent the destruction of the element. There is a self-defense function.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-266 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-266-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released April 1983 at ¥650,000. A stereo power amplifier developed in pursuit of the ideal power amplifier for the new era. To compensate for the large output with continuous operation, the output stage consists of 14 wide-band transistors with a Pc (collector loss) of 200W per channel, 7-parallel push-pull, providing a power capacity of 2.8 kW. It is possible to drive a low load of up to 2 Ω even under normal operating conditions. However, a Low Load Impedance Operation switch is provided to drive with even lower impedance for commercial use. This switch allows a large current to be supplied while maintaining the safety of the output transistor, so that an output of 450W/ch can be obtained for a 1 Ω load. The drive stage that drives the output stage is composed of a MOS FET for power amplification. It performs low-impedance large-current drive and significantly improves high-frequency characteristics. Since the thermal characteristics stabilize the bipolar transistor, the bias current of the output stage is stabilized. As a result, the emitter resistance of the output stage can be lowered.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-600-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-21-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥42,800. Full automatic player with electronic control tonearm. The turntable drive is a linear drive motor drive using DENON’s proprietary magnetic record detection method. Also, the control circuit adopts a newly developed microprocessor, which ensures the rotational performance by DENON quartz by both directions servo. The newly developed microprocessor drives horizontal operation and lifter operation with two separate dedicated motors, enabling manual use of arm horizontal operation and lifter operation during performance. In addition, the contactless structure ensures excellent arm sensitivity and operability, without being mechanically restrained during auto-mechanical operation. In addition, the electronic servo lifter is used to keep the upper and lower arms at a constant speed without being disturbed such as the smallest and ambient temperature of the needle pressure. Tonearm is equipped with a dynamically straight arm with an electronic needle pressure applied method. The torque of the vertical drive motor is always used to determine the appropriate needle pressure. The needle pressure can be increased and decreased by the operation of the volume control.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-21 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-21f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-35-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥49,800. A full automatic player with a dynamic servo tracer. DP-45F has improved cost performance by omitting some functions. Tonearm is equipped with an electronic arm, a dynamic servo tracer. This arm inherits DP-100M pure electronic arm and damping mechanism. In general, the Q damping mechanism is only horizontal in this class, but the dynamic servo tracer also has a vertical Q damping mechanism, which effectively controls the arm vibration caused by too high low frequency resonance Q, and pursues more purity music reproduction by improving low frequency output and crosstalk failure. In addition, Q damping control volume control is specified for a wide range of cartridges. arm has a light weight straight arm. The full automatic mechanism is equipped with electronic contactless full automatic mechanism by microprocessor control. Tonearm has a contactless structure that does not affect arm sensitivity or rotational system. Built-in quick repeat mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-35 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-35f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-52-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥89,800. Full auto player equipped with dynamic servo tracer and MC cartridge. Adopts a full auto mechanism. The tone arm is driven by a non-contact structure that does not affect the tone arm sensitivity or rotation system, and smooth operation is achieved by microprocessor commands. In addition, it is designed for safety. When there is no record on the turntable, the tone arm does not operate, so there is no trouble of needle tip. In addition, by the adoption of electronic servo lifter, it is not affected by temperature and needle pressure, etc., and the tone arm shows up and down movement at a constant speed, and the impact between the needle tip and the record is minimized. With the full auto function, when you press the Start button, the sensor automatically detects the size and rotation speed of the record (33 1/3 rotation for 30 cm, 45 rotation for 17 cm) and the performance starts. In the case of a record such as a 45 rotation disc for 30 cm records, you can respond by pressing the Start button and then pressing the specified rotation speed button. The tone arm is equipped with a dynamic servo tracer light mass straight arm.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-52 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/player/dp-52f-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-67-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥95,000. The automatic lift player adopts the dynamic servo and tracer, and has a thorough anti-vibration measures. Tonearm is equipped with an electronic arm, a dynamic servo tracer. This arm inherits DP-100M pure electronic arm and damping mechanism. In general, the Q damping mechanism is only horizontal in this class, but the dynamic servo tracer also has a vertical Q damping mechanism, which effectively controls the arm vibration caused by too high low frequency resonance Q, and pursues more purity music reproduction by improving low frequency output and crosstalk failure. In addition, Q damping control volume control is specified for a wide range of cartridges. Tonearm has a light weight straight arm (PCL-67) and S-shaped arm pipe replacement method. In addition, the lateral balance generated when the end detection is replaced with a S-shaped arm with an auto lift machine, and the end detection point is automatically switched electronically during pipe exchange. Turntable is a thick turntable table of about 2 times. This turntable is almost equal to the weight distribution from the center to the outer circumference.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-67 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-67l.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-790":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥178,000. an integrated amplifier designed for digital sources with strong construction centered on a non-feedback 0 db power amplifier. Equipped with a non-feedback 0 db power amplifier that eliminates negative feedback loops. This system is an application of the non-feedback technology developed in POA-8000, and uses a direct distortion servo circuit. The direct distortion servo circuit compares the input signal with the signal obtained from the output side (main signal + distortion component) to detect only the distortion component, and then applies the inverted phase of this distortion component to the input side. This action drives the static distortion into the 0 region, and the noise appearing at the output side of the amplifier is treated as a difference from the input signal and is removed in the same way as the distortion component. As a result, there is no signal feedback and no time delay, so the dynamic distortion which affects the auditory quality is suppressed. In addition, since there is no NFB circuit, it is not affected by the back electromotive force from the speaker, so the increase and generation of the distortion when the speaker is connected are suppressed. In the PMA 790, the direct distortion servo circuit, which is the core of the non-feedback system, has been thoroughly polished and the slew rate of the circuit itself has been improved in order to be compatible with digital sources.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-790 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-790-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pra-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥100,000. The first step is to load the current mirror circuit, and the code boots circuit that works to the effect t system for the rise of the signal source impedance has been added to match the inside and outside cartridge. The preamplifier output has a non-return buffer amplifier, and the signal is sent out in the optimal condition to the load amplifier. Flat amplifier is composed of high speed OP amplifier and ultra low noise FET differential amplifier. Cascode boots circuit is added to the first stage to prevent distortion caused by initial volume control. In addition, tone control circuit is formed by incorporating tone control element into the return circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PRA-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pra-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-hk-825":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥125,000. phono stage circuit is equipped with dualAAAA equalization circuit. This has improved transient characteristics compared to the general negative feedback (NF) type while clearing three elements of sound quality, S/N ratio and dynamic range. High thru rate of 120V/μs is realized. In hk825, the signal line is integrated into the pattern, and there are no lead wires. In addition, the MC head amplifier is designed to be turned on and off by the push-pull solenoid relay, and the touch panel has a self-cleaning method.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 825 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk825.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-hk-870":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥125,000. Stereo power that improves dynamic output such as HICC (current supply capacity). In order to enhance the HICC, hk870 aims to make power supply and power stage low impedance, which enhances driving capacity during low impedance. The HICC Mechanism acquires 60A supply capacity. Equipped with a proprietary protection circuit. This circuit is composed of pure electron circuits and is constantly monitored over current and time, and all circuits are stopped immediately before the risk area. In addition, the output side does not use relays that cause sound degradation. The Otara Circuit is adopted, and it has been all possible measures against dynamic distortion such as TIM, PIM, and IIM.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 870 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk870.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-pm-660":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥118,000. A660 PM660 was awarded '82HI-FI GRAND PRIX' by AudioVideo magazine. This also supports the impedance of loudspeaker, which changes every time by input signal. In pursuit of a shallow NFB and a broadband as possible, we have introduced an inverter darlington connection to improve open-loop characteristics. 70μV high sensitivity MC amplifier In addition, the MM4 position is set to switch the cartridge capacity load.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM 660 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm660.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-pm-660.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm660.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm660.jpg"}},"harman-kardon-hk-590i":{"more":[{"t":"The Harman Kardon HK-590i was produced in 1982 and the design differed quite a bit from HK’s earlier receivers. It featured a digital synthesized quartz locked FM tuner and 45 watts per channel. It measures 17.5″ W x 13″ D x 5.5″ H inches. Harman Kardon was started by two men – Dr. Sidney Harman and Bernard Kardon in 1953. They are credited with bringing true hi fidelity equipment to the general public. Harman Kardon is still very active in the audio and home theater market today but it is of course the older vintage components that most collectors are after. While the 590i and other i series receivers aren’t in great demand they still have a fairly loyal following. Prices range from $100 to $300.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Harman Kardon hk 590i","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/harman-kardon-hk-590i","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-hk-590i.jpg","xc":0,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/harman-kardon-hk-590i","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/08/harman-kardon-hk-590i-2-1.jpg"}},"hitachi-ha-md-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥52,000. Achieve a graphical display of sound quality. It is equipped with a centralized display panel using a FL tube, and graphically displays the state of function, volume control, and sound quality control. The tone control state is stored by a microcomputer. In this function, you can reproduce the level adjustment state with one touch by memory by adjusting the level of High, Mid and Low. Up to 12 memory Microphone mixing is available. Fazer touch is available for volume control and function balancer. By adopting a microcomputer, operability is improved, the volume control is slow and the down is easy to use.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HA-MD 50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/amp/ha-md50.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-500-mkii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥53,000. Turntable This turntable is made of aluminum die-casting turntable and stainless steel plate. It has the ability to transmit harmful vibrations due to the friction of the two metals. The drive motor is powered by the Unitorque motor. It realizes stable rotation. In addition, we adopt a center shaft and roller bearings of 0.1μ-class roundness using ultra-precision processing technology. In addition, we have improved rotation accuracy by thoroughly reviewing servo circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-500 MKII (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-500mkii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"hitachi-ht-l-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥52,000. Front loading record player with program repeat function. With the front loading method, turntable slides to the front to set records. Tonearm uses a linear tracking method and traces the record with the same linear movement as the cutting machine. A thin Unitorque motor spindle. With the program repeat function, you can repeat your favorite sections up to 16 times. We use a full automatic computer control mechanism to control all the return detection on record size and speed performance. Auto-return by detecting record size and speed by simply tapping the start button. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-L 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/hitachi-ht-l-3.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l3.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l3.jpg"}},"hitachi-ht-l-33":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥37,000. Linear tracking player with a compact size of 32cm in width and depth. Tonearm is equipped with a linear tracking arm. Contactless optical electronic tracking error detection significantly reduces tracking errors. The arm has an effective length of 95mm, with the Roman dynamic arm and gimbal suspension. Program repeat function You can repeat any number of times by setting the starting point and end point optionally. Microcomputer control enables easy and smooth operation of auto-in, auto-return, auto-cut, arm-in-out, arm-up-down mechanism and program repeat mechanism, auto-size and auto-speed detection mechanism. In addition, it is an operation method that does not put extra load on linear mechanisms and needles such as contactless auto size and auto speed detection mechanism, and speed detection mechanism by contactless optical sensor. Mute Switch Manual priority operation is free.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-L 33 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l33.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/hitachi-ht-l-33.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l33.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l33.jpg"}},"hitachi-ht-l-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥57,000. Linear tracking player with front loading type. The front loading method that turnstable is placed forward by the switch operation. Because of this, there is no dust cover and it is possible to overlay the same as other equipment. A series of floating operations, such as front cover and turntable horizontal movement, are all performed by microcomputer control. The arm is equipped with a gimbal suspension linear tracking arm that the needle tip makes the same linear movement as the record cutting machine. This arm has excellent follow-up and significantly reduces tracking errors and in-side force, especially tracking errors have about 1/20 of traditional swing arms. Unitorque motor is used for the drive motor, and stable rotation is realized by applying a that almost does not receive the influence of voltage ctuation and overtime temperature change. With the program repeat function, you can auto-repeat many times by setting the start and end points of the repeat. Equipped with a contactless auto-size and auto-speed detection mechanism, it detects the size and speed of the record by simply clicking the Start button and automatically plays.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Hitachi HT-L 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LO-D/player/ht-l5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-x-900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥79,800. Dynamic Super A and Gm Circuit The Victor's original Gm circuit is available. In addition, when listening with a small sound, the unnecessary gain is cut with a Gm selector. These circuits reduce noise levels by up to 25dB. In addition, the dynamic super A is used to achieve both the sound quality of the A-class amplifier and the high efficiency of the B-class amplifier. The equalizer amplifier adopts dual-slope DC servo's ultra-low distortion rate circuit, which brings out the performance of the MC cartridge. Also, the power distortion of power supply is eliminated by the powerant lock power supply. Low impedance power supply","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-X 900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-l-e-33":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥45,000. Full automatic player with 8 random selected 15 times memory. It is equipped with a linear tracking arm integrated with high power MC cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC L-E 33 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e33.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-l-e-33.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e33.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/l-e33.JPG"}},"jvc-ql-e-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥55,000. The linear tracking method of microcomputer control is available. The drive motor has a coreless type.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC QL-E 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-e55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-ql-e-55.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-e55.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-e55.JPG"}},"kenwood-ka-2200":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1982 at ¥158,000. Equipped with DLD (Dynamic Linear Drive) circuit. The DLD circuit is a structure with two amplifiers: low power amplifier and high power amplifier. It handles most of the signal with a low power amplifier of 0.001% or less. The high power amplifier also has fewer heat generation and fewer internal losses because the peak signal is only a short moment. KA-2200 is also equipped with a dynamic power supply by a powerful power supply section. It is possible to send 340W and 430W instant power at 230WΩΩ at 8Ω. In addition, the Σ drive method is used to improve performance with the input terminal of loudspeaker. This method maintains a low distortion rate of 0.003% even with the input terminal of loudspeaker. Multi power supply system is available to reduce circuit between circuits on each stage.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-2200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-2200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-03-a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥180,000. an integrated amplifier with a dynamic linear drive circuit. Equipped with a unique dynamic linear drive circuit to support digital audio. On the other hand, the high power amplifier works in the instantaneous input of large signals, maintaining low distortion rate even at full power, low heat generation, and almost no internal loss. In addition, the instant maximum output is 340W+340W with 4Ω load and 430W+430W with 2Ω load. We have a unique Σ drive system to drive loudspeaker system with signals that are similar to the input waveform of amplifier. When the waveform is observed in the input terminal of loudspeaker in general amplifier, the deformation of the waveform itself is seen far beyond the order of the distortion rate in the normal wire system. The Σ drive method improves this, not only the waveform transmission in the input and output terminal of the amplifier, but also the waveform deformation in the input terminal of the loudspeaker system using a few meters connection cable. Dual head equalizer","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-03 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-03a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-cl-40":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1983 at ¥330,000. This is the first preamplifier in Luxman that uses a GE vacuum tube. An S. R. P. P. (Shunt Regulated Push-Pull) output circuit is used for the equalizer circuit. This circuit uses a twin triode 7025/12AX7A with a Takamasu width-ratio, and sets an optimum operating point to improve performance. The flat amplifier uses a 2-stage direct-coupled differential-amplifier. The first stage uses a twin triode 7028/6BK7B with a Nakamashi ratio, and the second stage uses a twin triode 7026/6CG7 with a low amplification ratio.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman CL-40 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/cl-40-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-mq-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1983 at ¥300,000. This is the first Luxman tube ball type stereo power amplifier that uses GE vacuum tubes. The output tube adopts a push-pull configuration using highly reliable 6550A/X. The newly designed 6550A/X UL connection transformer, OY15-Z4K, is used for the output transformer. A bi-triode 7030/12AU7A is used for the first stage, and by configuring a differential amplification push-pull circuit with a negative power supply, the required gain is obtained while phase inversion is performed. The driver stage is a push-pull circuit using bi-triode 7024/6AQ8. In the output stage, a kind of bootstrap circuit is provided in the input circuit to increase the effective impedance of the input circuit so that the driver stage can drive the output stage sufficiently. The power transformer has a large capacity with a margin. In addition, as for the structure, the negative power supply at the first stage constant voltage to eliminate the influence of power supply voltage fluctuations.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman MQ-50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/mq-50-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-291":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥59,800. A full automatic player that pursues high performance with simple configuration. The drive system adopts direct drive method, and the drive motor adopts quartz lock DD motor. If the rotation speed reaches the constant speed, the green lock indicator is lit and expressed, so you can enjoy without worrying about the disturbance of the rotation speed. It detects all information such as the position of tonearm on the record, the position of the speed selector, and the size of the disk. It can also be used as a manual player by switch. LUXMAN MC cartridge is 320C.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-291 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd291.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-pd-350":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1983 at ¥240,000. A belt drive system is used to drive a belt drive system. It is driven by a super-aramid belt with a self-heavy 9.5kg and a turntable with a 1.2t iner mass. It is designed to use the vacuum unit VS300 sold separately. VS300 has PD350 power supply. arm base is sold separately, so you can choose tonearm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman PD-350 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/player/pd350.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-6-a":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier equipped with QuarterA system. In QuaterA, the bias current is fixed until a certain power level (30W for PM-6a) is reached and the operation is fully pure class A. When the power level is exceeded (from 30W to 120W for PM-6a), the operation is automatically switched to class AB. The switching is done purely electronically using a high-speed switching circuit newly developed by Marantz. The power amplifier section equipped with this QuaterA system is fully push-pull DC configuration with built-in DC-servo circuit, and excellent characteristics are obtained by the Low-TIM design that reduces transient distortion by improving bare characteristics and reducing NFB of the amplifier. Dedicated to the MC cartridge, it is equipped with a genuine headphone amplifier with 13 transistors per channel from the 4-parallel push-pull input stage with ultra-low noise transistors to the SEPP configuration output stage. The phono amplifier section uses Marantz's unique push-pull circuit configuration for all stages to achieve high SN and high dynamic range. In addition, the equalizer element uses a metal-coated resistor with an error of 1% and a polypropylene capacitor with an error of 2% to achieve excellent characteristics. Equipped with a TONE switch that can bypass the entire tone amplifier circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-6 a (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-6a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-84":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier equipped with Marantz digital support technology and designed for high sound quality with Quarter A and AVSS. A Quarter A circuit has been developed and installed on the PM-84 in order to achieve both high output, which does not clip even at high level, and quality at low output, which reproduces low level. This Quarter A operates in pure A class with excellent linearity for low level up to 1/4 (quarter) of maximum output, and moves to AB class at higher level to realize high power. Each operation achieves a smooth shift by controlling the bias current with a high-speed switch circuit. Equipped with an AVSS (Auto Voltage Shift Supply) that shifts the output supply voltage according to the power. The optimum output supply voltage allows the power element to operate in a region with minimal distortion and noise, etc., realizing high quality at all power levels from small output to large output. Moreover, improves stability by suppressing unnecessary temperature rise at low power. Designed for low impedance, it maintains power even when the speaker impedance momentarily fluctuates to an extremely low value. Equipped with a direct switch, power is directly connected to enable higher SN ratio and high-speed signal transmission.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-84 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-84-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-25":{"more":[{"t":"This Onkyo TX-2500 receiver is a low to mid-range offering from Onkyo with the TX-8500 being the big dog at the time. I’ve always liked the look of the Onkyo receivers – even the bolt on front dial glass. When all the bulbs work and they are lit up they have the warm glow of candle light. This particular TX-2500 is the MK II version which does differ slightly from the regular TX-2500. I believe the TX-2500 came out around 1976-77 and the revised MK II around 1978. The MK II had a retail price of around $360.00. Onkyo’s TX-2500 is listed at 27 watts per channel while the Tx-2500 MK II is listed at 40 watts per channel. Of course, the late 70’s were the height of the receiver wars where each manufacturer was trying to outdo the other with more watts per channel and other features. This is probably why Onkyo decided to up the ante with the power output.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-25","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-2500-mki","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-65":{"more":[{"t":"This is one of the less common receivers – the Onkyo TX-6500 MK II. It was made by Onkyo from around 1978 to 1981. They made a series of receivers with the entry level unit being the TX-1500. From there was the TX-2500, the TX-4500, the TX-6500 and the monster TX-8500. I believe they were 40, 60, 100, 160 watts per channel respectively. So, the TX-6500 MkII chimed in at 100 watts per channel. The TX-2500 and TX-4500 were Onkyo’s last ditch effort to survive in the audio market around 1977. They had originally entered the U.S. market selling speakers in a collaboration with Mitsubishi but that did not go well. So, they put everything they had into the development of their receiver line.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-65","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-6500-mkii","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-tx-85":{"more":[{"t":"Onkyo’s contribution to the Monster receiver genre is the Onkyo TX-8500. It was Onkyo’s top of the line receiver at the time and put out an under rated 150 watts per channel into 4 ohms and 110 watts per channel into 8 ohms. This line of Onkyo receivers including the TX-2500, TX-4500, TX-6500 and TX-8500 are all under appreciated units. The build quality, performance and features are all second to none. Onkyo was a little late to the scene with their monster receiver so it didn’t receive the fanfare that the Pioneer and Marantz receivers received at the time but it is easily comparable. A later MK II version was released that had a digital tuner along with the analog tuner. As you can see below it is fairly easily distinguished from the original TX-8500 shown above. The TX-8500 does not have an Aux input though it does have 3 Tape inputs so you shouldn’t be short inputs. The amplifier section is one of the best around and the tuning section is no slouch either.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-85","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-8500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-340":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥39,800. Full Auto DD Player. The corkidal suspension cabinet has improved the hauling properties. The drive motor adopts the DC servo and hole motor of high torque using the Pioneer original hole element. It is equipped with a front operation full automatic mechanism which improves operability. Tonearm's od operation is driven by a dedicated motor. Tonearm is equipped with a mass concentration method.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-340 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-340.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-340.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-340.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-340.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-505":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥49,800. Record player with full auto mechanism based on high sound quality design. The turntable drive motor features a coreless motor with no ko. This DRA is equipped with a sub-resonant with a moderate spring property damper and weight. It absorbs resonance by giving a positive opposite vibration against arm resonance. This makes it possible to pick up extra ingredients other than the sound groove at the needle tip, making it clearer. In addition, the arm material adopts carbon graphite, and the unique vibration analysis technology is formed into a high stability straight pipe. In addition to carbon fiber headshell and cartridge, the mass concentration method with the arm axis of the weight is used to make the whole pick-up system oscillation, high rigidity and non-resonance. The cartridge is a high output MC cartridge developed by the pioneer.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-505 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-505.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-55-fs":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥58,000. Front loading type DD full auto player. Front loading mechanism is available. In this method, the slider with fono motor and tonearm slides out to the front. This makes it possible to compact the audio system and make it easier to layout. The slider can be inserted with a touch key on the front control. The front door is automatically opened and closed according to the slider movement. The drive system adopts direct drive method, and the drive motor is equipped with a coreless motor of the SH/lower method. motor adopts coreless DC servo motor with coreless structure.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-55 FS (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-55fs.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-pl-55-fs.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-55fs.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-55fs.JPG"}},"pioneer-pl-707":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥59,800. PL-70LII, etc. The turntable drive motor adopts the coreless motor which combines the SH/lower method. By the SH/Router method and Quartz PLL with increased rotational accuracy of the bearing structure itself, the rotation mura is reduced. This DRA is equipped with a sub-resonant with a moderate spring property damper and weight. It absorbs resonance by giving a positive opposite vibration against arm resonance. This makes it possible to pick up extra ingredients other than the sound groove at the needle tip, making it clearer. Tonearm is powered by a dedicated motor with microcomputer control. In addition, the rotation speed change and rotation stop of the foro motor are controlled by a microcomputer, preventing malfunction.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-707 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-707.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-x-9":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥69,800. Front-loaded full automatic player. Program Selection This feature is controlled by optical dual-sensors and microcomputers, and can be heard in any order, up to 8 songs and 15 steps. The front loading design of the 21cm depth enables installation and stacking on narrow shelves. MC cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-X 9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-x9.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-50":{"more":[{"t":"The Pioneer SX-50 was introduced in 1983 and had a retail price of $380. It is a computer controlled stereo receiver and embraced emerging audio technologies, supporting TV audio inputs and also anticipating the rise of the compact disc. It pioneered multiple audio inputs and allowed switching between emerging formats like CD players and hi-fi videodisc soundtracks. Its forward-thinking design made high quality audio integration intuitive and uncomplicated. The SX-50 produces 50 watts per channel and has a very low rating of .007% total harmonic distortion. The sound is characterized as clean as opposed to warm and the tuner is adequate in areas of strong signals. It was part of Pioneer’s lineup that included the SX-40, SX-60, and the top of the line SX-V90 which came out a bit later. Here are the prices and power outputs of the models: If you’re into the retro 1980’s look then the Pioneer SX-50 probably looks cool to you. The numerous push buttons with different coloration and of course the large green vacuum fluorescent display give it a new wave look.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer SX-50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x50-e.html","lang":"en"},{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-50","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-50","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sx-50.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x50-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/speaker/s-x50.JPG"}},"sansui-au-d-707-g-extra":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥118,000. AU-D F Extra is an integrated amplifier with improved ground floating circuits and more. This circuit eliminates the influence of loudspeaker by using output amplifier and load ( loudspeaker) and power supply as a complete closed loop, and the supply power part is also floating configuration. Linear step MC cartridge is installed to support MC cartridge. This SN is powered by AU-D907F Extra. The power amplifier is equipped with a diamond differential circuit in the pre-drive stage and a super FF in the power stage.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 707 G Extra (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d707gextra.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-907-g-extra":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥178,000. AU-D907F Extra is based on ground floating circuit. Ground Floating Circuit This circuit was developed from the review of the amp ground circuit, and it has a complete closed loop for output amplifier, load (louspeaker) and power supply circuit. This minimizes IHM distortion that is harmful to sound quality. The power supply unit is equipped with equalizer / tone amplifier, power amplifier part pre-drive stage Lch, power stage Lch and Rch. Linear step MC cartridge is installed to support MC cartridge. In addition, special annealing suppresses the occurrence of distortion.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 907 G Extra (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d907gextra.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-b-2301":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥470,000. This high-grade stereo power amplifier was developed through analysis and technical challenges from a new point of view based on the technology and results accumulated in the integrated amplifier. The output stage adopts a newly developed four parallel configuration diamond power stage using eight Pc200W power transistors per channel, and the pre-drive stage adopts a cascode-connected push-pull configuration with improved high-frequency characteristics. The power supply section is equipped with a large toroidal transformer of 178x173x120mm. This transformer weighs as much as 12 kg and has a capacity of 1.3 kva. In addition, we have incorporated unprecedented know-how into the coil winding method and have taken into consideration the sound quality even with fillers. The power supply consists of a 60000 μ F pure focus capacitor for the power stage and a 40000 μ F pure focus capacitor for the prethe pre-drive stage with the transformer as the core. It is a six power supply system with independent stages and independent left and right channels. This supports high power with plenty of room and completely eliminates IHM, which is extremely harmful to sound quality. The chassis structure uses a sub-chassis made of pure copper to provide electromagnetic and electromagnetic shielding and vibration isolation through moderate internal loss.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui B-2301 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/b-2301-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-lx-22":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥25,000. Auto-player system with auto-return mechanism etc. Romans Straight tonearm is used to utilize a light needle pressure and high compliance type cartridge. MM cartridge VL-42G The rotation system is equipped with a linear BSL motor to achieve stable rotation performance. Arm Lifter Includes a disc centering guide to make 30cm LP board easy to board. Dust cover was sold separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-LX 22 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx22.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-lx-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥38,000. Fully auto player with linear tracking arm reduces tracking errors. Tonearm is a linear tracking method that reduces noise distortion caused by tracking errors. Plug-in shell connectors are available to replace cartridges designed for unified standards. In the cartridge, the MM type cartridge XL-250G is designed based on the standard of shell plug, self-weight and proper needle pressure. The rotation system uses a linear BSL motor which removes brushes and slots from the DC motor and suppresses mechanical torque changes called co. The optical electronic disk size selector is equipped with a safety design that automatically sorts the record board, leads in precisely, and does not drop when the record board is placed. It is equipped with a muting mechanism that eliminates noise when the record board and the needle tip are contacted.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-LX 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-lx55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-q-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥35,000. The size of the LP jacket is approximately two- rds. Fully automatic function with auto start and auto return. The straight tonearm series adopts the needle pressure marking method by dynamic balance type that does not change the needle pressure even if the player is diagonally placed. MM type cartridge The direct drive method is used for the rotation system. Also, the polarized motor is the same as turntable. It is equipped with a one-touch selector that combines the tonearm lead-in position switch of the 33-turn and 45-turn speed switch, 30-cm and 17-cm. With the built-in headphone amplifier, you can play records directly by connecting a stereo mini-p headphone.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-Q 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-q7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x-555-es":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥70,000. A full automatic player who pursues everything from all angles to the ideal of picking up all musical information en d in the sound groove. Equipped with Sony’s unique biotracer. This is a system that electronically controls all operations with speed, position detection sensor, and linear motors, which enables low frequency resonance peaks to be suppressed within 3dB even if any cartridge is installed. In addition, the sound quality such as the sound rise, the standing position, the dynamic range, and the distortion are improved. The arm is equipped with a linear tracking method. In order to make turntable quiet and smooth, we have developed advanced technology in the development of motor technology and control method. BSL motor is a multi-gap head that uses multi-gap heads to detect high-density magnetic detection signals on the table turn, which eliminates brushes and slots from the DC motor, and uses the high oscillation accuracy of the crystal to quickly detect minor rotational changes. MC cartridge (XL-333E) which can be replaced by a samarium cobalt 8-shaped coil is equipped as standard. The electronic needle pressure marking method can be adjusted by the volume control controller on the panel during recording.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X 555 ES (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x555es.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-22":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥29,800. Equipped with a sound effector with a display. Tone control is equipped with a sound effector that can be used with a single switch. In addition, you can control the detailed manual. Two tape terminals can be copied from tape 1 to 2. Power supply to sound mixer MX-22 is available.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 22 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax22.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-ax-22.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax22.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax22.JPG"}},"sony-ta-ax-44":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥48,000. Integrated amplifier to improve operability by microcomputer control by ASP IC. This does not cancel the power supply code and keeps it permanently. Power supply Capac capac Straight transmission using heat pipe is available. Equipped with audio muting, subsonic filter, and high filter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 44 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax44.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-ax-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥55,000. Integrated amplifier with CD direct function. The preamplifier and the power amplifier are equipped with the audio current amplifier model that electrically independently independently of the amplifier. In this way, we have almost ignored the effects of elements that have stained sound such as contact resistance of switches and connectors, and unique impedance of wire material. The power amplifier is equipped with a regat linear method.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-AX 500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-ax500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-555-es":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥99,000. Equipped with our unique technology, we are able to brush up the details at a low level and respond to digital sources. We use the audio current method to cut off between four amplifiers. By separating between L/R channels at the same time, the characteristics of each preamplifier, power amplifier, and L/R channels are pursuant to the ideal grounding. In addition, input signals and loads are determined clearly, and there is no influence of ground loops or power supply impedance, and the external disturbance of wires and switches intervened in the signal path is also ignored. Two-ter Linear Gain Control Attenuator is available for volume control. Because of this, the characteristics of actual use are good.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 555 ES (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f555es.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-777-es":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥185,000. In addition to circuit technology, the high-end model of the ES series is integrated with the concept of simple and straight music signals. The preamplifier amplifier output is converted to the current signal, and the linear gain control attenuator set at the end of the current conversion amplifier is converted to the voltage signal again. Therefore, the preamplifier part seen from the power amplifier has infinite impedance, and it has been completely separated electrically. This enables independent arbitration of characteristics for each arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary arbitrary al arbitrary ar arbitrary ar arbitrary ar ar ar arbitrary ar irrigative irrigative irrigative irrigative irrigative irrigation. In addition, by adopting the linear gain control method attenuator which can be used in the audio, current, and branching method, volume control is used to adjust the volume, so the impedance is reduced so that the actual volume control position has improved. The power supply of the preamplifier part adopts a constant current centre polarizer, which eliminates the influence of power supply and ensures stable regulation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 777 ES (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f777es.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-n-902":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥280,000. 3 years and a half years of age, using ears and sensitivity to carefully tune the three elements of the circuit-device mechanism. The TA-N902 can be used in two ways: stereo power amplifier and mono power amplifier. The switch is switched on the rear panel. The Sony’s unique distortion reduction circuit is designed to control the drive voltage to correct the linearity of the power stage and to operate the A class in most areas. We also pay attention to the power supply code and use the Starcad structure line with good transmission characteristics. By adopting the layout that exposed the heat sink externally, we are equipped with a power supply circuit design that can afford. In addition, the heat sink itself is made with a large and rigid aluminum die cast, and it is a strong structure base for the entire cabinet.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-N 902 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n902.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-v-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥32,000. Attached to the Liberty series. Equipped with microphone mixing mechanism with volume control. You can use one-touch stereo cable to facilitate connection with the components of the Liberty Series. Equipped with loudness switch.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-V 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-v3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-v-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥52,000. Equipped with slim design and sheet key. Self-illuminated sheet keys are used for function switches and tape monitor switches. Equipped with loudness and base boost switch. By adopting the screwdriver IC, high power is ensured while thin design. Equipped with a lighting indicator that indicates the use of graphic equalizer. We use semiconductor switches with less contact resistance to function and tape monitor switches. High efficiency power supply","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-V 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-v5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-v-5.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-v5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-v5.JPG"}},"sony-ta-v-7":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥70,000. A self-illuminated sheet key switch is available for function switches and tape monitor switches. Semiconductor switches are available with less contact resistance to function and tape monitor switches. It is equipped with a centralized display by FL tube. Equipped with a lighting indicator that indicates the use of graphic equalizer. power supply ON","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-V 7 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-v7.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-a-3-mk-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥500,000. New class A stereo power amplifier with a computer drive. By installing a computer drive circuit and introducing a microcomputer into the bias control of the signal system, transient distortion of the output stage is eliminated in real time, and high power low distortion rate is realized. Equipped with a plug-in power block, the output stage and power supply part are integrated with an ingenious structure to eliminate electromagnetic radiation that causes high-frequency distortion. The power supply is equipped with a 400 VA transformer for each channel and two 22,000 μ F (105 v) high-capacity capacitors. This fully monaural construction reduces interference between the two channels. The final stage is a 4-stage Darlington configuration using a Pc200W high-voltage transistor with 4-para connection and realizes high power. Equipped with a large peak power meter with high precision and instantaneous response, it can read directly from 0.0001W minute output to 1W without switching the meter range. Computer control is also used in purely electronic protective circuits to improve safety.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 3 MK 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a3mk2-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-a-5-mk-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥150,000. This is a stereo power amplifier developed with Technics's original technology as a power amplifier for the digital audio age. The output stage is a 3-stage Darlington configuration using high-voltage transistors of Pc150W connected by two pins, and a total of 1.2 kW Pc has been obtained. The power supply circuit uses a large transformer of 390 VA and a large capacitor of 80 V / 8200 μ Fx4, and is designed independently on the left and right sides to eliminate interference between channels. It is equipped with a power linear circuit unique to Technics. This is a development of linear feedback circuit technology. This effect is brought to the output stage of the amplifier, and linearity is dramatically improved, and distortion caused by low impedance load of the speaker at every moment is suppressed. It is equipped with a unique computer drive circuit and by introducing a computer to the bias control of the signal system, the output transistor, which repeats rapid temperature changes in response to changes in the music signal, is always driven at the optimum idle current (ICQ), eliminating transient crossover distortion. Equipped with a linear feedback circuit (LFB), which is an independent feedback circuit in the NFB loop that enables infinite amplification. It realizes theoretical distortion = 0.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 5 MK 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a5mk2.-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-se-a-5-mk-2.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a5mk2.-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a5mk2.JPG"}},"technics-sl-m-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥64,800. Quartz direct-drive Player System with a focus on basic performance. In addition, the drive unit has a brushless DC motor with a 1.5kg startup torque and a cm. The unique integrated direct-drive and quartz control ensure excellent characteristics. Tonearm is equipped with high sensitivity gimbal suspension tonearm, providing superior initial sensitivity of 7mg or less in all directions due to its high-precision bearing structure. A dynamic damping mechanism that greatly improves pick-up low frequency characteristics. By dividing damping weights in a spring and controlling the resonance of the pickup process with silicon oil and damping cylinder, low-fr ency resonance is suppressed and the mixed distortion is greatly reduced. The auto lift-up mechanism automatically increases tonearm when playing. In addition, the optical contactless method is used to detect the end of the record, and does not burden the arm or cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-M 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-m1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-q300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥49,800. Quartz direct-drive full automatic player with basic performance and operation performance. We have introduced quartz for rotation control, making full-fr ency detection F.G. and electronic circuit technology possible to achieve rotational accuracy within ±0.002%. The direct-drive The straight pipe tonearm is used to provide high sensitivity gimbal suspension for the bearing structure. Plug-in connector type MM cartridge With the full automatic mechanism, you can set the rotation speed and start playing with the start button. In addition, all operation buttons are layoutd on the front of the cabinet, and all operations can be done until the dust cover is closed. The upper and lower cabinets are composed of TNRC with excellent vibration absorption.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-Q300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-sl-q300.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q300.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q300.JPG"}},"technics-sl-qx-300":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥49,800. Full automatic pressure control with ±6% pitch accuracy. We use our proprietary Q.L.S. direct-drive turntable is used in the drive unit. Tonearm uses a zimbal suspension bearing structure, which combines four bearings with pivot and ball bearings to achieve high initial sensitivity of 7mg or less in all directions. Plug-in connector type MM cartridge You can also use conventional cartridges by changing headshell. The full automatic mechanism automatically detects the set record size, sets the rotation speed, and starts playing with the start button. The cabinet adopts precision aluminum die-casting and TNRC on the bottom base, which has excellent vibration resistance and vibration damping rate, and it is a double vibration damping structure with strong external vibration.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-QX 300 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-qx300.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-v-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥49,800. A vertical direct-drive full automatic player that can be installed in a narrow space. It has a linear tracking arm, which realizes stable trace performance by unique dynamic balance method. High accuracy rotation performance is realized by adopting integrated structure direct-drive and full-fr ency detection F.G. All operations such as arm up/down, forward/back control can be done until the dust cover is closed. Plug-in connector type MM cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-V 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-v5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/technics-sl-v-5.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-v5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-v5.JPG"}},"technics-su-a-4-mk-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥250,000. preamplifier equipped with amorphous MC step-up transformer. The phono equalizer circuit is equipped with an amorphous MC step-up transformer for the first time in the world. It achieves a wide bandwidth of 15 Hz to 100 kHz ± 0.2 dB and a high SN ratio of 82 dB at the MC input. In addition, the input sensitivity of Phono1 can be switched to a total of four levels: two MC levels and two MM levels. By making all stages A class operation, switching distortion and crossover distortion are eliminated. The circuit is fully DC up to the output terminal. Equipped with a SEPP buffer amplifier, it realizes an output impedance of 2 Ω and improves high frequency characteristics.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A 4 MK 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a4mk2-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-a-6-mk-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥100,000. preamplifier with wide D range design. The equalizer section is equipped with a low-noise ICL equalizer circuit of parallel FET differential and MC basic design. It employs a newly developed wide dynamic range volume that greatly improves the practical SN ratio. By combining a low-impedance volume with a high-performance drive amplifier, it prevents the SN ratio from deteriorating due to resistance changes. By installing a SEPP buffer amplifier, a low-output impedance of 2 Ω is realized, and there is no high-frequency degradation caused by the shield wire when the power amplifier is installed remotely. A newly developed low-distortion LSI for audio-only is used in the electronic switch for the input selector, which has succeeded in reducing distortion by nearly 20 dB compared with the conventional one. Moreover, audio and video signals can be separated on the printed circuit board, preventing degradation of audio signal quality. The four input jacks (video/aux1, TV/aux2, tape2/VTR, and tape3/DAtape) are connected to the video input jacks, and the video can be switched using the input selector. Equipped with video/aux1 inputs that can be used by switching the front / rear jacks.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A 6 MK 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a6mk2-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"thorens-prestige":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥1,600,000. The prestige can be equipped with two long/sh arms, but five different arm variations were included in the original system. A floating suspension method is used to shut out vibrations from outside that are harmful to music playback. This absorbs and damps the external vibration of the frequency band that affects the music signal. The belt drive method is used for driving. The belt drive method prevents knocking, vibration, and twisting of the motor body which is a problem with the direct drive method and directs to turntable. It also has the advantage that it can drive a large turntable with a quiet motor of small torque. In addition, there is also a characteristic that the phase error between the expected motor and turntable can be compensated by the elasticity of the belt when using the floating suspension method. The turntable part has a double turntable structure.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Thorens Prestige (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/THORENS/player/prestige.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"victor-ql-a-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥69,800. Record player with large turntable. Turntable is a large aluminum die-cast turntable with a diameter of 35cm, weight of 2.9kg (including mats) and iner mass of 560kg-cm2. In addition, DD motor is used to drive this large table. The magnetic support method reduces the load on the motor rotation axis to 500g with the magnetic suction force. The servo circuit is equipped with a double servo quartz circuit, which increases the stability of the quartz lock to 30 times. Tonearm has S-shaped universal type. The high-sensitivity and high-stable new gimbal bearings of Victor and long arms of effective length 254mm are combined to achieve smooth trace performance with less distortion and needle jumping. In addition, the S-shaped pipe has an anti-vibration material, and the arm base adopts a large aluminum die-cast base to make it unresonable and non-vibration. Equipped with pure electronic silent servo queuing function.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor QL-A 70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-a70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-101-m":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥1,000,000. Audio amplifier The best-in-class stereo amplifier with huge power and toughness of the studio amplifier. 101M is a complete twin mono structure that incorporates two mono amplifiers into one unit. The power stage is a new concept, including the power supply circuit, which enables low distortion to supply the power of the survivor. The power trans is made of 10 Pc200W metal case pieces, and it is based on 5 paras with ±70V operation. For this reason, while having a high-voltage operation capacity of ±120V as a whole power stage, 5 paras on the ±70V side can be sintered, and 4 paras on the ±120V side are not required to operate at all times, and the power stage is high enough. ZDR (zero distortion rule) is equipped to zero the occurrence of any distortion in the power stage. In addition, the main power supply is equipped with ±70V and ±120V according to the power stage configuration, and the real-time power supply control circuit is a method that enables the voltage to be higher if necessary.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha 101 M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/101m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥128,000. Dual amplifier Class A circuit The basic circuit configuration of A-1000 is the same as A-2000. It is the A-class power amplifier by DC servo negative feedback (NF)-CR type real-time equalizer with twin servoAA element configuration, richness circuit and DualAmp Class A with ZDR. If you turn off the Richness circuit and turn on the direct switch, pass the tone control circuit, etc. and connect to the pre-main directly. CD inputs are also designed with a focus on CD, and are directly input to the 150mV sensitivity amplifier via the function switch. This circuit is composed of A-weight amplifier and AB-weight amplifier. The load is connected with each output of A-weight amplifier and AB-weight amplifier, and NFB is connected from both ends of load to A-weight amplifier. As a result, the A-class amplifier is fully controlled by the load current, and the AB-class amplifier has only received power loss. This enables high-power A-class drives throughout the amplifier output. The Dual Class Class A circuit features a unique ZDR circuit (Zero Distortion circuit) for superior linearity.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥49,800. amplifier circuit technology such as ZDR circuit. 's own ZDR (Zero Distration circuit) circuit. This circuit is composed of two distortion detection circuits and additional circuits. The end of the circuit is to remove only the distortion component by the bridge configuration, and to suppress the occurrence of distortion. In the distortion reduction technology such as NFB, I returned something mixed with music signal components, but ZDR has the effect of suppressing distortion in principle by giving feedback only the distortion component. In addition, the distortion caused by the reverse current at the time of the loudspeaker drive is also zero in real time. This Pure Current Dam prevents signal current from flowing to earth and power supply lines by supplying constant current from power supply by Pure Current Dam.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-c-200-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1984. This stereo preamplifier was developed based on the C-200X and taking over the circuit technology of the advanced C-280. The circuit configuration of the equalizer and high-level amplifier employs a cascode A-class push-pull system with an FET buffer for direct connection to the input. The next stage is a cascode A-class push-pull and the output is a Darlington A-class push-pull. The cascode connection is characterized by low feedback between input and output and excellent characteristics, especially at high frequencies, high gain, linearity is maintained up to the operating limit of the element, distortion is reduced and S/N is improved, and excellent characteristics can be obtained. In addition, a Darlington A class push-pull is adopted for the output, and the input impedance can be raised, so that the operation of the preceding stage is hardly affected by the load, and the amplifier can be composed of low distortion factor and wide dynamic range. The head amplifier for the MC cartridge uses a full-scale method in which a dedicated amplifier is inserted in front of the equalizer amplifier. The circuit configuration consists of three stages: cascode differential push-pull, cascode push-pull, and Darlington push-pull. Since the signal level of the head amplifier is extremely low, S/N is improved by carefully selecting low-noise elements and designing the circuit with low impedance. Each unit amplifier is equipped with an IC-based DC servo circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-200 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-200L-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-e-302":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1984 at ¥220,000. Based on the development technology and element amplifierd by the high-end separating amplifier for many years, it is an integrated amplifier that reflects digital sources. There are two types of Champagne Gold E-302 and E-302B black color. MOS FET is the ideal element for low output impedance and high drive voltage. It is combined with low emitter resistance of the output stage, and has high quality output without notching distortion. The E-302 power amplifier is designed to support low impedance load, and the output stage Pc is a large power configuration of about 500W, and a large power supply of 700VA is available. All the units of each stage are directly connected from the Disc input. The equalizer amplifier is equipped with the MM and MC's necessity gain.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Accuphase E-302 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ACCUPHASE/amp/e-302.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-300-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1984 at ¥330,000. Based on the P-300X, this is the 4th generation stereo power amplifier of the P-300 series that has been improved by renewing the detailed circuit, materials used and construction. The output stage has a 5-parallel configuration with 10 transistors with a Pc (collector loss) of 100W. The total Pc is equivalent to 1000W. By mounting these on a large aluminum heat sink, sufficient heat radiation is achieved and a large output is achieved. By combining this high-power output stage with a powerful power supply, it is compatible with a low impedance load of 2 Ω. In addition, a non-switching distortion design is applied to improve the distortion at the time of small signal. Power MOS FET is used for the drive stage that drives the output stage, and it is composed of cascode push-pull with excellent high-frequency characteristics. In addition, the pre-drive stage that sends a signal to the MOS FET drive stage is also A-class cascode push-pull to improve the element characteristics. The input circuit constitutes a cascode bootstrap push-pull circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-300 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-300L-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-av-u8":{"more":[{"t":"AV amplifier with built-in 4-inch small monitor television. Equipped with a 4-inch monitor, it is possible to check back programs during recording and the contents of dubbing. Moreover, it is also possible to monitor audio by using headphones. Equipped with four audio and four video input jacks, you can switch between audio and video monitors, dub between videos, and dubbing audio sources to video. The power amplifier section uses a DC amplifier configuration. It is also equipped with a dynamic noise reduction system (DNR) that reduces hissing during playback by approximately 10 dB. In preparation for 2-language broadcasting, it is equipped with a mode selector mechanism that can select Japanese and foreign languages with one touch. It is equipped with a picture control mechanism that can adjust the image quality of the monitor television to your preference. In addition, it has a brightness volume that can adjust the brightness of the built-in monitor television.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Akai AV-U8 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/AKAI/amp/av-u8-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-37f":{"more":[{"t":"Released March 1984 at ¥54,800. A full automatic player with a dynamic servo trailer arm. DENON turntable is used in the turntable section. A stable rotation performance is realized by adding both directions servo to the combination of magnetic recording detection method and quartz lock. Tonearm is equipped with an electronically controlled contactless tonearm with a dynamic servo tracer. The dynamic servo tracer is electronically damping the low fre cies of cartridge compliance and tonearm, both horizontally and vertically. It effectively suppresses crosstalk deterioration and mixed distortion. The arm has a light weight straight arm. The cabinet has a mirror finish. DL-65 is used as a cartridge as a light self-weight cartridge with elliptic needle.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-37F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-37f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-poa-3000-z":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1984 at ¥380,000. POA-3000 is the latest high-tech model. A dual super non-return circuit that applied and developed non-return technology developed by POA-8000 etc. In addition, in servo amplifier A1, the distortion component is removed to the overall by comparing the input signal and output signal in the final output stage. This configuration achieves a low distortion rate (high frequency distortion 0.002%, mixed modulation distortion 0.0015%) that exceeds the NPB method while completely eliminating the negative return loop. In addition, there is no increase in distortion even at the time of the loudspeaker connection because of the NFB circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon POA-3000 Z (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-3000z.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-e-50":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥300,000. Acoustic measuring device that can accurately and easily measure the frequency characteristics of the audio system, transmission characteristics of the listening room, reverberation time, sound insulation characteristics, and noise levels. In particular, the resilience time can be automatically measured only by level adjustment and displayed digitally. It comes with a trunk case that is convenient for storing and moving. The microphone stand is sold separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-E 50 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/etc/ae-50.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-g-90":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥69,000. Compact integrated amplifiers that incorporate dynamic super A and Gm circuits used for advanced machines. In order to accommodate a wide range of digital sources, you can use the Gm circuit to increase the SN ratio and loudspeaker driving force at actual use. 7 input terminals","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-G 90 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-g90.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-a-x-1000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥129,000. Equipped with dynamic super A and all stage Gm circuits. From Phono equalizer to power amplifier, you can use Gm circuit to all signal circuits. For example, Gm equalizer is a Phono equalizer that combines the advantages of negative feedback (NF) type and CR type. It realizes transient characteristics that are difficult to obtain with negative feedback (NF) type and a broadband high S/N, low distortion rate and wide dynamic range that is difficult for CR type. by volume control element. This Gm circuit also improves noise levels at volume control positions at 10-25dB. In general, if the impedance of loudspeaker is lowered, the input impedance of the power stage is also lowered. However, the output impedance of the Gm driver is low enough, so it is possible to maintain the required drive power without interruption.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC A-X 1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/a-x1000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ql-y-66-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥85,000. A full automatic player that pursues the sound quality that is not inferior to the manual machine. Turntable is a large turntable table with a diameter of 35cm, weight of 2.9kg (including mat), and iner mass of 560kg-cm2. This increases the iner mass of 30% or more than 30cm long turntable, which is equal to weight and shape, and increases the basic rotation performance. The bearing load is about 1/10 of the conventional method and is reduced to just 500 g. This reduces noise and wear caused by bearing friction. tonearm uses ED (electrodynamic) servo arm. ED servo tonearm is an electronic Q-dumping arm that detects arm vibrations by two coreless linear motors directly connected to horizontal and vertical bearings and generates reverse torque by microcontroller feedback control to cancel vibration. This suppresses needles and vibrations caused by low frequency resonance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC QL-Y 66 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y66f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/jvc-ql-y-66-f.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y66f.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y66f.JPG"}},"kenwood-ka-770":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥64,800. Equipped with DLD (Dynamic Linear Drive) circuit. The DLD circuit can be used to demonstrate high current supply capability even at low impedance loads and to bring out the performance of any loudspeaker. This improves instant power supply and enables you to drive a loudspeaker system that repeats complex movements. Σ drive method is available. In addition to waveform transmission in the input terminal of amplifier, the waveform change in the input terminal of loudspeaker is suppressed even with a few meters connection cable. The equalizer amplifier is equipped with high SN and low distortion circuit with ICL high GmFET differential input and OPE amplifier. In particular, around the earth, we use a wire material with a conventional 6-story cross-section area that twists 26 single wires of 0.26 mm directly. The layout of each stage is arranged according to the flow of the signal, and the B class and A class stage are set on a separate board in the power amplifier, and the equalizer and the main stage are shielded with a large heat sink to reduce interference between each block.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-770 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-770.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-105":{"more":[{"t":"Hybrid integrated amplifier introduced as the first product of the new concept component \"Bridge series\" which combines advanced technology and traditional materials It uses a vacuum tube with excellent musical characteristics and an FET with power and characteristics. FET is used in the first stage, 3-pole tube is used in the pre-driver stage where high voltage resistance and linearity are required, and MOS FET is used in the last stage. In order to eliminate current distortion, a voltage-controlled amplifier circuit is employed in all stages to prevent interference distortion caused by current amplification. S. T. A. R. circuits are used to eliminate interference between circuit blocks and signal paths. In this circuit, the sharing of the ground line and power supply line, which was often done in the conventional amplifier circuit, is abolished, and all lines are drawn directly from the reference point to each circuit block and signal path to realize smooth signal flow. It is also equipped with an input section for video signals to support AV equipment.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman LV 105 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/lv-105-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/luxman-lv-105.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/lv-105-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/lv-105.JPG"}},"marantz-pm-54":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥62,000. This integrated amplifier was developed along with the PM-64 based on the concept of digital compatibility and realized AVSS mounting and low-impedance compatibility. Equipped with AVSS (Auto Voltage Shift Supply) that shifts the output supply voltage according to the power. By driving the power element at the output supply voltage most suitable for each power from small output to maximum output, high power is realized while maintaining the quality. Designed for low impedance, it maintains power even when the speaker impedance momentarily fluctuates to an extremely low value. It is equipped with a direct switch for higher SN ratio and high-speed signal transmission of digital source. In addition to the MM input, an MC input is also installed for playing analog discs.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-54 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-54-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-64":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥74,000. This integrated amplifier inherits the digital support concept of the PM-84 and is refined by inheriting the AVSS. Equipped with AVSS (Auto Voltage Shift Supply) that shifts the output supply voltage according to the power. By driving the power element at the output supply voltage most suitable for each power from small output to maximum output, high power is realized while maintaining the quality. Designed for low impedance, it maintains power even when the speaker impedance momentarily fluctuates to an extremely low value. Equipped with a direct switch, you can jump the tone amplifier and subsonic filter to feed the digital source directly to the power amplifier. As a result, the signal path becomes the shortest path between the selector, volume, and power amplifier, enabling more pure playback. In addition to the MM input, an MC input is also installed for playing analog discs. There was a side wood sold separately.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-64 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-64-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sc-11":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥300,000. In response to the digital age, this preamplifier is centered on a circuit configuration that requires a wide dynamic range and high-speed playback. It uses an negative feedback (NF)-CR type equalizer that performs low-frequency turn-over with an negative feedback (NF) circuit and high-frequency roll-off with a CR network. In addition, the equalizer amplifier and flat amplifier are DC unit amplifiers with push-pull circuit configuration for all stages from input to output. This improves distortion characteristics and SN ratio at low NFB. The first stage is equipped with an ultra-low noise, high gmFET + cascode bootstrap circuit to prevent adverse effects of impedance fluctuations. The output stage of the 2-stage SEPP circuit provides sufficient idle current to achieve complete class A operation. Equipped with a direct switch that can be directly connected to the power amplifier through the selector and volume. By simplifying the signal line, the freshness of sound is kept and the SN ratio in practical conditions is improved. It is equipped with an MC head amplifier to draw out the regenerative capacity of the MC cartridge.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SC-11 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sc-11-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-sm-11":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥400,000. This is a stereo power amplifier that Marantz completed by taking the right approach that he had accumulated through the development of various high power amplifiers. In order to obtain high power with high quality, power transistors with especially excellent linearity are adopted. A total of 16 power transistors are used in a 4-parallel 3-stage Darlington circuit configuration. In addition, by adopting a cascode circuit for all voltage amplification stages, simplification has been achieved, and bare characteristics have been improved to achieve low noise and low distortion without applying a large amount of NFB. The power supply section is equipped with a high-regulation large power transformer and a specially developed custom electrolytic capacitor for audio. Electrolytic capacitors, in particular, use computer-grade high-grade screw terminals to achieve high reliability. Equipped with a large peak power meter. By adopting logarithmic compression type indication, it is possible to monitor from small output to maximum output without switching the range. The recovery time of the meter can be switched between Normal and Peak Hold by the switch on the front panel.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz SM-11 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/sm-11-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-bl-111":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1981 at ¥270,000. armless thread drive player system with direct coupling of rotation mechanism and arm support. Metal eyewear frames are available. A large shaft assembly with a 16mm diameter oil bath on the other side of this frame, and the tonearm base is fixed on the other side. This structure was developed to reduce energy conversion loss. It is ideal to move only the needle tip to convert the sound groove energy to electric signal without loss when playing records. However, conversion loss occurs when tonearm, arm board, phono motor, shaft, and table turn are moved and resonated simultaneously. The longer the signal circulation system, the more the conversion loss is likely to occur, BL-111 provides a metal frame to shorten the vibration circulation system and increase rigidity. This frame is made of zinc, and the weight of 10kg and the sturdyness of the weight is realized. Gunmetal is used for tartable.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki BL-111 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/player/bl-111.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nad-7140":{"more":[{"t":"The mid to late 1980’s saw a transition toward cheaper less robust audio components mostly made of plastic. During that transition there were some interesting receivers made by companies such as NAD. This NAD 7140 receiver is a good example. Produced from around 1983/84 through late 1989 is is a high quality stereo that moved away from the shiny brushed aluminum faceplates and beveled knobs so popular in the 1970’s and very early 1980’s. It retailed for $478.00. The build quality and circuit design is excellent and, best of all, it can accommodate tape, phono and CD. The phono input can be switched from MM to MC as well. The rating of 80 watts per channel is conservative and NAD’s amp circuit is designed with a lot of headroom. There is a switch on the back to adjust for speaker impedance and the 7140 will provide 40 watts per channel at 2, 4, and 8 ohms.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – NAD 7140","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/nad-7140","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"onkyo-m-510":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥850,000. This is a stereo power amplifier developed using technologies such as the double-trans drive system to enable the ultimate music playback. In a general amplifier, the current that is out of phase due to the characteristics of the speaker is returned to the amplifier through flux, ground, or B power supply. This out-of-phase signal is superimposed on the input signal, and the mixed phase acts as the input signal. Therefore, the correct phase information originally contained in music information is disturbed, and the sound field feeling that produces a subtle phase difference is also disturbed. The M-510 is equipped with an in-phase transformer in the current path to prevent out-of-phase components from returning to the amplifier. In this in-phase transformer, when a current with a waveform on the positive side flows, the current with the same waveform flows on the negative side with exactly opposite phases. This allows the positive side and the negative side to mutually control each other, canceling only the extra components that come back on the power supply current. This improves low-frequency braking and provides excellent low-frequency playback. In addition, the in-phase transformer suppresses the overburden of the flux generated from the power supply and improves the low-level regeneration capability.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Onkyo M-510 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/ONKYO/amp/m-510-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"quad-510":{"more":[{"t":"A mono power amplifier developed for professional use. QUAD’s unique casing damping circuit is used for the circuit method. This circuit is the world’s first successful feed-forward theory circuit. The distortion component found in the bridge circuit is canceled by the distortion component of the small output amplifier and the crossover distortion is reduced. In 510, accuracy and stability are improved by improving the bridge part of this current damping circuit. It is equipped with a protective circuit that protects even if it is overload, continuous use for long time, short circuit etc. Cannon connectors are available for input and output terminals.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Quad 510 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/QUAD/amp/510.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-507-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥65,000. X-Ba amplifier This circuit is a structure that is separated from the earth, and it is a complete balance configuration until it is in the signal circuit, power supply circuit, and NPB circuit. Tape input 2 circuit Also, you can record and output another source from the playing source. Two-system loudspeaker can be connected with a twin relay loudspeaker switch. Equipped with subsonic filter.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 507 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d507x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-607-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥79,800. This reduces the occurrence of IHM distortion caused by inter-interference between power supply Ripple current and external noise and reverse power generated by concurrently using loudspeaker with conventional amplifier. In addition, thanks to the configuration of balance feedback on two output stages plus and negative, the distortion and characteristics of the actual operation of the amplifier have been greatly improved. The power supply unit is a 3 power supply system using large-size EI, which has excellent regulation, and it supports high power regeneration by the power supply of pre-drive/ equalizer and L/R independent 2 power supply. The circuit configuration uses low-noise and high-gm dual-FETs in the first stage, and is used as a push-pull drive net-complementary SEPP output by two differentials and current differentials with a current mirror. It is also a discrete configuration to prioritize sound quality.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 607 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d607x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-707-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥129,000. This reduces the occurrence of IHM distortion caused by inter-interference between power supply Ripple current and external noise and reverse power generated by concurrently using loudspeaker with conventional amplifier. In addition, thanks to the configuration of balance feedback on two output stages plus and negative, the distortion and characteristics of the actual operation of the amplifier have been greatly improved. In addition, the pre, pre-drive, and power part L/R are separate 4 power supply configurations to reduce interoperability between circuits. In addition, the noise generated from power supply is prevented by power with the power supply system without ground. MC cartridge is installed to support MC cartridge. This MC uses high-purity, low-magnetic distortion permal as a superior core of characteristics.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 707 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d707x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-907-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥189,000. X Balance amplifier In AU-D907X, X-Ba AMP is added to the basic configuration of AMP. X Balance A amplifier is composed of six technologies: differential balance input configuration, balance output configuration, balance feedback configuration, balance power supply, balance current drive configuration, and twin diamond balance differential circuit. By driving loudspeaker to + side and - side by the balance output stage with two amplifiers, the sound quality deterioration caused by the ground is eliminated by the single drive method and the distortion of the circuit itself is minimized. In addition, it is a balance feedback configuration that puts NNFB on each of the two amplifiers of the balance output stage, which greatly improves distortion and characteristics during actual operation. There is a differential balance input in the input stage. In this way, CMRR (Common Mode Rejection Ratio) is higher than 90dB, and the differential input is only affected by 1/30,000 from Earth. Twin Diamond Balance Differential Circuit is available in the pre-drive stage. This circuit is focused on the four differential circuits that have four different outputs. It uses four outputs to achieve two output stages.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 907 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d907x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-333-esx":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥79,800. G chas is adopted for non-vibration and non-resonance design. The material is examined from the size of internal losses that quickly evaporate even if the vibration occurs, and the same composition of calcium carbonate is used in addition to uns rated polyester, and in addition to fiberglass. The power supply unit adopts a large power supply of 350VA, and is equipped with the S.T.D. (SpontaneousTwin Drive) power supply.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 333 ESX (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f333esx.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-m-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥99,800. Fully automatic player with linear tracking system. By detecting arm polarization with optical sensor and obtaining high accuracy detection signal, the tracking error angle is within ±0.05 °. Tonearm uses its own dynamic balance system and arm bearings with four-point support gimbal suspension system. In addition, arm is designed to be effective mass 13g, including cartridge. Large and heavyweight aluminum die-cast turntable is available in diameter 32.5cm, weight 2.5kg, iner mass 427kg and cm2. It is equipped with electronic control full automatic mechanism. Plug-in connector type MM cartridge cabinet uses TNRC and high density particle board.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-M 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-m3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-q5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥44,800. Jacket size and full automatic player with direct-drive Equipped with a full automatic electronic control mechanism, it automatically detects the size and rotation speed of the record by simply setting the record and tapping the start of the front panel. The upper cabinet is equipped with a linear tracking arm. Microcomputer control ensures that the tracking error angle is within 1% and the inside force is almost zero. By adopting the arm bearing structure of the gimbal suspension method, it realizes the same high sensitivity in all directions. The dynamic balance arm delivers stable trace performance. In addition to the adoption of TECHNICS' proprietary integrated structure direct-drive Plug-in connector type MM cartridge The bottom cabinet and the bottom base are all composed of TNRC to improve the vibration-proof performance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-Q5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-q6":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥49,800. Jacket size and quartz direct-drive player that can perform auto-chosen by 8 programs. You can play your favorite songs in the LP automatically with a 1 to 8 program button. It is equipped with an electronic control full automatic mechanism, it detects the size and rotation speed of the record automatically by just tapping the start of the front panel. The upper cabinet is equipped with a linear tracking arm. Microcomputer control ensures that the tracking error angle is within 1% and the inside force is almost zero. The arm bearing structure of the gimbal suspension system has the same high sensitivity in all directions. Also, the dynamic balance arm eliminates the need for strict horizontal adjustment of the cabinet. By in the quartz for rotation control, the rotation speed is ±0.002%. The plug-in connector type cartridge is standard.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-Q6 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-q6.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v7-x":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier based on SU-V10X to pursue cost performance. The pre-drive stage employs a gain control circuit with a high-performance operational amplifier. This eliminates the adverse effect of the output stage caused by the speaker load that fluctuates during actual driving and suppresses the generation of distortion in the pre-drive stage itself. By installing a power linear circuit, the linearity of the output stage is improved, and high-quality speaker drive is realized. The computer drive eliminates transient distortion in the output stage in real time by the microcomputer. Linear feedback reduces range of audibility distortion by constructing an independent feedback circuit that enables infinite amplification in the NFB loop. In addition, switching distortion and crossover distortion are eliminated by a bias circuit independent of the signal system. The power supply section is equipped with a low-loss, high-capacity power transformer. oxygen-free copper wire is used for the winding, and the regulation is greatly improved by adopting a unique perfectly aligned winding that can wind wires 20% thicker than conventional wires at high density. The smoothing power capacitor uses a low ESR (equivalent series resistance) type with very low loss.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V7 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v7x-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-z-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥35,600. integrated amplifier with an information concentrated display on the front. Two decks can be connected.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-Z 55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-z55-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-z35":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥35,600. integrated amplifier for easy operation. Equipped with an LED peak power meter that graphically displays the left and right outputs. Two decks can be connected.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-Z35 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-z35-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"thorens-td-320":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥268,000. Player system developed by inheriting pre-stage technology. TD320 has three variations, each with different arms. The TP16mkIV used for TD320 is a method to stop pipe arm detachment and rotate head 180 ° to replace cartridge. This method is a structure that supports turntable, arm, motor and operation part independently. Vibration from motor is difficult to transmit to the regeneration mechanism. In addition, we use highly resonant materials to reduce the impact of any vibration. A belt drive method is used for the drive unit. The turntable part has a double turntable structure. It is a structure that combines the main turntable and the concentric drive sub turntable.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Thorens TD 320 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/THORENS/player/td320.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-gt-750":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥69,800. A record player who made a high C/P by changing a part of cabinet or motor from GT-1000. Turntable is a 30mm thick aluminum die-casting turntable with a diameter of 360mm. In addition, the motor adopts a DC 4-phase 8-pole coreless motor with a 1.2kg startup torque and a cm, and it measures stable rotation by the quartz PLL method. Tonearm uses a static balance S-shaped tonearm to achieve a horizontal and vertical initial sensitivity of 7mg. We also have a 27mmφ pole brace of zinc die-cast arm base and brass cutting. It is equipped with a thread suspension anti-skating mechanism and height adjustment mechanism. We supply aluminum die-cast headshell which prevents harmful vibration by thickening the connector part. The cabinet is equipped with a cabinet with a 18mm thick high density particle board.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha GT-750 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/gt-750.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released May 1985 at ¥510,000. A stereo power amplifier developed with AccuPhase's traditional technology for the new era of audio. The output stage consists of six parallel push-pull transistors with collector loss Pc150W for a total of 12 transistors / ch. When the power efficiency of the output stage is assumed to be 70%, the theoretical limit output is 4,200W. Therefore, even if the rated maximum output is taken out, there is a sufficient margin to improve the safety of the output stage. In order to suppress the switching distortion generated at the output stage at the time of small output, the operating point is strictly set so that each element of PNP and NPN is not cut off by the input signal. A MOS FET equivalent to a non-switching class A drive is used for the front stage of driving the final stage, and it is composed of cascode push-pull. The front stage of sending a signal to this MOS FET is also composed of class A cascode push-pull. As a result, the output stage is composed of low distortion and stable against load from small output in the noise region to large output in the rated output. The input circuit constitutes a cascode bootstrap push-pull circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-500-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-45-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥59,800. A full automatic player developed with DENON technology including a dynamic servo tracer. Tonearm is equipped with an electronic arm, a dynamic servo tracer. This arm inherits DP-100M pure electronic arm and damping mechanism. In general, the Q damping mechanism is only horizontal in this class, but the dynamic servo tracer also has a vertical Q damping mechanism, which effectively controls the arm vibration caused by too high low frequency resonance Q, and pursues more purity music reproduction by improving low frequency output and crosstalk failure. In addition, Q damping control volume control is specified for a wide range of cartridges. arm has a straight arm. The full automatic mechanism is equipped with electronic contactless full automatic mechanism by microprocessor control. Built-in record size automatic detection mechanism, quick repeat mechanism, and locale mechanism. The unique double-action mechanism is used to expand the tonearm movable range manually. This gives you a feeling like a manual player, and improves cartridge conversion.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-45 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-45f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-47f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥59,800. A full automatic player with a dynamic servo trailer arm. DENON turntable is used in the turntable section. By adding both servo and electronic brakes to the combination of magnetic recording detection method and quartz lock, stable rotation performance and prompt operation are realized. Tonearm is equipped with an electronically controlled contactless tonearm with a dynamic servo tracer. The dynamic servo tracer is electronically damping the low fre cies of cartridge compliance and tonearm, both horizontally and vertically. It effectively suppresses crosstalk deterioration and mixed distortion. The arm body has a light weight arm. The automatic size detection and speed change mechanism automatically detects LP record (33, 1/3 rotation) and single record (45 rotation) by automatic performance, and automatically switches speed. In addition, it has a safety design that the tonearm does not work even if the start button is pressed when the record is pressed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-47F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-47f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-960":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier with dual super non-feedback circuit. The PMA 960 is equipped with a dual super non-feedback circuit that enhances the non-feedback system. This circuit consists of a distortion servo circuit in which the N-channel and P-channel transistors of the power stage mutually cancel out the distortion. The dual super no-feedback circuit has no NFB loop that returns the signal to the input side, so the transmission speed of the signal approaches that of the bare circuit, and there is no dynamic distortion that greatly affects the auditory quality. It also has the advantage of theoretically making the static distortion 0 and increasing the slew rate. In addition, the dual super no-feedback circuit with a high removal effect has an excellent distortion removal effect up to the high-order harmonic distortion region of 20 kHz or more. In addition, since there is no NFB loop, the influence of the back electromotive force, etc. does not reach the voltage amplification stage (pre-driver stage, etc.) when the speaker is connected, and dynamic distortion does not occur. There are various other advantages. The flat amplifier, which is heavy for CD playback, has been thoroughly upgraded to high speed to improve the slew rate.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-960 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-960-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"dual-cs-5000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥115,000. Quartz control belt drive player with unique technology. The turntable part adopts the belt drive method, and the drive motor adopts the speed detection quartz control DC motor by the microprocessor. The turntable uses a 1.5kg vibration tamping die-cast platter to achieve a clearer sound. tonearm is equipped with a gyroscope, gimbal, tonearm. This tonearm has four bearings that support the movement of the upper and lower sides, making it a point contact support method with precision polishing finish. This enables us to follow the changes and warpage of records and realizes superior tra. In addition, we maintain accurate needle pressure by using a dynamic balance method using high precision springs. OPS (OptimumPivot System) is equipped with a tonearm bearing point set to the same height as the record surface. If the point is the same height as tonearm, the wow flutter will be deteriorated by 15% if the record is warped up to 1.5mm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Dual CS 5000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/cs5000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-pm-625":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥45,000. And this reactance delays the current waveform against the added voltage waveform and confuses the amplifier output. In the PM series, we deal with this problem by securing the output of 2Ω or more of 8Ω at 2Ω. The reactance load requires maximum current at zero voltage. This is a special circuit that drives the driver stage constant voltage. The PM series has a low NFB structure, and the frequency characteristics from 1 Hz to 150 kHz are cleared in the range of 12-20 dB. This NFB volume is equivalent to the vacuum tube type.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM 625 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm625.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-pm-625.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm625.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm625.jpg"}},"harman-kardon-pm-645":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥59,800. A PM series integrated amplifier that pursues the music of the source by improving its own naked characteristics and minimizing NPB. Even if loudspeaker impedance is drastically reduced, stable power supply is always possible even if a major threshold occurs in phase. Low NFB is achieved by increasing naked characteristics, and the frequency characteristics from 1 Hz to 150 Hz are cleared in the range of 12-20 dB. The protection circuit provides unique high-speed electronic protection. This circuit continuously monitors current and time, and stops operation immediately before the hazard area. This method prevents sound quality deterioration without using relay on the output side. By adopting the inverter darlington method, the driver step is constant voltage drive.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM 645 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm645.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-pm-645.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm645.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm645.jpg"}},"harman-kardon-pm-665":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥158,000. A PM series integrated amplifier that pursues the music of the source by improving its own naked characteristics and minimizing NPB. Even if loudspeaker impedance is drastically reduced, stable power supply is always possible even if a major threshold occurs in phase. Low NFB is achieved by increasing naked characteristics, and the frequency characteristics from 1 Hz to 150 Hz are cleared in the range of 12-20 dB. The protection circuit provides unique high-speed electronic protection. This circuit continuously monitors current and time, and stops operation immediately before the hazard area. This method prevents sound quality deterioration without using relay on the output side. By adopting the inverter darlington method, the driver step is constant voltage drive.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM 665 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm665.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-1100-sd":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥129,000. Super DLD (Dynamic Linear Drive) The Super DLD Circuit is equipped with a new supercharger to fully utilize the DLD’s four power supply circuits to configure a powerful power supply section. As a result, the power supply capacity is always mixed with four power supply at any output, so it is comparable to that of the conventional 300W power supply when the low power amplifier drive which has received up to 50W. We are developing and adopting our own equalizer amplifier, which replaces differential circuit and negative feedback (NF) element of input in each MM cartridge. This enables MC only and MM only when MC is regenerated. In addition to the 8 inputs, the adapter IN-OUT terminal can be connected directly to the graphics equalizer. In addition, the CD Direct Switch is equipped with a single-switch switch and a balance volume control. By simplifying the signal path, the CD sound is played more faithfully. In addition, all GNDs are concentrated on the loudspeaker terminal of the amplifier, preventing the increase of interference with patterns and fine materials of the GND line.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-1100 SD (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-1100sd.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-880-sd":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥62,000. Super DLD (Dynamic Linear Drive) The Super DLD circuit is equipped with a new supercharger to fully utilize the DLD’s four power supply circuits to form a powerful power supply section. Conventional DLD circuits used to switch between high power amplifier and dedicated power supply, low power amplifier and dedicated power supply, and four power supply respectively, which has the effect of increasing the real capacity of supply power, and have the same effect as double power supply capacity when low power amplifier is working with the sound quality. The Super DLD circuit is designed to strengthen this powerful power supply circuit, and the supercharger provides energy from the high-power power supply that had been suspended during low power amplifiers so far. It is designed to supply energy from low-power supply power, which had been suspended during high power amplifiers. By applying negative feedback (NF) loops to the amplifier's loudspeaker terminal, all parts that have been outside the negative feedback (NF) loop have been imported into the loop, including impedance of patterns and wiring materials, phase compensation coils, relays and loudspeaker switch. In addition, since all GNDs were concentrated on the loudspeaker terminal, it suppresses the increase of inter-interference by pattern and wire material of the GND line. ICL high GmFET differential input and equalizer amplifier amplifier by IC. It has multi-tape dubbing function. By TapeA, you can automatically take a large amount to TapeA→TapeB/TapeC.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-880 SD (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-880sd.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-990-sd":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥79,800. Super DLD (Dynamic Linear Drive) The Super DLD Circuit is equipped with a new supercharger to fully utilize the DLD’s four power supply circuits to configure a powerful power supply section. The conventional DLD circuit uses four power supply and four power supply sources, such as high power amplifier, dedicated power supply, low power supply, and dedicated power supply. It has the effect of increasing the real capacity of power supply, and it has the same effect as having multiple power supply capacity with a controlled impact on sound quality. This makes it possible to play more clear and heavy sound because the power supply capacity is always mixed with four power supply. 8 input terminals In addition, there is also an adapter IN-OUT terminal, so it is possible to connect graphic equalizer etc. Σ Drive TypeB is a sigma drive typeB company that pursues ease of use as it is. By applying the negative feedback (NF) loop to the loudspeaker terminal, the parts that cause distortion and sound quality are put in the negative feedback (NF) loop and the performance of the amplifier's loudspeaker terminal is increased. In addition, all GNDs are concentrated on the loudspeaker terminal of the amplifier to reduce the cross-interference of GND line patterns and wire materials.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-990 SD (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-990sd.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kyocera-a-710":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥189,000. an integrated amplifier developed under the theme of playing the most vivid digital sound. Direct In & Out System In addition to normal input, Direct in position is installed. The program source connected to this input is inputted to the volume control via the LC-OFC shield line and sent to the amplifier. This is a simpler route, unlike a general bypass (line direct) switch, because it does not pass any circuit boards or related products before volume control. A-710 is equipped with a Direct Out terminal. This terminal eliminates the output relay which negatively affects the sound quality, and it is a complete direct output that eliminates the loudspeaker switch and the pulling of the line material. A unique CCR-based chas amplifier on the bottom. The main parts and circuit boards are directly attached to this base chas, and the height adjustable foot which can be fixed to the rigid at the bottom is reduced the harmful vibrations of the external and inside.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kyocera A-710 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/KYOCERA/amp/a-710.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-cl-360":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1985 at ¥364,800. Tube bulb type preamplifier. Bi-triode 12AX7 with Takamasu depth factor is used for the first stage of the equalizer stage and the output stage. In addition, 12AU7 is used for the flat amplifier, which is basically the same circuit as the equalizer stage. The final stage adopts 12AU7 and all stages have a simple design of S. R. P. P. output. In order to avoid the degradation of sound quality by applying too much NFB, we aim to improve the naked characteristics of the amplifier while maintaining the freshness of sound by applying the optimum NFB. The power supply to the equalizer circuit and tone circuit is completely separated, and independent stabilization reduces distortion caused by signal interference between amplification sections.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman CL-360 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/cl-360-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-mq-360":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1985 at ¥319,400. Bulb-tube type power amplifier. In order to make full use of the attractiveness and real power of vacuum tubes, it operates in the class A range. MQ-360 uses a self-bias method. The driver circuit that drives the power stage employs a bi-triode 6CG7 that provides drive power with low impedance, and provides ample operation within the push-pull configuration of all stages. The power supply is equipped with a high-capacity transformer to ensure high regulation even in the event of overcurrent, while also giving careful consideration to polarity control. The output transformer uses an ultra-linear connection dedicated transformer that is ideal for a self-bias circuit. The high-frequency characteristics smoothly extending to 100 kHz and the distortion factor realize the sound quality unique to the tube bulb type. The S. T.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman MQ-360 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/mq-360-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-94":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier with Marantz's separate amplifier technology. The output stage is a triple push-pull configuration using MOS FET. MOS FET has characteristics such as \"excellent high-frequency characteristics, high withstand voltage and high power can be applied at the same time\", \"because it operates only with majority carriers in principle, high input impedance higher than that of J-FET is realized\", and \"because there is little accumulation effect during switching, turn-off time is extremely shortened and high-speed switching is possible\". Together with Marantz's original Quarter A, MOS FET realizes ideal operation. Using a unique Quarter A circuit, it performs full class A operation up to 1/4 of the maximum output and automatically shifts to class AB operation up to the maximum output. This autoshift is controlled by an electronic control. It detects the output voltage of the main amplifier and controls the bias current with a high-speed switching circuit. The detection speed of the PM-94 circuit is higher than that of the conventional Quarter A circuit, enabling smoother control. In order to fully demonstrate the performance of the MC cartridge, two high performance MC transformers are mounted on the MC input independently on the left and right sides.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-94 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-94-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-c-34-v":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1986 at ¥680,000. A preamplifier that reduces interference by using an optional external interlocking switching method for video signal selection. Equipped with a 5-band equalizer and compensator, it can also be inserted into a recording system. As an accessory circuit, there is a video selector MVS-1, which can be connected to a C34V to switch the video signal without affecting the audio circuit. The speaker control relay SCR-2 allows switching between two AC-systems and two speaker systems.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh C 34 V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/c34v-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"mcintosh-mc-7270":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥680,000. Stereo power amplifier equipped with original digital sonic overload collector.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – McIntosh MC 7270 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc7270-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/mcintosh-mc-7270.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc7270-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MCINTOSH/amp/mc7270.JPG"}},"sansui-au-d-907-x-decade":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥193,000. AU-D907X is an integrated amplifier based on power supply. The basic structure of the twin diamond X balance amplifier. In the conventional amplifier, the current to loudspeaker was sent from the + side, and the side was simply a single drive connected to the earth. Therefore, IHM distortion caused by inter-interference with the ripple current of the current was occurred when the reverse power flows to the ground of the side. In addition, NPB for reduction of distortion is only + side, and - side is not controlled at all. Twin Diamond X Balance A circuitifier is a balance structure of all signal circuits, power supply circuits, and NFB circuits from input to output. In addition to adopting the balance power supply method, the power amplifier unit increases the stability by independentizing the pre-drive unit, the power unit and the L/R unit. The CD Direct Input Terminal is equipped to enable pure CD playback without passing the input selector.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-D 907 X Decade (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-d907xdecade.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-x-111-mos-vintage":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥330,000. Based on the circuit technology and know-how up to that time, this integrated amplifier was developed through uncompromising selection of parts, improvement and hearing test. While applying the know-how accumulated in the development of the C-2301 and B-2301L Separate Amplifiers, we have implemented thorough anti-vibration design, deadening, and electromagnetic wave splash prevention measures. In addition, we have developed custom-made parts and used proven parts. A MOS FET is used as the power element. Four parallel push-pull elements are used at four locations on the left and right sides of the power stage and plus / minus sides, for a total of 16 elements. This enhances the low-impedance drive capability and provides a highly stable drive. In addition, hum and noise components are canceled by balance transmission and amplification, and the ground is separated from the - side so that it is not affected by the ground. Therefore, it is resistant to noise interference and hum from the outside, and the SN ratio and transparency of the auditory sense are improved. In order to prevent AC lines contaminated with clock pulses and phase control noise from home appliances and microcomputers, the power supply circuit is a balanced power supply configuration with a closed loop regardless of the ground color, similar to the amplifier circuit.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-X 111 Mos Vintage (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-x111mosvintage-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-555-es-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1984 at ¥128,000. In addition, the linear gain control method attenuator that can be used with the audio current function method is adopted in volume control, and various characteristics are improved at the general listening level. In addition to 5 audio lines, 2 video lines are included. Video2 to Video1 Low noise Hi-gmFET is available to fono equalizer amplifier compatible with MC cartridge. After the power supply is inserted, the standby indicator will flash the state of the music until the amplifier is moved to stable operation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 555 ES II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f555esii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-se-a-100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥300,000. Stereo power amplifier equipped with ClassAA circuit. In the ClassAA circuit, the voltage preamplifier and the current drive amplifier are respectively handled by separate amplifiers. This frees the voltage preamplifier from the current supply and enables voltage control faithful to the input signal, thereby realizing low distortion. The current drive amplifier can stably supply the current required for speaker drive, and has acquired excellent speaker drive capability. The SE-A100 has a VC-4 configuration with two voltage control amplifiers and two current drive amplifiers for the left and right, for a total of four. The voltage preamplifier employs a Darlington configuration with a differential amplifier input stage using one chip dual FET and a Pc150Wx2ch output transistor, and is a complete A-class amplifier that realizes ultra-low distortion close to the limit of measured values. The current drive amplifier consists of a FET differential amplifier input, a high-speed amplitude amplifier stage equipped with a newly developed feed-forward type bootstrap power supply, and a Pc450Wx2/ch 4-stage Darlington output stage using 3-parallel output transistors. It supplies a large current at 50A / μ s to obtain a strong power. The power supply section has a 3-transformer configuration, equipped with a power transformer for the left and right current drive amplifiers and a transformer for the left and right voltage drive amplifiers.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-A 100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-a100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-l-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥59,800. Quartz direct-drive full automatic player with 8 songs program mechanism. Includes 8 music programs. In addition, the electronic control full automatic mechanism starts playing with one start button. With the skip function, you can head back and forth songs. arm requires linear tracking arm. Turntable Plug-in connector type MM cartridge","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-L 3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-l3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-a-200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥200,000. This preamplifier is designed for higher quality reproduction and power amplifier drive by adopting ClassAA method for equalization amplifier and output amplifier. The phono equalizer amplifier uses the ClassAA method. The SEPP output stage current drive amplifier with high current supply capability eliminates the adverse effect of the impedance fluctuation of the RIAA element on the output current, and realizes voltage amplification in an ideal A-class state. It also realizes ultra-low distortion by combining with dual ultra-low noise FET differential amplification and the first stage high current rate circuit configuration with cascode. The ClassAA method is also adopted for the output-amplifier section, making it possible to reproduce A-class low-distortion high-definition images without being affected by the load state caused by the input impedance or connection code of the power amplifier, which occurs in the output-section of the conventional preamplifier. Newly developed 4-row configuration wide D-range volume is used. This volume achieves low distortion and low noise by using a new resistor with a smooth mirror surface and a gold-plated multi-contact brush. In addition, the SN ratio in actual use has been greatly improved by using a new circuit that operates two of the four volumes as gain control of the output amplifier. A newly developed active servo power supply is used for the power supply.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A 200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a200-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v-10-x":{"more":[{"t":"This is an integrated amplifier equipped with high-definition reproduction and growth capability for the full-scale digital assistant era. The pre-drive stage employs a gain control circuit with a high-performance operational amplifier. This eliminates the adverse effect of the output stage caused by the speaker load that fluctuates during actual driving and suppresses the generation of distortion in the pre-drive stage itself. By installing a power linear circuit, the linearity of the output stage is improved, and high-quality speaker drive is realized. The computer drive eliminates transient distortion in the output stage in real time by the microcomputer. Linear feedback reduces range of audibility distortion by constructing an independent feedback circuit that enables infinite amplification in the NFB loop. In addition, switching distortion and crossover distortion are eliminated by a bias circuit independent of the signal system. Pc for the output stage of the power amplifier is excellent H of total 1.2 kw. FE A large chip size power transistor with linearity is used.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V 10 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v10x-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v6x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥69,800. Computer drive an integrated DC amplifier equipped with a new power linear circuit in a new class A amplifier. It is equipped with a power linear circuit unique to Technics. This is a development of linear feedback circuit technology. This effect is brought to the output stage of the amplifier, and linearity is dramatically improved, and distortion caused by low impedance load of the speaker at every moment is suppressed. Equipped with computer drive new class A system. In this computer drive, a microcomputer was introduced for the first time in the world for the bias control of the amplifier signal system. Based on information from the signal sensor, the instantaneous temperature operating state of the output transistor in response to changes in the music signal is calculated, and the ICQ (idling current) is always controlled to the optimum value. This ensures that no transient crossover distortion due to excess or deficiency of ICQ occurs during playback of any music signal. After the power is turned on, the circuit can be checked by the display on the front panel until stable operation is achieved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V6X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v6x-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v8-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1983 at ¥108,000. Computer drive an integrated DC amplifier equipped with a new power linear circuit in a new class A amplifier. It is equipped with a power linear circuit unique to Technics. This is a development of linear feedback circuit technology. This effect is brought to the output stage of the amplifier, and linearity is dramatically improved, and distortion caused by low impedance load of the speaker at every moment is suppressed. Equipped with computer drive new class A system. In this computer drive, a microcomputer was introduced for the first time in the world for the bias control of the amplifier signal system. Based on information from the signal sensor, the instantaneous temperature operating state of the output transistor in response to changes in the music signal is calculated, and the ICQ (idling current) is always controlled to the optimum value. This ensures that no transient crossover distortion due to excess or deficiency of ICQ occurs during playback of any music signal. After the power is turned on, the circuit can be checked by the display on the front panel until stable operation is achieved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V8 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v8x-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"thorens-td-520":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥398,000. TD520 has a number of variations in a model with arm. TD521 is armless model. The appearance finish is made of rose wood finish with RW at the end of the model number, and the end is black finish. In this method, the turntable and arm board are suspended in one wire, and the regeneration system and the rotation system are completely independent from the vibration of the motor. The belt drive method is used for driving. In addition, the energy from the motor is received from the ideal transmission ratio.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Thorens TD 520 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/THORENS/player/td520.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-b-2x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥270,000. A stereo power amplifier that aims to balance power and quality, and pursues the most natural and most authentic sound. This circuit is composed of pure A-weight amplifier and AB-weight amplifier. The load is connected to the output of A-weight amplifier and AB-weight amplifier, and NFB is attached to the A-weight amplifier from both ends of the load. AB-class amplifiers support A-class amplifiers. They share power loss without quality, and A-class amplifiers provide high power quality and characteristics. ZDR circuit In this circuit, the NFB loop is equipped with a gain 1 correction amplifier. The same power amplifier unit base is prepared independently and independently. This maintains a structural balance and eliminates the inter-interference of the left and right channels to improve channel separation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha B-2x (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/b-2x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-c-2x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥220,000. High-gm Low Noise Dual FET As with the MC head amplifier, the ZDR circuit is installed, and the current noise suppression circuit is used to improve the noise at the time of cartridge mounting. In addition, Phono input is equipped with two lines, and Phono2 is fixed with 47kΩ and 220pF. In Phono1, it is possible to select 100Ω and 1kΩ at MC position and 100, 200 and 300pF at MM position at 47kΩ. In addition, the gain of the equalizer amplifier can be switched on the rear panel, making it easy to adjust with other inputs. negative feedback (NF) tone control circuit with high quality film capac. High precision 21-point click special volume control and center defeit mechanism.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha C-2x (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-2x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-c-2x.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-2x.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/c-2x.JPG"}},"yamaha-gt-2000-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥320,000. Record player announced as the vertex model of the GT series. Motor has a new DC 4-phase 8-pole coreless hole motor that considers the effects of ripple noise during real performance rather than earning startup torque. The motor shaft has a diameter of 20mm and a length of 60mm. tonearm is equipped with YSA-1 of gimbal support straight arm. This arm uses brass to remove magnetic elements from the signal path. The headshell is non-magnetic and aluminum cutting. In addition, 0.15Ω signal reciprocating resistance is realized by using 1.2mmφ OFC lead wire and ITK#3000. GT-2000X is equipped with an optional auto lifter YAL-1 for GT-2000. YAL-1 is non-contact optical, smooth operation and excellent operability.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha GT-2000 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/gt-2000x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-p-100-x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥49,800. Fully automatic DD player with linear tracking. A linear tracking arm that does not cause tra distortion both inside and outside of the record board. The front operation method can be operated by closing the dust cover. MC cartridge is used for the T4P plug-in method. FG servo motor is used for motor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-100 X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-100x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-p-100-x.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-100x.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-100x.JPG"}},"yamaha-p-701":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥44,800. MC cartridge The front operation method can be operated without closing the dust cover. The cartridge has a dual MC type. ARS arm arm. The motor adopts a DC 4-phase 8-pole coreless hole type motor that does not cause ko in principle, and it realizes stable rotation by the quartz PLL servo method.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-701 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-701.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-p-701.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-701.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-701.JPG"}},"accuphase-c-270":{"more":[{"t":"Released April 1986. Stereo preamplifier following the flow of C-280. The sound quality is transparent and emphasizes the texture of the original sound field. The circuit configuration is all stage cascode A class push-pull configuration to improve the element characteristics before NFB is applied. The cascode method combines two amplifying elements in a column and operates as a single element. It increases the input impedance and gain, and at the same time greatly improves the high-frequency characteristics. Linearity is also maintained up to the operating limit of the device, reducing distortion and improving the signal-to-noise ratio. DC servo system is used for all unit amplifiers. It detects the direct current generated at the output and returns to the input, so that the output correctly maintains the 0 potential. As a result, all signal systems from the input to the output of the analog disk (AD) are directly connected, and high-quality playback sound without coloring is obtained.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-270 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-270-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"akai-am-a-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥69,800. Integrated amplifier with open loop circuit. NFB is equipped with an open loop circuit that pursues simplicity. This circuit eliminates all-over NPB loops, and the basic configuration of amplifier is a simple configuration of voltage amplifier and current amplifier. AM-A70 is equipped with Phono equal amplifier and power amplifier. In addition, we incorporate our unique zero-drive circuit between V amplifier and I amplifier to improve the low impedance driving capacity and increase the stability of the circuit with a 2-pole DC servo amplifier. In particular, capac reduces the use of electrolytic capac to a third of the conventional amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Akai AM-A 70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AKAI/amp/am-a70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"akai-am-a-90":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥99,800. an integrated amplifier that pursues the simplicity of the circuit. NFB is equipped with an open loop circuit that pursues simplicity. This circuit eliminates all-over NPB loops, and the basic configuration of amplifier is a simple configuration of voltage amplifier and current amplifier. AM-A90 is equipped with Phono equal amplifier and power amplifier. In addition, we incorporate our unique zero-drive circuit between V amplifier and I amplifier to improve the low impedance driving capacity and increase the stability of the circuit with a 2-pole DC servo amplifier. It eliminates sound quality degradation by using high resolution FBET. This MOS-FET is fixed to a large aluminum heat sink through high thermal conductive insulation sheet with low annual change. The electrolytic capac adopts the AS-1 for audio, and the rectifier circuit for V amplifier / I amplifier adopts the first recovery diode.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Akai AM-A 90 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/AKAI/amp/am-a90.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-59-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1984 at ¥89,800. A record player developed with all DENON player technology from broadcasting station player to DP-100M. DP-59L is equipped with an auto lift mechanism. The smart lift mechanism adopts a contactless structure that does not affect rotation accuracy or arm sensitivity. The detection of the record end is a unique method that combines two methods: optical position detection and speed detection of magnetic properties. It protects the needle tip and record. Turntable is 32.5cm in diameter, 7mm in thickness and 2.2kg in weight. AC servo motor with low center of gravity design. This motor shaft is provided with a thick diameter of 10mm and supports weight turn turntable firmly. This method detects 1,000 magnetic pulses on the outer circumference of the turntable which is easy to speed change and checks 555.55 times per second (33, 1/3 rotation).","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DP-59 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/player/dp-59l.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-500-v":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA 500 V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-500v-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/denon-pma-500-v.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-500v-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-500v.JPG"}},"denon-pma-300-v":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-300 V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/PMA-300V-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pma-700v":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon PMA-700V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/pma-700v-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"denon-poa-2200":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥160,000. The primary signal is transmitted to the loudspeaker terminal without feedback, and there is no NFB circuit, and there is no increase in distortion from loudspeaker. High-speed trans of fT150MHz in the pre-driver stage. The voltage amplifier adopts high-speed, wide dynamic range circuit and device.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon POA-2200 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-2200.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-pra-1100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥120,000. preamplifier with excellent transmission characteristics and full interface characteristics. Unity Gain Interface amplifier The PRA-1100 output stage is not just a buffer amplifier, but it adopts UGI amplifier with Pch/Nch FET Full Complementary Push-Pull circuit, which realizes signal feed in ultra-low impedance such as 10Ω. This eliminates the deterioration of high-fr ency characteristics and the effects of high-fr ency noises such as digital devices due to the long connection code to power amplifiers. The equalizer amplifier is equipped with DENON's own wideband super equalizer amplifier. This circuit combines the equalizer characteristics of CR type and negative feedback (NF) type, and the two-parallel differential amplifier configuration that adopted the ultra-low noise Hi-gmFET four at the first stage of each channel achieves excellent wide range characteristics with improved SN ratio and distortion rate. The flat amplifier is composed of a high-speed amp amplifier with a cast-code boots circuit attached to the high-Gm type FET differential amplifier. In addition, the volume control is set in the front and rear part of the amplifier, and the volume control is improved by matching the impedance amount of the volume control in the front and rear stage to the sibbia.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon PRA-1100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/pra-1100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-pm-635":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥39,800. A PM series integrated amplifier that pursues the music of the source by improving its own naked characteristics and minimizing NPB. Even if loudspeaker impedance is drastically reduced, stable power supply is always possible even if a major threshold occurs in phase. Low NFB is achieved by increasing naked characteristics, and the frequency characteristics from 1 Hz to 150 Hz are cleared in the range of 12-20 dB. The protection circuit provides unique high-speed electronic protection. This circuit continuously monitors current and time, and stops operation immediately before the hazard area. This method prevents sound quality deterioration without using relay on the output side. By adopting the inverter darlington method, the driver step is constant voltage drive.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM 635 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm635.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-1100-d":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥129,000. Super DLD (Dynamic Linear Drive) New VIG circuit is installed to realize linear signal delivery. The output trans boots is placed on the base of the final trans, and the buffer is inserted. To drive loudspeaker with higher quality signals, click the DLD circuit button. This demonstrates excellent power supply capability and purely plays the peak signal of the CD, which is 100 times the average signal. Low power amplifier takes up to 50W, and the most of the music signals are treated with low-level amplifiers with low distortion rate, thus delivering superior expression. In addition, the power supply impedance is reduced because it is driven by a huge power supply that can emit this low power amplifier of 300W or more. In addition, 4 chemicons for DLD are used for block chemicone.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-1100 D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-1100d.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-990-v":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥79,800. The VIG circuit is designed with low impedance from the amplifier side, with high impedance from the power supply side, making it difficult to pass through the noise through only direct current energy from power supply. This eliminates ripple, signal component, and mixed modulation distortion component of power supply. With the same effect as a huge battery, the large power supply without ripple significantly increases power supply capacity. In addition, we have introduced vibration analysis in the housing design, and we have a structure that prevents resonance against vibration from loudspeaker and direct vibration from the floor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-990 V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-990v.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-101":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1986 at ¥56,000. integrated amplifier of the Brid series. Equipped with CD straight function. When this function is turned ON, part of the signal path is bypassed, so that sound quality degradation due to switch contacts and wiring can be prevented. Equipped with two video input systems. MOS-FET is used in the driver stage of the power amplifier section. In addition, S. T. A. R.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman LV-101 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/lv-101-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-102":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1985 at ¥66,000. integrated amplifier of the Brid series with functions such as sound enhancer. It is equipped with a sound enhancer as a unique effect function, and effects are obtained by expanding the dynamic range of music (expand) and compressing (compress) (compress). With the Dynamic AV position, you can expand the dynamic range of the music source to increase the sense of scale. This position can be selected from two levels. In the Midnight position, the dynamic range is compressed to suppress sound thinning when the volume is reduced. Equipped with CD straight function. When this function is turned ON, part of the signal path is bypassed, so that sound quality degradation due to switch contacts and wiring can be prevented. Equipped with two video input systems. The LV 102 has a built-in video buffer amplifier that allows high-quality dubbing.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman LV-102 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/lv-102-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-103":{"more":[{"t":"This is a hybrid integrated amplifier that uses a vacuum tube with excellent musical reproduction power and a Bridd circuit using high-speed and high-power MOS FET. FET in the first stage, 3-pole tube in the pre-driver stage, and MOS FET in the last stage are applied, and voltage amplification is carried out in all stages to suppress interference distortion caused by current amplification. The S. T. A. R. circuit is adopted in which all lines are directly connected from the reference point to each point without sharing the power supply line and ground line in the circuit, and the silence and nuance between sounds are reproduced as transparent as possible.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman LV-103 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/lv-103-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-103-u":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1986 at ¥89,000. LV-103 As with LV-103, it is a hybrid configuration of the vacuum tube and MOS-FET. In the first stage, it uses the FET, and the pre-driver tube with high pressure resistance and linearity is 3 poles, and the MOS-FET is used at the end. The S.T.A.R. circuit is used to directly supply power supply lines and ground lines to each stage. In addition, LV-105u adopts the S.T.A.R. circuit as a signal pathway. In general, the signal system earthline treated as a shared part is independent from each amplifier stage. This improves the sound quality by improving the S/N of the hearing sense. With the CD straight function, you can bypass a part of the circuit and send it to the power amplifier at the shortest distance. This prevents the sound quality deterioration caused by the switch or wiring draw. Two AV terminals are installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman LV-103 u (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lv-103u.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-105-u":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1986 at ¥129,000. LV-105 As with LV-105, it is a hybrid configuration of the vacuum tube and MOS-FET. In the first stage, it uses the FET, and the pre-driver tube with high pressure resistance and linearity is 3 poles, and the MOS-FET is used at the end. The S.T.A.R. circuit is used to directly supply power supply lines and ground lines to each stage. In addition, LV-105u adopts the S.T.A.R. circuit as a signal pathway. In general, the signal system earthline treated as a shared part is independent from each amplifier stage. This improves the sound quality by improving the S/N of the hearing sense. With the CD straight function, you can bypass a part of the circuit and send it to the power amplifier at the shortest distance. This prevents the sound quality deterioration caused by the switch or wiring draw. Two AV terminals are installed.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman LV-105 u (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lv-105u.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-109":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1986 at ¥195,000. Built-in D/A converter to support digital sources. The internal D/A converter reduces the impact of the transmission system of analog signals after D/A conversion. The D/A converter is independently designed and shielded from other circuits. In addition, the clock obtained from the input is processed with the PLL circuit, and the timing pulse of the digital filter is adopted. Digital filter is a double-over-sampling 80-degree linear phase FIR type, with a sampling of over 90dB at 25kHz. For this reason, the lower path filter in the rear is a light amount of water. The first actuation a ification circuit uses a low-noise joint FET, and the entire MOS-FET is available from the pre-driver to the final.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman LV-109 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lv-109.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nakamichi-ca-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥400,000. preamplifier to simplify the amplifier circuit without losing sound quality. In order to realize pure signal transmission in a simple circuit configuration without relying on a large amount of NPB, each section adopts low-noise FET in the input stage, and the end is composed of emitter followers with a simple and large current supply capacity. Besides DC servo, high accuracy discrete parts are used. The end of each amplifier section adopts an emitter follower with a large current current, while a simpler configuration than a regular cascade connection.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nakamichi CA-70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/ca-70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"nakamichi-pa-70":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥380,000. STASIS circuit STASIS circuit is installed to realize the ideal of driving loudspeaker perfectly. The biggest feature of the STASIS circuit is that the high-quality signal transmission has been avoided while eliminating the overall NPB in a very simple circuit. In addition, because the coil used for oscillation prevention is unnecessary for general amplifier, uniform output impedance is increased in all bands.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Nakamichi PA-70 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/pa-70.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/nakamichi-pa-70.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/pa-70.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/NAKAMICHI/amp/pa-70.jpg"}},"pioneer-c-90":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥170,000. This stereo preamplifier was developed as the culmination of a review of the amplifier from its starting point. Based on the design philosophy of \"Simple is best\", the technologies developed by Pioneer are generously invested. It is a twin monoconstruction structure based on 3 transformer multi-power supply. The power supply for the L/R has been made independent of each transformer, and the layout on the printed circuit board has been separated into blocks to eliminate the unstable orientation caused by the deterioration of separation. In addition, the power supply for the video circuit and electronic control system is supplied from a power transformer and constant voltage circuit separate from the power supply for the audio system. The video circuit is equipped with a new circuit (PAT. P) that automatically turns off the power of the video circuit in conjunction with the function switch when the audio source is played back. Various anti-vibration parts are used to cancel out vibration. Polycarbonate is used for the insulator, which has a large internal loss and efficiently absorbs vibrations.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer C-90 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/c-90-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-m-90":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥200,000. A completed stereo power amplifier that is compatible with digital sources by generously investing Pioneer's technologies. The power supply section is thoroughly separated to prevent mutual interference. Large transformers are used independently on the left and right sides, and electrolytic capacitors with a total capacity of 48,000 μ F are used. In addition, a bridge rectifier circuit with high-speed low-noise diodes is used independently on the plus and minus sides of each of the left and right sides, achieving a large current supply capacity of 47A. The power transistor uses a Pc = 130W type 4-parallel push-pull configuration. In addition to the normal input terminal from the preamplifier, there is also a CD direct input terminal that connects the CD player and power amplifier directly. In addition, there is also a Line direct terminal, which can be used like a CD direct terminal. This CD/Line direct connector is also equipped with a dedicated output connector which can be returned to the preamplifier. To keep the signal path as short as possible, the volume itself is placed near the rear panel, close to the input terminal, and can be controlled from the front via an aluminum remote shaft.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer M-90 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/m-90-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-3-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥59,800. A full automatic player who inherits the technology and know-how of the advanced manual player. The drive motor adopts the coreless motor, eliminating the co that causes the rotation uneven. In addition, SH/Router method is used for bearings. This method adopts the structure that moved the bearing branch to the bottom of the motor immediately below the turntable. This succeeds to almost match the gravity and branching of turntable, eliminating the back conical movement of the motor shaft that was problematic in the conventional structure and the side pressure applied to the bearing. DRA was developed using computer-based vibration analysis technology. It is equipped with a side resonator composed of a damper and weight with a moderate spring characteristics for the arm pipe. It absorbs the resonance of the arm pipe itself. The combination of lightweight, rigid and non-resonant carbon graphite as an arm pipe eliminates the resonance of the arm itself that negatively affects the sound.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-3 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-3f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-5-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥69,800. A record player who uses the latest technology to thoroughly eliminate vibrations. Tonearm is equipped with straight arm with DRA. It is a sub-resonant composed of dampers and weights with moderate spring characteristics. This has a function to absorb the original resonance by giving positive opposite vibration to the arm resonance and prevents the needle tip from picking up excess ingredients by the neutronization of the vibration. The arm pipe adopts super duralumin straight pipe, and the shape of the straight pipe has gained high strength in terms of weight. The auto lift-up mechanism automatically increases the arm and stops the turntable rotation. Turntable SH Rotor and Coreless Motor are available in the drive unit. The coreless structure prevents the occurrence of ko that causes rotation uneven.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-5 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-5l.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-pl-7-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥99,800. A record player who developed the basic performance of each part and introduced the latest technology. DRA is a sub-resonant composed of a damper and weight with moderate spring characteristics, eliminating the resonance of the arm itself. By adopting alumina sintering, which is the ideal material for light weight and stiffness to the arm pipe, it effectively suppresses tonearm vibration by the synergy of two technologies. The shape of the arm pipe is strong on the weight surface, and the strength is high. Tonearm's weights are equipped with a one-point support method of anti-vibration structure. This eliminates resonance between the weight axis supporting the balance weight and the part affected by the pipe holder. We also use die-casts for arm-based and supportive parts to support pickup parts. It is equipped with a smart lift up mechanism and automatically lifts the arm to stop turningtable. The turntable drive servo motor features a quartz PLL DC servo motor.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Pioneer PL-7 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/player/pl-7l.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-1000":{"more":[{"t":"This is the Pioneer SX-1000TD which is one of Pioneer’s first all solid state receivers. There were a couple other similar models in the SX-1000TW and SX-1000TA. I believe the TA model actually had one tube in the tuner section while the all solid state TD version was a European release and the TW was sold in the U.S. Still, it also looks like the SX-1000TD was rebadged and sold as an Allied receiver in the U.S. as well. The SX-1000TD is a 50 watt per channel receiver and has a great lates 60’s vintage look to it. It measures 15 15/16″ X13 3/4″ X 5 3/8″ and weighs roughly 23 pounds. The TD and TW models look very similar on the outside. Here is the TW model in a wood case: As I mentioned above, the TA version has a tube in the tuner section as well as two Nuvistors which are actually tubes as well so there are really 3 tubes in the tuner section. The Nuvistors were used in some RF applications during the mid 60’s because transistors were still hard to produce and were less than reliable.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-1000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1000t","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-sx-1000.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-1000t","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/08/pioneer-sx-1000TD-left.jpg"}},"quad-306":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥150,000. The original capac damping circuit is used for stereo power. The current is supplied to the loudspeaker from the small output pure A-weight amplifier. When the signal level is larger, the damper circuit is operated and the large current is measured. This method detects and corrects errors between input signals and output signals, and cancels the distortion component of the output stage. The circuit is also equipped with a unique circuit that provides reliable and stable current supply capability for short circuit and overload.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Quad 306 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/QUAD/amp/306.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"quad-606":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥280,000. A striking power amplifier with a current damping circuit. The current is supplied to the loudspeaker from the small output pure A-weight amplifier. When the signal level is larger, the damper circuit is operated and the large current is measured. This method detects and corrects errors between input signals and output signals, and cancels the distortion component of the output stage. The protection circuit also has its own ingenuity to realize stable current supply capability for short circuits and overloads. It seems that the type name of the front panel is different depending on the time of production.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Quad 606 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/QUAD/amp/606.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d-707-xcd-decade":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier developed with the aim of purer playback of digital sources such as CDs. The CD Direct Position is installed to reproduce the sound quality of the CD as completely as possible. When the CD Direct switch is pressed, the signal from the CD player goes directly to the Twin Diamond X Balance section via the dedicated volume without passing through any switches or circuits. The volume section uses a special 4-row detent volume in which a CD-only volume and a master volume are co-located, and is also a low-impedance type that advantageous in sound quality. The volume level display in the CD Direct Position is separate from that in the normal position. The CD Direct Position Indicator lights up to indicate the volume knob. Twin Diamond X balance system is adopted for the power amplifier section. In this circuit system, balanced input, transmission, and amplification are performed on the plus side and the minus side equally, and hum and noise are canceled. Moreover, since it is completely separated from ground, it is not affected by ground.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-D 707 XCD Decade (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707xcddecade-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-d-707-xcd-decade.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707xcddecade-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d707xcddecade(1).jpg"}},"tandberg-tpa-3016-a":{"more":[{"t":"Dual mono-configuration stereo amplifier. loudspeaker Increases driving force and enables low impedance loads of 2Ω or less. The power stage uses 8 MOS-FETs per channel to realize the current supply capacity of 100A. The driver adopts feed forward circuit to eliminate the ON resistance of MOS-FET. This ensures low output impedance up to several hundred kHz and improves medium and high resolution. Equipped with an auto fan that operates at 60°C or higher. The thermal servo is used instead of the return type servo which causes sound quality degradation. Zero-NFB circuit We have selected parts such as polypropylene capac, metal film resistance, gold plated input/output terminal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Tandberg TPA 3016 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TANDBERG/amp/tpa-3016a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-130":{"more":[{"t":"Multi-function receiver with built-in microphone mixing circuit with an upright see-through deck and microphone echo. The deck is equipped with TPS (Automatic Tape Selection Mechanism), which is convenient when you want to listen to the song you just listened to again, or when you skip a song and listen to the next song.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SA-130 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/sa-130-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-m-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥74,800. The turntable is made of aluminum die-casting and is available in 2.5kg. This makes it possible to achieve stable rotation performance by acquiring a huge iner moment of 427 kg and cm2. This enables constant-speed rotation in 0.9 seconds and 1/4 rotation, while also obtaining excellent negative variable motion characteristics. The stop mechanism adopts a reliable pure electronic brake. TECHNICS' unique integrated structure direct-drive is used to integrate motor's rotary magnet with turntable. In addition, it has excellent rotation characteristics by equipped with quartz control to compensate the rotation performance with excellent accuracy. In addition, all-round detection F.G. is highly accurate for rotation speed detection. We use quartz, linear and synthesizer method to control pitch freely within the range of ±6% constant speed rotation while maintaining superior rotation by quartz control.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-M 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-m2.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-ma-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥59,800. Quartz direct-drive full automatic player with electronic drive tonearm. The electronic drive tonearm was developed based on technics traditional player technology. It eliminates the complexity of operation and realizes arm ability to demonstrate cartridge performance. The electronic drive tonearm is equipped with a proprietary direct-drive arm control motor with one vertical and horizontal drive motor. It is designed with no load on the drive motor in the arm part in the playing state and realizes high sensitivity arm that does not change to conventional arm while full auto arm of motor drive. It is equipped with a full automatic electronic control mechanism, and you can start playing just by putting the record and clicking on the start button. In addition, the end detection of the record adopts a contactless type auto mechanism that utilizes magnetic properties, making it a design that does not force the arm to participate. In addition, all queuing and arm movements in search of songs in the middle of the record are available with the front button operation, and the LED multi-display is equipped with the arm base part to display these operating conditions easily. A convenient search function is installed to find songs and parts you want to hear in the middle of a record, and you can search two speeds depending on how you push the search key.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-MA 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-ma1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v40":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier with classAA technology. ClassAA has a VC-4 amplifier configuration with two types of amplifiers for each L and R. One is a pure class A voltage-controlled amplifier that is free from switching distortion and crossover distortion, and the other is a current-driven amplifier that drives speakers dynamically. As a result, the voltage-controlled amplifier is freed from the burden of current supply, and the voltage can be controlled faithfully to the input signal. The current-driven amplifier supplies the current required to drive the speaker and eliminates adverse effects such as impedance fluctuations of the speaker. The power supply section uses a large transformer and a large capacitor with an instantaneous current supply capacity of 300A and excellent linearity. In addition, the output stage and power supply section are integrated with an ingenious configuration by a unique concentrated power block, eliminating the negative effects of electromagnetic fields from the root and eliminating high-frequency distortion caused by electromagnetic radiation. Equipped with a Route 6 input jack, you can check the selected source with an indicator. Equipped with the CD direct function, it is possible to connect directly to a volume without using the input selector.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V40 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v40-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v60":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier with classAA technology of SE-A100/SU-A200. ClassAA has a VC-4 amplifier configuration with two types of amplifiers for each L and R. One is a pure class A voltage-controlled amplifier that is free from switching distortion and crossover distortion, and the other is a current-driven amplifier that drives speakers dynamically. As a result, the voltage-controlled amplifier is freed from the burden of current supply, and the voltage can be controlled faithfully to the input signal. The current-driven amplifier supplies the current required to drive the speaker and eliminates adverse effects such as impedance fluctuations of the speaker. The power supply section is equipped with a large transformer and a large capacitor with an instantaneous current supply capacity of 300A and excellent linearity. In addition, the output stage and the power supply section are integrated with an ingenious configuration by a unique concentrated power block, eliminating high-frequency distortion caused by electromagnetic radiation. Equipped with a REC mode selector that allows you to select the recording source independently. Equipped with the CD direct function, it is possible to connect directly to a volume without using the input selector.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V60 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v60-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v80":{"more":[{"t":"An integrated amplifier developed with SE-A100 and SU-C200 technologies. The amplifier circuit is equipped with VC-4 amplifier configuration and ClassAA. A ClassAA system is adopted in which a voltage-controlled amplifier and a current-driven amplifier are separated. In addition, a VC-4 amplifier configuration is adopted in which the left and right amplifiers are independent from each other. As a result, voltage control that is extremely faithful to the input signal and current supply that is sufficient for speaker drive are compatible. A 300 VA high-power transformer is used for the power supply. The transformer is wound with oxygen-free copper wire made of the highest quality materials. A high-density and extremely thick winding has been realized by our unique perfectly aligned winding method. A coil 1.4 times larger than the conventional one can be wound in the same cross-sectional area.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v80-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"victor-ql-y-44-f":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥59,800. Full automatic player with big turntable, high torque low vibration motor, electronic control arm, etc. The turntable uses a 32.7cm long turntable, which increases the iner mass by a large turntable. In addition, the FG speed detection method and double servo FGtz circuit improve the stability of the quartz lock. Contactless electronic control is available for full automatic system. The pulse count of the light sensor and microcomputer automatically detects the presence and size of the record, automatically selects the rotation speed and sends the arm to the start position accurately. In addition, since it can correspond to record of special rotation speed, it is equipped with a manual switch of rotation speed. When you want to hear from the middle of the record, you can freely tap the arm operation button. It is also possible to move arm by hand during operation. Tonearm is equipped with a high rigid tapered straight pipe arm using electro servo method.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor QL-Y 44 F (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/player/ql-y44f.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ax-500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥49,800. In order to transmit the high sound quality of the CD straight, CD Direct Switch is equipped with a CD source that can be enjoyed at the top priority for other inputs. The normal volume control position is as it is, the sound volume of the medium is increased by narrowing down the consistency as well as the bass and high fre cies are set to the optimal volume according to the changing volume of the medium narrowed down. controls, Treble tone control The tone bypass switch is equipped with a tone circuit. MM/MC cartridge selector","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha AX-500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ax-500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ax-900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥79,800. LiD power supply, ALA circuit Low-impedance Drivability power supply GTGT (7.5kg, 350VA) is a twin-vibration design that is filled with silicon sand and polybutagene resin. 22000μFx2 is equipped with high speed, low impedance design Digital Ready Kemicon, and pole OFC power supply cable to improve the affordability. The power supply circuit is equipped with a power supply circuit. The signal base is completely separate from the fountain collisorator, the pre and power section, and the placement is collected so that the signal path is not overlapping, increasing S/N and ensuring low distortion rate. In addition, the remote type loudspeaker switch by connecting rod is used to avoid the wiring pulling of large output loudspeaker output signal. In order to transmit the high sound quality of the CD straight, CD Direct Switch is equipped with a CD source that can be enjoyed at the top priority for other inputs. The CD Direct Pre is a simple and straight preamplifier configuration that is only used for audio muting, volume control, and CD Direct Pre.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha AX-900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ax-900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cx-10000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥800,000. Preamplifier was developed to comm rate the 100th anniversary of its founding. The waves of digitalization and the waves of regeneration of the sound field that began to germinate, and the waves of high-quality visualization that cannot be seen from the shore, were created with a collection of the current highest level of electronics that can be possessed. DEQ (Digital Parametric equalizer) This DEQ is different from the conventional variant GEQ, and it can be precisely set the center frequency, level, and Q (the sharpness of the valley), which are the three major elements of the equalizer, and the logic control does not damage the sound quality that is precisely corrected by remote control. This DEQ incorporates LOW-cut filters and HIGH-cut filters in three-band parametric configurations: LOW-band, MID-band, and HIGH-band. The LOW band covers 20 Hz to 500 Hz, and the HIGH band covers 2 kHz to 20 kHz. The MID band covers up to 22 Hz to 18 kHz, which is the center frequency set by LOW and HIGH bands. Level adjustment can be adjusted from -12dB to +6dB in 0.1dB steps for both 3 bands. Q is from standard 0.7, 4 steps for1.4 1.4, 3.0 and 6.0. It is possible to change the amount of icola in broad and narrow.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CX-10000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cx-10000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-cx-10000.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cx-10000.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cx-10000.JPG"}},"yamaha-m-35":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥39,800. 2ch/4ch multi-use power amplifier. 2ch and 4ch can be switched by switch. 4 When the amplifier is F/R (front and back), 2 loudspeaker, 2 loudspeaker level adjustment function that can adjust the volume of L/R (left and right). Equipped with an AC outlet and built-in DC detection protection circuit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha M-35 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/m-35.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-mx-10000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥800,000. amplifier was developed to comm rate its 100th anniversary. The HC (Twin-Screen) A-class operation circuit is used to eliminate migration to AB-class operation during low impedance drive. This keeps the A-class operation and keeps the linearity of input and output even if it exceeds twice the idling current. However, HC circuit does not have gain, so we have a power MOS FET and power current mirror output circuit. This is composed of 4 para push pulls. In order to eliminate large-scale fever problems with A-class amplifier, the dual AMP class A configuration is used for two SEPP amplifiers in one ch. In addition to the output stage, the power buffer is equipped to supply the required power. The dual amplifier class A eliminates the unstable element of the amplifier due to the fact that the current flows to the earth because the earth is a non-current earth that only determines the ground potential.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha MX-10000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/mx-10000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-mx-10000.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/mx-10000.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/mx-10000.JPG"}},"accuphase-c-200-v":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1987. This is the fifth model of the C-200 series. Based on full amplification stage push-pull drive, it is composed of cascode, bootstrap and complimentary service class A push-pull circuit. The amplifier consists of a constant current load and FET buffer input with fet buffer input with a cascode bootstrap to reduce heavy noise and lower distortion factor. Next, a class A class Cascode differential push-pull and a class A class Cascode push-pull drive the Darlington class A push-pull output. The feature of the cascode connection is that there is little feedback between input and output, and good characteristics can be obtained especially in the high frequency range. Also, the gain is large, linearity is maintained up to the operating limit of the element, distortion is reduced, and S/N is improved. In addition, the important power supply section is reinforced with a full-scale constant-voltage power supply circuit on each of the left and right channel boards. An equalizer amplifier is used to play back analog disks. The MC/MM switching is performed by changing the gain.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-200 V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-200V-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-c-202":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1987. In addition to the normal line amplifier, this stereo preamplifier has a built-in CD-only amplifier for maximum sound quality. In addition to the normal line amplifier, a CD-specific buffer amplifier is built in in order to play CDs at the marginal quality. The CD amplifier consists of a class A push-pull -pull balance circuit in all stages. The signal enters directly from the input terminal. The functions are limited to the minimum necessary functions of volume adjustment and attenuator. This simplifies the signal path and provides a detailed and stereophonic sound field. All stages of the line-only amplifier are A-class push-pull. It performs high-purity amplification and is equipped with the necessary functions as a preamplifier in preparation for multiple inputs. Only a -20dB attenuator and volume control are installed in the CD signal path.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-202 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-202-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-c-280-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1987. The C-280 is a stereo preamplifier with two balanced line amplifiers and ten input terminals. In order to realize balanced transmission with higher quality than conventional transformers, we have installed a balanced transmission line amplifier composed of two amplifiers, one for the hot side and the other for the cold side. The same complimentary service differential push-pull amplifier circuit is used for each amplifier. Also, the volume is controlled by a precision 4-channel volume (linked to LR channel) which is completely divided into hot and cold. In addition to Class A push-pull in all amplifier stages, the cascode system is further advanced, and an FET is used in the load side of the cascode-connected amplifier, so that there is no need to worry about base current leakage when using a bipolar transistor. Thus, a reproduction sound with less coloring is required. DC servo system by IC is adopted for all unit amplifiers, and DC drift is prevented by detecting DC generated at output and returning to input. With the DC servo system and precise design, there is almost no DC drift, and all signal systems from MC input to output are directly connected. The base plate is firmly fixed with screws, and the output element of class A amplifier and the element of constant voltage power supply are tightly fixed to the housing for heat dissipation, preventing resonance due to induction and vibration.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-280 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-280L-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-e-305":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1987. This integrated amplifier was developed for the new audio era by making use of the development technology and materials of the separate amplifier cultivated over many years. A full-scale 3-amp configuration consisting of an equalizer amplifier for analog disks, a high-gain pre-amplifier and a power amplifier has been adopted to enhance the perfection of each. The output stage of the power amplifier is 3 parallel push-pull with 6 transistors, and Pc (collector loss) is 130W per element, making up a powerful output stage with a total of 780W. This realizes \"low load drive\" that can deliver sufficient power even for low load impedance. MOS FET is used in the front stage of driving the output stage. In addition, the input stage is a cascode system, and together with a constant current load, wide bandwidth and high linearity are realized. The second stage differential amplifier circuit consists of a single-chip dual transistor as a complimentary service circuit, resulting in low noise and excellent stability. All the unit amplifiers of each stage are connected directly from the analog disk input. The problem of DC drift caused by direct connection is solved by stabilizing each unit amplifier with DC servo.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase E-305 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/E-305-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-m-1000":{"more":[{"t":"This monaural power amplifier was developed as the first full-scale high-output power amplifier for consumer use for the new era of audio. Not only high output but also high sound quality is emphasized, and the technology developed by AccuPhase is used to pursue maximum performance. It is composed of a balanced system in which two push-pull drive unit amplifiers of all stages are bridge-connected to improve the performance. By adopting a balanced method with a transmission system dedicated to plus and minus signals, in principle external noise is cancelled, and at the same time distortion generated in the amplifier is also cancelled by the output circuit, making it possible to extract pure signal components. Each unit amplifier has a deluxe configuration of 14-parallel push-pull, and the output transistor is specified to have a collector loss of 150W and a total of 56 output transistors in two units. In addition, a large solid aluminum radiator is attached, and it can be used without a radiator fan under normal conditions. The output stage is arranged so that it can be switched to the operation state which matches each condition so that large power can be taken out in any load impedance. By switching the low load impedance with the switch for switching the applied voltage, large currents of 1600W at 1 Ω load and 1100W at 2 Ω load can be extracted.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase M-1000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/M-1000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-102":{"more":[{"t":"Released January 1987 at ¥235,000. This is a class A stereo power amplifier that adopts a fully balanced push-pull system. Balanced transmission is applied to all systems from input to output, enabling high-quality power transmission. In the balanced transmission method, a dedicated transmission system is installed for each of the plus and minus signals. In principle, this system cancels the external noise and at the same time cancels the distortion generated by the amplifier, so that the pure signal component can be extracted. Class A drive system is adopted, and the input stage and output stage are class A operated. The output stage is composed of parallel push-pull transistors for high-band power amplification with collector loss Pc = 80W. The total Pc of the unit amplifier on one side is 320W, realizing an output stage with a margin. The output stage can withstand low impedance loads by providing a margin, and the pre-drive stage employs a power MOS FET drive, an original Accu-Phase system, to achieve an ideal drive. Class A cascode differential push-pull is adopted for the input stage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-102 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-102-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-300-v":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1987 at ¥350,000. This integrated amplifier is based on the push-pull drive of all amplification stages and is composed entirely of cascode connection with excellent high-frequency characteristics up to the drive stage. Following the original P-300, the model has been changed to P-300S, P-300X, P-300L, and P-300V. In the fifth generation, an ultra-low impedance drive capable of withstanding 1 Ω load and a more complete balanced input circuit have been realized. The output stage consists of 10 parallel wide-band transistors with collector loss Pc of 130W for a total of 20 transistors. As a result, the total Pc is 2600W per channel, and when the power efficiency of the output stage is assumed to be 70%, the theoretical limit output reaches 3700W. This structure allows linear high-quality power to be sent even at low load impedance. Since 20 transistors are configured in 10 parallel, it can cope with a large current under a low impedance load and can drive even at a low impedance of 1 Ω. Bridge connection is enabled. Bridge connection is a method in which signals of the same magnitude but opposite phase (reversed phase) are input to the same amplifier, and a speaker is connected to the output terminals of both amplifiers to obtain double output at the 4 Ω load in stereo driving.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-300 V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-300V-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"dbx-bx-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥800,000. 4 channel power amplifier with powerful output for wide dynamic range of digital sources. In order to respond to digital sources, we are constantly seeking to maintain high-power headrooms, not just in the instant, but also in front of the short circuit. It is also possible to use it as a high-power stereo amplifier by bridge connection as well as as a amplifier channel power amplifier. 250W high speed bipolar power trans is used for output stage. There is no fan or limiting circuit, and it is designed to shut down automatically when the temperature rises. This enables quiet operation while being large output.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – DBX BX-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DBX/amp/bx-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/dbx-bx-1.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DBX/amp/bx-1.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DBX/amp/bx-1.jpg"}},"denon-dap-5500":{"more":[{"t":"Released March 1987 at ¥200,000. Digital preamplifier with a thorough separation of digital and analog parts. In addition, both chas substrates are divided into two sheets up and down depending on the nature of the circuit and shielded between them with aluminum plates. This structure eliminates common ground lines between both digital and analog chas and is completely separate from independent power supply and prevents inter-interference between digital and analog. The D/A conversion unit has 4DA push pull and superlinear converter. This circuit adds the idea of hi-fi audio to the superlinear converter. We use carefully selected 4 D/A converters to convert digital data from the Opto-Isolator output into two positive and reverse data, and send each data to two D/A converters of the push-pull configuration, and add the output to the arithmetic instrument.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon DAP-5500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/dap-5500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dra-75-vr":{"more":[{"t":"An AV receiver with a synthesizer tuner and wireless remote control. We emphasize the quality of the amplifier section and incorporate DENON's amplifier technology. The power stage adopts a non-switching class A power amplifier stage with a complete DC amplifier configuration. The main signal and power supply are completely separated via a heat sink to prevent quality degradation. Equipped with a 16-station random preset FM/AM synthesizer tuner. 16 random preset memories are available by combining FM and AM stations. It uses a 4-way tuning system. For example, one touch random preset tuning that directly calls the desired station out of 16 stored stations, automatic tuning that automatically finds and tunes radio waves by auto-scanning, manual tuning that detects weak radio waves, and last-channel memory tuning that selects the station that was last received. A terminal type low-impedance loop antenna is used in the AM section.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DRA-75 VR (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/amp/dra-75vr-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"dual-cs-505-3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥85,000. Semi-auto belt drive player with ULM type tonearm and floating structure. The turntable part uses a belt drive method using a 16-pole beltronus motor. Tonearm is equipped with ULM (Ultra Light Mass) tonearm. This arm inherits advanced technology with four-point support gyro structures in both the upper and lower directions, making it easier to simplify its structure and makes it lighter. A dynamic balance type with spring tension is available for needle pressure. In order to prevent the coloration of the sound by resonance of the arm, the arm pipe and the balance weight are separated. The structure of the cabinet is integrated with tonearm, motor and turntable on a rigid board. This board is floating from the cabinet through a dedicated spring that enhances the anti-vibration effect. This structure keeps the interconnection between turntable and tonearm even if it is a big shock, and prevents howling and needle jumping.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Dual CS 505-3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/cs505-3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-pm640-vxi":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥48,000. New PM Vxi Series The number of video input/output and some functions are non-installed. The new PM Vxi series adopts the unique amplifier theory \"HighVoltage/High Current\" which optimizes current and voltage for ΩΩ and 8Ω load. Firstly, if you want to ring 8Ω loudspeaker, you can specify sufficient high voltage so that the current corresponding to the rated output is obtained. The inrush current of 8Ω loudspeaker is less than 4Ω loudspeaker, so it is not necessary to limit the current. In the case of loudΩ loudspeaker, the current consumption is increased, so it is designed to lower the maximum voltage to ensure sufficient current. To prevent dynamic distortion by using NFB, it is designed to enhance naked properties and lower NFB structure.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM640 Vxi (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm640vxi.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/harman-kardon-pm640-vxi.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm640vxi.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm640vxi.JPG"}},"harman-kardon-pm645-vxi":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥65,000. New PM Vxi Series The same technology as advanced machines is introduced. The new PM Vxi series adopts the unique amplifier theory \"HighVoltage/High Current\" which optimizes current and voltage for ΩΩ and 8Ω load. Firstly, if you want to ring 8Ω loudspeaker, you can specify sufficient high voltage so that the current corresponding to the rated output is obtained. The inrush current of 8Ω loudspeaker is less than 4Ω loudspeaker, so it is not necessary to limit the current. In the case of loudΩ loudspeaker, the current consumption is increased, so it is designed to lower the maximum voltage to ensure sufficient current. To prevent dynamic distortion by using NFB, it is designed to enhance naked properties and lower NFB structure.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM645 Vxi (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm645vxi.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-pm655-vxi":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥95,000. New PM Vxi Series The new PM Vxi series adopts the unique amplifier theory \"HighVoltage/High Current\" which optimizes current and voltage for ΩΩ and 8Ω load. Firstly, if you want to ring 8Ω loudspeaker, you can specify sufficient high voltage so that the current corresponding to the rated output is obtained. The inrush current of 8Ω loudspeaker is less than 4Ω loudspeaker, so it is not necessary to limit the current. In the case of loudΩ loudspeaker, the current consumption is increased, so it is designed to lower the maximum voltage to ensure sufficient current. To prevent dynamic distortion by using NFB, it is designed to enhance naked properties and lower NFB structure. The frequency characteristics from 1Hz to 150kHz are cleared from 12 to 20dB range.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM655 Vxi (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm655vxi.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ax-990":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥79,800. Developed from the idea and technology to clean up music signals from various external elements and receive them to loudspeaker. The P.S.R. circuit is used for CD-1 input. This reduces servo noise and microcontroller noise from CD players. In addition, by connecting the ground terminal of the CD player and AX-990 with the attached earth wire, the noise that flowed into the shield wire is bypassed and the sound quality can be improved. In order to prevent the negative impact of vibration and sound pressure, we have adopted the exclusive chas structure of H.S. (high commodity) design. We also deal with slight sound quality deterioration due to the fine vibration of parts. C&D (clean & dynamic) power supply circuit is equipped with direct connection of rectification circuit to power supply circuit with large capacity. The output stage is equipped with the H.D.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC AX-990 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ax-990.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-880-d":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥59,800. This cuts ripple, signal component, and mixed modulate distortion component from power supply, and supplies clean energy to power amplifier, and also has the same effect as a huge battery, and the power supply without ripple increases power capacity. Σ drive is a method that suppresses the occurrence of distortion and sound quality by applying negative feedback (NF) loops to the loudspeaker terminal. The equalizer amplifier includes ICL high GmFET differential input and circuit configuration by IC. CD Direct Switch enables you to pass the balance volume control with the power of input selectors, modes and subsonic switches. The line straight circuit that passes this CD direct circuit and tone control can send the input signal from the CD directly to the amplifier. A dual-lec selector that combines traditional Rec out selectors and source selectors.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-880 D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-880d.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-990-d":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1986 at ¥79,800. It cuts the noise component of power supply. It delivers clean energy to the power amplifier and demonstrates the performance of the DLD circuit that delivers high-quality power. The DLD circuit drives two high power and low power amplifiers together with dedicated power supply to achieve energy-filled sounds that could not be heard in conventional 130W classes. You can use Σ drive to suppress the occurrence of distortion during the loudspeaker implementation. In normal amplifiers, there were impedance of patterns and wiring materials outside the negative feedback (NF) loop, phase compensation coil, relay, loudspeaker switch, etc., and the performance degradation caused by the output terminal of the amplifier, but the Σ drive puts the negative feedback (NF) loop to the loudspeaker terminal, increasing the performance of the loudspeaker terminal of the amplifier. The equalizer amplifier is equipped with 40mS Hi-Gm FET differential input and high SN and low distortion rate circuit using IC.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-990 D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-990d.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-990-ex":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥79,800. an integrated amplifier designed to achieve higher purity sound quality with a thorough vibration-proof design. In order to reduce noise and distortion due to vibration from outside, we have developed and adopted a strut air suspension. In addition, these main parts have higher rigidity in the moving parts of aluminum die casting, and the vibration from the floor is eliminated as much as possible. In addition, the case uses a high-strength anti-vibration case with a steel plate, which increases weight and uses a new structure such as a logical flow constructor to prevent sound quality degradation. In order to reduce the influence of sound quality degradation by in-home power supply, we have developed our own clean room power supply. This cuts ripple, signal component, and mixed modulation distortion component from power supply, and supplies clean energy to power amplifier, and also has the same effect as a huge battery, making power supply substantially increased by large power supply without ripple.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-990 EX (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-990ex.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-c-06":{"more":[{"t":"Released March 1988 at ¥260,000. Preamplifier pursuing faithful transmission capability and rich musical expression ability. C-06 is equipped with a duo balance amplifier that has excellent balance characteristics, and it is a simple configuration with a pair-balanced amplifier that can be used for balance input and unbalance input. In addition, after passing the amplifier, it minimizes the sound quality of the reverse-phase output caused by passing the different amplifier (normally gained amplifier) twice. In addition, we have obtained more clear sound quality by simplifying the signal path. volume control is equipped with a new 4th Altimate Attenuator. In addition, we distribute glass epoxy substrates, gold-plated finishes, non-magnetic resistors, and use shields by die-casts and extrusions to improve quality. The power supply unit is equipped with a copper-plated case Troidal.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman C-06 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/c-06.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-117":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1987 at ¥135,000. D/A converter integrated integrated amplifier developed as the successor of LV-109. Built-in D/A converter supports digital input. This enables the transmission of digital signals to the last minute of power amplifier. LV-117 adopts a versatile interface format that supports both coaxial and light systems. With a line straight function, you can jump all functions other than the input selector directly to the power amplifier. In this function, tone circuit, mode function, and balance function are difted, which is effective for improving sound clarity. 3 video inputs are available for visual sources such as Hi-Fi VTR and video disk. LV-117 has built-in video buffer amplifier to support high image quality playback.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman LV-117 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lv-117.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-06":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1987 at ¥330,000. A true pure A-class model and a very powerful power supply unit. We have a genuine Pure A-grade system that measures a certain bias current up to the maximum output. It also supports low impedance load from 2Ω, and has earned stable loudspeaker driving capacity. Digital display peak power meter This meter can be switched to 3 stages of 1/3/5 sec. In addition, it can be switched to 4/6/8. The meter brightness can be adjusted to three stages by dimer switch. In addition, it is possible to completely separate power supply from the signal system by turning off the power supply of the entire display system.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-06 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m-06.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-m-07":{"more":[{"t":"Released December 1987 at ¥750,000. A true pure A-class model and a very powerful power supply unit. In addition to the pure A-weight amplifier, we have achieved high power of 100W+100W. This structure eliminates interference thoroughly and improves sound quality. High energy supply capacity and long output level support 2Ω low impedance load. Digital peak power meter is mounted to display the instantaneous output change of the music signal at peak value.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman M-07 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/m-07.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-r-117":{"more":[{"t":"Some audio purists believe that quality audio died in the late 1970’s. However, the Luxman R-117 refutes this view. No, it doesn’t have a silver face. Yes, it was built in late 1980’s at the edge of what some might call the vintage era. But, at 160 watts per channel it is a monster receiver. Not only does it have power it has the features to make it arguably the best receiver Luxman ever made. Referred to in the advertising literature as the Ultimate Power Receiver it was theirs top of the line receiver and was made in Japan. It retailed for $1200 in 1987 but had dropped to close out pricing of $1000 by 1992. With the advent of the compact disc era audio manufacturers had to adapt to the changing market.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Luxman R-117","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/luxman-r-117","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"micro-seiki-ap-m-1":{"more":[{"t":"This record player was developed by condensing the high-inertia concept realized in the SX 8000 II into an integrated small player and taking into consideration the design concept of the first micro CD player, the CD-M2. In order to completely eliminate the influence of external vibration and reproduce the analog source more pure, we have developed an oil floating suspension and adopted it in the AP-M1. This system consists of a high-precision floating spring with upper and lower diaphragms filled with damping oil, and a damping plate to absorb vibration. As a result, we have obtained the best howling margin in our class. This suspension can be adjusted by a 3-point screw at the top of the body. For the turntable, we have adopted a super-heavy composite double-structure turntable with a high-inertia concept, inheriting the blood line of the SX 8000 II. In order to rotate this turntable stably, we have also adopted the same control system as the SX 8000 II. The structure of the motor is a motor unit with a built-in ultra-small BTL amplifier. A high-precision 8-pole synchronous motor is driven by a bi-amplifier.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Micro Seiki AP-M 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MICRO/player/ap-m1-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"nad-7220-pe":{"more":[{"t":"Introduced around 1987 this NAD 7220PE Power Envelope receiver was one of NAD’s lower end offerings at the time. It is rated at just 20 watts per channel into 8 ohms. NAD’s goal was to build affordable audio gear that performed well sonically and they did just that. The money they saved, by utilizing a very basic design on the front panel, they used on internal components along the signal path. This resulted in a very good sounding receiver for what some would call a budget price. And, at less than a $300 list price it was definitely within most peoples budgets. The features on the 7220PE are minimal with only bass and treble controls, a phone jack, mono and loudness switches, and various input switches. It also has 5 station presets. While the NAD 7220PE is a great sounding receiver, NAD receivers in general are known for being problematic.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – NAD 7220 PE","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/nad-7220pe","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-a-616":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥64,800. This is a stereo integrated amplifier designed to minimize signal paths, eliminate vibration and resonance, and improve speaker drive performance at low load. The input block is designed to minimize signal routing, and the volume and power amplifier are directly connected when the source / direct switch is turned ON, so you can enjoy more pure sound. The power amplifier block is laid out along the signal flow to minimize the distance from the power supply. In the speaker selector block, the relay board and the speaker terminal are connected directly to reduce unnecessary wiring. A honeycomb shape with high rigidity and excellent vibration damping is adopted everywhere, and vibration is dispersed and damped in many directions, while vibration distortion noise is kept low by high rigidity. In addition, the honeycomb heat sink of the chimney type has an excellent heat radiation effect. In addition, we have adopted a honeycomb structure for the insulator to reduce vibration from outside. The volume has a balanced structure that reduces the mechanical stress of the volume body and uses a floating structure to minimize the effect of vibration. Non-switching circuit TypeII which further expands the region of 0 switching distortion is adopted.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer A-616 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-616-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-a-717":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥79,800. This integrated amplifier was developed as the culmination of a fundamental review of the circuit, construction and physical properties, which are the origins of the amplifier, in order to respond to digital sources. The design philosophy of this amplifier is roughly divided into three points. First, each signal block is appropriately arranged in order to make the signal path the shortest distance. Second, thorough anti-vibration and anti-resonance measures are taken. Third, the drive performance of the speaker is improved at low load. We are solving various problems by investing various technologies in these areas. First, a structure called direct construction is adopted in order to make the signal path the shortest distance. By separating each circuit block and shielding the I/O block, adverse effects such as internal signal degradation and interference between signals can be prevented. The input block allows remote mechanical control of the Input & Recording Selector and the main volume to minimize signal routing.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer A-717 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-717-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-a-90-d":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥220,000. The EX series stereo prestereo integrated amplifier with built-in D/A converter and improved internal construction to eliminate factors that cause noise and distortion. Digital input / output is equipped with two optical input systems and one optical output system. In order to prevent the pulse width from changing when the optical fiber is bent or vibrated, an optical transmission distortion correction circuit is mounted on the input side and output side respectively to reduce noise. In the DAC section, the phase difference is eliminated by mounting a D/A converter for each L/R, and the separation is improved by separating the L/R. This D/A converter employs a specially developed glitch less IC that minimizes the occurrence of glitches. This eliminates the analog switch called a digricher, thereby improving performance and sound quality. Furthermore, by adding an MSB error correction circuit to each IC, the linearity at the 0 cross point is greatly improved. In addition, in order to prevent degradation of sound quality due to jitter (fluctuation of the clock edge), a PLL with an extremely high jitter suppression effect is adopted for the PLL that generates the clock, and the oscillation circuit is bonded with special resin in order to avoid the effect of vibration. When the D/A converter operates, only one master clock system is used, and the generation of unnecessary beat components is suppressed by eliminating other asynchronous clocks (such as microcomputer clocks).","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer A-90 D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-90d-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"revox-b-150":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥195,000. B250SG Computer-controlled tone circuits, warnings, etc.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Revox B 150 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/amp/b150.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/revox-b-150.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/amp/b150.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/amp/b150.JPG"}},"revox-b-250":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥328,000. Integrated amplifier with B226.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Revox B 250 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/amp/b250.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-222-esr":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥50,700. This material has the characteristics of vibration damping, which has high internal loss compared to metal, and has high strength and high precision machining. The TA-F222ESR is based on the G chas tuned to 12 minutes ally.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 222 ESR (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f222esr.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f-333-esr":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥79,800. Based on TA-F333ESXII, power supply unit and heat sink are tuned to improve the perfection. This material has the characteristics of vibration damping, which has high internal loss compared to metal, and has high strength and high precision machining.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 333 ESR (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f333esr.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"tandberg-tca-3018-a":{"more":[{"t":"Preamplifier designed for analogues. The equalizer amplifier is the CR equalizer. The line amplifier part is a high input design, and it is designed to not affect inputs of 20V or more. Zero-NFB circuit We use carefully selected parts, such as polypropylene capac with no dielectric loss, reliable metal film resistance, gold plated input and output terminal with high durability.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Tandberg TCA 3018 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TANDBERG/amp/tca-3018a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"tandberg-tpr-3080-a":{"more":[{"t":"A receiver that pursues high performance comparable to a single compo. 16 stations can be preset in the tuner section. In addition, the tuner part adopts IF filter by computer design, making it possible to satisfy both the selected and distortion rate. tuner Digital display is displayed in the display section. The preamplifier is equipped with MC/MM automatic switch equalizer with dedicated input terminal. Includes Rec out selector, pre-out terminal and video input terminal. The thermal servo button does not affect the sound quality. Full remote control is available with optional remote control unit.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Tandberg TPR 3080 A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TANDBERG/amp/tpr-3080a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/tandberg-tpr-3080-a.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TANDBERG/amp/tpr-3080a.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TANDBERG/amp/tpr-3080a.jpg"}},"technics-su-v-100-d":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier equipped with D/A converter. The D/A conversion section uses a 4-DAC 18-bit conversion system. In the 4DAC 18-bit conversion system, two D/A converters are installed in each L/R channel to process the + and - components of the input signal independently. A total of four D/A converters are used in the 4DAC conversion system. In this circuit, first of all, a newly developed 4 DAC processor LSI distinguishes between + and - signals from the input digital signal, and high-speed processing is performed by switching two D/A converters. This realizes D/A conversion without 0 cross distortion in principle. In addition, the D/A converter achieves 18-bit operation at an average music level of -12dB or less by using a 4 DAC processor LSI. This, combined with the use of a 4 x oversampling 18-bit digital filter, provides more faithful analog waveform reproduction capability. Three sampling frequencies, 32 kHz, 44.1 kHz and 48 kHz, are available for use with CD players, DAT and BS tuners.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V 100 D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v100d-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v-90-d":{"more":[{"t":"Integrated amplifier equipped with D/A converter. The D/A conversion section uses a 4-DAC 18-bit conversion system. In the 4DAC 18-bit conversion system, two D/A converters are installed in each L/R channel to process the + and - components of the input signal independently. A total of four D/A converters are used in the 4DAC conversion system. In this circuit, first of all, a newly developed 4 DAC processor LSI distinguishes between + and - signals from the input digital signal, and high-speed processing is performed by switching two D/A converters. This realizes D/A conversion without 0 cross distortion in principle. In addition, the D/A converter achieves 18-bit operation at an average music level of -12dB or less by using a 4 DAC processor LSI. This, combined with the use of a 4 x oversampling 18-bit digital filter, provides more faithful analog waveform reproduction capability. Three sampling frequencies, 32 kHz, 44.1 kHz and 48 kHz, are available for use with CD players, DAT and BS tuners.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V 90 D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v90d-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-100x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥64,800. 340mm wide compact component series. CD Direct Switch In addition, it is possible to connect portable audio devices easily by specifying the sound input terminal with mono input in the sealing panel.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-100X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-100x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-a-100x.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-100x.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-100x.JPG"}},"yamaha-a-2000a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥195,000. integratedation with Pure A grade amplifier and high power AB grade amplifier (boot strap) with Dual Class Class A with ZDR circuit. ZDR circuit cancels the slight distortion component generated in the output stage. It has a large capacity of 240,000μF in both ch55000μFx2 and ch4700μFx2 in the voltage amplifier. The volume control adopts precision four-column volume control, which narrows down before and after flat amplifier, and improves the actual use S/N to reduce noise even when the volume is small. We are striving to improve sound quality such as copper plated chas, oxygen-free copper wire material, gold plated pin jack terminal, etc.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-2000a (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-2000a.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-a-200x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥79,800. 340mm wide compact component series. ZDR circuit circuit is installed in the class A turbo system that migrates to AB-class operation when small output is A-class operation. Equipped with 3 video inputs (VD, VTR1, and front VTR2), CD direct switch is available.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha A-200X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-200x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-a-200x.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-200x.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/a-200x.JPG"}},"yamaha-mvs-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥19,800. This greatly improves S/N during real use.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha MVS-1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/etc/mvs-1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-p-530":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥39,800. Record player with full automatic function. The direct drive method is used for the turntable drive. The motor uses DC motor to achieve stable rotation by the FG servoz servo method which compares FG (fr ency generator) signal and quartz signal. MM type cartridge is used for cartridge. The front operation method is used to close the dust cover all operations. AVC-30/AVC-50","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-530 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-530.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-p-530.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-530.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-530.JPG"}},"yamaha-p-m-77":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥22,000. Compact size full automatic player developed as AV EDGE option. Front operation method is available. AV EDGE99CDR MM type cartridge is used for cartridge.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha P-M 77 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-m77.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-p-m-77.jpg","xc":2,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-m77.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/p-m77.JPG"}},"accuphase-p-800":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1988 at ¥750,000. This stereo power amplifier is based on the development technology of the M-1000 and aims to achieve both high quality sound and high output. It is composed of a balanced system in which two sets of all stage push-pull drive unit amplifiers are connected to a bridge to improve performance. The balanced method requires a dedicated transmission system for plus and minus signals. However, in principle, external noise is canceled, and at the same time, distortion generated by the amplifier is also canceled by the output circuit, making purer signal transmission possible. In order to achieve the same performance as a monaural amplifier, the power supply section uses an independent power supply for left and right. In addition, two power supplies with only half the power capacity increase the impedance of the power supply compared to a single transformer system, which is disadvantageous. Therefore, the P-800 uses a 1.5 kVA high-capacity transformer that can be used for stereo by one power supply, ensuring sufficient margin. In addition, the filter condenser is 82,000 μ Fx4 with a total capacity of 328,000 μ F. The output stage of each unit amplifier employs a 7-parallel push-pull configuration of wide-band transistors with a collector loss (Pc) of 130W.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-800-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"dual-golden-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1994 at ¥148,000. Gyroscope Gimbal tonearm The drive unit has a microprocessor-controlled quartz belt drive method. Turntable is made of aluminum with anti-vibration coating. With high-pression spring balance and weight tracking force functionality, it delivers smooth sound. Carbon fiber headshell cartridge is equipped with a MM type cartridge DMS750. The cabinet is black lacquered for piano and other purposes.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Dual Golden 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/golden1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/dual-golden-1.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/golden1.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DUAL/player/golden1.jpg"}},"harman-kardon-pm665-vxi":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥168,000. In addition to the High Voltage/High Current theory, the new PM Vxi series has become the top of the high-HICC. The new PM Vxi series adopts the unique amplifier theory \"HighVoltage/High Current\" which optimizes current and voltage for ΩΩ and 8Ω load. Firstly, if you want to ring 8Ω loudspeaker, you can specify sufficient high voltage so that the current corresponding to the rated output is obtained. The inrush current of 8Ω loudspeaker is less than 4Ω loudspeaker, so it is not necessary to limit the current. In the case of loudΩ loudspeaker, the current consumption is increased, so it is designed to lower the maximum voltage to ensure sufficient current. To prevent dynamic distortion by using NFB, it is designed to enhance naked properties and lower NFB structure. The frequency characteristics from 1Hz to 150kHz are cleared from 12 to 20dB range.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon PM665 Vxi (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/pm665vxi.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"jvc-ax-z-911":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥89,800. Equipped with digital pure A circuit. However, because the pure A class operation always keeps constant flow of the output current required for full power, there was a problem that huge power supply is required, and the heat generation is high, and the efficiency is poor. In order to solve these problems, AX-Z911 features a digital pure A signal prediction circuit, which quickly determines the size of the input digital signal, and supplying the power supply voltage to the amplifier when needed to perform high-efficiency pure A-class operation without waste power consumption. The D/A converter is equipped with a four-fold digital filter. The digital signal processing unit is shielded with a plate to cut off the digital and power supply parts that are the source of noise. In addition, the top plate of 3.2mm thickness and the bottom plate of 1.6mm thickness are adopted to reduce the negative impact from the structure and material. The circuit reduces the accuracy of the transmission line. The relay and electronic switch are used to pull the input signal and the loudspeaker terminal is also one. In addition, the DAC Direct Switch is turned on until the digital signal is just before the D/A converter, and the wire length is only 0.5m.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – JVC AX-Z 911 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/amp/ax-z911.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-kp-9010":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥99,800. An analog player with the aim of the expression of quietness that was difficult for an analog player. The motor and arm are equipped with a high-rigidity mechanical short circuit that clarifies the points of motor and arm. The motor and arm are rigid with frames and forms a regeneration circuit that picks up the sound. In addition, it is a unified aluminum die-cast frame that completely float from the regeneration circuit, the cabinet, the cabinet, and the dust cover, which is the source of vibration. This makes it possible to clarify the motor’s branching and arm’s branching, which eliminates vibrations caused by loudspeaker’s sound pressure and vibrations from the floor. This greatly improves sound turbidity. Kenwood’s unique DS (Dynamic Stability) tonearm features a unique knife edge that fixes the points. This makes it possible to trace the tonearm groove without being dragged in the rotation direction even if the tip traces any large signal groove. The DL (Dynamic Center Lock) motor is used to lock the spindle to the absolute center point.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KP-9010 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/kp-9010.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-lv-113":{"more":[{"t":"Released March 1988 at ¥65,700. Integrated amplifier with D/A converter. The D/A converter is equipped with two-stage FIR cascade connection. Passive low-level LPF is used for analog low-pass filter. Digital input supports both optical and coaxial interfaces. The sampling frequency corresponds to 3 types of 32/44/48 kHz. PhonoMM and fono input terminals compatible with high gain MC are installed. It is equipped with a line straight function that connects the input signal directly to the power amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman LV-113 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/lv-113.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-95":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥319,000. Digital integrated amplifier with D/A converter. The D/A converter uses the TDA1541A-S1 LSI, which is carefully selected from the \"A Version\" of the Philips / Marantz group and has a crown mark that certifies the highest quality. It realizes sound quality with excellent reproducibility especially at low levels. The power amplifier section has a simple structure in which the input signal is directly sent from the volume. The first stage is differential amplification with cascode connection, and sufficient gain is secured by the combination of FET and bipolar transistor. The output stage has a triple push-pull configuration and uses a Power-MOS FET, which is an audio power amplifier. In addition, two types of operation, pure class A operation and class AB operation class AB operation. The power supply is equipped with a large toroidal transformer and a large-capacity LowESR type condenser, and a oxygen-free copper 1.53 mm in diameter is used for the wiring material to powerfully drive the speakers. In addition, in order to prevent digital noise from entering the analog circuit, independent power supply parts are adopted, and the analog circuit is equipped with high-speed power supply utilizing high-integration IC with low-noise broadband.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-95 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-95-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"naim-nait-2":{"more":[{"t":"Released August 1988 at ¥140,000. Compact integrated amplifier. There were two types of NAIT2, CD type and MM type. The control section is equipped with an input selector, volume, balance control, tape monitor switching and power switch, making the signal circuit simple and straight. It is designed with an emphasis on power supply capacity. In this method, the power supply voltage is kept low, and instead of disclosing the rated output, the high-capacity circuit of the toroidal transformer quickly responds to the peak current, thereby increasing the speaker drive capacity. An optional pre-out expansion kit is available to upgrade your system with the more powerful NAP90 or NAP140 power amplier. This option bypasses the internal power amplier for better sound quality.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Naim NAIT 2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/NAIMAUDIO/amp/nait2-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/naim-nait-2.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/NAIMAUDIO/amp/nait2-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/NAIMAUDIO/amp/nait2(1).JPG"}},"onkyo-tx-850":{"more":[{"t":"Onkyo’s contribution to the Monster receiver genre is the Onkyo TX-8500. It was Onkyo’s top of the line receiver at the time and put out an under rated 150 watts per channel into 4 ohms and 110 watts per channel into 8 ohms. This line of Onkyo receivers including the TX-2500, TX-4500, TX-6500 and TX-8500 are all under appreciated units. The build quality, performance and features are all second to none. Onkyo was a little late to the scene with their monster receiver so it didn’t receive the fanfare that the Pioneer and Marantz receivers received at the time but it is easily comparable. A later MK II version was released that had a digital tuner along with the analog tuner. As you can see below it is fairly easily distinguished from the original TX-8500 shown above. The TX-8500 does not have an Aux input though it does have 3 Tape inputs so you shouldn’t be short inputs. The amplifier section is one of the best around and the tuning section is no slouch either.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Onkyo TX-850","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-8500","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/onkyo-tx-850.jpg","xc":1,"site":"classicreceivers.com","page":"https://classicreceivers.com/onkyo-tx-8500","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/02/onkyo-tx-8500.jpg"}},"ortofon-ppa-600":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥350,000. A professional stereo amplifier developed for the first time in 20 years from Ortophone. However, PPA600 focuses on the benefits of FET listening. The DC-NFB (DC-NFB) is used for reverse input from the output terminal to the first stage. There is no DC servo for circuit simplification, but there is no worry about DC drift. We use the forced air cooling system by the fan to ensure reliability. In PPA600, fans are not rotated in the internal temperature of about 40°C or less, and when the temperature rises above 40°C, the rotation gradually becomes faster. If the amplifier overheats and the internal temperature exceeds 70°C, the sensor will operate, turn off the protection relay, and disconnect the loudspeaker.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Ortofon PPA 600 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ORTOFON/amp/ppa600.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/ortofon-ppa-600.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ORTOFON/amp/ppa600.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/ORTOFON/amp/ppa600.jpg"}},"pioneer-a-717v":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥96,000. A stereo integrated amplifier based on A-717 and equipped with S terminal. It inherits all the technologies used in the A-717, such as direct construction, vibration-free and resonance-free construction, and low-load drive construction. Equipped with S jacks for two input systems and an output Route 3, it is possible to dub each other by video selector while maintaining high quality image. The power supply for video is equipped with a dedicated transformer, and the circuit and ground for audio and video are separated to minimize adverse effects on sound quality. Also, if the V function is set to OFF, the power supply for the video system is turned OFF, preventing interference with the audio system circuit from the root, and the system is designed to be compatible with video while maintaining superior sound quality.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer A-717V (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-717v-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-a-717v.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-717v-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-717v.JPG"}},"pioneer-c-90a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥180,000. This is a preamplifier that uses Pioneer's amplifier manufacturing technology and know-how, and adheres to the design concept of \"simple is best\". The C-90a employs a monoconstruction structure based on a 3-transformer multi-power supply. The left and right power supply sections are separated for each transformer, and the layout on the printed circuit board is separated for each block to improve the separation. The power supply for the video circuit and the electronic control circuit is supplied from a power transformer and constant voltage circuit separate from the power supply for the audio circuit to prevent mutual interference. The audio and video systems are completely separated from the circuit board and ground board to minimize adverse effects on sound quality. The Phono equalizer uses a hybrid MC transformer system that combines an MC transformer with half the conventional winding ratio and an equalizer amplifier with an increased gain corresponding to the decrease in the step-up ratio. Because the winding ratio is reduced, thicker wire can be used, DC resistance is reduced and stray capacitance between windings is also reduced. This greatly improves the high-frequency characteristics. In addition, the gain of the equalizer amplifier can be made smaller than that of the high-gain equalizer amplifier, so that the total SN ratio can be improved.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer C-90a (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/c-90a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-c-90a.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/c-90a-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/c-90a.JPG"}},"pioneer-m-90a":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥220,000. A stereo power amplifier developed using Pioneer's technology. We pursue three technical themes: direct construction to minimize signal paths in order to eliminate mutual interference of signals, low-load drive capability to improve dynamic drive capability of speakers, and vibration-free and resonance-free construction to reduce vibration and resonance harmful to sound. Two large power transformers are used independently on the left and right, and a 10,000 μ Fx2 resin-coated electrolytic capacitor is used for each channel. In addition, the positive and negative sides of the power supply are divided into two parts from the winding of the power transformer, and each part is bridge rectified by high-speed low-noise diodes. This makes it possible to supply high-power music signals with low distortion. In addition, the power transistor is a Pc = 130W 4-parallel push-pull configuration, realizing a large current supply capability of 47A. In addition to the power input from the normal preamplifier, there are two input jacks, CD direct and line direct. These direct inputs are level-controllable. The CD/Line direct terminal also has a dedicated output terminal, which can be returned to a preamplifier for copying to tape.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer M-90a (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/m-90a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-x-1111-mos-vintage":{"more":[{"t":"This is the last amplifier in the X series that started with AU-X1. Earth-based amplifiers drive the speakers between the output of the amplifier and the ground, so they are susceptible to noise and distortion from the ground, which degrade sound quality. In order to solve this problem, we have adopted a balanced circuit that is not grounded. In this circuit, the - side of the speaker is double-push-pull driven in both directions under the same conditions as the + side. This eliminates unnecessary high-frequency components such as noise and distortion, and realizes an excellent sound image at a low distortion rate. In addition, there is no noise from the power supply and no IHM (Interface Hum Modulation) caused by back electromotive force from the speakers. It also supports changes in the impedance and phase of speakers. The power supply circuit that operates the balanced circuit is also a closed loop with no connection to the ground circuit. In addition, we have achieved low impedance and high speed in the entire power supply by adopting a newly developed heavy-duty transformer that has been carefully examined from the viewpoints of sound quality and electrical performance without simply pursuing a sense of weight.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-X 1111 Mos Vintage (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-x1111mosvintage-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-n-110":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥32,800. Switches can be used as high power mono power amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-N 110 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n110.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-n-110.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n110.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n110.JPG"}},"technics-se-m-100":{"more":[{"t":"Digital straight amplifier using D. D. D. (Digital Direct Drive) system. In the digital direct drive system, the output voltage of the DAC is raised to the required volume voltage, and is directly connected to a power amplifier with an amplification factor of 1 (0 dB) without any connection to the amplifier of the analog source. As a result, the output voltage of the DAC is equal to the voltage at the terminals of the speakers. This realizes playback taking advantage of the high S/N ratio of the digital source. As an output voltage variable means for volume control, a high-voltage I/V converter is provided in the DAC output section to vary the output voltage by changing the exchange ratio. An amplifier with a voltage amplification factor of 1 (0 dB) basically achieves excellent transmission characteristics including low noise level because it does not amplify the voltage.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SE-M 100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/se-m100-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"thorens-td-320-mk-ii":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥268,000. Record player developed as an improved type of TD320. TD320mkII has several variations in tonearm, including SME3009RBlack, SME3009/S2 and TP90. TD321mkII is armless model. In this method, the switchtable, tonearm and motor are independently supported, so the vibration from the motor is difficult to transmit to the regeneration system mecha. In addition, the vibration is reduced by adopting the material which is strong in resonance. The double turntable structure is adopted for prestige. This is a structure that combines the main turntable and the concentric drive sub turntable. It has a strong resonance/sound compared to the conventional shape, and it has a high drive efficiency by the belt.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Thorens TD 320 MK II (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/THORENS/player/td320mkii.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-cx-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥270,000. Stereo preamplifier developed for reference in the multimedia era. In the digital part, a wide capture range Jitterless PLL circuit is mounted to correspond to the time-axis loosening (Jitter) caused by the difference of the ON/OFF speed of the LED which performs optical/electric conversion. This makes it possible to receive high-stable digital data by expanding the capture range to infinite. The D/A conversion features a high-bit system consisting of 8fsx18bit digital filters and 18bit twin D/A converters. This enables pure DAC direct playback that sends D/A conversion signals as it is without setting up the analog low-pass filter which has a high sound quality.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha CX-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/cx-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-mx-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥300,000. Stereo amplifier developed as a reference for the AV multimedia era. 's proprietary HCA (single conversion a ification) circuit enables A-feed operation for all loads and power areas. It realizes the input and output linearity of the A-feed operation regardless of the load level and power value. In addition, HCA circuit has a good transient response because it works as a pure converter without having a feedback loop or gain. Power MOS FET is added to the output terminal of the power buffer. Power MOS FET is a high-voltage control element with input impedance and has features such as reducing the burden of the driver and simplifying the circuit. The A-class rated output 150W+150W is realized with the 4 para-pull configuration using 8 power MOS FETs per channel. Dual FET differential input/cascode boots circuit is used for voltage a ification. The combination of high-fr ency dual FET and wide-band trans with low current leak provides a high-through rate for wideband and transient input.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha MX-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/mx-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-c-11":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1989. This stereo preamplifier was developed by gathering together carefully selected elements and development technologies accumulated over many years. It has a balanced input / output circuit. The high-level flat amplifier that handles signals other than analog disks employs a cascode differential input and a class A push-pull output stage to improve various characteristics. This amplifier has XLR-type balanced connectors for input and output, making ideal balanced transmission possible. The equalizer amplifier has a dedicated input circuit for each MC and MM type cartridge. Considering that the output voltage and output impedance of the MM cartridge are high at the time of MM input, an FET para-input circuit is used to maintain high input impedance over the entire frequency band. Since the signal voltage at the MC input is low, it is important to improve the S/N ratio. Therefore, the input circuit is composed of carefully selected elements with low intrinsic noise. These switching are done by relay, and at the same time, the amplification degree is also switched according to MM/MC.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase C-11 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/C-11-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-e-405":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1989 at ¥350,000. In order to overcome the limitation of the integrated amplifier, the integrated amplifier is composed by combining a pre-amplifier and a power amplifier which are substantially independent. The output stage of the power amplifier is a 5-parallel push-pull configuration with 10 output elements. Each element has a Pc (collector loss) of 130W, so that sufficient power can be sent even under low load. The drive stage that drives the output stage employs a two stage cascode direct-coupled circuit of cascode push-pull and MOS FET cascode push-pull. The cascode connection improves high-frequency characteristics, while the MOS FET minimizes distortion at small outputs. All amplifier stages, including the preamp section, are directly connected. In addition, a selector switch and an input terminal are provided so that the preamp section and the power section can be separated and used as an independent amplifier. When DC voltage is applied for some reason, it is amplified as it is and a large DC appears in the output, which may damage the speaker. Therefore, we have adopted the \"DC servo method\" to cut unnecessary DC components and stabilize the DC drift of the amplifier itself due to temperature changes.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase E-405 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/E-405-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-11":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1989 at ¥230,000. In addition to basic performance such as frequency characteristics, distortion factor, and S/N, a stereo power amplifier with improved low-impedance driving capability to send sufficient energy to speakers with complex characteristics. The output stage consists of three parallel push-pull large output transistors with a Pc (collector loss) of 130W, which provides stable output even at low impedance. The drive stage uses an original power MOS FET only for Accu-phase as a power element with excellent characteristics of withstanding high voltage. The voltage amplification of the preceding stage is carried out by the differential amplifier stage, and a buffer stage is provided to prevent interference with the preamp connected before this stage and the input level control. This buffer stage adopts a cascode method using FET, and has excellent high-frequency characteristics and stable operation even in a large change of input impedance. The power supply section uses a large toroidal transformer with excellent fluctuation coefficient to provide sufficient margin even at maximum output. In order to prevent interference at each stage, separate windings of the transformer are supplied to the output stage and the front stage, respectively. In addition, the front stage is composed of independent left and right rectifiers and filters, so that interference at the front and rear stages and left and right channels is minimized.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-11 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-11-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"accuphase-p-500-l":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1989 at ¥530,000. This is a stereo power amplifier developed using the development technology of the M-1000 and P-800 with the aim of achieving both high output and small signal reproduction. The output stage consists of a parallel push-pull circuit in which 10 wide-band transistors with collector loss (Pc) of 150W per channel are connected in parallel to each other. This reduces the impedance to 1/10 of that when a single unit is used. In addition, the total Pc reaches 3000W, enabling output that is not affected by the load even for speakers whose impedance characteristics fluctuate wildly. In order to improve the switching distortion generated at the output stage at the time of small output, the operating point is strictly set so that each element of PNP and NPN is not cut off (a state in which no current flows) by the input signal. MOS FET, equivalent to non-switching class A drives, is adopted for the front stage driving the last stage, and it is composed of cascode push-pull. Cascode is a circuit used for high-frequency amplification that provides stable operation over a wide frequency band, good input linearity, and enables amplification over a wide dynamic range. A class A cascode push-pull is also used for the pre-stage of sending a signal to the MOS FET. This realizes a stable output stage with little distortion from a small output in the noise region to a large output in the rated output.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Accuphase P-500 L (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/Accuphase-kensonic/amp/P-500L-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"c-e-c-st-930":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥135,000. Record player developed as a collection of CEC players. Newly developed 3-phase brushless FG servo motor is used for drive motor. In order to suppress the occurrence of co, we used to weaken the magnetic force in the motor, and to release the magnetic force between the rotary magnet and the stator. However, this method reduces motor efficiency and torque. Double suspension structure is available. The primary shock absorber suppresses vibration from the internal mechanism and the outermost rover from loudspeaker. The vibrations from vibrations and floors that cannot be absorbed here are absorbed by secondary shock absorbers. With a 3.5kg aluminum die-casting board, it has a high rigidity to control howling.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – C.E.C. ST-930 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/CEC/player/st930.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-poa-7700":{"more":[{"t":"Mono power amplifier with low impedance loudspeaker driving capacity along with digital sources. The output stage is a four-parallel push-pull configuration using the Pc130W high-capacity high-speed power trans. This realizes high power that clears 420W/4Ω. For example, even if loudspeaker drops to 1Ω instantaneously, it realizes high loudspeaker driving ability to drive up to 1.1kW. Dual super free return circuit is available in the amplifier section. This circuit method enables high-speed transmission of signals because the audio signal is a one-way circuit configuration. The distortion servo circuit supports static distortion and unique noise caused by non-linear characteristics of amplifiers such as power trans. The POA-7700 servo of three servo circuits, which eliminate the total distortion of the power stage N and P channels, and the distortion of the total distortion of the loudspeaker output stage. In addition, UCI (Unity Current Interface) circuit is adopted, focusing on the interface characteristics between this amplifier and power stage.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Denon POA-7700 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-7700.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/denon-poa-7700.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-7700.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/DENON/amp/poa-7700.jpg"}},"harman-kardon-hk-6100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1990 at ¥48,000. In addition to our proprietary amplifier technology, High Voltage/High Current, the HK Series integrated amplifier was created with new sound quality improvements.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 6100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk6100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-hk-6500":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1990 at ¥75,000. In addition to our proprietary amplifier technology, High Voltage/High Current, the HK Series integrated amplifier was created with new sound quality improvements.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 6500 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk6500.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-hk-6800":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1990 at ¥135,000. In addition to our proprietary amplifier technology, High Voltage/High Current, the HK Series integrated amplifier was created with new sound quality improvements.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 6800 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk6800.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"harman-kardon-hk-6900":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1990 at ¥185,000. In addition to our proprietary amplifier technology, High Voltage/High Current, the HK Series integrated amplifier was created with new sound quality improvements.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Harman Kardon HK 6900 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/HARMAN_KARDON/amp/hk6900.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-5010":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥45,400. This is a newly developed integrated amplifier that has been developed from the fundamental aspects such as construction, circuit, and characteristics. The power trans is designed as a discrete configuration to determine the drive capability during low impedance of loudspeaker. In this method, all power supply ripples and various noise components are guided to the loudspeaker terminal by the dedicated ground line, and all the ground lines are combined for the first time. This makes it possible to a ify signals only with pure signals. Equipped with a source direct circuit that bypasses tone control, balance control, subsonic filter, etc.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-5010 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-5010.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-ka-7010":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1988 at ¥63,700. Equipped with improved loudspeaker drive capability during low impedance load. The power supply section has a dedicated power for both the plus and the minus side. We develop and adopt pure signal ground line to prevent distortion caused by mixing the ground line of music signal and power supply. In this method, power supply ripple and various noise components are connected to the loudspeaker terminal by the dedicated ground line, and all the ground lines are connected to the first time. In order to shorten the signal path and eliminate inter-interference between each part, the internal layout is considered. The internal layout of INPUT→VOOR→VOLUME→POWER AMP→SPEAKER is realized by specifying the volume control in the center. The equalizer amplifier is equipped with ICL high GmFET differential input and IC.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood KA-7010 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/ka-7010.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-540":{"more":[{"t":"Released February 1989 at ¥240,000. This is an integrated amplifier designed with the same concept as the L-570 that reproduces life in music as it is pure. The power amplifier section adopts a pure A class system, inheriting the design concept of the M-07. In this system, the bias current necessary for the class A operation region is always supplied, and in the region exceeding the class A operation (15W + 15W), the operation naturally shifts to the class AB operation based on the class A. Thus, the sound quality of class A and the power of class AB are obtained. In the power supply section, the winding of the power transformer is made independent for each stage to eliminate the influence between the stages with different output levels as much as possible. The input terminal uses a flexible switch and a nitrogen gas sealed contact relay to realize a simple multi-input circuit, shortening the signal path and improving the sound quality. The Phono circuit consists of four equalizer amplifiers. The MC cartridge amplifier and the MM cartridge amplifier are each dedicated and independent, and the L/R is also independent. The MC amplifier uses a super low-noise High Gm FET in parallel, and a low-noise reference voltage power supply combining constant current and constant voltage to realize a low-impedance, low-noise power supply.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-540 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-540-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-570":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1989 at ¥350,000. This is an integrated amplifier developed by combining the know-how for ultra-low frequency expression obtained with the M-07 and techniques for processing very small signals obtained with the C-06 and E-06. The power amplifier section uses a pure class A operation method. In this method, a constant bias current is always supplied up to the maximum output, so that there is no fluctuation in the operation point due to the signal, and the high-quality power characteristic of class A operation is achieved. The power supply uses a large-capacity power transformer that is 30% larger than a normal same class amplifier. In addition, the constant voltage power supply section of each stage independent winding has been thoroughly designed to have low impedance to improve instantaneous response capability. In particular, the current capacity to the power stage has a margin of 1.5 times that of the normal one to achieve ultra-low impedance. The signal path from the input terminal to the speaker terminal is structured to completely eliminate complicated routing and unnecessary small objects. For input switching, the wiring is shortened by remotely switching only the selected terminal including the ground terminal at the optimum position near the input terminal. For switching, a nitrogen gas sealed contact relay is used to improve sound quality.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-570 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-570-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"marantz-pm-80":{"more":[{"t":"This integrated amplifier was developed after studying the latest digital source in addition to the traditional amplifier technology of Marantz. In addition to a large power transformer, a special 18,000 μ Fx2 electrolytic capacitor is used for the power supply. In addition, very thick OFC wires are used for speaker circuits and power cords. A noise killer circuit is installed to suppress the rectification noise generated when converting AC to DC. It blocks high-frequency noise from several hundred kHz to around 1 MHz to ensure sound quality without turbidity. Moreover, we have succeeded in increasing the low-frequency power by lowering the primary circuit impedance of the power supply. In addition, noise is completely eliminated by wiring and careful circuit configuration. The power stage consists of parallel push-pull Pc-100W power transistors with high linearity, and three stage Darlington connection for higher gain. In addition, a copper shield plate is mounted on the power transistor to suppress the radiation and vibration from the transistor and to completely eliminate the influence on minute signals.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Marantz PM-80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-80-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/marantz-pm-80.jpg","xc":0,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-80-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/MARANTZ/amp/pm-80.JPG"}},"micro-seiki-cl-m-2-dc":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥290,000. Preamplifier pursuing high sound quality with a simple circuit composed of carefully selected luxury parts. The signal part is driven by the independent DC power supply battery. DC-M2, the power supply unit, has a charging control module. In addition, the battery adopts a sealed lead-acid battery with very small internal resistance (8A) for the load current of CL-M2DC 0.2A. Charging stops automatically while playing music, and the electromagnetic negative effects were canceled. This DC-M2 was sold separately from CL-M2DC. Chas has its own vibration control structure to reduce mechanical vibration. In CL-M2DC, we supply brazing materials with copper plating on new alloy cosmar.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Micro Seiki CL-M 2 DC (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/MICRO/amp/cl-m2dc.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-a-636":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1989 at ¥64,800. an integrated amplifier that inherits the design concept of A-838 and adopts a non-vibration and non-resonance design such as a clean ground system and direct construction II. It uses a clean ground system to prevent harmful noise currents generated by power transformers and heat sinks. Power transformer and heatsink isolated from chassis and installed Noise is prevented from entering the signal path, and a special bypass is provided to return the noise current to the noise source to prevent noise from entering the music signal. It is equipped with Direct Construction II which realized the shortest signal path length of 85 cm by further developing the direct construction which achieved the signal path length of 120 cm. The input block is designed to mechanically remotely control the input selector and main volume. In addition, the source direct switch is turned ON to prevent input signals from flowing to the front panel. In addition, by laying out the volume substrate on the power amplifier, the routing of excess wiring is extremely shortened compared to conventional ones. In addition, the power amplifier block is arranged along the signal path to direct the output of the power stage directly to the speaker selector block to minimize the distance from the power supply. In the speaker selector block, the speaker terminals are directly attached to the circuit board on which the relay is attached, eliminating the waste of wiring.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer A-636 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-636-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/pioneer-a-636.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-database.com","page":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-636-e.html","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-636.JPG"}},"pioneer-a-838":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1989 at ¥120,000. This integrated amplifier is designed with no vibration and no resonance and incorporates new technologies such as a clean ground system. A clean ground system is used to shut out harmful noise current generated in the power supply and large current section from the electric circuit. The power transformer and heat sink, which are sources of noise, are isolated from the chassis to prevent noise from entering the signal path. In addition, the contact points between the circuit and the chassis are connected at appropriate points to provide a bypass for returning noise current to the noise source so that noise does not enter the signal current. Direct Construction II is used to shorten the signal path and prevent signal degradation and interference. While inheriting the conventional direct construction technology, the power amplifier board and the main volume board are integrated to greatly reduce the number of wiring steps and realize a signal path length of 85 cm. The input block has a structure in which the input selector and main volume are mechanically controlled remotely to minimize the signal path. In addition, by turning on the source direct switch, the input signal does not flow to the front panel at all, so you can enjoy a purer sound. The power amplifier block is laid out along the signal flow so that the output of the power stage is directed straight to the speaker block and the distance from the power supply is minimized.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Pioneer A-838 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/PIONEER-EXCLUSIVE/amp/a-838-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-307":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥53,000. DC amplifier We use capac for signal and negative feedback (NF) loop. The DC amplifier method has excellent phase characteristics up to ultra-low range and has excellent responsiveness to input signals. AU-307 pursues naked characteristics and reduces the occurrence of the required minimum negative feedback (NF) amplifier transient modulation distortion as well as the DC amplifier configuration. This not only improves the dynamic characteristics of the ultra-low range, but also improves the dynamic characteristics of the ultra-high range. The circuit configuration is an OCL system that is directly connected to all stages. As with the DC power amplifier part, it suppresses the generation of transient mixed modulation distortion, and the external influence is prevented by detaching the power supply part to the shield case.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sansui AU-α 307 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-307.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sansui-au-307.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-307.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SANSUI/amp/au-307.jpg"}},"sony-ta-f-303-esd":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥64,600. Equipped with D/A converter based on TA-F222ESR. D/A converter is equipped with PDM (Pulse Densityulationulation). The PDM method is composed of one current source and one electronic switch. This eliminates the occurrence of fine nonlinear distortion, glitch and zero cross distortion. TA-F505ESD features two optical inputs and one coaxial input. The LED indicator is also available for 48kHz and 32kHz sampling frequency. This material has the characteristics of vibration damping, which has high internal loss compared to metal, and has high strength and high precision machining.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F 303 ESD (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f303esd.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-n-330-es":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥44,800. The power supply unit is equipped with a large-size Troidal. In addition, S.T.D. power supply system is equipped with separate A-class and power-stage rectification circuit. The velvet-like electrostatic planting is installed on the vibration proof platform to fix the power supply capac. 2 input selector Switches can be used as mono amplifier.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-N 330 ES (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n330es.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/sony-ta-n-330-es.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n330es.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-n330es.JPG"}},"sony-ta-nr-1":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1992 at ¥500,000. A mono power amplifier with structural gradation and careful design while realizing a 1Ω load continuous drive. 6,800μFx2/3,300μFx2 for voltage amplifier, 22,000μFx2 for power amplifier. This is applied with epoxy-based adhesives by skipping the ultra-thin and short nylon piles with the power of static electricity. The surface of the case is damped well, eliminating the impact of external vibrations, and effectively suppressing its own vibration.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-NR 1 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-nr1.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-v-460":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1989 at ¥32,000. Integrated amplifier with classAA circuit. A classAA circuit is adopted, and voltage control and current drive are each carried out by a dedicated amplifier, so that it is resistant to load fluctuation, and voltage control faithful to input signal and current supply with margin are compatible. High-purity OFC winding is used for the power transformer to realize excellent regulation. In addition, a high-speed EX electrolytic capacitor is used to reduce distortion. Power Amp Direct is installed. With this function, the input signal is directly input to the power amplifier via only the classAA buffer and the power amplifier input volume, thereby achieving higher quality playback. It has an Route 6 input selector and an independent Rec selector.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-V 460 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-v460-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-ast-a-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥50,000. A power amplifier for active servo loudspeaker. The input can be connected from integrated amplifier because it can connect three kinds of accessories terminal, pre-out terminal and loudspeaker terminal. The included general-purpose cartridge can be replaced to ring the conventional loudspeaker.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha AST-A 10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ast-a10.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-ast-a-10.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ast-a10.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ast-a10.JPG"}},"yamaha-ast-a-5":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1989 at ¥30,000. Active servo loudspeaker dedicated small power amplifier. If you replace the standard cartridge sold separately, you can also play the traditional loudspeaker. Banana plug fit screw type SP terminal is available.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha AST-A 5 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ast-a5.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{},"photo":{"ph":"photos/x/yamaha-ast-a-5.jpg","xc":1,"site":"audio-heritage.jp","page":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ast-a5.html","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ast-a5.JPG"}},"yamaha-ax-2000":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥230,000. D/A converter integrated stereo amplifier with advanced digital direct yesterday. The advanced digital direct function has improved the SN at the actual volume control level around -22dB. The output of the built-in D/A converter unit is a high level signal of 2.0Vrms to 7.5Vrms. The volume control controller adopts active volume control by combination with variable resistor and linear amplifier. This is the maximum value of volume control, and the noise level decreases as narrowing down. Direct playback for 7.5V high-level D/A output and filter playback for 2.0V normal D/A output. amplifier's unique HCA circuit is available in the power amplifier section.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha AX-2000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/ax-2000.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-mx-35":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1990 at ¥36,500. 4ch or 2ch There are two types of titanium color and black color.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha MX-35 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/mx-35.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-mx-55":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1987 at ¥98,000. 4ch/2ch switchable power amplifier developed for DSP system. Two independent power supply system with two chmetrical design. 4ch/2ch switch can be used as a stereo power amplifier. With a level control, you can adjust the volume level of each left and right at 2 channels.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha MX-55 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/amp/mx-55.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-g-9000":{"more":[{"t":"Ahhh…the beautiful look of the late 70’s Sansui receivers. The warm golden glow from the dial and meter lights and the smorgasbord of buttons, knobs, and switches below. It’s a stereo lovers delight. The best Sansui I ever had was the G-8000. Here we have the Sansui G-9000. There was also a G-9000DB with only a minor difference that I’ll get into in a moment. The G-9000 put out a massive 160 watts per channel and it was one of the more popular choices for military men overseas in the 70’s. It retailed for around $1000.00 but was discounted at some of the miltary exchanges. It is known for good clean power and you’ll be hard pressed to find any G-9000 owner that does not love the unit.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui G-9000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-g-9000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sa-1000":{"more":[{"t":"This giant Technics SA-1000 receiver is one of the rarer monster receivers. You don’t see them come up for sale very often. And, while they may not be as popular as Marantz or Pioneer they still bring big bucks on the auction market. They were produced from 1977 to 1979 at the height of the receiver wars when every manufacturer was trying to outdo the rest. The SA-1000 probably isn’t the best styled receiver from the late 70’s but it does look nice and has the distinctive Technics / Panasonic look of the time. What really got people’s attention was the performance. Are you ready for these stats? The SA-1000 put out 330 watts per channel! That’s far more then most other receivers on the market at the time.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Technics SA-1000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/technics-sa-1000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"revox-b780":{"more":[{"t":"Revox, the consumer division of Studer, is probably more known for their fantastic reel-to-reel machines, such as the B77 and PR99, than anything else. However, this German made Revox B780 is one fine receiver and was introduced to the market in 1980. It is not an AM/FM receiver. It is FM only and produces 70 watts per channel into 8 ohms with no more than 0.05% total harmonic distortion. It definitely has a distinctive appearance and looks a little more like a piece of electronic test equipment you’d see in a lab rather than a receiver. There is something about the look that is appealing though. I guess the stereo has a feel of precision to it. Pretty straightforward credo. To achieve this Revox took their B760 digital frequency synthesizer tuner and their B750 mkII integrated amplifier, re-engineered them into what they called a ‘symbiotic relationship’, and created the B780.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Revox B780","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/revox-b780","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sony-str-v7":{"more":[{"t":"The Sony STR-V7 is a sleek and powerful vintage receiver that was first introduced in 1978. At 150 watts per channel it is a classic monster receiver. As the flagship model of Sony’s STR receiver lineup at the time, the STR-V7 retailed for a premium price of $900 and combined Sony’s top engineering and technology into one very cool stereo. With its classy styling and restrained aesthetics, the STR-V7 exudes elegance. The brushed metal faceplate, with its chrome accents, and green glow of the tuning dial give the STR-V7 a polished, high-end look. The use of different textures and finishes for the knobs, meters, and display windows balanced functionality with sophisticated design. The front panel of the STR-V7 focuses on intuitive controls and informative displays. Two large, left/right channel power meters show the amplifier’s output up to 200 watts. A third meter shows center tuning.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sony STR-V7","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sony-str-v7","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"pioneer-sx-d7000":{"more":[{"t":"In 1980 Pioneer introduced the Pioneer SX-D7000 and made a statement that it was heading into the digital future. It’s similar in many ways to the SX-3900 except that Pioneer did away with nearly all of the knobs – replacing them with push buttons. There are no analog meter or dials either as Pioneer utilized their Fluroscan technology for the power meter and digital tuning display. The SX-D7000 retailed for about $800. Aesthetically it’s a beautiful receiver. It has a modern, clean look to it and the symmetrical layout of the controls give it balance to the eye. It’s rated at 120 watts per channel and 0.005% total harmonic distortion. The power output and tuning meters are Fluroscan and the Treble and Bass controls are adjusted via sliders with 11 click stops. The Adaptor switch allows the user to patch in a signal processor such as a graphic equalizer or reverb unit.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Pioneer SX-D7000","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/pioneer-sx-d7000","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-d907":{"more":[{"t":"A DC integrated amplifier equipped with Sansui's original diamond actuation circuit to improve dynamic distortion for live music playback. The equalizer, flat amplifier / tone control and power amplifier are all configured as push-pull output DC amplifiers with improved bare characteristics. In addition, in pursuit of sound quality, input capacitors for all block stages are eliminated, and a direct-coupled system with FET inputs for all stages is adopted to achieve pure music signal transmission and a wide range. All the FETs used are selected to have low-noise and high-gm characteristics. In addition, each block stage has a symmetrical circuit structure with symmetry, which greatly reduces harmful TIM distortion and envelope distortion and improves sound quality. The power amplifier section is a drive circuit with a power stage and 3-step amplification configuration. The first stage is an operation circuit with constant current using dual FET that allows large current to flow with low noise, the second pre-drive stage is a diamond operation circuit (PAT. PEND) with dual complimentary service that suppresses the generation of TIM distortion with powerful drive capability, and the third stage is a current operation push-pull circuit. The final power stage uses Sansui Custom NM (Non Magnetic) transistors, and the entire circuit is composed of symmetrical symmetrical circuits.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-D907 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-d907-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-l-58a":{"more":[{"t":"Released September 1979 at ¥149,000. This is an integrated amplifier with an original duo-beta circuit that not only improves the characteristics but also improves the quality of the amplifier to improve sound quality. Duo Beta Circuit means a circuit that combines two NFBs. This circuit does not attempt to improve various characteristics of the amplifier by investing a large amount of NFB. Instead, various characteristics are improved by creating an amplifier with good quality (bare characteristics) and combining it with a small amount of NFB and DC servo. In the power amplifier section, a pure complimentary service differential push-pull circuit using FETs for N-channel 2SK163 and P-channel (2SJ44) is adopted at the input stage to improve bare distortion characteristics as a DC-amplifier configuration. In addition, everything from the input stage to the output stage is composed of a push-pull circuit, and at the same time, a transistor and FET with high ft (high cutoff frequency) and low Cob (collector output capacitance) are adopted to reduce distortion. The output stage employs MOS FETs (2SK134 and 2SJ49) with an ft of approximately 500 MHz. In addition to allowing a bias current of 300 mA or more, a high-speed driver circuit is combined to create a \"notchless class A\" amplifier that does not perform switching operation.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Luxman L-58A (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/LUXMAN/amp/l-58a-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"technics-su-a2":{"more":[{"t":"Released November 1977 at ¥1,600,000. A preamplifier with low distortion by class-A operation in all stages. In order to completely remove switching distortion and crossover distortion, all stages are operated as class A. As a result, the rated distortion factor of 0.003% is achieved at 20 Hz to 20 kHz and 1 V output from the Phono MM to the output terminal. A low-noise dual FET is used for MM, and newly developed low-noise transistors M67L and M68L are used for MC preamp, resulting in high S / N ratio. The SU-A2 employs a DC amplifier configuration that eliminates the interstage capacitor of the signal system and the capacitor with a time constant in the NFB loop. As a result, the amplifier has a DC gain and eliminates the phase loop, improving the fidelity of waveform transmission. Moreover, the coupling capacitor is removed from the phono equalizer to form a DC equalizer. In order to suppress DC drift, which is the most important point of DC amplifier, an active thermal servo amplifier with thermal feedback is adopted. For switching the input selector and the recording mode selector, a touch switch method is adopted in which a high-reliability relay for small signals is operated by a micro switch.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Technics SU-A2 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/TechnicsPanasonic/amp/su-a2-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"krell-ksa-100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1980 at ¥930,000. Cler’s first stereo power amplifier. The circuit adopts Pure A-Class Operations Pure Complementary Circuit, which is considered to be a simple amount of harmonic distortion, as well as the appearance of distortion modes that affect hearing. In addition, NFB is suppressed to 15dB by focusing on motion characteristics. In order to deal with the heat generation problem caused by pure A class operation, the power block is set up with heat sink and ultra-quiet cooling fan, and the temperature of the power block is strictly controlled from 75 to 80 degrees to prevent thermal distortion. This is a large power supply equivalent to 400W amplifier for general B-class operation. This enables stable output of 800W+800W as the calculation value even if the impedance decreases to 1Ω. The inside is a fully L/R independent twin-monoral structure, and the power switch and AC cord are all in common.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Krell KSA-100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/KRELL/amp/ksa-100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-07m":{"more":[{"t":"The power amplifier needs to keep the loudspeaker code within 1m to fully drive the loudspeaker system. A mono power amplifier developed from the conclusion. The circuit is very simplified and the signal is supplied to the output terminal by following the shortest route from the input terminal. These circuit designs improve various characteristics such as S/N ratio and distortion rate.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-07M (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/amp/l-07m.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ta-f555es":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥99,000. Equipped with our unique technology, we are able to brush up the details at a low level and respond to digital sources. We use the audio current method to cut off between four amplifiers. By separating between L/R channels at the same time, the characteristics of each preamplifier, power amplifier, and L/R channels are pursuant to the ideal grounding. In addition, input signals and loads are determined clearly, and there is no influence of ground loops or power supply impedance, and the external disturbance of wires and switches intervened in the signal path is also ignored. Two-ter Linear Gain Control Attenuator is available for volume control. Because of this, the characteristics of actual use are good.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony TA-F555ES (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/amp/ta-f555es.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sp-10mk3":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1982 at ¥250,000. DD turntable is the highest grade quartz synthesizer made full use of all technics' player technology. This value is 2.5 times higher than SP-10mk2, and the super weight turntable of 10kg is 0.25 seconds, and the rotation angle is 30 °. The stop mechanism is equipped with an electronic brake that instantaneously operates the drive circuit of mechanical brake and reverse rotation. This makes it possible to stop the superweight turntable of 10kg in 0.3 seconds, and there is almost no shock sound even if it stops instantaneously by using mechanical brakes and electronic brakes. SP-10mk3 is equipped with parts selected as the first-class product. In particular, turntable is a two-layer structure that combines 15mm thick copper alloy turntable to aluminum die-cast turntable, and realizes ultra-high iner mass of weight 10kg and 1.1ton/cm2. There is no change in rotation speed for constant load within 10kg/cm.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SP-10MK3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/etc/sp-10mk3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"revox-b790":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1978 at ¥198,000. Turntable using linear tracking method. The turntable part adopts the direct drive method by quartz control. The tonearm section contains only 38mm ultra short Tangential tonearm. Tonearm control requires an electronic servo. VMS20EmkII","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Revox B790 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/STUDER-REVOX/player/b790.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"kenwood-l-07d":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1979 at ¥380,000. Record player of the L series, based on R-6197 released in the audio fair in 1978. Direct drive system is available for driving. Direct drive improves wow-flotter characteristics by in a quartz lock in a servo circuit. The drive motor has a slotless new quartz PLL servo motor. This motor incorporates a dynamic conpensator that automatically corrects phase against load ctuations such as viscous changes in the bearing part oil, eliminating adverse effects such as temperature changes in the bearing part oil. In addition, the double servo coupling is adopted to automatically switch the control method at ±3% of the rated rotation speed. When the speed is up to 3%, the torque is obtained by phase control operation.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Kenwood L-07D (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TRIO-KENWOOD/player/l-07d.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sony-ps-x9":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥380,000. A high-end player system with MC head amplifier and equal amplifier amplifier thanks to the integrated idea that the record player has equal amplifier. motor is a linear slotless motor with a traditional 6-fold torque developed specifically. Linear slotless motor achieves quiet and smooth rotation by removing the slots causing the torque mura (co ). In addition, it has more stable rotational accuracy by adopting linear drive method, and it realizes powerful torque of starting torque 7kg-cm by polarized structure and large magnet ring. The motor housing uses 5mm thick iron castings, and the rotational system is modified by its robust structure. The crystal lock is applied to the servo circuit by the crystal oscillator, and the magnetic disk rotation speed detection method is used for the rotation speed detection unit. A large weight turntable button with a diameter of 38cm. Because it is a turntable with conventional iner mass and weight, it suppresses the madness of the rotation speed caused by needle pressure load. It is also considered for transmission system because it supports head amplifier and equal amplifier built-in.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Sony PS-X9 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/SONY-ESPRIT/player/ps-x9.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-80":{"more":[],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-80 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/etc/dp-80-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"victor-jvc-tt-101":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1977 at ¥150,000. The basic servo system is the same as the conventional direct drive method. The motor drive circuit controls the motor drive circuit by obtaining the servo signal from the integrated FG of the 180 slots in the motor. The other quartz lock servo system compares the same FG detection signal and the base signal phase based on the accurate oscillation frequency of the crystal, and sends the difference to the phase control circuit to drive the motor drive circuit. Rotation accuracy is improved by adding quartz locks, especially for long-cycle wowes and drifts. ± servo system is used for basic servo system. Because the rotational motorctuation of motor occurs in the direction (minus direction) where the rotation is slow in most cases, the conventional servo method is emphasized for speed reduction. On the other hand, the drive current of the motor is often applied to the speed bar (plus direction), and the response is delayed. In the ± servo system, the speed over is quick to respond, and the speed reduction from 45rpm to 33-1/3rpm is performed immediately. The world's first variable pitch control.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Victor / JVC TT-101 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/VICTOR/etc/tt-101.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-9090":{"more":[{"t":"I wouldn’t be exaggerating if I said that the Sansui 9090 receiver is one of the best receivers ever made because it is. A fully restored Sansui 9090 is something to behold both visually and aurally. Produced in 1975 it was top of the line for Sansui and the bigger brother of the Sansui 8080. It produced 110 watts per channel. That was a lot of power for that time. In fact, when Radio Electronics reviewed it in 1976 it was the most powerful integrated receiver they had ever tested. It retailed for around $750 and was meant for those audio enthusiasts that either didn’t have the space for separate components (amplifier, tuner, preamplifier) or couldn’t afford them. The 9090 definitely lessened the performance gap that existed at the time between integrated receivers and separate components. When the Sansui 9090 stereo is powered on via the power switch just under the tuning meters an adjacent red light will flash for a few seconds until voltages have been stabilized after which it will turn green and the audio signal will be sent to the speakers.","s":"classicreceivers.com"}],"src":[{"t":"classicreceivers.com – Sansui 9090","u":"https://classicreceivers.com/sansui-9090","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"luxman-sq38fd":{"more":[{"t":"Released July 1970 at ¥98,000. SQ38 Series 50CA10 is used for output pipes, and OY15 is used for output pipes. The power amplifier part is based on the murad type circuit, which improves the distortion characteristics of the high area by improving the details to maximize the features of this circuit. The preamplifier part has two-stage negative feedback (NF) type equalizer and LUX type negative feedback (NF) type tone control. The tone control is independent and can be switched to two curve points for both low and high. Because the output impedance of the loudspeaker can be selected by each system, you can choose the optimal load even if you connect the different loudspeaker of the impedance.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Luxman SQ38FD (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/LUXMAN/amp/sq38fd.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sp-10":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1972 at ¥82,000. Turntable is a direct drive system developed by Technics Technology Team. This eliminates mechanical vibrations caused by the reduction mechanism. The turntable has a weight of 2.8 kg and iner mass of 330 kg and cm2. Each item is strictly dynamically adjusted. In addition, it is possible to adjust rotation speed independently by 33, 1/3, and 45 rotations.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SP-10 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/etc/sp-10.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"dual-701":{"more":[{"t":"A record player with an electronically controlled direct drive motor. It uses a direct drive system in which the motor itself rotates at record speed. A unique feedback circuit keeps the rotational speed constant, and since it is a DC motor, the effects of fluctuations in power supply voltage and frequency are prevented. In addition, the double structure of the field coil cancels out the continuous pulses of the rotating magnetic field, thereby suppressing uneven rotation and vibration trouble. The tone arm part has dual unique 4-point gimbal, and horizontal friction is maintained at 0.015g or less, and reliable tracing is realized with 0.25g ultra-light needle pressure. A special resonance filter built into the balance weight eliminates resonance from the drive system and interference with the cartridge. The cartridge uses the Orthophone M20E exclusive model for the dual 701, which has the same or better performance than the commercially available M15E Super. Since the turntable is a DD type, it is integrated with the rotor section of the motor to achieve stable rotation.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Dual 701 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DUAL/player/701-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"garrard-zero-100":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1960 at ¥56,000. The base was sold separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Garrard Zero 100 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/GARRARD/player/zero100.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"denon-dp-3000":{"more":[{"t":"Released June 1972 at ¥43,000. A direct drive turntable that inherits the performance and design of the DP 5000 and pursues cost performance. In the DP 3000, the pulse recorded inside the rim of the turntable is first detected by a magnetic head for speed detection. The pulse signal is amplified and passed through a limiter circuit. A demodulation circuit converts the change in speed into a change in voltage. This voltage is compared with a reference voltage set in advance to achieve the specified speed. The voltage difference is used to control the motor drive power supply voltage for servo control. As a result, the speed can be easily changed by changing the reference voltage. The circuit and elements used are highly stable, and highly reliable characteristics can be obtained even with temperature change, aging change, negative variable and simultaneously. In speed detection, the inside of the rim of the turntable is coated with a magnetic material with a large coercive force.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Denon DP-3000 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/DENON-COLUMBIA/etc/dp-3000-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"sansui-au-x1111-mos-vintage":{"more":[{"t":"This is the last amplifier in the X series that started with AU-X1. Earth-based amplifiers drive the speakers between the output of the amplifier and the ground, so they are susceptible to noise and distortion from the ground, which degrade sound quality. In order to solve this problem, we have adopted a balanced circuit that is not grounded. In this circuit, the - side of the speaker is double-push-pull driven in both directions under the same conditions as the + side. This eliminates unnecessary high-frequency components such as noise and distortion, and realizes an excellent sound image at a low distortion rate. In addition, there is no noise from the power supply and no IHM (Interface Hum Modulation) caused by back electromotive force from the speakers. It also supports changes in the impedance and phase of speakers. The power supply circuit that operates the balanced circuit is also a closed loop with no connection to the ground circuit. In addition, we have achieved low impedance and high speed in the entire power supply by adopting a newly developed heavy-duty transformer that has been carefully examined from the viewpoints of sound quality and electrical performance without simply pursuing a sense of weight.","s":"audio-database.com"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-database.com – Sansui AU-X1111 MOS Vintage (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-database.com/SANSUI/amp/au-x1111mosvintage-e.html","lang":"en"}],"facts":{}},"yamaha-gt-2000x":{"more":[{"t":"Released 1985 at ¥320,000. Record player announced as the vertex model of the GT series. Motor has a new DC 4-phase 8-pole coreless hole motor that considers the effects of ripple noise during real performance rather than earning startup torque. The motor shaft has a diameter of 20mm and a length of 60mm. tonearm is equipped with YSA-1 of gimbal support straight arm. This arm uses brass to remove magnetic elements from the signal path. The headshell is non-magnetic and aluminum cutting. In addition, 0.15Ω signal reciprocating resistance is realized by using 1.2mmφ OFC lead wire and ITK#3000. GT-2000X is equipped with an optional auto lifter YAL-1 for GT-2000. YAL-1 is non-contact optical, smooth operation and excellent operability.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Yamaha GT-2000X (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/YAMAHA/player/gt-2000x.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}},"technics-sl-1200mk3":{"more":[{"t":"Released October 1989 at ¥69,800. The third generation record player of the SL-1200 series. A continuous pitch control method is adopted for rotation control, and the pitch can be changed continuously in the range of ±8% while the quartz lock is closed. All-round detection FG is adopted, and more accurate detection signal is realized by detecting all-round of rotation axis. The drive motor adopts an integrated DD motor with 1.5kg and cm start torque, and the weight turntable reaches the constant speed at 0.7 seconds (0.7/3rpm). Turntable has improved vibration resistance by deadning rubber on the back of the rubber sheet and turntable. Tonearm uses a gimbal suspension method to achieve superior initial sensitivity of 7mg horizontally and vertically. It is equipped with a lock type armrest adjustment mechanism, and the height adjustment ring of the precision helicoid finish enables fine adjustment in the range of 6mm. The cabinet is an integrated type of heavy-weight special rubber that uses aluminum die casting and has a large vibration damping rate. In addition, DD motor, tonearm, and dust cover are connected to this special rubber, and we provide thorough anti-vibration measures to isolate each part separately.","s":"audio-heritage.jp, translated from Japanese"}],"src":[{"t":"audio-heritage.jp – Technics SL-1200MK3 (catalogue commentary)","u":"https://audio-heritage.jp/TECHNICS/player/sl-1200mk3.html","lang":"ja"}],"facts":{}}};
